      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"reset code at $0000","comment":"read return PC from ROM"},
        "3": {"comment":"not interrupt for now"},
        "4": {"comment":"duplicated because soft RST00h arrives here"},
        "8": {"comment":"I=0, reset ID"},
        "12": {"comment":"remember interrupt status"},
        "14": {"comment":"flap tested later during reset"},
        "15": {"comment":"enable tick interrupt"},
        "19": {"comment":"reset command register"},
        "21": {"synopsis":"snooze on coma and wait for interrupt\nEntry: H = interrupt mask L = RTC mask."},
        "24": {"comment":"preset kernel bank"},
        "26": {"comment":"enable and ack RTC interrupts"},
        "31": {"comment":"enable and ack interrupts"},
        "36": {"comment":"wait until interrupt"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"delay ~300 000 clock cycles             ; used by card interrupt and screen driver","comment":"10 000*30 cycles"},
        "45": {"comment":"7+11+12 cycles"},
        "51": {"comment":"pad FFh's until 0038H (Z80 INT vector)"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"Maskable interrupt entry at $0038, run in two situations: at $0038 while bank 0 is paged at\n$0000 after a hard reset, and at $C038 through the low-RAM INT vector, which nmi_halt points\nhere before the machine enters coma. I <> 0 means a wake-up from coma and goes to NMIWakeup.\nI = 0 means a reset: SP is pointed at a two-byte stack in this ROM and VerifySlotType checks\nslot 1 (D = 1, E = $3F), returning to Bootstrap through that stack.\nEntry: I = 0 during reset, COMA_RDSK in coma.\nChanges: AF, DE, SP (reset path).","comment":"I=0? INT occured during reset"},
        "58": {"comment":"try to awake in segment 3 already bound"},
        "61": {"comment":"read return PC from ROM"},
        "64": {"comment":"check slot 1, max size 63 banks"},
        "67": {"comment":"ret at ROMstack"},
        "70": {"synopsis":"stack in ROM","comment":"if OZ ROM is in slot 0, then poll for OZ in slot 1,,,"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"Reset step reached through the ROM stack after VerifySlotType: decides whether OZ in slot 1\nboots instead of this one. If slot 1 holds a bootable ROM (BU_B_ROM in D) whose card header\nsubtype is CB_OS1 ('Z') and the Escape key is not the only key held, it jumps to the card's\nCH_HOOK ($BFF8 in S2) to boot the slot 1 OZ. Otherwise it falls into Boot_reset.\nEntry: D = slot type from VerifySlotType; slot 1's top bank bound in S2.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"check for bootable ROM in slot 1"},
        "74": {"comment":"not application ROM? skip"},
        "76": {"comment":"subtype"},
        "79": {"comment":"'Z' for OZ_SLOT1"},
        "83": {"comment":"OZ ROM exists in slot 1, poll for ESC to boot from ROM.0 instead..."},
        "88": {"comment":"Escape key is pressed?"},
        "90": {"comment":"ESC not pressed, boot ROM.1"},
        "93": {"synopsis":"Continues the reset in this OZ: binds kernel bank 1 into segment 2 (port BL_SR2) and jumps\nto Reset there, which initialises internal RAM, the Blink, the low-RAM code and SP. Also the\ntarget of the ROM header's reset path of an OZ that runs from slot 1.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: A."},
        "95": {"comment":"get kernel 1 into segment 2"},
        "97": {"comment":"init internal RAM, blink and low-ram code and set SP"},
        "100": {"comment":"pad FFh's until 0066H (Z80 NMI vector)"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"Non-maskable interrupt entry at $0066, run while bank 0 is paged at $0000 after a reset and\nat $C066 through the low-RAM NMI vector while the machine is in coma. If SP is in page $00xx\nthe machine is still starting up and Reset0 restarts it. Otherwise it binds kernel bank 0\ninto segment 3 and continues at HW_NMI2.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"if stack points to $00xx we go back to reset"},
        "108": {"comment":"reset if SP=$00xx"},
        "112": {"comment":"MS3b00"},
        "114": {"comment":"into ROM code"},
        "117": {"synopsis":"all 2-byte calls use OSframe","comment":"Bank DC, $8x00"},
        "119": {"comment":"dc/dc.asm"},
        "123": {"synopsis":"Entry of the OZ call table for the two-byte GN calls: selects bank GN_BNK and the GN_TBL\npage, then shares the dispatcher with CallOS2byte. The dispatcher steps the caller's PC past\nthe second opcode byte, builds the OS frame (OSFramePushMain), reads the function address\nfrom the bank's table at the second opcode byte, binds kernel bank 1 into S2 and the code\nbank into S3, and jumps to the function. The function returns to $xx03 of the table page in\nS3, the bank's exit through the OS frame.\nEntry: E = second opcode byte; the caller's BC, DE, HL in the alternate set and AF in AF';\nstack holds the S2/S3 bindings and the caller's PC (as CallOZMain leaves them).\nExit: into the function with the caller's registers, Fz = 1, Fc = 0, IY = OS frame.","comment":"Bank GN, $8x00"},
        "125": {"comment":"gn/gnmisc1.asm"},
        "129": {"synopsis":"Entry of the OZ call table for the two-byte OS calls ($xx06 codes): selects kernel bank 0\nand the OS_TBL page ($FFxx) and runs the dispatcher shared with CallGN, which reads the\nfunction address from the word table at the end of OS_TBL and jumps to it in segment 3.\nEntry: E = second opcode byte; the caller's registers in the alternate set and AF', as\nCallOZMain leaves them.\nExit: into the function with the caller's registers, Fz = 1, Fc = 0, IY = OS frame.","comment":"Kernel0 bank, $FFxx"},
        "131": {"comment":"os/ostables.asm"},
        "133": {"comment":"S2/S3"},
        "134": {"comment":"caller PC"},
        "136": {"comment":"caller PC"},
        "137": {"comment":"return here"},
        "140": {"comment":"OSPUSH and ret below"},
        "143": {"comment":"Fz=1, Fc=0"},
        "144": {"comment":"alt register"},
        "145": {"comment":"bind code in"},
        "148": {"comment":"alt registers"},
        "149": {"comment":"function address into DE"},
        "153": {"comment":"or $4000 - return into S3"},
        "155": {"comment":"return call always at $xx03"},
        "157": {"comment":"return address"},
        "158": {"comment":"function address"},
        "160": {"comment":"caller A"},
        "162": {"comment":"code bank"},
        "163": {"comment":"S2 is always kernel 1 with 2 bytes calls"},
        "166": {"comment":"main registers"},
        "167": {"comment":"bind code into S3 and ret to it"},
        "170": {"synopsis":"Handler of unused OZ call table entries: returns to the caller through OZCallReturn2 with Fc\n= 1 and A = RC_OK (zero), the caller's other registers unchanged.\nEntry: none.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_OK."},
        "176": {"synopsis":"send character directly to printer filter","comment":"bind K1 in S2"},
        "179": {"comment":"!! just L"},
        "184": {"comment":"no cli, print direct"},
        "186": {"comment":"otherwise use DC"},
        "189": {"comment":"no error? exit"},
        "193": {"comment":"timeout? retry forever"},
        "198": {"comment":"in K1, binded by OSFramePush"},
        "204": {"synopsis":"OS_Dom: opens the director's memory pool (internal two-byte call $FE06), calling OS_Mop with\nA = MM_S1|MM_MUL|MM_FIX and BC = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: IX = memory pool handle.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Mop."},
        "209": {"comment":"allocate memory pool, A=mask"},
        "212": {"synopsis":"Sets up the fixed RAM of a bad or ugly application when it is entered; does nothing for a\nwell-behaved one.\n1. Size in pages: ubAppContRAM, or the default ubBadSize (in KB) times 4 when zero, at most\n160 pages (40K), and at most 32 pages (8K) on a machine without a 128K RAM card.\n2. Stores the size in ubAppContRAM and the size plus 32 pages in ubBadInfoEndPage.\n3. Sets ubAppBindings: S0 = $21, then the expansion's first banks for S1 and S2 when the\narea needs them.\n4. Opens a memory pool (OS_Mop) into pAppBadMemHandle and allocates the pages with\nAllocBadRAM2; on failure CloseBadRAM frees what was allocated.\nEntry: application DOR flags in ubAppDORFlags.\nExit: Fc = 0 (Fz = 1 for a well-behaved application).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "215": {"comment":"nice? exit with Fc=0"},
        "222": {"comment":"default bad process size in kb"},
        "225": {"comment":"translate into pages, max 160 pages"},
        "231": {"comment":"max 160 pages, 40 KB"},
        "237": {"comment":"remember size"},
        "241": {"comment":"remember bottom bank of the expansion"},
        "242": {"comment":"limit size to 32 pages on unexpanded machine"},
        "246": {"comment":"Fc=1, unexpanded machine"},
        "257": {"comment":"8K more"},
        "265": {"comment":"S0 b20 upper half - first 8KB of bad app RAM"},
        "269": {"comment":"less than 16KB? done"},
        "273": {"comment":"16KB more in seg1"},
        "276": {"comment":"less than 32KB? done"},
        "280": {"comment":"total 40KB"},
        "288": {"comment":"allocate memory pool"},
        "290": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "299": {"comment":"didn't get all RAM needed? free what we got"},
        "305": {"synopsis":"For a bad or ugly application, closes the memory pool in pAppBadMemHandle (OS_Mcl), which\nfrees all its bad application memory.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, IX."},
        "309": {"comment":"nice? exit"},
        "313": {"comment":"free all bad app memory"},
        "323": {"synopsis":"For a bad or ugly application, allocates the swap pages of its fixed area (AllocBadRAM2) and\nthen exchanges, page by page, the contents of the fixed area with the pages its table\nentries name (BadSwapAll, which follows). An entry with bank 0 or 1 is skipped; a fixed page\nthat is still free is marked allocated and its entry flagged to be freed later.\nEntry: none.\nExit: AF as AllocBadRAM2 left it: Fc = 0 when all pages were found.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "326": {"comment":"nice? exit"},
        "330": {"synopsis":"swap all memory between swap banks and IY table"},
        "334": {"synopsis":"do until b=0"},
        "336": {"comment":"ld a,bank; cp 1"},
        "339": {"comment":"bank zero? skip"},
        "341": {"comment":"bank 1? skip"},
        "346": {"comment":"part of chain, don't tag"},
        "355": {"synopsis":"swap memory between AHL=MATPtr and page pointed by IY"},
        "358": {"comment":"copy into stack buffer"},
        "366": {"comment":"Fc=0, copy HL -> DE"},
        "367": {"comment":"copy after first page"},
        "370": {"comment":"then copy first over the second"},
        "375": {"comment":"Fc=1, copy DE -> HL"},
        "376": {"comment":"copy second page over the first one"},
        "382": {"comment":"not done? loop"},
        "389": {"synopsis":"Swaps the fixed area of a bad or ugly application back with BC = DE = 0, so no page is\nfreed; falls into BadSwapAndFree.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "394": {"synopsis":"For a bad or ugly application, swaps its fixed area back (BadSwapAll), then frees the swap\npages of the region the application reported as unused: from the page of BC (rounded up) to\nthe page before D. Entries with bank 0 are left; freed entries get bank 0.\nEntry: BC = start, DE = end of the unused region (from the enquiry entry, see\nAppReleaseMem)."},
        "410": {"synopsis":"Entry inside BadSwapAndFree, after the swap: frees the swap pages of the table for the page\nnumbers from E to A - 1 with OS_Mfr, then restores the bindings. Also used by AllocBadRAM2\nto free what it allocated before an allocation failed.\nEntry: A = end page number, E = first page number.\nExit: returns at once when A <= E."},
        "426": {"comment":"ld a,bank; cp 1"},
        "429": {"comment":"bank 0? don't free"},
        "431": {"comment":"bank>1? get page too"},
        "434": {"comment":"bank=1? convert HL into ptr"},
        "440": {"comment":"L=0"},
        "441": {"comment":"Free page AH0"},
        "443": {"synopsis":"Hangs in a loop to itself: OS_Mfr could not give the RAM page the bad-memory handler asked for.","comment":"error? crash"},
        "445": {"comment":"clear bank"},
        "451": {"comment":"not done? loop"},
        "457": {"synopsis":"Fills the bad application's page table (pAppBadMemTable, two bytes per page: page with flag\nbit 7, then bank). For each entry without a bank: if the fixed page is free it is claimed in\nplace (bank 1, page 0), else a page is allocated with OS_Mal and its page and bank are\nrecorded. On an allocation error the pages got so far are freed (bsf_1). Clears the flag bit\nin every entry at the end.\nEntry: ubAppContRAM = number of pages; pAppBadMemHandle = memory pool.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Mal."},
        "470": {"comment":"part of chain? skip"},
        "475": {"comment":"page=0"},
        "477": {"comment":"bank=1"},
        "481": {"comment":"allocate new page"},
        "487": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "489": {"comment":"bank"},
        "494": {"comment":"not zero? skip"},
        "501": {"comment":"below 8KB of bad app RAM"},
        "503": {"comment":"yes? Fc=0 if slot 0 expanded"},
        "507": {"comment":"<8KB or slot 1 expanded"},
        "509": {"comment":"skip b21"},
        "515": {"comment":"remember page"},
        "518": {"comment":"and bank"},
        "524": {"comment":"not done yet? loop"},
        "526": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "540": {"comment":"free all allocated blocks"},
        "544": {"synopsis":"clear all flags in table","comment":"ld b,(ubAppContRAM)"},
        "561": {"synopsis":"E=0 - free each page from table"},
        "575": {"comment":"flag=0? skip"},
        "582": {"comment":"free each page"},
        "589": {"comment":"free page AH0"},
        "591": {"synopsis":"Hangs in a loop to itself: OS_Mfr could not give the RAM page asked for.","comment":"crash"},
        "593": {"comment":"0"},
        "609": {"synopsis":"Copies the 256-byte page at AH0 into the stack temporary buffer (pStkTempStkTop): sets Fc =\n0 and goes into CopyPage, which binds bank A into S1 and copies HL to DE.\nEntry: A = bank; H = page address in S1.\nExit: DE = buffer + 256; BC = $100; L = 0.\nChanges: BC, DE, L, S1 binding."},
        "612": {"synopsis":"Copies the stack temporary buffer (pStkTempStkTop) over the 256-byte page at AH0: sets Fc =\n1 and goes into CopyPage, which binds bank A into S1 and copies DE to HL.\nEntry: A = bank; H = page address in S1.\nExit: DE = buffer + 256; BC = $100; L = 0.\nChanges: BC, DE, L, S1 binding."},
        "617": {"synopsis":"copy 256 bytes\nEntry: A=MS1 bank; Fc=0 - copy HL -> DE; Fc=1 - copy DE -> HL.\nExit: DE advanced by 256 bytes."},
        "627": {"comment":"Fc=1? copy DE->HL"},
        "639": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the running application is bad or ugly: A = ubAppDORFlags AND\n(AT_BAD|AT_UGLY).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fz = 1 for a well-behaved application; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "645": {"synopsis":"Reads the page of the bad memory table entry at IY (flag bit 7 removed), then falls into\nsub_C3F8 to read its bank.\nEntry: IY = table entry.\nExit: H = page; A = bank; Fc = 1 if bank 0, Fz = 1 if bank 1.\nChanges: AF, H.","comment":"page"},
        "650": {"synopsis":"Reads the bank of the bad memory table entry at IY and compares it with 1.\nEntry: IY = table entry.\nExit: A = bank; Fc = 1 if bank 0; Fz = 1 if bank 1.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"bank"},
        "653": {"comment":"Fc=1 if A=0"},
        "656": {"synopsis":"push ix-iy-S1/S2, bind b21 into S2, return with HL=$20","comment":"return address"},
        "661": {"comment":"ld b,(ubSlotRAMoffset)"},
        "665": {"comment":"$21 always?"},
        "666": {"comment":"remember S1/S2 and do MS2BankB"},
        "669": {"comment":"ld b,(ubAppContRAM)"},
        "685": {"synopsis":"undo previous","comment":"return address"},
        "693": {"comment":"return address"},
        "698": {"synopsis":"Loop step of the bad memory table walks: moves IY to the next entry and the page number to\nthe next page. Past page $3F (the b20 swap area) it binds the expansion's first RAM bank\ninto S2, and when that is not slot 1 it jumps from page $40 to $80, skipping b21. The\ncaller's loop keeps BC and the page number on the stack: they are popped here.\nEntry: stack = return address, page number, loop counter (BC).\nExit: HL = next page number; B = counter - 1; Fz = 1 when it reaches zero; IY + 2.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"return address"},
        "699": {"comment":"next entry in table"},
        "703": {"comment":"PageN"},
        "709": {"comment":"still in b20 SWAP area? skip"},
        "714": {"comment":"bind first RAM bank in S2"},
        "719": {"comment":"slot 1"},
        "726": {"comment":"skip b21"},
        "728": {"comment":"decrement page count"},
        "729": {"comment":"return address"},
        "731": {"synopsis":"OS_Out entry: write character to standard output\nEntry: A = character to be written.\nExit: Fc = 0 always (error handler is never provoked).\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "734": {"comment":"write char to screen driver"},
        "740": {"synopsis":"OS_Bout entry: write null-terminated string block at (B)HL to standard output\nEntry: BHL = extended pointer to string to be written (not crossing segments); B = 0, then\nlocal address space pointer in caller bank binding.\nExit: Fc = 0 always (error handler is never provoked); HL points at byte after\nnull-terminator.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "743": {"comment":"write string at (B)HL to screen driver"},
        "749": {"synopsis":"OS_Pout entry: write embedded null-terminated string at caller (PC) following\nthis system call, to standard output.\nEntry: None.\nExit: Fc = 0 always (error handler is never provoked).\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "755": {"comment":"pointer to start of string at OZ call"},
        "761": {"comment":"strip segment mask (if any)"},
        "772": {"comment":"updated OZ caller return address to instruction following the null-terminator"},
        "778": {"synopsis":"OS_Hout entry: write hexadecimal byte to standard output\nEntry: A = byte to be written.\nExit: Fc = 0 always (error handler is never provoked).\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "806": {"synopsis":"Converts a value 0-15 into its upper-case hexadecimal digit.\nEntry: A = value (0-15).\nExit: A = '0'-'9' or 'A'-'F'.\nChanges: AF."},
        "816": {"synopsis":"OsBoutKernel, used only within kernel that has already established the register stack frame"},
        "822": {"comment":"Extended address for OS_Bout?"},
        "824": {"comment":"bind BHL pointer to segment 1 and send string to OS_Out"},
        "829": {"comment":"point at null-terminator"},
        "830": {"comment":"strip segment mask (if any)"},
        "839": {"comment":"return updated HL pointer to caller (points at byte after null-terminator)"},
        "847": {"synopsis":"Writes the null-terminated string at HL, given in the OZ caller's address space, to standard\noutput. Below $8000 it is read with the current bindings; in segment 2 or 3 the caller's\nbank from the OS frame (OSFrame_S2 or OSFrame_S3) is bound into S1 first (bind_strptr).\nEntry: HL = string; IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = byte after the terminator (an S1 address when the bank was rebound).","comment":"bind source bank of HL pointer if inside current kernel bindings"},
        "851": {"comment":"HL pointer might be in segment 2 bank binding before OS_Bout"},
        "858": {"comment":"HL pointer was in segment 3 bank binding before OS_Bout"},
        "861": {"synopsis":"Binds bank B into segment 1 (OSBixS1, HL moved into S1), writes the null-terminated string\nat HL with OSOutString and restores the previous S1 binding (OSBoxS1).\nEntry: B = bank; HL = string.\nExit: HL = byte after the terminator, as an S1 address."},
        "865": {"comment":"call subroutine: write string at HL to screen driver"},
        "872": {"synopsis":"Writes the null-terminated string at HL to standard output a character at a time\n(OsOutKernel: the screen driver, or DC_Out while a CLI is active). The characters are read\nwith PeekHLinc, which takes a pointer crossing from S1 into S2 into the caller's S2 bank.\nEntry: HL = string; IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = byte after the terminator; A = 0; Fz = 1.","comment":"if HL is crossing from S1 to S2, then get char from pointer in bank in (OSFrame_S2)"},
        "876": {"comment":"null-terminator reached, string was sent to screen driver..."},
        "884": {"synopsis":"OsOutKernel, used only within kernel that has already established the register stack frame"},
        "893": {"comment":"Write to CLI"},
        "897": {"synopsis":"quit process (application)","comment":"exit"},
        "901": {"synopsis":"enter an application","comment":"enter"},
        "907": {"comment":"save Fc"},
