        "1394": {"comment":"A=0, Fc=0, Fz=0"},
        "1399": {"comment":"enter thru Os_Ent"},
        "1402": {"synopsis":"Last step before an application is entered or resumed: checks the stack limits, binds the\napplication's banks into S0-S2 (AppBindS012), restores the call level from ubOldCallLevel,\nincrements the resumption cycle (ubAppResCycle), loads SP from pAppStackPtr and jumps to the\nreturn address.\nEntry: return address on the stack.\nExit: SP = pAppStackPtr.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, SP.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "1420": {"comment":"get return address"},
        "1426": {"synopsis":"Binds the running application's S2, S1 and S0 banks from ubAppBindings+2 down to\nubAppBindings, through BindSx; a zero entry leaves that segment as it is.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "1438": {"synopsis":"Binds the bank at (HL) into the segment whose soft copy is at BC, writing the soft copy and\nthe port C (the soft copy's low byte is the port number); a zero bank is skipped. Then steps\nHL and BC back by one (cpd) for the next lower segment.\nEntry: HL = wanted bank; BC = soft copy address (BLSC_SRx).\nExit: HL - 1; BC - 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "1440": {"comment":"0 indicates no bank binding, skip it..."},
        "1448": {"synopsis":"Fc=0 - restore caps flags\nFc=1 - remember caps flags","comment":"kbd_flags"},
        "1451": {"comment":"application kbd cfg"},
        "1457": {"comment":"!! bits match - and 3; or (hl); ld (hl),a"},
        "1465": {"comment":"CAPSE"},
        "1474": {"synopsis":"stack file current process"},
        "1482": {"comment":"Fc=1, remember caps flags"},
        "1494": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "1510": {"synopsis":"Raises the application's environment overhead (uwAppEnvOverhead) to the size of the file IX\nwhen that is larger.\nEntry: IX = environment file handle.\nError: Fc = 1 when GetFileSize fails.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"HL=size"},
        "1513": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1514": {"comment":"store size if larger than previous"},
        "1526": {"synopsis":"exit current application"},
        "1530": {"comment":"remove error handler"},
        "1556": {"synopsis":"Hangs in a loop to itself: DC_Bye does not come back to the process that ended.","comment":"crash if we come back here"},
        "1558": {"synopsis":"Releases memory when the running application is stacked (OS_Stk). A well-behaved application\nonly has its environment file closed (CloseAppEnvHnd). An ugly one releases all its bad\nmemory (AppReleaseAllMem). A bad one is asked through its enquiry entry (entry point + 3, in\nits S3 bank, called with A = RC_Esc): Fc = 0 returns the unused region in BC to DE, which\nBadSwapAndFree frees; Fc = 1 releases everything.\nEntry: none."},
        "1570": {"comment":"call enquiry function"},
        "1585": {"synopsis":"Swaps the bad application's fixed area back without freeing any page (BC = DE = $2000, an\nempty unused region), then closes the environment file (CloseAppEnvHnd).\nEntry: none.","comment":"BC-DE is free, ie. none"},
        "1593": {"synopsis":"Closes the application's environment file handle (pAppEnvHandle) with OS_Cl and falls into\nSetAppEnvHandle, which stores IX as OS_Cl leaves it.\nOZ source name: CloseAppEnvHandle.\nEntry: none."},
        "1600": {"synopsis":"Stores IX as the application's environment file handle (pAppEnvHandle).\nEntry: IX = handle.\nChanges: none."},
        "1605": {"synopsis":"fetch information about process card usage\nEntry: IX=application static handle.\nExit: A=running slot (0-4, 4 = :APP.- device)."},
        "1619": {"comment":"slot number"},
        "1623": {"comment":"slot app"},
        "1630": {"synopsis":"OS_Dor: the DOR (Document Object Record) interface. Builds the OS frame, runs OSDorMain with\nthe reason code in B and leaves through OSFramePop.\nEntry: A = reason code (DR_Get ... DR_Rd2); IX = DOR handle, HL, BC, DE as the reason needs.\nExit: as the reason defines (IX = handle, A = DOR type, BC, records).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Unk for an unknown reason)."},
        "1633": {"comment":"reason code"},
        "1640": {"synopsis":"Dispatches OS_Dor on the reason code in B, with a chain of djnz tests: DR_Get (handle for\nthe name \":\"), DR_Dup, DR_Sib, DR_Son, DR_Fre, DR_Cre, DR_Del, DR_Ins, DR_Rd, DR_Wr and\nDR_Rd2 (handled as DR_Rd).\nEntry: B = reason code; IY = OS frame; IX, HL as the reason needs.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Unk for an unknown reason)."},
        "1642": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=name.\nExit: Fc=0, IX=handle, A=device DOR type; Fc=1, A=error."},
