        "2445": {"comment":"DMDEV/ROM/RAM"},
        "2448": {"synopsis":"Stores the DOR pointer BHL in handle IX, with HL turned into a segment 2 address.\nEntry: IX = handle; BHL = DOR.\nExit: H = H with bit 7 set and bit 6 clear.\nChanges: H.","comment":"S2 fix"},
        "2462": {"synopsis":"Checks that IX is a device-type (HND_DEV) handle with a nonzero DOR bank.\nEntry: IX = handle.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Hand for bank 0).\nChanges: AF."},
        "2479": {"synopsis":"OS_Alm: the alarm manipulation call. Builds the OS frame, sets Fz in it, and calls OSAlmMain\nin kernel bank 1 with interrupts disabled. Then requests an OZ window redraw and leaves\nthrough OSFramePopX.\nEntry: A = reason code (AH_SUSP ... AH_ARES); B and others as the reason needs.\nExit: as OSAlmMain sets the frame."},
        "2489": {"comment":"Fz=1"},
        "2500": {"comment":"request OZ window redraw"},
        "2503": {"comment":"pop OS frame without error"},
        "2506": {"synopsis":"Processes the first alarm in the list (pFirstAlarm): when the bank byte of its handler\n(ahnd_Func+2) is zero it calls GN_Alp with IX = the handler word; otherwise does nothing.\nCalled from the keyboard input loop when an alarm has expired.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, AF', the alternate BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2535": {"comment":"process an expired alarm"},
        "2549": {"synopsis":"Exit: Fc=0, A4=shift lock - if only both shifts (and maybe shift lock) down.","comment":"row7, kbd port"},
        "2554": {"comment":"we rotate shifts to bit0 to use inc near the end"},
        "2555": {"comment":"SQR ESC IDX LCK  .   /   ï¿½  SHR"},
        "2556": {"comment":"row6"},
        "2562": {"comment":"TAB DMN MNU  ,   ;   '  HLP SHL"},
