        "3838": {"synopsis":"move bytes between stream and memory\nEntry: IX,BC,DE,HL.\nExit: BC,DE,HL."},
        "3847": {"synopsis":"OS_Mv body: moves BC bytes between the stream IX and memory. A special handle goes to\nOsMvSpecial. For a file, HL <> 0 writes from HL to the file (DE must be 0, file writable)\nand DE <> 0 reads from the file to DE (HL must be 0, file readable). Puts the updated BC, DE\nand HL into the OS frame; a write error marks the file to be deleted.\nEntry: IX = handle; BC = count; caller's DE and HL from the OS frame.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Bad, RC_Wp, RC_Rp, RC_Hand)."},
        "3864": {"comment":"update BC and DE too"},
