        "3959": {"comment":"return byte"},
        "3965": {"synopsis":"OS_Gb/OS_Gbt body: gets a byte from handle IX. Special handles: 5 reads the serial port\n(OSSiGbt), 1 the keyboard buffer, 4 (NUL) gives RC_Eof, 6 (standard input) goes to OSTin, 2,\n3, 7 and 8 give RC_Rp, others RC_Hand. A file handle must be readable (RdFileByte).\nEntry: IX = handle; BC = timeout (-1 = none).\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Rp, RC_Eof, RC_Hand, RC_Time).","comment":"examine if handle in IX < 9, returns E = low byte of IX handle"},
        "3968": {"comment":"handle was not special. Examine file handle, then process byte through file handle"},
        "3970": {"comment":"get byte from special process handle..."},
        "3973": {"comment":"5 - read byte from serial port"},
        "3977": {"comment":"1 - read keyboard"},
        "3981": {"comment":"2 - read screen. Signal error: Read protected."},
        "3984": {"comment":"3 - read printer direct. Signal error: Read protected."},
        "3990": {"comment":"4 - read NUL. Signal error: EOF"},
        "3997": {"comment":"7 - read stdout. Signal error: Read protected."},
        "4000": {"comment":"8 - read printer filter. Signal error: Read protected."},
        "4002": {"comment":"Signal error: Bad Handle"},
