        "4162": {"synopsis":"OS_Frm body: answers reason B for handle IX. FA_PTR: the file position, or for IX = 0 or -1\nthe number of free handles (high word) and the OZ version (low word). FA_EXT: the file size,\nor the free RAM. FA_EOF: Fz = 1 at end of file, or for IX = 0 or -1 when the machine is\nexpanded. FA_BST: the serial buffer status of handle 5 (OS_Si SI_ENQ) in the frame's HL and\nDE. The 32-bit results go to the caller's DE buffer, or to its DEBC when DE = 0.\nEntry: B = reason code; IX = handle; IY = OS frame.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Unk, RC_Hand, RC_Na).","comment":"!! VerifyFileHandle here, djnz preserves flags"},
        "4170": {"comment":"bad handle? exit"},
