        "4334": {"synopsis":"OS_Fwm body: for file IX, FA_PTR sets the sequential pointer (expanding the file if needed)\nand FA_EXT sets the file size, keeping the position; the 32-bit value is read from HL. A\nwrite error marks the file to be deleted. Handles 0 and -1 return without action.\nEntry: B = reason code; IX = file handle; HL = pointer to the 32-bit value.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Unk for an unknown reason)."},
