        "4744": {"synopsis":"SI_PX (L = $1E), put multiple bytes to serial port, using default timeout (SI_TMO)\n\nFc = 1\nA = RC_TIME, timeout elapsed\nA = RC_EOF, end of file reached\nA = RC_RP, input device is read protected\n\nBC = number of bytes not written\n\n......../IXIY same\nAFBCDEHL/.... different\nEntry: BC = number of byte to write to serial port, maximum 16384, one bank; DE = input; DE\n= 0, input is a file/device opened with its handle in IX; DE > 0, input is memory at (DE);\nIX = file handle (if DE = 0).\nExit: Fc = 0; BC = remaining time (SI_TMO)."},
        "4752": {"comment":"small timer counts default timeout"},
