        "4825": {"comment":"get byte from IX file/device"},
        "4829": {"comment":"write byte to serial port"},
        "4838": {"synopsis":"Part of OS_Si SI_PX: writes the byte in A to the serial port with the default timeout\n(OSSiPbt with BC = -1), using the alternate registers.\nEntry: A = byte.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Time, RC_Esc, RC_Susp).\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "4839": {"comment":"use default timeout"},
        "4842": {"comment":"write byte to serial port"},
        "4846": {"comment":"with or without error"},
        "4847": {"synopsis":"SI_GX (L = $1B), get multiple bytes from serial port, using default timeout (SI_TMO)\n\nFc = 1\nA = RC_TIME, timeout elapsed\nA = RC_EOF, end of file reached\nA = RC_WP, input device is read protected\n\nBC = number of bytes not read\n\n......../IXIY same\nAFBCDEHL/.... different\nEntry: BC = number of byte to get from serial port, maximum 16384, one bank; DE =\ndestination; DE = 0, write bytes to a file opened with its handle in IX; DE > 0, write bytes\nto memory at (DE); IX = file handle (if DE = 0).\nExit: Fc = 0; BC = remaining time (SI_TMO); DE = points at last byte fetched + 1 (if DE(IN)\n> 0)."},
        "4855": {"comment":"small timer counts default timeout"},
        "4864": {"comment":"reset timeout flag"},
        "4880": {"comment":"get original s3 bank"},
        "4884": {"comment":"preserve b"},
        "4885": {"comment":"(sp+3) = BLSC_SR3"},
        "4886": {"comment":"hl = start"},
        "4887": {"comment":"bind BHL in S1"},
        "4893": {"comment":"push S1 for OSBoxS1"},
        "4898": {"comment":"read byte from serial port"},
        "4908": {"comment":"pv flag, reset if bc=0"},
        "4914": {"comment":"time remaining"},
        "4918": {"comment":"DE points at last byte fetched + 1"},
        "4919": {"comment":"Fc = 0 (from ld a,b + or c)"},
        "4924": {"comment":"read byte from serial port"},
        "4928": {"comment":"preserve bc"},
        "4929": {"comment":"use same timeout"},
        "4933": {"comment":"put byte to IX file/device"},
        "4943": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte from the serial port with the default timeout (OSSiGbt with BC = uwSerTimeout),\nusing the alternate registers. Used by SI_GX and SI_GXT.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Time, ...).\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "4944": {"comment":"use default timeout"},
        "4948": {"comment":"read byte from serial port"},
        "4952": {"comment":"with or without error"},
        "4953": {"synopsis":"SI_GXT (L = $21), get multiple bytes until ESC <x> terminator, using default timeout (SI_TMO)\n\nOut if call succeeded, Fc = 0:\nFz = 1,\nBC <> 0, A = ESC terminator encountered, number of bytes not read\nFz = 0,\nA = FFh\nBC = 0, all bytes read, no terminator encountered\nDE = points at last byte fetched + 1 (if DE(in) > 0)\n\nOut if call failed, Fc = 1:\nA = RC_TIME, timeout elapsed\nA = RC_EOF, end of file reached\nA = RC_WP, input device is read protected\n\nBC = number of bytes not read\n\n......../IX.. same\nAFBCDEHL/..IY different\nEntry: BC = number of byte to get from serial port, maximum 16384, one bank; DE =\ndestination; DE = 0, write bytes to a file opened with its handle in IX; DE > 0, write bytes\nto memory at (DE); IX = file handle (if DE = 0)."},
        "4961": {"comment":"small timer counts default timeout"},
        "4970": {"comment":"reset timeout flag"},
        "4986": {"comment":"get original s3 bank"},
        "4990": {"comment":"preserve b"},
        "4991": {"comment":"(sp+3) = BLSC_SR3"},
        "4992": {"comment":"hl = start"},
        "4993": {"comment":"bind BHL in S1"},
        "4999": {"comment":"push S1 for OSBoxS1"},
        "5004": {"comment":"read byte(s) from serial port"},
        "5007": {"comment":"serial port error, probably timeout"},
        "5009": {"comment":"ESC terminator encountered"},
        "5019": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, indicate buffer full"},
        "5025": {"comment":"DE points at end of buffer + 1"},
        "5027": {"comment":"read byte from serial port"},
        "5030": {"comment":"serial port error, probably timeout"},
        "5031": {"comment":"ESC terminator encountered"},
        "5033": {"comment":"preserve bc"},
        "5034": {"comment":"use same timeout"},
        "5038": {"comment":"put byte to IX file/device (this is a slow operation..)"},
        "5041": {"comment":"file I/O error..."},
        "5048": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, indicate buffer full"},
        "5051": {"synopsis":"Part of OS_Si SI_GXT: reads a byte from the serial port and decodes Escape sequences: ESC\n'B' followed by two hexadecimal digits gives that byte value; ESC followed by any other\ncharacter is a terminator.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 0, E = byte, A = $FF; or Fc = 0, Fz = 1, A = character after ESC.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, E.","comment":"read byte(s) + ESC handling, from serial port, in (iy+0)"},
        "5059": {"comment":"read byte from serial port"},
        "5068": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 1 (indicate ESC x terminator encountered)"},
        "5069": {"comment":"read first 4bit hex nibble from serial port"},
        "5073": {"comment":"convert Ascii hex nibble into integer"},
        "5079": {"comment":"first hex nibble * 16"},
        "5084": {"comment":"serial port error or timeout"},
        "5085": {"comment":"calculate second 4 bit nibble"},
        "5088": {"comment":"'binary' byte received."},
        "5090": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, indicate byte received (not ESC terminator)"},
        "5093": {"synopsis":"Converts an ASCII hexadecimal digit into its value: '0'-'9' give 0-9, anything from ':'\nupwards has $37 subtracted, so 'A'-'F' give 10-15 (lower case is not handled).\nEntry: A = digit.\nExit: A = value.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"digit >= \"a\"?"},
        "5095": {"comment":"digit is in interval \"a\" - \"f\""},
        "5097": {"comment":"digit is in interval \"0\" - \"9\""},
        "5103": {"synopsis":"OS_Ht: hardware time manipulation (internal two-byte call $F206). HT_RES waits until the\nTIM0 tick counter reads zero and pulses BM_COMRESTIM to reset the hardware timer. HT_RD\ncopies TIM0-TIM4 (TIM0 in 1/100 s) to the caller's 5-byte buffer at HL. HT_MDT returns BHL =\nthe month/date/time block (uwSysDateLow in bank $20).\nEntry: A = reason code (HT_RES, HT_RD, HT_MDT); HL = buffer for HT_RD; IY = OS frame.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Unk."},
        "5106": {"synopsis":"HT_RES, reset hardware timer\nChanges: AF.","comment":"wait until TIM0=0"},
        "5108": {"comment":"in seconds"},
        "5113": {"comment":"reset timer"},
        "5127": {"comment":"copy hardware clock to stack buffer"},
        "5130": {"comment":"b = 0 from djnz"},
        "5136": {"comment":"copy into caller buffer"},
        "5150": {"comment":"purge stack"},
        "5172": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=buffer[5].\nExit: TIM0-4 are written to (HL),.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"5 loops to read TIM0-4"},
        "5175": {"comment":"check for same value"},
        "5178": {"comment":"get TIMx"},
        "5184": {"comment":"mark as different"},
        "5185": {"comment":"inc pointer"},
        "5186": {"comment":"inc port"},
        "5191": {"comment":"loop until changed"},
        "5194": {"comment":"TIM0 at (HL) in seconds"},
        "5199": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=TICK value.\nExit: A=0.01 sec value.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"-128"},
        "5201": {"comment":"no underflow, skip"},
        "5204": {"comment":"make positive"},
        "5206": {"comment":"/2 to make it 0.01s clock"},
        "5209": {"synopsis":"update small timer\n\nold timer(BC)=new timer(BC)\nFz according to old time, A=RC_Time if Fz=1"},
        "5215": {"comment":"small  timer"},
        "5219": {"comment":"reset"},
        "5227": {"comment":"set new time"},
        "5231": {"comment":"restore old value"},
        "5240": {"comment":"Timeout"},
        "5244": {"comment":"Fz=1"},
        "5251": {"synopsis":"Builds the OS frame for a one-byte OZ call handler: takes the handler's return address and\nthe caller's S2/S3 bindings off the stack, binds kernel bank 1 into segment 2 and falls into\nOSFramePushMain.\nEntry: stack = return address, then the S2/S3 bindings and the caller's PC (as CallOZMain\nleaves them); caller's BC, DE, HL in the alternate set and AF in AF'; DE = OZ call word.\nExit: the caller's registers; IY = OS frame; frame's F = 0.\nChanges: AF', IY and the alternate BC, DE, HL.","comment":"caller PC"},
        "5252": {"comment":"S2/S3"},
        "5253": {"comment":"bind in more kernel code"},
        "5256": {"synopsis":"Pushes the OS frame (see OSFrame_* in oz.def): the S2/S3 bindings, HL, DE, BC and AF of the\ncaller, the OZ call word, the bindings again and IY; points IY at it, clears the frame's F,\nand returns to HL with the caller's registers.\nEntry: HL = return address; BC = S2/S3 bindings; DE = OZ call word; caller's BC, DE, HL in\nthe alternate set and AF in AF'.\nExit: the caller's registers; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: AF', IY and the alternate BC, DE, HL.","comment":"0E - S2S3"},
        "5258": {"comment":"0C - HL"},
        "5259": {"comment":"0A - DE"},
        "5260": {"comment":"08 - BC"},
        "5262": {"comment":"06 - AF"},
        "5264": {"comment":"04 - OZCall"},
        "5265": {"comment":"02 - S2S3"},
        "5266": {"comment":"00 - IY"},
        "5274": {"comment":"clear flags"},
        "5278": {"comment":"RET caller"},
        "5279": {"comment":"use caller registers"},
        "5281": {"comment":"00 - IY"},
        "5283": {"comment":"save return value"},
        "5284": {"comment":"02 - S2S3"},
        "5286": {"comment":"bind out other half of kernel"},
        "5289": {"comment":"back to return value"},
        "5290": {"comment":"04 - OZCall"},
        "5291": {"comment":"06 - AF"},
        "5292": {"comment":"restore BC-HL"},
        "5294": {"synopsis":"Removes the OS frame and returns to the OZ caller. With Fc = 1, A and F are returned as\ngiven (the error); with Fc = 0 it goes into OSFramePopX and the frame's AF is returned.\nEntry: IY = OS frame (at SP); Fc = 1, A = error code, or Fc = 0.\nExit: through OZCallReturn1: BC, DE, HL from the frame, IY and the S2 and S3 bindings\nrestored."},
        "5296": {"synopsis":"Removes the OS frame without an error: restores IY and the S2 binding, returns the frame's\nAF, BC, DE and HL, and leaves through OZCallReturn1, which restores S3 and decrements the\ncall level.\nEntry: IY = OS frame (at SP).\nExit: AF, BC, DE, HL from the frame.","comment":"00 - IY"},
        "5298": {"comment":"02 - S2S3"},
        "5300": {"comment":"bind out other half of kernel"},
        "5303": {"comment":"04 - OZCall"},
        "5304": {"comment":"06 - AF"},
        "5305": {"comment":"08 - BC"},
        "5306": {"comment":"0A - DE"},
        "5307": {"comment":"0C - HL"},
        "5308": {"comment":"restore S2S3 and return"},
        "5311": {"synopsis":"Reads the OZ caller's BC from the OS frame.\nEntry: IY = OS frame.\nExit: BC = caller's BC.\nChanges: BC."},
        "5318": {"synopsis":"Reads the OZ caller's DE from the OS frame.\nEntry: IY = OS frame.\nExit: DE = caller's DE.\nChanges: DE."},
        "5325": {"synopsis":"Reads the OZ caller's HL from the OS frame.\nEntry: IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = caller's HL.\nChanges: HL."},
        "5332": {"synopsis":"Stores BC in the OS frame as the value the OZ caller gets back.\nEntry: IY = OS frame; BC = value.\nChanges: none."},
        "5339": {"synopsis":"Stores C in the OS frame and falls into PutOSFrame_DE: the caller gets CDE back.\nEntry: IY = OS frame; CDE = value.\nChanges: none."},
        "5342": {"synopsis":"Stores DE in the OS frame as the value the OZ caller gets back.\nEntry: IY = OS frame; DE = value.\nChanges: none."},
        "5349": {"synopsis":"Stores B in the OS frame and falls into PutOSFrame_HL: the caller gets BHL back.\nEntry: IY = OS frame; BHL = value.\nChanges: none."},
        "5352": {"synopsis":"Stores HL in the OS frame as the value the OZ caller gets back.\nEntry: IY = OS frame; HL = value.\nChanges: none."},
        "5359": {"synopsis":"restore bindings after OS_Bix"},
        "5366": {"synopsis":"bind in extended address"},
        "5367": {"comment":"remember S2S1 in de'"},
        "5374": {"comment":"bind in BHL"},
        "5384": {"comment":"not kernel space, no bankswitching"},
        "5388": {"comment":"HL in S2 - S1=caller S2, S2=caller S3"},
        "5390": {"comment":"S1=caller S3"},
        "5391": {"comment":"S2=caller S2"},
        "5394": {"comment":"S1=B"},
        "5395": {"comment":"S2=B+1"},
        "5396": {"comment":"store pointers"},
        "5401": {"comment":"HL=local"},
        "5403": {"comment":"S1 fix"},
        "5421": {"synopsis":"OSBixS1 Replacement of OSBix for the kernel\ncan be called from S2 and faster\n\n....D.H./....  different\nEntry: BHL.\nExit: D previous S1 binding, H is fixed to S1.","comment":"S1 fix"},
        "5423": {"comment":"could handle b=0 local by inc b, dec b, ret z"},
        "5429": {"comment":"previous S1 binding in D"},
        "5436": {"synopsis":"OSBoxS1 Replacement of OSBox for the kernel\ncan be called from S2 and faster\n\n......../....  different\nEntry: D previous binding returned by OSBixS1.\nExit: -."},
        "5438": {"comment":"restore previous binding"},
        "5446": {"synopsis":"Binds bank C into segment 1 and bank B into segment 2, updating both soft copies (BLSC_SR1,\nBLSC_SR2) and the ports.\nEntry: C = S1 bank; B = S2 bank.\nChanges: A."},
        "5457": {"synopsis":"Binds bank B into segment 1: copies B into A and falls into MS1BankA.\nEntry: B = bank.\nExit: A = B; bank B bound in S1 and recorded in BLSC_SR1.\nChanges: A."},
        "5458": {"synopsis":"Binds bank A into segment 1: records it in the soft copy BLSC_SR1 and writes it to the\nBL_SR1 port.\nEntry: A = bank.\nExit: bank A bound in S1 and recorded in BLSC_SR1.\nChanges: none."},
        "5464": {"synopsis":"translate file pointer into memory pointer, bind memory in\nOZ source name: FPtr2MemPtrBindS2."},
        "5467": {"synopsis":"Binds bank B into segment 2: copies B into A and jumps to MS2BankA.\nEntry: B = bank.\nExit: A = B; bank B bound in S2 and recorded in BLSC_SR2.\nChanges: A."},
        "5470": {"synopsis":"call VerifySlotType(), then restore b07 into S2\n!! all calls come from b07 in S2 - move code in b00 to avoid this"},
        "5473": {"synopsis":"bind in other half of kernel"},
        "5475": {"synopsis":"Binds bank A into segment 2: records it in the soft copy BLSC_SR2 and writes it to the\nBL_SR2 port. MS2BankK1 falls into it with the other half of the kernel (KN1_BNK).\nEntry: A = bank.\nExit: bank A bound in S2 and recorded in BLSC_SR2.\nChanges: none."},
        "5481": {"synopsis":"allocate tri-handle\nEntry: A=subtype, B=func bank, H=func page, L=func segment.\nExit: Fc=0, IX=handle; Fc=1, A=error.\nChanges: AF, IX."},
        "5487": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "5501": {"synopsis":"free tri-handle\nEntry: IX=handle, A=type.\nExit: Fc=0; Fc=1, A=error.","comment":"verify"},
        "5504": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "5505": {"comment":"go free it"},
        "5507": {"synopsis":"verify tri-handle\nEntry: IX=handle, A=type.\nExit: Fc=0, B=bank, H=page, L=segment; Fc=1, A=error."},
        "5513": {"comment":"type mismatch? exit"},
        "5519": {"comment":"bad handle? exit"},
        "5520": {"comment":"return BHL"},
        "5532": {"synopsis":"Builds the free list of the handle table at reset: walks the NUMHANDLES (96) entries from\nHandles, marks each free (type and dynamic ID zero) and links it to the previous one, so\npFirstHandle ends on the last entry.\nEntry: none.\nExit: every handle free and chained through hnd_Next from pFirstHandle.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, IX.","comment":"handles in $0500-$0bff"},
        "5536": {"comment":"96 handles (6 pages of 16 handles)"},
        "5538": {"comment":"get previous handle  !! use registers inside loop"},
        "5542": {"comment":"link this to prev"},
        "5549": {"comment":"mark as free"},
        "5555": {"comment":"make this previous"},
        "5559": {"comment":"advance to next and loop if handles left"},
        "5567": {"synopsis":"Entry: IX=handle, A=type.\nExit: Fc=0, IX=0; Fc=1, A=error."},
        "5571": {"comment":"type mismatch? exit"},
        "5573": {"comment":"verify low 4 bits - always zero"},
        "5582": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "5593": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=type.\nExit: Fc=0, IX=handle; Fc=1, A=error.\nChanges: AF, IX."},
        "5595": {"comment":"!! should verify it's non-zero"},
        "5596": {"comment":"first handle  !! ld hl, Firsthandle to optimize jump"},
        "5608": {"comment":"no more handles? exit"},
        "5610": {"comment":"!! do this before branch to remove ld ix,0"},
        "5617": {"comment":"found free? init and return"},
        "5619": {"comment":"check next"},
        "5627": {"comment":"clear all fields"},
        "5630": {"comment":"set type and DynID"},
        "5642": {"synopsis":"clear handle except link\nEntry: IX=HANDLE."},
        "5645": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=HANDLE."},
        "5646": {"comment":"skip link, clear rest of handle"},
        "5651": {"comment":"Fc=0, but A unchanged"},
        "5658": {"synopsis":"Entry: IX=handle, if 0 then start from beginning; B=type, C=DynID to match - if 0 then it's\nnot checked.\nExit: IX=handle, DE incremented for each free handle."},
        "5659": {"comment":"if IX=0 start from first"},
        "5674": {"comment":"no more handles? EOF"},
        "5683": {"comment":"free? inc DE and skip"},
        "5685": {"comment":"compare B to type if not zero"},
        "5695": {"comment":"compare C to DynID if not zero"},
        "5705": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "5708": {"comment":"increment free count"},
        "5709": {"comment":"jump to next handle"},
        "5717": {"synopsis":"Entry: IX=handle, A=old type, B=new type.\nExit: Fc=0 if ok; Fc=1, A=error."},
        "5720": {"comment":"bad handle? exit"},
        "5725": {"synopsis":"verify handle\nEntry: IX=handle, A=type.\nExit: Fc=0, handle ok; Fc=1, A=error Fz=1 if special (<256) handle."},
        "5732": {"comment":"handle <256? error Fz=1"},
        "5737": {"comment":"type ok? return Fc=0"},
        "5742": {"synopsis":"miscellaneous OS functions\nEntry: A=reason."},
        "5751": {"synopsis":"check A for alphanum status\n'0'-'9': a=val(A); Fz=1; Fc=1\n'A'-'Z': a=A; Fz=0; Fc=0\n'a'-'z': a=A; A=upper(A); Fz=0; Fc=0\nelse   : a=A; Fz=0; Fc=1","comment":"a'=A"},
        "5756": {"comment":"Fc=1 Fz=0"},
        "5761": {"comment":"a'=val(A)"},
        "5766": {"comment":"Fc=1 Fz=1"},
        "5769": {"comment":"Fc=1 Fz=0"},
        "5776": {"comment":"Fc=1 Fz=0"},
        "5784": {"comment":"Fc=1 Fz=0"},
        "5785": {"comment":"upper(), Fc=0, Fz=0"},
        "5788": {"synopsis":"clear A bytes at HL\nChanges: AF."},
        "5789": {"comment":"no bytes to clear? exit"},
        "5792": {"comment":"HL<256? exit"},
        "5806": {"synopsis":"copy C bytes from DE to HL","comment":"local ptr"},
        "5809": {"synopsis":"copy C bytes FROM HL to BDE"},
        "5810": {"synopsis":"copy C bytes from DE to BHL"},
        "5812": {"comment":"no bytes to copy? exit"},
        "5824": {"synopsis":"copy C bytes from HL to DE","comment":"local ptr"},
        "5826": {"synopsis":"copy C bytes from BHL to DE"},
        "5828": {"comment":"no bytes to copy? exit"},
        "5840": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte at HL in the caller's address space with PeekHL, then increments HL.\nEntry: HL = address (IY = OS frame when HL >= $8000).\nExit: A = byte; HL = HL + 1.\nChanges: AF, HL, AF'."},
        "5845": {"synopsis":"Increments HL, then reads the byte there with PeekHL. Nothing in the source calls it.\nEntry: HL = address - 1 (IY = OS frame when the address is >= $8000).\nExit: A = byte; HL = HL + 1.\nChanges: AF, HL, AF'."},
        "5848": {"synopsis":"Reads the byte at BHL. With B = 0 the address is local and falls into PeekHL; otherwise bank\nB is bound into S1 for the read (HL masked into S1) and the previous S1 binding is put back.\nEntry: B = bank (0 = local pointer); HL = address.\nExit: A = byte; BHL unchanged.\nChanges: AF, AF'."},
        "5852": {"synopsis":"Reads the byte at the local address HL as the caller sees it. Below $8000 it reads directly.\nAt $8000 and above, where the kernel is bound, it binds the caller's S2 or S3 bank\n(OSFrame_S2/OSFrame_S3, chosen by A14) into S1, reads through the S1 window and restores S1.\nEntry: HL = address; IY = OS frame.\nExit: A = byte; HL unchanged.\nChanges: AF, AF' (only when HL >= $8000).","comment":"read byter, hoping it's valid"},
        "5855": {"comment":"not kernel, done"},
        "5856": {"comment":"remember S1"},
        "5860": {"comment":"select caller S2/S3based on A14"},
        "5870": {"comment":"bind in S1  !! could use S2 to avoid 'res7,h'"},
        "5873": {"comment":"!! another option is to use code at peek_2"},
        "5876": {"comment":"S1 fix"},
        "5880": {"comment":"peek"},
        "5881": {"comment":"restore HL"},
        "5882": {"comment":"restore S1"},
        "5888": {"comment":"return byte"},
        "5890": {"comment":"remember S1"},
        "5915": {"synopsis":"Reads the byte at BHL with PeekBHL, then falls into IncBHL to advance the pointer. For an\nextended pointer (B <> 0) a carry out of the 16K segment keeps A14-A15 of H and increments\nthe bank instead.\nEntry: BHL = address (B = 0 for a local pointer).\nExit: A = byte; BHL = next address.\nChanges: AF, B, HL, AF'."},
        "5918": {"synopsis":"increment BHL, handle bank change\nChanges: F, B, HL, AF'."},
        "5919": {"comment":"remember original A14-A15"},
        "5923": {"comment":"local pointer, no bank bump"},
        "5925": {"comment":"get changed bits in A14-A15"},
        "5928": {"comment":"no segment change, exit"},
        "5930": {"comment":"change A14-A15 back"},
        "5935": {"synopsis":"Writes A at BHL with PokeBHL, then jumps to IncBHL to advance the pointer, moving to the\nnext bank when an extended pointer crosses the end of its segment.\nEntry: A = byte; BHL = address (B = 0 for a local pointer).\nExit: A unchanged; BHL = next address.\nChanges: F, B, HL, AF'."},
        "5941": {"synopsis":"Writes A at the local address HL with PokeHL, then increments HL.\nEntry: A = byte; HL = address (IY = OS frame when HL >= $8000).\nExit: A unchanged; HL = HL + 1; B = 0.\nChanges: F, B, HL, AF'."},
        "5946": {"synopsis":"Writes A at the local address HL as the caller sees it: sets B = 0, steps HL back and\nforward again through IncBHL (no net change) and falls into PokeBHL, which writes at $8000\nand above through the caller's S2 or S3 bank bound into S1.\nEntry: A = byte; HL = address; IY = OS frame when HL >= $8000.\nExit: A and HL unchanged; B = 0.\nChanges: F, B, AF'.","comment":"local ptr"},
        "5948": {"comment":"!! these two (dec; call) unnecessary"},
        "5949": {"comment":"!! most likely for unused PokeIncBHL"},
        "5952": {"synopsis":"Changes: F, AF'."},
        "5954": {"comment":"far"},
        "5958": {"comment":"not kernel, just poke"},
        "5961": {"comment":"remember S1"},
        "5965": {"comment":"select caller S2/S3 based on A14"},
        "5975": {"comment":"bind in S1  !! could use S2 to avoid 'res7,h'"},
        "5978": {"comment":"!! another option is to use code at poke_2"},
        "5981": {"comment":"S1 fix"},
        "5986": {"comment":"poke"},
        "5988": {"comment":"restore HL"},
        "5989": {"comment":"restore S1"},
        "5995": {"comment":"return original byte"},
        "6000": {"comment":"remember S1"},
        "6005": {"comment":"bind it in"},
        "6027": {"synopsis":"fix caller address HL into BHL\nChanges: AF, B, H."},
        "6029": {"comment":"kernel space"},
        "6031": {"comment":"prepare for S1"},
        "6036": {"comment":"was S1? easy"},
        "6038": {"comment":"prepare for S0 $0000-$1fff"},
        "6042": {"comment":"<$2000? done"},
        "6044": {"comment":"prepare for S0 odd bank"},
        "6053": {"comment":"S0 even bank"},
        "6057": {"comment":"get correct bank"},
        "6067": {"comment":"S0 fix"},
        "6071": {"comment":"set bank"},
        "6073": {"synopsis":"Minute interrupt service\nEntry: -.\nExit: -.\nChanges: E, IX, IY.","comment":"ack MIN"},
        "6085": {"comment":"already shutting down? exit"},
        "6090": {"comment":"negative? restore - no timeout"},
        "6094": {"comment":"request shutdown"},
        "6102": {"synopsis":"Minute part of the RTC service, called by Int_RTCM after the acknowledge: reads the clock\nwith ReadHWClock and, when an alarm is pending, counts the 24-bit minute counter at\nuwNextAlmMinutes up towards zero. When it reaches zero and the seconds counter\nubNextAlmSeconds is zero too, it goes to ProcessAlm to activate the alarm.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "6105": {"comment":"no alarms? exit"},
        "6114": {"comment":"no next alarm"},
        "6115": {"comment":"otherwise 24bit increment"},
        "6133": {"synopsis":"Second interrupt service\nEntry: -.\nExit: -.\nChanges: E, IX, IY.","comment":"ack SEC"},
        "6137": {"synopsis":"Entry inside Int_RTCS after the second-tick acknowledge, the second part of the RTC service:\nreads the clock with ReadHWClock and, when an alarm is pending and no minutes are left,\ncounts ubNextAlmSeconds up towards zero. At zero (or when it already was zero) it falls into\nProcessAlm, which clears IST_B_ALARM, sets AHNF_B_ACTIVE in the next alarm's handle and\nfalls into IncActiveAlm.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "6140": {"comment":"no alarms? exit"},
        "6145": {"comment":"ubNextAlmMinutes+1"},
        "6147": {"comment":"ubNextAlmMinutes"},
        "6149": {"comment":"still minutes to go"},
        "6151": {"comment":"ubNextAlmSeconds"},
        "6153": {"comment":"do alarm if 0 or -1 seconds left"},
        "6162": {"comment":"ld  ix, (pNextAlmHandle)"},
        "6169": {"comment":"set AHNF_B_ACTIVE, (ix+ahnd_Flags)"},
        "6175": {"synopsis":"Counts one more active alarm in ubNumActiveAlm and jumps to MaySetPendAlmTsk to update the\nalarm task request.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "6181": {"synopsis":"Counts one active alarm less in ubNumActiveAlm and falls into MaySetPendAlmTsk to update the\nalarm task request.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "6185": {"synopsis":"Updates the alarm task request in ubIntTaskToDo. When alarms are enabled (ubAlmDisableCnt =\n0) and at least one is active (ubNumActiveAlm), it sets ITSK_B_ALARM and, if\nITSK_B_PREEMPTION is set, locks the keyboard (KBF_B_LOCKED in KbdData); otherwise it clears\nITSK_B_ALARM.\nOZ source name: MaySetPendingAlmTask.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "6192": {"comment":"disabled? remove alarm task"},
        "6198": {"comment":"none active? remove alarm task"},
        "6204": {"comment":"no wake up? ret"},
        "6205": {"comment":"else lockout"},
        "6214": {"synopsis":"Reads the hardware clock (TIM0-TIM4, through ReadRTC) into time buffer A (ubTIM0_A) when bit\n0 of ubTimeBufferSelect is 1, otherwise into buffer B (ubTIM0_B), then flips the selector,\nsets IST_B_ALMTIMEOK in ubIntStatus and tests IST_B_ALARM.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fz = 0 when an alarm is pending, Fz = 1 when none; HL = ubIntStatus.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"read hardware clock to either buffer A or B"},
        "6217": {"comment":"bit 0 selects buffer"},
        "6223": {"comment":"(&255)  ; buffer B"},
        "6232": {"comment":"alternate timer set changing bit 0"},
        "6238": {"comment":"return alarms status"},
