        "6691": {"comment":"internal keycode"},
        "6695": {"comment":"key canceled"},
        "6696": {"synopsis":"Puts a keycode into the keyboard buffer; GetKey falls into it. ESC sets the escape flag\nthrough MaySetEsc when enabled, then DeadKeys may swallow or translate the key. Otherwise it\nsets KBF_B_KEY, writes the key at ubKbBufWrPos in the 32-byte circular buffer, advances the\nwrite position and sets ITSK_B_BUFFER. A full buffer loses the key. Runs inside the\ninterrupt, so it does not disable interrupts.\nEntry: A = keycode; IX = KbdData.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the key was swallowed by DeadKeys.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "6698": {"comment":"set ESC flag if enabled"},
        "6704": {"comment":"exit if key swallowed"},
        "6709": {"comment":"preserve key to be written in buffer"},
        "6718": {"comment":"32 bytes circular buffer"},
        "6720": {"comment":"apply address mask"},
        "6723": {"comment":"buffer is full, key is lost"},
        "6724": {"comment":"update WrPos"},
        "6727": {"comment":"previous WrPos before increment"},
        "6730": {"comment":"write byte in buffer"},
        "6734": {"comment":"buffer task performed"},
        "6737": {"synopsis":"Handles the special keys and qualifiers for a key from the matrix:\n1. CAPS LOCK: disables repeat and toggles caps lock; with <> it forces CAPS, with [] it\nforces caps; redraws the OZ window (DrawOZwd) and returns through SetKeyDown (swallowed).\n2. ESC: disables repeat. With SHIFT or <> while a CLI is active it records the qualifier\n(CLISHIFT/CLIDMND bits of ubIntStatus), asks for an OZ window update and swallows the key;\nwith SHIFT or <> and no CLI it swallows the key; plain ESC goes to ApplyQualToESC.\n3. Any other key goes to ApplyQualToA for the qualifier translations.\nEntry: A = internal keycode; D = qualifiers (QB_SHIFT, QB_DIAMOND, QB_SQUARE); IX = KbdData.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = keycode to store.\nError: Fc = 1 when the key is to be ignored.","comment":"process caps lock"},
        "6741": {"comment":"disable repeat"},
        "6752": {"comment":"force CAPS"},
        "6758": {"comment":"force caps"},
        "6762": {"comment":"toggle enable"},
        "6772": {"comment":"ESC signal, is it SHIFT(CLI) or <>(CLI) ?"},
        "6774": {"comment":"all other key go there"},
        "6776": {"comment":"disable repeat"},
        "6783": {"comment":"CLI count"},
        "6784": {"comment":"qualifiers"},
        "6789": {"comment":"is CLI active"},
        "6791": {"comment":"CLI byte counter=0"},
        "6793": {"comment":"interrupt status"},
        "6796": {"comment":"low 2 bits match exactly (qualifiers/intstatus)"},
        "6797": {"comment":"set/res bit 0 (CLISHIFT) and 1 (CLIDMND)"},
        "6798": {"comment":"hl = ubIntTaskToDo"},
        "6799": {"comment":"update OZ window"},
        "6801": {"synopsis":"Sets KBF_B_KEY in the keyboard flags (KbdData) to record that a key is down, and returns Fc\n= 1 so a caller can return through it to swallow the key.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "6805": {"comment":"any (not <>/[]) key down"},
        "6810": {"synopsis":"Get the translation table pointer\n\nAF....HL/....\nEntry: A = keymap table ID (matrix, shift, caps, diamond, square).\nExit: HL = keymap table.","comment":"=2"},
        "6814": {"comment":"start of keymap table pointers"},
        "6822": {"synopsis":"KMT_MATRIX (0) -> 00, KMT_SHIFT (1) -> 40"},
        "6830": {"synopsis":"Generic pair-matching routine, ascending order tables\nFaster than CPIR as we skip odd bytes and can exit prematurely\nwithout finding match\n\n..BCDE.. IXIY\nAF....HL ....\nEntry: A=keycode, L=table.\nExit: Fc=0, A=newcode translated; Fc=1, A=in(A) not translated."},
        "6842": {"synopsis":"Looks up a keycode in a translation table of sorted pairs: a length byte, then pairs of\n(key, translated key) in ascending key order. The search stops early at a larger key.\nTranslateTable reaches it after finding the table.\nEntry: A = keycode; HL = table.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = translated key.\nError: Fc = 1, A unchanged when the key is not in the table.\nChanges: F, B, HL.","comment":"table length"},
        "6843": {"comment":"take care of empty table"},
        "6848": {"comment":"entries sorted, shortcut false"},
        "6856": {"comment":"get translated char, exit with Fc=0"},
        "6858": {"synopsis":"Handle qualifier to ESC (from ProcessKey)\nOZ source name: ApplyQualifiersToESC."},
        "6860": {"synopsis":"Handle qualifier translations\nOZ source name: ApplyQualifiersToA.\nExit: Fc=0, A=outchar if no error; Fc=1, ignore key.","comment":"enter/tab/del/menu/index/help or cursor key"},
