        "7373": {"synopsis":"open memory (allocate memory pool)\nEntry: A=flags, C=slot/bank (if MM_B_SLT set in A).\nExit: IX=MemHandle."},
        "7382": {"synopsis":"Body of OS_Mop: opens a memory pool. Allocates a memory handle, stores the flags from the\ncaller's A in mhnd_AllocFlags and, with MM_B_SLT, the slot or bank in C as\nmhnd_ExclusiveBank (not documented). Unless MM_B_MUL is set, SetExclusiveBank then chooses\none bank for the pool.\nEntry: OSFrame_A = flags; C = slot/bank when MM_B_SLT is set.\nExit: Fc = 0, IX = memory handle.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from AllocHandle."},
        "7387": {"comment":"no handle? exit"},
        "7401": {"synopsis":"set ExclusiveBank unless multiple banks required","comment":"use multiple banks"},
        "7406": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "7408": {"synopsis":"close memory (free memory pool)\nEntry: IX=MemHandle.\nExit: Fc=0 if no error."},
        "7417": {"synopsis":"Body of OS_Mcl: closes a memory pool. Verifies the memory handle, then for slots 3 to 0\nbinds the slot's MAT in S2 and frees every page in the handle's allocation chain for that\nslot. The chain's last entry must point back at the handle, otherwise it fails through\nOZwd__fail. Finally it frees the handle.\nEntry: IX = memory handle.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (bad handle)."},
        "7422": {"comment":"bad handle? exit"},
        "7423": {"comment":"do slots 3-0"},
        "7425": {"comment":"decrement slot"},
        "7426": {"comment":"and remember it"},
        "7429": {"comment":"bind slot MAT in S2"},
        "7434": {"comment":"no RAM? skip slot"},
        "7436": {"comment":"get allocation chain for this slot"},
        "7439": {"comment":"no mem from this slot? skip it"},
        "7441": {"synopsis":"free all memory allocated from this slot","comment":"HL=MAT entry"},
        "7442": {"comment":"point HL to allocation MAT entry"},
        "7445": {"comment":"DE=next entry"},
        "7449": {"comment":"remember last_flag"},
        "7452": {"comment":"remove flags"},
        "7455": {"comment":"mark page HL as free"},
        "7458": {"comment":"restore last_flag"},
        "7459": {"comment":"not last? free next"},
        "7461": {"comment":"next*16 should be MemHandle"},
        "7466": {"comment":"does it match?"},
        "7472": {"comment":"nope? fail as we just freed unknown memory"},
        "7475": {"comment":"restore slot"},
        "7476": {"comment":"was not 0? loop"},
        "7483": {"synopsis":"allocate memory\nEntry: A=slot, 1-3; BC=allocation size, max. 256 bytes; IX=MemHandle.\nExit: Fc=0 - BHL=memory, C=segment; Fc=1, A=error if failed."},
        "7486": {"comment":"remember S1"},
        "7495": {"comment":"restore S1"},
        "7504": {"synopsis":"Body of OS_Mal: allocates memory from a pool.\n1. A size above 256 bytes goes to mal_block, which finds and allocates whole pages with\nOS_Fma and OS_Axm.\n2. A size of 256 allocates a whole page with osmal_AllocPage.\n3. A smaller size first looks for a big enough chunk in the split pages already allocated\nfrom slots 3 to 0 (ValidatePage, AllocChunk); failing that it allocates a new page, makes it\none free chunk of 255 bytes at offset 1 and allocates from it. The address is returned for\nthe pool's segment; in segment 0 it is in $2000-$3FFF, and a page from the upper half of a\nbank is returned with the odd bank number. Unless MM_B_MUL is set the bank becomes the\npool's exclusive bank.\nEntry: BC = size; IX = memory handle; IY = OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0; OSFrame BHL = memory; OSFrame_C = segment.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Fail for a bad size, RC_Room)."},
        "7512": {"comment":"more than 1 page requested"},
        "7518": {"comment":"bad size? exit"},
        "7519": {"comment":"size=256? allocate whole page"},
        "7521": {"comment":"slot 3-2-1-0"},
        "7526": {"comment":"bind slot MAT in S2"},
        "7531": {"comment":"no RAM in slot? skip slot"},
        "7533": {"comment":"MATentry in DE"},
        "7536": {"comment":"no allocations from this slot? skip slot"},
        "7538": {"comment":"HL=MatEntry, DE=ptr to it"},
        "7545": {"comment":"dont use 'dec l' it could change Fz, 'dec hl' does not"},
        "7546": {"comment":"non-splitted? skip page"},
        "7548": {"comment":"point HL to this page"},
        "7551": {"comment":"and bind it in"},
        "7557": {"comment":"invalid? crash"},
        "7560": {"comment":"size, possibly fixed in MemCallAttrVerify"},
        "7563": {"comment":"ptr to MATentry"},
        "7564": {"comment":"HL=memory if succesfull"},
        "7569": {"comment":"!! unnecessary"},
        "7578": {"comment":"got chunk"},
        "7580": {"comment":"HL=MATptr"},
        "7581": {"comment":"get pointer to next"},
        "7587": {"comment":"HL=MAToffset(DE)"},
        "7588": {"comment":"remove flags"},
        "7594": {"comment":"not last? try next page"},
        "7596": {"comment":"try previous slot"},
