        "8351": {"synopsis":"Checks the handle for OS_Axp, OS_Axm and OS_Fxm and fits the page address to the pool's\nsegment: puts the segment bits of mhnd_AllocFlags into H. For a segment 0 pool an address in\nthe upper half sets bit 0 of OSFrame_B (odd bank) and H is moved to $2000-$3FFF. Stores the\nresult in OSFrame_H.\nEntry: H = page address high byte; IX = memory handle; IY = OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0; H = OSFrame_H = adjusted page.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from VerifyHandle.","comment":"verify handle type"},
