        "8915": {"comment":"ret with RC_Room and Fc=1"},
        "8916": {"comment":"reload pushframe with original values of HL"},
        "8925": {"synopsis":"Scans one slot for OS_Fma. Turns the slot number into its first bank (slot 0 starts at bank\n$20) in OSFrame_B, binds the slot's MAT in S2 (MS2SlotMAT67) and puts the last bank + 1 in\nOSFrame_C. Then for each bank it counts the free pages at the offset in OSFrame_H (or, with\nFM_B_NOF, finds a run anywhere with fma_nof), honouring FM_B_FIX and FM_B_EVN.\nEntry: A = OS_Fma options with the slot in bits 0-1; OSFrame_H = page offset; OSFrame_L =\npages wanted; IY = OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0, OSFrame_B = bank with room.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Room when no bank has room; Fc = 1 with no error code when the slot\nhas no RAM.","comment":"slot number to mask"},
        "8927": {"comment":"slot mask"},
        "8931": {"comment":"slot 0 begins at bank $20"},
        "8933": {"comment":"set bank to scan in OSFrame_B"},
        "8938": {"comment":"slot a becomes MAT bank bound in s2, bc and iy destroyed"},
        "8941": {"comment":"ubSlotRAMSize 0, 1, 2 or 3 (IY was ubSlotRAMOffset)"},
        "8944": {"comment":"restore pushframe"},
        "8946": {"comment":"no RAM in slot ? skip"},
        "8947": {"comment":"add number of banks in slot + slot offset"},
        "8950": {"comment":"keep last bank+1 in OSFrame_C"},
        "8953": {"comment":"bank to scan"},
        "8956": {"comment":"MAT entry of bank D is in HL"},
        "8959": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "8960": {"comment":"no offset"},
        "8967": {"comment":"try next bank in slot"},
        "8969": {"comment":"now in DE"},
        "8970": {"comment":"page offset"},
        "8973": {"comment":"zero"},
        "8975": {"comment":"1 word per page"},
        "8976": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "8977": {"comment":"HL holds MAT entry"},
        "8978": {"comment":"bank in s2"},
        "8986": {"comment":"add allocation FIX flag if requested"},
        "8990": {"comment":"BC=number of pages to scan"},
        "8997": {"comment":"c' number of free pages"},
        "8999": {"comment":"number of pages wanted = free pages ?"},
        "9005": {"comment":"found, B bank number (OSFrame_B)"},
        "9006": {"comment":"pre-increment bank"},
        "9012": {"comment":"end of slot ?"},
        "9015": {"comment":"loop to next bank"},
        "9017": {"comment":"no free memory area"},
        "9021": {"synopsis":"Accepts a bank for OS_Fma's FM_B_EVN option: without the option it returns Fz = 1; with it,\nFz = 1 only when the bank in OSFrame_B is even.\nEntry: OSFrame_A = options; OSFrame_B = bank.\nExit: Fz = 1 when the bank is accepted."},
        "9026": {"comment":"zero is even Fz=1, odd bank returns Fz=0"},
        "9030": {"comment":"and thus try next bank in slot"},
        "9031": {"synopsis":"For OS_Fma's FM_B_NOF option: finds the first run of OSFrame_L free pages in the bank whose\nMAT starts at HL, skipping swappable pages when FM_B_FIX is asked for. The run's first page\noffset is put in OSFrame_H.\nEntry: HL = bank's first MAT entry; OSFrame_A = options; OSFrame_L = pages wanted.\nExit: Fc = 0, HL = bank's first MAT entry; OSFrame_H = page offset.\nError: Fc = 1 when no run is found.","comment":"store MAT entry of bank in DE"},
        "9033": {"comment":"scan 1 bank (64 pages)"},
        "9040": {"comment":"64->0, 63->1 ... 2->62, 1->63"},
        "9042": {"comment":"set offset (0-63) to be tested"},
        "9045": {"comment":"reload number of pages requested"},
        "9048": {"comment":"next page in MAT"},
        "9050": {"comment":"get page attributes"},
        "9053": {"comment":"want fixed mem?"},
        "9057": {"comment":"no? check this"},
        "9059": {"comment":"verify page is fixed"},
        "9061": {"comment":"no? skip this"},
        "9064": {"comment":"Fz=1 if next=NULL"},
        "9068": {"comment":"in use? retry with next page"},
        "9071": {"comment":"found"},
        "9079": {"comment":"reload HL with MAT entry of bank"},
        "9080": {"comment":"ok, offset is in (iy+OSFrame_H)"},
        "9082": {"synopsis":"Chooses the exclusive bank of a memory pool: the bank with the most unused pages within the\npool's limit in mhnd_ExclusiveBank (0 = any slot, below $20 = a slot, otherwise that bank),\ncounted by FindUnusedBnkAny, FindUnusedBank or CntUnusedPgsBank. The bank is stored in\nmhnd_ExclusiveBank when one with free pages is found.\nEntry: IX = memory handle."},
        "9083": {"comment":"reset max_unused_pages variables"},
        "9087": {"comment":"get slot/bank limit"},
        "9090": {"comment":"memory mask will be used by FindUnusedBank"},
        "9097": {"comment":"any slot"},
        "9102": {"comment":"if it is RAM allocate from single bank"},
        "9106": {"comment":"otherwise allocate from slot D"},
        "9111": {"comment":"just bank D"},
        "9115": {"comment":"bank with most unused pages"},
        "9118": {"comment":"no free pages found? exit"},
        "9123": {"synopsis":"Count unused pages in bank\nOZ source name: CountUnusedPagesInBank.\nEntry: D=bank; E=segment mask (bit 6 & 7) and alloc FIX flags.\nExit: A=c'=unused pages in bank; d'=bank with most (c') pages; Fc=0 if totally free."},
        "9126": {"comment":"no RAM?"},
        "9134": {"comment":"check if bank full"},
        "9136": {"comment":"out of memory? exit"},
        "9138": {"comment":"64 pages, 32 if segment 0"},
        "9146": {"comment":"!! ld c,32"},
        "9149": {"comment":"use upper half of bank if bank LSB=1"},
        "9155": {"comment":"c'=unused_count"},
        "9158": {"comment":"64 pages, 32 if segment 0"},
        "9159": {"comment":"!! push it above, pop here"},
        "9169": {"comment":"all free, Fc=0 - all other returns with Fc=1"},
        "9171": {"comment":"compare with most_free"},
        "9173": {"comment":"smaller or same"},
        "9178": {"comment":"d'=bank, e'=max most_free"},
        "9184": {"comment":"!! just ret"},
        "9187": {"synopsis":"check one slot for completely free bank\nEntry: D=slot; E=segment mask (00: 32 pages, 40/80/C0: 64 pages are searched).\nExit: Fc=0 if empty bank found; c'=max_free, d'=bank."},
        "9189": {"comment":"slot (0-3)"},
        "9193": {"comment":"no RAM? skip  !! ld b/pop iy above to optimize exits"},
        "9195": {"comment":"ubSlotRAMSize 0, 1, 2 or 3 (IY was ubSlotRAMOffset)"},
        "9198": {"comment":"bank of MAT (00-3F) bound in s2, first bank of slot"},
        "9199": {"comment":"remember count"},
        "9200": {"comment":"and bank"},
        "9201": {"comment":"in bank D"},
        "9206": {"comment":"totally empty? exit"},
        "9208": {"comment":"try next bank"},
        "9209": {"comment":"as long as RAM bank left in slot D"},
        "9214": {"synopsis":"try to find totally unused bank in any slot\nOZ source name: FindUnusedBankAnySlot.\nEntry: -.\nExit: 'c incremented for each free page; Fc=0 if completely free bank found.","comment":"!! not necessary, A=0 on entry"},
        "9215": {"comment":"next slot, 1-2-3-0"},
        "9224": {"comment":"got totally free bank? exit"},
        "9227": {"comment":"slots left? loop"},
        "9229": {"comment":"Fc=1, no free bank found"},
        "9231": {"synopsis":"count unused pages in bank\nEntry: BC=number of pages; HL=MATptr of first page.\nExit: c' incremented for each free page."},
        "9232": {"comment":"reset counter in c'"},
        "9238": {"comment":"HL++, BC--"},
        "9240": {"comment":"BC underflow? return"},
        "9241": {"comment":"get page attributes"},
        "9244": {"comment":"want fixed mem?"},
        "9246": {"comment":"no? check this"},
        "9248": {"comment":"verify page is fixed"},
        "9250": {"comment":"no? skip this"},
