        "9259": {"comment":"increment unused_count"},
        "9262": {"comment":"and check next"},
        "9264": {"synopsis":"Verify ROM/EPROMcard\n\n*** IMPORTANT NOTE ***\nThis call must not use any stack related instruction\nIt is also called on boot when there is still no stack set\nEntry: D=slot in low bits; E=bank to test.\nExit: D=card type.","comment":"get last bank in slot"},
        "9268": {"comment":"slot 0 always contains an OZ ROM"},
        "9275": {"comment":"and bind into S2"},
        "9278": {"comment":"WE CANT USE MS2BankA (no stack when called from boot)"},
        "9280": {"comment":"card header tag"},
        "9285": {"comment":"EPROM 'oz' tag"},
        "9291": {"comment":"\"oz\" found"},
        "9293": {"comment":"BU_ROM"},
        "9300": {"comment":"\"OZ\" not found"},
        "9302": {"comment":"verify read"},
        "9309": {"comment":"card size"},
        "9312": {"comment":"handle this case (else is zero)"},
        "9316": {"comment":"a is last unused bank in slot"},
        "9318": {"comment":"bank to test"},
        "9319": {"comment":"size ok? ret"},
        "9320": {"comment":"nothing inthe bank"},
        "9323": {"synopsis":"Return Fc = 1, if less than 128K RAM was found in slot 0, 1 or 2.\nIf expanded RAM was found (>=128K), then return Fc = 0, A = bottom bank of found RAM card.","comment":"check expanded RAM in slot 1 first."},
        "9331": {"comment":"then, for expanded RAM in slot 2"},
        "9339": {"synopsis":"Entry inside Chk128KB, after slots 1 and 2: checks whether slot 0 holds at least 128K of RAM\n(ubSlotRamSize).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = $21; Fc = 0 when slot 0 has 128K or more, Fc = 1 when less.","comment":"finally, check if RAM in slot 0 >= 128K"},
        "9342": {"comment":"(less likely, since it requires hardware modification)"},
        "9347": {"synopsis":"Adds a RAM card inserted in a slot: initialises its RAM with InitSlotRAM, binds the other\nhalf of the kernel in S2 and, for slot 1 or 2, calls ExpandMachine (which expands the\nmachine when the card has 128K or more). Falls into MountAllRAM.\nEntry: A = first bank of the slot ($40, $80 or $C0)."},
        "9358": {"comment":"slot1? expand if 128KB or more"},
        "9364": {"comment":"slot2? expand if 128KB or more"},
        "9367": {"synopsis":"Writes the front DORs of the RAM devices, from RAMDORtable. For each entry it binds the bank\nin S1 and, when the bank has RAM (RAM.- always), copies RAMFrontDOR with the device's\ncharacter to the DOR address. RAM.0-RAM.3 also get the CT_RAM tag at $4000; RAM.- gets\nAPPFrontDOR at $4060. On a soft reset a bank already tagged is left alone.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "9373": {"comment":"21 21 40 80 c0  bank"},
        "9380": {"comment":"address high byte"},
        "9382": {"comment":"80 40 40 40 40  address low byte"},
        "9384": {"comment":"-  0  1  2  3  RAM number"},
        "9391": {"comment":"skip if no RAM"},
        "9405": {"comment":"0 = hard reset"},
        "9409": {"comment":"soft reset & already tagged, skip"},
        "9422": {"comment":"just copy 00 FF"},
        "9427": {"comment":"install APP device and tag RAM if not RAM.-"},
        "9431": {"comment":"tag RAM"},
        "9440": {"comment":"APPFrontDOR at $4060"},
        "9453": {"synopsis":"Table of the RAM devices for MountAllRAM, 3 bytes each, ended by a 0 byte: bank, DOR address\nlow byte (at $40xx in S1) and the device character ('-' for RAM.-, '0' to '3' for\nRAM.0-RAM.3)."},
        "9469": {"synopsis":"Template of a RAM device's front DOR, 19 bytes, copied by MountAllRAM: three 3-byte links\n($FF,0,0 then zeros), type DM_DEV, length 9, DT_NAM key, name length 6, \"RAM.\" (the device\ncharacter is written after it), then the 0 name terminator and the $FF end mark."},
        "9488": {"synopsis":"Template of the APPL device's front DOR, 19 bytes, which MountAllRAM copies to $4060 in the\nRAM.- bank: three empty 3-byte links, type DN_APL, length 8, DT_NAM key, name length 5,\n\"APPL\", 0 and the $FF end mark."},
        "9507": {"synopsis":"Initialize all RAM (called from Reset)"},
