        "10102": {"synopsis":"Get current bank binding in segment\n\nOUT, if call successful:\nFc = 0\nB = bank number currently bound to that segment\nC = C(in)\n\nOUT, if call failed:\nFc = 1\nA = error code:\nRC_ERR ($0F), C was not valid\nEntry: C = memory segment specifier (MS_S0, MS_S1, MS_S2 & MS_S3).\nChanges: AF, B.\nKeeps: C, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "10103": {"comment":"segment"},
        "10104": {"comment":"pop S3 bank into B"},
        "10109": {"comment":"seg 3? we're done"},
        "10111": {"comment":"seg >3? error"},
        "10113": {"comment":"OZ V4.1: get bank binding status in B for C = MS_Sx"},
        "10116": {"comment":"return current bank binding for MS_Sx"},
        "10118": {"synopsis":"Set new bank binding in segment.\n\nOUT, if call successful:\nFc = 0\nB = bank number previously bound to that segment\n\nOUT, if call failed:\nFc = 1\nA = error code:\nRC_Ms ($0F), C was not valid\nEntry: C = memory segment specifier (MS_S0, MS_S1, MS_S2 & MS_S3); B = bank number to bind\ninto this segment ($00 - $FF).\nChanges: AF, B.\nKeeps: C, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "10119": {"comment":"segment"},
        "10122": {"comment":"segment 3? handle separately"},
        "10124": {"comment":"segment >3? error"},
        "10126": {"comment":"OZ V4.1: execute bank binding, B = bank number, C = MS_Sx"},
        "10127": {"comment":"return old bank binding in B"},
        "10129": {"comment":"pop S3 into A"},
        "10130": {"comment":"push new bank"},
        "10131": {"comment":"return old bank in B"},
        "10143": {"synopsis":"select fast code (fast bank switching)\nfor API compatibility (slower than RST 30H)"},
        "10150": {"comment":"reason not 1? exit"},
        "10152": {"comment":"copy pointers from alternate registers"},
        "10153": {"comment":"and translate slot number into blink port"},
        "10159": {"comment":"DE=destination"},
        "10160": {"comment":"IX=DE"},
        "10163": {"comment":"copy 6 bytes"},
        "10166": {"comment":"from here"},
        "10171": {"comment":"set softcopy low byte"},
        "10174": {"comment":"set output port"},
        "10177": {"comment":"point HL to 'ret'"},
        "10179": {"comment":"DE=jump address"},
        "10182": {"comment":"no jump, we're done"},
        "10184": {"comment":"jp opcode"},
        "10190": {"comment":"return code size  !! bug - overrides error code"},
        "10203": {"synopsis":"print MTH string, expand $7f-codes","comment":"if C not xxxxxx00 then try again"},
        "10211": {"comment":"jump to function"},
        "10217": {"synopsis":"Prints the null-terminated string that follows the call, returning past it. A $7F byte\nstarts a code taken from the next byte (case ignored): A prints the active application's\nname, T the active topic, F the active command, C, L, N and R set the justification, D\nresets the screen toggles; $7F $7F prints $7F. Characters go out through OS_Out.\nEntry: string inline after the call.\nChanges: AF; BC, DE and HL when a $7F code runs.","comment":"get char from caller PC"},
        "10222": {"comment":"null? exit"},
        "10225": {"comment":"not 7F, print"},
        "10227": {"comment":"get next byte"},
        "10231": {"comment":"7F, print as is"},
        "10235": {"comment":"upper()"},
        "10240": {"comment":"command table"},
        "10243": {"comment":"!! don't use cpir, use sorted table like in new kbd routines"},
        "10245": {"comment":"found, execute it"},
        "10247": {"comment":"print char and loop back"},
        "10251": {"synopsis":"char, function, pad"},
        "10283": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the address in DE: a call to it calls the routine at DE.\nEntry: DE = routine address."},
        "10285": {"synopsis":"Sets centre justification: sends SOH \"2JC\" through OS_Out.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "10289": {"synopsis":"Sets right justification: sends SOH \"2JR\" through OS_Out.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "10293": {"synopsis":"Sets normal justification: sends SOH \"2JN\" through OS_Out.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "10297": {"synopsis":"Sends the justification sequence SOH \"2J\" followed by the character in A (C, L, N or R)\nthrough OS_Out; the other Justify entries load the character into B and join it.\nEntry: A = justification character.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"A keeps justi char"},
        "10311": {"synopsis":"Draws the help window of the active topic: the heading \"The <application> <topic> topic\",\nthe topic's help text (PrintTopicHelp), and the key hints for the other topics, for going\nback to the application and, when the topic has command help, for its entries. Ends through\nHelp2Wd_bottom.\nEntry: none.\nError: Fc = 1 when input is pending (from InitHelpWd or the printing)."},
        "10314": {"comment":"input pending? exit"},
        "10368": {"comment":"no more help? skip"},
        "10428": {"comment":"no command help? skip"},
        "10451": {"comment":"!! join this to above"},
        "10463": {"synopsis":"Sends SOH SD_DTS, which resets the screen driver's toggles; falls into ScrDrv_SOH_A.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10465": {"synopsis":"Sends a screen driver code: SOH followed by A, through OS_Out.\nEntry: A = code.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10474": {"synopsis":"Draws the help window of the active command: a heading with the application's name, the\ncommand's name and key sequence, the command's help text (PrintTopicHelp), and the key hints\nfor the other entries and for going back to the topic. Ends through Help2Wd_bottom.\nEntry: none.\nError: Fc = 1 when input is pending (from InitHelpWd or the printing)."},
        "10535": {"comment":"no other enties? skip"},
        "10609": {"synopsis":"Prints the name of the help's active application (ubHlpActiveApp): finds its DOR with\nGetAppDOR, binds it in with OSBixS1 and prints the name at ADOR_NAME with OS_Bout.\nEntry: none."},
        "10618": {"comment":"skip to DOR name"},
        "10622": {"comment":"print string"},
        "10628": {"synopsis":"Loads the active help topic number (ubHlpActiveTpc) and falls into PrintTopic.\nEntry: none."},
        "10631": {"synopsis":"Prints the name of topic A of the active help application: binds in the topic list\n(GetHlpTopics, OSBixS1), skips to the topic with SkipNTopics and writes its tokenized name\nwith MayWrt, between the screen driver toggles of MTH_ToggleLT.\nEntry: A = topic number.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "10644": {"comment":"skip length byte"},
        "10648": {"comment":"print tokenized string"},
        "10664": {"synopsis":"Prints the name of the active command (ubHlpActiveCmd) of the active topic: binds in the\ncommand list, finds the topic (GetCmdTopicByNum) and the command (GetRealCmdPos), skips its\nkey sequence and writes the tokenized name with MayWrt.\nEntry: none.","comment":"!! get this after OS_Bix to avoid push/pop"},
        "10687": {"comment":"skip length/command code"},
        "10689": {"comment":"skip kbd sequence"},
        "10694": {"comment":"print tokenized sring"},
        "10706": {"synopsis":"Prints a help text given by its offset: returns when input is pending or the offset is 0,\notherwise adds the offset to the help base (GetHlpHelp), moving to the next bank on a carry\nout of the segment, and falls into MTHPrintTknzd.\nEntry: BC = help text offset (0 = none).\nError: Fc = 1 when input is pending."},
        "10709": {"comment":"input bending? exit"},
        "10712": {"comment":"no help text? exit"},
        "10713": {"comment":"help offset into DE"},
        "10715": {"comment":"get help base"},
        "10718": {"comment":"go to help text start"},
        "10719": {"comment":"handle bank change"},
        "10726": {"comment":"S0 fix"},
        "10730": {"synopsis":"Prints a tokenized text at BHL, centred (JustifyC), until its end or until input arrives;\nbinds it in with OSBixS1 and writes it with OSWrt. Falls into InputEmpty.\nOZ source name: MTHPrintTokenized.\nEntry: BHL = text (address in segment 0 form).\nExit: Fc = 0 when no input is pending.\nError: Fc = 1 when input is pending."},
        "10751": {"comment":"no error/end? print more"},
        "10757": {"synopsis":"drop thru\nExit: Fc=1 if input bending.","comment":"examine input"},
        "10772": {"synopsis":"Prints the inline string after the call with MTHPrint when no input is pending. When input\nis pending it drops the string's return address and returns to its caller's caller, so the\ncalling routine ends with Fc = 1.\nEntry: string inline after the call.\nError: Fc = 1, caller abandoned, when input is pending."},
        "10775": {"comment":"only print if not pre-empted"},
        "10778": {"comment":"double ret  !! should we get rid of this?  it's"},
        "10779": {"comment":"!! potentially dangerous if one forgets it"},
        "10781": {"synopsis":"The 12-character path prefix \":ROM.*/HELP/\" (no terminator). OpenAppHelpFile copies it to\nthe stack and appends the application's name to open its help file."},
        "10793": {"synopsis":"copy topic/command/help/token pointers"},
        "10794": {"comment":"4 loops, C=255 to make sure no underflow from C to B"},
        "10806": {"comment":"bank=0? leave alone"},
        "10810": {"comment":"already fixed (installed app)"},
        "10814": {"comment":"already fixed (installed app)"},
        "10816": {"comment":"else fix slot"},
        "10828": {"synopsis":"Return DOR handle in (ActiveAppHandle) to first application in slot A (0-3)"},
        "10839": {"comment":"ROM.x"},
        "10841": {"comment":"init handle"},
        "10845": {"comment":"return child DOR"},
        "10849": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "10852": {"comment":"return brother DOR"},
        "10854": {"comment":"not app? try brother"},
        "10856": {"comment":"return child DOR"},
        "10858": {"comment":"DOR interface"},
        "10861": {"synopsis":"Gets a DOR handle for a filename: calls GN_Opf with OP_DOR, a local name and no output\nbuffer.\nEntry: HL = filename (local pointer).\nExit: Fc = 0, IX = DOR handle.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "10862": {"comment":"return DOR handle"},
        "10864": {"comment":"local pointer, bufsize=255"},
        "10867": {"comment":"ouput=3, NOP"},
        "10875": {"synopsis":"Moves the help to the next application: GetAppDOR with ubHlpActiveApp + 1, then stores the\nreturned ID in ubHlpActiveApp.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BHL = application DOR; A = application ID."},
        "10881": {"synopsis":"Moves the help to the previous application: GetAppDOR with ubHlpActiveApp - 1, then stores\nthe returned ID in ubHlpActiveApp.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BHL = application DOR; A = application ID."},
        "10892": {"synopsis":"Makes application A the help's active application (ubHlpActiveApp) and falls into GetAppDOR,\nwhich finds its DOR, records it in eHlpAppDOR and copies its topic, command, help and token\npointers when no MTH help file is open.\nEntry: A = application ID (bit 7 = installed APP, bits 5-6 = slot, bits 0-4 = number).\nExit: BHL = application DOR; A = application ID found.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Esc when the ID is past the last application."},
        "10895": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=application ID (A7=ROM/APP, A5-6=slot, A0-4=number).\nExit: BHL=DOR.","comment":"bind in other part of kernel"},
        "10897": {"comment":"remembers old S2 bank binding on stack, returns also B = old bank binding"},
        "10900": {"comment":"routine uses IX for temporary DOR handle processing, preserve call IX register..."},
        "10903": {"comment":"remember A"},
        "10904": {"comment":"mask out slot"},
        "10906": {"comment":"#app=0, goto previous app"},
        "10910": {"comment":"slot0-3 application"},
        "10915": {"comment":"#app=0, goto previous app"},
        "10918": {"comment":"app slot 4"},
        "10938": {"comment":"wrap goto first app of slot 0 with error"},
        "10950": {"comment":"previous, app (or last app in prev slot)"},
        "10951": {"comment":"remember #app"},
        "10956": {"comment":"end of list reached, exit to return the last Application DOR pointer to caller"},
        "10959": {"comment":"loop until E passed"},
        "10963": {"comment":"the previous application ID was the end of the list -"},
