        "11020": {"comment":"Fc=0 to indicate successfull fetch of DOR pointer"},
        "11023": {"comment":"first of slot 4"},
        "11028": {"comment":"validate device handle before fetching pointer to DOR"},
        "11058": {"comment":"point at bank of fetched application DOR pointer"},
        "11061": {"comment":"read it into BHL and return back to caller"},
        "11063": {"synopsis":"Returns the help text base of the active help application in BHL; falls into GetHlp_sub with\nthe eHlpHelp pointer.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BHL = help text base (address in segment 0 form).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "11067": {"synopsis":"Returns the token table of the active help application in BHL. It is the system token table\n(MTH_BNK, SysTokenBase) when SF1_B_SYSTOKENS is set or the application's pointer is $FFFFFF\n(or $3F3FFF), otherwise the application's own (GetHlp_sub with eHlpTokens).\nEntry: none.\nExit: BHL = token table.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "11070": {"comment":"use default system tokens if SYSTOKENS set"},
        "11079": {"comment":"$FFFFFF will use default system tokens"},
        "11081": {"comment":"$3F3FFF will use default system tokens too"},
        "11085": {"comment":"not $FFFFFF"},
        "11092": {"synopsis":"Returns the topic list of the active help application in BHL; jumps to GetHlp_sub with the\neHlpTopics pointer.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BHL = topic list (address in segment 0 form).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "11096": {"synopsis":"Exit: BHL=commands for suspended app."},
        "11101": {"synopsis":"Exit: BHL=help."},
        "11103": {"synopsis":"Reads one of the help pointers (topics, commands, help, tokens) as BHL. When the help's\napplication DOR (eHlpAppDOR) is the running application's (eAppDOR_2) it reads the\napplication's own copy (eAppTopics_2 and on), otherwise the help copy at eHlpTopics and on.\nA14-A15 of H are cleared.\nEntry: L = low byte of the pointer's bank byte in the eHlpTopics block.\nExit: BHL = pointer (address in segment 0 form).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "11105": {"comment":"if help DOR matches app DOR, use app pointer"},
        "11106": {"comment":"otherwise use help pointer"},
        "11116": {"comment":"!! 'jr nz' to lower pop to save pop/push here"},
        "11117": {"comment":"not same, use help pointers"},
        "11140": {"comment":"S0 fix"},
        "11145": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=count.\nExit: Fc=1, A=0 - last command.","comment":"store count"},
        "11146": {"comment":"skip start mark"},
        "11147": {"comment":"validate pointer by going forward and back"},
        "11153": {"comment":"count into B"},
        "11156": {"comment":"only one command/topic? exit Fc=1"},
        "11157": {"comment":"c = 0"},
        "11161": {"comment":"Fc=0, A=count"},
        "11166": {"comment":"not end of list? loop"},
        "11173": {"comment":"go back to last vommand/topic"},
        "11176": {"comment":"return count"},
        "11179": {"comment":"go back to start of topic"},
        "11188": {"synopsis":"Moves HL from the start mark of a topic/command list to the first entry of topic A, skipping\nwhole topics with NextTopic.\nEntry: HL = start mark of the list; A = topic number (1 = first).\nExit: Fc = 0, HL = first entry of the topic.\nError: Fc = 1 when the list ends first.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"skip start mark"},
        "11200": {"synopsis":"Finds command A of the topic around HL and its place on screen: rewinds to the topic's\nstart, then steps forward with NextCommand, counting the position and the column and row\n(from column 1, row 0). Hidden commands are passed over: a hidden target gives the next\nvisible command, or the previous one at the topic's end, and a search that finds none starts\nagain with command 1.\nOZ source name: GetRealCmdPosition.\nEntry: HL = an entry of the topic; A = command number.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = position; HL = command; D = column; E = row.\nError: Fc = 1, A = 0 when the list holds no command; a fallback also returns Fc = 1."},
        "11201": {"comment":"back to start of topic"},
        "11206": {"comment":"validate by going forward and backward"},
        "11212": {"comment":"B=count"},
        "11215": {"comment":"start of list? Fc=1, A=0"},
        "11217": {"comment":"start of topic? Fc=1"},
        "11218": {"comment":"column=1, row=0"},
        "11221": {"comment":"c = 0"},
        "11222": {"comment":"bump actual position"},
        "11223": {"comment":"not done yet? go forward"},
        "11225": {"comment":"B=1 for hidden  !! do this only if necessary"},
        "11231": {"comment":"hidden? skip"},
        "11233": {"comment":"return position in A, Fc=0"},
        "11239": {"comment":"not end of list or topic? go back"},
        "11243": {"comment":"!! bit 7,b; jr z"},
        "11244": {"comment":"B<0? wanted was hidden, go to previous"},
        "11245": {"comment":"else rewind to topic start and search for cmd 1"},
        "11261": {"comment":"back to start of topic"},
        "11266": {"comment":"only way we could here is we searched with A=0, try with 1"},
        "11271": {"comment":"column=1, row=0"},
        "11276": {"synopsis":"Moves HL past the end-of-topic mark to the first entry of the next topic, stepping with\nNextCommand.\nEntry: HL = an entry of the topic; D = column; E = row.\nExit: Fc = 0, HL = first entry of the next topic; DE updated.\nError: Fc = 1 at the end of the list.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "11279": {"comment":"end mark"},
        "11280": {"comment":"not end_of_topic? loop"},
        "11282": {"comment":"skip eot mark"},
        "11284": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=command/topic.\nExit: Fc=1, Fz=0 - start of list; Fc=1, Fz=1 - start of topic; Fc=0 - HL=command/topic."},
        "11285": {"comment":"length byte"},
        "11289": {"comment":"0, start of list- Fc=1, Fz=0"},
        "11291": {"comment":"1, start of topic - Fc=1, Fz=1"},
        "11292": {"comment":"HL-=A"},
        "11300": {"synopsis":"Hangs in a loop to itself when HL - DE borrows (Fc set).","comment":"error? crash"},
        "11303": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=command/topic, E=row, D=column.\nExit: Fc=1 - end of list; Fc=0, Fz=1 - end of topic; Fc=0, Fz=0 - HL=command/topic, E=row,\nD=column."},
        "11304": {"comment":"get length"},
        "11307": {"comment":"skip current command/topic"},
        "11308": {"synopsis":"Hangs in a loop to itself when HL + DE overflows (Fc set).","comment":"invalid? crash"},
        "11311": {"comment":"length"},
        "11314": {"comment":"0=start/end mark, Fc=1"},
        "11315": {"comment":"1=topic end, Fz=1"},
        "11316": {"comment":"store Fc=0, Fz=0"},
        "11317": {"comment":"command attribute"},
        "11320": {"comment":"hidden"},
        "11322": {"comment":"yes? skip"},
        "11324": {"comment":"advance row"},
        "11325": {"comment":"new column"},
        "11327": {"comment":"yes? skip"},
        "11330": {"comment":"row too big?"},
        "11332": {"comment":"no? skip"},
        "11334": {"comment":"advance column"},
        "11335": {"comment":"reset row"},
        "11339": {"synopsis":"Reads the help pointer of a topic or command definition through GetAttr_Help and tests its\nCMDF_HELP attribute bit.\nEntry: HL = topic or command definition (its length byte first).\nExit: Fz = 0, DE = help pointer when the entry has help; Fz = 1, DE = 0 when it has none; Fc\n= 0 in both cases (the source comment's Fc = 1 does not happen: AND clears Fc).\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "11342": {"comment":"help"},
        "11344": {"comment":"Fc=0, DE=help"},
        "11345": {"comment":"ld de, 0"},
        "11347": {"comment":"Fc=1, DE=0"},
        "11348": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=command definition.\nExit: A=attribute byte."},
        "11354": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=command definition.\nExit: A=attribute byte, DE=help text."},
        "11356": {"comment":"length byte"},
        "11362": {"comment":"attribute byte"},
        "11364": {"comment":"help pointer"},
        "11370": {"synopsis":"Fetches the DOR of the application whose help is shown (ubHlpActiveApp) with GetAppDOR and\nfalls into ChgHelpFile to switch the help file to it.\nEntry: none (reads ubHlpActiveApp).","comment":"!! could do these 2 instructions at caller"},
        "11373": {"comment":"!! to reduce number of subroutines"},
        "11376": {"synopsis":"Closes the open help file (frees the DOR handle in pMTHHelpHandle with OS_Dor DR_FRE) and,\nunless A = 0, opens the help file of the application whose DOR is at BHL: binds the DOR into\nS1, binds kernel bank 1 into S2 and calls OpenAppHelpFile with the DOR's name. The new\nhandle is stored in pMTHHelpHandle.\nEntry: A = application ID, 0 to close only; BHL = application DOR.\nExit: pMTHHelpHandle = handle of the new help file (or what DR_FRE left)."},
        "11381": {"comment":"free DOR handle"},
        "11383": {"comment":"DOR interface"},
        "11392": {"comment":"Bind in extended address"},
        "11415": {"synopsis":"Draws the MTH menu window of the active topic (ubHlpActiveTpc).\n1. Defines and clears window 6 across the screen.\n2. Without topics it prints \"<application> has no topics\"; a topic without commands prints\n\"The <application> <topic> topic has no functions\"; both return Fc = 1.\n3. Otherwise it lists the topic's commands that are not hidden in columns of 8 rows\n(InitMenuColumnE starts a column, CMDF_B_COLUMN forces one), each name followed by its key\nsequence (PrintCmdSequence); it stops early when input is waiting.\n4. When the list is done it calls DrawMenuWd2 for the topic line and key hints.\nEntry: none (reads ubHlpActiveTpc).\nExit: Fc = 0 when the menu was drawn; Fc = 1 when there was nothing to list or input is\nwaiting."},
        "11445": {"comment":"has topics? skip"},
        "11479": {"comment":"Fc=1"},
        "11493": {"comment":"not eol/eot? skip"},
        "11542": {"synopsis":"Shared exit of DrawMenuWd for a topic list or a topic with nothing to show: sets Fc = 1 and\nreturns.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1."},
        "11555": {"comment":"hidden? skip"},
        "11558": {"comment":"move to kbd sequence"},
        "11561": {"comment":"skip kbd sequence to get cmd name"},
        "11569": {"comment":"column change? handle"},
        "11575": {"comment":"not last row? skip"},
        "11588": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11590": {"comment":"print command name"},
        "11632": {"synopsis":"Starts the first menu column: sets D = 1 and falls into InitMenuColumnE.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as InitMenuColumn (D = 2, E = 0 when the column was opened)."},
        "11634": {"synopsis":"Sets the column width E = 27 and falls into InitMenuColumn, which defines window 7 at column\nD of the menu: x = 28 * (D - 1), width E, 8 rows, and clears window 6. A width under 16\nplaces the window at x = 85, the narrow last column.\nEntry: D = column number (1 to 3 for a full column).\nExit: Fc = 0; D = D + 1 and E = 0 when the column was opened; D and E unchanged when the\ncolumn would pass x = 93.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "11636": {"synopsis":"e=width"},
        "11638": {"comment":"calculate xpos"},
        "11640": {"comment":"0/28/56/84"},
        "11667": {"comment":"x"},
        "11671": {"comment":"y"},
        "11676": {"comment":"w"},
        "11693": {"synopsis":"Prints the key sequence of a command right justified, then a space, CR and LF. A sequence\nstarting with a letter is printed as the <> symbol followed by the string; any other first\nbyte is printed as a key name by MTHPrintKeycode.\nEntry: HL = command definition (length byte, command code, key sequence).\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "11695": {"comment":"skip length/code"},
        "11707": {"comment":"a-z/A-Z"},
        "11714": {"comment":"print <>"},
        "11719": {"comment":"print string"},
        "11737": {"synopsis":"Called from OS_In to find the command\nExit: Fc=1 - no command matches; Fc=0, Fz=0, A=code - partial match, buffer not ready yet;\nFc=0, Fz=1, A=code - perfect match."},
        "11741": {"comment":"commands in BHL"},
        "11748": {"comment":"skip start mark"},
        "11752": {"comment":"end of list"},
        "11754": {"comment":"end of topic? skip it"},
        "11758": {"comment":"command code"},
        "11767": {"comment":"match? return C"},
        "11769": {"comment":"get length"},
        "11772": {"comment":"skip command"},
        "11773": {"comment":"compare next command"},
        "11775": {"comment":"get command code"},
        "11781": {"synopsis":"Compares the key sequence of a command with the typed OZ command buffer. Called by FindCmd\nfor each command of the application.\nEntry: HL = command's key sequence (zero terminated); DE = typed buffer (OZcmdBuf).\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1 when they match exactly (or the buffer is empty and the command starts\nwith '@'); Fc = 0, Fz = 0 when the buffer is a prefix of the command.\nError: Fc = 1 when they differ or the command's sequence is empty.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "11784": {"comment":"cmd end? Fc=1"},
        "11787": {"comment":"buffer not end yet? skip"},
        "11789": {"comment":"cmd char"},
        "11792": {"comment":"'@'? Fc=0, Fz=1"},
        "11794": {"comment":"otherwise Fc=1"},
        "11799": {"comment":"end? return Fc=0, Fz=1"},
        "11803": {"comment":"buf end? Fc=0, A=1"},
        "11808": {"comment":"same? continue compare"},
        "11810": {"comment":"different? Fc=1"},
        "11815": {"synopsis":"OS_Wtb: sets the token table base used to expand tokens. A new base with B = 0 and HL not\nzero is a local address, turned into a bank and address by FixPtr. The base is stored in\neAppTokens_2; the old base is returned in the caller's OS frame.\nEntry: BHL = new token table base (0 for none).\nExit: Fc = 0; BHL = previous token table base."},
        "11816": {"comment":"ld b,(eAppTokens_2+2)"},
        "11820": {"comment":"HL=address"},
        "11827": {"comment":"if new base is zero then write as is"},
        "11832": {"comment":"fix pointer if in bank 0"},
        "11837": {"comment":"bank"},
        "11840": {"comment":"address"},
        "11845": {"synopsis":"Writes A through OS_Wrt unless it is a control code: a byte below $20 returns Fc = 1 without\noutput, which ends DrawMenuWd's name loop at the terminating zero.\nEntry: A = character or token.\nExit: Fc = 0 after writing; Fc = 1 when A < $20 (A unchanged)."},
        "11847": {"comment":"control char? return Fc=1"},
        "11848": {"synopsis":"OS_Wrt: writes a character or token to standard output: 1 to $7E as is, $7F as CR and LF,\nand $80 to $FF as the token of the help token table (WrFarToken), or as the byte itself when\nthere is no token table. Tokens may contain tokens.\nEntry: A = character or token code.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Eof when A = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL.","comment":"!! 'or a; jr z', 'scf' at EOF"},
        "11850": {"comment":"0 - EOF"},
        "11855": {"comment":"1-7e? print"},
        "11857": {"comment":"80-ff? token"},
        "11859": {"comment":"7f -> cr,lf"},
        "11871": {"comment":"already handled"},
        "11873": {"comment":"print new char"},
        "11875": {"comment":"print old char"},
        "11876": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11881": {"comment":"!! is this necessary?"},
        "11884": {"synopsis":"Writes token E from the help token table (GetHlpTokens): binds the table's bank into S2\n(setting bit 7 of its address), prints the token with WriteToken and restores S2.\nEntry: E = token code ($80 to $FF).\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 0, A = $7F when the token was handled.\nError: Fc = 1, Fz = 1 when there is no token table."},
        "11891": {"comment":"no tokens? Fc=1, Fz=1"},
        "11892": {"comment":"S2 fix"},
        "11900": {"comment":"restore S2"},
        "11903": {"comment":"A=7F, Fz=0, Fc=0"},
        "11907": {"synopsis":"Prints one token from a token table. The table starts with the recursion boundary byte and\nthe number of tokens, followed by a word offset per token (the next one marks its end).\nTokens numbered from the boundary up (all of them when its bit 7 is set) are printed through\nOS_Wrt so they can hold tokens; the others go to OS_Out. $7F prints as CR and LF.\nEntry: HL = token table base; E = token code ($80 + number).\nExit: Fc = 0; BC = table base.\nError: Fc = 1 when the token number is not below the number of tokens.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC=token base"},
        "11913": {"comment":"A=#tokens"},
        "11917": {"comment":"token to print"},
        "11918": {"comment":"D=D-127"},
        "11922": {"comment":"not enough tokens in table"},
        "11926": {"comment":"DE=token start"},
        "11930": {"comment":"D=token end"},
        "11938": {"comment":"token length"},
        "11939": {"comment":"token start"},
        "11941": {"comment":"length=0? exit"},
        "11943": {"comment":"length"},
        "11944": {"comment":"recursive token boundary"},
        "11946": {"comment":"bit7 set, Fc=1"},
        "11949": {"comment":"Fc=1 if recursive"},
        "11954": {"comment":"7f -> crlf"},
        "11960": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11964": {"comment":"restore flags"},
        "11966": {"comment":"restore char"},
        "11967": {"comment":"not recursive, print - Fc=0 on return"},
        "11971": {"comment":"recursive call"},
        "11980": {"comment":"loop until length done"},
        "11987": {"synopsis":"Reads two bytes of the token table and falls into GetTokenChar for the second one.\nEntry: BC = token table base; HL = offset.\nExit: E = byte at BC + HL; A = D = byte at BC + HL + 1; HL = HL + 2.\nChanges: A, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "11991": {"synopsis":"Reads one byte of the token table.\nEntry: BC = token table base; HL = offset.\nExit: A = D = byte at BC + HL; HL = HL + 1.\nChanges: A, D, HL.\nKeeps: BC, E."},
        "11998": {"synopsis":"Delay a given period\nEntry: BC = delay in centiseconds.\nExit: Fc=1, BC remaining time, A=error; RC_ESC ($01), escape was pressed; RC_SUSP ($69),\nprocess suspended; RC_TIME ($02), timeout.","comment":"force int enabled (for RTC)"},
        "12002": {"comment":"reset timeout flag"},
        "12004": {"comment":"small timer counts timeout"},
        "12014": {"comment":"pre-empted? exit"},
        "12016": {"comment":"Fc=1 if ESC pending"},
        "12020": {"comment":"wait for event, returns ITSK in A"},
        "12025": {"comment":"pre-empted? cancel buffer task and exit"},
        "12029": {"comment":"ESC pending? exit"},
        "12033": {"comment":"timeout? exit"},
        "12035": {"comment":"otherwise exit with pre-emption"},
        "12037": {"comment":"acknowledge preemption"},
        "12052": {"comment":"time remaining"},
        "12060": {"synopsis":"Purge keyboard buffer\nEntry: -.\nExit: Fc=0, always.\nChanges: F."},
        "12063": {"comment":"cancel any [] or <> command"},
        "12077": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "12078": {"comment":"return AF and undo exx"},
        "12081": {"synopsis":"Examine input\nEntry: -.\nExit: Fc = 0, OS_In will return immediately possibly with error; Fc = 1, A=RC_EOF ($09),\nOS_In will wait.\nChanges: AF, DC_Xin?"},
        "12089": {"comment":"have extended char? exit"},
        "12096": {"comment":"pre-empted? exit"},
        "12100": {"comment":"ESC pending? exit"},
        "12107": {"comment":"keyboard buffer not empty? exit"},
        "12114": {"comment":"seria RX buffer not empty? exit"},
        "12120": {"comment":"CLI active? check it's input"},
        "12125": {"comment":"return AFbcdehl with Fc=1, A=error"},
        "12131": {"comment":"return afbcdehl with fc=0, a unchanged"},
        "12136": {"comment":"Examine CLI input"},
        "12139": {"comment":"return AFBCDEHL"},
        "12142": {"synopsis":"Reads standard input with BC = $FFFF, the default timeout of RdKbBuffer; falls into RdStdin.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as RdStdin."},
        "12145": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte from standard input. With a CLI active it reads from the CLI (DC_In, after\nUpdateRnd and ResetTimeout), reads again at the end of a CLI file and marks a read ESC with\nMaySetEsc. Otherwise it jumps to RdKbBuffer to wait for a key in the keyboard buffer.\nEntry: BC = timeout ($FFFF for the default).\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte; BC = time remaining (keyboard).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Time, RC_Esc, RC_Susp, or the CLI's error)."},
        "12149": {"comment":"no cli? read keyborad"},
        "12157": {"comment":"Read from CLI"},
        "12160": {"comment":"no error? exit"},
        "12162": {"comment":"End Of File"},
        "12164": {"comment":"EOF? read again"},
        "12166": {"comment":"return error"},
        "12176": {"synopsis":"Get byte from keyboard circular buffer with timeout\n\nFc=1, A=error if fail\nEntry: BC = timeout, $FFFF for default.\nExit: Fc=0, A=data, BC=remaining time if success.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12179": {"comment":"reset timeout flag"},
        "12181": {"comment":"reset buffer flag"},
        "12183": {"comment":"small timer counts timeout"},
        "12189": {"comment":"pre-empted? exit"},
        "12191": {"comment":"Fc=1 if ESC pending"},
        "12203": {"comment":"buffer is empty, wait"},
        "12208": {"comment":"get byte in b"},
        "12210": {"comment":"32 bytes circular buffer"},
        "12212": {"comment":"apply address mask"},
        "12219": {"comment":"byte read from buffer"},
        "12220": {"comment":"reset Fc"},
        "12221": {"comment":"buffer task done"},
        "12226": {"comment":"time remaining"},
        "12240": {"comment":"acknowledge preemption"},
        "12247": {"comment":"dont wait for OSWaitMain to do that..."},
        "12255": {"comment":"wait for event, returns ITSK in A"},
        "12260": {"comment":"pre-empted? cancel buffer task and exit"},
        "12264": {"comment":"ESC pending? exit"},
        "12268": {"comment":"buffer job?  check for data"},
        "12272": {"comment":"timeout? exit"},
        "12274": {"comment":"otherwise exit with pre-emption"},
        "12276": {"synopsis":"read character from standard input with timeout"},
        "12287": {"synopsis":"read character from standard input without timeout"},
        "12302": {"synopsis":"The body of OS_In and OS_Tin: reads a character for the application.\n1. Saves the timeout, pushes IX and IY as OS_Ent does, records SP in pAppStackPtr, the S0 to\nS2 bindings in ubAppBindings and the call level in ubOldCallLevel.\n2. Runs DoTasks (switch off, expired alarms, OZ window).\n3. A pending second byte of an extended character (SF1_B_XTNDCHAR) is returned now.\n4. Otherwise reads a byte with RdStdin; MENU, HELP and INDEX (ostin_tbl) go to DoHelp, other\nkeys through sub_EF92, the <> and [] command handling.\n5. An extended character returns A = 0 with Fz = 1 in the OS frame and keeps the character\nfor the next call. ostin_4, inside it, is where an application is entered from OS_Ent.\nEntry: BC = timeout ($FFFF for none).\nExit: Fc = 0, A = character.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Time, RC_Esc, RC_Susp)."},
        "12306": {"comment":"push like OS_Ent for ostin_4"},
        "12310": {"comment":"remember SP"},
        "12314": {"comment":"remember bindings"},
        "12325": {"comment":"remember call level"},
        "12331": {"comment":"handle shutdown, expired alarm, update OZ window"},
        "12358": {"comment":"!! should cancel <> too"},
        "12371": {"synopsis":"Entry of application from OS_ENT"},
        "12381": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "12390": {"comment":"get char"},
        "12399": {"comment":"Timeout"},
        "12407": {"comment":"could compare without table"},
        "12410": {"comment":"for only 3 cases"},
        "12415": {"comment":"menu/help/index"},
        "12436": {"comment":"Fz=1"},
        "12443": {"synopsis":"Table of 3 bytes: the keys OSTinMain hands to DoHelp, IN_MEN, IN_HLP and IN_IDX (searched\nwith CPIR)."},
        "12446": {"synopsis":"Applies a pending <> or [] of the OZ window to a key. With neither pending, or with letters\nalready typed into OZcmdBuf, the key is returned as it is. Otherwise <> adds the QUAL_CTRL\nand [] the QUAL_ALT qualifier (ApplyQualifiers) and the OZ command is cancelled.\nEntry: A = key; HL = ubSysFlags1.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = key, qualified when ApplyQualifiers accepted it.\nError: Fc = 1, A = key when the key is <> or [] itself and one of them is pending.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "12447": {"comment":"(ubSysFlags1)"},
        "12451": {"comment":"neither [] nor <> in OZwd? exit Fc=0"},
        "12455": {"comment":"<>? Fc=1"},
        "12459": {"comment":"[]? Fc=1"},
        "12461": {"comment":"ld c,(OZcmdBuf)"},
        "12467": {"comment":"no command? Fc=0"},
        "12470": {"comment":"<>"},
        "12472": {"comment":"<> active? use it as qualifier"},
        "12474": {"comment":"[]"},
        "12478": {"comment":"A char, D qualifier"},
        "12490": {"synopsis":"Passes one key through the OZ window's command handling. <> or [] starts a command (the\nsymbol is shown, the buffer cleared); following keys are converted by Char2OZwdChar, added\nto OZcmdBuf and matched against the application's commands (FindCmd); [] keys are also\npassed to the CLI with DC_Alt. Control keys cancel the command. A key outside a command is\nreturned to the caller.\nEntry: A = key.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = key or matched command code for the application; Fz = 1 asks OSTinMain to\nreturn it as an extended character.\nError: Fc = 1, A = 0 when the key was taken by the command handling."},
        "12496": {"comment":"<> or [] already pressed and handled"},
        "12503": {"comment":"<>"},
        "12509": {"comment":"[]"},
        "12515": {"comment":"[]+"},
        "12519": {"comment":"[]-"},
        "12531": {"synopsis":"Entry inside sub_EF92 for the []+ and []- keys ($80, $9F), also used by DoHelp to send a\nmade-up []I: cancels any OZ command, then handles A as a [] command key. A control code\ncancels; otherwise [] becomes active, $80 shows as '+', $9F as '-', the key is shown in the\nOZ window and passed to DC_Alt.\nEntry: A = key ($80 to $9F).\nExit: as sub_EF92."},
        "12539": {"comment":"00-1F : ctrl char, cancel OZ command"},
        "12542": {"comment":"handled"},
        "12546": {"comment":"A0-FF : ctrl char, cancel OZ command"},
        "12549": {"comment":"handled"},
        "12555": {"comment":"80->'+'"},
        "12561": {"comment":"9f->'-'"},
        "12571": {"comment":"Pass an alternative character"},
        "12584": {"comment":"clear any [] command"},
        "12585": {"comment":"Pass an alternative character"},
        "12589": {"comment":"ubSysFlags1, set SF1_OZSQUARE or SF1_OZDMND"},
        "12591": {"comment":"clear command buffer"},
        "12604": {"comment":"?? why H ?? (= ubSysFlags1) ??"},
        "12618": {"comment":"match? skip"},
        "12633": {"comment":"00 - ret"},
        "12637": {"comment":"01-EF -> cont"},
        "12644": {"comment":"01-AF -> ret"},
        "12649": {"comment":"B0 (IN_ASPC) -> 20"},
        "12662": {"comment":"E9-EF"},
        "12666": {"comment":"E5-E8"},
        "12675": {"comment":"E0-E4 -> space, enter, tab, del, esc"},
        "12695": {"comment":"full match? done, return A and Fc=0"},
        "12706": {"comment":"A=0, Fc=1"},
        "12709": {"synopsis":"Table of 5 bytes: the keys for the <> command codes $E0 to $E4, IN_SPC, IN_ENT, IN_TAB,\nIN_DEL and IN_ESC, read by sub_EF92."},
        "12714": {"synopsis":"Converts a key into the character the OZ window shows. A foreign key becomes its ISO\ncharacter through Key2Chr_tbl (Fc = 0). System keys: $00, $1B to $1F and $7F give Fc = 1\n($7F with Fz = 1); $01 to $1A give Fc = 1 with A = 'A' to 'Z'; $20 to $7E give Fc = 0, Fz =\n0; $A0 and $A3 give Fc = 0, Fz = 1; the others Fc = 1.\nEntry: A = key.\nExit: A = character; B = the original key (system keys) or the character (foreign).\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "12718": {"comment":"restore original char"},
        "12719": {"comment":"it is a system key, do not translate"},
        "12725": {"comment":"change foreign key to ISO char"},
        "12728": {"comment":"character code"},
        "12733": {"comment":"$1B"},
        "12739": {"comment":"00    - Fc=1"},
        "12743": {"comment":"01-1A - Fc=1, A=41-5A"},
        "12746": {"comment":"1B-1F - Fc=1"},
        "12750": {"comment":"20-7E - Fc=0 Fz=0"},
        "12751": {"comment":"7F    - Fc=1 Fz=1"},
        "12754": {"comment":"A3    - Fc=0 Fz=1"},
        "12757": {"comment":"A0    - Fc=0 Fz=1"},
        "12760": {"synopsis":"Cancels the OZ window's command: ends a pending [] for the CLI (DC_Alt with 0), clears\nubSysFlags1, the dead key (kbd_lastkey) and OZcmdBuf, and redraws the OZ window.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12772": {"comment":"Pass an alternative character"},
        "12777": {"comment":"dead key"},
        "12791": {"synopsis":"Appends a character, upper-cased by AtoN_upper, to the OZ command buffer (OZcmdBuf, at most\n4 characters and a zero) and redraws the OZ window. With A = 0 it writes a zero, which\nclears the buffer after a cancel.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: Fc = 0, A unchanged.\nError: Fc = 1 when the buffer is full; the command is cancelled.\nChanges: F, B, HL."},
        "12799": {"comment":"end of OZcmdBuf reached"},
        "12809": {"comment":"last byte +1 is zero"},
        "12811": {"comment":"last byte (was zero)"},
        "12815": {"comment":"write A"},
        "12816": {"comment":"and redraw"},
        "12822": {"synopsis":"Runs the tasks the interrupt left in ubIntTaskToDo: a switch-off request (OSOff), an expired\nalarm (DoAlarms) and an OZ window refresh (DrawOZwd). Returns at once when none is pending.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "12827": {"comment":"exit if none, faster"},
        "12828": {"comment":"process shutdown request from machine timeout"},
        "12830": {"comment":"AF changed"},
        "12833": {"comment":"reload A"},
        "12838": {"comment":"process expired alarm"},
        "12846": {"comment":"redraw OZ window"},
        "12850": {"synopsis":"set Panel and PrinterEd values","comment":"Framepush and bind K1"},
        "12853": {"comment":"in K1"},
        "12859": {"synopsis":"A lone RET. OSSpMain and OSNqMain (kernel bank 1) push its address before jumping to a\nreason's handler, so the handler returns through it.\nEntry: none."},
        "12860": {"synopsis":"read Panel and PrinterEd values","comment":"idem"},
        "12869": {"synopsis":"Uses the handle structure laid over the system variables at pFsMemPool (its first block,\nposition and attribute are pFsMemFirstBlock, eFsMemFilePos and ubFsMemAttr): sets its first\nblock to DE and rewinds it (SetFhnFirstBlock).\nEntry: DE = file pointer of the first block.\nExit: IX = pFsMemPool; as RewindFile."},
        "12875": {"synopsis":"Points IX at the handle structure at pFsMemPool and falls into InitMemHandle.\nEntry: none.\nExit: IX = pFsMemPool; as InitMemHandle."},
        "12879": {"synopsis":"Clears a memory file handle for a new file: keeps only its readable, writable and memory\nattribute flags and falls into AllocFirstBlock.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: as AllocFirstBlock.","comment":"keep only rd/wr/mem flags"},
        "12887": {"synopsis":"Clears the handle's first block, allocates a new block (AllocHandleBlock) and falls into\nSetFhnFirstBlock to make it the first block and rewind.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: Fc = 0; DE = file pointer of the block; position at its first data byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Room, or OS_Mal's)."},
        "12888": {"comment":"reset first block"},
        "12898": {"synopsis":"Stores DE as the handle's first block and falls into RewindFile.\nEntry: IX = file handle; DE = file pointer of the first block.\nExit: as RewindFile.","comment":"set first block"},
        "12904": {"synopsis":"Rewinds a memory file: reads the handle's first block and falls into fsAdvanceBlock.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: as fsAdvanceBlock; DE = first block.","comment":"read first block"},
        "12910": {"synopsis":"Makes block DE the handle's current block, with the position on its first data byte (block\nstart + 2). A file pointer is D = bank, E = 64-byte block in the bank; a block holds the\nnext block's pointer in bytes 0 and 1 (D = 0 in the last block, whose byte 0 is then its\nbyte count) and FSBLOCK_SIZE (62) data bytes.\nEntry: IX = file handle; DE = file pointer of the block.\nExit: BHL = memory pointer of the block (HL in S2); C = 2.\nChanges: BC, HL.\nKeeps: AF, DE."},
        "12911": {"comment":"DE->BHL"},
        "12914": {"comment":"set position"},
        "12921": {"comment":"point pos_lo to start of data area"},
        "12928": {"synopsis":"Frees the data of a memory file: takes the handle's first block, clears it in the handle and\njumps to FreeMemData when there was one.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: as FreeMemData."},
        "12941": {"comment":"!! unnecessary check"},
        "12946": {"synopsis":"Returns a chain of file blocks to the free lists: each block, followed through its link,\ngoes to AddAvailableFsBlock. Returns at once for DE = 0.\nEntry: DE = file pointer of the first block.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12949": {"comment":"bind in DE"},
        "12953": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr to next"},
        "12956": {"comment":"HL=fsPtr to this"},
        "12957": {"comment":"DE=this, HL=next"},
        "12965": {"comment":"DE=next"},
        "12968": {"comment":"has next? free it"},
        "12972": {"synopsis":"Converts the handle's current block into a memory pointer (FilePtr2MemPtr), without binding\nit.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: Fc = 0; BHL = memory pointer of the current block (HL in S2); C = 2.\nChanges: F, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "12984": {"synopsis":"Marks a block free: stores DE as its link and the signature $DE $AD in bytes 2 and 3, which\nAddAvailableFsBlock2 looks for.\nEntry: HL = memory pointer of the block (bound in); DE = file pointer of the next block.\nExit: L = L + 3.\nChanges: L."},
        "12991": {"comment":"'dead'!"},
        "12994": {"synopsis":"Makes a slot's free-block chain the current one: copies its head from uwSlotAvailFsBlocks\ninto uwFsAvailBlock and leaves the address of the slot's entry on the stack, under the\nreturn address, for SetSlotBlocks.\nEntry: B = slot (0 to 3).\nExit: (SP + 2) = address of the slot's entry.\nChanges: A, HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"slot"},
        "12997": {"comment":"!! ld hl,uwSlotAvailFsBlocks; add a,l; ld l,a"},
        "13002": {"comment":"first block available in slot"},
        "13012": {"comment":"push hl for caller"},
        "13016": {"synopsis":"Pops the slot entry left by GetSlotBlocks and stores the head of the current free-block\nchain (uwFsAvailBlock) back into it.\nEntry: the slot entry address under the return address.\nChanges: DE', HL'.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "13018": {"comment":"return address"},
        "13019": {"comment":"pushed in fsSetAvailableBlock"},
        "13020": {"comment":"put fsPtr back to slot chain"},
        "13029": {"comment":"return address"},
        "13033": {"synopsis":"Allocates a 64-byte file block for a handle. When the handle's attributes carry a slot (bits\n3 and 4 beside other flags) the block comes from that slot; otherwise slots 1, 2, 3 and 0\nare tried in turn.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: Fc = 0; DE = file pointer of the block; BHL = its memory pointer; C = 2.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Room (no RAM) or OS_Mal's error."},
        "13038": {"comment":"no flags? any slot"},
        "13040": {"comment":"bits 3&4 to top - slot"},
        "13043": {"synopsis":"Entry inside AllocHandleBlock that allocates the block from one slot: fails with RC_Room\nwhen the slot has no RAM (ubSlotRamSize), otherwise takes a block from the slot's free chain\n(GetSlotBlocks, fsGetBlock with OS_Mal flags slot OR $10, SetSlotBlocks). The alarm\napplication's own label ahb_1 is a different one.\nEntry: IX = file handle; A = slot in bits 7 and 6.\nExit: Fc = 0; DE = file pointer of the block; BHL = its memory pointer.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Room or OS_Mal's error."},
        "13047": {"comment":"save slot"},
        "13048": {"comment":"!! ld hl,ubSlotRamSize; add a,l; ld l,a"},
        "13055": {"comment":"No room"},
        "13058": {"comment":"no RAM in slot"},
        "13063": {"comment":"for OS_Mal"},
        "13072": {"comment":"40-80-C0-00, slot 1-2-3-0"},
        "13089": {"synopsis":"Takes a block from the current free chain (fsGetAvailableBlock); when the chain is empty it\nallocates a new page of blocks (fsAllocBlock) and tries again.\nEntry: A = OS_Mal flags; uwFsAvailBlock = current free chain.\nExit: Fc = 0; DE = file pointer of the block; BHL = its memory pointer; C = 2.\nError: Fc = 1, A = OS_Mal's error."},
        "13093": {"comment":"got block, return"},
        "13105": {"synopsis":"Allocates a 256-byte page from the file system's memory pool (pFsMemPool) with OS_Mal and\nsplits it into four free 64-byte blocks, each linked to the next, the last to the old head\nof uwFsAvailBlock; the page's first block becomes the new head.\nEntry: A = OS_Mal flags.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = OS_Mal's error.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "13114": {"comment":"allocate full page"},
        "13119": {"comment":"bind it in"},
        "13157": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: fsGetAvailableBlock.\nExit: Fc=0, BHL=fsBlock."},
        "13163": {"comment":"scf"},
        "13164": {"comment":"no available, allocate more"},
        "13166": {"comment":"bind it in, BHL=memptr"},
        "13169": {"comment":"DE=next available block"},
        "13172": {"comment":"clear next pointer"},
        "13177": {"comment":"make this.Next new head of chain"},
        "13184": {"comment":"pop block and return it as MemPtr too"},
        "13185": {"synopsis":"!! wouldn't it be enough to 'ld b,d; ret'?\nEntry: DE=fsPTR.\nExit: BHL=memPtr.","comment":"bank"},
        "13188": {"comment":"zero, start from beginning"},
        "13197": {"comment":"10eeeeee"},
        "13199": {"comment":"ee000000"},
        "13201": {"comment":"segment  !! do this first to avoid duplicate code"},
        "13207": {"comment":"segment"},
        "13211": {"synopsis":"D=B\nE=(HL>>6) & $00ff"},
        "13218": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: AddAvailableFsBlock.\nEntry: DE=fsPtr.","comment":"FsPtr"},
        "13223": {"comment":"slot"},
        "13234": {"synopsis":"Puts a freed block into the current free chain (uwFsAvailBlock, set by GetSlotBlocks).\nOZ source name: AddAvailableFsBlock2.\n1. If a lower block of the same page is free ($DEAD and in the chain, FindPrevBlock), the\nblock is linked in after it.\n2. Else if a higher block of the page is free, it is linked in before it.\n3. Else it becomes the head of the chain.\n4. When all four blocks of the page then follow each other in the chain they are taken out\nand the page is given back with OS_Mfr; an error there hangs (JR to itself).\nEntry: DE = file pointer of the block.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "13235": {"comment":"bind in DE -> BHL"},
        "13240": {"synopsis":"try to add block after lower free block in same page","comment":"previous block"},
        "13242": {"comment":"block_of_page"},
        "13244": {"comment":"!! 'lda a,e' before 'dec e', avoids cp"},
        "13246": {"comment":"page change? skip"},
        "13251": {"comment":"check $DEAD signature"},
        "13252": {"comment":"this is to avoid expensive FindPrevBlock"},
        "13256": {"comment":"not DEAD? in use"},
        "13262": {"comment":"not DEAD? in use"},
        "13264": {"comment":"BC=fsPtr of block pointing to first block on same page as DE"},
        "13267": {"comment":"this block not in chain? in use"},
        "13272": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr this"},
        "13273": {"comment":"HL=memPtr this"},
        "13276": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr next"},
        "13280": {"comment":"HL=memPtr in"},
        "13281": {"comment":"in.next=this.next"},
        "13284": {"comment":"memPtr this"},
        "13285": {"comment":"fsPtr in"},
        "13286": {"comment":"this.next=in"},
        "13291": {"comment":"Fz=1 from FindPrevBlock"},
        "13292": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr in, BC=fsPtr prev"},
        "13293": {"comment":"!! why branch into jr nz? branch after it"},
        "13295": {"comment":"swap stack vars"},
        "13299": {"synopsis":"try to add block before higher free block in same page"},
        "13303": {"comment":"page change? exit"},
        "13308": {"comment":"check $DEAD signature"},
        "13313": {"comment":"in use? check next"},
        "13319": {"comment":"in use? check next"},
        "13324": {"comment":"not found? in use"},
        "13328": {"comment":"fsPtr this"},
        "13329": {"comment":"memPtr in"},
        "13330": {"comment":"in.next=this"},
        "13334": {"comment":"de=prev"},
        "13335": {"comment":"HL=memPtr prev"},
        "13338": {"comment":"de=memPtr, HL=fsPtr"},
        "13339": {"comment":"hl=fsPtr in"},
        "13340": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr in, HL=memPtr prev"},
        "13344": {"comment":"prev.next=in"},
        "13347": {"comment":"BC=fsPtr prev, DE=fsPtr in"},
        "13350": {"synopsis":"no other block from this page, insert ahead of list","comment":"memPtr in"},
        "13358": {"comment":"fsPtr in"},
        "13368": {"comment":"not first block in page? exit"},
        "13370": {"comment":"point filePtr (in) to  first block in page"},
        "13374": {"comment":"prev"},
        "13378": {"comment":"next fsBlock"},
        "13381": {"comment":"doesn't point to next? exit"},
        "13386": {"comment":"doesn't point to next? exit"},
        "13388": {"comment":"!! remove this, add a, $3f"},
        "13390": {"comment":"next block"},
        "13395": {"comment":"not at last block in page? loop"},
        "13397": {"comment":"BC=fsPtr to next"},
        "13400": {"comment":"DE back to first block in page"},
        "13403": {"comment":"HL=fsPtr last"},
        "13404": {"comment":"HL=fsPtr prev"},
        "13405": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr prev"},
        "13407": {"comment":"HL=memPtr prev"},
        "13410": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr next"},
        "13411": {"comment":"bind prev in"},
        "13414": {"comment":"prev.next=next"},
        "13417": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr last"},
        "13418": {"comment":"HL=memPtr last"},
        "13431": {"comment":"Free memory"},
        "13435": {"synopsis":"Hangs in a loop to itself when Fc is set, an error from the call before it.","comment":"error? crash"},
        "13446": {"synopsis":"Entry: DE=fsPtr.\nExit: BC=fsPtr of block pointing to first block on same page as DE.","comment":"BC=in"},
        "13451": {"comment":"DE=1, Fz=0"},
        "13456": {"comment":"end? error"},
        "13460": {"comment":"different bank"},
        "13463": {"comment":"have changed stack? skip"},
        "13465": {"comment":"fsPtr in"},
        "13466": {"comment":"mask out non-page part"},
        "13469": {"comment":"different page"},
        "13471": {"comment":"replace original DE with HL - prev"},
        "13473": {"comment":"pointer to first block on same page as BC"},
        "13477": {"comment":"same block? exit"},
        "13479": {"comment":"HL=fsPtr this, DE=fsPtr next"},
        "13495": {"comment":"BC=prevblock"},
        "13496": {"comment":"Fc=0, keep Fz=1"},
        "13499": {"comment":"DE=fsPtr in"},
        "13505": {"synopsis":"Opens a memory file (OS_Op with OP_MEM) and makes it HL bytes long by seeking there\n(SeekFileMayExpand). A size of 0 opens nothing and returns IX = 0. On an error the file is\nclosed again.\nOZ source name: AllocMemFile_SizeHL.\nEntry: HL = size.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = handle of the memory file (0 for size 0).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "13511": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "13515": {"comment":"BC=0, HL=0"},
        "13520": {"comment":"internal open"},
        "13530": {"comment":"close file/stream"},
        "13535": {"synopsis":"Converts a file pointer into a memory pointer (FilePtr2MemPtr) and falls into fsMS2BankB to\nbind its bank into S2.\nEntry: DE = file pointer.\nExit: BHL = memory pointer, bound in S2; C = 2; the old bindings on the stack, for\nfsRestoreS2.\nKeeps: AF, DE."},
        "13538": {"synopsis":"Binds bank B into S2 and leaves the previous S1 and S2 bindings on the stack under the\nreturn address; the caller must call fsRestoreS2 before it returns.\nEntry: B = bank.\nExit: (SP) = previous S1 and S2 bindings.\nChanges: AF', HL'.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "13541": {"comment":"S1S2"},
        "13544": {"comment":"push it, pop return address"},
        "13548": {"comment":"return address"},
        "13550": {"comment":"old bank"},
        "13553": {"synopsis":"Stores DE at (HL) and (HL + 1), the link of a bound block, and falls into fsRestoreS2.\nOZ source name: fsLinkHL_DE_RestoreS2.\nEntry: HL = memory pointer of the link; DE = file pointer; bindings left by fsMS2BankB.\nExit: as fsRestoreS2; L = L + 1."},
        "13556": {"synopsis":"Undoes fsMS2BankB: pops the saved bindings word under the return address and binds the saved\nS2 bank again.\nEntry: (SP + 2) = bindings saved by fsMS2BankB.\nExit: B = the S2 bank bound again.\nChanges: B, AF', HL'.\nKeeps: AF, C, DE, HL."},
        "13562": {"synopsis":"write identifier A, length BC, and BC bytes of data from (HL)","comment":"HL=local"},
        "13564": {"comment":"A=type"},
        "13578": {"synopsis":"write BC bytes from (DHL)"},
        "13643": {"synopsis":"Entry inside MoveToFromFile that moves BC bytes between the file's current position and a\nbuffer inside one 16K segment, block by block. The buffer is bound into S1: a far buffer by\nits bank, a local one by the bank its segment has (S2 and S3 from the caller's OS frame);\nthe file blocks are bound into S2. A write extends the last block and allocates new blocks\n(AllocHandleBlock). The S1 and S2 bindings are restored.\nEntry: DHL = buffer (D = 0 for a local address); BC = count; IX = file handle; Fc of F' = 1\nto write, 0 to read; IY = OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = HL + bytes moved; BC = bytes not moved.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Eof (read past the end) or AllocHandleBlock's error.\nKeeps: DE, IY."},
        "13648": {"comment":"far ptr"},
        "13652": {"comment":"kernel space, bind in S1"},
        "13656": {"comment":"S0, no binding"},
        "13658": {"comment":"S1 bank into S2"},
        "13663": {"comment":"A14 selects S2/S3 bank"},
        "13673": {"comment":"store bank"},
        "13674": {"comment":"S2 fix"},
        "13680": {"comment":"remember S1/S2"},
        "13686": {"comment":"IY=BC"},
        "13689": {"comment":"buffer in S1"},
