        "13831": {"comment":"read? HL->DE"},
        "13833": {"comment":"write? DE-HL"},
        "13836": {"comment":"read? skip"},
        "13838": {"comment":"restore HL/DE"},
        "13839": {"comment":"has next block? skip"},
        "13845": {"comment":"store r/w flag"},
        "13846": {"comment":"store new position"},
        "13849": {"comment":"bytes left to read/write"},
        "13857": {"comment":"into IY"},
        "13859": {"comment":"done? exit"},
        "13861": {"comment":"handle next block"},
        "13924": {"synopsis":"compare next byte of stream with A\nif match, read length into BC and read that many bytes to (HL)","comment":"HL=local"},
        "13933": {"comment":"Unexpected type *"},
        "13946": {"synopsis":"move BC bytes to (HL)"},
        "13950": {"synopsis":"Saves an application's state into a new process handle (AllocHandle HND_PROC) holding a\nmemory file: record $A0 with the application variables (SaveAppVars), record $A1 with the\nstack from pAppStackPtr to pAppUnSafeArea, the screen (SaveScreen) when the application has\nAT_Draw, then the end mark $00 $0E $0F.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = process handle.\nError: jumps to FreeMemHandle to free the handle."},
        "13960": {"comment":"save app variables"},
        "13976": {"comment":"A1 - stack"},
        "13978": {"comment":"!! ex de,hl"},
        "13986": {"comment":"save screen if needed"},
        "13995": {"comment":"get application data"},
        "14008": {"comment":"write end mark - 00 0E 0F"},
        "14034": {"synopsis":"Restores an application's state saved by SaveAllAppData: rewinds the process file, reads the\nvariables (LoadAppVars), the stack (record $A1), the screen when the application has\nAT_Draw, and checks the end mark. Any failure jumps to OZwd__fail. The first end-mark byte\nis not checked (OR A clears Fc before its JR C).\nOZ source name: RestoreAllAppData.\nEntry: IX = process handle.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = 1, Fz = 0 when the screen was restored; A = 0, Fz = 1 when not."},
        "14042": {"comment":"error? fail"},
        "14044": {"comment":"BC=size of saved stack"},
        "14055": {"comment":"A1 - stack"},
        "14074": {"comment":"enquire (fetch) parameter"},
        "14090": {"comment":"check tail bytes - 00 0E 0F"},
        "14094": {"comment":"!! bug? jr nz?"},
        "14116": {"synopsis":"Writes the application's static handle low byte into a saved process: rewinds the file and\noverwrites the first byte of the $A0 record's data (after type and length).\nOZ source name: UpdateAppStaticHnd.\nEntry: IX = process handle; C = low byte of the application's static handle.\nExit: as WrFileByte."},
        "14123": {"comment":"app static handle is first byte after type, length (2 bytes)"},
        "14134": {"synopsis":"Writes record $A0: the $40 bytes of application variables from uwAppStaticHnd\n(WrHeaderedData).\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: as WrHeaderedData.","comment":"A0 - app vars"},
        "14145": {"synopsis":"Reads record $A0 back into the $40 bytes of application variables at uwAppStaticHnd\n(RdHeaderedData).\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: as RdHeaderedData (Fc = 1, A = RC_Type when the next record is not $A0).","comment":"A0 - app vars"},
        "14156": {"synopsis":"Tells whether a memory file is at its end: compares the position with the byte count of the\ncurrent block and, at the end of a full block, looks at the next block. The block's bank is\nleft bound in S2.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: Fc = 0 when bytes are left.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Eof at the end of the file.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14162": {"comment":"DE=next"},
        "14168": {"comment":"last block? use size from block"},
        "14181": {"comment":"pos<num, no EOF"},
        "14182": {"comment":"!! just jr nz,EOFcode below"},
        "14184": {"comment":"!! unnecessary"},
        "14185": {"comment":"pos>num? EOF"},
        "14188": {"comment":"last block, pos=num? EOF"},
        "14195": {"comment":"next has bytes? not EOF"},
        "14200": {"synopsis":"Exit: DEHL=size."},
        "14221": {"synopsis":"Exit: DEHL."},
        "14227": {"comment":"are we in current block yet?"},
        "14231": {"comment":"no, bump size and go to next"},
        "14237": {"comment":"current block"},
        "14244": {"comment":"last block,  still not current"},
        "14265": {"synopsis":"Adds FSBLOCK_SIZE (62) to the 32-bit counter DE'HL', falling into Add_dehl_A.\nEntry: DE'HL' = counter.\nExit: DE'HL' = DE'HL' + 62.\nChanges: AF, BC'."},
        "14267": {"synopsis":"Adds A to the 32-bit counter in the alternate registers DE'HL'.\nEntry: A = value; DE'HL' = counter.\nExit: DE'HL' = DE'HL' + A.\nChanges: F, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: A."},
        "14279": {"synopsis":"Subtracts FSBLOCK_SIZE (62) from the 32-bit counter DE'HL', falling into Sub_dehl_A.\nExit: as Sub_dehl_A."},
        "14281": {"synopsis":"Subtracts A from the 32-bit counter in the alternate registers DE'HL'.\nEntry: A = value; DE'HL' = counter.\nExit: DE'HL' = DE'HL' - A; A = new L'; Fc = 1 when the result went below zero.\nChanges: AF, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "14296": {"synopsis":"Starts a walk through a file's blocks: DE = the handle's first block, DE'HL' = 0.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: DE = file pointer of the first block; DE'HL' = 0.\nChanges: DE, DE', HL'.","comment":"!! reorder instructions so SeekFile() can use them"},
        "14302": {"comment":"dehl'=0"},
        "14310": {"synopsis":"Moves the file position to DEHL (SeekFile); when that is past the end, the file is extended\nby the missing bytes (ExpandFile).\nOZ source name: SeekFileMayExpand.\nEntry: IX = file handle; DEHL = position.\nExit: Fc = 0, position set.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Wp, or the write's error)."},
        "14316": {"synopsis":"Entry: DEHL=new size."},
        "14345": {"synopsis":"Extends a memory file at its end by DE'HL' bytes, writing filler in pieces of 32 bytes\n(expf_3).\nEntry: IX = file handle, positioned at the end; DE'HL' = bytes to add.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Wp when the file is not writable, or the write's error."},
        "14349": {"comment":"Write protected"},
        "14358": {"comment":"less than 32 bytes to expand"},
        "14360": {"comment":"write 32 bytes"},
        "14372": {"comment":"no error? loop"},
        "14375": {"comment":"number of bytes remaining"},
        "14380": {"synopsis":"Entry inside ExpandFile that writes BC bytes of filler with MvToFile from D = $10, HL =\nbyte_F843 (a far pointer: bank $10, the address taken into S1).\nEntry: BC = count (up to 32); IX = file handle.\nExit: as MvToFile."},
        "14388": {"synopsis":"32 bytes of $3F, the filler ExpandFile means to write into new file space (expf_3 points at\nit, but with bank $10; see the notes)."},
        "14420": {"synopsis":"Entry: DEHL=position."},
        "14434": {"comment":"update position block"},
        "14443": {"comment":"DE=next"},
        "14449": {"comment":"not end, advance one block"},
        "14451": {"comment":"substract last bytes"},
        "14455": {"comment":"still not wanted position? EOF"},
        "14457": {"synopsis":"Entry inside SeekFile that sets the position's low byte to L + A + E + 2: the block start,\nA, the last block's byte count E and the 2 link bytes. Called with A = 0 to put the position\nafter the last byte of the file.\nEntry: IX = file handle; A = bytes; E = byte count of the last block; L = block start.\nExit: Fc = 0; (ix+fhnd_filepos_lo) set.","comment":"+last bytes"},
        "14458": {"comment":"+2 to skip header"},
        "14461": {"comment":"put position low byte"},
        "14471": {"comment":"set position to the last byte"},
        "14478": {"synopsis":"Writes a byte at the file's position and advances it; writing past the last byte extends the\nlast block, and at the end of a block fsmv_4 moves into (or allocates) the next one.\nEntry: IX = file handle; A = byte.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (no room for a new block).\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Fc=1, write into file"},
        "14481": {"synopsis":"Reads the byte at the file's position and advances it; at the end of a block fsmv_4 moves\ninto the next one.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Eof at the end of the file.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Fc=0, read from file"},
        "14486": {"comment":"BHL=mem ptr"},
        "14489": {"comment":"!! pop this after binding, looks better :)"},
        "14490": {"comment":"bind mem in"},
        "14499": {"comment":"end of block? handle"},
        "14505": {"comment":"not last block? skip"},
        "14512": {"comment":"A=#databytes"},
        "14515": {"comment":"not past end? skip"},
        "14518": {"comment":"read request? EOF"},
        "14520": {"comment":"increment size of last block"},
        "14522": {"comment":"get block pointer"},
        "14525": {"comment":"and increment it"},
        "14528": {"comment":"read byte from file"},
        "14530": {"comment":"read request? skip write"},
        "14533": {"comment":"return written byte"},
        "14552": {"comment":"remember char"},
        "14553": {"comment":"r/w flag into f'"},
        "14554": {"comment":"read/write one byte"},
        "14557": {"comment":"from DHL"},
        "14564": {"comment":"restore char"},
        "14569": {"synopsis":"Fatal error display: shows FAIL flashing in the first row of the OZ window and loops here\nfor ever. Reached by a jump when the system state cannot be trusted.\nEntry: none.\nExit: never returns."},
        "14583": {"synopsis":"Shows CARD flashing in the first row of the OZ window, with the screen bound in S1 for the\nwrite (ScreenOpen, ScreenClose).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "14588": {"synopsis":"Shows INDEX flashing in the first row of the OZ window, with the screen bound in S1 for the\nwrite (ScreenOpen, ScreenClose).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "14604": {"synopsis":"Redraws the OZ window, the right edge of the screen, and acknowledges the refresh request\n(ITSK_B_OZWINDOW).\n1. Row 1: OZ in grey, or LOCKOUT flashing when the keyboard is locked.\n2. Row 2: the keymap's country letters; row 3: CLI flashing while a CLI runs; row 4: the\nbell while an alarm is shown.\n3. Rows 6 and 7: BAT LOW when the battery is low; row 8: the CAPS state.\n4. Rows 5 to 8: the dead key, or the [] or <> symbol and up to 4 typed command characters,\ngrey while a command is active.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14610": {"comment":"ack OZWd refresh"},
        "14615": {"comment":"show \"lock out\" if locked"},
        "14637": {"synopsis":"Country (line 2)"},
        "14669": {"synopsis":"BELL (line 4)"},
        "14689": {"synopsis":"BATLOW (lines 6 and 7)"},
        "14707": {"comment":"get attributes, grey if <> or [] active"},
        "14756": {"comment":"default char is a space in OZ font (8 bits width)"},
        "14767": {"comment":"'[]'"},
        "14773": {"comment":"'<>'"},
        "14784": {"comment":"column 2 in OZ window"},
        "14791": {"comment":"cmd char"},
        "14793": {"comment":"end of command? exit"},
        "14795": {"comment":"into char"},
        "14797": {"comment":"onto screen"},
        "14802": {"comment":"next char"},
        "14803": {"comment":"next line"},
        "14809": {"comment":"Fc=0, why?"},
        "14811": {"synopsis":"Tells whether an OZ command is shown: <> or [] pending, or a character in OZcmdBuf below\n$80, and gives the attribute to draw with.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = grey attribute when a command is active; Fc = 1, A = normal attribute\n(LCDA_HIRES, LCDA_UNDERLINE, LCDA_CH8) when not; HL = OZcmdBuf.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "14814": {"comment":"<> or [] in OZ wd"},
        "14819": {"comment":"char in the 00-127 range"},
        "14823": {"comment":"Fz=1"},
        "14824": {"comment":"ret with Fc=1 and A screen attributes"},
        "14826": {"comment":"first app/command char"},
        "14830": {"comment":"Fc=1 if no command"},
        "14831": {"comment":"Fc=0 if command"},
        "14834": {"synopsis":"Writes the blank character pair (OZW_BLANK) in the normal attribute; falls into OZwd_write.\nEntry: HL = screen address of an OZ window row.\nExit: as VDUputBCA.\nChanges: A, BC, L."},
        "14837": {"synopsis":"Writes character pair BC in the normal OZ window attribute; falls into VDUputBCA.\nEntry: HL = screen address; BC = characters.\nChanges: A, L."},
        "14839": {"synopsis":"Writes two characters with their attribute into screen memory: B, A, C, A.\nEntry: HL = screen address; B, C = characters; A = attribute.\nExit: L = L + 3.\nChanges: L."},
        "14847": {"synopsis":"Writes character pair BC in the grey OZ window attribute (VDUputBCA).\nEntry: HL = screen address; BC = characters.\nChanges: A, L."},
        "14851": {"synopsis":"Writes two characters to the OZ window, flashing: loads A with the hires, flash, underline\nand CH8 attributes and jumps to VDUputBCA. The screen must be bound in (ScreenOpen).\nEntry: HL = screen address of the character cell; B = first character; C = second character.\nExit: (HL) = B, (HL+2) = C, both with the attribute in the following byte; L advanced by 3.\nChanges: A, L."},
        "14855": {"synopsis":"request OZ window redraw"},
        "14861": {"synopsis":"bind screen into S1, $7800-$7fff"},
        "14873": {"synopsis":"Undoes ScreenOpen: takes the return address and the S1 binding that ScreenOpen pushed from\nthe stack and binds that bank into segment 1 again through MS1BankA. Must be called at the\nsame stack level as the ScreenOpen it closes.\nEntry: the stack holds the S1 bank (and flags) that ScreenOpen saved.\nExit: segment 1 bound as before ScreenOpen; A = that bank; F as it was at ScreenOpen.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "14877": {"synopsis":"move to x,y","comment":"C=first arg, B=second arg"},
        "14888": {"synopsis":"search attribute table, return\ntHiLo in DE, ~tHiLo in BC\nOZ source name: ScrDrvGetAttrBits.\nChanges: F, BC, DE."},
        "14908": {"comment":"tLo"},
        "14910": {"comment":"~tLo"},
        "14913": {"comment":"tHi"},
        "14915": {"comment":"~tHi"},
        "14919": {"synopsis":"Exit: Fc=0, DE=func; Fc=1, not found."},
        "14932": {"comment":"c,b = command"},
        "14936": {"comment":"not found Fc=1"},
        "14961": {"synopsis":"set attributes","comment":"E=-1"},
        "14962": {"synopsis":"reset attributes"},
        "14976": {"comment":"if E=0 then just mask flags"},
        "14982": {"comment":"no toggle bits"},
        "14991": {"synopsis":"ToggleScrDrvFlags: applies an attribute letter's masks and toggle bits to the window's\nflags: flagsLo = (flagsLo AND C) XOR E and flagsHi = (flagsHi AND B) XOR D. Characters that\nare not letters are ignored.\nOZ source name: ToggleScrDrvFlags.\nEntry: A = attribute character; BC = keep masks (high, low); DE = toggle bits (high, low),\nas ScrDrvGetAttrBts returns them; IX = window frame.\nExit: Fc = 0, window flags updated; A = new flagsHi.\nError: Fc = 1 when A is not a letter (nothing changed).\nChanges: AF, AF'."},
        "14994": {"comment":"not alpha"},
        "14999": {"comment":"tLo"},
        "15007": {"comment":"tHi"},
        "15012": {"synopsis":"call function with following parameters:\nA,B,C - first 3 VDU arguments-$20\nE - 0\nFc=1"},
        "15017": {"comment":"arg3"},
        "15023": {"comment":"arg2"},
        "15027": {"comment":"arg1"},
        "15034": {"synopsis":"Box Characters","comment":"$01-0F"},
        "15036": {"comment":"$81-8F"},
        "15038": {"comment":"LORES $181-$18F"},
        "15044": {"synopsis":"Carriage return (CR) of the screen driver: moves the cursor to the window's first column.\nEntry: IX = window frame; HL = cursor position (H line, L byte offset in the line).\nExit: L = the window's start column (wdf_startx).\nChanges: L."},
        "15048": {"synopsis":"cursor backwards\n\nFc=0 if no line change"},
        "15060": {"comment":"need scrolling"},
        "15062": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: bs_1."},
        "15067": {"comment":"left edge? previous line"},
        "15070": {"comment":"attributes"},
        "15076": {"comment":"null char? backspace again"},
        "15078": {"comment":"Fc=0, Fz=1"},
        "15080": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: bs_2.","comment":"end of line"},
        "15083": {"comment":"previous line"},
        "15086": {"comment":"Fc=1"},
        "15100": {"comment":"bytes to copy"},
        "15101": {"comment":"test direction"},
        "15104": {"comment":"B=0"},
        "15108": {"comment":"move chars right"},
        "15115": {"comment":"move chars left"},
        "15117": {"comment":"put $000, space"},
        "15124": {"synopsis":"advance cursor\n\nFc=0 if no line change"},
        "15136": {"comment":"need scrolling"},
        "15141": {"comment":"right edge? next line"},
        "15146": {"comment":"attributes"},
        "15152": {"comment":"null? forward again"},
        "15157": {"comment":"x ok, return Fc=0"},
        "15158": {"comment":"start of line"},
        "15161": {"comment":"next line"},
        "15164": {"comment":"Fc=1"},
        "15166": {"synopsis":"previous line"},
        "15175": {"comment":"Fc=0, no scrolling"},
        "15186": {"comment":"Fc=1, screen scrolled"},
        "15188": {"comment":"wrap to last line"},
        "15191": {"comment":"Fc=1, wrap"},
        "15193": {"synopsis":"Line feed of the screen driver: moves the cursor down one line. ScrollLock first holds the\noutput while the scroll-lock keys are down. Past the last line the window scrolls up (after\na Delay300Kclocks pause when the window's delay flag is set) if vertical scrolling is on,\notherwise the cursor wraps to the first line.\nEntry: IX = window frame; HL = cursor position (H line, L byte offset).\nExit: Fc = 0, moved down within the window; Fc = 1, the window scrolled or the cursor\nwrapped; H = new line.\nChanges: AF, H; BC, DE when the window scrolls."},
        "15202": {"comment":"Fc=0, no wrap/scroll"},
        "15221": {"comment":"scroll up"},
        "15224": {"comment":"Fc=1, scroll"},
        "15226": {"comment":"wrap to first line"},
        "15229": {"comment":"Fc=1, wrap"},
        "15231": {"synopsis":"freeze output if <> and lshift down","comment":"row6"},
        "15235": {"comment":"check for sh-l and <>"},
        "15240": {"synopsis":"clear to EOW"},
        "15246": {"synopsis":"Form feed (FF), clears the window: draws the side borders when the window has them\n(WdBorders), resets the control prefix (Zero_ctrlprefix), puts the cursor at the top left\nand falls into ClearEOWm.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: window cleared; HL = window start (H = first line, L = first column).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "15260": {"synopsis":"Clears from the cursor to the end of the window, line by line through ceol_1, moving to the\nnext line with CursorDown while vertical scrolling is switched off; when the cursor wraps it\nfalls into GetWdStartXY. The fill is a space in the window's colours (sub_FD8B), or, when\nopen-flag bit 6 is set, character $A0 in hires (and $FF in reverse, flash and grey when bit\n5 is set too).\nEntry: IX = window frame; HL = cursor position.\nExit: HL = window start (first line, first column).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "15304": {"synopsis":"Returns the window's top-left position.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: H = first line (wdf_starty); L = first column (wdf_startx).\nChanges: HL."},
        "15311": {"synopsis":"Clears from the cursor to the end of the line with a space in the window's colours: sets BC\nfrom sub_FD8B and falls into ceol_1.\nEntry: IX = window frame; HL = cursor position.\nExit: Fc = 0, line cleared; HL unchanged.\nError: Fc = 1 when HL is outside the window (nothing written).\nChanges: AF, BC, E."},
        "15314": {"synopsis":"Entry inside ClearEOL: fills the line from the cursor to the window's last column with the\ncharacter and attribute in BC. When the window's grey or ungrey open flag is set (during +G\nor -G) it rewrites the existing characters with their attribute greyed or ungreyed instead;\nopen-flag bits 6 and 5 select the pattern fill that ClearEOWm uses.\nEntry: IX = window frame; HL = cursor position; C = character; B = attribute.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1; HL unchanged.\nError: Fc = 1 when HL is outside the window (nothing written).\nChanges: AF, BC, E."},
        "15326": {"comment":"left offset"},
        "15329": {"comment":"check mod(xpos,4)=0"},
        "15349": {"comment":"increment char"},
        "15356": {"comment":"char"},
        "15358": {"comment":"attrs"},
        "15377": {"comment":"char"},
        "15379": {"comment":"attr"},
        "15389": {"comment":"~LCDA_TINY"},
        "15418": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window up one line: copies each line from the second to the last one line up\n(su_2), clears the last line (ClearEOL), then moves the cursor up one line unless that would\nleave the window.\nEntry: IX = window frame; HL = cursor position.\nExit: Fc = 0; H = the cursor's line, one less when still inside the window; L unchanged.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, H."},
        "15444": {"synopsis":"Step of ScrollUp: copies line H of the window onto line H-1 (from the first column, the\nwindow's width plus one character, attributes included) when both lines are inside it.\nEntry: IX = window frame; H = source line.\nExit: Fc = 0, line copied; Fc = 1, line H or H-1 is outside the window (nothing copied); H\nunchanged.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, L."},
        "15472": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the window down one line: copies each line from the last but one to the first one\nline down (sd_2), clears the first line (ClearEOL), then moves the cursor down one line\nunless that would leave the window.\nEntry: IX = window frame; HL = cursor position.\nExit: Fc = 0; H = the cursor's line, one more when still inside the window; L unchanged.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, H."},
        "15498": {"synopsis":"Step of ScrollDown: copies line H of the window onto line H+1 (from the first column, the\nwindow's width plus one character, attributes included) when both lines are inside it.\nEntry: IX = window frame; H = source line.\nExit: Fc = 0, line copied; Fc = 1, line H or H+1 is outside the window (nothing copied); H\nunchanged.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, L.","comment":"!! add hl,bc etc to re-use code"},
        "15517": {"comment":"width"},
        "15526": {"synopsis":"Returns the window's bottom-right position.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: H = last line (wdf_endy); L = last column (wdf_endx).\nChanges: HL."},
        "15533": {"synopsis":"Returns the fill used to clear the window: character 0 with the window's reverse, flash,\ngrey and underline attributes.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: B = attribute (wdf_flagsLo masked); C = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "15542": {"synopsis":"Draws the window's side borders: a vertical bar (character $18A) one character left and one\ncharacter right of every line. When the brackets flag is set, the first line gets the shelf\nbrackets ($1BE on the left, $1BF on the right) instead of the bars.\nEntry: IX = window frame; C = the window's open flags (wdf_OpenFlags).\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "15549": {"comment":"height"},
        "15551": {"comment":"!! stupidity, ld l,wdf_startx here"},
        "15554": {"comment":"left one char"},
        "15556": {"comment":"last line"},
        "15559": {"comment":"VDU $18A, vertical bar"},
        "15565": {"comment":"previous line"},
        "15570": {"comment":"no brackets"},
        "15572": {"comment":"1st line"},
        "15573": {"comment":"VDU $1BE, window left bracket"},
        "15582": {"comment":"right one char"},
        "15584": {"comment":"VDU $18A, vertical bar"},
        "15590": {"comment":"previous line"},
        "15595": {"comment":"no brackets"},
        "15596": {"comment":"last line"},
        "15597": {"comment":"VDU $1BF, window right bracket"},
        "15603": {"synopsis":"Checks that the cursor position is inside the window: tests the line (NewYValid) and then\nfalls into NewXValid for the column.\nEntry: IX = window frame; H = line; L = column byte offset.\nExit: Fc = 0 when both are inside the window; Fc = 1 otherwise.\nChanges: AF."},
        "15607": {"synopsis":"Fc=0 if L inside window"},
        "15608": {"comment":"Fc=1 if L<StartX"},
        "15615": {"comment":"Fc=0 if L<=EndX  !! ret z; ccf; ret"},
        "15620": {"synopsis":"Fc=0 if H inside window"},
        "15621": {"comment":"Fc=1 if H<StartY"},
        "15628": {"comment":"Fc=0 if H<=EndY  !! ret z; ccf; ret"},
        "15633": {"synopsis":"Beep sequence (VDU)"},
        "15642": {"comment":"Fc=1 if A=0"},
        "15644": {"comment":"A=2*A, 1 if A was 0"},
        "15649": {"comment":"sound count"},
        "15651": {"comment":"space count"},
        "15653": {"comment":"mark count"},
        "15661": {"synopsis":"Sounds two bleeps (OS_Blp with A = 2, B = 5, C = 10).\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "15670": {"synopsis":"Bell (BEL) of the screen driver: sounds one bleep (OS_Blp with A = 1, B = 0, C = 20).\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "15677": {"comment":"Bleep"},
        "15683": {"synopsis":"Save & Restore"},
        "15689": {"comment":"in kernel 1"},
        "15695": {"synopsis":"Restores the screen from a file: sets E = 0 (read) and falls into SrScreen, which binds the\nscreen in, reads 8 blocks of type $A3 of 228 bytes each (the 114 characters of a line after\nthe first 10) into the screen lines with RdHeaderedData, redraws the OZ window (DrawOZwd)\nand restores the S1 binding.\nEntry: the filing-system stream that RdHeaderedData reads is set up by the caller.\nExit: Fc = 0, screen restored.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Type when a block has the wrong type)."},
        "15699": {"synopsis":"Saves the screen to a file: sets E = $FF (write) and falls into SrScreen, which binds the\nscreen in and writes the 8 lines as blocks of type $A3 of 228 bytes each (the 114 characters\nafter the first 10) with WrHeaderedData, redraws the OZ window and restores the S1 binding.\nEntry: the filing-system stream that WrHeaderedData writes is set up by the caller.\nExit: Fc = 0, screen saved.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "15704": {"comment":"address high byte"},
        "15706": {"comment":"lines to do"},
        "15710": {"comment":"this type"},
        "15712": {"comment":"this many bytes"},
        "15715": {"comment":"address low byte - skip 10 chars"},
        "15724": {"comment":"next line"},
        "15737": {"synopsis":"Reads or writes one headered block for SrScreen: WrHeaderedData when E = $FF, RdHeaderedData\nwhen E = 0.\nEntry: E = $FF (write) or 0 (read); A = block type; BC = length; HL = local address.\nExit: Fc = 0, block transferred.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "16182": {"comment":"Os_Ugb"},
        "16266": {"comment":"$8A"},
        "16269": {"comment":"$8D"},
        "16272": {"comment":"$90"},
        "16275": {"comment":"$93"},
        "16278": {"comment":"$96"},
        "16284": {"comment":"end at $003F9E"},
        "16318": {"comment":"$BE"},
        "16320": {"comment":"$C0"},
        "16322": {"comment":"$C2"},
        "16324": {"comment":"$C4"},
        "16326": {"comment":"$C6"},
        "16380": {"comment":"$FC06"},
        "16382": {"comment":"$FE06"}
      }
    },
