      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"granularity table used by OSSci\n! must start a page in kernel 1 !","comment":"#low bits ignored"},
        "6": {"synopsis":"alter screen information\nEntry: A=reason code; SC_LR0 LORES0 (512 bytes granularity, 13 bits width); SC_LR1 LORES1\n(4K granularity, 10 bits width); SC_HR0 HIRES0 (8K granularity, 9 bits width); SC_HR1 HIRES1\n(2K granularity, 11 bits width); SC_SBR screen base (2K granularity, 11 bits width); B=0,\nget pointer address; B<>0, set pointer address.\nExit: Fc=0, BHL = old pointer address; Fc=1, A=error if fail.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "10": {"synopsis":"OS_Sci: alters the screen information, the base addresses of LORES0, LORES1, HIRES0, HIRES1\nand the screen base file. The address in BHL is reduced to the Blink register value by the\nreason's granularity (OSSciTable), the old value is read from the soft copies at $046x and\n$047x and returned, and the new one is written when B is not 0. Setting the screen base also\nreinitialises the screen: windows 7 and 8, the application window and the OZ window are set\nup again.\nEntry: A = reason (SC_LR0, SC_LR1, SC_HR0, SC_HR1 or SC_SBR); B = 0 to read, otherwise BHL =\nnew address.\nExit: Fc = 0; BHL = old address (in the caller's OS frame).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail (reason not 1-5).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "11": {"comment":"A = 0, bad reason"},
        "15": {"comment":"A > 5, bad reason"},
        "24": {"comment":"BLINK register"},
        "25": {"comment":"granularity"},
        "29": {"comment":"shift count, B=0 status"},
        "30": {"comment":"H<<2, get rid of segment bits"},
        "34": {"comment":"BH>>A"},
        "41": {"comment":"B=0 status"},
        "43": {"comment":"AB=blink value"},
        "44": {"comment":"HL=$047x"},
        "47": {"comment":"old value into DE"},
        "48": {"comment":"$046x"},
        "50": {"comment":"old value"},
        "51": {"comment":"B=0? don't set"},
        "53": {"comment":"$047x"},
        "56": {"comment":"$046x"},
        "61": {"comment":"blink register"},
        "63": {"comment":"B=shift count"},
        "67": {"comment":"normalize HL"},
        "82": {"comment":"screen base reg."},
        "84": {"comment":"not SBR? exit"},
        "85": {"comment":"B=0"},
        "87": {"comment":"read only? exit"},
        "88": {"comment":"init screen"},
        "106": {"comment":"window 8 @+104,0 4x8 $40"},
        "115": {"comment":"select & clear 8"},
        "119": {"comment":"window 7 @+0,0 10x8"},
        "147": {"synopsis":"entries in descending order\nlow limit, meta key, key table"},
        "201": {"synopsis":"length mask, character codes\nCareful - can't cross page boundary","comment":"cursor keys"},
        "206": {"synopsis":"Key2MetaTable's character list for the special keys: a mask byte (7) and the 8 meta letters\n\" ETX?MIH\" (Enter, Tab, Del, Esc, Menu, Index, Help per the source). Key2Meta masks the key\ncode with the mask byte and picks the letter.","comment":"enter tab del (esc) menu index help"},
        "215": {"synopsis":"Key2MetaTable's character list for control characters: a mask byte ($1F) and 32 meta\ncharacters, \"=\", \"A\"-\"Z\", \"[\", \"\\\", \"]\", the pound sign ($A3) and \"-\". Key2Meta masks the\nkey code with the mask byte and picks the character.","comment":"control chars"},
        "243": {"comment":"[\\]ï¿½-"},
        "248": {"synopsis":"Key2MetaTable's character list for the CTRL key itself: a mask byte (0) and \"C\".","comment":"ctrl"},
        "250": {"synopsis":"Key2MetaTable's character list for the ALT key itself: a mask byte (0) and \"A\".","comment":"alt"},
        "252": {"synopsis":"End of Key2MetaTable (the source checks that the table stays in one page). The same address\nstarts CLI2KeyTable, used by CLIchar2key: a length byte (24) and 12 pairs of a letter after\n\"~\" in a CLI string and its key code (D down, E enter, H help, I index, L left, M menu, R\nright, T tab, U up, X del, C ctrl, A alt).\nOZ source name: Key2MetaTable_end.","comment":"table length"},
        "253": {"comment":"D down"},
        "255": {"comment":"E enter"},
        "257": {"comment":"H help"},
        "259": {"comment":"I index"},
        "261": {"comment":"L left"},
        "263": {"comment":"M menu"},
        "265": {"comment":"R right"},
        "267": {"comment":"T tab"},
        "269": {"comment":"U up"},
        "271": {"comment":"X del"},
        "273": {"comment":"C ctrl"},
        "275": {"comment":"A alt"},
        "277": {"synopsis":"On entry: we have OSFrame so remembering S2 is unnecessary, as is remembering IY"},
        "281": {"comment":"add reason"},
        "285": {"comment":"adjust for page crossing."},
        "286": {"comment":"restore hl and push address"},
        "287": {"comment":"goto reason"},
