        "1237": {"comment":"write"},
        "1239": {"synopsis":"Clears bits in the Blink COM register: complements the mask, ANDs it into the soft copy\nBLSC_COM with interrupts disabled (chgcom_1), writes the soft copy and BL_COM, and enables\ninterrupts again.\nEntry: A = bits to clear.\nExit: A = new COM value; interrupts enabled.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"reverse bit mask"},
        "1241": {"comment":"get old bits"},
        "1244": {"comment":"and out new ones"},
        "1253": {"synopsis":"Shared step of OrCom and AndCom: disables interrupts (so that slot polling cannot run while\na byte is blown) and reads the COM soft copy.\nEntry: A = new bits.\nExit: B = new bits; A = BLSC_COM; interrupts disabled.\nChanges: A, B.","comment":"new bits into B"},
        "1254": {"comment":"avoid slot polling during blowing of byte"},
        "1255": {"comment":"old bits into A"},
        "1259": {"synopsis":"Makes a caller's local pointer reachable in segment 1: a pointer in segment 2 or 3 has the\ncaller's S2 or S3 bank (from the OS frame) bound into S1 and is moved into S1; a pointer\nbelow $8000 is taken to be in S1 already and the S1 binding is only read (OZ_MGB).\nEntry: HL = caller's local pointer; IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = the pointer in segment 1; B = previous S1 bank (to restore with OZ_MPB); C =\nMS_S1.\nChanges: B, C, HL."},
        "1261": {"comment":"caller local address is in segment 01 already"},
        "1263": {"comment":"caller local address = 1?......"},
        "1268": {"comment":"Bind caller local address = 10...... (segment 2) into s1"},
        "1270": {"comment":"Bind caller local address = 11...... (segment 3) into s1"},
        "1273": {"comment":"modify local pointer to be in S1"},
        "1279": {"comment":"bind into local address space in segment 1"},
        "1283": {"comment":"get current S1 binding"},
        "1286": {"synopsis":"Sub types, used to define UV programming method in slot 3:\n7E: 32K               01111110\n7C: 128K, 256K        01111100\n7A: Unknown           01111010\nFlash sub types (returned as abstractions in OS_Epr, EP_Req), only used to differentiate that it\nis not an UV Eprom (not in this table for UV Eprom only):\n77: Intel Flash       01110111\n6F: AMD Flash         01101111","comment":"subtype"},
        "1287": {"comment":"BL_EPR before data byte, prefixed by following"},
        "1288": {"comment":"ORed into BL_COM"},
        "1289": {"comment":"BL_EPR after data byte, prefixed by following"},
        "1290": {"comment":"ORed into BL_COM"},
        "1291": {"comment":"BL_EPR before overwrite, prefixed by following"},
        "1292": {"comment":"ORed into BL_COM"},
        "1308": {"synopsis":"Switch Z88 LCD Screen On or Off.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Aug 2006\nEntry: Fz = 1, Turn LCD screen On; Fz = 0, Turn LCD screen Off.\nExit: None.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "1310": {"comment":"Address of soft copy of COM register"},
        "1314": {"comment":"Screen LCD Off by default"},
        "1316": {"comment":"but caller wants to switch On..."},
        "1320": {"comment":"signal to Blink COM register to do the LCD..."},
        "1325": {"synopsis":"Entry inside SetBlinkScreen, called when Fz = 1: sets the LCD-on bit (BB_COMLCDON) in A.\nEntry: A = COM register value.\nExit: A with the LCD-on bit set.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Screen LCD On"},
        "1328": {"synopsis":"Switches the LCD on: calls SetBlinkScreen with Fz = 1, which sets the LCD-on bit in the COM\nsoft copy and the Blink COM register. Used after blowing or erasing flash.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "1335": {"synopsis":"Evaluate Standard Z88 Application ROM Format (Front DOR/ROM Header).\n\nReturn Standard Application ROM \"OZ\" status in slot x (0, 1, 2 or 3).\n\nFailure:\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF, Application Eprom not found\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Apr-Aug 1998, Aug 2006, Aug 2012\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3).\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0,; A = Application Eprom type (with Rom Front Dor):; $80 = external\nEPROM,; $81 = system/internal OZ ROM,; $82 = external RAM; B = size of reserved Application\nspace in 16K banks.; C = size of physical Application Card in 16K banks.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "1337": {"comment":"slot C"},
        "1340": {"comment":"top 256 byte page of top bank in slot C"},
        "1343": {"comment":"Convert to physical pointer..."},
        "1351": {"comment":"get Application ROM type ($80 or $81)"},
        "1352": {"comment":"offset $FC"},
        "1357": {"comment":"size of reserved Application space, $3FFC"},
