        "1613": {"comment":"result in DEBC, new abs. address"},
        "1614": {"comment":"new abs. address to BHL logic..."},
        "1619": {"comment":"slot mask restored in bank number"},
        "1622": {"comment":"segment mask restored in offset"},
        "1624": {"comment":"C register restored"},
        "1628": {"synopsis":"Convert 1MB 20bit address to relative pointer in BHL\n(B = 00h - 3Fh, HL = 0000h - 3FFFh).\n\nThis routine is primarily used File Eprom management\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997\nEntry: EBC = 24bit integer (actually 20bit 1MB address).\nExit: BHL = pointer.\nChanges: B, HL.\nKeeps: AF, C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "1637": {"comment":"OFFSET READY..."},
        "1638": {"comment":"now divide top 6 address bit with 16K"},
        "1639": {"comment":"and place it into B (bank) register"},
        "1648": {"comment":"BHL now (relative) ext. address"},
        "1649": {"synopsis":"Convert relative pointer BHL (B = 00h - 3Fh, HL = 0000h - 3FFFh)\nto absolute 20bit 1MB address.\n\nThis routine primarily used for File Eprom Management.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997\nEntry: BHL = pointer.\nExit: DEBC = 32bit integer (actually 24bit).\nChanges: BC, DE.\nKeeps: AF, HL, IX, IY."},
        "1665": {"comment":"DEBC = <BankNumber> * 16K + offset"},
        "1667": {"comment":"DEBC = BHL changed to absolute address in Eprom"},
        "1671": {"synopsis":"File Entry Management:\nInternal support library routine for FileEprFetchFile & FlashEprCopyFileEntry.\n\nDefine a block size to transfer, which is from the current bank offset and within 16K bank boundary,\nconsidering the remaining file size to copy.\nOZ source name: FileEprTransferBlockSize.\nEntry: BHL = current pointer to file block data; cde' = current file size.\nExit: hl' = size of block in File Area to transfer; cde' = updated according to adjusted\nblock size (that can be transferred within the bank boundary).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "1675": {"comment":"16K bank boundary..."},
        "1678": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "1679": {"comment":"HL = <BankSpace>"},
        "1683": {"comment":"get a copy of current file size (CDE)"},
        "1685": {"comment":"and preserve a copy..."},
        "1688": {"comment":"divisor in CDE (current size of file)"},
        "1689": {"comment":"dividend in BHL (remaining bytes of bank)"},
        "1691": {"comment":"<blocksize> = <FileSize> MOD <BankSpace>"},
        "1696": {"comment":"(restore current file size)"},
        "1706": {"comment":"copy remaining bank space from file inside current bank"},
        "1712": {"comment":"<blocksize> = 0 ?"},
        "1713": {"comment":"no, FileSize > BankSpace"},
        "1716": {"comment":"Yes, FileSize <= BankSpace"},
        "1719": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_TransferBlockSize."},
        "1723": {"synopsis":"Step of FileEprXferBlkSz when the rest of the file fits in the current bank: the whole\nremaining size becomes the block size.\nEntry: DE' = remaining file size (at most 16K; C' is not changed).\nExit: HL' = block size (the remaining size); DE' = 0.\nChanges: DE', HL'.","comment":"remaining file image to be copied is"},
        "1724": {"comment":"smaller than <BankSpace>, therefore"},
        "1725": {"comment":"the last image block is resident in the"},
        "1728": {"comment":"current bank..."},
        "1729": {"comment":"HL' = FileSize (max. 16K)"},
        "1730": {"synopsis":"Step of FileEprXferBlkSz when the rest of the file crosses the bank boundary: the block is\nDE bytes, and the remaining size CDE' is reduced by it.\nEntry: DE = block size; CDE' = remaining file size; Fc = 0.\nExit: HL' = block size; CDE' = CDE' - DE.\nChanges: C', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: AF, DE.","comment":"size of remaining file image crosses current"},
        "1731": {"comment":"bank boundary..."},
        "1732": {"comment":"define block size only of <BankSpace> size."},
        "1743": {"comment":"FileSize = FileSize - BankSpace"},
        "1744": {"comment":"HL' = BankSpace ..."},
        "1748": {"synopsis":"BHL/CDE -> BHL=quotient, CDE=remainder"},
        "1753": {"comment":"alt"},
        "1761": {"comment":"main"},
        "1787": {"comment":"alt"},
        "1795": {"comment":"main"},
        "1803": {"synopsis":"Check for \"oz\" File Eprom (on a conventional Eprom or on a Flash Memory)\n\n1) Check for a standard \"oz\" File Eprom, if that fails -\n2) Check if that slot contains an Application ROM, then check for the  Header Identifier below\nthe application bank area. For Flash Cards, the File Header might be on first top bank of a\nfree 64K sector. For Eproms, the File Header might be on the first top bank below the\napplication bank area.\n3) If a Rom Front Dor is located in a RAM Card, then this slot is regarded as a non-valid card as\na File Eprom, ie. not present.\n4) Check for embedded 'oz' watermark inside an 'OZ' application header. If found, then this\nindicates that a file area is located at the top of a card above an application area or at the\ntop of an OZ ROM.\n\nA) A standard 'oz' header is recognized by the top two watermark bytes in the top bank of the\nfile area (either typically at the top of the card, in modulus 64K sectors in Flash Cards or\nmodulus 16K banks on traditional EPROM's. The complete header has the following format:\n$3FC0       $00's until\n$3FF7       $01\n$3FF8       4 byte random id\n$3FFC       size of card in banks (2=32K, 8=128K, 16=256K, 64=1Mb)\n$3FFD       sub-type: $7E, $7C, $7A for UV 32K, 128K & 256K cards. $77, $6F for Intel and Amd Flash\n$3FFE       'o'\n$3FFF       'z' (file eprom identifier, lower case 'oz')\nin hex dump (example):\n00003fc0h: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 ; ................\n00003fd0h: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 ; ................\n00003fe0h: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 ; ................\n00003ff0h: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 73 D1 4B 3C 02 7E 6F 7A ; ........sï¿½<.~oz\n\nB) A sub-standard 'oz' header is recognized at offset $3FEE inside an application 'OZ' header that\nalways placed at the top of the card, with the following format:\nApplication Front DOR:\n$3FC0         0 0 0           Link to parent\n$3FC3         0 0 0           Link to brother - this may point to the HELP front DOR\n$3FC6         x x x           Link to son - this points to the first application DOR\n$3FC9         $13             DOR type, ROM Front DOR\n$3FCA         8               DOR length\n$3FCB         'N'             Key for name field (DT_NAM)\n$3FCC         5               Length of name and terminator\n$3FCD         'APPL', 0       NULL-terminated name\n$3FD2         $FF             DOR terminator\n\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nOptional file area at top card, above application area:\n$3FEC         x               Size of file area in banks, eg. $02 for a 32K size\n$3FED         $00             64K Reclaim Sector (0=not used)\n$3FEE         'oz'            Application/ROM Card holds file area\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\n$3FF8         @0xxxxxxx       Low byte of card ID\n$3FF9         @0xxxxxxx       High byte of card ID\n$3FFA         @0000xxxx       4 bit country code\n$3FFB         $80             Marks external application\n$3FFC         x               Size of card in banks, eg. $02 for a 32K card\n$3FFD         $00             Subtype of card - future expansion\n$3FFE         'OZ'            Card holds applications\nin hex dump (example):\n00003fc0h: 00 00 00 00 00 00 48 25 08 13 08 4E 05 41 50 50 ; ......H%...N.APP\n00003fd0h: 4C 00 FF 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 ; L..............\n00003fe0h: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 14 00 6F 7A ; ..............oz\n00003ff0h: 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 54 43 4C 81 20 00 4F 5A ; ........TCL .OZ\n\nOn partial success, if a Header is not found, Fz = 0 and the returned BHL pointer indicates\nthat the card might hold a file area, beginning at this location.\n\nIf the routine returns Fz = 1, it's an identified File Area Header (pointing to 64 byte header\nin the top of bank B).\n\nRegister parameters:\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, July-Sept 2004, July 2006\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3).\nExit: Success, File Area (or potential) available:; Fc = 0,; BHL = pointer to File Header\nfor slot C (B = absolute bank of slot).; (or pointer to free space in potential new File\nArea).; C = size of File Eprom Area in 16K banks; Fz = 1, File Header found; A = \"oz\" File\nEprom sub type; D = size of card in 16K banks (0 - 64); Fz = 0, File Header not found; A\nundefined; D undefined; Failure:; Fc = 1,; C = C(in); A = RC_ONF (File Eprom Card/Area not\navailable; possibly no card in slot); A = RC_ROOM (No room for File Area; all banks used for\napplications).\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.\nKeeps: E, IX, IY."},
        "1806": {"comment":"check for standard \"oz\" File Eprom in top bank of slot C..."},
        "1811": {"comment":"found \"oz\" header at top of card..."},
        "1812": {"comment":"return C = D = number of 16K banks of card"},
        "1813": {"comment":"offset pointer to \"oz\" header at top of card..."},
        "1816": {"comment":"indicate \"Header found\" (Fz = 1)"},
        "1818": {"comment":"copy of slot number"},
        "1822": {"comment":"Application ROM Header not present either..."},
        "1824": {"comment":"Front Dor located in RAM Card?"},
        "1826": {"comment":"Yes - indicate Card Not Available..."},
        "1828": {"comment":"preserve card size in E"},
        "1829": {"comment":"C = slot number"},
        "1830": {"comment":"locate and validate File Eprom Header"},
        "1833": {"comment":"whole card used for Applications..."},
        "1835": {"comment":"old DE"},
        "1836": {"comment":"D = size of card in 16K banks, C = size of File Area in banks"},
        "1837": {"comment":"restore original E"},
        "1838": {"comment":"BHL = absolute pointer to \"oz\" File Header below applications in slot"},
        "1841": {"comment":"A = File Eprom sub type, Fc = 0, Fz = indicated by DefHeaderPosition"},
        "1842": {"comment":"restore original C (slot number)"},
        "1848": {"comment":"restore original C (slot number)"},
        "1854": {"synopsis":"Define the position of the Header, starting from top bank\nof free card space area, calculated by number of reserved banks for\napplication usage, then\nFor Flash Cards:\nCheck the top bank of the first free 64K block below the last used\n64K block containg application code, for a File Header.\nFor Eprom's:\nCheck the top bank below the last application bank for a File Header.\n\nIf no space is left for a file area (all banks used for applications),\nthen Fc = 1 is returned.\nOZ source name: DefHeaderPosition.\nEntry: E = total of physical 16K banks on application card; B = number of banks reserved\n(used) for ROM applications; C = slot number.\nExit: Fc = 0 (success),; Fz = 1, Header found; A = sub type of File Eprom or File Flash\nCard; C = size of File Eprom Area in 16K banks; Fz = 0, Header not found; A undefined; C\nundefined; B = absolute bank of \"oz\" header (or potential); Fc = 1 (failure),; A = RC_ROOM\n(No room for File Eprom Area).\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "1857": {"comment":"poll for known flash card types"},
        "1860": {"comment":"preserve chip type (FE_28F or FE_29F)..."},
        "1861": {"comment":"if flash card was found, then B contains physical size in 16K banks"},
        "1862": {"comment":"(this overrules the card size supplied to this routine)"},
        "1864": {"comment":"there's no Flash Card, so check top bank below app area"},
        "1866": {"comment":"E = the physical size of the flash"},
        "1867": {"comment":"<Total banks> - <ROM banks> = lowest bank of ROM area"},
        "1870": {"comment":"Application card uses banks"},
        "1873": {"comment":"in lowest 64K block of card..."},
        "1878": {"comment":"File area are only found in Flash Card sector (64K) boundaries"},
        "1891": {"comment":"if Intel Flash was found then the sub type is always $77"},
        "1894": {"comment":"if Amd/Stm Flash was found then the sub type is always $6F"},
        "1898": {"comment":"use supplied card size in E"},
        "1899": {"comment":"<Total banks> - <ROM banks> = lowest bank of ROM area"},
        "1903": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_DefHeaderPosition."},
        "1905": {"synopsis":"Step of DefHdrPos: looks for a file area header in the bank below the given one. The bank is\nmoved into the upper 512K when the card has 32 banks, and ChkFileEprHdr checks it.\nEntry: A = bank above the file area (slot relative); E = card size in 16K banks; C = slot\nnumber.\nExit: Fc = 0; Fz = 1, header found: A = sub type, B = absolute bank of the header, C = size\nof the file area in banks; Fz = 0, no header: B = absolute bank where a new header would go,\nC = potential size of the file area in banks.\nChanges: AF, BC, E.","comment":"A = Top Bank of File Area"},
        "1906": {"comment":"is physical size of Flash / Epr $20 banks? (usually is $40)"},
        "1908": {"comment":"relative top bank is size of file area + 1 (returned in C later)"},
        "1911": {"comment":"for 512K Flash or Epr redefine bank location in upper 512K address map"},
        "1913": {"comment":"B = relative bank number of \"oz\" header (or potential), C = slot number"},
        "1917": {"comment":"header found, at absolute bank B, C = File Area in banks"},
        "1921": {"comment":"C = potential size of file area in banks"},
        "1925": {"comment":"relative bank B --> absolute bank B"},
        "1927": {"comment":"\"oz\" File Eprom Header not found, but potential area..."},
        "1929": {"comment":"B = absolute bank of \"oz\" Header, C = size of File Area in banks"},
        "1930": {"comment":"return flag status = found!"},
        "1931": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, indicate potential file area"},
        "1933": {"synopsis":"Returns the no-room error for DefHdrPos when the application area leaves no 64K block for a\nfile area (called with CALL Z and CALL C).\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_ROOM.\nChanges: AF."},
        "1937": {"synopsis":"Return File Eprom Area status in slot x (0, 1, 2 or 3),\nwith top of area at bank B (00h - 3Fh).\n\nThe routine automatically adjusts for slot 0 bank range; $00 - $1F, and\nalso recognizes the new sub-file area watermark in an application 'OZ'\nheader when located at top of card (or top of ROM at bank $1F in slot 0).\n\nFailure:\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF (\"oz\" File Eprom not found)\nC = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3)\nB = bank of \"oz\" header (slot relative, 00 - $3F)\nOZ source name: CheckFileEprHeader.\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3); B = bank of \"oz\" header (slot relative, 00 - $3F).\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0, Fz = 0; File Eprom found; A = Sub type of Eprom; B = absolute bank\n(embedded slot mask) of File Eprom Header; C = size of File Eprom Area in 16K banks.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "1941": {"comment":"look for official 'oz' file area header in top of bank BHL"},
        "1944": {"comment":"BHL points to slot C"},
        "1955": {"comment":"are we at top of ROM/FLASH in current slot?"},
        "1957": {"comment":"no, then certainly, no File Header was recognized"},
        "1959": {"comment":"$3FEC"},
        "1961": {"comment":"check for embedded 'oz' watermark in App/Rom header in top of slot"},
        "1964": {"comment":"(this sub-watermark indicates a file area above an application area)"},
        "1966": {"comment":"A = sub type of File Eprom, B = absolute bank no of hdr,"},
        "1967": {"comment":"return Fc = 0"},
        "1968": {"comment":"C = size of File Area in banks"},
        "1969": {"comment":"original HL restored"},
        "1970": {"comment":"ignore old BC -> new values are returned..."},
        "1971": {"comment":"original DE restored"},
        "1978": {"comment":"original BC, DE & HL restored"},
        "1980": {"synopsis":"ValidateOzWaterMark: checks for an \"oz\" watermark at the top of a bank. It reads the size\nbyte, the sub type and the \"oz\" word, then writes 0 over the word and reads it again: only a\nword that is still \"oz\" (ROM or flash, not RAM) counts. A changed word is written back.\nOZ source name: ValidateOzWaterMark.\nEntry: BHL = absolute pointer to the size byte ($3FFC, or $3FEC in an application header).\nExit: Fz = 1, watermark found: C = sub type, D = size of the area in banks; Fz = 0, not\nfound.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.\nKeeps: B, HL."},
        "1984": {"comment":"$3FxC, get size of File Eprom in Banks"},
        "1987": {"comment":"$3FxD, get sub type of File Eprom"},
        "1993": {"comment":"$3FxE, D <-- 'z', E <-- 'o'"},
        "2001": {"comment":"0 --> ($3FxE)"},
        "2003": {"comment":"0 --> ($3FxF)"},
        "2006": {"comment":"D <-- 'z', E <-- 'o'"},
        "2010": {"comment":"preserve bank offset to 'oz' header..."},
        "2014": {"comment":"$(3FxE) = 'oz' ?"},
        "2019": {"comment":"0 was written at $(3FFE) and 'oz' was still returned!"},
        "2021": {"comment":"we might have written to a RAM card,"},
        "2023": {"comment":"restore original values to ($3FxE)"},
        "2026": {"comment":"return D = size of area (if file area found)"},
        "2028": {"synopsis":"EP_Empty interface:\nOZ source name: FileEprEmptyFileArea.\nEntry: C = poll for empty file area in slot number 0, 1, 2 or 3.\nExit: Fz = 1, File area is empty (all bytes are FFh); Fz = 0, File area is not empty; B =\nbank that contains non-empty bytes; Fc = 1,; A = RC_ONF (File Eprom Card/Area not available;\npossibly no card in slot).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY."},
        "2033": {"comment":"no file area, report back to application"},
        "2034": {"comment":"file header found, proceed to validate file area"},
        "2037": {"comment":"signal no file area, header hasn't been created yet"},
        "2040": {"synopsis":"Validate bank contents to be 'empty' or containing data; an empty bank only\ncontains FFh bytes.\nOZ source name: validate_filearea.\nEntry: BHL = pointer to File Header for slot C (B = absolute bank of slot).; C = size of\nFile Eprom Area in 16K banks; Fz = 1, File Header found; A = \"oz\" File Eprom sub type; D =\nsize of card in 16K banks (0 - 64).\nExit: Fz = 1, File area is empty (all bytes are FFh); Fz = 0, File area is not empty; B =\nbank that contains non-empty bytes.","comment":"first check bank B of file header, HL = bytes to check..."},
        "2043": {"comment":"not good!"},
        "2044": {"comment":"now, check complete bank"},
        "2047": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: check_empty_fileara."},
        "2048": {"comment":"remaining banks to check..."},
        "2049": {"comment":"complete file area checked successfully"},
        "2053": {"comment":"this bank was empty too, check next (below)"},
        "2056": {"synopsis":"Validate bank contents to be 'empty' or containing data; an empty bank only\ncontains FFh bytes.\nEntry: B = Bank to validate; HL = total bytes to scan in bank (usually 16K).\nExit: Fz = 1, Bank was empty; Fz = 0, Bank contains data / code.\nChanges: AF..../.... different.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2061": {"comment":"get bank into S1, preserve old bank binding"},
        "2063": {"comment":"BC = total byte to scan..."},
        "2064": {"comment":"begin scanning from bottom of bank (in S1) upwards.."},
        "2067": {"comment":"$ff = empty byte to check for.."},
        "2069": {"comment":"byte used?"},
        "2071": {"comment":"all bytes of BC length checked, bank is empty"},
        "2074": {"comment":"(hl) = $ff, check next byte"},
        "2076": {"synopsis":"Fz = 0, non-empty byte encountered..."},
        "2077": {"comment":"restore previous S1 bank binding"},
        "2080": {"comment":"Fz = 0, (hl) <> $ff, bank is not empty"},
        "2081": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: signal_empty_bank.","comment":"Fz = 1"},
        "2084": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\nArea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nFetch file (image) from File Eprom Card, identified by File Entry at BHL\n(B=00h-FFh embedded slot mask, HL=0000h-3FFFh bank offset) and store it into\nan open file (enabled for writing) in the RAM file system (using the IX handle).\n\nThe application is responsible for opening/creating a RAM file, then using\nthis library routine to transfer the contents from the File Eprom to the\nRAM file system, and then finally close the new RAM file.\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF, File Eprom or File Entry was not found in slot\nA = RC_xxx, I/O error during saving process.\n\nDesign & programming:\nGunther Strube, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, Sep 2004, Oct 2006, Feb 2007\nEntry: IX = handle of file stream (opened previously with GN_Opf, A=OP_OUT); BHL = pointer\nto Eprom File Entry (bits 7,6 of B is the slot mask).\nExit: Fc = 0,; File Image transferred successfully to RAM file.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2087": {"comment":"get size of file in CDE, of entry BHL"},
        "2090": {"comment":"there was no File Eprom Entry at BHL!"},
        "2093": {"comment":"preserve size of file (in CDE)"},
        "2094": {"comment":"get pointer to file image in BHL"},
        "2099": {"comment":"file size in CDE'"},
        "2103": {"comment":"file size = 0 ?"},
        "2107": {"comment":"No, bytes still left to transfer to RAM..."},
        "2113": {"comment":"Yes, completed Eprom Image transfer to RAM file!"},
        "2115": {"comment":"get size of block to transfer in HL'"},
        "2118": {"comment":"then transfer block at BHL to RAM file..."},
        "2121": {"comment":"File I/O error occurred, abort..."},
        "2126": {"comment":"return Fc = 1, error code \"Object not found\""},
        "2132": {"synopsis":"Transfer File Block, at (BHL), size hl to file (IX)\nOZ source name: TransferFileBlock.\nEntry: BHL = pointer to file block; hl' = size of block to transfer.\nExit: Fc = ?, file I/O status; A = RC_xxx, if I/O error occurred; BHL = updated to point at\nfirst byte of next block to save (or EOF).","comment":"preserve bank number of ext. address"},
        "2139": {"comment":"Bind Bank into segment 1 address space"},
        "2140": {"comment":"preserve original bank binding of segment"},
        "2143": {"comment":"preserve remaining file size..."},
        "2145": {"comment":"HL = source (inside current bank B)"},
        "2146": {"comment":"BC = length of block to transfer to RAM file"},
        "2150": {"comment":"move memory to file (IX)..."},
        "2154": {"comment":"restore remaining file size..."},
        "2157": {"comment":"restore previous segment bank binding..."},
        "2158": {"comment":"writing current block to file failed, exit..."},
        "2166": {"comment":"we're still inside the current bank after block save..."},
        "2167": {"comment":"set offset at start of new bank"},
        "2169": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: err_TransferFileBlock."},
        "2171": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format.\n\nRead File Entry information, if available.\n\nNB:     This routine might be used by applications, but is primarily called by\nFile Eprom library routines\n\nFc = 1, File Entry not available ($FF was first byte of entry)\nA = RC_Onf (Object not found)\nBHL unchanged.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 1997, Mar 2007\nOZ source name: FileEprFileEntryInfo.\nEntry: BHL = pointer to start of file entry; The Bank specifier contains the slot mask, ie.\ndefines which slot; is being read. HL is the traditional bank offset.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Entry available; Fz = 1, deleted file; Fz = 0, active file; A = length of\nfilename; BHL = pointer to next File Entry (or free space); CDE = length of file.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"Read first byte of File Entry"},
        "2176": {"comment":"previous File Entry was last in File Eprom"},
        "2180": {"comment":"pointing at start of ROM header!"},
        "2185": {"comment":"preserve length of string"},
        "2186": {"comment":"get first char of filename"},
        "2189": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 1, if file marked as \"deleted\" (0)"},
        "2190": {"comment":"Fz = 0, if '/' character..."},
        "2191": {"comment":"preserve length of filename, status"},
        "2196": {"comment":"skip filename, point at length of file..."},
        "2210": {"comment":"CDE is length of file"},
        "2211": {"comment":"point at beginning of file image"},
        "2214": {"comment":"BHL points at next File Entry (or none)"},
        "2218": {"comment":"return length of filename, deleted status"},
        "2223": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nFind active File(name) on Standard File Eprom in slot C.\n\n(wildcard search algorithm implemented by Kirk J. Krauss <kjkrauss@us.ibm.com>,\nadapted & optimized for Z80 assembler by G. Strube)\n\nDesign & programming by G. Strube, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, Sep 2004, Nov 2015\nEntry: C = slot number of File Eprom (Area); DE = pointer to null-terminated filename to be\nsearched for.; The filename is excl. device name and must begin with '/'.; '*' and '?'\nwildcards may be used in filename.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; Fz = 1, File Entry found.; BHL = pointer to File Entry\nin card at slot; Fz = 0, No file were found on the File Eprom.; BHL = pointer to free byte\non File Eprom in slot; Fc = 1,; A = RC_Onf; File Eprom was not found at slot C.\nChanges: F, B, HL.\nKeeps: A, C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2228": {"comment":"preserve ptr to filename"},
        "2229": {"comment":"preserve slot number"},
        "2230": {"comment":"check for presence of \"oz\" File Eprom in slot C"},
        "2236": {"comment":"File Eprom not available in slot..."},
        "2239": {"comment":"slots (0), 1, 2 or 3 possible"},
        "2242": {"comment":"converted to Slot mask $40, $80 or $C0"},
        "2244": {"comment":"C = total banks of File Eprom Area"},
        "2246": {"comment":"B is now bottom bank of File Eprom Area"},
        "2247": {"comment":"DE points at local null-terminated filename"},
        "2248": {"comment":"BHL points at first File Entry"},
        "2251": {"comment":"get length of file entry name"},
        "2256": {"comment":"last File Entry was searched in File Eprom"},
        "2260": {"comment":"pointing at start of ROM header!"},
        "2264": {"comment":"BHL = beginning of filename"},
        "2267": {"comment":"found file in File Eprom?"},
        "2272": {"comment":"Yes, return ptr. to current File Entry..."},
        "2274": {"comment":"get pointer to next File Entry in slot C..."},
        "2279": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, File not found."},
        "2281": {"comment":"original C restored"},
        "2283": {"comment":"original A restored"},
        "2285": {"comment":"original IX restored"},
        "2292": {"comment":"ignore old AF..."},
        "2294": {"comment":"original IX restored"},
        "2297": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nFind active File(name) on Standard File Eprom, beginning at File Entry in BHL, forwards.\n\n(wildcard search algorithm implemented by Kirk J. Krauss <kjkrauss@us.ibm.com>,\nadapted & optimized for Z80 assembler by G. Strube)\nOZ source name: FileEprFindFileAt.\nEntry: BHL = pointer to File Entry in card at slot; DE = pointer to null-terminated filename\nto be searched for.; The filename is excl. device name and must begin with '/'.; '*' and '?'\nwildcards may be used as part of filename.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; Fz = 1, File Entry found.; BHL = pointer to File Entry\nin card at slot; Fz = 0, No file were found on the File Eprom.; BHL = pointer to free byte\non File Eprom in slot; Fc = 1,; A = RC_Onf; File Eprom was not found at slot C.\nChanges: F, B, HL.\nKeeps: A, C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2305": {"comment":"File Entry was not found..."},
        "2309": {"synopsis":"Compare file entry name (BHL) with wild card search string (DE)\nEntry: A = length of file entry name; BHL = points at first character of file entry name; DE\n= local pointer to null-terminated wild card search string.\nExit: Fz = 1, file entry name found (case independent comparison); Fz = 0, this file entry\nname did not match.\nChanges: AF, IX.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IY."},
        "2310": {"comment":"DE = pWildText"},
        "2311": {"comment":"BHL = pFenText (Fen = File Entry Name)"},
        "2312": {"comment":"C = length of file entry name in File Area..."},
        "2313": {"comment":"pWildBookmark = 0"},
        "2318": {"comment":"pFenBookmark = 0 (BHL' = File Entry Name Book Mark pointer)"},
        "2322": {"comment":"while(1) {"},
        "2325": {"comment":"if (*pWildtxt == '*') {"},
        "2328": {"comment":"while (*(++pWildTxt) == '*'); // \"xy\" matches \"x**y\""},
        "2333": {"comment":"if (!*pWildText) return Fz = 1; // \"x\" matches \"*\""},
        "2336": {"comment":"if (*pWildText != '?') {"},
        "2338": {"comment":"// Fast-forward to next possible match."},
        "2340": {"comment":"while (*pFenText != *pWildText) {"},
        "2345": {"comment":"if (!(*(++pFenText))) {"},
        "2351": {"comment":"return Fz = 0; // \"x\" doesn't match \"*y*\""},
        "2352": {"comment":"}"},
        "2354": {"comment":"pWtxtBookmark = pWildText;"},
        "2362": {"comment":"pFenBookmark = pFenText;"},
        "2364": {"comment":"} else"},
        "2366": {"comment":"if (*pFenText != *pWildText && *pWildText != '?') {"},
        "2368": {"comment":"// Got a non-match.  If we've set our bookmarks, back up to one"},
        "2370": {"comment":"// or both of them and retry."},
        "2375": {"comment":"if (pWildBookmark) {"},
        "2379": {"comment":"if (pWildText != pWtxtBookmark) {"},
        "2391": {"comment":"pWildText = pWtxtBookmark;"},
        "2395": {"comment":"if (*pFenText != *pWildText) {"},
        "2400": {"comment":"// Don't go this far back again."},
        "2409": {"comment":"pFenText = ++pFenBookmark;"},
        "2410": {"comment":"continue; // \"xy\" matches \"*y\""},
        "2412": {"comment":"pWildText++;"},
        "2413": {"synopsis":"}\n}","comment":"if (*pFenText) {   // (check if length of BHL > 0)"},
        "2417": {"comment":"pFenText++;"},
        "2420": {"comment":"continue; // \"mississippi\" matches \"*sip*\""},
        "2421": {"comment":"}"},
        "2423": {"synopsis":"}","comment":"return Fz = 0; // \"xy\" doesn't match \"x\""},
        "2424": {"comment":"}"},
        "2426": {"comment":"pFenText++;"},
        "2429": {"comment":"(also decrease remaining length of File Entry Name)"},
        "2430": {"comment":"pWildText++;"},
        "2432": {"comment":"// How do you match a tame text string?"},
        "2433": {"comment":"if (!*pFenText) {"},
        "2435": {"comment":"// The tame way: unique up on it!"},
        "2436": {"comment":"while (*pWildText == '*') {"},
        "2440": {"comment":"pWildText++;     // \"x\" matches \"x*\""},
        "2441": {"comment":"}"},
        "2443": {"comment":"if (!*pWildText)"},
        "2444": {"synopsis":"return Fz = 1;   // \"x\" matches \"x\" (EOF wildcard string)\nelse\nreturn Fz = 0;   // \"x\" doesn't match \"xy\"\n}","comment":"original HL restored"},
        "2445": {"comment":"original DE restored"},
        "2446": {"comment":"original BC restored"},
        "2448": {"synopsis":"(BHL) = (DE)?\n\nreturn Fz = 1 if they match, otherwise Fz = 0"},
        "2463": {"synopsis":"ToUpper - convert character to upper case if possible.\n\n..BCDEHL/IXIY  same\nAF....../....  different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Copyright (C) InterLogic 1995\nEntry: A = ASCII byte.\nExit: A = converted ASCII byte.","comment":"if a <= 'z'  &&"},
        "2467": {"comment":"if a >= 'a'"},
        "2470": {"comment":"then a = a - 32"},
        "2473": {"comment":"if a <= $fe  &&"},
        "2476": {"comment":"if a >= $e1"},
        "2479": {"comment":"then a = a - 32"},
        "2482": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn first file entry pointer on Standard File Eprom, inserted in slot C.\n\nIf the NULL file is identified as the first file, it is skipped and the next\nfile entry pointer is automatically returned.\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or File Entry not available\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, Sep 2004, July 2005\nEntry: C = slot number containing File Eprom.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; Fz = 1, File Entry marked as deleted; Fz = 0, File Entry\nis active.; BHL = pointer to first file entry in slot (B=00h-FFh, HL=0000h-3FFFh).; (NULL\nfile skipped if found on Intel Flash Card).\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2483": {"comment":"preserve CDE"},
        "2484": {"comment":"preserve slot number"},
        "2485": {"comment":"check for presence of \"oz\" File Eprom in slot C"},
        "2490": {"comment":"File Eprom not available in slot..."},
        "2493": {"comment":"C = total banks of File Eprom Area"},
        "2495": {"comment":"B is now bottom bank of File Eprom in slot C"},
        "2496": {"comment":"BHL points at first File Entry..."},
        "2504": {"comment":"CDE = length of file entry"},
        "2507": {"comment":"Ups - no File Entry found..."},
        "2509": {"comment":"first file is an active file..."},
        "2512": {"comment":"CDE = 0 means that NULL file is present."},
        "2515": {"comment":"ignore NULL file, get pointer to next file (entry)"},
        "2518": {"comment":"get pointer to next file entry and return Fz status"},
        "2520": {"comment":"return Fz = 1, deleted file was not a Null file..."},
        "2521": {"comment":"BHL = pointer to first File Entry"},
        "2522": {"comment":"original C restored"},
        "2525": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: no_entry."},
        "2526": {"comment":"\"Object not found\""},
        "2529": {"comment":"original C register restored"},
        "2532": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn pointer to previous file entry on Standard File Area.\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or current File entry was the first\nFile Entry (an attempt was made to go beyond the bottom of the file area)\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 2004\nEntry: BHL = pointer to current file entry in slot (B=00h-FFh, HL=0000h-3FFFh).\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; Fz = 1, File Entry marked as deleted; Fz = 0, File Entry\nis active.; BHL = pointer to previous file entry in slot (B=00h-FFh, HL=0000h-3FFFh).\nChanges: F, B, HL.\nKeeps: A, C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2534": {"comment":"preserve A & CDE"},
        "2537": {"comment":"slots (0), 1, 2 or 3 possible"},
        "2540": {"comment":"Bank number of BHL converted to slot number 0-3."},
        "2541": {"comment":"C = slot number"},
        "2542": {"comment":"Get first file entry in File Area"},
        "2545": {"comment":"no File Area!"},
        "2551": {"comment":"first file entry in BHL,"},
        "2552": {"comment":"current file entry (lib routine argument) in CDE"},
        "2560": {"comment":"BHL lib routine argument was the first file entry!"},
        "2567": {"comment":"get rid of old file entry"},
        "2569": {"comment":"preserve current File Entry"},
        "2570": {"comment":"get next file entry in BHL"},
        "2585": {"comment":"scanning found current File Entry (lib routine argument)"},
        "2586": {"comment":"get 'previous' entry in BHL and return that to caller"},
        "2587": {"comment":"get File Status of Previous File Entry..."},
        "2590": {"comment":"BHL = pointer to previous File Entry, Fz = file status"},
        "2591": {"comment":"original C restored"},
        "2592": {"comment":"original DE restored"},
        "2593": {"comment":"original A restored"},
        "2598": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: no_entry."},
        "2599": {"comment":"\"Object not found\""},
        "2602": {"comment":"original C register restored"},
        "2603": {"comment":"ignore original AF..."},
        "2606": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn next file entry pointer on Standard File Eprom, inserted in slot\n(B=00h-FFh embedded slot mask, HL=0000h-3FFFh bank offset)\n\nFc = 0, File Eprom available\nFz = 1, File Entry marked as deleted\nFz = 0, File Entry is active.\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or File Entry not available\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, Sep 2004, Mar 2007\nEntry: BHL = pointer to File Entry.\nExit: BHL = pointer to next file entry on File Eprom in slot, or first byte of empty space.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2611": {"comment":"No files are present on File Eprom..."},
        "2613": {"comment":"check file status of next file"},
        "2616": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_FileEprNextFile.","comment":"returned BHL is next file entry, or Fc = 1, A = RC_Onf if End Of List"},
        "2617": {"comment":"original C register restored"},
        "2619": {"comment":"original DE register restored"},
        "2621": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn pointer to last file entry on Standard File Eprom, inserted in slot C\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or File Entry not available\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 2004\nEntry: C = slot number containing File Eprom.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; Fz = 1, File Entry marked as deleted; Fz = 0, File Entry\nis active.; BHL = pointer to last file entry in slot (B=00h-FFh, HL=0000h-3FFFh).\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2622": {"comment":"preserve CDE"},
        "2623": {"comment":"Get first file entry in File Area"},
        "2626": {"comment":"no file area found..."},
        "2628": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: scan_filearea."},
