        "2632": {"comment":"get next file entry in BHL"},
        "2635": {"comment":"validate status of next file entry."},
        "2643": {"comment":"file status of last file entry restored."},
        "2645": {"comment":"BHL = pointer to last File Entry"},
        "2646": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FileEprLastFile."},
        "2647": {"comment":"original C restored"},
        "2648": {"comment":"original DE restored"},
        "2650": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format.\n\nRead File Entry Status information, if available.\n\nNB:     This routine might be used by applications, but is primarily called by\nFile Eprom library routines\n\nFc = 1, File Entry not available ($FF or $00 was first byte of entry)\nA = RC_Onf (Object not found)\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 2004, Mar 2007\nOZ source name: FileEprFileStatus.\nEntry: BHL = pointer to start of file entry; The Bank specifier contains the slot mask, ie.\ndefines which slot; is being read. HL is the traditional bank offset.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Entry available; Fz = 1, deleted file; Fz = 0, active file.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"Read first byte of File Entry"},
        "2655": {"comment":"previous File Entry was last in File Eprom..."},
        "2659": {"comment":"pointing at start of ROM header!"},
        "2666": {"comment":"get first char of filename"},
        "2669": {"comment":"Fc=0, Fz=1 (marked as \"deleted\"), Fz=0 ('/' character)"},
        "2672": {"comment":"return file status"},
        "2673": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_eprfile."},
        "2677": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\nArea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn file size of File Entry at pointer BHL\n(B=00h-FFh embedded slot mask, HL=0000h-3FFFh bank offset)\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or File Entry not available\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, Sep 2004, Feb 2007\nEntry: BHL = Pointer to File Entry in card at slot.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; Fz = 1, File Entry marked as deleted; Fz = 0, File Entry\nactive; CDE = size of file (24bit integer, C = high byte).\nChanges: AF, C, DE.\nKeeps: B, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2678": {"comment":"preserve pointer"},
        "2679": {"comment":"filename size in A, file status (Fz)"},
        "2682": {"comment":"if Fc = 0, length of file in CDE"},
        "2684": {"comment":"BHL restored"},
        "2685": {"comment":"return filestatus (Fz) or error status (Fc)"},
        "2686": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn file name of File Entry at BHL\n(B=00h-FFh embedded slot mask, HL=0000h-3FFFh bank offset)\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or File Entry not available\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, Sep 2004, Feb-Mar 2007\nEntry: CDE = buffer to hold returned filename, (C = 0, local pointer); BHL = pointer to\nEprom File Entry in card at slot.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; Fz = 1, File Entry marked as deleted; Fz = 0, File Entry\nmarked as active; A = length of filename; (CDE) contains a copy of filename,\nnull-terminated.\nChanges: AF...../.... different.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2688": {"comment":"preserve pointer"},
        "2690": {"comment":"preserve \"to\" pointer"},
        "2691": {"comment":"preserve pointer to File Entry"},
        "2698": {"comment":"file entry not found..."},
        "2700": {"comment":"copy filename into local buffer, null-terminated"},
        "2703": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FileEprFileName."},
        "2704": {"comment":"original pointer restored"},
        "2705": {"comment":"original buffer pointer restored"},
        "2707": {"synopsis":"Fetch filename at BHL, length C characters.\nEntry: A = length of filename; CDE = buffer to hold returned filename; BHL = pointer to\nlength byte of filename (start of File Entry).\nExit: Fc = 0, always.; (DE) contains a copy of filename, null-terminated, DE points at\nnull.; BHL points at byte beyond filename (start of file length 32bit integer); First char\nof filename always set to \"/\" (due to deleted filenames).\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: AF, IX, IY."},
        "2712": {"comment":"begin filename with '/'"},
        "2716": {"comment":"point at start of filename (of A length)"},
        "2719": {"comment":"point at first real character of filename"},
        "2723": {"comment":"BHL++"},
        "2730": {"comment":"flnmlength--"},
        "2734": {"comment":"null-terminate filename"},
        "2739": {"synopsis":"Stores one character of a file name for FetchFilename and advances the buffer pointer.\nEntry: A = character; CDE = buffer pointer (C = bank).\nExit: (CDE) = A; DE + 1.\nChanges: DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "2749": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn pointer to start of file image of File Entry at BHL\n(B=00h-FFh embedded slot mask, HL=0000h-3FFFh bank offset)\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or File Entry not available\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997 - Aug 1998, Mar 2007\nEntry: BHL = pointer to Eprom File Entry in card at slot.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available, File Entry available; BHL = pointer to start of file\nimage.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2752": {"comment":"preserve pointer to File Entry"},
        "2758": {"comment":"No files are present on File Eprom..."},
        "2760": {"comment":"length of filename + length byte"},
        "2761": {"comment":"+ 4 bytes (32bit integer containing file size)"},
        "2767": {"comment":"BHL = start of file image..."},
        "2770": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FileEprFileImage."},
        "2771": {"comment":"original C register restored"},
        "2772": {"comment":"original DE restored"},
        "2774": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn file pointer to file entry image as extended address in BHL\n(B=00h-FFh embedded slot mask, HL=0000h-3FFFh bank offset)\n\nNo File Entry EOF boundary check is done.\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found in slot, or File Entry not available\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, June 2014\nOZ source name: FileEprGetFilePointer.\nEntry: BHL = pointer to Eprom File Entry in card at slot; CDE = offset into file image\n(24bit), 0 = first byte of file.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available, File Entry available; BHL = file pointer into File\nEntry.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "2776": {"comment":"BHL <- start of file image..."},
        "2779": {"comment":"not a file entry..."},
        "2781": {"comment":"BHL += CDE offset"},
        "2785": {"comment":"original C register restored"},
        "2786": {"comment":"original DE restored"},
        "2788": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn amount of active and deleted file space (in bytes) in File Eprom Area,\ninserted in slot C.\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF\nFile Eprom was not found in slot C.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, July 2005\nOZ source name: FileEprTotalSpace.\nEntry: C = slot number containing File Eprom Area.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; BHL = Amount of active file space in bytes (24bit\ninteger, B = MSB); CDE = Amount of deleted file space in bytes (24bit integer, C = MSB).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"preserve slot number"},
        "2789": {"comment":"check for presence of \"oz\" File Eprom in slot"},
