        "2847": {"comment":"use IX temporarily as 16bit accumulator..."},
        "2858": {"synopsis":"Adds a file entry's size to the sum of active file space for CalcFileSpace.\nEntry: CDE = size of the entry (header and image); BHL' = sum so far.\nExit: BHL' = BHL' + CDE.\nChanges: B', HL', IX (CalcFileSpace saves IX).\nKeeps: AF.","comment":"preserve Z80 status flags"},
        "2860": {"comment":"add file size (in CDE) to BHL'..."},
        "2869": {"comment":"original DE restored (of deleted file space)"},
        "2872": {"comment":"HL += active file size (low 16bit of 24bit)"},
        "2874": {"comment":"B += active files size (high 8 bit of 24bit)"},
        "2878": {"synopsis":"Adds a file entry's size to the sum of deleted file space for CalcFileSpace.\nEntry: CDE = size of the entry (header and image); CDE' = sum so far.\nExit: CDE' = CDE' + CDE.\nChanges: C', DE', IX (CalcFileSpace saves IX).\nKeeps: AF.","comment":"preserve Z80 status flags"},
        "2880": {"comment":"add file size (in CDE) to CDE'..."},
        "2890": {"comment":"DE += deleted file size (low 16bit of 24bit)"},
        "2892": {"comment":"C += deleted files size (high 8 bit of 24bit)"},
        "2896": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn amount of active (visible) file space in File Eprom Area, inserted in slot C.\n(API wrapper of FileEprTotalSpace)\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF\nFile Eprom was not found in slot C.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, July 2005\nOZ source name: FileEprActiveSpace.\nEntry: C = slot number containing File Eprom Area.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; DEBC = Active space (amount of visible files) in bytes;\n(DE = high 16bit, BC = low 16bit).\nChanges: F, BC, DE.\nKeeps: A, HL, IX, IY."},
        "2901": {"comment":"File Area not available"},
        "2904": {"comment":"BHL = Amount of active file space in bytes"},
        "2907": {"comment":"BHL -> DEBC"},
        "2909": {"comment":"original A restored"},
        "2910": {"comment":"original HL restored"},
        "2912": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: err_FileEprActiveSpace.","comment":"discard old AF..."},
        "2913": {"comment":"original HL restored"},
        "2915": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\nArea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn free space in Standard File Eprom Area, inserted in slot C\n\nFc = 1, File Area was not found in slot C\nA = RC_ONF\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Dec '97-Aug '98, July '05, Feb '07\nEntry: C = slot number containing File Eprom Area.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Area available; DEBC = Free space available.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "2916": {"comment":"preserve slot number"},
        "2917": {"comment":"check for presence of \"oz\" File Eprom in slot"},
        "2922": {"comment":"File Eprom not available in slot..."},
        "2924": {"comment":"preserve slot number in A"},
        "2927": {"comment":"File Header at relative BHL (seen from bottom of bank)"},
        "2930": {"comment":"File header -> DEBC (total bytes in file area)"},
        "2935": {"comment":"slot number."},
        "2946": {"comment":"used file space in file area, BHL + CDE -> DEBC"},
        "2948": {"comment":"<Capacity> - <UsedSpace> = Free Space"},
        "2955": {"comment":"return free space of File Eprom in DEBC"},
        "2956": {"comment":"restored original HL"},
        "2958": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: err_FileEprFreeSpace."},
        "2961": {"comment":"restored original HL"},
        "2963": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nCount total of active and deleted files on File Eprom in slot C\n(excl. NULL file on Intel Flash card)\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Eprom was not found at slot C\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997-Aug 1998, July 2005\nEntry: C = slot number containing File Eprom Area.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; HL = total of active (visible) files; DE = total of\n(marked as) deleted files; (HL + DE are total files in the file area).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC, IX, IY."},
        "2964": {"comment":"preserve slot number"},
        "2965": {"comment":"check for presence of \"oz\" File Eprom in slot C"},
        "2970": {"comment":"File Eprom (Area) not available in slot..."},
        "2973": {"comment":"slots (0), 1, 2 or 3 possible"},
        "2976": {"comment":"converted to Slot mask $40, $80 or $C0"},
        "2978": {"comment":"C = total banks of File Eprom Area"},
        "2980": {"comment":"B is now bottom bank of File Eprom"},
        "2981": {"comment":"BHL points at first File Entry..."},
        "2987": {"comment":"reset \"deleted\" files counter"},
        "2988": {"comment":"reset active files counter"},
        "2990": {"synopsis":"scan all file entries, and count\nOZ source name: scan_eprom."},
        "2993": {"comment":"No File Entry was available in File Eprom"},
        "3010": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: finished.","comment":"Fc = 0, File Eprom parsed."},
        "3012": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_count_files2."},
        "3014": {"synopsis":"Counts a deleted file entry for FileEprCntFiles, which calls it with the register sets\nexchanged: the deleted-file counter DE is incremented unless the entry's file length (CDE in\nthe other set) is 0, the null file of Intel flash cards. Fz is kept, so the following CALL\nNZ, ActiveFile is skipped.\nEntry: DE = deleted-file count; CDE' = file length; Fz = 1.\nExit: DE = DE + 1 for a real file.\nChanges: DE, AF'."},
        "3015": {"comment":"preserve file status of entry"},
        "3020": {"comment":"ignore NULL file on Intel flash cards"},
        "3025": {"synopsis":"Counts an active file entry for FileEprCntFiles.\nEntry: HL = active-file count (in the exchanged register set).\nExit: HL = HL + 1.\nChanges: HL."},
        "3027": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format, including support for sub File Eprom\narea in application cards (below application banks in first free 64K boundary)\n\nReturn BHL pointer to new file entry (also first byte of free space in File\nEprom Area, inserted in slot C).\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_Onf\nFile Area was not found in slot C\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997 - Aug 1998\nOZ source name: FileEprNewFileEntry.\nEntry: C = slot number containing File Eprom Area.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Eprom available; BHL = pointer to first byte of free space (B = absolute\nbank of slot C).\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "3029": {"comment":"preserve slot number"},
        "3030": {"comment":"check for presence of \"oz\" File Eprom Area in slot"},
        "3035": {"comment":"File Area not available in slot..."},
        "3038": {"comment":"slots (0), 1, 2 or 3 possible"},
        "3041": {"comment":"converted to Slot mask $40, $80 or $C0"},
        "3043": {"comment":"C = total banks of File Eprom Area"},
        "3045": {"comment":"B is now bottom bank of File Eprom"},
        "3046": {"comment":"BHL points at first File Entry..."},
        "3049": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: scan_eprom.","comment":"scan all file entries, to point at first free byte"},
        "3054": {"comment":"reached pointer to new file entry, don't return Fc = 1"},
        "3057": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: err_FileEprNewFileEntry."},
        "3058": {"comment":"return A = RC_Onf (File Area not found)"},
        "3063": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FileEprNewFileEntry."},
        "3066": {"comment":"BHL points at first free byte..."},
        "3069": {"comment":"strip segment attributes of bank offset, if any..."},
        "3072": {"synopsis":"Relative offset definitions for allocated work buffer on stack\nStandard Z88 File Eprom Format.\n\nSave RAM file to Flash Memory or UV Eprom file area in slot C.\n(files to UV Eprom only in slot 3)\n\nThe routine does NOT handle automatical \"deletion\" of existing files\nthat matches the filename (excl. device). This must be used by a call\nto <FlashEprFileDelete>.\n\nShould the actual process of blowing the file image fail, the new\nFile Entry will be marked as deleted, if possible.\n\nThe screen is turned off while saving a file to flash file area that is in\nthe same slot as the OZ ROM. During saving, no interference should happen\nfrom Blink, because the Blink reads the font bitmaps each 1/100 second:\nWhen saving a file is part of OZ ROM chip, the font bitmaps are suddenly\nunavailable which creates violent screen flickering during chip command mode.\nFurther, and most importantly, avoid Blink doing read-cycles while\nchip is in command mode.\nBy switching off the screen, the Blink doesn't read the font bit maps in\nOZ ROM, and the Flash chip can be in command mode without being disturbed\nby the Blink.\n\nImportant:\nINTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require the 12V VPP pin in slot 3\nto successfully blow data to the memory chip. If the Flash Eprom card\nis inserted in slot 1 or 2, this routine will report a programming failure.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to\nevaluate the Flash Memory (using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the\nuser that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the Z88 slot 3 hardware, so\nthis type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nEqually, the application should evaluate that saving to a file that is on an\nUV Eprom only can be performed in slot 3. This routine will report failure\nif saving a file to slots 0, 1 or 2.\n\nFc = 1,\nFile (Flash) Eprom not available in slot A:\nA = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip)\nNot sufficient space to store file (and File Entry Header):\nA = RC_Room\nFlash Eprom Write Errors:\nIf possible, the new File Entry is marked as deleted.\nA = RC_VPL, RC_BWR (see \"error.def\" for details)\n\nRAM File was not found, or other filename related problems:\nA = RC_Onf\nA = RC_Ivf\nA = RC_use\n\nDesign & Programming, Gunther Strube\nDec 1997-Apr 1998, Sep 2004, Aug 2006, Nov 2006,\nMar 2007, Feb 2009, Nov 2015\nOZ source name: FileEprSaveRamFile.\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3); IX = size of I/O buffer.; DE = pointer to I/O buffer,\nin segment 0/1.; HL = pointer to filename string (null-terminated), in segment 0/1.;\nFilename may contain wildcards (to find first match).\nExit: Fc = 0, File successfully saved to Flash File Eprom.; BHL = pointer to created File\nEntry in slot C.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY.","comment":"preserve IX"},
