        "3777": {"comment":"return BHL = updated to pointer after block"},
        "3780": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: ozFlashEprReduceFileArea.","comment":"C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3) of Flash Memory Card"},
        "3783": {"comment":"Return: BHL = absolute pointer to new \"oz\" header in card"},
        "3784": {"comment":"C = Number of 16K banks of File Eprom Area"},
        "3786": {"synopsis":"Generic error return codes used by INTEL/AMD/STM low level flash routines."},
        "3790": {"synopsis":"Error return of the flash erase routines.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_BER (block or sector erase failed).\nChanges: AF."},
        "3794": {"synopsis":"Error return of the flash write routines.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_BWR (byte not written).\nChanges: AF."},
        "3798": {"synopsis":"Prepare AMD Command Mode sequense addresses.\nOZ source name: AM29Fx_InitCmdMode.\nEntry: HL points into bound bank of Flash Memory.\nExit: BC = $aa55; DE = address $x2AA (derived from HL); HL = address $x555 (derived from\nHL).\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: AF, IX, IY."},
        "3799": {"comment":"B = Unlock cycle #1 code, C = Unlock cycle #2 code"},
        "3809": {"comment":"HL = address $x555"},
        "3812": {"comment":"DE = address $x2AA"},
        "3815": {"synopsis":"Erase sector defined in B (00h-0Fh), on Flash Memory Card inserted in slot C.\n\nThe routine will internally ask the Flash Memory for identification and intelligently\nuse the correct erasing algorithm. All known Flash Memory chips from INTEL, AMD & STM\n(see flashepr.def) uses 64K sectors, except the AM29F010B/ST29F010B 128K chip, which uses 16K sectors.\n\nImportant:\nINTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require the 12V VPP pin in slot 3 to successfully erase\na block/sector on the memory chip. If the Flash Eprom card is inserted in slot 1 or 2, this\nroutine will automatically report a sector erase failure error.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to evaluate the Flash\nMemory (using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the user that an INTEL Flash Memory Card\nrequires the Z88 slot 3 hardware, so this type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nDesign & programming by:\nGunther Strube, Dec 97-Apr 98, Aug '04, Aug '06, Oct-Nov '06, Feb '07, Oct '07\nThierry Peycru, Zlab, Dec 1997\nOZ source name: FlashEprSectorErase.\nEntry: B = block/sector number on chip to be erased (00h - 0Fh); (available sector size and\ncount depend on chip type); C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3) of Flash Memory Card.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; Failure:; Fc = 1; A = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip); A\n= RC_BER (error occurred when erasing block/sector); A = RC_VPL (Vpp Low Error).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3819": {"comment":"sector number range is only 0 - 15..."},
        "3821": {"comment":"preserve sector in D (not destroyed by FlashEprCardId)"},
        "3822": {"comment":"preserve slot no in E (not destroyed by FlashEprCardId)"},
        "3823": {"comment":"poll for card information in slot C (returns B = total banks of card)"},
        "3828": {"comment":"preserve FE Programming type in A'"},
        "3832": {"comment":"yes, it's a 16K sector architecture (same as Z88 bank architecture!)"},
        "3834": {"comment":"no, it's a 64K sector architecture"},
        "3835": {"comment":"sector number * 4 (16K * 4 = 64K!)"},
        "3836": {"comment":"(convert to first bank no of sector)"},
        "3838": {"comment":"B = size of card, decrease 1 to get relative top bank number.."},
        "3840": {"comment":"only slots 0, 1, 2 or 3 possible"},
        "3842": {"comment":"we're in slot 0, so flash chip can only be in lower 512K of slot 0"},
        "3846": {"comment":"bank no of sector is on lower 512K address (128K or 512K chip),"},
        "3848": {"comment":"then use upper 512K address lines (to be compatible with hybrid card)"},
        "3851": {"comment":"Converted to Slot mask $40, $80 or $C0"},
        "3852": {"comment":"the absolute bank which is the bottom of the sector"},
        "3853": {"comment":"preserve a copy of bank number in D"},
        "3861": {"comment":"Card < 1Mb: for calculation, adjust bank number within size of card..."},
        "3863": {"comment":"this is the X'th bank of the card.."},
        "3865": {"comment":"make sure that the Flash Memory Card (A = total 16K banks on Card)"},
        "3866": {"comment":"contains the sector (to be erased)"},
        "3867": {"comment":"(total_banks_on_card - sector_bank < 0) ..."},
        "3869": {"comment":"Fc = 1, sector not available (could not erase block/sector)"},
        "3873": {"comment":"bind sector to"},
        "3874": {"comment":"segment 1 (segment 2 & 3 contains OZ kernel banks)"},
        "3876": {"comment":"HL points into segment"},
        "3880": {"comment":"preserve old bank binding"},
        "3881": {"comment":"FE Programming type in A"},
        "3882": {"comment":"no maskable interrupts allowed while doing flash hardware commands..."},
        "3883": {"comment":"erase sector in slot C"},
        "3886": {"comment":"maskable interrupts allowed again"},
        "3888": {"comment":"Restore previous Bank bindings"},
        "3889": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FlashEprBlockErase."},
        "3893": {"synopsis":"Erase block, identified by bank A, using segment x, which\nHL points into.\nEntry: A = FE_28F or FE_29F (depending on Flash Memory type in slot); E = slot number (1, 2\nor 3) of Flash Memory Card; HL = points into bound bank of Flash Memory.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; Failure:; Fc = 1; A = RC_BER (error occurred when erasing\nblock/sector); A = RC_VPL (Vpp Low Error).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "3895": {"comment":"execute AMD/STM sector erasure in lowram.def, return error in AF..."},
        "3899": {"comment":"when chip is FE_28F series, we need to be in slot 3"},
        "3900": {"comment":"Ups, not in slot 3, signal error!"},
        "3903": {"synopsis":"Erase block on an INTEL 28Fxxxx Flash Memory, which is bound\ninto segment x that HL points into.\nOZ source name: FEP_EraseBlock_28F.\nEntry: HL = points into bound Flash Memory sector.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; A = undefined; Failure:; Fc = 1; A = RC_BER (error occurred when\nerasing block/sector); A = RC_VPL (Vpp Low Error).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY.","comment":"Address of soft copy of COM register"},
        "3907": {"comment":"Vpp On"},
        "3909": {"comment":"Force Screen enabled (don't push 21V to Intel flash!)..."},
        "3912": {"comment":"signal to HW"},
        "3914": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "3915": {"comment":"execute Erasure of sector in lowram.def..."},
        "3920": {"comment":"chip didn't detect VPP pin ..."},
        "3927": {"comment":"chip could erase sector..."},
        "3930": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_EraseBlock_28F."},
        "3932": {"comment":"Vpp Off"},
        "3935": {"comment":"Signal to HW"},
        "3937": {"comment":"return error status from chip sector erasure"},
        "3939": {"synopsis":"Erase block on an AMD 29Fxxxx Flash Memory, which is bound\ninto segment x that HL points into.\nOZ source name: FEP_EraseBlock_29F.\nEntry: HL = points into bound Flash Memory sector.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; A = undefined; Failure:; Fc = 1; A = RC_BER (error occurred when\nerasing block/sector); A = RC_VPL (Vpp Low Error).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "3942": {"comment":"Erase sector in lowram.def, then use RET in lowram.def to get back to caller"},
        "3945": {"synopsis":"Erase Flash Memory Card inserted in slot C.\n\nThe routine will internally ask the Flash Memory for identification\nand intelligently use the correct erasing algorithm.\n\nImportant:\nINTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require the 12V VPP pin in slot 3\nto successfully erase the memory chip. If the Flash Memory card is\ninserted in slot 1 or 2, this routine will automatically report a\nsector erase failure error.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call)\nto evaluate the Flash Memory (using the FlashEprCardId routine) and\nwarn the user that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the Z88\nslot 3 hardware, so this type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nPrior to this call, it is also the responsibility of the application\nto avoid erasing a slot which contains the operating system.\nUse the OZSlotPoll library to validate the specified slot.\n\nDesign & programming by:\nGunther Strube, Dec 1997-Apr 1998, Aug 2004, Aug 2006\nThierry Peycru, Zlab, Dec 1997\nOZ source name: FlashEprCardErase.\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3) of Flash Memory.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; Failure:; Fc = 1; A = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip); A\n= RC_BER (error occurred when erasing block/sector); A = RC_VPL (Vpp Low Error).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "3947": {"comment":"poll for card information in slot C (returns B = total banks of card)"},
        "3952": {"comment":"Erase the individual sectors, one at a time"},
        "3954": {"comment":"total of 16K banks on card -> total of 64K sectors on card."},
        "3956": {"comment":"sectors, from (total sectors-1) downwards and including 0"},
        "3957": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: erase_2xF_card_blocks.","comment":"erase top sector of card, and downwards..."},
        "3968": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FlashEprCardErase."},
        "3971": {"synopsis":"Copy a block of bytes to the Flash Card, from address BHL to CDE of block size IX. If a block\non the destination will cross a bank boundary, it is automatically continued on the next adjacent\nbank of the card. Block at BHL+IX must be within the bank boundary because source and destination\npointers are bound into unique segments in the address space temporarily.\n\nBHL points to an absolute bank of the source block.\nCDE points equally to an absolute bank of the destination block (to be written) on the flash memory.\n\nOn return, CDE points at the byte after the end of the block, without segment mask.\n\nThe routine is used by the File Area Management libraries, but is well suited for other\napplication purposes.\n\nThe routine can be told which programming algorithm to use (by specifying the FE_28F or FE_29F\nmnemonic in A); these parameters can be fetched when investigating which Flash Memory chip is\navailable in the slot, using the FlashEprCardId routine that reports these constants.\n\nHowever, if neither of the constants are provided in A, the routine can be specified with A = 0\nwhich internally polls the Flash Memory for identification and intelligently use the correct\nprogramming algorithm. The identified FE_28F or FE_29F constant is returned to the caller in A\nfor future reference (when the block was successfully programmed to the card).\n\nImportant:\nINTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require the 12V VPP pin in slot 3 to successfully blow data to\nthe memory chip. If the Flash Eprom card is inserted in slot 1 or 2, this routine will report a\nprogramming failure.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to evaluate the Flash Memory\n(using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the user that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the\nZ88 slot 3 hardware, so this type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nDesign & programming by\nGunther Strube, Oct 2006, Feb 2007\nOZ source name: FlashEprCopyBlock.\nEntry: A = FE_28F, FE_29F or 0 (poll card for blowing algorithm); BHL = extended address to\nstart of source (any memory); (bits 7,6 of B is the slot mask); CDE = extended address to\nstart of destination (pointer into flash card); (bits 7,6 of C is the slot mask); IX = size\nof block (at BHL) to copy (blow) to CDE (must be within bank boundary).\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; A = FE_28F or FE_29F (if A(in)=0, depending on found card); BHL, CDE\nupdated to reflect block copy (segment masks stripped from HL, DE offset); Failure:; Fc = 1;\nA = RC_BWR (block not blown properly); A = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip); A =\nRC_UNK (chip type is unknown: use only FE_28F, FE_29F or 0).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "3974": {"comment":"preserve FE Programming type in A'"},
        "3977": {"comment":"bind BHL to segment 1"},
        "3981": {"comment":"bind CDE to segment 3 (this code executes in segment 2)"},
        "3988": {"comment":"Bind bank of source data into segment C"},
        "3989": {"comment":"preserve old bank binding of segment C"},
        "3992": {"comment":"BHL <- CDE"},
        "3994": {"comment":"FE Programming type"},
        "3995": {"comment":"DE now source block in current address space, BHL destination pointer"},
        "3998": {"comment":"preserve error status ..."},
        "4001": {"comment":"restore old segment C bank binding of BHL source data block"},
        "4007": {"comment":"block size + offset = updated block pointer (installed in HL below)"},
        "4015": {"comment":"return updated CDE destination pointer to caller"},
        "4017": {"comment":"HL = updated to byte beyond source block offset"},
        "4019": {"comment":"original B restored"},
        "4020": {"comment":"source pointer crossed bank boundary?"},
        "4022": {"comment":"nope (withing 16k offset)"},
        "4025": {"comment":"source block copy reached boundary of bank..."},
        "4027": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FlashEprCopyBlock.","comment":"restored original IX"},
        "4030": {"comment":"return A = FE Programming type, or error condition in AF"},
        "4031": {"synopsis":"Get Flash Card Data.\n\nDesign & programming by\nGunther Strube, Aug 2006, Nov 2006\nEntry: HL = Polled from Flash Memory Chip (see FlashEprCardId):; Manufacturer & Device Code.\nExit: Fc = 0; ID was found (verified):; A = chip generation (FE_28F or FE_29F); B = total of\n16K banks on Flash Memory; CDE = extended pointer to null-terminated string description of\nchip; Fc = 1; ID was not found.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "4036": {"comment":"no. of Flash Memory ID's in table"},
        "4039": {"comment":"Device Code found?"},
        "4040": {"comment":"points at Manufacturer Code"},
        "4044": {"comment":"Manufacturer Code found?"},
        "4045": {"comment":"points at no of banks of Flash Memory"},
        "4048": {"comment":"B = total of 16K banks on Flash Eprom"},
        "4050": {"comment":"A = chip generation"},
        "4054": {"comment":"DE points at chip description string"},
        "4055": {"comment":"C = bank that contains this string"},
        "4057": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Flash Eprom data returned..."},
        "4059": {"comment":"points at no of banks"},
        "4060": {"comment":"points at chip generation"},
        "4061": {"comment":"point mnemonic low byte"},
        "4062": {"comment":"point mnemonic high byte"},
        "4063": {"comment":"point at next entry"},
        "4064": {"comment":"and check for new Device Code"},
        "4066": {"comment":"Manufacturer and Device Code wasn't verified, indicate error"},
        "4067": {"comment":"return FE_28F or FE29F in A (if device was successfully verified)"},
        "4069": {"synopsis":"Table of the known flash chips, read by FlashEprCardId: a count byte (7), then 7 entries of\n6 bytes: device code, manufacturer code, size in 16K banks, chip generation (FE_28F or\nFE_29F) and a word pointing to the chip's name string (mnem_i004 and the following)."},
        "4070": {"comment":"Intel flash"},
        "4072": {"comment":"8 x 64K sectors / 32 x 16K banks (512Kb)"},
        "4076": {"comment":"Intel flash"},
        "4078": {"comment":"16 x 64K sectors / 64 x 16K banks (1024Kb)"},
        "4080": {"comment":"appears like I28F008S5"},
        "4082": {"comment":"Intel flash"},
        "4084": {"comment":"16 x 64K sectors / 64 x 16K banks (1024Kb)"},
        "4088": {"comment":"Amd flash"},
        "4090": {"comment":"8 x 16K sectors / 8 x 16K banks (128Kb)"},
        "4094": {"comment":"Amd flash"},
        "4096": {"comment":"8 x 64K sectors / 32 x 16K banks (512Kb)"},
        "4100": {"comment":"Amd flash"},
        "4102": {"comment":"16 x 64K sectors / 64 x 16K banks (1024Kb)"},
        "4106": {"comment":"Amic flash"},
        "4108": {"comment":"8 x 64K sectors / 32 x 16K banks (512Kb)"},
        "4112": {"synopsis":"Name string of the Intel I28F004S5 flash chip, \"I28F004S5 (512K)\", null-terminated."},
        "4129": {"synopsis":"Name string \"I28F008S5 (1Mb)\", null-terminated, shared by the Intel I28F008SA and I28F008S5\nentries of DeviceCodeTable."},
        "4145": {"synopsis":"Name string of the AMD AM29F010B flash chip, \"AM29F010B (128K)\", null-terminated."},
        "4162": {"synopsis":"Name string of the AMD AM29F040B flash chip, \"AM29F040B (512K)\", null-terminated."},
        "4179": {"synopsis":"Name string of the AMD AM29F080B flash chip, \"AM29F080B (1Mb)\", null-terminated."},
        "4195": {"synopsis":"Name string of the AMIC29F040B flash chip, \"AMIC29F040B (512K)\", null-terminated."},
        "4214": {"synopsis":"Identify Flash Memory Chip in slot C.\n\nFailure:\nFc = 1\nA = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip)\n\nDesign & programming by\nGunther Strube, Dec '97-Apr '98, Jul-Sep '04, Sep '05, Aug-Oct-Nov 06, Feb 07, Oct 07\nThierry Peycru, Zlab, Dec 1997\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3).\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0, Fz = 1; A = FE_28F or FE_29F, defining the Flash Memory chip\ngeneration; HL = Flash Memory ID; H = Manufacturer Code (FE_INTEL_MFCD, FE_AMD_MFCD); L =\nDevice Code (refer to flashepr.def); B = total of 16K banks on Flash Memory Chip.\nChanges: AF, B, HL, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY, AF'."},
        "4219": {"comment":"only slots 0, 1, 2 or 3 possible"},
        "4221": {"comment":"preserve a copy of slot argument in E"},
        "4223": {"comment":"Converted to Slot mask $40, $80 or $C0"},
        "4227": {"comment":"use segment 1 (not this executing segment which is MS_S2)"},
        "4232": {"comment":"skip RAM check for upper 512K in slot 0 (always available)"},
        "4234": {"comment":"check for hybrid hardware; 512K RAM (bottom) and 512K Flash (top)"},
        "4238": {"comment":"point at top of bank of slot"},
        "4244": {"comment":"abort, if RAM card was found in slot C..."},
        "4248": {"comment":"if not RAM, get info of AMD Flash Memory chip in top of slot (if avail in slot C)..."},
        "4251": {"comment":"flash chip not found"},
        "4253": {"comment":"verify Flash Memory ID with known Manufacturer & Device Codes (could be bogus ID from Intel)"},
        "4256": {"comment":"an Intel Flash will fail when polled at the top, so check it now (at the bottom)..."},
        "4258": {"comment":"an AMD ID was found"},
        "4259": {"comment":"ignore old bank/segment parameters and return B = total banks of card to caller"},
        "4262": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: check_card_bottom."},
        "4263": {"comment":"use segment 1 (not this executing segment which is MS_S2)"},
        "4269": {"comment":"abort, if RAM card was found in bottom of slot C..."},
        "4271": {"comment":"get info of intel Flash Memory at bottom of chip in HL (if avail in slot C)..."},
        "4274": {"comment":"no ID's were polled from a (potential FE card)"},
        "4276": {"comment":"verify Flash Memory ID with known Manufacturer & Device Codes"},
        "4281": {"comment":"B = banks on card, A = chip series (28F or 29F)"},
        "4282": {"comment":"original C restored"},
        "4283": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_FlashEprCardId.","comment":"original DE restored"},
        "4286": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 1"},
        "4289": {"comment":"signal error..."},
        "4293": {"synopsis":"Get the Manufacturer and Device Code from a Flash Eprom Chip\ninserted in slot C (Bottom bank of slot C has already been\nbound into segment 1; address $0000 - $3FFF is bound at\n$4000 - $7FFF)\n\nThis routine will poll for known Intel I28Fxxxx and AMD AM29Fxxx\nFlash Memory chips and return the appropriate ID, if a card\nis recognized.\n\nThe core polling routines are available in OZ lowram.def.\nEntry: B = lowest Bank (number) of slot where to poll for Card ID; C = MS_S1 (segment 1\nspecifier); HL = points into bound bank of potential Flash Memory; E = API slot number.\nExit: Fc = 0 (FE was recognized in slot C); H = manufacturer code (at $00 0000 on chip); L =\ndevice code (at $00 0001 on chip); Fc = 1 (FE was NOT recognized in slot C).\nChanges: F, BC, HL, IY, BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: A, DE, IX, AF'."},
        "4297": {"comment":"slot number supplied to this library from outside caller..."},
        "4298": {"comment":"Get bottom Bank of slot C into segment 1"},
        "4299": {"comment":"old bank binding in BC..."},
        "4301": {"comment":"preserve pointer to Flash Memory segment"},
        "4304": {"comment":"get a copy into DE of the slot contents at the location"},
        "4305": {"comment":"where the ID is fetched (through the FE command interface)"},
        "4306": {"comment":"back at $00 0000"},
        "4308": {"comment":"run INTEL card ID routine in lowram.def"},
        "4313": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "4314": {"comment":"Assume that no INTEL Flash Memory ID is stored at that location!"},
        "4316": {"comment":"if the ID in HL is different from DE"},
        "4317": {"comment":"then an ID was fetched from an INTEL FlashFile Memory..."},
        "4321": {"comment":"pointer to Flash Memory segment"},
        "4326": {"comment":"run AMD/STM card ID routine in lowram.def"},
        "4329": {"comment":"H = Manufacturer Code, L = Device Code"},
        "4332": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "4336": {"comment":"if the ID in HL is equal to DE"},
        "4338": {"comment":"then no AMD/STM Flash Memory responded to the ID request..."},
        "4343": {"comment":"restore original bank in segment 1 (defined in BC)"},
        "4347": {"comment":"get preserved AF"},
        "4348": {"comment":"restore original A"},
        "4350": {"synopsis":"Investigate if a RAM card is inserted in slot C\n(by trying to write a byte to address $00 0000 and\nverify that it was properly written)\nEntry: B = lowest Bank (number) of slot where to poll for Card ID; C = MS_S1 (segment 1\nspecifier); HL points into bank of potential Flash Memory or RAM.\nExit: Fc = 0, empty slot or EPROM/FLASH Card in slot C; Fc = 1, RAM card found in slot C.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4351": {"comment":"Get bottom Bank of slot C into segment 1"},
        "4352": {"comment":"old bank binding in BC..."},
        "4354": {"comment":"preserve the original byte (needs to be restored)"},
        "4355": {"comment":"initial test bit pattern (bit 0 set)"},
        "4357": {"comment":"write bit pattern to card at bottom location"},
        "4358": {"comment":"and check whether it was written"},
        "4359": {"comment":"bit pattern wasn't written..."},
        "4361": {"comment":"check that all bits are written properly"},
        "4364": {"comment":"restore original byte at RAM location"},
        "4366": {"comment":"restore original A"},
        "4368": {"comment":"restore original bank in segment 1 (defined in BC)"},
        "4371": {"comment":"Fc = 0, this is not a RAM card"},
        "4374": {"synopsis":"IY points at base of stack workspace\n\nStandard Z88 File Eprom Format (using Flash Eprom Card).\n\nCopy file entry from one file area to another file area in slot C (or to file area in same slot).\n\nThe routine does NOT handle automatical \"deletion\" of existing files that matches the filename\n(excl. device). This must be used by a call to <FlashEprFileDelete>.\n\nShould the actual process of blowing the file image fail, the new File Entry will be marked as\ndeleted, if possible.\n\nThe screen is turned off while copying a file to flash file area that is in the same slot as the\nOZ ROM. During copying, no interference should happen from Blink, because the Blink reads the font\nbitmaps each 1/100 second:\nWhen copying to a file area which is part of the OZ ROM chip, the font bitmaps are suddenly\nunavailable which creates violent screen flickering during chip command mode. Further, and most\nimportantly, the Blink must be prohibited doing read-cycles while chip is in command mode.\nBy switching off the screen, the Blink doesn't read the font bit maps in OZ ROM, and the Flash chip\ncan be in command mode without being disturbed by the Blink.\n\nImportant:\nINTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require the 12V VPP pin in slot 3 to successfully blow data to\nthe memory chip. If the Flash Eprom card is inserted in slot 1 or 2, this routine will report a\nprogramming failure.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to evaluate the Flash Memory\n(using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the user that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the\nZ88 slot 3 hardware, so this type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nDesign & Programming by Gunther Strube, Oct 2006\nOZ source name: FlashEprCopyFileEntry.\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3); BHL = pointer to file entry to be copied.\nExit: Fc = 0,; File successfully copied to File Area in slot C.; Fc = 1,; File (Flash) Eprom\nnot available in slot C:; A = RC_Nfe (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip); File Entry at BHL\nwas not found, or no file area in slot C:; A = RC_Onf; No sufficient space to store file\n(and File Entry Header) in slot C:; A = RC_Room; Flash Write Errors:; If possible, the new\nFile Entry is marked as deleted.; A = RC_Vpl, RC_Bwr (see \"flashepr.def\" for details).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"preserve IX"},
        "4378": {"comment":"preserve CDE"},
        "4379": {"comment":"preserve original IY"},
        "4381": {"comment":"use alternate registers temporarily"},
        "4386": {"comment":"create temporary work buffer on stack"},
        "4394": {"comment":"preserve a copy of original SP on return"},
        "4396": {"comment":"preserve slot number of File Eprom Card"},
        "4401": {"comment":"discard segment mask, if any..."},
        "4409": {"comment":"preserve pointer to source File Entry..."},
        "4412": {"comment":"return CDE = file image size, A = length of entry filename"},
        "4415": {"comment":"File entry not recognised, exit with error..."},
        "4418": {"comment":"file entry header size = length of filename + 1 + file length (4 bytes)"},
        "4423": {"comment":"total size of file entry = header + image"},
        "4426": {"comment":"total file size > 64K, adjust 24bit high byte"},
        "4427": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: preserve_entrysize."},
        "4438": {"comment":"high word of file entry size"},
        "4439": {"comment":"low word of file entry size"},
        "4440": {"comment":"scan File Eprom in slot X for free space"},
        "4443": {"comment":"returned in DEBC (Fc = 0, File area is available from FileEprFileEntryInfo...)"},
        "4447": {"comment":"HL = low word of 32bit free space..."},
        "4451": {"comment":"HL = high word of 32bit free space..."},
        "4452": {"comment":"DE = high word of file size"},
        "4455": {"comment":"there's room for file in slot C, start to copy..."},
        "4459": {"comment":"file size (incl. File Entry Header) > free space, don't copy..."},
        "4465": {"comment":"make sure that a flash card is available in slot C.."},
        "4468": {"comment":"yes, remember flash type for later"},
        "4471": {"comment":"no flash card - no copying..."},
        "4474": {"comment":"poll slot (in A) for running OZ"},
        "4477": {"comment":"yes, copying file to file area in OZ ROM (slot 0 or 1) requires LCD turned off"},
        "4480": {"comment":"Now, copy source file entry to file area in slot C..."},
        "4483": {"comment":"always turn on screen after copy file operation"},
        "4486": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_FlashEprCopyFileEntry."},
        "4487": {"comment":"restore original SP"},
        "4488": {"comment":"IY"},
        "4490": {"comment":"and the usual gang..."},
        "4496": {"synopsis":"Copies a file entry to the file area of a flash card for FlashEprCopyEnt: gets a new entry\npointer (FileEprNewEntry), then blows the entry block by block, each block ending at a bank\nboundary (FileEprXferBlkSz, FlashEprCopyBlock). If a block fails, the new entry is marked as\ndeleted.\nEntry: C = slot number; IY = work buffer with SrcFileEntry, SrcFileSize and FepType set.\nExit: Fc = 0, entry copied.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (no file area, or the write error of FlashEprCopyBlock).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, BC', DE', HL'.","comment":"BHL = pointer to free file space on File Eprom Card"},
        "4499": {"comment":"no file area recognized in slot C!"},
        "4505": {"comment":"preserve destination File Entry pointer if copy fails.."},
        "4508": {"comment":"(and needs to marked as deleted)"},
        "4517": {"comment":"BHL = pointer to source File Entry..."},
        "4527": {"comment":"total file size to copy to slot C..."},
        "4531": {"comment":"file size = 0?"},
        "4535": {"comment":"No, bytes still left to copy..."},
        "4541": {"comment":"File entry was successfully copied to file area!"},
        "4542": {"comment":"get block size in hl' based on current BHL pointer & file size in cde'"},
        "4545": {"comment":"get chip programming type FE_xxx"},
        "4550": {"comment":"preserve remaining file size"},
        "4552": {"comment":"size of block to copy"},
        "4555": {"comment":"copy file entry from BHL to Flash Card at CDE, block size IY"},
        "4560": {"comment":"restore remaining file size = CDE"},
        "4562": {"comment":"if block successfully blown (Fc = 0), then get next block from source file"},
        "4564": {"comment":"write block failure!"},
        "4574": {"comment":"mark Destination File Entry as deleted, if possible."},
        "4577": {"comment":"and exit with error code from FlashEprCopyBlock"},
        "4579": {"synopsis":"Flash Eprom File Area Formatting.\n\nCreate/reformat an \"oz\" File Area below application Rom Area, or on empty\nFlash Cards to create a normal \"oz\" File Eprom that is also recognized by\nFiler popdown in slot 3.\nReformat file areas that are embedded as part of application cards, located\nat top of card above the application area (automatically preserving 'OZ'\nheader during reformat of file area).\n\nAn 'oz' file card header or 'OZ' application card header with embedded 'oz'\nfile area watermark is 64 bytes large, and is located at the top (last bank)\nof the file area at offset $3FC0.\n\nDefining 8 banks in the ROM Front DOR for applications will leave 58\nbanks for file storage in a 1Mb Flash Card. This scheme is however always\nperformed with only formatting the Flash Eprom in free modulus 64K blocks,\nie. having defined 5 banks for ROM would \"waste\" three banks for applications.\n\nHence, ROM Front DOR definitions should always define bank reserved for\napplications in modulus 64K, eg. 4 banks, 8, 12, etc...\n\nThe screen is turned off while formatting a file area when we're in the\nsame slot as the OZ ROM. During formatting, no interference should happen\nfrom Blink, because the Blink reads the font bitmaps each 1/100 second:\nWhen formatting is part of OZ ROM chip, the font bitmaps are suddenly\nunavailable which creates violent screen flickering during chip command mode.\nFurther, and most importantly, avoid Blink doing read-cycles while\nchip is in command mode.\nBy switching off the screen, the Blink doesn't read the font bit maps in\nOZ ROM, and the Flash chip can be in command mode without being disturbed\nby the Blink.\n\nImportant:\nThird generation AMD Flash Memory chips may be erased/programmed in all\navailable slots (1-3). Only INTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require\nthe 12V VPP pin in slot 3 to successfully erase or blow data on the\nmemory chip. If the Flash Eprom card is inserted in slot 1 or 2,\nthis routine will report a programming failure.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to\nevaluate the Flash Memory (using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the\nuser that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the Z88 slot 3 hardware, so\nthis type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nDue to a strange side effect with Intel Flash Chips, a special \"NULL\" file\nis saved as the first file to the Card. These bytes occupies the first\nbytes that otherwise could be interpreted as a random boot command for the\nIntel chip - the behaviour is an Intel chip suddenly gone into command\nmode for no particular reason.\n\nThe NULL file prevents this behaviour by saving a file that avoids any\nkind of boot commands which sends the chip into command mode when the card\nhas been inserted into a Z88 slot.\n\nAll sectors erased and a new header blown.\n\nFailure:\nFc = 1\nA = RC_ONF (File Eprom Card / Area not available; possibly no card in slot)\nA = RC_ROOM (No room for File Area; all banks used for applications)\nA = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip)\nA = RC_BER (error occurred when erasing block/sector)\nA = RC_BWR (couldn't write header to Flash Memory)\nA = RC_VPL (Vpp Low Error)\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube,\nDec 1997-Apr 1998, Aug 2004, July 2005, July 2006, Aug-Oct-Nov 2006, Mar 2007\nOZ source name: FlashEprFileFormat.\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3) of Flash Memory Card.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0,; BHL = pointer to File Header for slot C (B = absolute bank of\nslot).; (or pointer to free space in potential new File Area).; C = size of File Eprom Area\nin 16K banks; Fz = 1, File Header available; A = \"oz\" File Eprom sub type; D = size of card\nin 16K banks (0 - 64).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
