        "4792": {"synopsis":"The null file that SaveNullFile blows at the bottom of an Intel flash card after formatting:\n6 bytes, a file entry with a 1-character name ($00) and a file length of 0."},
        "4798": {"synopsis":"Return Fz = 1, if Flash chip sector size is 16K (otherwise it's a 64K sector architecture)\n\nThis library routine is used as an internal shared support library by several other public\nFlash chip libraries.\nOZ source name: FlashEprPollSectorSize.\nEntry: HL = Flash Memory ID; H = Manufacturer Code (FE_INTEL_MFCD, FE_AMD_MFCD); L = Device\nCode (refer to flashepr.def).\nExit: Fz = 1, Flash chip uses a 16K sector size; Fz = 0, Flash chip uses a 64K sector size.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4799": {"comment":"AM29F010B Flash Memory?"},
        "4802": {"comment":"Fc = 0..."},
        "4809": {"synopsis":"Flash Eprom File Area Shrinking.\n\nReduce an existing \"oz\" File Area below application/OZ Rom Area, or on sole\nFlash Card by one or several 64K sectors.\n\nThis routine will signal failure (\"file area not found\") if an\napplication wants to reduce a file area that is part of the OZ ROM in slot 0\n\nImportant:\nThird generation AMD Flash Memory chips may be erased/programmed in all\navailable slots (1-3). Only INTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require\nthe 12V VPP pin in slot 3 to successfully erase or blow data on the\nmemory chip. If the Flash Eprom card is inserted in slot 1 or 2,\nthis routine will report a programming failure.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to\nevaluate the Flash Memory (using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the\nuser that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the Z88 slot 3 hardware, so\nthis type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nCurrent files in file area are intact.\nNew header blown (for reduced file area) and old header sector erased.\n\nFailure:\nFc = 1\nA = RC_ONF (File Eprom Card / Area not available; possibly no card in slot)\nA = RC_ROOM (File area cannot be reduced - files are located inside reducing sector)\nA = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip)\nA = RC_BER (error occurred when erasing block/sector)\nA = RC_BWR (couldn't write header to Flash Memory)\nA = RC_VPL (Vpp Low Error)\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Feb 2006, July-Aug 2006, Feb 2009\nOZ source name: FlashEprReduceFileArea.\nEntry: B = total sectors to reduce file area; C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3) of Flash Memory\nCard.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0,; BHL = absolute pointer to new \"oz\" header in card; C = Number of\n16K banks of File Eprom Area.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY."},
        "4813": {"comment":"argument defined as slot 0?"},
        "4818": {"comment":"file area cannot be shrinked in slot 0..."},
        "4820": {"comment":"poll slot (in A) for running OZ"},
        "4823": {"comment":"OZ is running in slot 1.."},
        "4826": {"comment":"(preserve sector number)"},
        "4827": {"comment":"Flash Card available in slot C?"},
