        "5063": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: err_FlashEprStdFileHeader.","comment":"restore registers..."},
        "5066": {"comment":"return error code in AF..."},
        "5070": {"synopsis":"Returns the flash chip generation of the card that holds a bank, for FlashStdFileHdr: the\nslot comes from the bank (GetSlotNo) and the type from FlashEprCardId.\nEntry: B = absolute bank.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = FE_28F or FE_29F.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_NFE (no known flash chip).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "5072": {"comment":"get slot C of bank B"},
        "5075": {"comment":"return A = FE_ chip type"},
        "5081": {"synopsis":"The last 6 bytes of a new \"oz\" file area header, copied by FlashStdFileHdr to $3FFA: the\nhigh word of the random id ($01, $80), a size placeholder ($40), a sub type placeholder\n($FF), both overwritten afterwards, and \"oz\"."},
        "5087": {"synopsis":"Unsigned 8bit division\nEntry: H = Dividend; L = Divisor.\nExit: Fc = 0, division completed; H = Quotient; L = Remainder; Fc = 1,; A = RC_Dvz (divide\nby 0).\nChanges: ......./IXIY same, AF...HL/.... different."},
        "5100": {"comment":"advancing a bit"},
        "5102": {"comment":"..."},
        "5103": {"comment":"checking if the divisor divides the digits chosen (in A)"},
        "5104": {"comment":"if not, advance without subtraction"},
        "5106": {"comment":"subtracting the divisor"},
        "5107": {"comment":"and setting the next digit of the quotient"},
        "5110": {"comment":"H = quotient, L = remainder"},
        "5114": {"synopsis":"Write a block of bytes to the Flash Eprom Card, from address\nDE to BHL of block size IX. If a block will cross a bank boundary, it is\nautomatically continued on the next adjacent bank of the card.\nOn return, BHL points at the byte after the last written byte.\n\nThe routine is used by the File Eprom Management libraries, but is well\nsuited for other application purposes.\n\nThe routine can be told which programming algorithm to use (by specifying\nthe FE_28F or FE_29F mnemonic in C); these parameters can be fetched when\ninvestigating which Flash Memory chip is available in the slot, using the\nFlashEprCardId routine that reports these constants.\n\nHowever, if neither of the constants are provided in A, the routine can\nbe specified with C = 0 which internally polls the Flash Memory for\nidentification and intelligently use the correct programming algorithm.\nThe identified FE_28F or FE_29F constant is returned to the caller in C\nfor future reference (when the block was successfully programmed to the card).\n\nUses the segment mask of HL(where BHL memory will be bound into the Z80\naddress space to blow the block of bytes (MM_S0 - MM_S3), which has to be\nin a different segment than DE is referring.\n\nBHL points to an absolute bank (which is part of the slot that the Flash\nMemory Card have been inserted into).\n\nFurther, the local buffer must be available in local address space and not\npart of the segment used for blowing bytes.\n\nImportant:\nINTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require the 12V VPP pin in slot 3\nto successfully blow data to the memory chip. If the Flash Eprom card\nis inserted in slot 1 or 2, this routine will report a programming failure.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to\nevaluate the Flash Memory (using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the\nuser that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the Z88 slot 3 hardware, so\nthis type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nDesign & programming by\nGunther Strube, Dec 97, Jan-Apr 98, Aug '04, Oct '05, Aug-Nov '06, Feb '07\nThierry Peycru, Zlab, Dec 1997\nOZ source name: FlashEprWriteBlock.\nEntry: C = FE_28F, FE_29F or 0 (poll card for blowing algorithm); DE = local pointer to\nstart of block (located in current address space); BHL = extended address to start of\ndestination (pointer into card); (bits 7,6 of B is the slot mask); (bits 7,6 of H = MM_Sx\nsegment mask for BHL); IX = size of block (at DE) to blow.\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; C = FE_28F or FE_29F (depending on found card); BHL updated;\nFailure:; Fc = 1; A = RC_BWR (block not blown properly); A = RC_NFE (not a recognized Flash\nMemory Chip); A = RC_UNK (chip type is unknown: use only FE_28F, FE_29F or 0).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY.","comment":"preserve DE"},
        "5115": {"comment":"preserve C"},
        "5117": {"comment":"preserve FE Programming type in A'"},
        "5123": {"comment":"A = slot number of BHL"},
        "5124": {"comment":"remember Flash Memory slot (of BHL pointer) number in C'"},
        "5131": {"comment":"C = MS_Sx"},
        "5133": {"comment":"Bind slot x bank into segment C"},
        "5134": {"comment":"preserve old bank binding of segment C"},
        "5135": {"comment":"but use current bank as reference..."},
        "5139": {"comment":"preserve current Bank number of pointer..."},
        "5141": {"comment":"restore old segment C bank binding"},
        "5143": {"comment":"return updated FEP_xxx type, if C(in) were 0..."},
        "5145": {"comment":"original C register restored..."},
        "5148": {"synopsis":"Write Block to BHL already bound, in slot x, of IX length.\nThis routine will clone itself on the stack and execute there.\nEntry: A' = FE_28F, FE_29F or 0; C' = slot number of BHL pointer; C = MS_Sx segment\nspecifier; DE = local pointer to start of block (available in current address space); BHL =\nextended address to start of destination (pointer into card); IX = size of block to blow.\nExit: Fc = 0, block blown successfully to the Flash Card; A = FE_28F or FE_29F, depending on\nfound chip type; BHL = points at next free byte on Flash Eprom; DE = points beyond last byte\nof buffer; Fc = 1,; A = RC_BWR (block not blown properly); A = RC_UNK (pre-specified chip\ntype is unknown: use only FE_28F, FE_29F or 0); DE,BHL points at byte not blown properly (A\n= RC_BWR).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY.","comment":"FE Programming type in A"},
        "5151": {"comment":"make sure that pre-selected INTEL flash is located in slot 3"},
        "5158": {"comment":"chip type = 0 indicates to get chip type to program it..."},
        "5161": {"comment":"unknown chip type specified!"},
        "5164": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: poll_chip_programming."},
        "5168": {"comment":"Flash in slot C?"},
        "5175": {"comment":"Fc = 1, A = RC error code (Flash Memory not found)"},
        "5176": {"comment":"now, we've got the chip type"},
        "5178": {"comment":"and this one may be programmed in any slot..."},
        "5180": {"comment":"remember FE_28F chip type"},
        "5184": {"comment":"when chip is FE_28F series, we need to be in slot 3"},
        "5186": {"comment":"to make a successful \"write\" of the byte..."},
        "5189": {"comment":"Ups, not in slot 3, signal write error!"},
        "5192": {"comment":"remember FE_29F chip type"},
        "5210": {"comment":"get chip type"},
        "5212": {"comment":"ignore chip type and return error code"},
        "5213": {"comment":"Block was successfully blown, return chip type in A"},
        "5214": {"comment":"Fc = 0 (signal successfull operation)"},
