        "5344": {"comment":"bind new bank into segment C..."},
        "5348": {"synopsis":"Write a byte (in C) to the Flash Memory Card in slot x, at address BHL.\n\nBHL points to a bank, offset (which is part of the slot that the Flash\nMemory Card have been inserted into).\n\nThe routine can be told which programming algorithm to use (by specifying\nthe FE_28F or FE_29F mnemonic in E); these parameters can be fetched when\ninvestigated which Flash Memory chip is available in the slot, using the\nFlashEprCardId routine that reports these constants back to the caller.\n\nHowever, if neither of the constants are provided in E, the routine can\nbe specified with E = 0 which internally polls the Flash Memory for\nidentification and intelligently use the correct programming algorithm.\n\nImportant:\nINTEL I28Fxxxx series Flash chips require the 12V VPP pin in slot 3\nto successfully blow the byte on the memory chip. If the Flash Eprom card\nis inserted in slot 1 or 2, this routine will report a programming failure.\n\nIt is the responsibility of the application (before using this call) to\nevaluate the Flash Memory (using the FlashEprCardId routine) and warn the\nuser that an INTEL Flash Memory Card requires the Z88 slot 3 hardware, so\nthis type of unnecessary error can be avoided.\n\nDesign & programming by\nGunther Strube, Dec 1997, Jan-Apr 98, Aug 2004, Sep 2005, Aug, Nov 2006\nThierry Peycru, Zlab, Dec 1997\nOZ source name: FlashEprWriteByte.\nEntry: C = byte to blow at address; E = FE_28F, FE_29F or 0 (poll card for blowing\nalgorithm); BHL = pointer to Flash Memory address (B=00h-FFh, HL=0000h-3FFFh); (bits 7,6 of\nB is the slot mask).\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0; Failure:; Fc = 1; A = RC_BWR (programming of byte failed); A =\nRC_NFE (not a recognized Flash Memory Chip); A = RC_UNK (chip type is unknown: use only\nFE_28F, FE_29F or 0).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "5350": {"comment":"preserve original pointer"},
        "5356": {"comment":"use segment 1 to write byte to flash.."},
        "5358": {"comment":"copy of bank number"},
        "5359": {"comment":"bind bank B into segment..."},
        "5361": {"comment":"blow byte in A to (BHL) address"},
        "5365": {"comment":"restore original bank binding"},
        "5370": {"synopsis":"Blow byte in Flash Eprom at (HL), segment 1, slot x\nThis routine will clone itself on the stack and execute there.\nEntry: A = byte to blow; D = bank of pointer; E = chip type FE_28F, FE_29F or 0; HL =\npointer to memory location in Flash Memory.\nExit: Fc = 0,; A = byte blown successfully to the Flash Memory; Fc = 1,; A = RC_ error code,\nbyte not blown.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "5371": {"comment":"no predefined programming was specified, let's find out..."},
        "5376": {"comment":"Flash Memory is in slot C (derived from original bank B)"},
        "5377": {"comment":"check for pre-defined Flash Memory programming"},
        "5380": {"comment":"Intel flash programming specified, are we in slot3?"},
        "5387": {"comment":"chip type = 0 indicates to get chip type to program it..."},
        "5390": {"comment":"unknown chip type specified!"},
        "5393": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: poll_chip_programming.","comment":"preserve HL (pointer to write byte)"},
        "5394": {"comment":"return chip ID in HL, FE_x programming type in A"},
        "5398": {"comment":"Fc = 1, A = RC error code (Flash Memory not found)"},
        "5399": {"comment":"now, we've got the chip series"},
        "5401": {"comment":"and this one may be programmed in any slot..."},
        "5403": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: check_slot3."},
        "5405": {"comment":"when chip is FE_28F series, we need to be in slot 3"},
        "5406": {"comment":"restore fetched constant that is returned to the caller.."},
        "5408": {"comment":"to make a successful \"write\" of the byte..."},
        "5410": {"comment":"Ups, not in slot 3, signal error!"},
        "5413": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: use_29F_programming."},
        "5414": {"comment":"blow byte on AMD/STM Flash"},
        "5416": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: use_28F_programming.","comment":"blow byte on INTEL Flash"},
        "5417": {"synopsis":"Program byte in A at (HL) on an INTEL I28Fxxxx Flash Memory\nOZ source name: FEP_ExecBlowbyte_28F.\nEntry: A = byte to blow; HL = pointer to memory location in Flash Memory.\nExit: Fc = 0 & Fz = 0,; A = byte successfully blown to Flash Memory; Fc = 1,; A = RC_BWR,\nbyte not blown."},
        "5418": {"comment":"Address of soft copy of COM register"},
