        "5451": {"comment":"VPP Off"},
        "5454": {"comment":"Signal to HW"},
        "5458": {"synopsis":"Program byte in A at (HL) on an AMD AM29Fxxxx Flash Memory\n\nFc = 0 & Fz = 0,\nA = byte successfully blown to Flash Memory\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_BWR, byte not blown\nOZ source name: FEP_ExecBlowbyte_29F.\nEntry: A = byte to blow; HL = pointer to memory location in Flash Memory.\nExit: B = A(in)."},
        "5468": {"comment":"we're back in Read Array Mode, byte was successfully programmed!"},
        "5472": {"synopsis":"Body of OS_Fn (OSFn calls it inside the OS frame): exchanges A and B and dispatches on the\nreason: FN_AH allocates a handle (AllocHandle), FN_VH verifies one (VerifyHandle), FN_FH\nfrees one (FreeHandle), FN_GH finds one by type and dynamic id (FindHandle), and FN_NH finds\nthe next handle of the same type.\nEntry: A = reason (FN_AH to FN_NH); B = handle type; C = dynamic id (FN_GH); IX = handle.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = handle (FN_AH, FN_GH, FN_NH).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Unk for an unknown reason, RC_Eof after the last handle).","comment":"exg a,b"},
        "5492": {"comment":"exchanged on entry"},
        "5506": {"comment":"last handle"},
        "5507": {"comment":"get type"},
        "5510": {"comment":"dont check dyn id"},
        "5512": {"comment":"jump to next handle"},
        "5525": {"synopsis":"Initialises a device handle: FindHandleDOR takes the first device in DevTable whose id is at\nleast A + 1 and that is present (RAM fitted, ROM or file area found). The device id, the\napplication slot of a ROM device, the DOR's address and the handle flags are stored, then\nthe DOR's bank is bound into S2 and its type returned (GetDORType).\nEntry: A = device id - 1; IX = handle.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = DOR type (Fz = 1 when it is 0); the DOR's bank bound into S2.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail (no such device left in DevTable).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5528": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "5534": {"comment":"not ROM? skip"},
        "5536": {"comment":"low 2 bits to top"},
        "5542": {"comment":"application handle start"},
        "5556": {"comment":"RAM.-? skip !! why not longer?"},
        "5558": {"comment":"!! 'rlca; rlca; rlca; or $80' for clarity"},
        "5563": {"comment":"mask out low bits"},
        "5565": {"comment":"low bits: RAM=01, others=11"},
        "5572": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=ID-1.\nExit: Fc=0, BHL=DOR address, C=device handle flags (bit 0 and 1); Fc=1, A=error if fail.\nChanges: ABCDEHL/...."},
        "5578": {"comment":"device ID"},
        "5580": {"comment":"end? error"},
        "5583": {"comment":"DE = DOR address"},
        "5588": {"comment":"smaller than wanted? loop"},
