        "5752": {"comment":"EPR.3 for Eprom Filing System"},
        "5757": {"synopsis":"DOR of the SCR.0 (screen) device, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (parent, brother, son, 3\nbytes each), type Dm_Chd, the length, the name record \"SCR.0\" and $FF. The parent field\nholds its handle for OS_Nq ($8606, NQ_Shn)."},
        "5777": {"synopsis":"DOR of the PRT.0 (printer) device, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (parent, brother, son,\n3 bytes each), type Dm_Chd, the length, the name record \"PRT.0\" and $FF. The parent field\nholds its handle for OS_Nq ($8609, NQ_Phn)."},
        "5797": {"synopsis":"DOR of the COM.0 (serial port) device, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (parent, brother,\nson, 3 bytes each), type Dm_Chd, the length, the name record \"COM.0\" and $FF. The parent\nfield holds its handle for OS_Nq ($8C1E, NQ_Chn)."},
        "5817": {"synopsis":"DOR of the NUL.0 (null) device, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (parent, brother, son, 3\nbytes each), type Dm_Chd, the length, the name record \"NUL.0\" and $FF. The parent field\nholds its handle for OS_Nq ($860C, NQ_Nhn)."},
        "5837": {"synopsis":"DOR of the INP.0 (input) device, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (parent, brother, son, 3\nbytes each), type Dm_Chd, the length, the name record \"INP.0\" and $FF. The parent field\nholds its handle for OS_Nq ($8615, NQ_Ihn)."},
        "5857": {"synopsis":"DOR of the OUT.0 (output) device, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (parent, brother, son, 3\nbytes each), type Dm_Chd, the length, the name record \"OUT.0\" and $FF. The parent field\nholds its handle for OS_Nq ($8618, NQ_Ohn)."},
        "5877": {"synopsis":"ROM.0 application DOR's only exist when compiling OZ for slot 0\n- booting OZ in slot 1 must ignore all applications in slot 0 due conflict with same in slot 1"},
        "5897": {"synopsis":"DOR of the ROM.1 device, 20 bytes: the parent and brother pointers (0), the son pointer to\nthe ROM Front DOR at the top of slot 1 (ROM_DOR in S2, bank RO1_BNK), type DM_ROM, the\nlength, the name record \"ROM.1\" and $FF."},
        "5917": {"synopsis":"DOR of the ROM.2 device, 20 bytes: the parent and brother pointers (0), the son pointer to\nthe ROM Front DOR at the top of slot 2 (ROM_DOR in S2, bank RO2_BNK), type DM_ROM, the\nlength, the name record \"ROM.2\" and $FF."},
        "5937": {"synopsis":"DOR of the ROM.3 device, 20 bytes: the parent and brother pointers (0), the son pointer to\nthe ROM Front DOR at the top of slot 3 (ROM_DOR in S2, bank RO3_BNK), type DM_ROM, the\nlength, the name record \"ROM.3\" and $FF."},
        "5957": {"synopsis":"DOR of the APP.- device, 20 bytes: the parent and brother pointers (0), the son pointer to\nthe Front DOR of the installed applications (APX_DOR in S2, bank APX_BNK), type DM_ROM, the\nlength, the name record \"APP.-\" and $FF."},
        "5977": {"synopsis":"DOR of the EPR.0 device of the Eprom filing system, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (all\n0), type Dm_Epr, the length, the name record \"EPR.0\" and $FF."},
        "5997": {"synopsis":"DOR of the EPR.1 device of the Eprom filing system, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (all\n0), type Dm_Epr, the length, the name record \"EPR.1\" and $FF."},
        "6017": {"synopsis":"DOR of the EPR.2 device of the Eprom filing system, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (all\n0), type Dm_Epr, the length, the name record \"EPR.2\" and $FF."},
        "6037": {"synopsis":"DOR of the EPR.3 device of the Eprom filing system, 20 bytes: the three link pointers (all\n0), type Dm_Epr, the length, the name record \"EPR.3\" and $FF."},
        "6057": {"synopsis":"Resets the machine, entered from Boot_reset with kernel bank 1 in S2; it never returns.\n1. A hard reset (the flap was open, or bank $21 does not start with the RAM tag) fills banks\n$21 and $20 with 0; a soft reset clears bank $20 except the preserved system variables. The\ntype ($00 hard, $FF soft) goes to ubResetType.\n2. Writes InitData to the Blink and its soft copies, copies the low-RAM code into bank $20,\nmaps it at $0000 (COM), sets SP = $2000 and the kernel bank soft copies.\n3. Resets the handles, sets the screen addresses with OS_Sci, clears the buffers\n(InitBuffers) and prints \"HARD RESET ...\" or \"SOFT RESET ...\".\n4. Allocates the filing-system memory pool, initialises RAM, marks the system and swap pages\nand expands the machine when a 128K card is present (ExpandMachine).\n5. After a soft reset restores the panel (PreserveSysPanel); sets the time (TimeReset), the\nrandom seed and the RAM devices, moves the screen base file to bank $21 and resets the\nserial interface.\n6. Sets the default device to the expanded RAM card (defDev), installs the panel defaults,\nenables interrupts and enters the Index (OS_Ent) in an endless loop.\nEntry: A' = interrupt status (its flap-open bit is tested)."},
        "6058": {"comment":"interrupt status"},
        "6063": {"comment":"flap open during reset? Reset bank $21 and $20 during hard reset"},
        "6065": {"comment":"flap not open,"},
        "6070": {"comment":"check RAM tag in bank $21"},
        "6076": {"comment":"not tagged? hard reset if memory is not partitioned"},
        "6078": {"comment":"soft reset - a' = $FF, fc'=1"},
        "6088": {"comment":"[0000-sysvar_area] is overwritten by lowram.bin"},
        "6113": {"comment":"fill banks $21 and $20 with 00"},
        "6122": {"comment":"bind A into S1"},
        "6131": {"comment":"loop if hard reset"},
        "6140": {"comment":"port"},
        "6144": {"comment":"end of init data"},
        "6146": {"comment":"data byte"},
        "6150": {"comment":"write blink"},
        "6152": {"comment":"softcopy in S1"},
        "6157": {"synopsis":"copy low RAM code and install it in lower 8K of segment 0"},
        "6159": {"comment":"bind MTH bank into S3"},
        "6164": {"comment":"and copy LOWRAM code into"},
        "6167": {"comment":"destination b20 in S1"},
        "6174": {"comment":"restore KNL0 bank"},
        "6186": {"comment":"install LOWRAM in lower 8K of segment 0"},
        "6188": {"comment":"init stack"},
        "6191": {"comment":"define soft copy of current kernel bank bindings"},
        "6194": {"comment":"because they are used by OZ call interface.."},
        "6207": {"comment":"LORES0 at 21:2200-22FF (32 UDG)"},
        "6215": {"comment":"LORES1 at 02(7C):1000-1DFF"},
        "6223": {"comment":"HIRES0 at 21:2000-21FF (64 pixels map, max 2K)"},
        "6231": {"comment":"HIRES1 at 02(7C):0800-25FF"},
        "6239": {"comment":"SBF at 20:7800-7FFF (2K) - temporary, will be moved"},
        "6245": {"comment":"print reset string"},
        "6289": {"comment":"allocate memory pool, A=mask"},
        "6291": {"comment":"crash if no memory"},
        "6293": {"comment":"filesystem pool"},
        "6305": {"comment":"b20, 0000-0fff - system variables"},
        "6313": {"comment":"b20, 1000-17ff - swap RAM"},
        "6321": {"comment":"b20, 1800-1fff - stack"},
        "6329": {"comment":"b20, 2000-3fff - 8KB for bad apps"},
        "6337": {"comment":"b21, 3800-3fff - SBF"},
        "6345": {"comment":"b21, 2000-22ff - Hires0+Lores0, lost if expanded !"},
        "6348": {"comment":"move Lores0/Hires0 and mark more swap RAM if expanded"},
        "6355": {"comment":"restore preserved system panel values"},
        "6361": {"comment":"set pointer system variable for random seed"},
        "6373": {"comment":"SBF at 21:7800-7FFF"},
        "6378": {"comment":"hard reset serial interface"},
