        "6392": {"comment":"point at device number"},
        "6393": {"comment":"get bottom bank of expanded RAM card.."},
        "6397": {"comment":"no expanded RAM were found"},
        "6405": {"comment":"define default expanded RAM card slot number"},
        "6411": {"comment":"install new default RAM device"},
        "6413": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: install_panel_defaults."},
        "6416": {"comment":"initialize panel, serial port and printer"},
        "6419": {"comment":"time to enter new application"},
        "6421": {"comment":"first handle (in slot 0, identified with slot mask $00)"},
        "6425": {"comment":"enter new Index process!"},
        "6430": {"synopsis":"The default device name \":RAM.0\" (6 bytes, no terminator). Reset copies it to $1800, and\nwhen an expanded RAM card is found replaces the digit with its slot and sets it with OS_Sp\nPA_Dev."},
        "6436": {"synopsis":"*** Reset subroutines ***"},
        "6439": {"comment":"not expanded? exit"},
        "6441": {"comment":"$21"},
        "6446": {"comment":"$0000-09ff - Hires0+Lores0"},
        "6451": {"comment":"$2800 - 2 pages"},
        "6455": {"comment":"LORES0 at $xx 0800"},
        "6460": {"comment":"$2000 - 8 pages"},
        "6464": {"comment":"HIRES0 at $xx 0000"},
        "6467": {"comment":"D = first expanded bank"},
        "6469": {"comment":"$0000 - 128 pages"},
        "6472": {"comment":"b22/b41/b81, $0000-7fff - 32KB more for bad apps"},
        "6475": {"synopsis":"PreserveSystemPanel: gives the panel values kept over a soft reset back to the panel,\ncalling OS_Sp with a length of 1 for PA_Loc down to $8001 with cCountry, ubBadSize, cSound,\ncKeyclick, ubRepeat and ubTimeout.\nOZ source name: PreserveSystemPanel.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "6482": {"comment":"length is 1 byte for each value"},
        "6484": {"comment":"specify parameter"},
        "6492": {"synopsis":"Sets the clock at reset. After a soft reset the elapsed time from the hardware clock copy\n(ubTIM1_A, or ubTIM1_B when bit 0 of ubTimeBufferSelect is set) updates the base time\n(GN_Msc MT_UBT); after a hard reset SetInitialTime sets the date and time of the build\n(GN_Dei, GN_Pmd, GN_Pmt). Both end in IntSecond.\nEntry: ubResetType ($00 hard, $FF soft)."},
        "6496": {"comment":"hard reset, init system clock"},
        "6498": {"comment":"use primary HW clock"},
        "6501": {"comment":"if bit 7 reset"},
        "6507": {"comment":"else use secundary HW clock"},
        "6509": {"comment":"seconds"},
        "6511": {"comment":"minutes"},
        "6513": {"comment":"minutes * 256"},
        "6515": {"comment":"minutes * 65536"},
        "6517": {"comment":"update base time"},
        "6519": {"comment":"maintain time over a soft reset"},
        "6531": {"comment":"convert to internal format"},
        "6534": {"comment":"date in ABC"},
        "6537": {"comment":"set machine date according to current date of compilation"},
        "6546": {"comment":"set clock according to current time of compilation"},
        "6551": {"synopsis":"Blink initialisation table read by Reset: pairs of port and value, ended by 0. SR2 gets\nkernel bank 1, the timer interrupt mask and acknowledge get tick, second and minute, INT\nenables flap, battery low, time and global interrupts, ACK acknowledges A19, flap, battery\nlow and keyboard, and EPR gets 0. Each value also goes to the port's soft copy.","comment":"SR2 = kernel bank 1"},
        "6561": {"comment":"reset EPROM port"},
        "6564": {"synopsis":"Initialize OZ buffers at reset","comment":"256 bytes for RX buffer"},
        "6576": {"comment":"32 bytes for buffer and 16 for pointers"},
        "6582": {"comment":"initialise Kb Rd and Wr position"},
        "6590": {"comment":"kb variables"},
        "6596": {"synopsis":"Zeroes BC bytes from HL: clears the first byte and copies it forward with LDIR. InitBuffers\ncalls it for the serial receive buffer and the keyboard buffer, then sets HL = KbdData and\nBC = kbd_SIZEOF and falls into it for the keyboard variables.\nEntry: HL = the area; BC = its length (at least 2: BC is decremented before the LDIR); HL\nnot at a $xxFF address (DE is made with INC E).\nExit: the area is zero; BC = 0; HL = its last byte; DE = the byte after it.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL; F (P/V).\nKeeps: A, IX, IY."},
        "6605": {"synopsis":"alarm manipulation\n\n!! some simple calls end with 'or a' to clear Fc, others don't\n!! better to do that in beginning to assert Fc=0\nEntry: A=reason; AH_SUSP ($01), suspend alarm; AH_REV ($02), revive alarms; AH_RES ($03),\nreset alarm enable state; AH_SINC ($04), display symbol; AH_SDEC ($05), remove symbol\n(subject to use count); AH_SRES ($06), reset symbol; AH_SET ($07), Set a new alarm; BDE =\nroutine address to be called on expiry !! needs more documentation; HL = 6 byte date, time;\nAH_CNC ($08), Cancel an alarm:; IX = alarm handle; AH_DG1 ($09), Ding-dong type 1; AH_DG2\n($0A), Ding-dong type 2; AH_AINC ($0B), action count increment; AH_ADEC ($0C), action count\ndecrement; AH_ARES ($0D), action count reset.\nExit: Fc=0 if ok SUSP-SRES, DG1-ARES always return this; Fc=1, A=error if fail; AH_SET\nreturns Fc=1, A=0 in case new alarm went active immediately.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6610": {"comment":"suspend alarms"},
        "6615": {"comment":"revive alarms"},
        "6620": {"comment":"reset alarm enable state"},
        "6624": {"comment":"ubAlmDisplayCnt"},
        "6627": {"comment":"display symbol"},
        "6631": {"comment":"remove symbol (subject to use count)"},
        "6635": {"comment":"reset symbol"},
        "6639": {"comment":"set a new alarm"},
        "6657": {"comment":"copy date/time into handle"},
        "6685": {"comment":"cancel an alarm"},
        "6688": {"comment":"BC=next from this"},
        "6709": {"comment":"if not found then we got bad handle"},
        "6714": {"comment":"not same? try next"},
        "6716": {"comment":"remove IX from list"},
        "6729": {"comment":"decrement active count and remove pending alarm task if needed"},
        "6749": {"comment":"ding-dong type 1"},
        "6760": {"comment":"ding-dong type 2"},
