        "6960": {"comment":"calculate time till next alarm"},
        "6989": {"synopsis":"OS_Cli: the CLI interface (internal). Reason 0 (undocumented) returns at once through\nOZCallReturn2 with A = ubCLIActiveCnt and IX = KbdData. Any other reason builds the OS frame\n(OSFramePush), exchanges A and B so that B holds the reason, runs OSCliMain and returns\nthrough OSFramePop.\nEntry: A = reason: 0, or CL_RIM, CL_MBC, CL_CMB, CL_INC, CL_DEC, CL_RES, CL_ACK (1-7); the\nother registers as the reason needs them (see OSCliMain).\nExit: reason 0: A = the CLI use count; IX = KbdData. Others: as OSCliMain.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Unk for a reason above 7; others as OSCliMain."},
        "6991": {"comment":"!! undocumented reason 0"},
        "6997": {"comment":"exchange A and B"},
        "7006": {"synopsis":"A=0 - return CLIActiveCnt and KbdData"},
        "7013": {"comment":"ret with AFbcdehl"},
        "7016": {"synopsis":"The body of OS_Cli: counts B down with DJNZ to pick the reason, with HL = ubCLIActiveCnt and\nFc = 0. Results go into the OS frame (IY). CL_RIM: reads raw input from the keyboard buffer\n(RdKbBuffer) with BC as the timeout; returns BC = the time left, D = 0, E = the character.\nCL_MBC: E = a character, D = its qualifiers; translates it (CLIchar2key for a control code\nor a special key, then ApplyQualifiers) and returns E = the result, D = 0. CL_CMB: E = a key\ncode; returns E = the base character and D = its qualifiers (Key2Meta). CL_INC: increments\nthe CLI use count; when it was 0, first clears IST_B_CLISHIFT and IST_B_CLIDMND in\nubIntStatus. CL_DEC decrements it, CL_RES sets it to 0. These three then request an OZ\nwindow redraw (SetPendingOZwd). CL_ACK: D = the keys to acknowledge (QUAL_B_CTRL clears\nIST_B_CLIDMND, QUAL_B_SHIFT clears IST_B_CLISHIFT); returns D = the remaining IST_CLISHIFT\nand IST_CLIDMND bits and Fz = 1 when neither is set.\nEntry: B = reason (1-7); A = the caller's B; C, DE as the reason needs; IY = the OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0; the results in the OS frame as above.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (from RdKbBuffer, or RC_Unk for an unknown reason)."},
        "7019": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "7023": {"comment":"get raw input"},
        "7026": {"comment":"return timeout"},
        "7033": {"comment":"meta/base to character conversion"},
        "7034": {"comment":"if ctlr char, translate to keycode"},
        "7036": {"comment":"!! nop, all inchars alphabetic"},
        "7041": {"comment":"special key? translate to keycode"},
        "7044": {"comment":"translate A with qualifiers D"},
        "7047": {"comment":"clear qualifiers"},
        "7049": {"comment":"return error"},
        "7050": {"comment":"else char just read/translated"},
        "7056": {"comment":"character to meta/base conversion"},
        "7060": {"comment":"return key and qualifiers"},
        "7064": {"comment":"increment CLI use count"},
        "7068": {"comment":"first active CLI, reset flags"},
        "7082": {"comment":"decrement CLI use count"},
        "7087": {"comment":"reset CLI use count !! ld (hl), b"},
        "7094": {"comment":"acknowledge CLI/Escape"},
        "7097": {"comment":"!! bits match, use ld a,d; and 3; cpl; and (hl); ld (hl),a"},
        "7109": {"comment":"return A=resulting shift/ctrl status, Fz=1 if neither active"},
        "7125": {"synopsis":"this is branched into from below"},
        "7128": {"synopsis":"translate char after '~' into keycode\nA=translate(A)"},
        "7145": {"comment":"found at even offset, return byte"},
        "7147": {"comment":"loop if not end"},
        "7151": {"synopsis":"translate keyboard code into meta char\nA,D=translate(A)","comment":"!! ld hl,tbl-2; inc hl; inc hl"},
        "7156": {"comment":"found key area, translate"},
        "7158": {"comment":"try next"},
        "7162": {"comment":"qualifier"},
        "7164": {"comment":"address low byte"},
        "7165": {"comment":"address high byte (was crsr)"},
        "7169": {"comment":"return if no table"},
        "7170": {"comment":"mask to range"},
        "7171": {"comment":"and point to char"},
        "7173": {"comment":"skip mask byte"},
        "7174": {"comment":"return meta char"},
        "7176": {"synopsis":"update application static handle in env process\nEntry: IX=current application, BC= new application static handle.\nExit: -."},
        "7179": {"synopsis":"poll for an application\nEntry: IX=current application, 0 for start of list.\nExit: IX=next application; Fc=0 if ok; Fc=1, A=error if fail."},
        "7190": {"synopsis":"Finds the application after the one in C: asks GetAppDOR for application C + 1 and returns\nits number in BC. OS_Poll calls it with BC = the caller's IX.\nEntry: C = the current application number (0 for the start of the list).\nExit: Fc = 0; BC = the next application's number (B = 0).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Eof when there is no further application.\nChanges: AF, BC, and what GetAppDOR changes."},
        "7191": {"comment":"next application"},
        "7192": {"comment":"go find it"},
        "7201": {"synopsis":"Poll for OZ usage in slot\nEntry: a=slot number (0-3).\nExit: Fz=0, if OZ is running in slot, otherwise Fz = 1; No registers changed except Fz.","comment":"exclude slot 2 and 3"},
        "7206": {"comment":"A=0, OZ in slot 0"},
        "7207": {"comment":"Fz=1, OZ not found"},
        "7211": {"comment":"Fc = 0, dont return error from this system call.."},
        "7213": {"synopsis":"clear unsafe stack area","comment":"stack top"},
        "7216": {"comment":"unsafe area start"},
        "7220": {"synopsis":"clear memory from DE (inclusive) to HL (exclusive)","comment":"A=0, Fc=0"},
        "7223": {"comment":"HL=DE? exit"},
        "7224": {"comment":"restore HL"},
        "7225": {"comment":"clear first byte"},
        "7229": {"comment":"HL=DE? exit"},
        "7230": {"comment":"BC=end-start"},
        "7232": {"comment":"HL=start"},
        "7234": {"comment":"over zero byte"},
        "7235": {"comment":"copy forward, ie. zero fill"},
        "7238": {"synopsis":"check that stack pointer and unsafe area are within stack limits\nfreeze if either outside limits","comment":"upper limit"},
        "7241": {"comment":"lower limit"},
        "7261": {"comment":"freeze"},
        "7264": {"synopsis":"Checks that DE lies between BC and HL. ChkStkLimits uses it for the application stack\npointer and the unsafe area start, with HL = $1FFE and BC = $1820, and freezes when either\nis outside.\nEntry: DE = the value; HL = the upper limit; BC = the lower limit.\nExit: Fc = 0 when BC <= DE <= HL; Fc = 1 when DE is above HL or below BC.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "7265": {"comment":"!! can do without pushing DE"},
        "7270": {"comment":"HL<DE? Fc=1"},
        "7273": {"comment":"DE<BC? Fc=1"},
        "7279": {"synopsis":"copy mailbox data into low stack area\nif $1852 contains $aa then $1811 is length of data starting at $1812\ndata length can't exceed 64 bytes"},
        "7282": {"comment":"B=ubMailboxBank"},
        "7287": {"comment":"!! 'dec a; cp 64; ld a,0; jr nc'"},
        "7294": {"comment":">64? exit"},
        "7306": {"comment":"mark as valid"},
        "7308": {"comment":"store identifier"},
        "7312": {"synopsis":"OS_Nq for the process enquiries ($86xx: NQ_Ain to NQ_Btl), entered from OSNqMain with the\nreason's low byte in A and C. Rejects a low byte of $27 or more, else jumps into\nOSNqPrcssTable, a table of 13 JP instructions (NQAin, NQKhn, NQShn, NQPhn, NQNhn, NQWai,\nNQCom, NQIhn, NQOhn, NQRhn, NQVoz, NQRoz, NqBtl).\nEntry: A = C = the reason's low byte (a multiple of 3); B = 0; IY = the OS frame.\nExit: as the handler.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Unk for a reason out of range.","comment":"range check"},
        "7362": {"synopsis":"application information\nEntry: IX=application ID.\nExit: application data: A=flags, C=key, BHL=name, BDE=DOR."},
        "7365": {"comment":"<IX"},
        "7371": {"comment":"not found? exit"},
        "7374": {"comment":"appl DOR"},
        "7381": {"comment":"application name"},
        "7384": {"comment":"bind in BHL"},
        "7390": {"comment":"IX=HL"},
        "7396": {"comment":"flags1 - good, bad, ugly etc"},
        "7402": {"comment":"code letter"},
        "7411": {"comment":"copy app pointers over help pointers"},
        "7414": {"synopsis":"read keyboard handle"},
        "7419": {"synopsis":"read screen handle"},
        "7424": {"synopsis":"read printer indirected handle"},
        "7429": {"synopsis":"read null handle"},
