        "7454": {"synopsis":"Who am I?"},
        "7458": {"comment":"!! just for C"},
        "7467": {"synopsis":"Application validates running OZ\nEntry: A = OZ version number, eg. $45 for OZV4.5.\nExit: Fc=0, Application is running on accepted OZ; Fc=1, RC_QUIT is returned (application is\nobliged to suicide).","comment":"in C"},
        "7470": {"comment":"get application-specific OZ version to compare against"},
        "7476": {"comment":"CURRENT_OZ (C) < VERIFY_OZ (A)"},
        "7480": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: oz_not_compatible."},
        "7558": {"comment":"get application-specific OZ version to compare against"},
        "7597": {"comment":"\"Press ESC to Resume\""},
        "7646": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: fatal_err_wait_key."},
        "7651": {"comment":"fatal error, request quit"},
        "7655": {"synopsis":"Waits for ESC or Q: reads raw keys with OS_Cli CL_RIM and no timeout until one arrives that\nis ESC or Q (either case), with no qualifier byte. An escape condition (RC_Esc) is\nacknowledged with OS_Esc and ends the wait too; RC_Susp and other errors read again. NQVoz's\nerror box uses it.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fz = 1 always; A = ESC or 'Q' for a key, or OS_Esc's result after an escape.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"wait infinitely"},
        "7658": {"comment":"raw input"},
        "7676": {"comment":"extended key? loop"},
        "7680": {"comment":"not 'Q'? loop"},
        "7681": {"comment":"not ESC? loop"},
        "7684": {"comment":"upper()"},
        "7691": {"synopsis":"GN_Win window definition for NQVoz's error box (7 bytes): $D1 (window 1, bars, banner and\nbottom line, a grey pop-up, 7-pixel banner), X = 20, Y = 0, width 45, height 8, and the\nbanner pointer errbanner."},
        "7698": {"synopsis":"The error box's banner text: \"ERROR\" and a 0. ErrWinDef points to it."},
        "7704": {"synopsis":"Reads the running OZ version: OS_Frm with A = FA_PTR, IX = -1 and DE = 0, which returns it\nin DEBC. NQVoz compares C with the version an application asks for.\nEntry: none.\nExit: DEBC = OS_Frm's result; C = the OZ version (e.g. $47).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "7712": {"comment":"result in DEBC"},
        "7720": {"synopsis":"Read OZ revision number\nEntry: -.\nExit: DEBC= 32 bits revision number."},
        "7731": {"comment":"OZ revision in DEBC"},
        "7734": {"synopsis":"The OZ revision number, a 32-bit value (ozrev) stored low word first; $0603C979 in this ROM.\nNQRoz returns it in DEBC."},
        "7738": {"synopsis":"Read battery status\nEntry: -.\nExit: Fz = 0, battery is good; Fz = 1, battery is low."},
        "7741": {"comment":"this bit is updated by INT"},
        "7744": {"comment":"Fz = 1 on Batt low"},
