        "8026": {"synopsis":"Sets up the slot loop shared by StoreCardIDs and ChkCardChange: D = 3 slots to visit (slot 3\ndown to 1), E = $3F (the source calls it the maximum card size), and HL' = the end of slot\n3's 4-byte card ID (ulSlot3ID + 4); the IDs are stored downwards from there.\nEntry: none.\nExit: D = 3; E = $3F; HL' = ulSlot3ID + 4.\nChanges: DE, HL'.","comment":"3 loops, max card size"},
        "8035": {"synopsis":"check that IX is a process handle"},
        "8037": {"comment":"ld hl, ix"},
        "8038": {"comment":"Last process handle"},
        "8042": {"comment":"Fc = 1, if Handle > 8"},
        "8045": {"comment":"Fc = 0, indicate special handle, DE = IX"},
        "8047": {"synopsis":"OS_Op with OP_MEM: opens a memory file. Allocates a file handle (AllocHandle, HND_FILE),\ninitialises it as a memory file (InitMemHandle), copies C bytes from BHL into it (MvToFile),\nmarks it readable, writable and memory, and rewinds it (RewindFile). If the copy fails, the\nhandle is freed (FreeMemHandle).\nEntry: BHL = the data; C = its length.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = the new handle, positioned at the start.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "8082": {"synopsis":"file rename"},
        "8094": {"comment":"Fz=1"},
        "8101": {"synopsis":"file delete","comment":"delete DOR"},
        "8103": {"comment":"DOR interface"},
        "8106": {"synopsis":"Writes a file DOR's name and dates. With Fz = 1 it first copies the 17-byte name at the\ncaller's HL (the OS frame) into a stack buffer and writes it as the 'N' record (OS_Dor\nDR_WR; a failure hangs in a loop). Then it reads the machine date and time (GN_Gmd, GN_Gmt,\nagain while they are inconsistent) and writes them as the 'U' (update) record, and also as\nthe 'C' (create) record when Fc = 1.\nEntry: IX = the DOR handle; Fz = 1 to rename (the name at the caller's HL); Fc = 1 to set\nthe creation date too; IY = the OS frame.\nExit: the records written; the 17-byte stack buffer released.","comment":"preserve Fz and Fc"},
        "8107": {"comment":"reserve stack buffer"},
        "8114": {"comment":"Fz=0? don't rename"},
        "8117": {"comment":"copy HL to stack buffer"},
        "8127": {"comment":"write DOR record"},
        "8129": {"comment":"Name, 17 chars"},
        "8134": {"comment":"crash if fail"},
        "8138": {"comment":"HL=stack buffer"},
        "8140": {"comment":"DE=stack buffer"},
        "8142": {"comment":"get current machine date in internal format"},
        "8146": {"comment":"get (read) machine time in internal format"},
        "8149": {"comment":"inconsistent, read again"},
        "8151": {"comment":"copy time after date"},
        "8156": {"comment":"DE=datetime"},
        "8157": {"comment":"write DOR record"},
        "8159": {"comment":"Update, 6 bytes"},
        "8165": {"comment":"Fc=0? don't set creation date"},
        "8167": {"comment":"write DOR record"},
        "8169": {"comment":"Create, 6 bytes"},
        "8174": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "8180": {"synopsis":"OS_Map: map control, the graphics area that PipeDream's map uses. Runs OSMapMain with IX\nkept.\nEntry: C = reason (MP_WR, MP_DEF, MP_GRA, MP_DEL, MP_MEM); the other registers as OSMapMain.\nExit: as OSMapMain.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "8188": {"synopsis":"The body of OS_Map: picks the reason in C with DJNZ. MP_WR writes one pixel line: E = the\nrow (masked to 0-63), HL = the line's data in the caller's space; the line is the window's\nmap width (GetMapWidth) / 8 bytes, poked 8 bytes apart into the HIRES0 bank (the bank and\naddress come from BLSC_PB2L/PB2H). MP_DEF and MP_GRA define the map (_mp_def). MP_DEL does\nnothing and returns Fc = 0. MP_MEM: B = an MS_Sx segment specifier; defines the map, then\nreturns DE = the widths from _mp_def, B = the map's bank, C = the segment specifier, and HL\n= the map's base (OS_Sci SC_HR0) addressed in that segment.\nEntry: C = reason; A = the window; as above; IY = the OS frame.\nExit: as above.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Unk for a reason above MP_MEM; Fc = 1 when the window is not found."},
        "8191": {"comment":"write a line to the map"},
        "8195": {"comment":"GetWindowFrame failed? exit"},
        "8197": {"comment":"mask row number to 6 bits (only allow values 0-63)"},
        "8200": {"comment":"prepare for entry"},
        "8211": {"comment":"row"},
        "8228": {"comment":"BC*=32"},
        "8234": {"comment":"no of bytes in pixel line to write to map"},
        "8235": {"comment":"HL = pointer to pixel line data to write"},
        "8244": {"comment":"C = bank of HIRES0, the PipeDream Map Area"},
        "8245": {"comment":"plot pixel line of B bytes to"},
        "8246": {"comment":"A = byte from pixel line data (in caller address space)"},
        "8251": {"comment":"plot 8 pixels in A at address pixel line at BHL, the PipeDream Map Area"},
        "8257": {"comment":"point to next adjacent 8 bits in current pixel map line"},
        "8268": {"synopsis":"Defines a map (MP_DEF; also MP_GRA and MP_MEM). Opens the screen data, finds the window\n(GetWindowFrame) and gets the map size (sub_9EBC). When there is a map, it defines the\nwindow (SOH 7 #) at X = 94 - C characters, Y = 0, C characters wide, 8 lines high, selects\nand clears it with the active window kept (GetCurrentWdInfo, RestoreActiveWd), and sets the\nwindow's right margin to D, the pixel width. Returns BC to the caller through the OS frame.\nEntry: A = the window; C = the reason (MP_GRA and MP_MEM take the width from the caller's L,\nMP_DEF from the Panel); IY = the OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0; BC (and the frame's BC) = B the pixel width, C the width in characters; BC = 0\nwhen there is no map (PA_Map not 'Y', or size 0).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Hand when the window is not found.","comment":"define a map using the Panel default width"},
        "8291": {"comment":"window A"},
        "8296": {"comment":"x"},
        "8301": {"comment":"y"},
        "8305": {"comment":"width"},
        "8343": {"comment":"mp_def"},
        "8347": {"comment":"mp_del (do nothing!)"},
        "8349": {"comment":"any argument bigger than MP_MEM is unknown functionality."},
        "8351": {"comment":"get MS_Sx argument"},
        "8360": {"comment":"the pixel- and character width are returned in DE"},
        "8367": {"comment":"get base address of map area (hires0) in BHL"},
        "8371": {"comment":"get MS_Sx argument (from B argument to OS_Map)"},
        "8373": {"comment":"return B = bank of map memory, C = Ms_Sx segment specifier"},
        "8383": {"comment":"Base of map area adjusted to MS_Sx address segment for BHL"},
        "8385": {"comment":"return address of base map memory for MS_Sx"},
        "8388": {"comment":"Unknown request (parameter in register) *"},
        "8392": {"synopsis":"Works out the map's size for _mp_def. Asks whether there is a map (sub_9F0C, 'Y' for MP_GRA\nand MP_MEM) and its width in pixels (sub_9EF6). A width above 96 is cut to 96 unless 128K of\nRAM was found (Chk128KB).\nEntry: IY = the OS frame (its C is the reason, its L the width for MP_GRA and MP_MEM).\nExit: Fc = 0; B = the width in pixels; D = the width rounded up to a multiple of 8 ($FF\nabove 248); C = the width in 6-pixel characters, (D - 1) / 6 + 1.\nError: Fc = 1, BC = 0 when there is no map, the width is 0 or OS_Nq fails."},
        "8403": {"comment":"PA_Map = No"},
        "8404": {"comment":"l = PA_Msz"},
        "8414": {"comment":"size = 0"},
        "8425": {"comment":"max. size on unexpanded"},
        "8450": {"synopsis":"Gets the map's width in pixels: the caller's L for MP_GRA and MP_MEM, else the Panel setting\nPA_Msz (sub_9F17); a value above 255 gives $FF.\nEntry: IY = the OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0; L = the width.\nError: Fc = 1 from OS_Nq."},
        "8462": {"comment":"map size in pixels"},
        "8475": {"synopsis":"Gets whether the map is on: L = 'Y' for MP_GRA and MP_MEM; otherwise sets BC = PA_Map and\nfalls into sub_9F17 to read the Panel setting ('Y' or 'N').\nEntry: IY = the OS frame.\nExit: L = 'Y' or 'N'.\nError: Fc = 1 from OS_Nq."},
        "8486": {"comment":"PipeDream map 'Y' or 'N'"},
        "8489": {"synopsis":"Reads a 2-byte Panel setting with OS_Nq (A = 2, the buffer on the stack).\nEntry: BC = the parameter (PA_xxx).\nExit: HL = the value.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Nq.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "8501": {"synopsis":"Return map pixel width"},
        "8502": {"comment":"get access to window data in segment 1, returns old bank binding in A"},
        "8506": {"comment":"setup IX to point at base of Window frame (in segment 1)"},
        "8509": {"comment":"BC=(rmargin+1)&$fffe"},
        "8515": {"comment":"BC = width of map in pixels (always even numbered)"},
        "8518": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding of segment 1"},
        "8523": {"synopsis":"handle menu/help/index from OSTin","comment":"reserve area of 20 bytes in stack"},
