        "8566": {"comment":"Fc=1"},
        "8569": {"comment":"store help state at DE"},
        "8581": {"comment":"save user screen"},
        "8592": {"comment":"not help? skip"},
        "8598": {"comment":"A=1"},
        "8603": {"comment":"information topic?"},
        "8616": {"comment":"not index/help/menu? Fc=1, Fz=1"},
        "8617": {"comment":"!! this shouldn't happen"},
        "8618": {"comment":"copy 20 bytes from ? to $0287"},
        "8624": {"comment":"HL points to saved help data"},
        "8627": {"comment":"ld hl,(iy+0)"},
        "8637": {"comment":"restore user screen"},
        "8644": {"comment":"couldn't restore screen?"},
        "8648": {"comment":"A=RC_Draw, Fz=0, Fc=1"},
        "8650": {"comment":"!! ld a,RC_Draw; cp $ff"},
        "8652": {"comment":"!! OP_LDB_IMM to hide pop"},
        "8662": {"comment":"free user screen"},
        "8678": {"synopsis":"Copies the active application's MTH pointers (eAppDOR_2 to eAppTokens_2: five 3-byte\npointers, DOR, topics, commands, help and tokens) over the help pointers (eHlpAppDOR to\neHlpTokens). Falls into the copy shared with CopyMTHHelp_App.\nEntry: none.\nExit: the 15 bytes copied; BC = 0.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL; F (P/V, H, N).\nKeeps: A, Fc, IX, IY.","comment":"copy App pointers into Help pointers"},
        "8686": {"synopsis":"Copies the help MTH pointers (eHlpAppDOR to eHlpTokens, 15 bytes) back over the active\napplication's (eAppDOR_2 to eAppTokens_2).\nEntry: none.\nExit: the 15 bytes copied; BC = 0.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL; F (P/V, H, N).\nKeeps: A, Fc, IX, IY.","comment":"copy Help pointers into App pointers"},
        "8692": {"comment":"5 ePointers"},
        "8698": {"synopsis":"Calls OS_Sr and stores the IX it returns in pMTHScreenSave: the help system saves, restores\nand frees the user screen through it.\nEntry: A = the OS_Sr reason (SR_SUS, SR_RUS, SR_FUS); IX as OS_Sr needs.\nExit: as OS_Sr; pMTHScreenSave = IX."},
        "8705": {"synopsis":"Draws the key legend beside the command menu (DrawMenuWd calls it), centred in tiny type,\nfour lines: MENU \"ADVANCE\" (HELP \"BROWSE\" when the active topic is an information topic),\nthe arrows \"SELECT\", ENTER \"ACTION\" (\"DETAIL\"), and ESC \"RESUME\". When no user screen was\nsaved (pMTHScreenSave high byte 0) the select and action lines become \"MEMORY LOW\".\nEntry: none (reads ubHlpActiveTpc)."},
        "8708": {"comment":"center"},
        "8721": {"comment":"\"advance\" \"action\""},
        "8724": {"comment":"advance/select/action/resume"},
        "8726": {"comment":"\"browse\" \"detail\""},
        "8729": {"synopsis":"else info topic: browse/select/detail/resume","comment":"get symbol"},
        "8730": {"comment":"1. line - advance/browse"},
        "8733": {"comment":"4. line - resume"},
        "8755": {"comment":"memory low? can't select/action"},
        "8757": {"comment":"2. line - select"},
        "8778": {"synopsis":"Entry inside DrawMenuWd2: prints the symbol of key A (MTHPrintKeycode), then the string that\nstarts at HL + 1 (OS_Bout, which leaves HL after its terminator). DrawMenuWd2 calls it for\nthe first line and falls into it for the third.\nEntry: A = the key code; HL = the byte before the string.\nExit: HL = the byte after the string's 0.","comment":"3. line - action/detail"},
        "8782": {"comment":"write string to std. output"},
        "8800": {"synopsis":"The legend for an ordinary topic: SD_MNU (the MENU key), then \"\\nADVANCE\" and \"\\nACTION\",\neach ended by a 0. DrawMenuWd2 prints them through dmwd_2."},
        "8818": {"synopsis":"The legend for an information topic: SD_HLP (the HELP key), then \"\\nBROWSE\" and \"\\nDETAIL\",\neach ended by a 0. DrawMenuWd2 prints them through dmwd_2."},
        "8835": {"synopsis":"MENU in the menu: moves to the next page of topics. Checks there are two command topics\n(mnu_m2), increments ubHlpActiveHelp, finds the next non-information topic after the active\none and falls into SetHlpActiveTpc.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as SetHlpActiveTpc; Fc = 1 when there is no further topic."},
        "8842": {"comment":"and drop thru"},
        "8845": {"synopsis":"Makes topic A the active one. When Fc = 1, or the topic window's line (ubHlpActiveHelp) is 8\nor more, it resets the line to 1 and moves to the first non-information topic from A\n(GetNonInfoTopicByNum).\nEntry: A = the topic number; Fc = 1 to reset the line.\nExit: Fc = 0; ubHlpActiveTpc (and maybe ubHlpActiveHelp) set."},
        "8873": {"synopsis":"SHIFT MENU in the menu: moves to the previous topic. Checks there are two command topics\n(mnu_m2), decrements ubHlpActiveHelp, finds the previous non-information topic and goes to\nSetHlpActiveTpc.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as SetHlpActiveTpc."},
        "8877": {"comment":"previous HlpActiveTpc"},
        "8880": {"comment":"previous NonInfoTopic"},
        "8885": {"synopsis":"Checks that the application has at least two non-information (command) topics; if so,\nselects the first command (ubHlpActiveCmd = 1).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = ubHlpActiveHelp.\nError: Fc = 1 when there are fewer than two such topics.","comment":"is there at least 1 topic ?"},
        "8889": {"comment":"is there 1 more ?"},
        "8893": {"comment":"set to 1, select first command"},
        "8900": {"synopsis":"UP in the menu: A = the active command (ubHlpActiveCmd), and falls into loc_A0C8 to find the\none before it."},
        "8903": {"synopsis":"Entry inside mnu_up2: finds the command before command A. Looks up A - 1, A - 2, ...\n(GetCmdAttrByNum) until the position it reports is not A.\nEntry: A = the command number.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 0; A = the previous command's position.\nError: Fc = 1, Fz = 1 when A is 1 and the lookup gives 1 back.\nChanges: AF, BC, and what GetCmdAttrByNum changes.","comment":"!! ld c,a; dec c and use C directly below"},
        "8905": {"comment":"!! can reuse 'dec c' if it's placed last"},
        "8913": {"comment":"compare real position with wanted position"},
        "8914": {"comment":"!! flags never used"},
        "8916": {"comment":"not same? Fc=0, Fz=0"},
        "8919": {"comment":"wanted/got 1? Fc=1, Fz=1"},
        "8935": {"comment":"mem not low? do key"},
        "8947": {"comment":"A=69=RC_Susp, Fc=1, Fz=0  !! ld a,RC_Susp; cp $ff"},
        "8953": {"comment":"close help file"},
        "8960": {"comment":"back to app - maybe into index/filer?"},
        "8963": {"synopsis":"Fills the first 3 bytes of the help state saved on entry to help (the 20-byte copy that\nExitHelp restores): with the current command, topic and line (ubHlpActiveCmd to\nubHlpActiveHelp) when help shows the suspended application (GetHlp_sub) and its active topic\nexists and is not an information topic, else with 1, 1, 1 (dummy).\nOZ source name: MayResetAppHelpData.\nEntry: IY = DoHelp's frame, whose first word points at the saved state.\nExit: Fz = 1 when the help values were kept, Fz = 0 when they were reset; DE = the saved\nubHlpActiveApp byte.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"only used to compare AppDOR with HlpAppDOR"},
        "8966": {"comment":"not same, reset suspended app cmd/tpc/hlp"},
        "8974": {"comment":"no such topic? reset app data"},
        "8978": {"comment":"not info topic? reset app data"},
        "8980": {"comment":"use help cmd/tpc/hlp"},
        "8988": {"comment":"Fz=0"},
        "8989": {"comment":"HL points to saved help data"},
        "8992": {"comment":"ld hl,(iy+0)"},
        "9002": {"synopsis":"Three 1 bytes: the command, topic and line that MayResetAppHelp stores when it resets the\nsaved help state."},
        "9005": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key in the help pages and jumps to its handler. The return address points at a\ntable: entries of a key code byte and a handler word, ended by a 0; the entry for code 1 is\nthe page's own redraw. Never returns to the table.\n1. Examines the input (OS_Xin). When there is none but ubSysFlags1 has SF1_B_INPUTPENDING,\ntakes code 1.\n2. Reads a key (RdStdinNoTO). RC_Susp reads again; ESC is acknowledged (OS_Esc SC_ACK) and\npassed as IN_ESC; another error leaves help with Fc = 1.\n3. INDEX becomes $89. That, the [] key and codes $80-$9F leave help with Fc = 1, A = the\ncode. ESC and DEL leave help with A = RC_Susp, Fc = 1.\n4. Otherwise looks the key up in the table and jumps to its handler with A = the key and Fc\n= 0. A key not in the table goes to RetryKeyJump, which handles OZ's own command keys\n(beeping when memory is low) and waits again.\nEntry: (SP) = the key table; IY = DoHelp's frame.\nExit: to the key's handler, or out of help through ExitKeyJump."},
        "9006": {"comment":"examine input"},
        "9008": {"comment":"may have input"},
        "9010": {"comment":"dummy value for ?"},
        "9024": {"comment":"no error? handle key"},
        "9026": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "9028": {"comment":"just retry"},
        "9030": {"comment":"Escape condition (e.g. ESC pressed)"},
        "9033": {"comment":"other error? exit help"},
        "9035": {"comment":"(A=1 already)"},
        "9037": {"comment":"ack ESC, flush buffer"},
        "9039": {"comment":"and pass ESC"},
        "9045": {"comment":"force Index entry"},
        "9058": {"comment":"[] or $80-$9F"},
        "9064": {"comment":"non-translated DEL"},
        "9068": {"comment":"search key in table at caller PC"},
        "9070": {"comment":"!! do one 'inc hl' here"},
        "9073": {"comment":"not found? wait more"},
        "9077": {"comment":"match? call function"},
        "9089": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "9091": {"synopsis":"The copyright page: prints CopyrightMsg (in mth/systoken.asm) as a full page (MTHFullPage)\nand falls into cr_waitkey.","comment":"in mth/systoken.asm"},
        "9097": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key on the copyright page (MTH_KeyJump, its table follows the call): HELP goes\nto the first application's help (cr_hlp), LEFT to MTH_HallOfFame, RIGHT to MTH_Help; MENU,\nUP, DOWN and ENTER wait again."},
        "9125": {"synopsis":"The hall of fame page: prints HallOfFameMsg (in mth/systoken.asm) as a full page\n(MTHFullPage) and falls into hf_waitkey.","comment":"in mth/systoken.asm"},
        "9131": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key on the hall of fame page (MTH_KeyJump, its table follows the call): HELP\ngoes to the first application's help (cr_hlp), RIGHT to MTH_Copyright, ENTER to cr_waitkey;\nMENU, UP, DOWN and LEFT wait again."},
        "9159": {"synopsis":"Prints a tokenized page across the screen: defines window 6 (X = 1, Y = 0, 92 wide, 8 high,\ntype $81), selects and clears it, centres the text, and prints the text from the MTH bank\n(MTHPrintTokenized) with the system tokens (SF1_B_SYSTOKENS set, then ubSysFlags1 restored).\nEntry: HL = the tokenized text in the MTH bank (MTH_BNK).\nChanges: AF, B, HL, and what MTHPrintTokenized changes."},
        "9176": {"comment":"center"},
        "9183": {"comment":"use default tokens"},
        "9193": {"comment":"restore SYSTOKENS bit state"},
        "9197": {"synopsis":"go to first app help","comment":"hlp/tpc/cmd=1"},
        "9203": {"synopsis":"The application help page: returns to the application whose help was shown\n(SetHlpAppChgFile), sets the line, topic and command to 1, draws the page (DrawHelpWd) and\nfalls into hlp_waitkey.","comment":"go back to help we were previously"},
        "9206": {"comment":"hlp/tpc/cmd=1"},
        "9212": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key on the application help page (MTH_KeyJump, its table follows the call): HELP\nto help_help, MENU to topic_menu, UP to help_up, DOWN to help_down, LEFT to MTH_Copyright,\nRIGHT to help_right; ENTER waits again."},
        "9240": {"synopsis":"UP on the help page: moves to the previous application (PrevAppDOR) and shows its help\n(MTH_Help)."},
        "9245": {"synopsis":"HELP on the help page: when the application has a topic with help (GetFirstTopicHelp), goes\nto MTH_Topic; otherwise falls into help_down.","comment":"if we have topic help we display it"},
        "9248": {"comment":"otherwise we act like key was crsr down"},
        "9250": {"synopsis":"DOWN on the help page: moves to the next application (NextAppDOR) and shows its help\n(MTH_Help)."},
        "9255": {"synopsis":"RIGHT on the help page: when the application has a topic with help (GetFirstTopicHelp),\nfalls into MTH_Topic; otherwise waits again (hlp_waitkey)."},
        "9260": {"synopsis":"The topic help page: selects the first command (ubHlpActiveCmd = 1), draws the active\ntopic's help (DrawTopicHelpWd) and falls into topic_waitkey.","comment":"cmd=1"},
        "9266": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key on the topic help page (MTH_KeyJump, its table follows the call): HELP to\ntopic_help, MENU to topic_menu, UP to topic_up, DOWN to topic_down, LEFT to MTH_Help, RIGHT\nto topic_right; ENTER waits again."},
        "9294": {"synopsis":"DOWN on the topic page: B = 1, and goes on at topic_up's search for the next topic with\nhelp."},
        "9298": {"synopsis":"UP on the topic page: B = -1. When at least two topics have help (Get2ndTopicHelp), steps\nfrom the active topic by B, wrapping, to the next one with help, makes it active\n(SetHlpActiveTpc, Fc = 0) and shows it (MTH_Topic); otherwise waits again."},
        "9305": {"comment":"only one topic? wait some other key"},
        "9311": {"comment":"find next/prev topic with help"},
        "9313": {"comment":"!! resets A if eol, so this wraps automagically"},
        "9319": {"comment":"no help? search for more"},
        "9321": {"comment":"Fc=0, don't reset help"},
        "9328": {"synopsis":"HELP on the topic page: shows the topic's first command with help (MTH_Command); without\none, the next topic with help (MTH_Topic), and after the last topic the next application's\nhelp (help_down)."},
        "9331": {"comment":"have command with help? print it"},
        "9339": {"comment":"have more topics with help? go there"},
        "9341": {"comment":"otherwise go to next app"},
        "9344": {"synopsis":"RIGHT on the topic page: when the topic has a command with help (GetFirstCmdHelp), makes it\nactive and falls into MTH_Command; otherwise waits again."},
        "9347": {"comment":"have no command help? wait more"},
        "9353": {"synopsis":"The command help page: draws the active command's help (DrawCmdHelpWd) and falls into\ncmd_waitkey."},
        "9356": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key on the command help page (MTH_KeyJump, its table follows the call): HELP to\ncmd_help, MENU to topic_menu, UP to cmd_up, DOWN to cmd_down, LEFT to MTH_Topic; RIGHT and\nENTER wait again."},
        "9384": {"synopsis":"UP on the command page: D = -1, and goes on at cmd_down's search for the previous command\nwith help."},
        "9388": {"synopsis":"DOWN on the command page: D = 1. Steps from the active command by D, wrapping, to the next\ncommand whose attributes have CMDF_B_HELP, makes it active and shows it (MTH_Command); after\na full round the active command stays."},
        "9390": {"comment":"remember active command"},
        "9396": {"comment":"we've looped thru all commands? use old one"},
        "9400": {"comment":"!! resets A=0 if oel, so this wraps automagically"},
        "9404": {"comment":"H=A from stack"},
        "9405": {"comment":"error? retry with A=0"},
        "9409": {"comment":"not wanted one? try next/prev"},
        "9413": {"comment":"no help? try next/prev"},
        "9417": {"synopsis":"HELP on the command page: shows the next command with help (MTH_Command); without one, goes\non at topic_nxhelp (the next topic with help, or the next application)."},
        "9423": {"comment":"found command help? show it"},
        "9425": {"comment":"no more commands with help?"},
        "9428": {"synopsis":"MENU from the help pages: updates the saved help state (MayResetAppHelp), resets the line,\ntopic and command to 1 when it was reset, makes the suspended application active again\n(SetActiveAppDOR, ChgHelpFile) and falls into menu_entry."},
        "9431": {"comment":"app data reset? reset help data too"},
        "9434": {"comment":"suspended app"},
        "9441": {"synopsis":"The command menu. Finds the first command topic, makes the active topic at least that one\nwith its line in the topic window (ubHlpActiveHelp) at most 7, and moves it to a command\ntopic (GetNonInfoTopicByNum). Then (loc_A2AD, also reached from DoHelp for an information\ntopic) draws the topic window (DrawTopicWd) and, when no input is waiting, marks the active\ntopic on its line in window 7; draws the menu (DrawMenuWd), selects window 6 (X = 1, Y = 0,\n92 wide, 8 high), highlights the active command (sub_A3EC, MTHHighlight) and waits\n(MTH_KeyJump): HELP to mnu_help, MENU to mnu_menu, SHIFT MENU to mnu_smenu, UP, DOWN, LEFT,\nRIGHT and ENTER to mnu_up, mnu_down, mnu_left, mnu_right and mnu_enter."},
        "9459": {"comment":"info topic? skip"},
        "9461": {"comment":"A=max(a-1,d)"},
        "9483": {"comment":"find next command topic"},
        "9497": {"comment":"no help active? exit"},
        "9502": {"comment":"input waiting? exit"},
        "9507": {"comment":"move to x=0, Y=activeHelp"},
        "9524": {"comment":"ypos"},
        "9529": {"comment":"no grey"},
        "9537": {"comment":"topic name"},
        "9627": {"synopsis":"MENU in the menu: next topic page (mnu_menu2); redraws the menu (menu_entry), or waits again\nwhen there is none."},
        "9635": {"synopsis":"SHIFT MENU in the menu: previous topic page (mnu_smenu2); redraws the menu (menu_entry), or\nwaits again when there is none."},
        "9640": {"synopsis":"UP in the menu: finds the previous command (mnu_up2) and moves the highlight to it\n(loc_A2C4)."},
        "9645": {"synopsis":"DOWN in the menu: moves the highlight to the command after the active one (loc_A2C4)."},
        "9651": {"synopsis":"ENTER in the menu: runs the active command. A command marked CMDF_B_SAFE beeps (Beep_X). A\ncommand with code 0 shows its help (DrawTopicWd, MTH_Command). Otherwise, when memory is not\nlow, help ends with A = the command code, Fc = 0, Fz = 1 (ExitKeyJump); when it is low, it\nbeeps."},
        "9661": {"comment":"it's safe? not from enter"},
        "9665": {"comment":"non-zero command code?"},
        "9677": {"comment":"mem not low? ok"},
        "9684": {"comment":"Fc=0, Fz=1"},
        "9685": {"comment":"A=command code"},
        "9689": {"synopsis":"RIGHT in the menu: when the menu has one column (GetCmdAttrByNum for command 0 gives D = 1),\nacts as DOWN. Otherwise searches forward from the active command (GetNextCmdAttr) for the\ncommand in the next column on the same row, D being the column and E the row, and moves the\nhighlight to it (loc_A2C4)."},
        "9753": {"synopsis":"LEFT in the menu: when the menu has one column (GetCmdAttrByNum for command 0 gives D = 1),\nacts as UP. Otherwise searches backward from the active command (loc_A0C8) for the command\nin the previous column on the same row and moves the highlight to it (loc_A2C4)."},
        "9785": {"comment":"A=8*E+D"},
        "9837": {"synopsis":"HELP in the menu: redraws the topic window (DrawTopicWd), then shows the application help\n(MTH_Help) for an information topic, else the active command's help (MTH_Command), else the\ntopic's (MTH_Topic), else the application's."},
        "9846": {"comment":"information topic?"},
        "9848": {"comment":"yes? goto help"},
        "9872": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to command A's place in the menu window: column 28 * (D - 1) and row E from\nGetCmdAttrByNum.\nEntry: A = the command number.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = the command's position; C = its row; B = 0; the cursor at its place.\nError: Fc = 1 when the command does not exist, its column starts at 66 or beyond, or no user\nscreen was saved (pMTHScreenSave high byte 0)."},
        "9888": {"comment":"0/28/56"},
        "9894": {"comment":">=66? Fc=1"},
        "9898": {"comment":"put xpos"},
        "9903": {"comment":"put ypos"},
        "9909": {"comment":"no saved screen? Fc=1"},
        "9916": {"synopsis":"Opens an application's help: builds \":ROM.*/HELP/\" and the 17-byte application name in a\n29-byte stack buffer, opens its DOR (FilenameDOR), reads the 12-byte 'H' record (the topics,\ncommands, help and tokens pointers) into eHlpTopics and fixes their slot (CopyAppPointers).\nThe DOR handle is freed if the read fails.\nEntry: HL = the application name.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = the help DOR handle; eHlpTopics to eHlpTokens set.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "9917": {"comment":"reserve stack buffer"},
        "9924": {"comment":"copy string to stack"},
        "9925": {"comment":"\":ROM.*/HELP/\""},
        "9933": {"comment":"append application name"},
        "9943": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "9951": {"comment":"was DR_Rd2 (same function)"},
        "9959": {"comment":"DOR interface"},
        "9968": {"synopsis":"Toggles reverse video over the 27 characters from the cursor (SOH R, SOH 2 E 27, SOH R): the\nhighlight bar of a menu command.\nEntry: the cursor at the command.\nChanges: F."},
        "9980": {"synopsis":"Starts the right-hand box of a help page, when no input is waiting (MayMTHPrint): defines\nwindow 6 (X = 63, Y = 0, 30 wide, 8 high, type $81), selects and clears it and prints \"FOR\nMORE INFORMATION:\" centred in tiny type.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when input was waiting (nothing printed)."},
        "9992": {"comment":"select & clear"},
        "9996": {"comment":"center"},
        "10026": {"synopsis":"Ends the right-hand box of a help page, when no input is waiting (MayMTHPrint): two lines of\nkey legends, MENU \"topic entries\", HELP \"browse\", INDEX \"the manager\" and ESC \"resume\".\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when input was waiting (nothing printed)."},
        "10031": {"comment":"left-justified"},
        "10091": {"synopsis":"Saves the active window for RestoreActiveWd: asks OS_Nq NQ_Wcur for the current window and\nleaves two words on the caller's stack, HL with H = the window number, then IX. The caller\nmust call RestoreActiveWd before it returns.\nEntry: none.\nExit: the two words pushed.\nChanges: AF, HL (the return address), and what OS_Nq NQ_Wcur returns."},
        "10096": {"comment":"get cursor information"},
        "10098": {"comment":"H=active wd"},
        "10099": {"comment":"push it, pop return address"},
        "10100": {"comment":"remember wd frame"},
        "10102": {"comment":"return"},
        "10103": {"synopsis":"Undoes GetCurrentWdInfo: takes the two words from the stack, restores IX and selects the\nsaved window again with SOH 2 H and its number.\nEntry: the two words GetCurrentWdInfo left on the stack.\nExit: IX restored; the saved window active; H = its number.\nChanges: HL, IX.\nKeeps: AF.","comment":"pop return address"},
        "10107": {"comment":"select & hold, window # comes below"},
        "10112": {"comment":"get wd frame"},
        "10114": {"comment":"push ret PC, pop wd"},
        "10117": {"comment":"restore active wd"},
        "10121": {"synopsis":"Draws the topic window (window 7): the application name (InitTopicWd), then seven lines of\ncommand topic names (PrintTopic between MTH_ToggleLT calls), from topic 1, or from the\nactive topic minus 6 when it is beyond 7. The active window is kept.\nEntry: none (reads ubHlpActiveTpc)."},
        "10156": {"comment":"line"},
        "10157": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "10159": {"comment":"clear EOL"},
        "10173": {"comment":"found command? print it"},
        "10180": {"comment":"no command? skip"},
        "10182": {"comment":"advance to next command"},
        "10190": {"synopsis":"Sends SOH L and SOH T, which toggle the caps (L) and tiny (T) attributes.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "10200": {"synopsis":"Clears the topic window's top line: selects window 7, resets underline, clears line 0 and\nprints the application name in tiny, caps and underline without reverse and grey, then\ntoggles underline and grey. The active window is kept.\nEntry: none."},
        "10219": {"comment":"clear EOL"},
        "10234": {"comment":"application name"},
        "10245": {"synopsis":"Draws the application help page: the window (InitHelpWd), the application name and its help\ntext (GetHlpHelp, MTHPrintTokenized), then the right-hand box (Help2Wd_Top) with \"other\nprograms\" and the up and down arrows, \" about <name> topics\" and the right arrow when a\ntopic has help, and the key legends (Help2Wd_bottom).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when input was waiting and drawing stopped."},
        "10254": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "10270": {"comment":"left"},
        "10287": {"comment":"right"},
        "10294": {"comment":"right"},
        "10306": {"comment":"no topics having help? skip"},
        "10311": {"comment":"left"},
        "10320": {"comment":"app name"},
        "10329": {"comment":"right"},
        "10338": {"synopsis":"Defines the help window (window 6 at column 1, row 0, 61 by 8, flags $81), selects and\nclears it and sets centred justification, through MayMTHPrint. Nothing is drawn when a key\nis waiting: MayMTHPrint then returns straight to this routine's caller.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0, window 6 drawn and selected.\nError: Fc = 1 when input is pending (nothing drawn)."},
        "10350": {"comment":"select & clear"},
        "10354": {"comment":"center"},
        "10358": {"synopsis":"Finds the second command of the active topic that has a help page: calls GetFirstCmdHelp,\nthen falls into GetNextCmdHelp.\nEntry: ubHlpActiveTpc = active topic.\nExit: as GetNextCmdHelp.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10361": {"synopsis":"Finds the next command of the active topic after command A that has a help page (the\nCMDF_B_HELP attribute bit), going on through GetCmdAttrByNum.\nEntry: A = command number to start after; ubHlpActiveTpc = active topic.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = number of the command found; B = its attributes; C = its command code; HL\n= its definition; DE = as GetCmdAttrByNum.\nError: Fc = 1 when no further command has help.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10364": {"synopsis":"Finds the first command of the active topic that has a help page: starts with command 1 and\ncalls GetCmdAttrByNum until a command has the CMDF_B_HELP attribute bit set.\nEntry: ubHlpActiveTpc = active topic.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = number of the command found; B = its attributes; C = its command code; HL\n= its definition; DE = as GetCmdAttrByNum.\nError: Fc = 1 when no command of the topic has help.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10376": {"synopsis":"Steps to the next command: increments A and falls into GetCmdAttrByNum.\nEntry: A = current command number; ubHlpActiveTpc = active topic.\nExit: as GetCmdAttrByNum for command A+1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10377": {"synopsis":"Looks up command A of the active help topic and returns its attributes. Binds in the help\ncommand list (GetHlpCommands, OSBixS1), skips to topic ubHlpActiveTpc (GetCmdTopicByNum),\nturns the count into a real position past hidden commands (GetRealCmdPosition), reads the\ncommand code and the attribute byte (GetAttr), then restores segment 1 (OSBoxS1).\nEntry: A = command number within the active topic; ubHlpActiveTpc = active topic.\nExit: A = command position; B = attribute byte (CMDF_xxx); C = command code; HL = command\ndefinition (in the list's bank, which is no longer bound); DE = the column and row\nGetRealCmdPosition left in DE.\nError: Fc = 1, A = 0 when the topic does not exist (B, C, HL not set); Fc = 1 also comes\nfrom GetRealCmdPosition at the start or end of the topic, with B, C and HL still set.\nCallers rely on A = 0 at the end of the list to wrap round.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10382": {"comment":"Bind in extended address"},
        "10386": {"comment":"c=count"},
        "10395": {"comment":"error? Fc=1, A=0"},
        "10397": {"comment":"a=count"},
        "10403": {"comment":"command code"},
        "10408": {"comment":"attributes"},
        "10410": {"comment":"IX=DE"},
        "10414": {"comment":"Restore bindings"},
        "10417": {"comment":"DE=IX"},
        "10421": {"synopsis":"Finds the second help topic that has a help page: calls GetFirstTpcHelp, then falls into\nGetNextTopicHelp.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as GetNextTopicHelp.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "10424": {"synopsis":"Finds the next topic after topic A that has a help page (the help bit, bit 4, of its\nattribute byte), going on through GetTpcAttrByNum.\nEntry: A = topic number to start after.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = number of the topic found; D = its attributes (TPCF_xxx); HL = its\ndefinition.\nError: Fc = 1 when no further topic has help.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "10427": {"synopsis":"Finds the first help topic that has a help page: starts with topic 1 and calls\nGetTpcAttrByNum until a topic has the help bit (bit 4) of its attributes set.\nOZ source name: GetFirstTopicHelp.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = number of the topic found; D = its attributes (TPCF_xxx); HL = its\ndefinition.\nError: Fc = 1 when no topic has help.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "10439": {"synopsis":"Finds the first topic that is not an INFO topic: sets A = 1 and falls into GetNonInfoByNum.\nOZ source name: GetFirstNonInfoTopic.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as GetNonInfoByNum.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "10441": {"synopsis":"Finds the first topic, from topic A upwards, that is not an INFO topic (TPCF_B_INFO clear in\nits attributes), calling GetTpcAttrByNum for each.\nOZ source name: GetNonInfoTopicByNum.\nEntry: A = topic number to start with.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = number of the topic found; D = its attributes; HL = its definition.\nError: Fc = 1 when the list ends first.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "10447": {"comment":"not info, ret"},
        "10448": {"synopsis":"Entry inside GetNonInfoByNum: increments A and goes on searching from the next topic for\none that is not an INFO topic.\nOZ source name: GetNextNonInfoTopic.\nEntry: A = current topic number.\nExit: as GetNonInfoByNum.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"inc count and loop"},
        "10451": {"synopsis":"Decrements A and searches from there with GetNonInfoByNum. The search runs upwards, so when\ntopic A-1 is an INFO topic the result is the next non-INFO topic after it.\nOZ source name: GetPrevNonInfoTopic.\nEntry: A = current topic number.\nExit: as GetNonInfoByNum.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL."},
        "10454": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=command/topic index.\nExit: Fc=0, D=attribute byte."},
        "10459": {"comment":"bind in BHL"},
        "10478": {"synopsis":"Prints the key legend of an internal key code: looks A up in CmdKeycodeTbl (3-byte entries:\nkey code, modifier symbol, key symbol, ended by 0) and prints SOH and the modifier symbol\nwhen there is one, then SOH and the key symbol, through ScrDrv_SOH_A (OS_Out). Prints\nnothing for a code not in the table.\nEntry: A = internal key code (IN_xxx).\nExit: legend printed.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "10484": {"comment":"!! use sorted table here as well"},
        "10507": {"synopsis":"inbyte, SOHm, SOHn"},
        "10601": {"synopsis":"Starts help for an application: stores A as the active help application (ubHlpActiveApp) and\nfalls into InitHlpActHelp, which sets help page, topic and command to 1.\nEntry: A = application number.\nExit: ubHlpActiveApp = A; ubHlpActiveHelp, ubHlpActiveTpc, ubHlpActiveCmd = 1; A = 1.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10604": {"synopsis":"Sets the active help page, topic and command to 1: loads A = 1 and falls into\nSetHlpActiveHelp.\nOZ source name: InitHlpActiveHelp.\nEntry: none.\nExit: ubHlpActiveHelp, ubHlpActiveTpc, ubHlpActiveCmd = 1; A = 1.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10606": {"synopsis":"Stores A as the active help page (ubHlpActiveHelp), sets the active topic to 1 and falls\ninto InitHlpActiveCmd.\nEntry: A = help page number.\nExit: ubHlpActiveHelp = A; ubHlpActiveTpc, ubHlpActiveCmd = 1; A = 1.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10614": {"synopsis":"Selects the first command of the active topic: sets ubHlpActiveCmd to 1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: ubHlpActiveCmd = 1; A = 1.\nChanges: AF."},
