        "11001": {"comment":"original stack is IX+$100"},
        "11008": {"synopsis":"Copies the default value of a Panel or ISO-translation setting into a buffer and falls into\nNqGetDest. The reason's low byte (OSFrame_C) indexes PrefTbl1 (panel, bit 7 clear) or\nPrefTbl2 (ISO, bit 7 set) in the MTH bank, which hold byte offsets: the data starts at the\nentry's offset and its length is the next offset minus this one.\nEntry: IX = temporary buffer (NqPanel makes 256 bytes on the stack); IY = OS frame.\nExit: DE = IX (the default value); C = its length; HL = caller's destination buffer; A =\ncaller's buffer size (see NqGetDest).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"C panel/ISO reason"},
        "11011": {"comment":"panel table"},
        "11018": {"comment":"00-7F"},
        "11020": {"comment":"ISO table"},
        "11025": {"comment":"bind PrefTbl in S1"},
        "11032": {"comment":"offset to data"},
        "11034": {"comment":"offset to next-offset=length"},
        "11037": {"comment":"length=0? done"},
        "11039": {"comment":"return pointer in DE"},
        "11040": {"comment":"previous S1 in D"},
        "11043": {"comment":"temp buffer address in DE for LDIR"},
        "11046": {"comment":"length"},
        "11049": {"comment":"restore S1"},
        "11055": {"comment":"source data in DE"},
        "11056": {"comment":"source length"},
        "11057": {"synopsis":"Finds where OS_Nq returns its data: the caller's buffer from the frame's DE, and its size\nfrom the frame's A. When the caller passed DE = 2, the value is returned in DE itself: the\nframe's DE is cleared and HL points to OSFrame_E, with A = 2.\nEntry: DE = source data; C = data length; IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = destination; A = buffer size (2 when DE = 2 was passed).\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "11058": {"comment":"get destination buffer"},
        "11068": {"comment":"buffer size"},
        "11071": {"comment":"buffer not 0002? exit"},
        "11076": {"comment":"clear DE"},
        "11085": {"comment":"destination is DE in OSFrame"},
        "11086": {"comment":"source"},
        "11087": {"comment":"length is 2 bytes"},
        "11090": {"synopsis":"if wanted size is smaller than attribute size we return EOF"},
        "11099": {"synopsis":"OS_NQ, NQ_Mfs ($8900), NQ_Slt ($8903) & NQ_Mfp ($8906)","comment":"function range test"},
