        "11191": {"comment":"no file area found in application card"},
        "11197": {"synopsis":"NQ_Mfp ($8906), Get total of free RAM pages in slot A\n\nFc = 1, it is not a RAM device\nA = RC_ONF (Object not found)\n\nOriginal code from RamDevFreeSpace library, designed by Thierry Peycru, Zlab, May 1998\nModified for OZ by Gunther Strube, Apr 2007\nEntry: A = slot number (0 for internal).\nExit: Fc = 0, it is a RAM device; A = total number of banks in Ram Card ($40 for 1MB); DE =\nfree pages (1 page = 256 bytes).\nChanges: AF..DE../... different.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11200": {"comment":"first, get the first device bank"},
        "11206": {"comment":"header of internal slot is in $21"},
        "11208": {"comment":"first bank of RAM slot"},
        "11209": {"comment":"start of bank in hl"},
        "11212": {"comment":"(in segment 1)"},
        "11215": {"comment":"preserve original bank binding status"},
        "11216": {"comment":"should be $5A"},
        "11218": {"comment":"should be $A5"},
        "11221": {"comment":"RAM device header"},
        "11230": {"comment":"number of banks in RAM Card"},
        "11231": {"comment":"even if internal (-1 for the system bank $20)"},
        "11232": {"comment":"from 2 (32K) to 64 (1024K)"},
        "11234": {"comment":"actual number of banks"},
        "11235": {"comment":"save it for exit"},
        "11237": {"comment":"data start at $0100"},
        "11239": {"comment":"free pages in DE"},
        "11241": {"comment":"parse table of B(anks) * 64 pages"},
        "11242": {"comment":"total of pages in a bank..."},
        "11246": {"comment":"must be 00 if free"},
        "11257": {"comment":"signal success (Fc = 0)"},
        "11258": {"comment":"return number of banks in RAM Card"},
        "11261": {"comment":"return number of free RAM pages in DE"},
        "11264": {"comment":"restore original bank binding"},
        "11267": {"comment":"RAM device not found"},
        "11269": {"comment":"signal failure..."},
        "11272": {"synopsis":"Skips one attribute of the saved preferences data: reads its length byte from the memory\nfile with RdFileByte and reads past that many bytes.\nEntry: memory file positioned on an attribute's length byte.\nExit: Fc = 0, positioned on the next attribute; A = 0 when the length was 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from RdFileByte.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "11275": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "11276": {"comment":"length to B, exit if 0"},
        "11286": {"synopsis":"Checks the length given to OS_Sp for a Panel or ISO setting against the default length in\nPrefTbl1/PrefTbl2 (MTH bank). The length is the frame's A, or 2 when the frame's DE is 2.\nEntry: IY = OS frame (C = reason low byte, A = length, DE = data or 2).\nExit: C = the default length; Fz = 1 when the given length is 255 (A = 0) or when it and the\ndefault length are both 0; Fz = 0 otherwise (SpPanel then writes the attribute).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"C panel/ISO reason"},
        "11289": {"comment":"panel table"},
        "11296": {"comment":"00-7F"},
        "11298": {"comment":"ISO table"},
        "11303": {"comment":"bind PrefTbl in S1"},
        "11309": {"comment":"offset to data"},
        "11311": {"comment":"offset to next-offset=length"},
        "11316": {"comment":"source length"},
        "11317": {"comment":"get destination buffer"},
        "11326": {"comment":"buffer size"},
        "11329": {"comment":"buffer not 0002? exit"},
        "11334": {"comment":"dest buffer length is 255, Fc=0"},
        "11336": {"comment":"source length"},
        "11337": {"comment":"Fc=0 if data fits dest"},
        "11340": {"synopsis":"Copies one byte from the old preferences data to the new memory file: reads it with\nPanelFsRdByte and falls into MemFsWrByte.\nEntry: both file states set up by SpPanel.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = the byte copied.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "11344": {"synopsis":"Writes A to the new preferences memory file: switches the file position to it (UseMemFs) and\njumps to WrFileByte.\nEntry: A = byte.\nExit: Fc = 0, byte written.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "11350": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte of the old preferences data: switches the file position to it (UsePanelFs) and\njumps to RdFileByte.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte read.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (end of file included).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "11356": {"synopsis":"Switches the kernel memory file position to the old preferences data: saves the 4-byte\neFsMemFilePos in pMTHScreenSave and loads it from lFsPanelArea. UseMemFs switches back.\nEntry: none.\nExit: eFsMemFilePos = the panel data's position.\nChanges: DE, HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "11381": {"synopsis":"Switches the kernel memory file position to the new preferences memory file: saves the\n4-byte eFsMemFilePos in lFsPanelArea and loads it from pMTHScreenSave. UsePanelFs switches\nback.\nEntry: none.\nExit: eFsMemFilePos = the new file's position.\nChanges: DE, HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "11406": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=reason low byte."},
