        "11850": {"synopsis":"OS_Out to the screen: opens the screen, takes the active window (sbf_ActiveWd) in IX, hides\nthe cursor, puts the byte through OSOut_Put, stores the cursor position, shows the cursor\nagain and closes the screen.\nEntry: A = byte to write.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "11880": {"synopsis":"Puts one byte through the screen driver. While a prefix sequence is open (sbf_CtrlPrefix not\n0) the byte goes to OsOut_Prefixed. Otherwise a control code cancels the prefix: CR, BEL,\nBS, HT, LF, VT and FF run their handlers, ESC is ignored, and any other code below $20\nstarts a prefix sequence (stored in sbf_CtrlPrefix, buffer cleared by OSIsq). A printable\nbyte is upper-cased when the window has caps (WDFH_B_CAPS) and falls into ScrD_PutChar.\nEntry: A = byte; IX = active window; HL = cursor position.\nExit: HL = new cursor position.","comment":"B=prefixseq"},
        "11954": {"synopsis":"put character code","comment":"do chr2vdu translation"},
