        "12043": {"comment":"source address"},
        "12046": {"comment":"copy 8 bytes"},
        "12053": {"synopsis":"Point to ISO Latin 1 Ascii byte at (HL), searching internal VDU in A.\nEntry: A = low byte of LORES1 screen offset.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1, VDU code recognized:; HL = pointer to Ascii byte representation; Fc =\n1, Fz = 1; HL = points to end of table.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "12056": {"synopsis":"Searches a column of the 4-byte-per-entry key/character/LORES table (Key2Chr_tbl,\nChr2VDU_tbl or VDU2Chr_tbl) for A. The search ends at an entry whose byte in this column and\nthe next are both 0. VDU2ChrCode loads HL = VDU2Chr_tbl and falls in here.\nEntry: A = byte to find; HL = the column's label.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1, HL = the matching entry's byte in the next column.\nError: Fc = 1 when not found (HL near the table's end).\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: A, DE."},
        "12057": {"comment":"remember byte"},
        "12061": {"comment":"if lores1 bitmap offset = 0, then end of table reached"},
        "12063": {"comment":"not found, Fc=1"},
        "12065": {"comment":"next entry"},
        "12070": {"comment":"compare next"},
        "12072": {"comment":"restore byte"},
        "12074": {"comment":"point HL to match+1"},
        "12078": {"synopsis":"this one handles tiny/bold too\nEntry: A = ISO to display ($00-$FF); D = attributes (SW1=Tiny, SW2=Bold).\nExit: A = LORES CHAR, B the OR-mask, C the AND-mask of attribute byte; Fc = 1 ISO is not\nimplemented...","comment":"clear ch8 and force it set"},
        "12083": {"comment":"SPACE - always $120"},
        "12091": {"comment":"EXACT SPACE - always $0a0"},
        "12101": {"comment":"Fz=!ch8"},
        "12103": {"comment":"set Fz"},
        "12105": {"comment":"screen code lo"},
        "12107": {"comment":"not found, exit"},
        "12108": {"comment":"ch8=0"},
        "12110": {"comment":"force ch8 set"},
        "12114": {"comment":"is TINY attribute set ? (SW2)"},
        "12116": {"comment":"TINY is not active"},
        "12118": {"comment":"is it Tinyable ?"},
        "12121": {"comment":"OK"},
        "12122": {"comment":"clear Fz, Fc"},
        "12123": {"comment":"CH8=0"},
        "12124": {"comment":"is BOLD attribute set ? (SW1)"},
        "12126": {"comment":"it is normal, use 000-07F"},
        "12127": {"comment":"is it Boldable ?"},
        "12131": {"comment":"ret, it is not boldable, use the same"},
        "12132": {"comment":"CH7=1 use BOLD font (!!! OR instruction ???)"},
        "12135": {"synopsis":"Tells whether a character has bold and tiny variants in the LORES font: codes $08-$7F do.\nOZ source name: IsBoldAndTinyAble.\nEntry: A = character code.\nExit: Fc = 0 when A is $08-$7F; Fc = 1 otherwise.\nChanges: F.","comment":"$08-$7F is boldable"},
        "12142": {"synopsis":"initialize prefix sequence\nclears buffer and sets buffer pointer\nEntry: HL=sequence buffer, 22 bytes.\nExit: --.\nChanges: F, HL."},
        "12154": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=char, HL=sequence buffer.\nExit: Fc=0 always; A=0 if sequence completed, -1 otherwise."},
        "12157": {"comment":"return -1 if sequence not complete yet"},
        "12162": {"synopsis":"Stores one byte of a prefix (SOH) sequence in its buffer: +0 the count of bytes still\nexpected, +1 the low byte of the write pointer, then the bytes. The first byte sets the\nlength: $80-$94 gives length 0-20, a digit gives its value, and any other byte is stored as\na one-byte sequence. A length of 0 cancels the sequence (falls into Zero_ctrlprefix). When\nthe last byte arrives, +0 is set to the sequence length.\nEntry: A = byte; HL = sequence buffer (sbf_PrefixSeq).\nExit: Fc = 0, A = 0 when the sequence is complete; Fc = 1 while bytes are still expected (A\n= -1, or the length that was set)."},
        "12164": {"comment":"length not zero, continue put"},
        "12170": {"comment":"$80-$94 is valid - 0-20"},
        "12177": {"comment":"alpha"},
        "12179": {"comment":"not num"},
        "12182": {"comment":"80-89"},
        "12184": {"comment":"store length"},
        "12188": {"comment":"not done yet, Fc=1"},
        "12189": {"comment":"if length is zero then cancel ctrl sequence"},
        "12190": {"synopsis":"Ends the open prefix sequence: clears sbf_CtrlPrefix. StorePrefixed falls in here when a\nsequence length of 0 is given.\nEntry: none.\nExit: sbf_CtrlPrefix = 0.\nKeeps: all registers and flags."},
        "12197": {"comment":"increase length"},
        "12199": {"comment":"increase pointer"},
        "12202": {"comment":"store char"},
        "12204": {"comment":"done, Fc=0, A=0"},
        "12207": {"comment":"increase pointer"},
        "12209": {"comment":"store char"},
        "12211": {"comment":"decrease remaining length"},
        "12215": {"comment":"not done yet, Fc=1, A=-1"},
        "12217": {"comment":"get pointer"},
        "12218": {"comment":"- start"},
        "12220": {"comment":"sequence length"},
        "12222": {"comment":"done, Fc=0, A=0"},
        "12231": {"comment":"not done yet"},
        "12236": {"comment":"not 1, cancel  !! jr nz"},
        "12239": {"comment":"was not SOH"},
        "12244": {"comment":"length not 1"},
        "12255": {"comment":"was not attribute char"},
        "12265": {"comment":"tHi"},
        "12273": {"comment":"1-4"},
        "12280": {"comment":"tLo"},
        "12287": {"comment":"clear ch8"},
        "12309": {"comment":"find cmd in table, return func in DE"},
        "12314": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor of window IX when the window has a cursor (WDFH_B_CURSOR) and it is not on\nalready: saves the attribute byte at the cursor cell in wdf_crsrattr and sets it to flash\n(LORES cells also get the LORES cursor bits), then sets WDFH_B_CURSORON.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: HL = cursor cell's attribute byte when shown.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "12319": {"comment":"no cursor? exit"},
        "12322": {"comment":"cursor not toggled on? exit"},
        "12333": {"comment":"hires? just flash"},
        "12335": {"comment":"keep ch8"},
        "12337": {"comment":"lores cursor"},
        "12347": {"synopsis":"Hides the cursor of window IX: when WDFH_B_CURSORON is set, puts the saved attribute byte\n(wdf_crsrattr) back at the cursor cell and clears the flag.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: HL = cursor position (L = wdf_crsrx, H = wdf_crsry).\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "12357": {"comment":"cursor not on? exit"},
        "12369": {"synopsis":"Turns window coordinates into a screen position: L = 2*C + wdf_startx (two bytes per\ncharacter cell), H = B + wdf_starty.\nEntry: B = row; C = column; IX = window frame.\nExit: HL = screen position.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"L=2*C+StartX"},
        "12376": {"comment":"H=B+StartY"},
        "12382": {"synopsis":"Turns a screen position into window coordinates, the inverse of ScrD_GetNewXY: C = (L -\nwdf_startx) / 2, B = H - wdf_starty.\nEntry: HL = screen position; IX = window frame.\nExit: B = row; C = column.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "12395": {"synopsis":"Screen driver command \"JC\": sets centred justification (3) by counting E up through\nSetLeftJustify and SetRightJustify into SetNormalJustify.\nEntry: E = 0 (set by CallFuncDE); IX = window frame.\nExit: justification bits of wdf_flagsHi = 3.\nChanges: AF, E."},
        "12396": {"synopsis":"Screen driver command \"JL\": sets left justification (2); falls through SetRightJustify into\nSetNormalJustify.\nEntry: E = 0 (set by CallFuncDE); IX = window frame.\nExit: justification bits of wdf_flagsHi = 2.\nChanges: AF, E."},
        "12397": {"synopsis":"Screen driver command \"JR\": sets right justification (1); falls into SetNormalJustify.\nEntry: E = 0 (set by CallFuncDE); IX = window frame.\nExit: justification bits of wdf_flagsHi = 1.\nChanges: AF, E."},
        "12398": {"synopsis":"Screen driver command \"JN\": writes E into the justification bits (WDFH_JUSTIFICATION) of\nwdf_flagsHi; E = 0 means normal justification.\nEntry: E = justification (0 normal, 1 right, 2 left, 3 centre); IX = window frame.\nExit: wdf_flagsHi updated.\nChanges: AF."},
        "12408": {"synopsis":"move chars as needed for justification"},
        "12414": {"synopsis":"Makes room for the next character under the window's justification. With normal\njustification it does nothing. Otherwise it finds the edges of the text on the cursor's row\n(a null cell or the window edge, from the right margin, the left margin or the middle of the\nmargins) and, unless the target cell is already null, moves the characters between the edges\none cell (two bytes) to the left.\nEntry: HL = cursor position; IX = window frame.\nExit: HL = the cell the next character goes to.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF'."},
        "12419": {"comment":"normal"},
        "12421": {"comment":"right"},
        "12425": {"comment":"left"},
        "12428": {"comment":"!! ld a,lmargin; add a,rmargin; rra"},
        "12431": {"comment":"into X coordinate"},
        "12436": {"comment":"into Y coordinate"},
        "12439": {"comment":"lmargin+rmargin"},
        "12442": {"comment":"rounded"},
        "12453": {"comment":"right edge reached"},
        "12456": {"comment":"left edge reached"},
        "12460": {"comment":"left=right? done"},
        "12461": {"comment":"into x coordinates"},
        "12471": {"comment":"into pointers"},
        "12478": {"comment":"char is null? done"},
        "12481": {"comment":"left=right? done"},
        "12482": {"comment":"#bytes to move"},
        "12485": {"comment":"move them from (HL+2) to (HL)"},
        "12514": {"synopsis":"Fz=1 if char at (HL) is NULL"},
        "12521": {"synopsis":"move right until edge or null char"},
        "12524": {"comment":"null char, exit"},
        "12530": {"comment":"Fc=1, edge reached"},
        "12535": {"synopsis":"move left  until at edge or null char"},
        "12538": {"comment":"null char, exit"},
        "12544": {"comment":"Fc=1, edge reached"},
        "12549": {"synopsis":"move to x"},
        "12553": {"comment":"out of bounds? exit"},
        "12556": {"synopsis":"move to y"},
        "12560": {"comment":"out of bounds? exit"},
        "12563": {"synopsis":"Set left margin"},
        "12567": {"comment":"out of bounds? exit"},
        "12568": {"comment":"assert rmargin >= lmargin"},
        "12581": {"synopsis":"Set right margin"},
        "12585": {"comment":"out of bounds? exit"},
        "12586": {"comment":"assert lmargin <= rmargin"},
        "12599": {"synopsis":"check if C is valid X/Y-coordinate"},
        "12609": {"synopsis":"Checks a new row against window IX: builds the position with row C and the cursor's column\n(ScrD_GetNewXY) and tests it with NewYValid.\nEntry: C = new row; HL = cursor position; IX = window frame.\nExit: Fc = 0, D = the new row's screen line, E = cursor column byte.\nError: Fc = 1 when the row is outside the window.\nChanges: AF, B, DE.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "12620": {"synopsis":"define std application window"},
        "12622": {"comment":"window 1 @abs10,0 94x8"},
        "12630": {"comment":"select & init 1"},
        "12636": {"synopsis":"make full screen grey"},
        "12647": {"comment":"remember active window"},
        "12670": {"comment":"grey/ungrey"},
        "12673": {"comment":"restore active window"},
        "12685": {"synopsis":"define window"},
        "12688": {"comment":"not valid? exit"},
        "12699": {"comment":"IX=DE"},
        "12702": {"comment":"VDU3, y"},
        "12703": {"comment":"VDU2, x"},
        "12706": {"comment":"60-df -> 00-7f"},
        "12709": {"comment":"e0-5f -> 80-ff -> ea-69"},
        "12712": {"comment":"C=width"},
        "12718": {"comment":"B=height"},
        "12724": {"comment":"flags"},
        "12734": {"synopsis":"Entry: IX = window frame, A=flagsF4, B=height, C=width, D=ypos, E=xpos.\nExit: -."},
        "12736": {"comment":"*2 + 1"},
        "12738": {"comment":"line width * 2"},
        "12741": {"comment":"x>=108? error"},
        "12747": {"comment":"y>8? error"},
        "12751": {"comment":"lst_row=ypos+height-1"},
        "12758": {"comment":"height+y>$7f? error"},
        "12761": {"comment":"width<1 or width>128? error"},
        "12767": {"comment":"line width * 2"},
        "12770": {"comment":"end>=108? error"},
        "12799": {"synopsis":"Resets the attributes of window IX: clears wdf_flagsHi, wdf_f2, wdf_f6 and wdf_flagsLo.\nInitWindowFrame falls in here; it is also the $7F function of ScrDrvAttrTable (reset all\ntoggles).\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1; BC = 0.\nChanges: F, BC."},
        "12816": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "12818": {"synopsis":"delete window - not implemented"},
        "12823": {"synopsis":"Select and Clear window"},
        "12827": {"synopsis":"Entry inside SelClearWd: resets the window's attributes (ResetWdAttrs), marks it initialised\n(WDF2_B_INITIALIZED) and jumps to ClearScr. SelInitWd calls it when a window is selected for\nthe first time.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: as ClearScr.","comment":"reset attrs"},
        "12837": {"synopsis":"Select and Init window"},
        "12844": {"comment":"first select? clear"},
        "12848": {"synopsis":"Select and Hold window"},
        "12867": {"synopsis":"Reads the cursor position of window IX. SelHoldWd falls in here after selecting a window.\nEntry: IX = window frame.\nExit: L = wdf_crsrx; H = wdf_crsry.\nChanges: HL."},
        "12874": {"synopsis":"Stores HL as the cursor position of window IX.\nEntry: HL = cursor position; IX = window frame.\nExit: wdf_crsrx = L; wdf_crsry = H.\nKeeps: all registers."},
        "12881": {"synopsis":"Entry: A = window number, A = 0 use current window.\nExit: Fc = 0, success and IX = frame, A = window number character '1' to '8'; Fc = 1,\nfailure and A = RC_Hand."},
        "12882": {"comment":"a<>0? don't use current window"},
        "12895": {"comment":"SBF page"},
        "12898": {"comment":"+$100 for each window"},
        "12902": {"comment":"window frame"},
        "12906": {"comment":"!! not enough to assert valid window"},
        "12910": {"synopsis":"Checks a window number argument: the screen driver passes it less $20, so A + $20 must be\nthe digit '1'-'8'.\nEntry: A = window digit - $20.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = window index 0-7.\nError: Fc = 1 when it is not '1'-'8'.\nChanges: AF."},
        "12931": {"synopsis":"Grey/Ungrey window"},
        "12966": {"synopsis":"Output n copies of the code m"},
        "12967": {"comment":"zero copies? exit"},
        "12980": {"synopsis":"EOR toggles"},
        "12985": {"synopsis":"apply toggles"},
        "12986": {"comment":"wdf_f6 always zero?"},
        "13014": {"synopsis":"Screen driver command \".\": passes the rest of the sequence to DC_Gen, with BHL = sbf_VDU1 in\nthe screen base bank (ubScreenBase) and C = the sequence length less 1.\nEntry: sbf_PrefixSeq = sequence length.\nExit: as DC_Gen.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "13015": {"comment":"screen base bank"},
        "13025": {"comment":"-1 for '.'"},
        "13026": {"comment":"length"},
        "13032": {"synopsis":"Table of the screen driver's SOH commands, read by FindSDCmd: 27 entries of 4 bytes (the\ncommand letter, a second byte that must match sbf_VDU1 or 0 for any, the handler's address),\nended by 0. CallFuncDE calls the handler with A, B, C = the next three sequence bytes less\n$20 and E = 0."},
        "13141": {"synopsis":"Table of the screen driver's one-letter SOH sequences, read by ScrDrvGetAttrBits. Three\nkinds of 3-byte entries, ended by 0: 12 attribute toggles (letter, wdf_flagsLo bits,\nwdf_flagsHi bits); three functions ($FF scroll up, $FE scroll down, $7F ResetWdAttrs) with\nthe handler's address; 27 special characters (code, LORES code, control byte: bit 0 selects\nLORES $100-$1FF, bits 1-2 make it 2 or 3 cells wide)."},
        "13147": {"comment":"!! not delete"},
        "13159": {"comment":"multiple output"},
        "13177": {"comment":"scroll up"},
        "13180": {"comment":"scroll down"},
        "13183": {"comment":"reset all toggles"},
        "13186": {"comment":"grave accent"},
        "13189": {"comment":"vertical bar"},
        "13192": {"comment":"exact"},
        "13195": {"comment":"shift         3*VDU $198"},
        "13198": {"comment":"diamond"},
        "13201": {"comment":"square"},
        "13204": {"comment":"pointer right"},
        "13207": {"comment":"pointer down"},
        "13210": {"comment":"pointer left"},
        "13213": {"comment":"pointer up"},
        "13216": {"comment":"bullet right"},
        "13219": {"comment":"bullet down"},
        "13222": {"comment":"bullet left"},
        "13225": {"comment":"bullet up"},
        "13228": {"comment":"space         3*VDU $100"},
        "13231": {"comment":"enter         3*VDU $103"},
        "13234": {"comment":"tab           3*VDU $106"},
        "13237": {"comment":"del           3*VDU $109"},
        "13240": {"comment":"esc           3*VDU $10c"},
        "13243": {"comment":"index         3*VDU $10f"},
        "13246": {"comment":"menu          3*VDU $112"},
        "13249": {"comment":"help          3*VDU $115"},
        "13252": {"comment":"bell          3*VDU $19b"},
        "13255": {"comment":"outline right 2*VDU $016"},
        "13258": {"comment":"outline down  2*VDU $094"},
        "13261": {"comment":"outline left  2*VDU $014"},
        "13264": {"comment":"outline up    2*VDU $096"},
        "13272": {"synopsis":"save & restore screen file\n\nA = reason code:\nSR_SUS ($01) Save user screen\nSR_WPD ($03) Write parameter data (mailbox)\nSR_RPD ($04) Read parameter data (mailbox)\nSR_FUS ($05) Free user screen\nSR_CRM ($06) Remove card (not implemented)\nSR_CIN ($07) Insert card (not implemented)\nSR_PWT ($08) Page wait\nSR_RND ($09) Occasionally a random number (system use)"},
        "13275": {"synopsis":"save user screen\nEntry: -.\nExit: IX = screen image handle."},
        "13319": {"comment":"length/bank"},
        "13323": {"comment":"data"},
        "13334": {"comment":"mailbox control, store"},
        "13348": {"comment":"no mail, exit"},
        "13352": {"comment":"compare mailbox name"},
        "13359": {"comment":"compare null-terminated strings"},
        "13392": {"synopsis":"free user screen\n\nIX = screen image handle"},
        "13398": {"synopsis":"Frees a handle and its memory: FreeMemData0 releases the data, FreeHandle releases the\nhandle by its type (hnd_Type). Entry inside OSSr_FUS after its handle check; file and\nfilesystem code jump here too.\nEntry: IX = handle.\nExit: handle and memory freed.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "13418": {"comment":"purge keyboard buffer"},
        "13424": {"comment":"CLI active? exit"},
        "13500": {"comment":"go see if it's extended char"},
        "13514": {"comment":"if pre-emption just redraw and wait more"},
        "13537": {"synopsis":"Key-to-character table, one table seen through three labels a byte apart: 90 entries of 4\nbytes (internal key code, ISO Latin-1 code, LORES font code low byte, high byte), bold and\ntiny variants included, followed by zero bytes that end the search. OS_In searches this\ncolumn with Chr2ScreenCode to turn a foreign key code into its ISO character.","comment":"Â£ internal code"},
        "13538": {"synopsis":"Second column of the key-to-character table (see Key2Chr_tbl): the ISO Latin-1 code of each\nentry. Char2VDU searches it with Chr2ScreenCode to find a character's LORES code, read from\nthe next two bytes.","comment":"Â£ char code"},
        "13539": {"synopsis":"Third column of the key-to-character table (see Key2Chr_tbl): the low byte of each entry's\nLORES font code, followed by the high byte. VDU2ChrCode searches it with Chr2ScreenCode.","comment":"Lores low byte, high byte in the font"},
