        "14043": {"comment":"set XONXOFF"},
        "14045": {"comment":"XON"},
        "14048": {"comment":"set serial control byte"},
        "14051": {"comment":"buffered RX routine if XON or parity set"},
        "14053": {"synopsis":"Serial interface buffer status enquiry\nEntry: -.\nExit: BC = TxStatus (B used, C free); DE = RxStatus (D used, E free); A = int status."},
        "14059": {"comment":"used"},
        "14061": {"comment":"free = 1 - used"},
        "14064": {"comment":"is Tx empty ?"},
        "14070": {"comment":"1 byte free in Tx"},
        "14073": {"comment":"1 byte used in Tx"},
        "14078": {"synopsis":"Serial interface timeout\nEntry: BC = timeout in centiseconds.\nExit: -."},
        "14082": {"comment":"no error"},
        "14084": {"synopsis":"Serial interface buffer flush\nEntry: -."},
        "14088": {"comment":"buffer empty"},
        "14094": {"synopsis":"OS_Si SI_FTX (flush transmit buffer), kernel 1 part: not available.\nEntry: none.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Na always.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"not available"},
        "14098": {"synopsis":"Serial interface common subroutines"},
        "14104": {"synopsis":"Reads a Panel parameter into DE: calls OS_Nq with DE = 2, which returns the value in DE.\nEntry: BC = parameter (PA_xxx).\nExit: DE = value.\nChanges: AF, DE.","comment":"return parameter in DE"},
        "14110": {"synopsis":"Turns a baud rate into its register code: looks DE up in BaudRates and returns its index. A\nrate not in the table gives BR_9600.\nEntry: DE = baud rate.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = code 0-7.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF'.","comment":"count from 0 upwards"},
        "14112": {"comment":"baud rate into BC"},
        "14117": {"comment":"de=(hl)++"},
        "14121": {"comment":"use 9600 if end of list"},
        "14131": {"comment":"found? exit"},
        "14133": {"comment":"increment and loop"},
        "14139": {"comment":"be sure to keep 3 first bits"},
        "14141": {"comment":"reset Fc"},
        "14143": {"synopsis":"Table of the baud rates the serial port supports, read by BaudToReg: 8 words (75, 300, 600,\n1200, 2400, 9600, 19200, 38400) in register code order, ended by a zero word."},
        "14161": {"synopsis":"OSPrtPrint\nPrint control sequence or char to printer filter.\nCalled from OS_PRT.\nStack frame is established (OSFramePush).\n\n..BCDEHL/IXIY   same\nAF....../....   different\nEntry: A = character to be written to printer filter.\nExit: success Fc = 0, failure Fc = 1 and A = RC_ESC or RC_WP."},
        "14163": {"comment":"we need screen because prt sequence buffer is in SBF"},
        "14167": {"comment":"ld l,(PrtSeqPrefix)"},
        "14172": {"comment":"have ctrl sequence? add to it"},
        "14176": {"comment":"not ctrl char? print"},
        "14180": {"comment":"ESC? print"},
        "14182": {"comment":"00-06, 0E-1F: ctrl sequence"},
        "14184": {"comment":"otherwise print"},
        "14190": {"comment":"store prefix char"},
        "14193": {"comment":"init sequence"},
        "14199": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "14202": {"comment":"put into buffer"},
        "14209": {"comment":"not done yet? exit, Fc=0"},
        "14211": {"comment":"ctrl char"},
        "14214": {"comment":"c,(PrtSequence) - length"},
        "14220": {"comment":"buffer"},
        "14223": {"comment":"see below"},
        "14228": {"comment":"see below"},
        "14232": {"comment":"reset prefix"},
        "14244": {"synopsis":"Printer Filter initialisation\ncalled from OSSp_Pagfi during reset or when applying new parameters\nEntry: -.\nExit: -.","comment":"func $C6"},
        "14266": {"comment":"enquire TrX"},
        "14268": {"comment":"store translation char or NULL"},
        "14325": {"comment":"not using placeholder"},
        "14329": {"comment":"uses placeholder"},
        "14359": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "14371": {"synopsis":"Printer Filter Print Char\nEntry: A=char.\nExit: -."},
        "14387": {"synopsis":"Printer filter, one character. FF, LF and CR go to PrntFF, PrntLF and PrntCR. Any other\ncharacter first sends pending attribute changes (ApplyAttrs); a space is only counted in\nPendingSpaces. Otherwise pending spaces are printed, then:\n1. When an attribute that is on uses a placeholder, its 'on' string is printed with the\nplaceholder replaced by the character.\n2. Otherwise the character is looked up in Translations; a match prints its translation\nstring (OS_Nq), and anything else goes to PutChar as it is.\nEntry: A = character, also in prtInChar; StackBufPtr = 33-byte stack buffer.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 from the serial output.","comment":"handle FF, LF, CR"},
        "14408": {"comment":"delay spaces"},
        "14417": {"comment":"print pending spaces"},
        "14437": {"comment":"try to translate non-NULL char"},
        "14451": {"comment":"not found, print as is"},
        "14453": {"comment":"print output string"},
        "14467": {"comment":"on"},
        "14473": {"comment":"no attribute, try translating"},
        "14476": {"comment":"store length"},
        "14477": {"comment":"find placeholder in string"},
        "14485": {"comment":"not found, try translating"},
        "14487": {"comment":"replace placeholder with current char"},
        "14492": {"comment":"and print"},
        "14496": {"comment":"forget spaces"},
        "14509": {"comment":"next line if allowed"},
        "14513": {"comment":"otherwise just CR"},
        "14515": {"comment":"forget spaces"},
        "14523": {"comment":"was LF done by CR already?"},
        "14529": {"comment":"otherwise print LF"},
        "14532": {"comment":"inc row, reset if pagelen reached"},
        "14538": {"comment":"if row++=pagelen then reset row"},
        "14548": {"synopsis":"Sends a byte to the printer: when output is enabled (PRT_B_ENABLED in Flags) writes it to\nthe serial port with OSSiPbt and the default timeout (BC = -1).\nEntry: A = byte.\nExit: Fc = 0 (also when output is disabled).\nError: as OSSiPbt.\nKeeps: BC, HL.","comment":"Fc=0"},
        "14549": {"comment":"return if printing disabled"},
        "14558": {"comment":"preserve hl"},
        "14559": {"comment":"default timeout"},
        "14562": {"comment":"write byte to serial port"},
        "14572": {"comment":"print Eop"},
        "14584": {"comment":"no Eop, send series of linefeeds"},
        "14592": {"comment":"find out how many lines to print"},
        "14597": {"comment":"pagelen-rows"},
        "14598": {"comment":"none, exit"},
        "14601": {"comment":"select CR or LF"},
        "14612": {"comment":"print char B times"},
        "14618": {"comment":"reset row/space counts"},
        "14626": {"synopsis":"Printer Filter Print control sequence\nEntry: A = control char (PrtSeqPrefix); C = length (PrtSequence); DE = buffer (PrtSeqBuf).\nExit: -.","comment":"prefix<>5, exit"},
        "14629": {"comment":"length=0, exit"},
        "14632": {"comment":"find char in table"},
        "14645": {"comment":"lower()"},
        "14648": {"comment":"found"},
        "14656": {"comment":"not found, exit"},
        "14660": {"comment":"not attribute toggle"},
        "14662": {"comment":"toggle ON/OFF flag"},
        "14691": {"comment":"push return address"},
        "14695": {"comment":"get func address and call it"},
        "14700": {"synopsis":"Table of 6 words: the handlers of the printer filter's control sequences after the 8\nattribute letters of CtrlChars, in its order: FilterOn ('['), FilterOff (']'), Microspace\n('h'), ResetAttrs ('s'), SetPageLen ('p'), SendHex ('$'). OSPrtPrntCtrlSeq reads it."},
        "14712": {"synopsis":"The printer filter's control sequence letters, ended by 0, searched by OSPrtPrntCtrlSeq\nafter OR $20: \"ubxilrae\" (attributes 0-7, toggled in AttrUnderline to AttrUserdef), then\n'{', '}', 'h', 's', 'p', '$' (handlers in CtrlSeqFuncs; '{' and '}' match '[' and ']')."},
        "14727": {"synopsis":"$ - output hex char"},
        "14730": {"comment":"skip '$'"},
        "14731": {"comment":"length<>3, exit"},
        "14739": {"comment":"high nibble"},
        "14743": {"comment":"*16"},
        "14749": {"comment":"low nibble"},
        "14757": {"synopsis":"Converts an ASCII hex digit ('0'-'9', 'A'-'F' or 'a'-'f') to its value.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = value 0-15.\nError: Fc = 0 when A is not a hex digit.\nChanges: AF."},
        "14764": {"comment":"upper()"},
        "14775": {"synopsis":"[ - turn filter on"},
        "14776": {"comment":"soft reset serial"},
        "14781": {"comment":"enable output"},
        "14789": {"comment":"print Pon"},
        "14794": {"synopsis":"] - turn filter off","comment":"print Pof"},
        "14800": {"comment":"disable output"},
        "14806": {"synopsis":"h - microspace","comment":"length<>2, exit"},
        "14815": {"comment":"print Mip"},
        "14825": {"comment":"get Mio, default to $20"},
        "14839": {"comment":"skip 'h'"},
        "14840": {"comment":"print Mio+char-$20"},
        "14847": {"comment":"print Mis"},
        "14854": {"synopsis":"get parameter and print it"},
        "14858": {"synopsis":"print stack buffer"},
        "14859": {"comment":"length = 0, exit"},
        "14874": {"synopsis":"reset attributes"},
        "14885": {"comment":"was already off"},
        "14887": {"comment":"off"},
        "14898": {"synopsis":"p - set page length","comment":"length<>2, exit"},
        "14904": {"comment":"reset row count"},
        "14910": {"comment":"skip 'p'"},
        "14914": {"comment":"length=char-$20"},
        "14919": {"synopsis":"Sends the pending attribute changes: for each of the 8 printer attributes, from AttrUserdef\ndown to AttrUnderline, with PRA_B_PENDING set, prints pending spaces and toggles it with\nToggleAttr (C = the new state).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 from the serial output.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14933": {"comment":"inverse on/off"},
        "14947": {"synopsis":"Toggles a printer attribute: flips PRA_B_ON at (HL), clears PRA_B_PENDING and, unless the\nattribute uses a placeholder, prints its 'on' or 'off' string (GetPAtoggle,\nPrntStackBuffer).\nEntry: HL = attribute byte; B = attribute number 1-8; C = 1 for on, 0 for off.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 from the serial output.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "14949": {"comment":"toggle state and mark as done"},
        "14968": {"synopsis":"get PA_On (C=1) or PA_Off (C=0) for attribute B (AttrUserDef=8 ... AttUndeLine=1)","comment":"(B-1)*4+28+1-c = 4*B+25-C"},
        "14976": {"comment":"25+4*B-C"},
        "14977": {"comment":"PA_OnX/PA_OffX"},
        "14985": {"comment":"enquire parameter"},
        "14988": {"synopsis":"Prints the spaces counted in PendingSpaces with PutChar and clears the count.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = $20 after printing, A = 0 when there were none.\nError: Fc = 1 from the serial output (count kept).\nKeeps: BC."},
        "15013": {"synopsis":"Reads a Panel or PrinterEd parameter into DE: OS_Nq with DE = 2, then tests the length.\nEntry: BC = parameter.\nExit: DE = value; A = returned length; Fz = 1 when it is 0 (parameter not set); Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "15016": {"comment":"enquire (fetch) parameter"},
        "15020": {"synopsis":"Gives the OS_Nq reason of a printer translation's character: B = $80, C = $48 + 2*A for\nTr1-Tr9 (A = 0-8) and $6E + 2*A for Tr10 upwards. The translation string is the next reason\n(BC + 1).\nEntry: A = translation index from 0.\nExit: BC = reason.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "15023": {"comment":"Tr1-Tr9"},
        "15025": {"comment":"Tr10-Tr37"},
        "15033": {"synopsis":"Resets the printer filter's state: clears the on and pending bits of the 8 attributes,\nkeeping their reset-at-CR and placeholder bits, sets PendingSpaces and Rows to 0 and PageLen\nto 66.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = 66.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."}
      }
    },
