        "13056": {"synopsis":"Date filter table of the UK, run at $7300 in segment 1, also used for the US, IS, JP and TR\ncountry settings. The country setup (os/spnq1.asm) stores the address of the selected\ncountry's table in uwGnDateFilter; GN_Gdt and GN_Pdt (gn/gnaconv.asm) and GNLdm\n(gn/gnldm.asm) open it with GN_Flo. It translates between the language's words and the\none-byte codes of the GN date routines (GN_Pdt uses reverse mode). Layout: a word, the\ntable's length; a byte of left-hand flags and one of right-hand flags (FL_ALPHA, FL_ISO,\n...); then pairs of length-prefixed strings, the length byte counting itself: the word, then\nthe code: $81-$87 the days, $A1-$A7 their short names, $88-$8B the ordinal suffixes, $8C/$8D\nAD and BC, $C1-$CC the months, $E1-$EC their short names, $91-$93 today, yesterday and\ntomorrow."},
        "13058": {"comment":"left-hand has Alpha"},
        "13059": {"comment":"right-hand has ISO chars"},
        "13416": {"synopsis":"End of the UK date filter and start of the French one (DateFilter_FR, used for the FR and CH\ncountry settings), with the same layout as DateFilter_UK.\nOZ source name: end_DateFilter_UK."},
        "13418": {"comment":"left-hand has ISO chars, Alpha & punctuation"},
        "13419": {"comment":"right-hand has ISO chars"},
        "13528": {"comment":"first (not applicable because apply to 1, 11, 21, 31)"},
        "13540": {"comment":"'AD'"},
        "13547": {"comment":"'BC'"},
        "13771": {"synopsis":"End of the French date filter and start of the Danish one (DateFilter_DK, used for the DK\ncountry setting), with the same layout as DateFilter_UK.\nOZ source name: end_DateFilter_FR."},
        "13773": {"comment":"left-hand has ISO chars, Alpha & punctuation"},
        "13774": {"comment":"right-hand has ISO chars"},
        "13852": {"comment":"Lï¿½rdag (Saturday)"},
        "13861": {"comment":"Lï¿½r (Sat)"},
