        "1154": {"synopsis":"convert ASCII string to internal date\nEntry: HL=source, DE=destination, IX=source handle (if HL<2); A=format, B=max chars in,\nC=delimter (if A5=1).\nExit: ABC=date, HL=input index/ptr; Fc=1, A=error."},
        "1157": {"comment":"bank of date filter table in S1 mandatory (else GN_FLO crashes)"},
        "1173": {"synopsis":"Main body of GN_Gdt, called by GNGdt once the date filter's bank (DAF_BNK) is bound in S1.\n1. Checks that the caller's B (maximum characters) is 1-128, else RC_Bad.\n2. Opens the localised date filter (uwGnDateFilter) with GN_Flo, case-insensitive and with a\nbuffer of B bytes, and copies up to B characters from the source (ReadOsfHL) into it with\nGN_Flw; end of file ends the copy.\n3. Reads the fields back through the filter: numbers with GN_Gdn, filter codes for month and\nweekday names, ordinal suffixes and AD/BC, separated by space, '/', '-', TAB, '.' or the\ncaller's C. The day/month order comes from the caller's A or the PA_Dat setting; a one- or\ntwo-digit year gets the current century.\n4. Converts day, month and year with GNDeiMain and returns the date through Wr_ABC_OsfDE.\n5. Closes the filter and returns the source index (HL < 256) or the advanced pointer.\nEntry: IY = OS frame with the caller's HL = source, DE = destination, A = format, B =\nmaximum characters, C = delimiter (if A bit 5 = 1).\nExit: frame ABC = date (DE < 256) or the date written at DE; frame HL = index or pointer.\nError: frame Fc = 1, A = RC_Bad, RC_Sntx or the read/filter error (PutOsf_Err).","comment":"check we have 1-128 chars"},
