        "1727": {"synopsis":"Main body of GN_Pdt, called by GNPdt with the date filter's bank bound in S1 and the date\ncopied to pGnTmpDate. Opens the date filter in reverse mode (20-byte buffer), writes the\nfields as the caller's A and B ask (leading space, weekday, day and month in European,\nAmerican or PA_Dat order, ordinal suffix, 2- or 4-digit year, AD/BC, trailing space), then\nmoves the filter's output to the destination with WriteOsfDE and closes the filter.\nEntry: IY = OS frame (caller's A, B = format, C = delimiter, DE = destination, IX = handle\nif DE < 2); date at pGnTmpDate.\nExit: frame DE = output pointer when it was > 255.\nError: frame Fc = 1, A = RC_Sntx (bad date) or the filter/write error; DE left as it was.\nKeeps: IX."},
