        "1981": {"synopsis":"Writes A into the GN_Pdt output filter with GN_Flw (IX = filter). On an error it discards\nits return address and leaves through pdt_Err, which stores the error in the frame, closes\nthe filter and returns from pdt_0; pdtFlw_spc, placed before it, writes a space.\nEntry: A = character or filter code; IX = filter; IY = OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "1989": {"synopsis":"Writes the delimiter after a GN_Pdt date field: the caller's C when bit 5 of the caller's A\nis set, otherwise a space; continues in pdtFlw (or pdtFlw_spc).\nEntry: IX = filter; IY = OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: as pdtFlw, leaves GN_Pdt.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"use C as delimeter?"},
