        "2367": {"synopsis":"Undoes GN_Gtm's OS_Bix of a memory source and updates the caller's pointer: the bytes used\n(HL minus the bound start in BC) are added to the frame's HL, and OS_Box restores the\nsegment bindings saved in DE. HL is subtracted with sbc, so Fc should be 0 on entry.\nEntry: HL = current (bound) source pointer; BC = bound start address from OS_Bix; DE =\nbindings from OS_Bix; IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = the caller's pointer advanced past the bytes read.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"output length"},
