        "6036": {"comment":"print chars backward"},
        "6039": {"comment":"until we are where we started"},
        "6041": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "6045": {"synopsis":"Moves GN_Sip's cursor one character left (PrintBackChar) and classifies the character there;\ncontinues in ClsBufChar.\nEntry: C = cursor; DE = buffer at the cursor.\nExit: C, DE one less; A = character; flags from GN_Cls.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"move left"},
        "6050": {"synopsis":"Prints the character at GN_Sip's cursor and moves one right (PrCharBumpC_DE), then\nclassifies the character there; continues in ClsBufChar.\nEntry: C = cursor; DE = buffer at the cursor.\nExit: C, DE one more; A = character; flags from GN_Cls.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"move right"},
        "6053": {"synopsis":"Reads the character at DE in the caller's buffer (Ld_A_HL) and classifies it with GN_Cls.\nEntry: DE = buffer pointer.\nExit: A = character; Fc = 1 for a letter (Fz = 1 lower case), Fc = 0 and Fz = 1 for a digit,\nFc = 0 and Fz = 0 otherwise.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"get buffer char and classify it"},
        "6064": {"synopsis":"Entry: B=right margin+1, C=left margin."},
        "6067": {"comment":"Set left margin"},
        "6080": {"comment":"Set right margin"},
        "6091": {"synopsis":"Moves GN_Sip's cursor one place left on screen and in the buffer: decrements C and DE, then\nprints BS, the character there (a null as a space) and BS again. An output error leaves\nthrough sip_PrChar, which drops one return address and goes to sip_err.\nEntry: C = cursor; DE = buffer at the cursor.\nExit: C, DE one less.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"decrement pos"},
        "6093": {"comment":"move left"},
        "6098": {"comment":"get char, replace NULL with space"},
        "6104": {"comment":"print it"},
        "6107": {"comment":"and move back"},
        "6112": {"synopsis":"Prints the buffer character at DE and moves GN_Sip's cursor right: increments C and DE. An\noutput error leaves through sip_PrChar to sip_err.\nEntry: C = cursor; DE = buffer at the cursor.\nExit: C, DE one more.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"get char in buffer"},
        "6113": {"comment":"print it"},
        "6116": {"comment":"increment pos"},
        "6119": {"synopsis":"Inverts the case of a letter for GN_Sip's ^S. Codes below 191 have bit 5 flipped (ASCII\nletters); a code from 191 up is flipped only when it or its lower-case form is in\nInvCaseTable (ISO Latin letters), otherwise it is returned unchanged.\nEntry: A = letter (classified by the caller).\nExit: A = letter in the other case.\nChanges: F, A.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "6123": {"comment":"normal ASCII alpha's can always be case inversed..."},
        "6134": {"comment":"check for upper case -> lower case"},
        "6137": {"comment":"check for lower case -> upper case"},
        "6147": {"comment":"case inverse the allowed ISO character"},
        "6152": {"synopsis":"Table of 9 bytes: the upper-case ISO Latin letters whose case InvCase may invert (196, 197,\n198, 199, 203, 209, 214, 216, 220); the lower-case form is the code + $20."},
        "6161": {"synopsis":"End of InvCaseTable, used only to count its entries. The same address starts\nSipExtended_tbl, GN_Sip's table of extended keys: a key code and a handler word each."},
        "6209": {"synopsis":"!! drops thru - is this intentional?"},
        "6237": {"synopsis":"write local string to standard output\nEntry: HL = local pointer to null-terminated string.\nExit: HL = pointer to null.\nChanges: F, HL.","comment":"fast OS_Bix"},
        "6240": {"comment":"remember old S1S2 bindings"},
        "6241": {"comment":"HL=local"},
        "6243": {"comment":"remember start of string in S1"},
        "6244": {"comment":"then display as local pointer beginning from S1 onwards"},
        "6247": {"comment":"get length of string that was sent to screen driver"},
        "6254": {"comment":"return original HL now updated to point at null-terminator"},
        "6257": {"comment":"restore S1 + S2 bindings"},
        "6262": {"synopsis":"Fast OS_Bix for a local pointer of the GN caller: when HL is in S2 it binds the caller's S2\ninto S1 and the caller's S3 into S2; when HL is in S3 it binds the caller's S3 into S1 and\nleaves S2 (the source comment says 'S1=caller S2'); HL is then moved into S1. A pointer\nbelow $8000 is left alone. The bindings come from the OS frame.\nEntry: HL = caller's local pointer; IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = pointer in S0/S1; DE = previous S1 (E) and S2 (D) bindings, for box_s1s2.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"remember S2S1 in DE"},
        "6268": {"comment":"not kernel space, no bankswitching"},
        "6277": {"comment":"HL in S2 - S1=caller S2, S2=caller S3"},
        "6279": {"comment":"HL in S3"},
        "6280": {"comment":"S1=caller S2"},
        "6284": {"comment":"S1 fix"},
        "6289": {"synopsis":"Binds bank C into segment 1 and bank B into segment 2, updating the soft copies at BLSC_SR1\nand the ports BL_SR1, BL_SR2. With the DE that bix_s1s2 returned, moved to BC, it restores\nthe bindings.\nEntry: C = bank for S1; B = bank for S2.\nChanges: A."},
        "6300": {"synopsis":"write string at extended address to standard output\nEntry: BHL = pointer to null-terminated string (B=0 isn't local, it's bank 0).\nExit: HL = pointer to null.\nChanges: F, HL.","comment":"bind BHL into S1"},
        "6304": {"comment":"then adjust offset to segment 1"},
        "6311": {"comment":"strip segment 1 mask (now a pure bank offset)"},
        "6319": {"comment":"restored original segment mask of pointer"},
        "6320": {"comment":"return pointer to null (bank unchanged)"},
        "6323": {"comment":"restore S1 bank binding"},
        "6326": {"synopsis":"!! Memory routines can be made quite a lot faster\n\nAlso worth considering are routines to write multiple bytes\nwith one call - Ld_ade_BHL, Ld_BHL_ade etc.\nwrite byte at extended address\nEntry: A=byte, BDE=address.\nExit: -.\nChanges: F."},
        "6331": {"comment":"B>0? far pointer"},
        "6336": {"comment":"check S3"},
        "6345": {"comment":"check S2"},
        "6354": {"comment":"local pointer, just write"},
        "6359": {"comment":"bind needed bank in S1"},
        "6364": {"comment":"S1 fix"},
        "6368": {"comment":"store byte"},
        "6369": {"comment":"restore S1"},
        "6374": {"synopsis":"read byte at extended address\nEntry: BHL=address (B=0: local address).\nExit: A=byte.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6381": {"synopsis":"Entry: BHL=address (B=0: local address).\nExit: A=byte.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6382": {"comment":"B>0? far pointer"},
