        "10078": {"synopsis":"Pushes a new 30-byte file system node on the wildcard handler's node list (OS_Mal from\nwc_pMemPool, wc_NodeCount + 1). It continues from the old top node, if any: its flags, a son\nof its DOR (DR_DUP, DR_SON) and its wildcard position (the start again for a \"//\" node);\notherwise it starts at the device root. Then it parses the next segment with GN_Pfs, marking\n\"//\" with FSNF_B_WILDDIR.\nEntry: IX = wildcard handler.\nExit: IY = new node, bound in S1; Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code; the new node is freed again and IY = the top of the list.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
