        "12115": {"comment":"cde' = monthday"},
        "12119": {"comment":"A=days high"},
        "12123": {"comment":"BHL=Ahl'"},
        "12124": {"comment":"main"},
        "12129": {"comment":"days in BHL"},
        "12130": {"comment":"validate weekday"},
        "12131": {"comment":"day of week"},
        "12133": {"comment":"unspecified"},
        "12135": {"comment":"!! 3*'rlca'"},
        "12139": {"comment":"weekday, 1-7"},
        "12141": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12146": {"comment":"main"},
        "12149": {"comment":"weekday doesn't match"},
        "12151": {"comment":"ABC=BHL=internal date"},
        "12156": {"synopsis":"Adds cde to Ahl in the alternate set for GNDeiMain (called with the alternate set active).\nOn signed overflow it switches back with exx, drops its return address and leaves GNDeiMain\nwith Fc = 1.\nEntry: A, HL = days; C, DE = days to add.\nExit: AHL = AHL + CDE.\nError: Fc = 1, returned from GNDeiMain.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "12159": {"comment":"main"},
        "12166": {"synopsis":"Step of GNDeiMain's year loop, accepting a subtraction: drops the AF and year the loop saved\nunder its return address, copies B into B' and adds the days cde' to Ahl'. On overflow it\nunwinds GNDeiMain's saved registers and leaves it with Fc = 1.\nEntry: called from dei_4/dei_5 inside GNDeiMain; cde' = days of the year rule.\nExit: Ahl' = Ahl' + cde'.\nError: Fc = 1, returned from GNDeiMain.","comment":"caller PC"},
        "12167": {"comment":"A !! isn't used at all?"},
        "12168": {"comment":"discard year"},
        "12170": {"comment":"caller pc"},
        "12171": {"comment":"remember A"},
        "12172": {"comment":"b'=B"},
        "12173": {"comment":"!! B0=0 means leap year"},
        "12175": {"comment":"restore A"},
        "12176": {"comment":"Ahl'+=cde'"},
        "12179": {"comment":"no overflow"},
        "12180": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "12182": {"comment":"and error"},
        "12184": {"synopsis":"basically it's 24bit/8bit division\nEntry: CHL=#days.\nExit: A=weekday (CHL=#weeks, not used)."},
        "12188": {"comment":"a=0, Fc=0"},
        "12189": {"comment":"ACHL << 1 + Fc"},
        "12191": {"comment":"!! 'adc hl, hl; rl c; rla'"},
        "12197": {"comment":"keep A in range 0-6"},
        "12199": {"comment":"!! just 'jr nc'"},
        "12206": {"synopsis":"Reads one rule of DaysInYears: the number of years and the days in them.\nEntry: IX = DaysInYears entry.\nExit: DE = years; C'DE' = days.\nChanges: DE, C', DE'.","comment":"DE = #years"},
        "12213": {"comment":"cde' = #days"},
        "12224": {"synopsis":"Negates DE and the alternate set's CDE: DE = -DE, C'DE' = -C'DE'.\nEntry: DE = years; C'DE' = days.\nExit: both negated.\nChanges: DE, C', DE', AF'.\nKeeps: AF, HL.","comment":"DE = -DE"},
        "12227": {"comment":"!! 'sub a, e;ld e, a'"},
        "12228": {"comment":"!! 'ld a, 0; sbc a, d; ld d, a'"},
        "12229": {"comment":"!! avoids push/pop"},
        "12233": {"comment":"cde' = -cde'"},
        "12236": {"comment":"!! same here"},
        "12247": {"synopsis":"Table of the 5 year rules of the calendar, 5 bytes each: days (3 bytes, low first), then\nyears (word): 3200 years = 1168775 days, 400 = 146097, 100 = 36524, 4 = 1461 and 1 = 365.\nRead through GetYearDays by GNDieMain and GNDeiMain. The 3200-year rule has no leap day (the\nsource notes there is no such official rule).","comment":"3200*365+8*97-1"},
        "12252": {"comment":"400*365+4*24+1"},
        "12257": {"comment":"100*365+25-1"},
        "12262": {"comment":"4*365+1"},
        "12272": {"synopsis":"Table of 12 bytes: the days in each month from March to February (31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31,\n30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 28), used by GNDieMain and GNDeiMain."},
        "12284": {"synopsis":"Writes the 11-byte time block (uwGnDateLow/Mid/High and GnHwTimeBuf) back into the system's\nmonth/date/time area, through GN_Wbe.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12288": {"comment":"copy into system time"},
        "12298": {"synopsis":"Sets up a copy of the system time block: BHL = its extended address (OS_Ht, A = HT_MDT), DE\n= uwGnDateLow, C = 11 bytes. Shared by GetSysTime and SetSysTime.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BHL = system time area; DE = uwGnDateLow; C = 11."},
        "12300": {"comment":"BHL=$2180AB (system time)"},
        "12309": {"synopsis":"Copies the 11-byte system time block (address from OS_Ht HT_MDT) into uwGnDateLow/Mid/High\nand GnHwTimeBuf through GN_Rbe.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12312": {"comment":"copy from system time"},
        "12322": {"synopsis":"hlBHL=date, CDE=seconds, A=cseconds"},
        "12342": {"comment":"BHL = top 24 bits"},
        "12347": {"comment":"cde = bottom 24 bits"},
        "12350": {"comment":"csec"},
        "12355": {"comment":"!! faster: (x/675 ) >> 7"},
        "12359": {"comment":"BHLcde/86 400"},
        "12369": {"synopsis":"Adds the hardware timer read into GnHwTimeBuf to the 48-bit base value at uwGnDateLow:\nresult = base + GnHwTimeBuf[2..4] * 60 + GnHwTimeBuf[1] (DEBCx60). GetSysDateTime divides it\nby 86 400.\nEntry: GnHwTimeBuf filled by OS_Ht HT_RD.\nExit: HL = high, DE = middle, IY = low word of the sum.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY."},
        "12382": {"comment":"HLDEIY=GnDate+HwTime[234]*60+HwTime[1]"},
        "12419": {"synopsis":"Function return routines"},
        "12427": {"synopsis":"Common exit of a GN call, reached when the function returns into the GN table page, whose\nfirst two jumps lead here. Unwinds the OS frame: restores IY and the S2 binding from it, and\nloads AF, BC, DE, HL from the frame, so the caller gets the values the function stored with\nPutOsf_xxx; leaves through OZCallReturn1, which rebinds S3 and returns.\nEntry: SP = OS frame (return address already taken)."},
        "12443": {"synopsis":"Exit of a GN call that returns its results in registers (GN_Die, GN_Dei, GN_D24 jump here\nwith their return address still on the stack). Drops it, restores IY and the S2 binding from\nthe frame and discards the frame's register copies, so the caller gets AF, BC, DE, HL as the\nfunction left them; leaves through OZCallReturn1.\nEntry: AF, BC, DE, HL = results; stack = return address, OS frame."},
        "12462": {"synopsis":"Exit of GN_Cls: drops the return address, restores IY and the S2 binding from the frame,\nreturns the function's AF (the classification flags) and the frame's BC, DE, HL; leaves\nthrough OZCallReturn0.\nEntry: AF = result; stack = return address, OS frame."},
        "12479": {"synopsis":"!! inline this for speed"},
        "12480": {"synopsis":"Binds bank A into segment 2: updates the soft copy BLSC_SR2 and the port BL_SR2. BindS2_C,\nplaced before it, binds bank C.\nEntry: A = bank.\nChanges: none."},
        "12486": {"synopsis":"AF....../.... af....\nEntry: HL=user space address.\nExit: A=byte."},
        "12488": {"comment":"S0 or S1? just read byte"},
        "12490": {"comment":"remember old S2 binding"},
        "12494": {"comment":"select saved S2 or S3"},
        "12508": {"comment":"S2 fix"},
        "12512": {"comment":"read byte"},
        "12514": {"comment":"restore S2 binding"},
        "12522": {"synopsis":"AF....../.... af....\nEntry: A=byte, DE=user space address."},
        "12524": {"comment":"S0 or S1? just write byte"},
        "12526": {"comment":"remember old S2 binding"},
        "12531": {"comment":"select saved S2 or S3"},
        "12545": {"comment":"S2 fix"},
        "12550": {"comment":"write byte"},
        "12553": {"comment":"restore S2 binding"},
        "12561": {"synopsis":"!! faster: DEBC = DEBC<<6 - DBC<<2"},
        "12572": {"comment":"HLIX += DEBC"},
        "12576": {"comment":"DEBC *= 2"},
        "12585": {"comment":"result: HLIX = 15*DEBC"},
        "12587": {"comment":"DEBC = HLIX"},
        "12591": {"comment":"*4"},
        "12593": {"comment":"DEBC *= 2"},
        "12608": {"synopsis":"Returns a 3-byte value ABC to the GN caller: when the caller's D is 0 it goes into the\nframe's A, B, C (PutOsf_ABC); otherwise C, B and A are written at the caller's DE with\nWriteOsfDE, which advances the frame's DE. Only the last write's result is kept.\nEntry: ABC = value; IY = OS frame.\nExit: flags of the last WriteOsfDE, or as PutOsf_ABC left them.\nChanges: F."},
        "12613": {"comment":"D=0, return in registers"},
        "12634": {"synopsis":"Reads the next byte of the GN caller's source given by the frame's HL (ReadHL) and stores\nthe advanced HL back in the frame.\nEntry: IY = OS frame; IX = handle or filter when the frame's HL is 0 or 1.\nExit: A = byte; Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Eof at the end).\nChanges: AF."},
        "12646": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte from a GN source: HL = 0 reads the file or device IX (OS_Gb), HL = 1 the filter\nIX (GN_Flr); any other HL reads the caller's memory (Ld_A_HL, using the caller's S2/S3\nbindings) and advances HL.\nEntry: HL = source; IX = handle or filter; IY = OS frame.\nExit: A = byte; Fc = 0; HL + 1 for memory.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Gb or GN_Flr.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "12648": {"comment":"HL=0? handle IX"},
        "12653": {"comment":"HL=1? filter IX"},
        "12656": {"comment":"else read memory"},
        "12662": {"comment":"read from file/device"},
        "12665": {"comment":"read from filter"},
        "12670": {"synopsis":"Writes A to the GN caller's destination given by the frame's DE (WriteDE) and stores the\nadvanced DE back in the frame.\nEntry: A = byte; IY = OS frame; IX = handle or filter when the frame's DE is 0 or 1.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: F."},
        "12682": {"synopsis":"Writes a byte to a GN destination: DE = 0 writes to the file or device IX (OS_Pb), DE = 1 to\nthe filter IX (GN_Flw), DE = 3 discards it; any other DE writes to the caller's memory\n(Ld_DE_A, using the caller's S2/S3 bindings) and advances DE.\nEntry: A = byte; DE = destination; IX = handle or filter; IY = OS frame.\nExit: Fc = 0; DE + 1 for memory.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Pb or GN_Flw.\nChanges: F, DE."},
        "12685": {"comment":"DE=0? handle IX"},
        "12690": {"comment":"DE=1? filter IX"},
        "12701": {"comment":"DE=3? nop"},
        "12704": {"comment":"write to memory"},
        "12711": {"comment":"write to file/device"},
        "12715": {"comment":"write to filter"},
        "12721": {"synopsis":"Puts a byte back into the GN caller's source given by the frame's HL: for memory (H <> 0)\nthe frame's HL is decremented; HL = 0 calls OS_Ugb on handle IX (marked in the source as not\nimplemented); 0 < HL < 256 pushes A back into filter IX with GN_Fpb.\nEntry: A = byte; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: F."},
        "12728": {"comment":"memory - decrement HL"},
        "12749": {"comment":"unget to file/device"},
        "12750": {"comment":"!! not implemented"},
        "12753": {"comment":"0<HL<256, push filter"},
        "12758": {"synopsis":"BHLcde/CDE -> hlBHL=quotient, CDE=remainder"},
        "12767": {"comment":"AHL=0"},
