        "12775": {"comment":"AHLBhlcde << 1"},
        "12785": {"comment":"main"},
        "12796": {"comment":"AHL-CDE(in)"},
        "12799": {"comment":"AHL>=CDE(in)? Fc=1, AHL -= CDE(in)"},
        "12802": {"comment":"else Fc=0"},
        "12807": {"comment":"fix stack"},
        "12811": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12814": {"comment":"cde<<1"},
        "12820": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12823": {"comment":"main"},
        "12824": {"comment":"B=c"},
        "12825": {"comment":"DE=HL"},
        "12826": {"comment":"main"},
        "12827": {"comment":"C=A"},
        "12828": {"comment":"HL=de"},
        "12829": {"comment":"hlBHL=hlcde CDE=AHL (remainder)"},
        "12831": {"synopsis":"CDE*BHL -> hlBHL=product"},
        "12834": {"comment":"DE=HL"},
        "12835": {"comment":"AHL=0"},
        "12838": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12840": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12841": {"comment":"adeIX=CDE(in)"},
        "12846": {"comment":"hl'=0"},
        "12851": {"comment":"b'"},
        "12853": {"comment":"adeIX << 1"},
        "12861": {"comment":"main"},
        "12864": {"comment":"main"},
        "12865": {"comment":"hlAHL+=BHL(in)"},
        "12869": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12871": {"comment":"main"},
        "12872": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12873": {"comment":"main"},
        "12874": {"comment":"hlAHL << 1"},
        "12876": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12879": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12882": {"comment":"main"},
        "12883": {"comment":"a7"},
        "12886": {"comment":"main"},
        "12887": {"comment":"hlAHL += BHL(in)"},
        "12891": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12893": {"comment":"main"},
        "12894": {"comment":"alt"},
        "12895": {"comment":"main"},
        "12896": {"comment":"hlBHL"},
        "12900": {"synopsis":"Marks the GN call as failed: stores A in the frame's A and sets Fc in the frame's F, so the\ncaller gets Fc = 1 and A = the error code.\nEntry: A = error code; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: none."},
        "12908": {"synopsis":"Loads BHL from the OS frame (the caller's B, H, L); continues in GetOsf_HL.\nEntry: IY = OS frame.\nExit: BHL = caller's BHL.\nChanges: B, HL."},
        "12911": {"synopsis":"Loads HL from the OS frame (the caller's HL).\nEntry: IY = OS frame.\nExit: HL = caller's HL.\nChanges: HL."},
        "12918": {"synopsis":"Loads BC from the OS frame (the caller's BC).\nEntry: IY = OS frame.\nExit: BC = caller's BC.\nChanges: BC."},
        "12925": {"synopsis":"Loads DE from the OS frame (the caller's DE).\nEntry: IY = OS frame.\nExit: DE = caller's DE.\nChanges: DE."},
        "12932": {"synopsis":"Stores DE in the OS frame, returned to the caller as DE.\nEntry: DE = value; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: none."},
        "12939": {"synopsis":"Stores BHL in the OS frame, returned to the caller as BHL; continues in PutOsf_HL.\nEntry: BHL = value; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: none."},
        "12942": {"synopsis":"Stores HL in the OS frame, returned to the caller as HL.\nEntry: HL = value; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: none."},
        "12949": {"synopsis":"Stores A, B and C in the OS frame, returned to the caller; continues in PutOsf_BC.\nEntry: ABC = value; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: none."},
        "12952": {"synopsis":"Stores BC in the OS frame, returned to the caller as BC.\nEntry: BC = value; IY = OS frame.\nChanges: none."},
        "12959": {"synopsis":"Standard window create with banner and bottom line.\nCursor and vertical scrolling is enabled when window is created.\n\nWindow Defintion Block offsets:\n0:  A = window ID (bits 0-3). The ID is in range 1-8\nbit 7=1, 6=1: Draw left & right bars, shelf brackets, banner text, bottom line\nbit 7=1, 6=0: Draw left & right bars, shelf brackets, banner text\nbit 7=0, 6=1: Draw left & right bars\nbit 7=0, 6=0: Just create window space (no visible borders)\nbit 5=1: 8 pixel inverted top banner (only evaluated with bit 7=1)\nbit 5=0: 7 pixel inverted top banner (only evaluated with bit 7=1)\nbit 4=1: For all windows: grey screen, then draw window to get a pop-up effect.\n1:  X coordinate (upper left corner) of Window\n2:  Y coordinate (upper left corner) of Window\n3:  WIDTH of Window (inclusive banner & bottom line)\n4:  HEIGHT of Window (inclusive banner & bottom line)\n5:  low byte, high byte address of window banner text\nOnly specified if bit 7 of window ID is enabled.\nSet pointer to 0, if using a dynamic banner (window with different banner each time)\n\nExample (Extended window \"2\" with 8 pixel banner and bottom line):\ndefb @11100000 | 2\nDEFW $0000\nDEFW $0811\nDEFW bannerptr\n\nRegister status on return:\n\nA.BCDEHL/IXIY  same\n.F....../....  different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, 1995-2008\nEntry: DE = (optional) \"dynamic\" pointer to banner (if banner pointer in definition block is\n0); BHL = pointer to 7 byte window definition block (if B=0, then local pointer).\nExit: None."},
        "12961": {"comment":"preserve old binding"},
        "12967": {"comment":"get Window ID"},
        "12970": {"comment":"X"},
        "12973": {"comment":"Y"},
        "12976": {"comment":"W"},
        "12979": {"comment":"H"},
        "12982": {"comment":"init base window \"1\""},
        "13004": {"comment":"grey entire screen (but not left side MTH menu window)"},
        "13011": {"comment":"create extended window (bars, banner, bottom line)"},
        "13020": {"comment":"create standard window without bars (bit 7=0,6=0)"},
        "13027": {"comment":"create standard window with bars"},
        "13031": {"comment":"clear window and enable cursor."},
        "13046": {"comment":"VDU cursor position (x and y sent below..)"},
        "13053": {"comment":"X position stored..."},
        "13057": {"comment":"y+height-1 (for bottom line)"},
        "13063": {"comment":"first display bottom left corner"},
        "13071": {"comment":"draw bottom line"},
        "13076": {"comment":"of width E"},
        "13081": {"comment":"finish with bottom right corner"},
        "13088": {"comment":"now create window"},
        "13095": {"comment":"window ID"},
        "13097": {"comment":"window adjusted to bottom line"},
        "13101": {"comment":"at x,    (absolute coords)"},
        "13106": {"comment":"y        (rel. to base window)"},
        "13109": {"comment":"width+32"},
        "13112": {"comment":"width    (rel. to base window)"},
        "13117": {"comment":"height+32"},
        "13124": {"comment":"adjust when a bottom line has been drawn... heigth - 1 (excl. bottom line)"},
        "13128": {"comment":"bars, shelf brackets ON"},
        "13143": {"comment":"8 pixel banner: just set tiny font in reverse"},
        "13153": {"comment":"7 pixel banner: set underline & tiny font in reverse"},
        "13162": {"comment":"centre text"},
        "13166": {"comment":"set cursor at (0,0) in window"},
        "13172": {"comment":"get banner pointer in HL"},
        "13175": {"comment":"write banner at top line of window"},
        "13180": {"comment":"apply attributes for banner width"},
        "13190": {"comment":"of window width, then apply to window banner"},
        "13194": {"comment":"now re-create window within window"},
        "13201": {"comment":"with id in A"},
        "13206": {"comment":"at x,"},
        "13211": {"comment":"y+1"},
        "13214": {"comment":"width"},
        "13217": {"comment":"heigth - 1 (excl. banner)"},
        "13225": {"comment":"heigth - 2 (excl. banner & bottom line)"},
        "13229": {"comment":"no bars, no shelf brackets"},
        "13231": {"comment":"window created, no cursor, no v. scrolling"},
        "13235": {"comment":"Enable cursor and vertical scrolling"},
        "13241": {"comment":"finished, return to caller"},
        "13244": {"synopsis":"Standard window dimensions (x,y,w,h)"},
        "13250": {"comment":"mask out type bits and convert to Ascii Window ID"},
        "13253": {"comment":"VDU 1,\"7#\",<ID>"},
        "13258": {"comment":"X position"},
        "13263": {"comment":"Y position"},
        "13268": {"comment":"width"},
        "13273": {"comment":"height"},
        "13276": {"synopsis":"Get banner pointer, using either static pointer from window definition\nblock or the dynamic DE(in) (if banner ptr is 0), then adjust it to\nOS_Bix segment, if needed."},
        "13289": {"comment":"HL = 0 in window definition block, use DE as dynamic banner"},
        "13297": {"comment":"pointer is in segment 0, OK!"},
        "13300": {"comment":"pointer in segment 1, OK!"},
        "13301": {"comment":"pointer in segment 2 or 3, define for segment 1"},
        "13305": {"comment":"banner and definition block are located in same bank"},
        "13306": {"comment":"mask segment specifier of OS_Bix for banner pointer"},
        "13308": {"synopsis":"convert integer to"},
        "13311": {"comment":"mask out window type bits..."},
        "13313": {"comment":"adjust for Ascii \"0\" - \"9\""},
        "13316": {"synopsis":"clear window (of specified ID in window definition block)"},
        "13318": {"comment":"clear window and enable cursor."},
        "13322": {"comment":"mask out type bits and convert to Ascii Window ID"},
        "13325": {"comment":"window ID to reset."},
        "13328": {"synopsis":"GN_Crc: calculates a CRC-32. A selects the source: 0 (CRC_MEMA) a local memory area, 1\n(CRC_FILE) an open RAM file from its pointer to the end, 2 (CRC_PARTFILEBYTE) part of a file\nbyte by byte, 3 (CRC_PARTFILEBUF) part of a file through a buffer, 4 (CRC_EPFILE) a file\ncard file entry, 5 (CRC_PARTEPFILE) part of a file entry.\nEntry: A = reason; for 0, 1, 3: HL = buffer, BC = its size, DE = 0 or pointer to the initial\nCRC; IX = file handle for 1-3; 2: HL = bytes to read (-1 = all), DEBC = initial CRC; 4: BHL\n= file entry, DE as above; 5: BHL = file entry or 0, DE = block size, IX = 12-byte state\nblock.\nExit: Fc = 0; DEBC = CRC-32 (complemented when complete).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Bad (bad reason or argument), RC_Eof (partial scan finished, final CRC\nreturned), or the file or file area error."},
        "13329": {"comment":"CRC_MEMA"},
        "13332": {"comment":"CRC_FILE"},
        "13335": {"comment":"CRC_PARTFILEBYTE"},
        "13338": {"comment":"CRC_PARTFILEBUF"},
        "13342": {"comment":"CRC_EPFILE"},
        "13346": {"comment":"CRC_PARTEPFILE"},
        "13349": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: crc_bad_arguments."},
        "13351": {"comment":"One or more bad arguments, return A = RC_BAD, Fc = 1"},
        "13354": {"synopsis":"Check that HL = pointer to (local) buffer is not 0\nCheck that BC = size of buffer is not 0"},
        "13356": {"comment":"HL must point to a local buffer"},
        "13360": {"comment":"size of buffer = 0!"},
        "13363": {"synopsis":"Perform CRC-32 of specified memory area and returned checksum in DEBC.\nMemory should not cross bank boundaries.\n\nExample:\nThe string \"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog\" returns 0x414FA339\n(DE = 0x414F, BC = 0xA339)\nEntry: A = 0, Iterate CRC-32 over local memory area; HL = pointer to buffer (local memory),;\nBC = memory area size; DE = 0, Initialize CRC-32 with FFFFFFFFh; DE > 0, (local) pointer to\ninitial 4-byte CRC-32 (litte endian format).\nExit: DEBC = CRC-32.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "13366": {"comment":"one of the buffer args were 0, signal Bad args & return"},
        "13367": {"comment":"initialize D'E'B'C', based on DE (input)"},
        "13371": {"comment":"ensure HL pointer is accessible in s0, s1 or s2"},
        "13374": {"comment":"size of memory area to CRC-32 scan"},
        "13375": {"comment":"remember old S1S2 bindings"},
        "13379": {"comment":"D'E'B'C' -> DEBC to caller"},
        "13382": {"comment":"restore S1 + S2 bindings"},
        "13386": {"synopsis":"Perform a CRC-32 of RAM file, already opened by caller, from current file pointer until EOF.\nIf the complete file is to be CRC'ed then it is vital that the current file pointer\nis at the beginning of the file (use FA_PTR / OS_FWM to reset file pointer) before\nexecuting this routine.\n\nThis routine utilizes OS_Mv to read from file.\nEntry: A = CRC_FILE, Iterate CRC-32 of open file (from current file pointer until EOF); HL =\npointer to file buffer (local memory),; BC = buffer size; DE = 0, Initialize CRC-32 with\nFFFFFFFFh; DE > 0, (local) pointer to initial 4-byte CRC-32; IX = file handle of open file\n(using GN_Opf).\nExit: Fc = 0,; DEBC = CRC-32; Fc = 1,; A = RC_xxx (file & handle related errors).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "13390": {"comment":"bad IX file handle"},
        "13396": {"comment":"one of the buffer args were 0, signal Bad args & return"},
        "13397": {"comment":"initialise CRC registers D'E'B'C' according to input"},
        "13401": {"comment":"ensure HL pointer is accessible in s0, s1 or s2"},
        "13404": {"comment":"size of memory area to CRC-32 scan"},
        "13405": {"comment":"remember old S1S2 bindings"},
        "13406": {"comment":"DE points to intermediate file buffer in s0, s1 or s2"},
        "13410": {"comment":"EOF reached, get current CRC in D'E'B'C' and complement it then return as DEBC to caller"},
        "13413": {"comment":"restore S1 + S2 bindings"},
        "13417": {"synopsis":"Runs Scanbuffer until an error or the end of the file, accumulating the CRC of an open RAM\nfile for GN_Crc's CRC_FILE.\nEntry: DE = buffer; BC = its size; IX = file handle; D'E'B'C' = CRC so far.\nExit: Fz = 1 at the end of the file; D'E'B'C' = CRC.\nError: Fc = 1, A = file error (already stored in the frame)."},
        "13420": {"comment":"RC_xxx error occurred"},
        "13421": {"comment":"EOF reached"},
        "13424": {"synopsis":"Perform a partial CRC-32 of RAM file, already opened by caller, from current file\npointer until EOF.\nIf the complete file is to be CRC'ed then it is vital that the current file pointer\nis at the beginning of the file (use FA_PTR / OS_FWM to reset file pointer) before\nexecuting this routine.\n\nThis routine utilizes OS_Gb to read from file.\nEntry: HL = max bytes to read, or -1 for rest of file; DEBC = Initial CRC-32 (typically\nFFFFFFFFh); IX = file handle of open file (using GN_Opf).\nExit: Fc = 0,; DEBC = CRC-32; Fc = 1,; A = RC_xxx (file & handle related errors); RC_Eof is\nalways set when complete CRC scan is done.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "13428": {"comment":"bad IX file handle"},
        "13431": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: init_scanfileByteIO."},
        "13436": {"comment":"installed inital CRC-32 into D'E'B'C'"},
        "13439": {"comment":"read byte from file (and preserve alternate bc, de)"},
        "13444": {"comment":"store return API, EOF / file I/O error occurred..."},
        "13449": {"comment":"EOF reached, get current CRC in D'E'B'C', complement, and return to caller"},
        "13453": {"comment":"calculate CRC-32 from A in D'E'B'C'"},
        "13464": {"comment":"HL = -1, keep reading from file until EOF"},
        "13469": {"comment":"max bytes not yet reached, continue processing"},
        "13471": {"synopsis":"Returns a partial CRC-32 to the GN_Crc caller: switches to the alternate set and stores its\nBC, DE (the running CRC, not complemented) in the frame. Ends CrcRamFileByteIO when the byte\ncount runs out. The source says Fz = 0, but cp a sets Fz = 1.\nEntry: D'E'B'C' = running CRC.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1; the alternate set is active.\nChanges: AF."},
        "13475": {"comment":"return partical CRC-32 (non-complemented!) result in D'E'B'C' to caller"},
        "13478": {"comment":"ensure Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "13480": {"synopsis":"Perform a partial CRC-32 of RAM file, already opened by caller, from current file\npointer until EOF.\nIf the complete file is to be CRC'ed then it is vital that the current file pointer\nis at the beginning of the file (use FA_PTR / OS_FWM to reset file pointer) before\nexecuting this routine.\n\nThis routine utilizes OS_Mv to buffer-read from file.\n\nOUT, if call successful:\nFc = 0\nDEBC = partial CRC-32 result (DE = high-word, BC = low-word), to be used for next scan\n\nFc = 1, A _RC_Eof\nDEBC = final CRC-32 result (DE = high-word, BC = low-word)\n\nOUT, if call failed:\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_BAD ($04) - bad argument\nA = RC_xxx (file & handle related errors)\nOZ source name: CrcRamFilePartial.\nEntry: A = CRC_PARTFILEBUF, Iterate CRC-32 of open file (from current file pointer until\nEOF); HL = pointer to file buffer (local memory),; BC = buffer size; DE = 0, Initialize\nCRC-32 with FFFFFFFFh; DE > 0, (local) pointer to initial 4-byte CRC-32; IX = file handle of\nopen file (using GN_Opf).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL, IX, IY."},
        "13484": {"comment":"bad IX file handle"},
        "13490": {"comment":"one of the buffer args were 0, signal Bad args & return"},
        "13491": {"comment":"initialise CRC registers D'E'B'C' according to input"},
        "13495": {"comment":"ensure HL pointer is accessible in s0, s1 or s2"},
        "13498": {"comment":"size of memory area to CRC-32 scan"},
        "13499": {"comment":"remember old S1S2 bindings"},
        "13500": {"comment":"DE points to intermediate file buffer in s0, s1 or s2"},
        "13504": {"comment":"EOF reached, get current CRC in D'E'B'C' and complement it then return as DEBC to caller"},
        "13509": {"comment":"indicate Fc = 1 & EOF to caller if"},
        "13512": {"comment":"block has been fetched, return current partial CRC in D'E'B'C'"},
        "13515": {"comment":"restore S1 + S2 bindings"},
        "13519": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format.\n\nGenerate CRC-32 of file entry in file area.\n\nDesign & Programming by Gunther Strube, June 2012. GN_Crc adpation 2014\nEntry: BHL = pointer to file entry to be CRC-32 scanned; DE = 0, Initialize CRC-32 with\nFFFFFFFFh; DE > 0, (local) pointer to initial 4-byte CRC-32 (litte endian format).\nExit: Fc = 0,; DEBC = CRC-32; Fc = 1,; File Entry at BHL was not found.; A = RC_Onf.\nChanges: AFBCDEHL/.. afbcdehl different.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "13524": {"comment":"File entry not recognised, exit with error..."},
        "13532": {"comment":"bind in bank at c = safe ms_s1 segment"},
        "13533": {"comment":"preserve original S1 binding for exit"},
        "13537": {"comment":"adjust BHL pointer to first byte of file image (beyond file entry header)"},
        "13542": {"comment":"BHL pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "13545": {"comment":"get caller DE"},
        "13548": {"comment":"initialize D'E'B'C', based on DE"},
        "13552": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: crc32_feentry_loop.","comment":"File Entry size in CDE = 0?"},
        "13555": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "13558": {"comment":"calculate CRC-32 result in D'E'B'C'"},
        "13561": {"comment":"BHL++"},
        "13564": {"comment":"CDE--"},
        "13569": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: return_final_crc32."},
        "13570": {"comment":"restore caller bank binding"},
        "13571": {"comment":"complete the final CRC-32 result in DEBC to caller"},
        "13574": {"synopsis":"Standard Z88 File Eprom Format.\n\nPartly generate CRC-32 of File Entry in file area.\n\nSubsequent calls:\nBHL = 0\nIX = pointer to updated local memory of CRC-32 variables (12 bytes):\n\nFc = 1\nBHL = 0 (always)\nA = RC_Eof (complete file scanned)\n(IX + 0,3)   : final CRC-32 result, low-byte, high-byte order;\n\nFc = 1\nA = RC_xxx (System error occurred - file entry corrupt, not found, etc.)\n\nIX variable offsets:\nOZ source name: FileEprFilePartCrc32.\nEntry: Initial call:; BHL = pointer to File Entry; DE = max. size of bytes to read per\npartial scan; IX = pointer to local memory (allocated in application/popdown workspace, 12\nbytes):; (IX + 0,3) : Initial CRC-32 or input from result of previous partial CRC-32 scan;\n(IX + 4,6) : Reserved for 24bit file pointer (initialized after first call); (IX + 7,9) :\nReserved for size of file entry (initialized after first call); (IX + 10,11) : Reserved for\nmax. bytes to read per partial scan.\nExit: Fc = 0; BHL = 0 (always); (IX + 0,3) : partial CRC-32 result, low-byte, high-byte\norder; (IX + 4,6) : 24bit file pointer updated for next partial scan; (IX + 7,9) : Remaining\nfile size updated for next partial scan; (IX + 10,11) : Updated max. bytes to read per\npartial scan.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "13581": {"comment":"IX must point to a File Entry information block, not 0!"},
        "13587": {"comment":"BHL <> 0, subsequent block to be scanned?"},
        "13596": {"comment":"current file pointer to file image data"},
        "13609": {"comment":"install partial CRC-32 from previous run"},
        "13618": {"comment":"preserve max bytes to read for subsequent calls"},
        "13623": {"comment":"get size of File entry in CDE"},
        "13626": {"comment":"File entry not recognised, exit with error..."},
        "13634": {"comment":"adjust BHL pointer to first byte of file image (beyond file entry header)"},
        "13640": {"comment":"first block scan, initialize D'E'B'C' to FFFFFFFFh"},
        "13647": {"comment":"BHL pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "13650": {"comment":"bind in bank at c = safe ms_s1 segment"},
        "13651": {"comment":"preserve original S1 binding for exit"},
        "13652": {"comment":"BHL points at first byte of file image block"},
        "13659": {"comment":"intialize file entry size for block loop scan"},
        "13666": {"comment":"hl' = max bytes (block) to read"},
        "13670": {"comment":"File Entry size in CDE = 0?"},
        "13673": {"comment":"Yes, complete the final CRC-32 result in D'E'B'C' to caller"},
        "13680": {"comment":"max bytes scanned of block, return partial CRC-32"},
        "13683": {"comment":"calculate CRC-32 result in D'E'B'C'"},
        "13686": {"comment":"BHL++"},
        "13689": {"comment":"CDE--"},
        "13694": {"comment":"blocksize--"},
        "13698": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: fe_partial_scan_block."},
        "13702": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: fe_partial_scan_eof."},
        "13704": {"comment":"indicate Fc = 1 & EOF to caller when complete file has been scanned"},
        "13719": {"comment":"update CRC-32 into runtime variable area fro caller"},
        "13723": {"comment":"preserve updated remaining file size in (IX + flentry_size)"},
        "13726": {"comment":"preserve updated File pointer in (IX + flentry_fptr)"},
        "13733": {"comment":"always return BHL = 0 to caller"},
        "13737": {"comment":"restore original bank binding (application level)"},
        "13740": {"synopsis":"Load contents of file (from current file pointer) into buffer and CRC-32 iterate\nthe buffer.\n\nReturns:\nFc = 1, A = RC_xxx error (file I/O error)\nFz = 1, if EOF has been reached\nD'E'B'C' contains updated CRC-32 checksum\nEntry: DE = pointer to buffer; BC = size of buffer.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY, /af...... same, AF, /..bcdehl different."},
        "13746": {"comment":"read bytes from file (and preserve alternate bc, de)"},
        "13754": {"comment":"file I/O error occurred..."},
        "13759": {"comment":"EOF reached, no bytes read..."},
        "13762": {"comment":"BC=#bytes actually read"},
        "13765": {"comment":"accumulate CRC on current value in D'E'B'C'"},
        "13772": {"comment":"Fz = 0, buffer fetched succesfully, not EOF"},
        "13777": {"comment":"Fc = 1, Fz = 0, file I/O error occurred..."},
        "13782": {"comment":"signal EOF"},
        "13784": {"synopsis":"Call OS_Gb and preserve current CRC-32 in in D'E'B'C'"},
        "13795": {"synopsis":"Call OS_Mv and preserve current CRC-32 in in D'E'B'C'"},
        "13806": {"synopsis":"Sets up the running CRC in D'E'B'C' for GN_Crc: $FFFFFFFF when DE = 0, otherwise the four\nbytes (low first) at the caller's address DE (Ld_A_HL). Also copies it to the frame's BC and\nDE.\nEntry: DE = 0 or pointer to the initial CRC; IY = OS frame.\nExit: D'E'B'C' = CRC; main set active.\nChanges: AF, BC', DE', HL'."},
        "13808": {"comment":"DE > 0, read CRC-32 from (DE)"},
        "13811": {"comment":"initialise CRC register D'E'B'C' to FFFFFFFFh"},
        "13816": {"synopsis":"Entry inside InitCrc: with the alternate set active holding the CRC in DEBC, stores it in\nthe frame's BC and DE and switches back with exx.\nEntry: alternate set active; DEBC = CRC; IY = OS frame.\nExit: main set active."},
        "13819": {"comment":"also preserve a copy to GN return registers"},
        "13826": {"comment":"initialise CRC register D'E'B'C' from (HL)"},
        "13848": {"synopsis":"Iterate current CRC-32 with memory area in HL (available in s0, s1 or s2), size BC\nEntry: HL = pointer to start of memory area; BC = size of memory area; D'E'B'C' = current\nCRC-32.\nExit: BC = 0; HL = end of memory area + 1; D'E'B'C' = updated.\nChanges: DE, ../IXIY same, AF, BC, HL, IX, IY, hl/.... different.","comment":"get byte from memory area"},
        "13850": {"comment":"calculate CRC-32"},
        "13856": {"comment":"back for more"},
        "13859": {"synopsis":"Iterate current CRC-32 with byte value in A\nEntry: A = byte to iterate CRC-32; D'E'B'C' = current CRC-32.\nExit: D'E'B'C' = updated.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, ../IXIY same, AF, IX, IY, hl/.... different."},
        "13868": {"comment":"AL=4xCRC index byte"},
        "13871": {"comment":"HL=index into CRC table"},
        "13875": {"comment":"shift and XOR 2nd byte to low"},
        "13879": {"comment":"shift and XOR 3rd byte to 2nd"},
        "13883": {"comment":"shift and XOR high byte to 3rd"},
        "13884": {"comment":"get new high byte"},
        "13887": {"synopsis":"Returns the final CRC-32 to the GN_Crc caller: switches to the alternate set, complements\nits DEBC and stores it in the frame's BC and DE.\nEntry: D'E'B'C' = running CRC; IY = OS frame.\nExit: DEBC = final CRC (the alternate set is now active); Fc = 0, Fz = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "13890": {"comment":"complement high byte"},
        "13893": {"comment":"complement 3rd byte"},
        "13896": {"comment":"complement 2nd byte"},
        "13899": {"comment":"complement low byte"},
        "13903": {"comment":"return DEBC to caller"},
        "13906": {"comment":"ensure Fc = 0, Fz = 1"},
        "13908": {"synopsis":"Stores the remaining file entry size CDE at IX+7..9 (flentry_size) of GN_Crc's partial scan\nblock.\nEntry: CDE = size; IX = state block.\nChanges: none."},
        "13914": {"comment":"preserve file entry size for next partial call"},
        "13918": {"synopsis":"Stores the file entry pointer BHL at IX+4..6 (flentry_fptr) of GN_Crc's partial scan block,\nwith the segment bits of H cleared.\nEntry: BHL = pointer; IX = state block.\nChanges: H."},
        "13920": {"comment":"preserve offset without segment mask"},
        "13928": {"comment":"preserce BHL for next partial call"},
        "13932": {"synopsis":"BHL++ (and bank crossing bound automatically)","comment":"remember original A14-A15"},
        "13934": {"comment":"get changed bits in A14-A15"},
        "13938": {"comment":"offset has crossed bank boundary"},
        "13939": {"comment":"change A14-A15 back"},
        "13944": {"comment":"page in new bank in segment 1,"},
        "13945": {"comment":"HL point to beginning of new bank (in S1)"},
        "13947": {"synopsis":"CDE = 0?","comment":"file size = 0?"},
        "13949": {"comment":"file size not yet 0"},
        "13952": {"comment":"Fz = 1, File entry was successfully CRC-32 scanned (CDE = 0)!"},
        "13953": {"synopsis":"CDE--"}
      }
    },
