      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"enum _Diary_","comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "5": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "9": {"comment":"suicide, when a ROM is older"},
        "10": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "20": {"comment":"use segment 2 for memory pool access"},
        "25": {"comment":"allocate memory pool, A=mask"},
        "35": {"comment":"3*79"},
        "38": {"comment":"Allocate memory"},
        "54": {"comment":"Allocate memory"},
        "70": {"comment":"Allocate memory"},
        "84": {"comment":"bind it in S2"},
        "85": {"comment":"S1, multiple banks"},
        "90": {"comment":"allocate memory pool, A=mask"},
        "103": {"comment":"b00 into S1"},
        "106": {"comment":"Bind bank B in slot C"},
        "139": {"comment":"Set (install) Error Handler"},
        "188": {"comment":"insert/overwrite"},
        "193": {"comment":"enquire (fetch) parameter"},
        "224": {"comment":"No room"},
        "229": {"synopsis":"Fills B bytes from HL with zero.\nEntry: HL = start; B = count (0 = 256).\nExit: HL = first byte after the block; A = 0; B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "296": {"synopsis":"The Diary's main editing loop. It enables ESC detection, shows the end-of-text marker and\nedits the current line in the input buffer with GN_Sip (77 columns, overwrite and reverse\nvideo as the mode and the block require), then acts on how GN_Sip ended:\n1. RC_Draw and RC_Susp: the line is stored, the mail date is checked and the window is\nredrawn; RC_Wrap goes to DoWrap; RC_Esc is acknowledged; RC_Quit quits.\n2. <>V toggles insert/overwrite; ENTER moves to the start of the next line.\n3. A command code $20-$40 is checked with CheckMemory (CmdFlags_tbl) and dispatched through\nCommands_tbl; other codes are ignored. Command $3E (Next Option) is this label itself.\nEntry: IX = state block; the current line is in the input buffer.\nExit: never returns; every command handler jumps back here."},
        "298": {"comment":"Enable ESC detection"},
        "311": {"comment":"return wrap,  special, insert/overwrite, forcei/o, has data"},
        "319": {"comment":"overwrite"},
        "326": {"comment":"reverse"},
        "328": {"comment":"buffer length (width of main window - 1)"},
        "336": {"comment":"system input line routine"},
        "366": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "370": {"comment":"Suspicion of  pre-emption"},
        "374": {"comment":"Wrap  condition met"},
        "379": {"comment":"Escape condition (e.g. ESC pressed)"},
        "383": {"comment":"SC_ACK, Examine special condition"},
        "387": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "394": {"comment":"Display an interactive error  box"},
        "429": {"comment":"Application exit"},
        "431": {"synopsis":"Closes the memory pool whose handle is in IX with OS_Mcl, unless the handle is 0.\nEntry: IX = memory pool handle (0 = none).\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "437": {"comment":"Close memory (free memory pool)"},
        "534": {"comment":"lbuf_InputBuffer+77"},
        "554": {"comment":"lbuf_InputBuffer+77"},
        "562": {"comment":"no spaces, cut at 77"},
        "564": {"comment":"change space into NULL"},
        "567": {"comment":"and move HL to next char"},
        "572": {"comment":"#chars to move to next line"},
        "584": {"comment":"no chars to move? done"},
        "586": {"comment":"copy  chars"},
        "598": {"comment":"DE=buf2"},
        "599": {"comment":"lbuf_InputBuffer+77"},
        "603": {"comment":"copy  one char"},
        "605": {"comment":"and NULL it"},
        "608": {"comment":"xpos<77? xpos++"},
        "618": {"comment":"NULL-terminate buf2"},
        "661": {"comment":"strlen()"},
        "684": {"comment":"<>V,  insert/overwrite"},
        "715": {"comment":"move to next line"},
        "751": {"synopsis":"Table of 33 words: the handler of each Diary command code $20-$40, from MarkBlock ($20) to\nSave ($40); the index is the code minus $20. NextOption reads it after CheckMemory."},
        "759": {"comment":"24"},
        "767": {"comment":"28"},
        "775": {"comment":"2C"},
        "783": {"comment":"30"},
        "791": {"comment":"34"},
        "799": {"comment":"38"},
        "807": {"comment":"3C"},
        "815": {"comment":"40"},
        "817": {"synopsis":"Table of 39 bytes, one per value of dix_ubCommand: $00-$20 for the commands $20-$40, then\n$22 line wrap, $23 ENTER, $24 insert/overwrite, $25 start-up and $26 resume after\npre-emption. CheckMemory reads the byte to know what it must be able to allocate before the\ncommand runs: bit 0 room to store the input line, bits 1 and 2 one 83-byte block each."},
        "856": {"synopsis":"Cursor Up command ($2E). When the current line has a previous line, it stores the input\nbuffer in the current line, moves to the previous line and moves the cursor up a row, or\nscrolls the window down and makes it the top line when the cursor is on the top row.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "872": {"comment":"ypos=0? need  scrolling"},
        "890": {"comment":"!! move this  to caller (enter handling)"},
        "896": {"synopsis":"Cursor Down command ($2D). When the current line has a next line, it stores the input\nbuffer, moves to the next line and moves the cursor down a row (clearing the row when the\nnew position is past the last line), or scrolls the window up and advances the top line when\nthe cursor is on the bottom row (row 7). ENTER and DoWrap enter at cdn_1, without the\nnext-line test.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "913": {"comment":"ypos=7? need  scrolling"},
        "976": {"synopsis":"Delete Line command ($3A). Stores the input buffer, removes the current line from the day's\nlist and frees it (FreeCurrentLine), deactivates any block marker or saved position on it\n(MayInactBlkSaved) and fixes the top line. The line after it becomes current; when there is\nnone, the cursor moves up a line. Then the window is redrawn.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1039": {"synopsis":"Join Lines command ($3B). Appends the next line to the current line as far as it fits in 77\ncolumns, breaking at the last space that fits. When all of the next line was taken (or it\nwas empty) the next line is deleted; otherwise its remainder stays as the next line. The\ncurrent line and the lines below it are reprinted.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1045": {"comment":"no next line? exit"},
        "1057": {"comment":"no next line? exit"},
        "1066": {"comment":"copy  next to Buf2"},
        "1083": {"comment":"next  not empty?"},
        "1104": {"comment":"#bytes left in buffer"},
        "1107": {"comment":"no next line? exit"},
        "1110": {"comment":"ptr to end(this)"},
        "1120": {"comment":"DE=split position"},
        "1130": {"comment":"remember breaking point"},
        "1144": {"comment":"bytes to append"},
        "1170": {"comment":"joined full line?"},
        "1174": {"comment":"joined full line?"},
        "1212": {"synopsis":"Insert Line command ($3C). Stores the input buffer and inserts a new empty line (a 4-byte\nnode) before the current line; the new line becomes current, and the top line when the old\nline was the top line. The lines from the cursor down are reprinted. When the node cannot be\nallocated the command does nothing.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1235": {"comment":"length=0"},
        "1248": {"synopsis":"Split Line command ($3D). Moves the text from the cursor to the end of the line onto a new\nline inserted after the current one, cuts the current line at the cursor and reprints the\nlines from the cursor down; the cursor stays on the first part.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1256": {"comment":"DE=buf2"},
        "1260": {"comment":"HL=buf1"},
        "1268": {"comment":"copy  rest of line from buf1 to buf2"},
        "1278": {"comment":"terminate buf1"},
        "1299": {"synopsis":"Tab command ($2A). Inserts spaces from the cursor to the next column that is a multiple of 8\nand moves the cursor there; the rest of the line follows the spaces, and the part that no\nlonger fits goes to a new line (AppendToCurrent). Nothing happens when the tab stop would be\ncolumn 78 or beyond.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1382": {"synopsis":"Save Position command ($2B). Stores the input buffer and pushes the current line and date\nonto the stack of saved positions (5 records of 7 bytes at dix_SavedStates, count in\ndix_ubNumSavedPositions) with SaveState; shows \"NO ROOM\" when all 5 are used.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1424": {"synopsis":"Restore Position command ($2C). Stores the input buffer and pops the last saved position;\nshows \"NO MARKER\" when there is none or it is no longer active. Otherwise the cursor goes to\ncolumn 0 of the saved line. On the same date only the cursor moves when the line is on\nscreen, else the window is redrawn with it in view; on another date the current date is\nremoved when empty and the saved date is shown (created when missing).\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1572": {"synopsis":"Last Line command ($2F). Stores the input buffer, scrolls the top line forward until the end\nof the day's lines is in the window and puts the cursor on the last line; redraws the window\nwhen it scrolled.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1594": {"comment":"on screen"},
        "1650": {"synopsis":"First Line command ($30). Stores the input buffer and moves to the first line of the current\ndate, cursor on the top row (sub_D969); redraws the window unless the first line already was\nthe top line.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1693": {"synopsis":"Screen Down command ($31). Stores the input buffer and moves the current line and the top\nline down by the same number of lines (at most 7, stopping at the last line), so the cursor\nstays on its row; then redraws the window.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1759": {"synopsis":"Screen Up command ($32). Stores the input buffer and moves the current line up by at most 7\nlines (stopping at the first line), and the top line up by as many as it can go; then\nredraws the window.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1830": {"synopsis":"Next Day command ($34). Stores the input buffer, removes the current date when it is empty\n(sub_D76E) and adds one day to dix_CurrentDate. A date that GN_Die rejects shows \"DATE\nRANGE\" and the old date is restored; then the date is shown, created when it has no node yet\n(loc_C0E4).\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1854": {"synopsis":"Previous Day command ($35). Stores the input buffer, removes the current date when it is\nempty (sub_D76E) and subtracts one day from dix_CurrentDate; then continues as NextDay (date\ncheck, \"DATE RANGE\", show the date).\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1900": {"synopsis":"Next Active Day command ($36). Stores the input buffer and, when there is a later date in\nthe diary, makes it current, removes the old date if it is empty (MayRemoveDate) and shows\nthe new date from its first line.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1917": {"synopsis":"Previous Active Day command ($37). Stores the input buffer and, when there is an earlier\ndate in the diary, makes it current; continues in NextActiveDay's code (remove the old date\nif empty, show the new one).\nOZ source name: PreviousActiveDay.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1956": {"synopsis":"Today command ($33). Stores the input buffer, removes the current date when it is empty,\nreads today's date into dix_CurrentDate (GN_Gmd) and shows it, creating its node when\nmissing (loc_C0E4).\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "1968": {"synopsis":"Last Active Day command ($38). Clears DF5D_B_0 to select the last date and continues in\nFirstActiveDay's code.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption.","comment":"local flag"},
        "1974": {"synopsis":"First Active Day command ($39), also the shared code of LastActiveDay (DF5D_B_0 set means\nthe first date). Stores the input buffer, removes the current date when it is empty and\nshows the first or the last date of the diary; when the diary has no dates, it shows the\ncurrent date, creating its node.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2010": {"comment":"loop until last found"},
        "2033": {"synopsis":"Mark Block command ($20). Stores the input buffer and sets a block marker on the current\nline (SaveState):\n1. No start marker: the line becomes the start.\n2. Both markers set: both are cleared and the line becomes the start.\n3. Only a start marker: when the line is before the start (an earlier date, or the same date\nand not after the start line) the old start becomes the end and the line the new start;\notherwise the line becomes the end. Then the window is redrawn.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2072": {"comment":"current < blkstart"},
        "2074": {"comment":"current > blkstart"},
        "2099": {"comment":"start -> end"},
        "2121": {"comment":"make  new start"},
        "2132": {"synopsis":"Clear Mark command ($21). Stores the input buffer, clears both block markers (InactivateBlk)\nand redraws the window.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2141": {"synopsis":"Clears the active bit of the block start and block end markers.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nChanges: none (only the two marker flags)."},
        "2150": {"synopsis":"Block Copy command ($22). Sets DF5B_B_ALLOCNEW and clears DF5B_B_FREEOLD, then continues in\nthe shared block code after Delete: every line of the block is copied after the current\nline, and the markers stay.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption.","comment":"local flag"},
        "2154": {"comment":"local flag"},
        "2160": {"synopsis":"Block Move command ($23). Sets DF5B_B_ALLOCNEW and DF5B_B_FREEOLD, then continues in the\nshared block code after Delete: every line of the block is copied after the current line and\nremoved from its place, and the markers are cleared.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption.","comment":"allocate more"},
        "2164": {"comment":"free old"},
        "2170": {"synopsis":"Block Delete command ($24), also the shared code of Copy and Move (DF5B_B_ALLOCNEW: copy\neach line, DF5B_B_FREEOLD: remove it). Stores the input buffer; shows \"NO MARKER\" when no\nstart marker is set and \"OVERLAPS\" when the cursor is inside the block. Otherwise it walks\nthe block from the start line to the end line (only the start line when there is no end\nmarker), date by date, copying each line after the current line and/or freeing it and fixing\nthe pointers that referred to it; ESC stops the walk. Move and Delete then clear the\nmarkers, and the window is redrawn with the cursor line in view.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2183": {"comment":"Enable ESC detection"},
        "2192": {"comment":"!! should be able to delete block with cursor in it"},
        "2198": {"comment":"local flag"},
        "2329": {"comment":"blkend<date2"},
        "2370": {"comment":"Acknowledge ESC key"},
        "2592": {"comment":"copy doesn't deselect block"},
        "2635": {"synopsis":"Search command ($26). Resets the options to \"ignore case\", opens the Search window (Search2)\nand reads the search string into Buffer3 with GN_Sip; '-' opens the options (SearchUI_tbl:\nignore case, search block, list, print list) with DoUI and ESC leaves. ENTER runs the search\nfrom the start of the diary or of the block (sub_CBF1): the cursor goes to the first match,\nor with the list options every matching line is listed with its date on the screen and/or\nthe printer.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2640": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "2642": {"comment":"ignore case"},
        "2662": {"comment":"width of main window - 2"},
        "2673": {"comment":"system input  line routine"},
        "2678": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "2686": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "2739": {"synopsis":"Next Match command ($27). Clears DF5C_B_MATCHBACKW and continues in PrevMatch's code at\nloc_CB00, searching forward from the column after the cursor.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2745": {"synopsis":"Previous Match command ($28), also the shared code of NextMatch. Stores the input buffer and\nchecks there is a search string (sub_D581); with the block option it needs a marker (\"NO\nMARKER\") and the cursor in the block (\"NOT MARKED\"). It searches the current line from the\ncursor, then the following (or previous) lines and dates (AdvanceSearchPos). A match moves\nthe cursor to it, changing date and redrawing when needed; otherwise \"NO MATCH\" is shown.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2950": {"synopsis":"List/Print command ($25). Opens the List window and its options (ListUI_tbl: screen,\nprinter, block) with DoUI, then lists every line of the diary or of the block, each date as\na heading, on the screen and/or the printer (sub_CBF1 with DF5C_B_SRCHRPLC clear). ESC\nleaves without listing.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "2955": {"comment":"Disable ESC detection"},
        "2957": {"comment":"DF5E_MAKESEARCHLIST"},
        "3001": {"comment":"Enable ESC detection"},
        "3069": {"comment":"bits  4 & 5, make or print search list"},
        "3115": {"comment":"Send  character directly to printer filter"},
        "3119": {"comment":"Send  character directly to printer filter"},
        "3135": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "3160": {"comment":"still same date, just print"},
        "3185": {"comment":"century, date suffix"},
        "3187": {"comment":"everything in expanded form"},
        "3189": {"comment":"convert internal date to ASCII string"},
        "3200": {"comment":"null-terminate"},
        "3210": {"comment":"print date"},
        "3238": {"comment":"Acknowledge escape"},
        "3289": {"synopsis":"Replace command ($29). Reads the search string (Buffer3) and the replacement (offset $7D of\nthe state block) with GN_Sip, with options from RplcUI_tbl (ignore case, confirm, block).\nENTER searches forward from the start of the diary or of the block; at each match it asks\n\"REPLACE Y/N\" when confirm is set, and replaces the text in the line (the part that no\nlonger fits goes to a new line, AppendToCurrent). ESC stops; the number of matches found is\nshown (ShowFoundCount) and the window is redrawn.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "3292": {"comment":"Disable escape detection."},
        "3331": {"comment":"width of main window - 2"},
        "3342": {"comment":"system input  line routine"},
        "3347": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "3355": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "3397": {"comment":"system input  line routine"},
        "3402": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "3410": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "3428": {"comment":"'.'"},
        "3454": {"comment":"Enable escape detection"},
        "3524": {"comment":"Acknowledge escap"},
        "3634": {"comment":"write a byte  to std. output"},
        "3641": {"comment":"write a byte  to std. output"},
        "3646": {"comment":"read  a byte from std. input"},
        "3656": {"comment":"Classify a character"},
        "3661": {"comment":"upper()"},
        "3665": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "3670": {"comment":"Escape condition (e.g. ESC pressed)"},
        "3674": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "3906": {"synopsis":"Shows the number in dix_uwFoundCount followed by \"FOUND\" in the message area (GN_Pdn,\nGN_Sop), marking the message as shown so RemoveError clears it.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3931": {"comment":"Integer to ASCII conversion"},
        "3939": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "3950": {"synopsis":"Appends the NUL-terminated text at HL to the current line at DE (the cursor position in the\ninput buffer). When it does not fit in the 77 columns, the part up to the last space that\nfits is appended, the line is cut there and stored, a new empty line is inserted after it\n(InsertEmptyLine) and becomes current, the rest is copied to the start of the input buffer,\nand DF5C_B_APPND_NEWLINE and DF5B_B_NEEDREDRAW are set.\nEntry: HL = text to append; DE = position in the input buffer; IX = state block.\nExit: DE = end of the copied text, not terminated (the caller writes the NUL)."},
        "3965": {"comment":"#bytes_after_cursor"},
        "3979": {"comment":"found NULL? can append"},
        "3987": {"comment":"found ' '? can append"},
        "4069": {"synopsis":"Load command ($3F). Reads the file name with GN_Sip, with the option \"start at date\"\n(LoadUI_tbl), opens the file and reads it in blocks with OS_Mv. Each text line (at most 77\ncharacters, control codes dropped, \"%%\" read as \"%\") is inserted as a line; a line that\nstarts with a single '%' is a date (GN_Gdt), whose day is found or created, shifted so that\nthe first date lands on the current date when \"start at date\" is set. Then it closes the\nfile, names the application after it and redraws the current date.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "4072": {"comment":"SC_DIS"},
        "4074": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "4100": {"comment":"width of main window - 2"},
        "4111": {"comment":"system input  line routine"},
        "4116": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "4134": {"comment":"load marked Filer name into BHL buffer"},
        "4138": {"comment":"Max size of buffer"},
        "4142": {"comment":"Read parameter data (mailbox)"},
        "4153": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "4208": {"comment":"parse filename"},
        "4222": {"comment":"open  file/stream (or device)"},
        "4230": {"comment":"Display an interactive error  box"},
        "4233": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "4238": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "4318": {"comment":"move  bytes between stream and memory"},
        "4435": {"comment":"convert ASCII string  to internal date"},
        "4655": {"comment":"move  bytes between stream and memory"},
        "4686": {"synopsis":"Save command ($40). Reads the file name with GN_Sip, with the option \"block\" (SaveUI_tbl),\nopens the file for output and writes the diary or the block: each date as a line '%' and the\ndate (GN_Pdt), then its lines, '%' doubled, every line ending with CR (SaveLn). A write\nerror is reported and the file is closed and deleted. When the whole diary was saved, the\napplication is named after the file.\nEntry: jumped to from NextOption through Commands_tbl; IX = state block.\nExit: jumps back to NextOption."},
        "4691": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "4721": {"comment":"width of main window - 2"},
        "4732": {"comment":"system input  line routine"},
        "4737": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "4745": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "4800": {"comment":"parse filename"},
        "4814": {"comment":"open  file/stream (or device)"},
        "4822": {"comment":"Display an interactive error  box"},
        "4825": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "4830": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "4926": {"comment":"convert internal date to ASCII string"},
        "4959": {"comment":"Display an interactive error  box"},
        "4975": {"comment":"delete file"},
        "5030": {"comment":"read/write filename segments"},
        "5034": {"comment":"Name  current application"},
        "5042": {"comment":"Display an interactive error  box"},
        "5068": {"synopsis":"Closes the diary file whose handle is in DiaryFileHandle (GN_Cl).\nEntry: DiaryFileHandle = open file handle.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "5074": {"comment":"close file/stream"},
        "5080": {"synopsis":"Entry: DE=line."},
        "5096": {"comment":"dest  buffer"},
        "5107": {"comment":"% -> %%"},
        "5114": {"comment":"'%'|$80 -> '%'"},
        "5141": {"comment":"move  bytes between stream and memory"},
        "5178": {"synopsis":"Exit: Fc=0, C=match offset."},
        "5197": {"comment":"max length"},
        "5203": {"comment":"no NULL found? Fc=1"},
        "5253": {"synopsis":"Loads HL with the start of the match being tried, kept in dix_68 by SearchForw and\nSearchBack.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: HL = pointer into Buffer2.\nChanges: HL."},
        "5260": {"synopsis":"Searches Buffer2 backwards for the search string in Buffer3, for a match that ends at or\nbefore column C, comparing with CmpChar. dix_uwFoundCount is used as scratch.\nEntry: C = column; IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0, C = column where the match starts.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is no match.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "5267": {"comment":"lbuf_InputBuffer+78"},
        "5277": {"comment":"lbuf_Buffer2+77"},
        "5300": {"comment":"lbuf_InputBuffer+78"},
        "5384": {"synopsis":"Points HL at column C of the string at line-buffer offset HL, or at its last character when\nthe string is shorter (one byte before its start when it is empty). SearchBack uses it to\nfind where to start in Buffer2 and the last character of the search string.\nEntry: HL = offset in the line buffers (Buffer2, Buffer3); C = column.\nExit: HL = pointer to the character.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "5401": {"comment":"found NULL"},
        "5409": {"synopsis":"Compares the character at DE with the one at HL; letters are compared in upper case when\nDF5E_B_IGNORECASE is set (GN_Cls).\nEntry: DE, HL = characters; IX = state block.\nExit: Fz = 1 when they match; B = character from DE; A = character from HL.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "5416": {"comment":"Classify a character"},
        "5421": {"comment":"upper()"},
        "5431": {"comment":"Classify a character"},
        "5436": {"comment":"upper()"},
        "5440": {"synopsis":"Checks there is a search string in Buffer3; when it is empty, shows \"NO STRING\".\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0 when there is a string.\nError: Fc = 1 when it is empty.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "5465": {"synopsis":"Moves the search line (eSrchLn) to the next line, or to the previous one when\nDF5C_B_MATCHBACKW is set. At the end of a date's lines it moves to the next (previous) date\nwith lines, starting at its first (last) line. When the search is limited to the block\n(DF5E_B_SEARCHBLOCK for search/replace, DF5E_B_LST_SV_BLOCK for list/save, chosen by\nDF5C_B_SRCHRPLC), it stops at the block's end (start) line and date.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0; the new line copied to Buffer2.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is no further line, the block boundary is reached or the block has\nno end marker."},
        "5484": {"comment":"not block limited? skip test"},
        "5490": {"comment":"no end? Fc=1"},
        "5493": {"comment":"compare to end/start  line"},
        "5512": {"comment":"match? Fc=1"},
        "5566": {"comment":"compare to end/start date"},
        "5593": {"comment":"match? Fc=1"},
        "5654": {"synopsis":"Copies the 78-byte input buffer to Buffer2.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: F (and DF5C_B_7).\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"local flag !! remove, use Fc"},
        "5660": {"synopsis":"Copies the 78 bytes of Buffer2 to the input buffer.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: F (and DF5C_B_7).\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5696": {"synopsis":"Creates a date node: allocates 9 bytes (AllocBindMulti) and inserts the node with GN_Xin\nbetween eSrchDatePrev and eSrchDate, where it becomes eSrchDate. Its date (bytes 3-5) is\ndix_Date2 and its line list (bytes 6-8) is empty; then InitSearchDate.\nEntry: dix_Date2 = date; eSrchDatePrev, eSrchDate = where to insert; IX = state block.\nError: no memory goes to ErrQuit (no return).\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "5801": {"synopsis":"Inserts a new empty line (a 4-byte node, length 0) after the current line and makes it the\ncurrent line.\nEntry: IX = state block; current line pointers.\nExit: BHL = IY = the new node.\nError: no memory goes to ErrQuit (no return)."},
        "5823": {"synopsis":"Moves the search date pointers (eSrchDatePrev, eSrchDate) along the date list to the node of\nthe date in dix_Date3, comparing with sub_D72D and stepping with sub_D750 and sub_D75F.\nEntry: dix_Date3 = date; search date pointers = where to start; IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the date has a node, eSrchDate = that node.\nError: Fc = 1 when it has none; the pointers then mark where it belongs (eSrchDate = the\nfirst later date or 0), ready for sub_D681."},
        "5868": {"synopsis":"Compares dix_Date3 with the date of the search date node (eSrchDate).\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: Fz = 1 when equal; Fc = 1 when dix_Date3 is earlier; Fc = 1 also when there is no node\n(eSrchDate = 0) or no previous pointer.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5903": {"synopsis":"Moves the search date pointers one node back (GetPrev), unless the previous pointer is 0.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5918": {"synopsis":"Moves the search date pointers one node forward (GN_Xnx), unless eSrchDate is 0.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5933": {"synopsis":"Removes the current date's node when it is empty: copies the current date pointers to the\nsearch pointers, calls MayRemoveDate and copies them back, so the current date becomes the\nnext one when it was removed.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the date was removed, Fc = 1 when it was kept."},
        "5942": {"synopsis":"Removes the date node at eSrchDate when it holds nothing: no lines, or one empty line that\nno block marker or active saved position points at. The node is taken out of the list with\nGN_Xdl (eSrchDate becomes the next date; the current date pointers follow when they pointed\nat it) and its 9 bytes are freed. The empty line node itself is not freed here.\nInitSearchDate is called first, so eSrchLn and dix_Date2 belong to that date.\nEntry: eSrchDatePrev, eSrchDate = the date; IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the date was removed.\nError: Fc = 1 when the date was kept; a failed free goes to ErrQuit."},
        "5948": {"comment":"no line?"},
        "5953": {"comment":"no next? Fc=1"},
        "5966": {"comment":"length<>0? Fc=1"},
        "5990": {"comment":"BlkStart=SrchLn? Fc=1"},
        "6004": {"comment":"match? Fc=1"},
        "6013": {"comment":"dix_SavedStates+6"},
        "6032": {"comment":"match? Fc=1"},
        "6039": {"comment":"remove date"},
        "6052": {"comment":"removed current? change it"},
        "6071": {"comment":"removed CurrentPrev?  change it"},
        "6090": {"comment":"free  date"},
        "6102": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the cursor line is inside the marked block: copies the current line pointers\nto the search line pointers and dix_CurrentDate to dix_Date2, then falls into\nDay2e15InsideBlk.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the line is inside the block.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6108": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the line at eSrchLn, on the date in dix_Date2, is inside the marked block:\nfrom the start marker to the end marker, or only the start line when no end marker is set.\nOn a marker's date it walks the following lines to see which marker comes first.\nOZ source name: Day2e15InsideBlock.\nEntry: eSrchLn, dix_Date2; IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the line is inside the block, Fc = 0 when not or no block is marked.\nChanges: F (and DF5D_B_DATE2_EQ_BLKDATE, DF5D_B_DATE2_EQ_BLKEND).\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6116": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "6139": {"comment":"Date2<BlkStart? Fc=0"},
        "6159": {"comment":"ln matches? Fc=1"},
        "6165": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "6183": {"comment":"BlkEnd<Date2? Fc=0"},
        "6207": {"comment":"ln matches? Fc=1"},
        "6213": {"comment":"surely in block? Fc=1"},
        "6221": {"comment":"end of list"},
        "6234": {"comment":"found BlkStart? Fc=0"},
        "6244": {"comment":"found BlkEnd? Fc=1"},
        "6264": {"synopsis":"Stores the input buffer in the current line, as ReallocCurrent, except when there is no\ncurrent line, no line before it and the input buffer is empty: then nothing is created.\nEntry: IX = state block; the line in the input buffer.\nError: no memory goes to ErrQuit (no return)."},
        "6291": {"synopsis":"Stores the input buffer in the current line node. When the node's length differs from the\ntext (or there is no node), the old node is freed and a new one of length + 4 bytes is\ninserted in its place. Then every pointer equal to the old node (block markers, saved\npositions, top line and its previous pointer) is changed to the new one (MayReplaceCur).\nEntry: IX = state block; the line in the input buffer.\nExit: eTmp = the old node pointer.\nError: no memory goes to ErrQuit (no return)."},
        "6312": {"comment":"strlen()"},
        "6319": {"comment":"no line? allocate new one"},
        "6321": {"comment":"bhl=e0F"},
        "6368": {"comment":"DE=node data"},
        "6371": {"comment":"store length"},
        "6376": {"comment":"no data? skip copy"},
        "6419": {"synopsis":"compare ePtr at HL with eTmp, if it matches replace it with eCurrent\nOZ source name: MayReplaceWithCurrent."},
        "6421": {"comment":"!! move this  below jr nz"},
        "6436": {"synopsis":"Moves to the first line of the current date: the current line pointers start at the date\nnode's line list (the previous pointer is the node's field at +6), the top line is the same\nline, the cursor goes to row 0, and the line is copied to the input buffer (falls into\nCpy_BHL_BufDE with DE = 0).\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: BHL = first line (0 when the date has none).\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IY."},
        "6492": {"synopsis":"Copies the text of the line node at BHL into a line buffer and NUL-terminates it; a node\npointer of 0 gives an empty string. Binds the node's bank into segment 1.\nEntry: BHL = line node (length at +3, text at +4); DE = buffer offset (input buffer 0,\nBuffer2 $4F).\nExit: DE = address of the terminating NUL.\nChanges: AF, DE, IY.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "6497": {"comment":"no source? NULL destination"},
        "6520": {"comment":"BC=length"},
        "6524": {"comment":"0? skip copy   !! do this test right after ld a"},
        "6535": {"comment":"NULL-terminate dest"},
        "6541": {"synopsis":"Removes the current line from the day's list (GN_Xdl), the next line becoming current, and\nfrees its node (length + 4 bytes). Does nothing when there is no current line.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Mfr.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY."},
        "6553": {"comment":"remove BHL from list"},
        "6580": {"synopsis":"Deactivates the block markers that point at the line in eTmp; when only the end marker is\nleft, it becomes the start. Then continues as MayInactSaved.\nOZ source name: MayInactivateBlkSaved.\nEntry: eTmp = pointer of a removed line; IX = state block.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6585": {"synopsis":"Deactivates the saved positions that point at the line in eTmp, then lowers\ndix_ubNumSavedPositions past the inactive records at the top of the stack.\nOZ source name: MayInactivateSaved.\nEntry: eTmp = pointer of a removed line; IX = state block.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6650": {"comment":"dix_SavedStates+5*7-1"},
        "6685": {"synopsis":"Clears the active bit (bit 0 of byte 6) of a 7-byte state record (block marker or saved\nposition) when its line pointer equals eTmp.\nOZ source name: MayInactivateState.\nEntry: HL = offset of the record in the state block; IX = state block.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6706": {"synopsis":"Compares the 3-byte pointer at state-block offset HL with eTmp (Cmp3_HL_DE).\nEntry: HL = offset in the state block; IX = state block.\nExit: Fz = 1 when equal; Fc = 1 when the pointer is lower than eTmp.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6726": {"synopsis":"Inserts the node at BHL into the day's line list with GN_Xin, between eCurrentLnPrev and\neCurrentLine, and makes it the current line.\nOZ source name: InsertCurrentLine.\nEntry: BHL = new node; IX = state block.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6740": {"comment":"push  ADE (next node)"},
        "6752": {"comment":"push  ADE (prev node)"},
        "6755": {"comment":"put new ptr"},
        "6764": {"comment":"push  BHL (insert node)"},
        "6771": {"comment":"insert entry"},
        "6774": {"comment":"fix stack"},
        "6785": {"synopsis":"Fills a 7-byte state record (block marker or saved position): the current line pointer at\n+0, dix_CurrentDate at +3, and sets the active bit (bit 0 of +6).\nEntry: HL = offset of the record in the state block; IX = state block.\nExit: HL = address of the record's flag byte.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "6821": {"comment":"mark  as active"},
        "6825": {"synopsis":"Brings the line whose pointer is in eTmp into view on the current date: starts at the first\nline (sub_D969) and moves the top line forward until FindLineOnScreen finds it, then makes\nit the current line, sets the cursor row and copies it to the input buffer. When the line is\nnot found, it falls back to the first line. The caller redraws.\nEntry: eTmp = line pointer; IX = state block."},
        "6861": {"synopsis":"Looks for the line whose pointer is in eTmp among the 8 lines shown from the top line (a 0\nin eTmp finds the end of the day's lines).\nEntry: eTmp = line pointer; IX = state block.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = row (0-7); BHL = the line, CDE = its previous pointer.\nError: Fc = 1 when it is not on screen; Fz = 1 when the lines ended first.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6878": {"comment":"!! jr to scf"},
        "6898": {"comment":"A=line, Fc=0"},
        "6901": {"comment":"Fz= BHL status"},
        "6906": {"synopsis":"Loads the current date pointers (dix_eCurrentDatePrev, dix_eCurrentDate).\nOZ source name: GetCurrentDatePtrs.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: BHL = current date node; CDE = previous node.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6911": {"synopsis":"Loads the search date pointers (dix_eSrchDatePrev, dix_eSrchDate).\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: BHL = search date node; CDE = previous node.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6916": {"synopsis":"Loads the current line pointers (dix_eCurrentLnPrev, dix_eCurrentLine).\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: BHL = current line node; CDE = previous node.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6921": {"synopsis":"Loads the search line pointers (dix_eSrchLnPrev, dix_eSrchLn).\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: BHL = search line node; CDE = previous node.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6926": {"synopsis":"Loads the top line pointers (dix_eTopLnPrev, dix_eTopLine); falls into GetDIXptrs.\nEntry: IX = state block.\nExit: BHL = top line node; CDE = previous node.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "6954": {"synopsis":"Stores CDE and BHL as the current date pointers (dix_eCurrentDatePrev, dix_eCurrentDate).\nOZ source name: PutCurrentDatePtrs.\nEntry: BHL = date node; CDE = previous node; IX = state block.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6959": {"synopsis":"Stores BHL as the search date pointer and CDE as the entry before it, in the 6-byte pointer\npair at its offset in the work area; falls into PutDIXptrs.\nOZ source name: PutSearchDatePtrs.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; BHL = list entry; CDE = previous entry.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6964": {"synopsis":"Stores BHL as the current line pointer and CDE as the entry before it, in the 6-byte pointer\npair at its offset in the work area; falls into PutDIXptrs.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; BHL = list entry; CDE = previous entry.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6969": {"synopsis":"Stores BHL as the search line pointer and CDE as the entry before it, in the 6-byte pointer\npair at its offset in the work area; falls into PutDIXptrs.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; BHL = list entry; CDE = previous entry.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6974": {"synopsis":"Stores BHL as the top line pointer (the first line shown in the window) and CDE as the entry\nbefore it; falls into PutDIXptrs.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; BHL = line entry; CDE = previous entry.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7008": {"synopsis":"Copies the 6-byte current date pointer pair (previous and current entry) over the search\ndate pair.\nOZ source name: Cpy6_CrntDate_SrchDate.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7013": {"synopsis":"Copies the 6-byte current line pointer pair over the search line pair.\nOZ source name: Cpy6_CrntLn_SrchLn.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7018": {"synopsis":"Copies the 6-byte search date pointer pair over the current date pair.\nOZ source name: Cpy6_SrchDate_CrntDate.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7023": {"synopsis":"Copies the 6-byte search line pointer pair over the current line pair; falls into the shared\ncopy, which uses the DF5D_B_CPY6UP flag for the direction.\nOZ source name: Cpy6_SrchLn_CrntLn.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7026": {"comment":"local flag"},
        "7071": {"synopsis":"Copies the 3-byte current date (internal format) to Date2.\nOZ source name: CpyDate_Current_2.\nEntry: Diary work area allocated.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7087": {"synopsis":"Copies the 3-byte Date2 back to the current date.\nOZ source name: CpyDate_2_Current.\nEntry: Diary work area allocated.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7103": {"synopsis":"Makes the current line the top line of the window: copies the current line pointer pair to\nthe top line pair.\nOZ source name: Cpy2e_CurrentLn_TopLn.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7116": {"synopsis":"Copies the 3-byte current date to Date3.\nOZ source name: CpyDate_Current_3.\nEntry: Diary work area allocated.\nExit: HL = offset of the current date ($21); DE = offset of Date3 ($62).\nChanges: F, DE, HL."},
        "7126": {"synopsis":"Copies the 3-byte current line pointer to the temporary pointer eTmp in the work area.\nOZ source name: Cpy_CurrentLine_eTmp.\nEntry: Diary work area allocated.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7140": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=src offset, DE=dst offset."},
        "7160": {"synopsis":"Tests the extended pointer BHL for null.\nEntry: BHL = pointer.\nExit: Fz = 1 when BHL = 0; Fc = 0; A = B OR H OR L.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7164": {"synopsis":"Tests the extended pointer CDE for null.\nEntry: CDE = pointer.\nExit: Fz = 1 when CDE = 0; Fc = 0; A = C OR D OR E.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7168": {"synopsis":"Tests whether a list entry has a successor: steps once with GN_Xnx and tests the result,\nkeeping the pointers.\nEntry: BHL = list entry; CDE = previous entry.\nExit: Fz = 1 when BHL is null or the entry is the last one.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7185": {"synopsis":"Tests whether a list entry has a real predecessor: steps back with GetPrev and tests the\npointer before that, so the list head (which has none before it) does not count.\nEntry: BHL = list entry; CDE = previous entry.\nExit: Fz = 1 when CDE is null or the previous entry is the list head.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7202": {"synopsis":"Tests the current line pointer for null (the current date has no line).\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: Fz = 1 when there is no current line.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7212": {"synopsis":"Tests whether a line follows the current line (TstNextNode on the current line pointers).\nOZ source name: CurrentHasNextLine.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: Fz = 1 when there is no current line or it is the last one.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7225": {"synopsis":"Tests whether a line precedes the current line (TstPrevNode on the current line pointers).\nOZ source name: CurrentHasPrevLine.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: Fz = 1 when the current line is the first one.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7238": {"synopsis":"Sets the search date pointers to the first date of the diary: the entry is the date list\nhead stored at offset $18 of the work area, and the address of that head is the previous\npointer. Continues in PutSrchDatePtrs.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: BHL = first date entry (0 if the diary is empty); CDE = address of the list head.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7262": {"synopsis":"Exit: BHL,CDE=LnPtrs."},
        "7268": {"comment":"DE=HL+6"},
        "7277": {"comment":"set LnPtrs"},
        "7289": {"comment":"Set Date2"},
        "7308": {"synopsis":"Moves the search line pointers to the last line of the search date: calls InitSearchDate,\nthen steps with GN_Xnx until the end of the line list and steps back once with GetPrev.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; search date pointers set.\nExit: BHL = last line; CDE = the line before it, stored as the search line pointers; Date2 =\nthe search date; the date entry's bank is bound in segment 1; Fz = 1 when the date has no\nlines.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY."},
        "7331": {"synopsis":"Positions the search date on the start of the marked block: when the block start is set,\ncopies the current date pointers to the search date pointers, copies the block start date to\nDate3 and searches the date list for it with sub_D700.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: Fc = 0 when a block start is set (the search date pointers moved).\nError: Fc = 1 when no block start is marked."},
        "7356": {"synopsis":"Advances the search line pointers until they reach the block start line: copies the block\nstart line pointer to eTmp, then steps the search line with GN_Xnx until it matches.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; search line pointers on the block start date's lines.\nExit: Fz = 1, Fc = 0 when the search line is the block start line.\nError: Fc = 1 when the end of the line list is reached first.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7384": {"synopsis":"Steps a list entry backwards: swaps the two pointers (xnx2_1), steps forward with GN_Xnx and\nswaps them back.\nEntry: BHL = list entry; CDE = previous entry.\nExit: BHL = previous entry; CDE = the entry before that.\nError: Fc = 1 when CDE is null; BHL and CDE are unchanged.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7390": {"synopsis":"Entry inside GetPrev: swaps the extended pointers BHL and CDE (GetPrev calls it, runs GN_Xnx\nand falls into it again).\nEntry: BHL, CDE = pointers.\nExit: BHL = old CDE; CDE = old BHL; A = old B.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7395": {"synopsis":"Moves the current line pointers one line forward with GN_Xnx and stores them back.\nOZ source name: AdvanceCurrentPtrs.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: BHL = next line (0 after the last); CDE = the old current line.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Eof when there is no current line (pointers unchanged).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7404": {"synopsis":"Moves the current line pointers one line back with GetPrev and stores them back.\nOZ source name: RetreatCurrentPtrs.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: BHL = previous line; CDE = the line before it.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is no previous entry (pointers unchanged).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7413": {"synopsis":"Compares two 3-byte values (dates or extended pointers), most significant byte first.\nEntry: HL = address of the first value; DE = address of the second.\nExit: Fz = 1 when they are equal; Fc = 1 when the value at HL is lower.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7416": {"comment":"!! inc hl; inc hl; in de; inc de"},
        "7424": {"comment":"!! drop 'ex de,hl' and 'ld a,(hl); cp (de)'"},
        "7436": {"synopsis":"Exit: Fz."},
        "7461": {"synopsis":"Reads up to 3 bytes of the \"DATE\" mailbox (OS_Sr SR_RPD) into the current date, which stays\nas it was when there is no such mail; then falls into WrMailDate, so the date is posted\nback.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"local flag"},
        "7468": {"synopsis":"Posts the 6 bytes at the current date ($21-$26 of the work area) as the \"DATE\" mailbox with\nOS_Sr SR_WPD (the mailbox keeps a pointer to them); falls into RdWrDate.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7472": {"synopsis":"Reads or writes the \"DATE\" mailbox with OS_Sr, the direction chosen by DF5D_B_WRMAILDATE:\nwrites 6 bytes from the current date when it is set, reads 3 bytes into it when it is clear.\nThe result of OS_Sr is discarded.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; DF5D_B_WRMAILDATE in dix_ubFlags5D.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7497": {"comment":"write 6 bytes"},
        "7499": {"comment":"SR_WPD"},
        "7503": {"comment":"read  3 bytes"},
        "7505": {"comment":"SR_RPD"},
        "7507": {"comment":"Save & Restore"},
        "7514": {"synopsis":"The mailbox name \"DATE\", null-terminated, read by RdWrDate."},
        "7519": {"synopsis":"Checks that the current date is in the range GN_Die can convert.\nOZ source name: VerifyCurrentDate.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nError: Fc = 1 when GN_Die rejects the date.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7530": {"comment":"convert from internal to zoned format"},
        "7536": {"synopsis":"Sets the current date to today's date with GN_Gmd (internal format).\nEntry: Diary work area allocated.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "7546": {"comment":"get current machine date in internal format"},
        "7552": {"synopsis":"Fetches the standard output handle with OS_Nq NQ_Out.\nEntry: none.\nExit: IX = output handle.\nChanges: AF, IX.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "7556": {"comment":"enquire (fetch) parameter"},
        "7560": {"synopsis":"Allocates a block from the Diary's line memory pool (AllocMultiMem) and binds its bank in\nsegment 1 (MayBindS1).\nEntry: C = size in bytes.\nExit: BHL = block (bank bound in segment 1); Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (from OS_Mal).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "7567": {"synopsis":"Allocates C bytes with OS_Mal from the memory pool whose handle is in pMemHandleMulti.\nEntry: C = size in bytes.\nExit: BHL = block; C = segment.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "7575": {"comment":"Allocate memory"},
        "7580": {"synopsis":"Binds bank B in segment 1 with OZ_MPB, unless S1Binding says it is bound already; records\nthe new binding in S1Binding.\nEntry: B = bank.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "7582": {"comment":"!! cp/ret before push"},
        "7594": {"comment":"Bind bank B in segment C"},
        "7595": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "7599": {"synopsis":"Frees a block of the line memory pool (pMemHandleMulti) with OS_Mfr.\nEntry: BHL = block; C = size in bytes.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL, IX."},
        "7610": {"comment":"Free  memory"},
        "7617": {"synopsis":"Checks that there is memory for the current command by allocating trial blocks and freeing\nthem again.\n1. Reads the command's flags from CmdFlags_tbl into dix_Tmp2.\n2. Bit 0: if the input buffer's text is longer than the current line's block (or there is no\ncurrent line), allocates its length plus 4.\n3. Bits 1 and 2: allocates a block of 83 bytes for each.\n4. Frees the blocks in reverse order; a failed allocation or free sets DF5B_B_ALLOC83ERR,\nand then the memory-low message is shown with ShowError.\n5. Rebinds the bank that was in segment 1.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; dix_ubCommand = command code.\nExit: Fc = 0 when there is enough memory.\nError: Fc = 1 (message shown) when memory is low.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7638": {"comment":"!! all these are local flags"},
        "7654": {"comment":"DF67  local as well"},
        "7676": {"comment":"strlen()"},
        "7699": {"comment":"InputBuffer fits? skip"},
        "7845": {"synopsis":"Redraws the text window from the current line down: sets the row counter to 8 minus the\ncursor row and continues in RedrawDiaryWd's printing loop with the current line pointers.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7858": {"synopsis":"Redraws the 8 rows of the text window from the top line.\n1. Stores the starting line in the search line pointers and copies the current date to\nDate2.\n2. Turns reverse video on when the date lies inside the marked block (Day2e15InsideBlk).\n3. For each row: prints the line with PrintOneLine, clears the row of an empty date, or\nprints \" END OF TEXT \" (PrntEndOfText) and stops after the last line.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7884": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "7897": {"comment":"no more to print? \"end of text\""},
        "7928": {"synopsis":"Shows the end-of-text marker below the cursor when the current line is the last one and the\ncursor is not on the last row, then moves the cursor back to column 0 of its row.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7965": {"synopsis":"Prints one diary line on the current row: turns reverse video on at the block start line,\nprints the input buffer for the current line (it is being edited) or the line copied to\nBuffer2 otherwise, clears to the end of the row, and clears the reverse flag at the block\nend line.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; BHL = line entry; cursor at the row's start.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7980": {"comment":"check if we need to turn reverse on"},
        "8009": {"comment":"not current?  use Buf2"},
        "8011": {"comment":"else  print InputBuf"},
        "8033": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "8065": {"comment":"check if we need to turn reverse off"},
        "8079": {"synopsis":"Shows \"INSERT MODE\" or \"OVERTYPE MODE\" (DF5B_B_OVERWRITE) on row 5 of the date window\n(window 3) in tiny centred text; continues in PrntErrorPost.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area."},
        "8142": {"synopsis":"Shows the current date in the date window (window 3): converts it with GN_Pdt into the work\narea's date buffer, clears rows 0 to 3, and prints the day name on row 0, the day number and\nmonth on row 1 and the next word (the year) on row 2. If GN_Pdt fails it prints the\nmemory-low message instead. Continues in PrntErrorPost.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area."},
        "8162": {"comment":"convert internal date to ASCII string"},
        "8176": {"comment":"clear lines 1-4"},
        "8223": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "8229": {"comment":"Display name of day line 0"},
        "8233": {"comment":"on next line, display day number of month"},
        "8242": {"comment":"display name of month (after day number of month)"},
        "8251": {"comment":"print date string lines 0 - 2"},
        "8256": {"synopsis":"Entry inside PrntLn: prints the word at DE at the cursor without moving it first.\nEntry: DE = text.\nExit: DE = past the space or null that ended the word.\nKeeps: A, HL."},
        "8260": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 0 of row A and prints the word at DE, up to a space or a null.\nEntry: A = row; DE = text.\nExit: DE = past the space or null that ended the word.\nKeeps: A, HL."},
        "8275": {"comment":"write a byte  to std. output"},
        "8282": {"synopsis":"Redraws the text window (RedrawDiaryWd) and the date (PrintDate).\nEntry: IX = Diary work area."},
        "8288": {"synopsis":"Draws the Search dialog after redrawing the diary screen (sub_E14A); falls into Search2's\ndrawing. It is the redraw routine in SearchUI_tbl.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8296": {"synopsis":"Draws the \"SEARCH DIARY\" dialog in window 4 (InitWin4): the search string from Buffer3 and\nthe Yes/No options case, marked block, produce list and print list; then shows the options\n(Show5EFlags with SearchUI_tbl) and toggles the cursor.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8496": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "8505": {"synopsis":"Draws the Replace dialog after redrawing the diary screen (sub_E14A); falls into Replace2's\ndrawing. It is the redraw routine in RplcUI_tbl.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8513": {"synopsis":"Draws the \"DIARY REPLACE\" dialog in window 4: the search string from Buffer3, the\nreplacement from offset $7D of the work area and the Yes/No options case, confirmation and\nmarked block; then shows the options (RplcUI_tbl) and toggles the cursor.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8740": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "8756": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "8765": {"synopsis":"Draws the List dialog after redrawing the diary screen (sub_E14A); falls into List2's\ndrawing. It is the redraw routine in ListUI_tbl.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8773": {"synopsis":"Draws the \"LIST DIARY\" dialog in window 4 with the Yes/No options list on screen, list on\nprinter and list only the marked block; then shows the options (ListUI_tbl) and toggles the\ncursor.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8894": {"synopsis":"Draws the Load dialog after redrawing the diary screen (sub_E14A); falls into Load2's\ndrawing. It is the redraw routine in LoadUI_tbl.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8902": {"synopsis":"Draws the \"LOAD (APPEND) FILE INTO DIARY\" dialog in window 4: the file name from the I/O\nbuffer and the option to start loading at the diary date; then shows the options\n(LoadUI_tbl) and toggles the cursor.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "9045": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "9054": {"synopsis":"Draws the Save dialog after redrawing the diary screen (sub_E14A); falls into Save2's\ndrawing. It is the redraw routine in SaveUI_tbl.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "9062": {"synopsis":"Draws the \"SAVE FILE FROM DIARY\" dialog in window 4: the file name from the I/O buffer and\nthe option to save only the marked block; then falls into ExitList, which shows the options\n(SaveUI_tbl), toggles the cursor and restores the registers.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "9186": {"comment":"write string  to std. output"},
        "9202": {"synopsis":"Redraws the diary screen's furniture: the date window (InitWd), the insert mode, the file\nname (PrntFilename) and the date (PrintDate).\nEntry: IX = Diary work area."},
        "9214": {"synopsis":"Shows the Yes/No state of every option of a dialog table: for each item, moves to column 57\nof the item's row and prints \"Yes\" or \"No \" as the item's mask bit in dix_ubFlags5E is set.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; DE = dialog table (count byte, redraw routine word, then a row\nbyte and a mask byte per item).\nExit: DE = past the table.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "9239": {"synopsis":"Prints \"Yes\" when Fz = 0, \"No \" when Fz = 1.\nEntry: Fz = option state (Fz = 0 for set)."},
        "9255": {"synopsis":"Runs a dialog's Yes/No options: shows the selected item (dix_ubTmp, from 1), puts the cursor\non it and reads keys. Y sets the option's bit in dix_ubFlags5E, N clears it, ? toggles it, -\nselects the next item and . the previous one; . on the first item, ESC and ENTER leave. On\nRC_Draw it posts the mail date and calls the table's redraw routine; other errors post the\ndate and redraw the item.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; DE = dialog table (as for Show5EFlags).\nExit: Fc = 0; A = $1B (ESC), $0D (ENTER) or '.' (left upwards).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Quit.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "9267": {"comment":"skip  N and Func"},
        "9274": {"comment":"ypos"},
        "9277": {"comment":"bit mask"},
        "9293": {"comment":"read  a byte from std. input"},
        "9309": {"comment":"Classify a character"},
        "9314": {"comment":"upper"},
        "9318": {"comment":"Request application to quit *"},
        "9325": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "9364": {"comment":"toggle"},
        "9410": {"comment":"exit  with A='.'"},
        "9425": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL = ptr to error message."},
        "9428": {"comment":"write string to std. output"},
        "9431": {"synopsis":"Entry inside ShowError: ends the message with PrntErrorPost and sets DF5C_B_ERRORSHOWN, so\nRemoveError clears it later. Called after printing a found-count message.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area."},
        "9434": {"comment":"local flag"},
        "9439": {"synopsis":"Removes a shown error message: when DF5C_B_ERRORSHOWN is set, clears row 5 of window 3,\nselects window 2 again and clears the flag.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area."},
        "9469": {"synopsis":"Draws the date window (window 3) with GN_Win from DiaryDateWdBlock, defines window 2 (the\ntext window, 76 columns by 8 rows at column 1) and clears it, and clears DF5C_B_ERRORSHOWN.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nChanges: F, B, HL."},
        "9510": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the date window: window 3 with bars, shelf brackets and an\n8-pixel banner, at column 78, row 0, 14 wide and 8 high, banner text date_banner."},
        "9517": {"synopsis":"The date window's banner text, \"DIARY DATE\", null-terminated."},
        "9528": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 0 of the cursor row (dix_ubCrsrYPos); falls into MoveTo_0Ya.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nExit: A = cursor row."},
        "9531": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 0 of row A of the current window.\nEntry: A = row.\nKeeps: A."},
        "9540": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 57 of row A, where a dialog shows an option's Yes/No.\nEntry: A = row.\nKeeps: A."},
        "9550": {"comment":"write a byte  to std. output"},
        "9554": {"synopsis":"Toggles the cursor (VDU 1,\"C\").\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "9562": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key after a page of list output: unless the line counter dix_ubTmp is 7, calls\nOS_Sr SR_PWT; if the wait reports RC_Draw it redraws the search or list dialog\n(DF5C_B_SRCHRPLC) and the list window (PrntSearchListWd). Then sets the counter to 7.\nEntry: IX = Diary work area.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "9571": {"comment":"SR_PWT"},
        "9573": {"comment":"Save  & Restore"},
        "9577": {"comment":"Application pre-empted and screen corrupted"},
        "9605": {"synopsis":"Outputs a null-terminated string for the search or list output: to the screen when\nDF5E_B_MAKESEARCHLIST is set (counting line feeds and calling MayPageWait when the page is\nfull) and to the printer with OS_Prt when DF5E_B_PRINTSEARCHLIST is set. Stops early on an\nescape condition (OS_Esc).\nEntry: IX = Diary work area; HL = string.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "9606": {"comment":"SC_BIT"},
        "9607": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "9632": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "9641": {"comment":"Send character directly to printer filter"},
        "9648": {"synopsis":"Sends a form feed (12) to the printer filter with OS_Prt.\nEntry: none."},
        "9650": {"comment":"Send character directly to printer filter"},
        "9653": {"synopsis":"Clears the current window's row from the cursor to its end (VDU 1,\"2C\",$FD).\nEntry: none."},
        "9661": {"synopsis":"Prepares the date window's message row: selects window 3, moves to row 4, sets tiny reverse\ntext, clears the row and sets centre justification. ShowError prints the message after it.\nEntry: none."},
        "9687": {"synopsis":"Shows the diary's file name: reads the last segment of the file name in the I/O buffer\n(eIOBuf_242 + iob_Filename) with GN_Esa into the buffer at offset $CC of the dix workspace\n(eMem_dix_254), or uses NotSaved_txt when there is none. Selects and initialises window 3,\nmoves to (0,6), switches bold and tiny off, clears to the end of the line and prints the\nname centred; falls into PrntErrorPost.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "9707": {"comment":"read/write filename segments"},
        "9718": {"comment":"no filename yet available"},
        "9752": {"synopsis":"Switches the tiny, reverse, caps lock and bold toggles off, restores normal justification\nand selects and initialises window 2.\nEntry: none."},
        "9771": {"synopsis":"Prints \" END OF TEXT \" in tiny reverse type at the cursor and clears the window from there\nto its end.\nEntry: none."},
        "9802": {"synopsis":"Defines window 4 at (1,0), 74 columns by 8 rows, with side bars and shelf brackets, selects\nand clears it, hides the cursor, moves to (0,0), switches tiny and reverse on, clears the\nline and sets centre justification, ready for a dialogue's title.\nEntry: none."},
        "9841": {"synopsis":"The Diary's error handler (installed with OS_Erh). A fatal error (Fz = 1) returns unchanged;\nRC_Quit leaves the application through Quit; any other error is cleared.\nEntry: A = error code; Fz = 1 for a fatal error.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1 for a non-fatal error."},
        "9849": {"synopsis":"A CR, LF pair, null-terminated: the line ending PrintList writes in the Diary's list output."},
        "9852": {"synopsis":"Defines window 5 at (1,1), 74 columns by 7 rows, with side bars, selects and clears it and\nswitches vertical scrolling on: the window search and list results are written to.\nEntry: none."},
        "9873": {"synopsis":"The text \"NAME\", null-terminated: the mailbox the Diary's Load command reads (OS_Sr, SR_RPD)\nfor the file name marked in the Filer."},
        "9878": {"synopsis":"Option table for the Diary's Search dialogue, read by DoUI and Show5EFlags: a count byte,\nthe address of the routine that redraws the dialogue, then a row and a bit mask in\ndix_ubFlags5E for each Yes/No option (4 options: ignore case, search block, list, print\nlist)."},
        "9881": {"comment":"ignore case, search block, list, print list"},
        "9889": {"synopsis":"Option table for the Diary's List dialogue, read by DoUI and Show5EFlags: a count byte, the\naddress of the routine that redraws the dialogue, then a row and a bit mask in dix_ubFlags5E\nfor each Yes/No option (3 options: screen, printer, block)."},
        "9892": {"comment":"screen, printer, block"},
        "9898": {"synopsis":"Option table for the Diary's Replace dialogue, read by DoUI and Show5EFlags: a count byte,\nthe address of the routine that redraws the dialogue, then a row and a bit mask in\ndix_ubFlags5E for each Yes/No option (3 options: ignore case, confirm, block)."},
        "9901": {"comment":"ignore case, confirm, block"},
        "9907": {"synopsis":"Option table for the Diary's Load dialogue, read by DoUI and Show5EFlags: a count byte, the\naddress of the routine that redraws the dialogue, then a row and a bit mask in dix_ubFlags5E\nfor each Yes/No option (1 option: start at date)."},
        "9910": {"comment":"start at date"},
        "9912": {"synopsis":"Option table for the Diary's Save dialogue, read by DoUI and Show5EFlags: a count byte, the\naddress of the routine that redraws the dialogue, then a row and a bit mask in dix_ubFlags5E\nfor each Yes/No option (1 option: block)."},
        "9915": {"comment":"block"},
        "9917": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"No memory for date conversion\", printed in the list output when a date\ncannot be converted, null-terminated."},
        "9947": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"MEMORY LOW\" followed by a BEL, null-terminated."},
        "9959": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"NO MATCH\" followed by a BEL, null-terminated."},
        "9969": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"NO STRING\" followed by a BEL, null-terminated."},
        "9980": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"NO ROOM\" followed by $7F, null-terminated."},
        "9989": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"NO MARKER\" followed by a BEL, null-terminated."},
        "10000": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"NOT MARKED\" followed by a BEL, null-terminated."},
        "10012": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"DATE RANGE\" followed by a BEL, null-terminated."},
        "10024": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"OVERLAPS\" followed by a BEL, null-terminated."},
        "10034": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"REPLACE Y/N\", null-terminated."},
        "10046": {"synopsis":"The Diary's message \"FOUND\", null-terminated."},
        "10052": {"synopsis":"The text \"NOT SAVED\" after a code that sets tiny type, null-terminated: what PrntFilename\nshows when the diary has no file name yet."},
        "10231": {"synopsis":"common code shared by Alarm, Clock & Calendar popdowns"},
        "10232": {"comment":"Application exit"},
        "10236": {"synopsis":"Runs the input fields of a form in turn: calls the routine of the first entry, then moves to\nthe next entry after Right, Shift Right, Diamond Right or Down and to the previous one after\nany other key, wrapping round at both ends. Returns when a routine reports Enter or an\nerror.\nEntry: HL = table: a 0 word, the field routines' addresses, then $FFFF; each routine returns\nthe key that ended it in A, or Fc = 1.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = IN_ENT.\nError: Fc = 1, A = the error a field routine returned.\nChanges: AF, HL, and what the field routines change.","comment":"skip start mark"},
        "10244": {"comment":"not start? skip"},
        "10246": {"synopsis":"find last entry in table\n!! remove pop/push hell"},
        "10254": {"comment":"!! and h; cpl; jr nz navt_2"},
        "10262": {"comment":"not end? loop"},
        "10265": {"comment":"skip end mark"},
        "10269": {"comment":"!! ld a,l; and h; cpl; jr nz"},
        "10272": {"comment":"not end? skip"},
        "10279": {"synopsis":"find first entry in the table\n!! remove pop/push hell"},
        "10288": {"comment":"not start? loop"},
        "10291": {"comment":"skip start mark"},
        "10295": {"comment":"!! use JpHL in low RAM"},
        "10302": {"comment":"error? return"},
        "10322": {"comment":"next entry !! could re-use INCs at NavigateTable"},
        "10326": {"comment":"previous entry"},
        "10330": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine with index A in a table of words (GetTableEntry). When the routine\nreturns Fc = 1, continues at tj_2.\nEntry: A = index; HL = table.\nExit: what the routine returns when Fc = 0."},
        "10333": {"comment":"!! call JpHL in low RAM"},
        "10340": {"synopsis":"Entry inside TableJump: handles an error result. RC_Esc is acknowledged (OS_Esc, SC_ACK) and\nturned into success; any other error is returned.\nEntry: A = error code.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = 0 after RC_Esc.\nError: Fc = 1, A = the error code."},
        "10344": {"comment":"!! already 1"},
        "10346": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "10350": {"synopsis":"Reads the word with index A from a table of words.\nEntry: A = index; HL = table.\nExit: HL = the word at HL + 2*A.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "10361": {"synopsis":"Dispatches a key through a command table: finds the entry with the key code and jumps to its\nroutine, which returns to KeyJump's caller.\nEntry: A = key code; HL = table of 3-byte entries (key code, routine address), ended by 0.\nExit: the routine runs with BC and DE as on entry and HL = the caller's BC.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail when the key is not in the table."},
        "10366": {"comment":"no more keys? RC_Fail"},
        "10369": {"comment":"same? execute"},
        "10371": {"comment":"retry next entry"},
        "10375": {"comment":"General Failure, cannot satisfy request"},
        "10384": {"comment":"!! pop bc; jp (hl)"},
        "10388": {"synopsis":"The command loop of a popdown: reads a key with OS_In (an extended key as 0 and its code),\ndispatches it through KeyJump and repeats while the routine returns Fc = 0. RC_Susp, RC_Fail\n(also an unknown key) and other errors read the next key; RC_Esc is acknowledged (OS_Esc,\nSC_ACK) and returns; RC_Quit and RC_Draw return.\nEntry: HL = command table (KeyJump's layout); DE is passed on to the routines.\nExit: after RC_Esc, the result of OS_Esc.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Quit or RC_Draw."},
        "10404": {"comment":"loop until error"},
        "10408": {"comment":"retry"},
        "10412": {"comment":"retry"},
        "10416": {"comment":"ack ESC"},
        "10418": {"comment":"return on Quit/Draw"},
        "10426": {"comment":"else retry"},
        "10428": {"comment":"!! already 1"},
        "10433": {"synopsis":"Prints a time to the standard output with GN_Ptm.\nEntry: A = GN_Ptm format; IX = 3-byte internal time.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "10446": {"comment":"print time"},
        "10452": {"synopsis":"Lets the user edit a date at a cursor position.\n1. Switches the cursor on and reserves a 14-byte buffer on the stack.\n2. Writes the date at IX into it in condensed form with '/' separators (GN_Pdt).\n3. Edits it with GN_Sip at (B,C) until a cursor key or Enter (TestKeys) ends the input;\nRC_Susp edits again.\n4. Converts the text with GN_Gdt; an invalid date beeps and returns to step 3, a valid one\nis stored at IX.\n5. Frees the buffer and switches the cursor off.\nEntry: IX = 3-byte internal date; B = column; C = row.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1; A = the key that ended the input; (IX+0..2) = the new date.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from GN_Pdt or GN_Sip.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, AF'.\nKeeps: BC, IX."},
        "10455": {"comment":"get stack buffer"},
        "10466": {"comment":"century, C delimeter, zero blanking"},
        "10468": {"comment":"condensed form, '/' delimeter"},
        "10471": {"comment":"print"},
        "10478": {"comment":"null-terminate"},
        "10480": {"comment":"cursor position"},
        "10492": {"comment":"has data, force overwrite, return special"},
        "10502": {"comment":"retry"},
        "10505": {"comment":"exit"},
        "10510": {"comment":"not special? retry"},
        "10521": {"comment":"into internal date"},
        "10526": {"comment":"ok? exit"},
        "10528": {"comment":"beep and retry"},
        "10547": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "10560": {"synopsis":"Lets the user edit a time at a cursor position, as AskDate does for a date: writes the time\nat IX with seconds and leading zeroes into a 9-byte stack buffer (GN_Ptm), edits it with\nGN_Sip until a cursor key or Enter, converts it with GN_Gtm (an invalid time beeps and is\nedited again) and stores it at IX. The cursor is on while editing.\nEntry: IX = 3-byte internal time; B = column; C = row.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1; A = the key that ended the input; (IX+0..2) = the new time.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from GN_Ptm or GN_Sip.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, AF'.\nKeeps: BC, IX."},
        "10563": {"comment":"get stack buffer"},
        "10582": {"comment":"cursor position"},
        "10604": {"comment":"retry"},
        "10607": {"comment":"exit"},
        "10612": {"comment":"retry"},
        "10622": {"comment":"into internal format"},
        "10629": {"comment":"beep and retry"},
        "10648": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "10661": {"synopsis":"!! test smallest first with 'ret c; ret z', then in decrementing order with 'ret nc'"},
        "10688": {"synopsis":"Fetches the handle of the standard output (OS_Nq, NQ_Out). The Clock, Calendar and Alarm\ncopy; the Diary has its own.\nOZ source name: GetOutHandle.\nEntry: none.\nExit: IX = standard output handle.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "10692": {"comment":"get out handle"},
        "10696": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to a column of the current row (SOH \"2X\").\nEntry: B = column.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10708": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to a position in the current window (SOH \"3@\").\nEntry: B = column; C = row.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10725": {"synopsis":"Applies the current hardware toggles (reverse, flash, grey, underline) to the next\ncharacters from the cursor (SOH \"2A\").\nEntry: A = 32 + number of characters."},
        "10734": {"synopsis":"Sets centre justification (SOH \"2JC\").\nEntry: none."},
        "10742": {"synopsis":"Sets normal justification (SOH \"2JN\").\nEntry: none."},
        "10750": {"synopsis":"Toggles tiny type, then falls into ToggleRvrs to toggle reverse video.\nEntry: none."},
        "10753": {"synopsis":"Entry inside ToggleTR: toggles reverse video (SOH \"R\").\nEntry: none."},
        "10759": {"synopsis":"Toggles tiny type (SOH \"T\").\nEntry: none."},
        "10765": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to (0,0) and clears the current window.\nEntry: none."},
        "10778": {"synopsis":"Toggles the cursor (SOH \"C\").\nEntry: none."},
        "10784": {"synopsis":"Clears from the cursor to the end of the line.\nEntry: none."},
        "10792": {"synopsis":"The text \"DATE\", null-terminated: the name of the mailbox the Calendar reads and writes with\nOS_Sr (SR_RPD, SR_WPD)."},
        "10797": {"synopsis":"The Clock popdown's entry, reached from the vector at the start of the code.\n1. Enables escape detection and checks the OZ version (OS_Nq, NQ_Voz); leaves with OS_Bye on\nan older OZ.\n2. Opens window 5 with GN_Win (MainWindowDef) and reserves 7 bytes at IX: a time, a date and\nthe menu selector (IX+6).\n3. Clears the window, prints the \"ESC SET\" menu on the bottom line and highlights it\n(ClkHighlight1).\n4. Reads the date (GN_Gmd), formats it in full (GN_Pdt) and prints the weekday, the day and\nmonth, and the year on three centred lines.\n5. Prints the time with seconds at (3,5) (DisplayTime); when GN_Gmt finds the time\ninconsistent with the date read (Fz = 0), redraws from step 3.\n6. Waits 25 centiseconds for a key (OS_Tin) and dispatches it through ClkKeyCmds_tbl;\nsuccess redraws from step 3, RC_Susp and RC_Time update the time, RC_Fail waits again,\nanything else (RC_Esc acknowledged) leaves through Exit."},
        "10801": {"comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "10806": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "10810": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: not_compatible."},
        "10811": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "10829": {"comment":"selector position"},
        "10872": {"comment":"reserve 38 bytes from stack,"},
        "10875": {"comment":"point HL to it, DE to buf+3"},
        "10876": {"comment":"first 3 bytes date value, rest is date string"},
        "10884": {"comment":"date into (DE)"},
        "10888": {"comment":"read date from buf[0], write to buf[3]"},
        "10889": {"comment":"century, date suffix"},
        "10891": {"comment":"everything in full form"},
        "10897": {"comment":"pop date value (keep C for GN_Gmt)"},
        "10898": {"comment":"skip high byte"},
        "10899": {"comment":"point HL into string !! 3 * (inc hl)"},
        "10903": {"comment":"push date value"},
        "10905": {"comment":"error? try to get time"},
        "10908": {"comment":"null-terminate string"},
        "10952": {"comment":"print year"},
        "10958": {"comment":"remember C"},
        "10959": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "10973": {"comment":"time consistent? continue"},
        "10976": {"comment":"else read date again"},
        "10979": {"comment":"push ABC"},
        "10996": {"comment":"seconds, leading xeroes"},
        "11003": {"comment":"!! 3 * 'inc sp'"},
        "11013": {"comment":"error?"},
        "11016": {"comment":"normal char?"},
        "11020": {"comment":"error?"},
        "11022": {"comment":"handle using command table"},
        "11028": {"comment":"no error? loop"},
        "11033": {"comment":"redraw seconds"},
        "11037": {"comment":"ditto"},
        "11041": {"comment":"wait key"},
        "11047": {"comment":"!! unnecessary, already 1"},
        "11049": {"comment":"ack ESC"},
        "11054": {"synopsis":"The Clock's command table for KeyJump: Right (Clock_Right), Left (Clock_Left) and Enter\n(Clock_Enter), ended by 0."},
        "11064": {"synopsis":"this code is written for more than two selectable values,\nthat's why it's overcomplicated"},
        "11067": {"comment":"!! and 1"},
        "11075": {"synopsis":"Left in the Clock: toggles the menu selector (IX+6) between ESC and SET and redraws the\nhighlight. Clock_Right continues here.\nEntry: IX = the Clock's 7-byte frame.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail, so the clock waits for the next key without redrawing.\nKeeps: BC.","comment":"toggle between 0/1  !! xor 1"},
        "11082": {"comment":"num_choises"},
        "11097": {"synopsis":"Right in the Clock: toggles the menu selector (IX+6) between ESC and SET; continues in\nClock_Left to redraw the highlight.\nEntry: IX = the Clock's 7-byte frame.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail.\nKeeps: BC.","comment":"toggle between 0/1  !! use code above"},
        "11102": {"comment":"num_choices-1"},
        "11111": {"synopsis":"Draws the Clock's menu highlight on row 6: removes the reverse from the 16-character bar,\nthen reverses the 7 characters of the selected entry (column 0 for ESC, 7 for SET, from bit\n0 of IX+6); then toggles tiny and reverse back.\nEntry: IX = the Clock's 7-byte frame.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "11126": {"comment":"B=0/9"},
        "11150": {"synopsis":"The Clock's SET command, reached through ClkCmds_tbl: clears the window, shows the \"NEW\nDATE\" and \"NEW TIME\" titles, reads the time into (IX+0..2) (GN_Gmt) and the date into\n(IX+3..5) (GN_Gmd), shows the time and runs the two fields of ClkSet_tbl with NavigateTable.\nAfter Enter, sets the time (GN_Pmt) and the date (GN_Pmd) with alarm handling suspended\n(OS_Alm AH_AINC, AH_ADEC). Selects ESC in the menu again.\nEntry: IX = the Clock's 7-byte frame.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from NavigateTable; the date and time are not set."},
        "11207": {"comment":"time into buf[0]"},
        "11210": {"comment":"date into buf[3]"},
        "11227": {"comment":"disable alarm list handling"},
        "11231": {"comment":"set time"},
        "11237": {"comment":"set date"},
        "11242": {"comment":"enable alarm list handling"},
        "11245": {"comment":"select \"exit\" in first menu"},
        "11255": {"synopsis":"The date field of the Clock's SET form: edits the date at IX+3 at (2,2) with AskDate.\nEntry: IX = the Clock's 7-byte frame Exit, Error: as AskDate.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "11271": {"synopsis":"The time field of the Clock's SET form: edits the time at IX at (3,5) with AskTime.\nEntry: IX = the Clock's 7-byte frame Exit, Error: as AskTime."},
        "11277": {"synopsis":"Prints the time at IX with seconds and leading zeroes at (3,5); continues in DisplayTime.\nEntry: IX = 3-byte internal time."},
        "11283": {"comment":"show seconds, leading zeroes"},
        "11288": {"synopsis":"The fields of the Clock's SET form for NavigateTable: a 0 start mark, SetDate, SetTime and\nthe $FFFF end mark."},
        "11296": {"synopsis":"The Clock's menu commands for TableJump, indexed by the selector: Exit (ESC) and Cl_Set\n(SET)."},
        "11300": {"synopsis":"The Clock's GN_Win window definition: window 5 with bars, shelf brackets and an 8-pixel\nbanner ($A5), at (78,0), 14 columns by 8 rows, banner clock_banner."},
        "11307": {"synopsis":"The Clock's banner, \"CLOCK\", null-terminated."},
        "11313": {"synopsis":"The Calendar popdown's entry, reached from the vector at the start of the code and again\nafter RC_Draw.\n1. Enables escape detection and checks the OZ version (OS_Nq, NQ_Voz); leaves with OS_Bye on\nan older OZ.\n2. Clears its 33 bytes of workspace and opens window 5 (CalWindow_txt).\n3. Reads a date and a diary entry from the \"DATE\" mailbox (OS_Sr, SR_RPD); with one, follows\nthe diary's entry list from it. Without one, or when InitMonth rejects it, takes today's\ndate (GN_Gmd), and a fixed date when that is rejected too.\n4. Writes the date into the mailbox (SR_WPD), draws its month (DrawMonth), highlights the\nday and runs the keys of CalKeyCmds_tbl with KeyJump0.\n5. Restarts after RC_Draw; leaves through Exit otherwise."},
        "11317": {"comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "11322": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "11326": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: not_compatible."},
        "11327": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "11356": {"comment":"read date"},
        "11358": {"comment":"no date in mail, use current"},
        "11395": {"comment":"get current machine date in internal format"},
        "11403": {"comment":"internal format for ???"},
        "11429": {"comment":"put date into mail"},
        "11454": {"comment":"redraw"},
        "11460": {"synopsis":"The Calendar's command table for KeyJump0: Enter (Cal_Enter), Shift Up and Down (Cal_SUp,\nCal_SDown), Diamond Up and Down (Cal_DUp, Cal_DDown), Down, Left, Up and Right (Cal_Down,\nCal_Left, Cal_Up, Cal_Right), Square Right and Left (Cal_ARight, Cal_ALeft), ended by 0."},
        "11494": {"synopsis":"!! make this generic -1/1/-7/7 day change for left/right/up/down"},
        "11500": {"comment":"not last of month? skip"},
        "11513": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "11516": {"comment":"remove highlight if no month change"},
        "11530": {"synopsis":"Left in the Calendar: moves to the previous day; from the 1st, draws the previous month and\nhighlights its last day.\nEntry: D = the highlighted day of the month.\nExit: Fc = 0; D = the new day."},
        "11532": {"comment":"not first of month? skip"},
        "11545": {"comment":"Fz=1"},
        "11550": {"comment":"remove highlight if no month change"},
        "11564": {"synopsis":"Down in the Calendar: moves a week on; past the month's end, draws the next month and\nhighlights the same weekday in its first week.\nEntry: D = the highlighted day of the month.\nExit: Fc = 0; D = the new day."},
        "11573": {"comment":"can add week inside month? skip"},
        "11575": {"comment":"keep day of week"},
        "11593": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "11595": {"comment":"remove highlight if no month change"},
        "11613": {"synopsis":"Up in the Calendar: moves a week back; in the first week, draws the previous month and\nhighlights the same weekday in its last week.\nEntry: D = the highlighted day of the month.\nExit: Fc = 0; D = the new day."},
        "11616": {"comment":"can go back week inside month? skip"},
        "11634": {"comment":"remove highlight if no month change"},
        "11651": {"synopsis":"Shift Down in the Calendar: moves to the same day of the next month (the month's last day if\nit is shorter); continues in Cal_SUpDn.\nEntry: D = the highlighted day of the month.\nExit: Fc = 0; D = the new day."},
        "11656": {"synopsis":"Shift Up in the Calendar: moves to the same day of the previous month (the month's last day\nif it is shorter). Falls into Cal_SUpDn, which takes the 1st of the new month in ABC, draws\nthe month and highlights the day.\nEntry: D = the highlighted day of the month.\nExit: Fc = 0; D = the new day."},
        "11674": {"comment":"day=max(day,nDays)"},
        "11693": {"synopsis":"Diamond Down in the Calendar: moves to the same day of the same month a year later; joins\nCal_DUp to make the date (GN_Dei) and continues in Cal_SUpDn.\nEntry: D = the highlighted day of the month.\nExit: Fc = 0; D = the new day."},
        "11697": {"comment":"!! inc hl"},
        "11703": {"synopsis":"Diamond Up in the Calendar: moves to the same day of the same month a year earlier; makes\nthe 1st of that month (GN_Dei) and continues in Cal_SUpDn.\nEntry: D = the highlighted day of the month.\nExit: Fc = 0; D = the new day."},
        "11707": {"comment":"!! dec hl"},
        "11716": {"comment":"1st of month"},
        "11718": {"comment":"convert from zoned format to internal format"},
        "11724": {"synopsis":"Enter in the Calendar: asks for a date after \"Look for : \" on row 7, starting from today's,\nand moves to it (MoveToDay), redrawing the month when needed; asks again when MoveToDay\nfails. Escape abandons the input (tj_2). Then clears the prompt line and highlights the day.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from AskDate other than RC_Esc.\nChanges: IX (left pointing at the freed 3-byte buffer)."},
        "11750": {"comment":"get date into buf[0]"},
        "11798": {"synopsis":"Makes the 1st of the month before the one in ubMonth and swYear (December of the year before\nfor January); shares its end with NextMonth.\nEntry: none (ubMonth, swYear).\nExit: ABC = internal date of the 1st of the month.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from GN_Dei.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "11807": {"comment":"month ok?"},
        "11809": {"comment":"decrement year  !! dec de"},
        "11819": {"synopsis":"Makes the 1st of the month after the one in ubMonth and swYear (January of the year after\nfor December) with GN_Dei.\nEntry: none (ubMonth, swYear).\nExit: ABC = internal date of the 1st of the month.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from GN_Dei.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "11830": {"comment":"month ok?"},
        "11832": {"comment":"increment year  !! inc de"},
        "11840": {"comment":"month"},
        "11841": {"comment":"1st of month"},
        "11843": {"comment":"into internal format"},
        "11848": {"synopsis":"Fills the Calendar's month variables from a date: MonthStart (the 1st, internal format),\nswYear, ubMonth, ubNMonthDays, ubDay (the date's day of the month) and ubWeekday (the\nweekday of the 1st), using GN_Die and GN_Dei.\nEntry: ABC = internal date.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 from GN_Die or GN_Dei.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE."},
        "11851": {"comment":"into zoned format"},
        "11856": {"comment":"remember weekday"},
        "11857": {"comment":"and calc for 1st of month"},
        "11859": {"comment":"into internal format"},
        "11871": {"comment":"into zoned format"},
        "11908": {"synopsis":"Makes a date the Calendar's current day: fills the month variables (InitMonth), stores the\ndate in CurrentDay and redraws the month (DrawMonth) when the date is outside the month\ndrawn.\nEntry: ABC = internal date.\nExit: Fc = 0; E = A.\nError: Fc = 1 from InitMonth; the month variables may be partly updated."},
        "11911": {"comment":"!! ret c"},
        "11927": {"comment":"past drawn month? check next  !! why?"},
        "11931": {"comment":"same month? no redraw"},
        "11945": {"comment":"past next month? redraw"},
        "11949": {"comment":"next month? redraw"},
        "11951": {"comment":"!! or OP_SCF, use operand for mtd_redraw"},
        "11971": {"synopsis":"Draws the month set up by InitMonth.\n1. Clears the window; records the month's first day (DrawnMonthStart, SearchDay) and the\nfirst day of the next month (NextMonthStart); positions the diary list before the month\n(FindPrevDiaryEntry).\n2. Prints the month name (GN_Ldm) and the year (GN_Pdn, at least 4 digits below 100, \" BC\"\nfor a negative year) centred on the first line, and reverses that line.\n3. Prints the short weekday names, Monday first, in tiny underlined type.\n4. Prints the day numbers from the weekday of the 1st, five columns each, with a bullet in\nfront of a day that has a diary entry (DrawMonthDay).\nEntry: none (the month variables).\nKeeps: DE."},
        "11996": {"comment":"BC=ubNMonthDays"},
        "11997": {"comment":"!! ld bc,ubNMonthDays-1; ld c,0"},
        "12030": {"comment":"printh month name"},
        "12041": {"comment":"AD? skip"},
        "12043": {"comment":"DE=-DE"},
        "12050": {"comment":"if year<100 force 4 digits"},
        "12059": {"comment":"width=4"},
        "12061": {"comment":"!! d already 0 from above"},
        "12069": {"comment":"leading space, leading zeroes"},
        "12074": {"comment":"print to screen"},
        "12080": {"comment":"AD? skip"},
        "12094": {"comment":"reverse first line"},
        "12118": {"comment":"seven days, day 1 = MON"},
        "12126": {"comment":"begin banner with a space"},
        "12137": {"comment":"string+spaces=5"},
        "12151": {"comment":"remove last space"},
        "12153": {"comment":"null terminated"},
        "12184": {"comment":"last day done? exit"},
        "12190": {"comment":"wrap E for each week"},
        "12202": {"synopsis":"Square Right in the Calendar: moves to the next day after the current one that has a diary\nentry (FindNextDiaryEntry, MoveToDay) and highlights it; continues in Cal_ALeft's tail.\nNothing moves when there is none.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0."},
        "12210": {"synopsis":"Square Left in the Calendar: moves to the previous day before the current one that has a\ndiary entry (FindPrevDiaryEntry, MoveToDay) and highlights it. Nothing moves when there is\nnone.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0."},
        "12216": {"comment":"no more diary entries? exit"},
        "12236": {"synopsis":"Copies the current day (CurrentDay) to SearchDay, where a diary-entry search starts.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: A, HL."},
        "12249": {"synopsis":"Finds the first diary entry dated after SearchDay. The Diary's entries form an XOR-linked\nlist walked with GN_Xnx (swapping BHL and CDE reverses the direction); the position is kept\nin DiaryEntry (previous) and NextDiaryEntry (current). The search walks backward until an\nentry dated before the search day, then forward until one dated after it. A walk stops at\nthe end of the list or back at OrigDiaryEntry, the entry the Diary passed with the date.\nOZ source name: FindNextDiaryEntry.\nEntry: SearchDay = the day to search from; DiaryEntry, NextDiaryEntry = list position.\nExit: Fc = 0: found; NextDiaryDay = its date; DiaryEntry, NextDiaryEntry = position on it.\nError: Fc = 1 when no later entry exists (the position is stored all the same).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "12256": {"comment":"no more entries? go forward"},
        "12261": {"comment":"before search day? go forward"},
        "12268": {"synopsis":"go forward until past search day"},
        "12272": {"comment":"no more entries? exit"},
        "12277": {"comment":"not past search day? continue"},
        "12279": {"comment":"not search day? found"},
        "12286": {"synopsis":"Finds the last diary entry dated before SearchDay: walks forward until an entry dated on or\nafter the search day, then backward until one dated before it, and turns the position to\nface forward again. Called by DrawMonth (with SearchDay = first day of the drawn month) and\nby Cal_ALeft. The list and its end tests are as in FindNextDiaryEnt.\nOZ source name: FindPrevDiaryEntry.\nEntry: SearchDay = the day to search from; DiaryEntry, NextDiaryEntry = list position.\nExit: Fc = 0: found; NextDiaryDay = its date; DiaryEntry, NextDiaryEntry = position on it.\nError: Fc = 1 when no earlier entry exists (the position is stored all the same).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "12290": {"synopsis":"go forward until past search day","comment":"no more entries? go backward"},
        "12295": {"comment":"past search day? go backward"},
        "12302": {"synopsis":"go bacward until before search day"},
        "12306": {"comment":"no more entries? exit"},
        "12332": {"synopsis":"Stores the diary list position: CDE (the previous entry) in DiaryEntry and BHL (the current\nentry) in NextDiaryEntry.\nEntry: CDE = previous entry; BHL = current entry.\nChanges: A."},
        "12348": {"synopsis":"Fz=1 if BHL is null"},
        "12366": {"synopsis":"Fz=1 if BHL=0 or BHL=OrigDiaryEntry","comment":"swap BHL with CDE"},
        "12372": {"comment":"BHL is null? return"},
        "12373": {"synopsis":"Fz=1 if BHL=OrigDiaryEntry"},
        "12388": {"synopsis":"Steps one entry along the diary list with GN_Xnx and tests for the end of the walk: Fz = 1\nwhen the new entry is null or is OrigDiaryEntry (the test at loc_EDF7).\nEntry: BHL = current entry; CDE = previous entry.\nExit: BHL = next entry; CDE = the entry left; Fz = 1 at the end of the walk.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12394": {"synopsis":"Exit: Fz=1 if match; Fc=1 if NextDiaryDay<SearchDay."},
        "12405": {"comment":"!! unnecessary"},
        "12414": {"comment":"!! unnecessary"},
        "12425": {"synopsis":"Reads the date of the diary entry at BHL, its bytes 3 to 5 read with GN_Rbe, into\nNextDiaryDay (a 3-byte internal date).\nEntry: BHL = diary entry (extended address).\nExit: NextDiaryDay = the entry's date; A = its high byte; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "12452": {"synopsis":"!! can combine these - use signed BC and 'add hl,bc; adc a,c'"},
        "12463": {"synopsis":"Subtracts BC days from CurrentDay, a 3-byte internal date, and falls into SetCurDay, which\nstores the result.\nEntry: BC = number of days.\nExit: CurrentDay = AHL = the new date.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "12481": {"synopsis":"Records D as the selected day of the month (ubDay) and falls into HighlightDay.\nEntry: D = day of the month.\nChanges: AF, D."},
        "12485": {"synopsis":"Shows the selected day (ubDay) in reverse: moves to its cell in the month grid, cell\nubWeekday - 1 + ubDay (MoveToDayXY), turns reverse on, applies it to the cell's 5 characters\nand turns reverse off again.\nEntry: ubDay = day of the month; ubWeekday = cell of the month's first day.\nChanges: AF, D."},
        "12508": {"synopsis":"Removes the highlight from the selected day: moves to its cell, as HighlightDay does, and\napplies the plain attributes (reverse off) to the cell's 5 characters.\nEntry: ubDay = day of the month; ubWeekday = cell of the month's first day.\nChanges: C.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "12528": {"synopsis":"Prints one day cell of the month grid at the cursor: a space, a bullet (BulletR_txt) when\nthe day has a diary entry or a space when not, then the day number in 2 digits with a\ntrailing space (GN_Pdn).\n1. Works out the day's date, DrawnMonthStart + C - 1, and compares it with NextDiaryDay.\n2. While the day is past NextDiaryDay, steps the diary list forward (GN_Xnx, PutDiaryList,\nPutNxtDiaryDay) and compares again; at the end of the list the day gets no bullet.\nEntry: C = day of the month (1 = first); NextDiaryDay and the list position from\nFindPrevDiaryEnt or the previous cell.\nExit: B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE."},
        "12561": {"comment":"below next diary day? skip"},
        "12565": {"comment":"above diary day? update it"},
        "12570": {"comment":"write string to std. output"},
        "12579": {"comment":"follow chain forward"},
        "12589": {"comment":"no error? compare again"},
        "12600": {"comment":"width=2, trailing space"},
        "12605": {"comment":"print number"},
        "12610": {"synopsis":"VDU string SOH, SD_BRGT, 0: the right-pointing bullet DrawMonthDay prints before the number\nof a day that has a diary entry."},
        "12613": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to cell A of the month grid (1 = the top left cell, seven cells a row): row\n2 + (A - 1) div 7, column 5 * ((A - 1) mod 7), through MoveToXYbc.\nEntry: A = cell number.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "12614": {"comment":"start at row 2"},
        "12621": {"comment":"next row"},
        "12624": {"comment":"make it positive"},
        "12626": {"comment":"B=5*A"},
        "12636": {"synopsis":"Text \" BC\", zero-terminated: DrawMonth prints it after the year of a month before year 1."},
        "12640": {"synopsis":"Text \"Look for : \", zero-terminated: the date prompt Cal_Enter prints on row 7."},
        "12652": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that sets up the Calendar's window: defines window 5 at column 42, row 0, 35\ncolumns wide and 8 rows high (SOH 7 #), selects and clears it (SOH 2 C 5) and turns off\nscrolling and the cursor (SOH 3 - S C). Printed by init_calendar with GN_Sop."},
        "12671": {"synopsis":"Alarm popdown: entry point.\n1. Checks the OZ version with OS_Nq (NQ_Voz) and leaves through Exit when it is not this\nOZ's version.\n2. Enables ESC detection (OS_Esc SC_ENA) and suspends alarms while the popdown runs (OS_Alm\nAH_SUSP).\n3. At alm_1: draws window 6 with the \"ALARMS\" title and the column header, and sets up\nwindows 4 and 5.\n4. Clears MailDate and the list state; reads the \"DATE\" mail into MailDate (OS_Sr SR_RPD).\nWithout one it takes today's date (GN_Gmd) and reads a \"NAME\" mail into scratch1; with a\nname it loads alarms from that file (AlmLoadMail, AlmLoad2).\n5. AlmEntry: draws the list (RedrawAlarms) and runs the key loop (KeyJump0 with\nAlmKeyCmds_tbl); RC_Draw starts again at alm_1, anything else falls into AlmExit.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return.","comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "12676": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "12685": {"comment":"disable alarms while in app"},
        "12851": {"comment":"read date"},
        "12853": {"comment":"ok? skip"},
        "12858": {"comment":"get current date"},
        "12872": {"comment":"read filename"},
        "12885": {"comment":"ok? exit"},
        "12889": {"comment":"redraw"},
        "12892": {"synopsis":"Leaves the Alarm popdown: re-enables alarms (OS_Alm AH_REV) and jumps to Exit (OS_Bye).\nReached at the end of the key loop, from the ESC button and with command code $04.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return.","comment":"re-enable alarms"},
        "12902": {"comment":"for the ret"},
        "12906": {"synopsis":"!! only low bits used in ubAlmActiveButton, remove masking"},
        "12917": {"synopsis":"Left arrow in the alarm list: moves the button highlight to the previous of ESC, SET ALARM,\nCLEAR ALARM and VIEW ALARM (the low 2 bits of ubAlmActiveButton), from the first to the\nlast. CLEAR ALARM and VIEW ALARM are refused while no alarm is shown. The shared code at\nalmlr_2 stores the button and redraws the row (AlmHilightButton).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail (KeyJump0 then reads the next key).\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "12928": {"comment":"prevent clr/view alarm if no alarms"},
        "12936": {"comment":"no alarms? exit"},
        "12954": {"synopsis":"Right arrow in the alarm list: moves the button highlight to the next button, from the last\nto the first, and joins Alm_Left's code at almlr_2.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail (KeyJump0 then reads the next key).\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "12968": {"synopsis":"Up arrow in the alarm list: moves the selection bar to the previous alarm.\n1. Inside the window it moves the bar up a row (ubSelectedAlmPos).\n2. On the top row with alarms above, it scrolls the window (SOH SD_UP), redraws the button\nrow, and prints the previous alarm on row 0 (ubTopVisibleAlarm - 1).\n3. On the first alarm it goes to the last: counts the alarms and, with more than five, shows\nthe last five (DrawAlarms) and selects the last row. Does nothing while no alarm is shown.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail (KeyJump0 then reads the next key)."},
        "12972": {"comment":"no alarms? exit"},
        "12981": {"comment":"need scrolling?"},
        "12983": {"comment":"easy, just move up"},
        "12993": {"comment":"we're on first alarm? go to last one"},
        "12997": {"comment":"!! this causes visual bug on last line"},
        "13009": {"comment":"decrement top alarm and print it"},
        "13025": {"comment":"get first alarm"},
        "13028": {"comment":"assume at least 5 alarms, last row"},
        "13033": {"comment":"ld b,0; inc b to re-use inc"},
        "13050": {"comment":"!! cp 6 so 'jr c' is enough"},
        "13073": {"synopsis":"Down arrow in the alarm list: moves the selection bar to the next alarm. Inside the window\nit moves the bar down a row; on the bottom row with an alarm below, it scrolls the window\n(SOH SD_DWN), prints that alarm on row 4 and redraws the button row; on the last alarm it\ngoes to the first, redrawing the list when the first is not shown. Does nothing while no\nalarm is shown.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1, A = RC_Fail (KeyJump0 then reads the next key)."},
        "13077": {"comment":"no alarms? exit"},
        "13091": {"comment":"need scrolling/wrap"},
        "13093": {"comment":"easy, just move down"},
        "13113": {"comment":"no more alarms? go to top"},
        "13141": {"comment":"move to first alarm"},
        "13149": {"comment":"first still visible? skip redraw"},
        "13165": {"synopsis":"CLEAR ALARM: removes the selected alarm (number ubTopVisibleAlarm + ubSelectedAlmPos) from\nthe alarm chain with GN_Uab and frees its block with GN_Fab when GN_Uab took it out (Fc = 0,\nFz = 1), then redraws the list. Returns at once while no alarm is shown.\nEntry: none.\nExit: AF as GN_Uab or GN_Fab left it; Fc = 0, A = 0 when no alarm is shown."},
        "13169": {"comment":"no alarm, ret"},
        "13178": {"comment":"get alarm to remove"},
        "13184": {"comment":"unlink"},
        "13187": {"comment":"failed? don't free"},
        "13189": {"comment":"not removed from queue? don't free"},
        "13191": {"comment":"free"},
        "13200": {"synopsis":"VIEW ALARM: shows the selected alarm in full (ViewSingleAlarm) and falls into PressEsc_txt,\nwhich waits for ESC. Returns at once while no alarm is shown.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as PressEsc_txt; Fc = 0, A = 0 when no alarm is shown."},
        "13204": {"comment":"no alarm, ret"},
        "13213": {"comment":"get alarm to view"},
        "13219": {"synopsis":"Entry inside AlmView, also called after alarms are loaded or saved: prints \"PRESS ESC WHEN\nREADY\" on row 5 and reads keys (OS_In) until ESC, ignoring keys and RC_Susp. ESC is\nacknowledged and the alarm list redrawn (RedrawAlarms). RC_Draw restarts AlmView, whoever\nthe caller was.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = 0 after ESC.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Quit and the like)."},
        "13267": {"comment":"no error? loop"},
        "13271": {"comment":"loop"},
        "13275": {"comment":"redraw"},
        "13280": {"comment":"no ESC? exit"},
        "13282": {"comment":"!! already 1"},
        "13284": {"comment":"ack escape"},
        "13287": {"comment":"!! call nc, ; ret is more clear"},
        "13291": {"synopsis":"SET ALARM: creates a new alarm and lets the user edit it.\n1. Allocates an alarm block (GN_Aab), binds it in segment 1 and clears its 47 bytes.\n2. Fills in the current time (GN_Gmt), the date from MailDate, ALMF_BELL and ALRF_NEVER.\n3. Runs the edit form (AlmSetMain); on success links the block into the alarm chain\n(GN_Lab). When GN_Lab fails with RC_Fail it beeps and returns to the form.\n4. On another error or ESC it frees the block (GN_Fab). Errors other than ESC are reported\n(GN_Err); RC_Quit returns at once, any other case redraws the alarm list.\nEntry: MailDate = the date to start from.\nExit: Fc = 0: the alarm is set.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Esc when the user left with ESC).","comment":"allocate"},
        "13294": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "13299": {"comment":"bind alarm in S1"},
        "13300": {"comment":"clear it"},
        "13310": {"comment":"alm_Time"},
        "13316": {"comment":"get current time"},
        "13350": {"comment":"error? free and exit"},
        "13352": {"comment":"put into chain"},
        "13355": {"comment":"ok, exit"},
        "13362": {"comment":"beep and retry"},
        "13381": {"comment":"error box"},
        "13384": {"comment":"don't bother redraw if quitting"},
        "13394": {"synopsis":"Redraws the alarm list (DrawAlarms) and the selection bar (DrawAlmHilight).\nEntry: ubTopVisibleAlarm, ubSelectedAlmPos."},
        "13400": {"synopsis":"Clears the list window and prints up to five alarms from number ubTopVisibleAlarm, one a\nline (GetAlarmByNum, PrintAlarm, GN_Nln). When that alarm no longer exists it starts again\nfrom the first, setting ubTopVisibleAlarm and ubSelectedAlmPos to 0. Stores the count in\nubNumVisibleAlarms, makes ESC the active button and falls into DrawAlmWdBottom.\nEntry: ubTopVisibleAlarm = number of the alarm on the top row.\nExit: ubNumVisibleAlarms = alarms shown (0 to 5); IX = last alarm block read."},
        "13409": {"comment":"loop counter"},
        "13417": {"comment":"no more above? exit"},
        "13419": {"comment":"go to top"},
        "13433": {"comment":"no more? exit"},
        "13438": {"comment":"newline"},
        "13457": {"synopsis":"Prints the button row on row 5 in tiny text (\"ESC SET ALARM CLEAR ALARM VIEW ALARM\") and\nfalls into AlmHilightButton.\nEntry: ubAlmActiveButton = the active button."},
        "13459": {"comment":"!!start from column 0 with space to fix scroll_up bug"},
        "13525": {"synopsis":"Highlights the active button of the button row: with tiny text on, applies the plain\nattributes to the 54 characters of row 5, then reverse to the 12 characters of the active\nbutton (low 2 bits of ubAlmActiveButton: 0 ESC at column 1, 1 SET ALARM at 14, 2 CLEAR ALARM\nat 27, 3 VIEW ALARM at 40) and turns tiny and reverse off (ToggleTR).\nOZ source name: AlmHighlightButton.\nEntry: ubAlmActiveButton = the active button.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "13541": {"comment":"!! do this with loop, counter in b"},
        "13543": {"comment":"ld a,-13; add a,14; djnz add; ld b,a"},
        "13562": {"synopsis":"Entry inside AlmHilightButton: moves to column B, row C, turns reverse on, applies the\nattributes to 12 characters and turns tiny and reverse off (ToggleTR).\nEntry: B = column; C = row (5); tiny text on.\nChanges: AF."},
        "13576": {"synopsis":"Finds alarm number A (0 = the first) in the alarm chain: starts at the list head pAlarmList\nand steps with GetNextAlarm.\nEntry: A = alarm number.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = the alarm block, bound in segment 1; B = its bank.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Eof when the chain has fewer alarms.\nChanges: AF, B, E, IX."},
        "13587": {"comment":"no more entries"},
        "13594": {"synopsis":"Follows the link of the alarm block at IX (alm_Next, 3 bytes) to the next alarm and binds\nits bank in segment 1.\nEntry: IX = alarm block or the list head pAlarmList.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = the next alarm block; B = its bank.\nError: Fc = 1 at the end of the chain (A = 0).\nChanges: AF, B, IX.\nKeeps: C, HL."},
        "13607": {"comment":"!! ld a,RC_Eof here to save it elsewhere"},
        "13611": {"comment":"return it in IX"},
        "13616": {"comment":"bind it in S1"},
        "13617": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "13621": {"synopsis":"Prints alarm IX on the current line: back to column 0 and clears the line, then the date at\ncolumn 0 (GN_Pdt, short form with century and '/'), the time with seconds at column 15\n(DisplayTime), the reason or command at column 25 and, when ALMF_SHOWBELL is set, a bell\nsymbol (SD_BLL) at column 50.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nChanges: DE, HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC, IX."},
        "13640": {"comment":"century, use C delimeter, zero blanking, trailing space"},
        "13642": {"comment":"short form, '/' delimeter"},
        "13650": {"comment":"print date"},
        "13667": {"comment":"seconds, leading zeroes"},
        "13669": {"comment":"print time"},
        "13686": {"comment":"print reason/command"},
        "13712": {"synopsis":"The alarm edit form: shows the alarm (ViewSingleAlarm) and runs the fields of AlmSet_tbl\nthrough NavigateTable (date, time, reason, bell, type, repeat, number of times); the arrow\nkeys move between fields, wrapping round, and ENTER ends the form.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: Fc = 0 after ENTER.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Esc after ESC)."},
        "13721": {"synopsis":"Shows one alarm in full: clears the window, prints the alarm on row 1 (PrintAlarm), the\nheader \"BELL | ALARM TYPE | REPEAT EVERY | No.OF TIMES\" on row 3 in tiny reverse, and on row\n4 the bell, the type, the repeat interval (GetAlmRepeat, AlmShowRepeat) and the number of\ntimes (AlmShowNTimes).\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in."},
        "13821": {"synopsis":"Date field of the alarm form: edits alm_Date at column 0, row 1 with AskDate.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: as AskDate: A = the key that ended the edit.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "13837": {"synopsis":"Time field of the alarm form: edits alm_Time at column 15, row 1 with AskTime.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: as AskTime: A = the key that ended the edit.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "13853": {"synopsis":"Reason field of the alarm form: edits alm_Reason at column 25, row 1 with GN_Sip (buffer of\n23, returning on special keys) and the cursor shown, until an arrow key or ENTER (TestKeys).\nRC_Susp edits again.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: Fz = 1; A = the key that ended the edit.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "13864": {"comment":"cursor position"},
        "13876": {"comment":"has data, return special"},
        "13885": {"comment":"retry"},
        "13888": {"comment":"else exit"},
        "13893": {"comment":"not movement/return key? retry"},
        "13901": {"synopsis":"Bell field of the alarm form: highlights it (DrawBellHilight); up and down toggle ALMF_BELL\nin alm_Flags and show it (AlmShowBell); an arrow key or ENTER (TestKeys) ends the edit and\nremoves the highlight. RC_Susp reads again.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: Fz = 1; A = the key that ended the edit.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "13917": {"comment":"retry"},
        "13930": {"comment":"toggle bell and loop"},
        "13954": {"synopsis":"Type field of the alarm form: as SetABell, with up and down toggling ALMF_EXECUTE (ALARM or\nEXECUTE, AlmShowType).\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: Fz = 1; A = the key that ended the edit.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "13970": {"comment":"retry"},
        "13983": {"comment":"toggle execute and loop"},
        "13999": {"comment":"retry"},
        "14007": {"synopsis":"Repeat field of the alarm form: edits the repeat interval as a value and a unit.\n1. Highlights the field and gets the value in the current unit (GetAlmRepeat).\n2. Down decrements the value, moving to the previous unit at 0; up increments it, moving to\nthe next unit from NEVER or past 59 seconds or minutes. Shift-down and shift-up change the\nunit (rotating alm_RepeatFlags) and reset the value to 1. Each change is shown\n(AlmShowRepeat).\n3. An arrow key or ENTER stores the value: days, months or years in alm_RepeatDays, weeks as\ndays (times 7), seconds, minutes or hours as centiseconds in alm_RepeatTime; NEVER stores\nnothing. Then removes the highlight.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: A = the key that ended the edit.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (nothing stored)."},
        "14026": {"comment":"retry"},
        "14029": {"comment":"exit"},
        "14036": {"comment":"BHL--"},
        "14047": {"comment":"value >0"},
        "14049": {"comment":"else decrement unit"},
        "14059": {"comment":"increment unit"},
        "14061": {"comment":"BHL++"},
        "14069": {"comment":"limit sec/min to 59"},
        "14072": {"comment":"ALRF_SEC|ALRF_MIN"},
        "14074": {"comment":"neither? skip"},
        "14081": {"comment":"increment unit"},
        "14087": {"comment":"decrement unit"},
        "14097": {"comment":"increment unit"},
        "14101": {"comment":"BHL=1"},
        "14109": {"comment":"show new value and retry"},
        "14117": {"comment":"retry"},
        "14125": {"comment":"exit"},
        "14129": {"comment":"set years"},
        "14133": {"comment":"set months"},
        "14137": {"comment":"set days"},
        "14141": {"comment":"set centiseconds"},
        "14143": {"comment":"multiply by 7 to handle weeks as days"},
        "14158": {"comment":"BHL*=CDE"},
        "14177": {"comment":"BHL*=CDE"},
        "14187": {"comment":"BHL*=CDE"},
        "14210": {"comment":"!! dbf OP_LDAn to skip push below"},
        "14217": {"synopsis":"Returns the alarm's repeat interval in the unit set in alm_RepeatFlags: 1 for NEVER;\nalm_RepeatTime (centiseconds) divided by 100, 6000 or 360000 for seconds, minutes or hours\n(GN_D24); alm_RepeatDays for days, months or years; alm_RepeatDays / 7 for weeks.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: BHL = the interval.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"!! ld hl,1; ld b,h"},
        "14227": {"comment":"never? use 1"},
        "14229": {"comment":"ALRF_SEC|ALRF_MIN|ALRF_HOUR"},
        "14247": {"comment":"seconds"},
        "14261": {"comment":"minutes"},
        "14275": {"comment":"hours"},
        "14292": {"comment":"!! is this unnecessary? only needed if"},
        "14294": {"comment":"!! both day and week can be set simultaneously"},
        "14305": {"comment":"BHL/=7"},
        "14309": {"synopsis":"Number of times field of the alarm form: edits alm_RepeatNum. Down and up change it by 1,\nwith shift by 10 and with diamond by 100, showing each value (AlmShowNTimes); an arrow key\nor ENTER stores it and removes the highlight. RC_Susp reads again.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nExit: A = the key that ended the edit.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (nothing stored)."},
        "14331": {"comment":"retry"},
        "14348": {"comment":"show value and loop"},
        "14393": {"comment":"retry"},
        "14407": {"synopsis":"Prints \"ON\" or \"OFF\" for ALMF_BELL at column 4, row 4, through the code it shares with\nAlmShowType (almt_1).\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "14424": {"synopsis":"Prints \"ALARM\" or \"EXECUTE\" for ALMF_EXECUTE at column 10, row 4.\nEntry: IX = alarm block, bound in.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "14450": {"synopsis":"Prints the repeat interval at column 21, row 4: blanks the 13 characters, prints the value\nin 5 characters (not for NEVER), the unit name from RepeatUnits_tbl for the lowest set bit\nof alm_RepeatFlags, and an 'S' unless the value is 1.\nEntry: HL = the value (16 bits are printed); IX = alarm block, bound in.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "14475": {"comment":"don't show value"},
        "14490": {"comment":"5 chars, trailing space"},
        "14492": {"comment":"print integer"},
        "14497": {"comment":"!! ld hl,tbl-2; inc hl; inc hl to re-use inc"},
        "14510": {"comment":"get string pointer into HL and print"},
        "14522": {"comment":"exit"},
        "14524": {"comment":"add either ' ' or 'S'"},
        "14540": {"synopsis":"Prints the number of times at column 35, row 4: \"NEVER\" for 0, \"FOREVER\" for $FFFF,\notherwise the number in 10 characters.\nEntry: HL = number of times; IX = alarm block, bound in.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "14553": {"comment":"0? Never"},
        "14558": {"comment":"!! ld a,h; and a,l; cpl; jr nz"},
        "14568": {"comment":"-1? forever"},
        "14574": {"comment":"exit"},
        "14589": {"comment":"10 chars, trailing space"},
        "14591": {"comment":"print num"},
        "14598": {"synopsis":"!! draw/remove hilight could be joined"},
        "14604": {"synopsis":"Highlights the type field of the alarm form (column 10, 10 characters) and jumps to\nDrawHilight, which moves to row 4, toggles tiny and reverse (ToggleTR) and applies them to\nthe field. The toggles stay set while the field is edited; RmTypeHilight turns them back.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "14610": {"synopsis":"Highlights the repeat field of the alarm form (column 21, 13 characters) through\nDrawHilight.\nOZ source name: DrawRepeatHilight.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "14616": {"synopsis":"Highlights the number of times field of the alarm form (column 35, 11 characters) and falls\ninto DrawHilight.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "14633": {"synopsis":"Removes the highlight from the bell field of the alarm form (column 4, 5 characters) and\njumps to RemoveHiligh, which moves to row 4, toggles tiny and reverse back (ToggleTR) and\napplies tiny text alone to the field.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "14639": {"synopsis":"Removes the highlight from the type field (column 10, 10 characters) through RemoveHiligh.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "14645": {"synopsis":"Removes the highlight from the repeat field (column 21, 13 characters) through RemoveHiligh.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "14651": {"synopsis":"Removes the highlight from the number of times field (column 35, 11 characters) and falls\ninto RemoveHiligh.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "14674": {"synopsis":"Draws the selection bar on the selected alarm: turns reverse on, applies it to the row\n(RemAlmHilight) and turns reverse off.\nEntry: ubSelectedAlmPos, ubNumVisibleAlarms.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "14686": {"synopsis":"Applies the current attributes to the selected alarm's row (49 characters at column 0),\nwhich removes the selection bar with reverse off. ubSelectedAlmPos is first limited to the\nlast row shown. Does nothing while no alarm is shown.\nEntry: ubSelectedAlmPos, ubNumVisibleAlarms.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "14692": {"comment":"no alarms? exit"},
        "14694": {"comment":"a=min(ubSelectedAlmPos,ubNumVisibleAlarms-1)"},
        "14720": {"synopsis":"LOAD FILE COMMAND"},
        "14763": {"comment":"attempt to open file"},
        "14766": {"comment":"exit if error"},
        "14769": {"comment":"check file signature"},
        "14798": {"comment":"get next alarm block from file"},
        "14800": {"comment":"move on if error"},
        "14802": {"comment":"allocate an alarm block"},
        "14807": {"comment":"save BHL"},
        "14811": {"comment":"bind in block"},
        "14815": {"comment":"mask address to segment 1"},
        "14819": {"comment":"zeroise link"},
        "14832": {"comment":"copy data to alarm block"},
        "14834": {"comment":"restore BHL"},
        "14836": {"comment":"link in (ignore errors if time is past)"},
        "14839": {"comment":"back for more"},
        "14843": {"comment":"exit if not EOF error"},
        "14853": {"comment":"FAIL error if block partially loaded"},
        "14855": {"comment":"close file"},
        "14897": {"synopsis":"Subroutine to get filename"},
        "14898": {"comment":"try to close file"},
        "14905": {"comment":"fatal error"},
        "14912": {"synopsis":"Asks for a file name: selects window 4, clears it, prints \"Filename: \" and reads up to 32\ncharacters into scratch1 (GN_Sip), then selects window 5. RC_Susp asks again; ESC is\nacknowledged; RC_Quit leaves the popdown (Exit); another error is reported by GN_Err\n(do_error), which returns with Fc = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0; scratch1 = the name.\nError: Fc = 1 after ESC."},
        "14936": {"comment":"get input"},
        "14948": {"comment":"exit if no error"},
        "14953": {"comment":"check for ESCape"},
        "14957": {"comment":"check for KILL"},
        "14975": {"synopsis":"SAVE FILE COMMAND","comment":"get first block in BHL"},
        "14978": {"comment":"Fc=1 if list empty"},
        "15020": {"comment":"attempt to create file"},
        "15023": {"comment":"exit if error"},
        "15026": {"comment":"output alarm file signature"},
        "15043": {"comment":"bind bank $20 to segment 1"},
        "15044": {"comment":"get first block in BHL"},
        "15050": {"comment":"exit if no more"},
        "15054": {"comment":"bind in block to segment 1"},
        "15058": {"comment":"mask address to segment 1"},
        "15061": {"comment":"save address"},
        "15071": {"comment":"write alarm block to file"},
        "15082": {"comment":"BHL contains link to next block"},
        "15085": {"comment":"close file"},
        "15127": {"synopsis":"Key table of the alarm list for KeyJump0: entries of a key code byte and a handler word,\nended by 0. Codes $01 to $06 run AlmSet, AlmClear, AlmView, AlmExit, AlmLoad and AlmSave;\nright, left, up, down and ENTER run Alm_Right, Alm_Left, Alm_Up, Alm_Down and Alm_Enter."},
        "15161": {"synopsis":"Field table of the alarm form for NavigateTable: a 0 start mark, the field routines\nSetADate, SetATime, SetAReason, SetABell, SetAType, SetARepeat and SetATimes, and a -1 end\nmark."},
        "15179": {"synopsis":"Table of 8 words: the unit names of the repeat interval, one per bit of alm_RepeatFlags from\nbit 0 (SEC, MIN, HOUR, DAY, WEEK, MONTH, YEAR, NEVER). Read by AlmShowRepeat."},
        "15195": {"synopsis":"Table of 4 words: the handlers of the button row (AlmExit, AlmSet, AlmClear, AlmView),\nindexed by the active button. Alm_Enter jumps through it with TableJump."},
        "15203": {"synopsis":"Text \" ON \", zero-terminated: the bell field when the bell is on (AlmShowBell)."},
        "15209": {"synopsis":"Text \" OFF \", zero-terminated: the bell field when the bell is off (AlmShowBell)."},
        "15215": {"synopsis":"Text \" ALARM \", zero-terminated: the type field of an alarm (AlmShowType)."},
        "15226": {"synopsis":"Text \" EXECUTE \", zero-terminated: the type field of a command (AlmShowType)."},
        "15237": {"synopsis":"Text \" NEVER \", zero-terminated: the number of times 0 (AlmShowNTimes) and the NEVER entry\nof RepeatUnits_tbl."},
        "15249": {"synopsis":"Text \" FOREVER \", zero-terminated: the number of times $FFFF (AlmShowNTimes)."},
        "15261": {"synopsis":"Text \"SEC\", zero-terminated: a unit name of the repeat interval (RepeatUnits_tbl)."},
        "15265": {"synopsis":"Text \"MIN\", zero-terminated: a unit name of the repeat interval (RepeatUnits_tbl)."},
        "15269": {"synopsis":"Text \"HOUR\", zero-terminated: a unit name of the repeat interval (RepeatUnits_tbl)."},
        "15274": {"synopsis":"Text \"DAY\", zero-terminated: a unit name of the repeat interval (RepeatUnits_tbl)."},
        "15278": {"synopsis":"Text \"WEEK\", zero-terminated: a unit name of the repeat interval (RepeatUnits_tbl)."},
        "15283": {"synopsis":"Text \"MONTH\", zero-terminated: a unit name of the repeat interval (RepeatUnits_tbl)."},
        "15289": {"synopsis":"Text \"YEAR\", zero-terminated: a unit name of the repeat interval (RepeatUnits_tbl)."},
        "15294": {"synopsis":"Text \"NAME\", zero-terminated: the name of the mail AlarmEnt reads for a file of alarms to\nload."}
      }
    },
