        "59": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "64": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "202": {"synopsis":"Wraps the edit line when bit 7 of (IY-69) is set and the line has grown past the column's\nwrap width; called from the main loop after a typed character, when OS_Xin returns Fc = 1.\n1. Returns unless L_8397 says the line can be wrapped and L_835B (for the current row) finds\na break point.\n2. When the cursor (IY-87) lies past the break, moves it back by the break's offset, clears\n(IY-88) and records the next row as the new position (L_82A2).\n3. Runs L_BC66 over the line (output at $1DAA), copies the result back to ($1D3D) and starts\na split with L_8320.\n4. Repeatedly cuts the line at the break found by L_8355, stores the first part as a slot\nwith L_823B (type $80 or $81, with format $0C or $0E when bit 6 of (IY-69) is set,\nalternated by bit 1 of (IY-71)), moves the rest to the start of the buffer and pulls words\nfrom the rows below with L_815B.\n5. Finishes at L_81BE: ends line editing (L_B411), adjusts the rows below when the number of\nrows changed ((IY-3) not 0), sets redraw flags and ends through L_8B80.\nEntry: none."},
        "359": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_80BE: pulls words from the following rows onto the end of the text in the\nedit line buffer, one word at a time through L_82B0, putting a space before each word when\nneeded. When the line becomes too wide (L_8355 returns Fc = 1) it continues at L_8101 to\nsplit it again; when the paragraph ends it stores the last line with L_823B and finishes at\nL_81BE. Also used by Format Paragraph (L_826F).\nEntry: DE = end of the text at ($1D3D); (IY-114..-112) = source text pointer and bank, set\nup by L_8323."},
        "583": {"synopsis":"Stores the edit line as a slot: ORs A with (IY-42), gets a slot for the current column at\nrow (IY-11/-10) through L_8CA2, increments the row counters (IY-3), (IY-9/-8) and\n(IY-11/-10), copies the text at ($1D3D) into the slot with L_B493 and clears (IY-42).\nEntry: A = slot type byte; (IY-40) = text length + 1.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: jumps to L_EB07, the error reporter, when L_8CA2 fails."},
        "635": {"synopsis":"Format Paragraph (command code 51, <>R): reflows the paragraph that starts at the cursor's\nslot. When L_8397 says the slot cannot be formatted it moves the cursor down instead\n(L_8E62). Otherwise it stores the edit line (L_B398), sets up the current slot's text as the\nsource with L_8323, refills the lines through L_815B and the splitting code of L_80BE, and\nfalls into L_8296 to move to the row after the paragraph ((IY-9/-8)).\nEntry: none."},
        "674": {"synopsis":"Records column A, row BC as the position to move to, with the row clamped to the last row:\nwhen BC is not below the row count at (IY-97/-96) (L_C9F9), BC becomes that count minus 1.\nFalls into L_82A2.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: (IY-104) = A; (IY-103/-102) = BC; bit 7 of (IY-100) set."},
        "686": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 7 of (IY-100) and falls into L_82A6 to record column A, row BC as the position to\nmove to.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: (IY-104) = A; (IY-103/-102) = BC."},
        "690": {"synopsis":"Stores column A in (IY-104) and row BC in (IY-103/-102), the recorded position to move to.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nChanges: none."},
        "700": {"synopsis":"Takes the next word for L_815B from the source text at (IY-114/-113) in bank (IY-112),\nbinding the bank with L_D887 when it is not (IY-111). When no source text is pending (H = 0)\nit first drops the slot whose text was taken (L_8B61 on row (IY-9/-8), decrementing (IY-3)),\ntoggles bit 1 of (IY-71) and opens the slot on the next row (L_D7AD), which must hold text\nthat continues the paragraph: a type byte with bit 7 set and not $C0 in bits 7-6, format\nbits ($0E) of 0, $0C or $0E, and a first character that is not 0 or a space. It then moves\npast one word and its following spaces with L_83C5.\nEntry: (IY-114..-112) = source pointer and bank; (IY-9/-8) = row.\nExit: Fc = 0; BC = position after the word and its spaces; (IY-114/-113) = that position, or\n0 at the end of the text.\nError: Fc = 1 when the paragraph ends (no next slot, or one that does not continue it)."},
        "812": {"synopsis":"Starts a split with no source text: HL = 0, then falls into L_8323.\nEntry: C = bank byte for (IY-112)."},
        "815": {"synopsis":"Sets up the state for wrapping or formatting: the source text pointer (IY-114/-113) = HL and\nits bank (IY-112) = C, both row variables (IY-11/-10) and (IY-9/-8) = the current row\n(L_D8B5), and (IY-3) and (IY-42) = 0. When the current slot exists and has format bits ($0E\nof its type byte (IX+3)) not 0, falls into L_834C.\nEntry: HL = source text pointer (0 for none); C = its bank.\nExit: Fc = 1 when there is no current slot (L_D7AA); IX = current slot otherwise."},
        "856": {"synopsis":"Toggles bit 1 of (IY-71), which L_80BE uses to alternate a new slot's format between $0E and\n$0C.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "865": {"synopsis":"Finds a break point in the edit line for the row in (IY-11/-10); falls into L_835B.\nEntry: none."},
        "871": {"synopsis":"Finds where the edit line must be broken to fit row BC's column: stores BC in (IY-26/-25),\ngets the width limit for the current column with L_C917 and walks the text at ($1D3D) word\nby word with L_83C5, counting the printing width in C.\nEntry: BC = row.\nExit: Fc = 1, HL = start of the first word that does not fit, when the line is wider than\nthe limit and can be broken after an earlier word; Fc = 0 when it fits or has no break\npoint.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "931": {"synopsis":"Says whether the edit line can be wrapped or formatted. Returns Fc = 0 while an expression\nis being edited (bit 6 of (IY-71)), when L_D249 returns Fc = 1, or when the current slot's\ntype byte (IX+3) has bit 7 clear or format bits ($0E) other than 0, $0C and $0E. Otherwise\n(and when there is no current slot) it checks the text at ($1D3D) at L_83B8.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the text holds a character other than a space; Fc = 0 otherwise.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "977": {"synopsis":"Moves HL over one item of slot text and counts its printing width in C. At a space it skips\nthe run of spaces and returns the next character. At a word it moves to the space or\nterminator after it; highlight codes ($18-$1F, L_CE2A) are not counted, and an '@' field\nthat L_840A recognises is skipped (one holding a 3-byte compiled reference sets bit 5 of\n(IY-42)).\nEntry: HL = text pointer; C = width so far.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = first character after the spaces, or A = $20 with HL at the space ending\nthe word.\nError: Fc = 1 at the end of the text, A = 0 (or $20 after trailing spaces).\nChanges: AF, C, HL."},
        "1046": {"synopsis":"Examines the text after an '@' at HL for L_83C5. A byte $10-$13 after it (L_FE32) marks a\ncompiled reference. Otherwise it tries to read a slot reference with L_BD57 (keeping\n(IY-110..-108)), accepted when an '@' closes it, and then accepts '@T', '@P', '@D' and '@@'.\nEntry: HL = address of the '@'.\nExit: Fc = 1, Fz = 1 for a recognised field, HL at its last character; Fc = 1, Fz = 0 for a\ncompiled reference, HL at the marker byte; Fc = 0 when the '@' starts nothing it knows.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "1121": {"synopsis":"Insert/Overtype (command code 56, <>V): toggles bit 2 of (IY-71), the overtype mode that\nRubout and character insertion test.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "1130": {"synopsis":"Insert Reference (command code 44, <>K): only while an expression is being edited (bit 6 of\n(IY-71)), writes the reference of the slot at the cursor (L_D0E2) into the edit line through\nL_BBBF, with L_84AE set at ($1D4B) as the routine that receives each character.\nEntry: none."},
        "1147": {"synopsis":"Insert Character (command code 37, <>U): inserts a space at the cursor in insert mode (bit 2\nof (IY-71) cleared for the call to L_84E3, then restored) and moves the cursor back onto it\n(L_8E97).\nEntry: none."},
        "1167": {"synopsis":"Underline (command code 85, <>PU): inserts highlight code $18 at the cursor through L_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1171": {"synopsis":"Bold (command code 86, <>PB): inserts highlight code $19 at the cursor through L_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1175": {"synopsis":"Ext. Sequence (command code 87, <>PX): inserts highlight code $1A at the cursor through\nL_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1179": {"synopsis":"Italic (command code 88, <>PI): inserts highlight code $1B at the cursor through L_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1183": {"synopsis":"Subscript (command code 89, <>PL): inserts highlight code $1C at the cursor through L_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1187": {"synopsis":"Superscript (command code 90, <>PR): inserts highlight code $1D at the cursor through\nL_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1191": {"synopsis":"Alt. Font (command code 91, <>PA): inserts highlight code $1E at the cursor through L_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1195": {"synopsis":"User Defined (command code 92, <>PE): inserts highlight code $1F at the cursor through\nL_84AE.\nEntry: none."},
        "1199": {"synopsis":"Insert Highlights (command code 93, <>PHI): stores the edit line (L_B398), asks for the\nhighlight number with L_87BE, reloads the edit line with L_B543 and falls into L_84AE to\ninsert the code $17 + number.\nEntry: none."},
        "1210": {"synopsis":"Inserts character A at the cursor. Called from the main loop with a typed character, from\nthe highlight commands and as the character routine of Insert Reference. Codes below $20 are\nignored while an expression is being edited (bit 6 of (IY-71)). The character goes into the\nedit line at L_84E9 when the current slot accepts text (its type byte (IX+3) has bit 7 set\nand L_C9B8 returns Fc = 0), when there is no slot or an empty one and bit 5 of (IY-69) is\nset, or while an expression is being edited. Otherwise it starts expression editing with\nL_9276, empties the edit line (L_B56E) and tries again.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: (IY-34) = A."},
        "1263": {"synopsis":"Inserts the printable character A at the cursor and moves the cursor right; codes below $20\nreturn at once. Only while a line is edited (L_8690). The line may not grow to (IY-86)\ncharacters: in insert mode (bit 2 of (IY-71) clear) the line length is checked, in overtype\nmode the cursor. A cursor past the end of the line is reached by padding with spaces. In\ninsert mode, or at the end, the rest of the line moves up by one. Falls into\nMthKey_CrsrRight after marking the line changed (L_8687).\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: (IY-34) = A.\nError: Fc = 1 after a beep (L_EFE9) when the line is full."},
        "1342": {"synopsis":"Cursor Right (command code 22): while a line is edited (bit 7 of (IY-72)), moves the cursor\n(IY-87) one place right unless it is at (IY-86); otherwise falls into L_8543 to move to the\nnext column.\nOZ source name: MthKey_CursorRight.\nEntry: none."},
        "1359": {"synopsis":"Next Column (command code 31, TAB): stores the edit line (L_B398) and records move request 3\nthrough L_8E8E ((IY-101) = 3, (IY-100) = 1).\nEntry: none."},
        "1367": {"synopsis":"Add Column (command code 50, <>EAC): stores the edit line (L_B398) and adds a column with\nL_D8CD (a 10-byte column entry of width 12), then flags the redraw (L_879F) and moves to the\nnew last column ((IY-98)) of the current row through L_8D30.\nEntry: none.\nError: jumps to L_EB07 when L_D8CD fails."},
        "1388": {"synopsis":"Start of Slot (command code 15): only while a line is edited (L_8690), puts the cursor\n(IY-87) at 0.\nEntry: none."},
        "1396": {"synopsis":"End of Slot (command code 16): only while a line is edited (L_8690), puts the cursor (IY-87)\nafter the last character of the edit line (L_8572).\nEntry: none."},
        "1406": {"synopsis":"Finds the end of the edit line at ($1D3D).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = address of its terminating 0; B = its length; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "1419": {"synopsis":"Gets the address of the cursor in the edit line: B = (IY-87), then falls into L_8582.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = ($1D3D) + (IY-87); B = (IY-87).\nChanges: B, DE, HL."},
        "1422": {"synopsis":"Gets the address of position B in the edit line at ($1D3D).\nEntry: B = position.\nExit: HL = ($1D3D) + B; DE = B.\nChanges: DE, HL."},
        "1430": {"synopsis":"Rubout (command code 35, DEL): only while a line is edited (L_8690) and the cursor is not at\n0. Moves the cursor (IY-87) one place left and clears (IY-88); in overtype mode (bit 2 of\n(IY-71)) it replaces the character there with a space and marks the line changed, otherwise\nit falls into L_85A7 to delete it.\nEntry: none."},
        "1459": {"synopsis":"Delete Character (command code 36, <>G): only while a line is edited (L_8690), removes the\ncharacter at the cursor by moving the rest of the edit line down one place, and marks the\nline changed (L_8687). Nothing happens at the end of the line.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when a character was removed."},
        "1481": {"synopsis":"Previous Word (command code 27): while a line is edited, moves the cursor to the start of\nthe previous word (to the end of the line when the cursor is past it, or to 0). At position\n0, or when no line is edited, and unless an expression is being edited, moves to the row\nabove: the cursor goes to the end of that slot's text when its type byte is $80 (L_B990,\nL_B53C), to 0 otherwise, and Cursor Up (L_8E81) follows. Nothing happens on row 0.\nEntry: none."},
        "1579": {"synopsis":"Next Word (command code 26): while a line is edited, moves the cursor to the start of the\nnext word (L_8697). At the end of the line, or when no line is edited, and unless an\nexpression is being edited, puts the cursor at 0 (L_8D45) and moves down a row (L_8E62);\nnothing happens on the last row (L_CA1E).\nEntry: none."},
        "1612": {"synopsis":"Delete Word (command code 38, <>T): only while a line is edited (L_8690), removes the text\nfrom the cursor to the start of the next word (L_8697) and marks the line changed (L_8687).\nNothing happens when the cursor is at or past the end of the line.\nEntry: none."},
        "1634": {"synopsis":"Swap Case (command code 53, <>S): only while a line is edited (L_8690), inverts the case of\nthe character at the cursor when GN_Cls classifies it as a letter (InvCase), marks the line\nchanged and moves the cursor right (MthKey_CrsrRight).\nEntry: none."},
        "1642": {"comment":"end of line reached..."},
        "1643": {"comment":"validate type of character"},
        "1646": {"comment":"skip, not classified as an alpha character..."},
        "1648": {"comment":"invert character case"},
        "1655": {"comment":"move cursor one character to the right"},
        "1658": {"synopsis":"Inverts the case of letter A. Codes below 191 have bit 5 flipped without a check; from 191\nup only the ISO letters in InvCaseTable (capitals) and the same codes with bit 5 set (small\nletters) are changed, other codes are returned unchanged.\nEntry: A = letter.\nExit: A = the letter in the other case.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "1662": {"comment":"normal ASCII alpha's can always be case inversed..."},
        "1673": {"comment":"check for upper case -> lower case"},
        "1676": {"comment":"check for lower case -> upper case"},
        "1686": {"comment":"case inverse the allowed ISO character"},
        "1691": {"synopsis":"Table of 9 bytes: the ISO-8859-1 capital letters whose case InvCase inverts (196, 197, 198,\n199, 203, 209, 214, 216, 220); the small letter is the code with bit 5 set."},
        "1724": {"synopsis":"Ends the edit line at HL (writes 0 there), then falls into L_8687 to mark the line changed.\nEntry: HL = address in the edit line.\nChanges: none."},
        "1726": {"synopsis":"Marks the edit line changed: sets bits 0 and 5 of (IY-72). Bit 0 is what L_B3D6 tests before\nit stores the line back into its slot.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "1735": {"synopsis":"Guard at the start of the line-editing commands: returns to its caller while a line is\nedited (bit 7 of (IY-72) set); otherwise it drops the caller's return address, so the caller\nreturns to its own caller and the command does nothing.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: DE when it drops the return address."},
        "1742": {"synopsis":"Finds the start of the word after the cursor: when the cursor (IY-87) is before the end of\nthe edit line, falls into L_86A4 from the cursor's address.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0 as L_86A4 returns.\nError: Fc = 1 when the cursor is at or past the end of the line, B = (IY-87)."},
        "1755": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_8697: moves HL past the rest of the word (or the spaces) at HL and then past\nthe spaces that follow, counting the position in B.\nEntry: HL = address in the edit line; B = its position.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL, B = the first character of the next word, A = that character and Fz = 0;\nor HL, B at the terminator, A = 0 and Fz = 1.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "1782": {"synopsis":"Dialog description read by L_D98A for Microspace Pitch (L_86E1): 1 field, type $87 with the\nprompt \"Microspace printed output\", two words 0 and 255, then the byte $81; a 0 ends the\nlist."},
        "1816": {"synopsis":"Microspace Pitch (command code 84, <>PM): stores the edit line (L_B398) and shows the dialog\nat L_86BF (L_D98A). When it is confirmed, clears bit 4 of (IY-70); when the returned A has\nbit 0 set, sets bit 4 again and puts the dialog's value (IY+51) into (IY+28), 12 when the\nvalue is 0.\nEntry: none."},
        "1849": {"synopsis":"Margin Left (command code 69): decreases the current column's wrap width (L_D551) by one\nwhen it is 3 or more, writes it with L_D76C as the margin byte of the column's entry and of\nthe following columns it reaches, and flags the redraw (L_CA8D).\nEntry: none."},
        "1863": {"synopsis":"Margin Right (command code 70): increases the current column's wrap width (L_D551) by one,\nunless it would wrap to 0, writes it with L_D76C as the margin byte of the column's entry\nand of the following columns it reaches, and flags the redraw (L_CA8D).\nEntry: none."},
        "1880": {"synopsis":"Dialog description read by L_D98A for Width and Set Margin (L_874B, L_8744): 2 fields, a\nnumber field (type $07) \"New width\" with the words 0 and 255 and a byte 0, and type $8A\n\"Specify column\" with the byte $81; a 0 ends the list."},
        "1915": {"synopsis":"Set Margin (command code 66, <>H): stores the edit line (L_B398) and continues in L_874B\nwith C = 1, so the new value goes into the margin byte (+1) of the column's entry.\nEntry: none."},
        "1922": {"synopsis":"Width (command code 65, <>W): stores the edit line (L_B398) and shows the dialog at L_8721\n(L_D98A). The column is the current one, or the value at (IY+53) when the returned A has bit\n0 set (\"Specify column\"). The new value (IY+51) goes into byte 0 (width) of the column's\n10-byte entry at ($1D3F), or byte 1 (margin) when entered at L_8750 with C = 1. A width of 0\nis refused with error $22 (L_EB07) when every other column already has width 0. Ends through\nL_879F.\nEntry: none."},
        "2006": {"synopsis":"Shared exit of the column commands: sets bit 0 of (IY-71) (L_B3C1) and jumps to L_CA85,\nwhich sets bits 7 and 1 of (IY-99).\nEntry: none."},
        "2012": {"synopsis":"Dialog description read by L_D98A for Insert Highlights (L_87BE): 1 field, a number field\n(type $07) \"Highlight number\" with the words 1 and 8 and a byte 0; a 0 ends the list."},
        "2037": {"synopsis":"Asks for a highlight number: stores the edit line (L_B398) and shows the dialog at L_87A5\n(L_D98A).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = (IY+51) + $17, the highlight code $18-$1F.\nError: when the dialog is cancelled, drops its caller's return address and returns to the\ncaller's caller."},
        "2056": {"synopsis":"Default Format (command code 81, <>LDF): applies the format change A = $40, B = 0, C = 0\nthrough L_8852 (via L_8838).\nEntry: none."},
        "2061": {"synopsis":"Sign Brackets (command code 77, <>LSB): applies the format change A = $40, B = $C0, C = $FF\nthrough L_8852 (via L_8838).\nEntry: none."},
        "2066": {"synopsis":"Sign Minus (command code 78, <>LSM): applies the format change A = $40, B = $40, C = $7F\nthrough L_8852 (via L_8838).\nEntry: none."},
        "2071": {"synopsis":"Trailing Characters (command code 80, <>LCT): applies the format change A = 0, B = $10, C =\n$EF through L_8852, which toggles the bit off again when a slot already has it.\nEntry: none."},
        "2076": {"synopsis":"Leading Characters (command code 79, <>LCL): applies the format change A = 0, B = $20, C =\n$DF through L_8852, which toggles the bit off again when a slot already has it.\nEntry: none."},
        "2082": {"synopsis":"Dialog description read by L_D98A for Decimal Places (L_881E): 2 fields, a number field\n(type $07) \"Number of decimal places\" with the words 0 and 9 and a byte 0, and type $84\n\"Floating format\" with the byte $81; a 0 ends the list."},
        "2133": {"synopsis":"Decimal Places (command code 76, <>LDP): stores the edit line (L_B398) and shows the dialog\nat L_87EB (L_D98A). Applies the format change A = $40, C = $B0, B = $40 OR the number of\nplaces (IY+51), or B = $4F when the returned A has bit 0 set (\"Floating format\"), through\nL_8852. Returns when the dialog is cancelled.\nEntry: none."},
        "2163": {"synopsis":"LCR Align (command code 74, <>LLCR): applies the format change A = $C0, B = 8, C = $F1\nthrough L_8852 (via L_884E), setting the alignment field (bits 3-1) of the format byte of\neach slot in the marked block, or of the current slot.\nEntry: none."},
        "2167": {"synopsis":"Left Align (LAL) command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 71): loads B = 2 and joins L_884E, which sets\nA = $C0 and the mask C = $F1 for the shared format routine L_8852. That routine writes\nalignment code 2 into bits 1-3 of the type byte (IX+3) of every slot in the marked block, or\nof the current slot when no block is marked (L_88C6). A slot that already has this alignment\nhas the field cleared instead.\nEntry: none.\nExit: through L_8852 (marks the sheet as changed with L_B3C1)."},
        "2171": {"synopsis":"Centre Align (LAC) command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 72): loads B = 4 and joins L_884E, which\nsets A = $C0 and the mask C = $F1 for the shared format routine L_8852. That routine writes\nalignment code 4 into bits 1-3 of the type byte (IX+3) of every slot in the marked block, or\nof the current slot when no block is marked (L_88C6). A slot that already has this alignment\nhas the field cleared instead.\nEntry: none.\nExit: through L_8852 (marks the sheet as changed with L_B3C1)."},
        "2175": {"synopsis":"Right Align (LAR) command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 70): loads B = 6 and joins L_884E, which\nsets A = $C0 and the mask C = $F1 for the shared format routine L_8852. That routine writes\nalignment code 6 into bits 1-3 of the type byte (IX+3) of every slot in the marked block, or\nof the current slot when no block is marked (L_88C6). A slot that already has this alignment\nhas the field cleared instead.\nEntry: none.\nExit: through L_8852 (marks the sheet as changed with L_B3C1)."},
        "2179": {"synopsis":"Free Align (LAF) command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 74): loads B = 0 and joins L_884E, which sets\nA = $C0 and the mask C = $F1 for the shared format routine L_8852. That routine writes\nalignment code 0 into bits 1-3 of the type byte (IX+3) of every slot in the marked block, or\nof the current slot when no block is marked (L_88C6). A slot that already has this alignment\nhas the field cleared instead.\nEntry: none.\nExit: through L_8852 (marks the sheet as changed with L_B3C1)."},
        "2301": {"synopsis":"Sets the block range used by the block commands. When a block is marked, L_D014 copies the\ntwo marks into the range, ordered: start column, row at (IY-58..-56) and end column, row at\n(IY-55..-53). Otherwise the current slot (L_D0E2) becomes both the start and the end.\nEntry: marks at (IY-67..-65) and (IY-64..-62), bit 7 of a mark's column byte set when unset.\nExit: block range at (IY-58..-53).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "2327": {"synopsis":"Returns at once when bit 6 of A is set (Fz = 0); otherwise falls into L_88E3. Called from\nthe number formatting code (line 17439 of the source).\nEntry: A = format byte; C = format bits.\nExit: as L_88E3 when bit 6 of A is clear.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "2330": {"synopsis":"Merges the default number format into C: sets bit 7 of C unless bit 2 of (IY-69) is set,\nthen ORs C with the default format byte at (IY+9). Used by the format routine L_8852 for a\nslot with no format of its own.\nEntry: C = format bits.\nExit: A = C = merged format byte.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "2344": {"synopsis":"Word Count command (BWC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 10). Counts the words in the text slots of the\nmarked block, or of the whole sheet when no block is marked (L_B2CC with A = 0), and shows\nthe result as \"<n> words\".\n1. Commits any line being edited (L_B398) and starts the block walk (L_FBBD).\n2. For each slot, L_8930 gives the text; each word found by L_86A4 adds 1 to DE.\n3. L_FB93 moves to the next slot of the block; at the end L_EE7C prints DE, OS_Pout prints \"\nwords\" and (IY-84) is set to $0B.\nEntry: none."},
        "2406": {"synopsis":"Looks up the slot at the block walk's position (IY-61..-59) and, when it is a text slot (bit\n7 of its type byte IX+3 set, bits 7 and 6 not both set), points HL at its text (L_B503).\nEntry: (IY-61..-59) = column, row.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = slot; HL = its text; A = type byte.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is no slot there or it is not a text slot.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "2437": {"synopsis":"Fix Column command (LFC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 67). Walks the column list from ($1D5B) with\nL_D0E8 (bit 7 of an entry = fixed, bit 6 = last entry). When any entry is fixed, clears bit\n7 of every entry; otherwise sets bit 7 of the entries from ($1D5B) up to the current\ncolumn's entry ($1D5D). Ends in L_CA85, which requests a redraw.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "2500": {"synopsis":"Fix Row command (LFR, MthKeyJmpTable entry 66). Works on the row list at ($1D61), 6-byte\nentries in which bit 7 of the first byte marks a fixed row and bit 6 the last entry. When\nthe first entry is fixed, notes its row in (IY-26..-25), calls L_D3E9 and clears bit 7 of\nevery entry. Otherwise calls L_D104 and rewrites the entries from ($1D61) up to the current\nrow's entry ($1D63) with bit 7 set. Ends by requesting a redraw (L_CA8D, bit 7 of (IY-23))\nand jumping to L_D45B.\nEntry: none."},
        "2606": {"synopsis":"Clear Mark command (Q, MthKeyJmpTable entry 1), also called after Move and Delete. Unsets\nboth block marks by writing $80 into their column bytes (IY-67) and (IY-64) and requests a\nredraw (L_CA8D).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = $80.\nChanges: AF."},
        "2617": {"synopsis":"Mark Block command (Z, MthKeyJmpTable entry 0). Marks the current slot (L_D0E2): the first\npress sets the first mark (IY-67..-65), the second the second mark (IY-64..-62); a further\npress starts again, setting the first mark and unsetting the second. Requests a redraw\n(L_CA8D).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "2662": {"synopsis":"Delete Row command (Y, MthKeyJmpTable entry 40). Deletes the slot of the current row in\nevery column, 0 to (IY-98) - 1, with L_8B61, then joins L_8A53 with A = $C0: L_B7A5 adjusts\nthe slot references by one row up, OS_Pur is called (L_EB49) and L_A341 marks the sheet\nchanged, recounts the rows and requests a redraw.\nEntry: none."},
        "2686": {"synopsis":"Delete Row in Column command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 39). Deletes the current slot (L_8B61),\nwhich moves the slots below it up a row, then adjusts the references with A = $80 (L_B7A5),\ncalls OS_Pur (L_EB49) and finishes through L_A341.\nEntry: none."},
        "2706": {"synopsis":"Join Lines command (EJL, MthKeyJmpTable entry 42). When the current slot and the slot below\nare both text slots, appends the text of the lower slot to the line in the edit buffer\n($1D3D): L_BB7E converts it, passing each character to L_8A92. The joined line is stored\n(L_B394) and the lower slot deleted (L_8A4E).\nEntry: none.\nError: returns with nothing done when either slot is missing or not text; an error from\nL_BB7E is reported through L_EB07."},
        "2792": {"synopsis":"Gives the position of the slot below the current one: L_D0E2, then BC + 1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = current column; BC = current row + 1; HL = ($1D5D).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "2797": {"synopsis":"Remove Highlights command (PHR, MthKeyJmpTable entry 93): sets Fc and joins L_8ABB, which\nshifts it into bit 7 of (IY-6) so that the highlight pass only removes the chosen highlight\ncode.\nEntry: none."},
        "2800": {"synopsis":"Highlight Block command (PHB, MthKeyJmpTable entry 94). Clears bit 7 of (IY-6), asks for the\nhighlight number (L_87BE, code = number + $17 in (IY-46)) and rebuilds every non-blank text\nslot of the marked block in the buffer $1DAA.\n1. L_9250 requires a marked block; L_FBBD starts the block walk.\n2. Copies the text without the existing highlight codes; in highlight mode, also puts the\ncode before and after each word (L_8B4E). The 4 bytes after a character $10-$13 (L_FE32) are\ncopied unchanged.\n3. Replaces the slot with the buffer (L_B8C7, L_B490) and flags it (L_C9CA); a line that\nwould reach $F5 bytes leaves the slot unchanged.\n4. Marks the sheet changed (L_B3C1) and requests a redraw (L_CA73).\nEntry: none."},
        "2948": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_8B51: loads A with the highlight code (IY-46) and stores it.\nEntry: HL = buffer position; (IY-40) = length so far.\nExit: as L_8B51."},
        "2951": {"synopsis":"Appends A to the highlight buffer: stores it at (HL), advances HL and increments the length\n(IY-40).\nEntry: A = byte; HL = buffer position.\nExit: HL + 1; A kept; Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 when the length has reached $F5.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC."},
        "2967": {"synopsis":"Deletes the slot at column A, row BC: when it exists (L_D797), unlinks it from its column's\nlist (L_BA24, L_BA44, L_B9C6) and frees its memory with OS_Mfr (L_D95E).\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is no slot there."},
        "2998": {"synopsis":"Recounts the sheet's rows: sets the row count (IY-97..-96) to 1 (L_D1E9), then for each\ncolumn 0 to (IY-98) - 1 finds its last row (L_D7A5, L_D788) and raises the count to that row\n+ 1 when it is larger (L_CA0F).\nEntry: none.\nExit: (IY-97..-96) = number of rows."},
        "3024": {"synopsis":"Dialog description read by L_D98A for the Insert Page command (L_8BC0): one field, flags\n$87, the zero-terminated prompt \"Specify no. of unbroken lines\", then the bytes $00, $00,\n$FF $00 and $81 $00."},
        "3062": {"synopsis":"Insert Page command (EIP, MthKeyJmpTable entry 44). Asks for the number of unbroken lines\n(L_8B9A); B = the number entered when bit 0 of the answer is set, else 0. Inserts a slot of\ntype $C0, length 2, in column 0 of the current row (L_8CA2) and stores B at its IX+5, then\njoins L_8C01 with A = 1 to insert a row in the other columns and adjust the references.\nEntry: none.\nError: a failed insert is reported through L_EB07."},
        "3114": {"synopsis":"Insert Row command (N, MthKeyJmpTable entry 46). Inserts a row at the current row in every\ncolumn (L_8C7F from column 0, C = $80: no column skipped), then adjusts the slot references\nby one row down (A = $C0, L_B7B0).\nEntry: none.\nError: a failed insert is reported through L_EB07."},
        "3140": {"synopsis":"Insert Row in Column command (EIRC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 45). Inserts an empty text slot\n(type $80, L_B8B6) at the current slot, pushing the column's slots below down a row\n(L_8CA2), then adjusts the references (A = $80, L_B7B0).\nEntry: none.\nError: a failed insert is reported through L_EB07."},
        "3163": {"synopsis":"Split Line command (ESL, MthKeyJmpTable entry 48). Splits the current text slot at the\ncursor position (IY-87), clamped to the line's length: the part before the cursor stays in\nthe slot (L_B394), the rest goes into a new text slot inserted below it (L_BC66, L_8CA2,\nL_B490). Ends the edit (L_B411) and adjusts the references (L_8C20).\nEntry: none.\nError: refused while an expression is edited (L_B388); returns when the slot is missing or\nnot text; a failed conversion or insert is reported through L_EB07."},
        "3253": {"synopsis":"Inserts a row at row (IY-109..-108) in the columns from A to the last one: in every column\nexcept column C that has a slot at that row (L_D79A), L_8CA5 inserts an empty text slot\n(L_B8B6) there.\nEntry: A = first column; C = column to skip ($80 for none); (IY-109..-108) = row.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 when an insert fails (out of memory)."},
        "3288": {"synopsis":"Inserts a new slot at column A, row BC: stores the position at (IY-110..-108) (L_D77E) and\nfalls into L_8CA5.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row; (IY-42) = type; (IY-40) = length.\nExit: as L_8CA5."},
        "3291": {"synopsis":"Inserts a new slot at the position (IY-110..-108) with L_8CAE and, when that succeeds, marks\nthe sheet changed (L_B3C1).\nEntry: position at (IY-110..-108); (IY-42) = type; (IY-40) = length.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 when the slot cannot be made."},
        "3300": {"synopsis":"Makes a slot at the position (IY-110..-108). When the position is empty, creates it there\n(L_B8C7). Otherwise allocates a new slot (L_D920), raises the row count (L_D788, L_CA0E),\nlinks it into the column's list in front of the slot already there (L_BA73, L_BA44, L_B9A8)\nand initialises it (L_D8F2), so the column's later slots move down a row.\nEntry: position at (IY-110..-108); (IY-42) = type; (IY-40) = length.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 when no memory is left."},
        "3351": {"synopsis":"Last Column command (CLC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 17): moves the cursor to the last column of\nthe current row. A = (IY-98), the number of columns, which L_8D30 reduces to the last column\nbefore setting the target (L_8296).\nEntry: none."},
        "3362": {"synopsis":"First Column command (CFC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 16): moves the cursor to column 0 of the\ncurrent row through L_8D30.\nEntry: none."},
        "3371": {"synopsis":"Dialog description read by L_D98A for the Go to Slot command (L_8D04): one field, flags $02,\nthe zero-terminated prompt \"Go to slot\", then two zero bytes."},
        "3386": {"synopsis":"Go to Slot command (CGS, MthKeyJmpTable entry 13). Asks for a slot (L_8CF5) and moves the\ncursor to the answer's column (IY+56) and row (IY+57..+58) through L_8D30, which keeps the\ncolumn inside the sheet.\nEntry: none.\nError: returns with Fc = 1 when the dialog is cancelled."},
        "3407": {"synopsis":"Bottom of Column command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 33): BC = $7FFF and joins L_8D27, which sets\nbit 5 of (IY-71) and moves to that row of the current column; L_8296 limits it to the last\nrow of the sheet.\nEntry: none."},
        "3415": {"synopsis":"Top of Column command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 31): BC = 0, then L_8D27 sets bit 5 of (IY-71)\nand moves to row 0 of the current column.\nEntry: none."},
        "3451": {"synopsis":"Clears the cursor position bytes (IY-88) and (IY-87). Also the end of the cursor move path\nL_8D30, reached when no expression is edited.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "3459": {"synopsis":"Restore Position command (CRP, MthKeyJmpTable entry 20). Takes the last saved position off\nthe stack of saved positions (count in (IY+99), entries from L_8D7B) and moves the cursor\nthere (L_B4F9, L_8D30). With no saved position, beeps (L_EFE9).\nEntry: none.\nError: Fc = 1 after the beep when no position is saved."},
        "3480": {"synopsis":"Save Position command (CSP, MthKeyJmpTable entry 19). Pushes the current slot's column and\nrow (L_D0E2) onto the stack of saved positions (3 bytes each, L_8D7B) and increments the\ncount (IY+99). With 5 positions saved, beeps (L_EFE9) instead.\nEntry: none.\nError: Fc = 1 after the beep when the stack is full."},
        "3505": {"synopsis":"Points HL at entry (IY+99) of the saved-position stack: IY + $54 + 3 * (IY+99).\nEntry: (IY+99) = entry number.\nExit: HL = entry; BC = 3 * entry number; A = C.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3523": {"synopsis":"Delete Column command (EDC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 41). With more than one column, frees all\nslots of the current column (L_BAC8, L_90FE), moves the column entries after it down by one\n10-byte entry, decrements the column count (IY-98), calls OS_Pur (L_EB49), adjusts the\nreferences (L_B794) and marks the sheet changed (L_B3C1). Falls into L_8DD5.\nEntry: none."},
        "3595": {"synopsis":"Recounts the rows (L_8B80) and requests a full redraw (L_CA7C, L_CA85).\nEntry: none."},
        "3604": {"synopsis":"Insert Column command (EIC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 47). When fewer than $40 columns exist and\nthe current column is inside the sheet, moves the column entries from the current one to\nentry $3F up by one 10-byte entry, initialises the current entry ($0C then 9 zero bytes,\nL_D8D1), adjusts the references (L_B79B) and finishes through L_879F.\nEntry: none.\nError: error 5 is reported through L_EB07 when $40 columns exist."},
        "3664": {"synopsis":"ENTER command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 18). While an expression is edited (bit 6 of (IY-71)),\nstores it in its slot (L_B41A; an error is reported through L_EB07), sets bit 1 of (IY-72)\nand falls into L_8E2A. Otherwise commits the line being edited (L_B398); when the current\nrow is the sheet's last, creates an empty text slot in the row below (L_B8C4) and requests a\nredraw. Then clears the cursor position (L_8D45) and requests a move one row down (L_8E6D).\nEntry: none."},
        "3680": {"synopsis":"ESCAPE command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 53). When an expression is edited (bit 6 of (IY-71)),\nleaves expression editing: clears the bit, ends the line edit (L_B411), requests a redraw\n(L_CA73), clears the cursor position (L_8D45) and calls L_EFD5. Otherwise does nothing.\nEntry: none."},
        "3736": {"synopsis":"Cursor Down command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 23): sets bit 4 of (IY-71) and bit 7 of (IY-68),\nthen requests a move with (IY-100) = 1 and direction (IY-101) = 1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: B = 1; C = 1."},
        "3751": {"synopsis":"Screen Up command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 27): commits any edit (L_B398) and requests a move\nwith (IY-100) = 2 and direction (IY-101) = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: B = 2; C = 0."},
        "3758": {"synopsis":"Screen Down command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 28): commits any edit (L_B398) and requests a move\nwith (IY-100) = 2 and direction (IY-101) = 1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: B = 2; C = 1."},
        "3767": {"synopsis":"Cursor Up command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 24): sets bit 4 of (IY-71) and bit 7 of (IY-68),\nthen requests a move with (IY-100) = 1 and direction (IY-101) = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: B = 1; C = 0."},
        "3789": {"synopsis":"Cursor Left command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 22). While a line is edited (bit 7 of (IY-72)) and\nthe cursor position (IY-87) is not 0, moves the cursor one character left. At position 0\ndoes nothing when bit 5 of (IY-70) or bit 6 of (IY-71) is set; otherwise falls into L_8EB1\nto move to the previous column.\nEntry: none."},
        "3815": {"synopsis":"Previous Column command (MthKeyJmpTable entry 29): commits any edit (L_B398) and requests a\nmove with (IY-100) = 1 and direction (IY-101) = 2.\nEntry: none.\nExit: B = 1; C = 2."},
        "3822": {"synopsis":"Move command (BM, MthKeyJmpTable entry 4). Moves the marked block to the current slot.\n1. L_9209 requires a marked block and gives C = its width - 1; L_9224 refuses (error $23) a\ncurrent column after the block's first and not after its last.\n2. For each block column, L_91B2 sets the target (IY-61..-59) and L_9050 moves that column's\nslots; the block range (IY-58..-53) is kept on the stack around it.\n3. Adjusts the references (L_B7BE with L_B671, offsets from L_919B in (IY-29..-27)), sets\nthe block range to the destination (L_9161), clears the marks (L_89F8) and finishes through\nL_8F92.\nEntry: none."},
        "3945": {"synopsis":"Copy command (BC, MthKeyJmpTable entry 3). Copies the marked block to the current slot.\n1. L_9209 requires a marked block and gives C = its width - 1; L_9224 refuses (error $23) a\ncurrent column after the block's first and not after its last.\n2. For each block column, L_91B2 sets the target (IY-61..-59) and L_8FCD copies that\ncolumn's slots; the block range (IY-58..-53) is kept on the stack around it. A failure ends\nat L_8FBB.\n3. Stores the offsets (L_919B, L_B690), sets the block range to the copy (L_9161), adjusts\nthe references in it (L_B62E, L_B7BE with L_B69A) and finishes through L_8F92.\nEntry: none."},
        "4049": {"synopsis":"Delete command (BD, MthKeyJmpTable entry 5). Requires a marked block (L_9209), moves the\ncursor to its start (L_82A2), deletes its slots column by column (L_908D for (IY-58) up to\n(IY-55)), clears the marks (L_89F8) and finishes through L_8FBB: L_D357, marks the sheet\nchanged (L_B3C1), recounts and redraws (L_8FC1).\nEntry: none."},
        "4087": {"synopsis":"Shared exit of the block commands: recounts the rows and requests a redraw (L_8DD5), then\nfalls into L_8FC4.\nEntry: none."},
        "4090": {"synopsis":"Sets bits 4 and 1 of (IY-72) (L_B3B8) and runs the recalculation pass L_929B twice.\nEntry: none."},
        "4099": {"synopsis":"Copies the block's slots in source column (IY-58), rows (IY-57..-56) to (IY-54..-53), to the\ntarget (IY-61..-59).\n1. L_91DE makes sure a slot exists at the end row; L_9238 finds the start slot.\n2. For each slot: L_9128 copies it to the buffer $1DAA, L_D920 and L_D8F2 make a new slot,\nwhich is linked after the previous copy (L_BA44), and L_913E fills it from the buffer.\n3. After the end row, L_90B6 links the run of copies into the target column.\nEntry: block range at (IY-58..-53); target at (IY-61..-59).\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, the copies made so far freed (L_90FE) and the error reported through L_EB07."},
        "4230": {"synopsis":"Moves the block's slots in source column (IY-58) to the target (IY-61..-59): makes sure a\nslot exists at the block's end row (L_91DE), cuts the run of slots out of the column\n(L_91FD, L_91F1, L_90E0) and links it in at the target (L_90B6). When the target is in the\nsame column below the block, the target row is first reduced by the block's height (L_9183).\nEntry: block range at (IY-58..-53); target at (IY-61..-59).\nError: Fc = 1 after the error is reported through L_EB07."},
        "4291": {"synopsis":"Deletes the block's rows from column (IY-58): cuts the run of slots from the start row to\nthe end row out of the column's list (L_91F1, L_9244, L_91FD, L_90E0), adjusts the\nreferences (L_B7BE with L_B6F7, BC = minus the block's height) and frees the cut slots\n(L_90FE).\nEntry: block range at (IY-58..-53).\nExit: bit 7 of (IY-58) clear again.\nError: Fc = 1, nothing done, when there is no slot at the start (L_9238)."},
        "4332": {"synopsis":"Links a run of slots into a column at the target (IY-61..-59). The run's first slot is in\nthe pointer at (IY+68..+70) and its last in (IY+71..+73). L_BA73 finds the slots before and\nat the target; the links between them are undone and the run is linked in between (L_BA44\ntoggles the XOR links of two slots). Ends in L_B9C6.\nEntry: run in (IY+68..+73); target at (IY-61..-59)."},
        "4374": {"synopsis":"Cuts a run of slots out of a column's list. The pointers at (IY+65..+76) hold the slot\nbefore the run, the run's first slot, its last slot and the slot after it; the links before\nand after the run are undone and the slots on either side linked to each other (L_BA44\ntoggles the XOR links of two slots). Ends in L_B9C6.\nEntry: pointers at (IY+65..+76)."},
        "4404": {"synopsis":"Frees a chain of slots from HL onwards: for each slot, undoes its link to the next one\n(L_BA44), frees its memory with OS_Mfr (L_D95E, size from L_B990) and continues with the\nnext slot until the link is zero.\nEntry: HL, C = address and bank of the first slot, already unlinked from the slot before it.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4446": {"synopsis":"Copies the slot's body to the buffer $1DAA: (IY-42) = its type (L_B0C0), (IY-40) = its\nlength (L_B990, L_B53C), then L_9148 and LDIR.\nEntry: slot at (IY-127..-125).\nExit: (IY-42) = type; (IY-40) = length; DE past the copy in $1DAA.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4468": {"synopsis":"Copies the buffer $1DAA into the body of the slot at (IY-127..-125) (L_B518, L_9148, LDIR).\nEntry: (IY-42) = type; (IY-40) = length.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4478": {"synopsis":"Sets up an LDIR between a slot's body and the buffer $1DAA: HL = IX + 4; BC = (IY-40), plus\n6 when bit 7 of (IY-42) is clear (a slot that is not text has a 6-byte value first); DE =\n$1DAA.\nEntry: IX = slot; (IY-40) = length; (IY-42) = type.\nExit: HL = IX + 4; BC = byte count; DE = $1DAA; A = C.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4503": {"synopsis":"Sets the block range to the destination of a move or copy: start column (IY-58) = (IY-104),\nend column (IY-55) = (IY-61), start row (IY-57..-56) = (IY-60..-59), end row (IY-54..-53) =\nthat row - BC - 1.\nEntry: BC = minus the block's height (L_9183).\nChanges: AF."},
        "4537": {"synopsis":"Returns BC = start row - end row - 1 of the block range, (IY-57..-56) and (IY-54..-53):\nminus the block's height in rows.\nEntry: block range at (IY-58..-53).\nExit: BC = minus the height.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "4553": {"synopsis":"Negates BC: BC = 0 - BC.\nEntry: BC = the value.\nExit: BC = its negative.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "4561": {"synopsis":"Computes how far the scan position, column (iy-61) and row (iy-60)/(iy-59), lies from the\nstart of the working range, column (iy-58) and row (iy-57)/(iy-56).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = the column difference, Fc from that subtraction; BC = the row difference.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "4584": {"synopsis":"Makes sure a slot exists in the cursor's row, B columns right of the cursor's column\n(L_D0E2), and makes that the scan position (iy-61), (iy-60)/(iy-59). L_D797 sets the\nposition and looks the slot up; when there is none, L_B8B6 and L_B8C7 create an empty one.\nWhen B = 0 the position is also recorded through L_82A2.\nEntry: B = the column offset; C = the count the caller keeps.\nExit: Fc = 0; BC as on entry.\nError: when the slot cannot be made, jumps to L_EB07 with the entry BC restored, so C is\ntaken as the message number."},
        "4628": {"synopsis":"Makes sure a slot exists at the working range's first column (iy-58) and last row\n(iy-54)/(iy-53): looks it up with L_9244 and, when there is none, creates an empty one\nthrough L_B8B6 and L_B8C4 (which also set the position (iy-110)-(iy-108)).\nEntry: the working range set.\nExit: Fc = 0: the slot exists or was made.\nError: Fc = 1 from L_B8C4; the callers pass C to L_EB07."},
        "4647": {"synopsis":"Jumps to L_BA73 with the working range's first column and first row: A = (iy-58); BC =\n(iy-57)/(iy-56). L_BA73 sets the position (iy-110)-(iy-108) and stores two 3-byte slot-chain\npointers in (iy+65)-(iy+67) and (iy+68)-(iy+70).\nEntry: the working range set."},
        "4659": {"synopsis":"Reads the two 3-byte slot-chain pointers that the column table holds for the working range's\nfirst column (iy-58) (L_BAC8) and stores them in (iy+71)-(iy+73) (L_BAFB) and\n(iy+74)-(iy+76) (L_BB19).\nEntry: the working range set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4671": {"synopsis":"Starts a block command (Copy, Move, Delete block): takes its own return address off the\nstack, checks that a command may run (L_B398), loads the marked block into the working range\n(L_9250), sets bits 4 and 1 of (iy-72) (L_B3B8) and returns through the saved address.\nBecause the return address is off the stack, the exits of L_B398 and L_9250 that drop a\nreturn address abandon the calling command.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = last column - first column of the block; HL = the return address, also kept in\n($1D4B)."},
        "4697": {"synopsis":"JP (HL): a CALL here calls the routine whose address is in HL.\nEntry: HL = the routine."},
        "4698": {"synopsis":"Checks a Copy or Move target against the block: compares the cursor's column (L_D0E5) with\nthe working range's columns. It returns when that column is at or left of the first column\n(iy-58) or right of the last (iy-55); otherwise it drops the caller's return address and\nreports \"Overlap\" (C = $23) through L_EB07, which abandons the command.\nEntry: the working range set.\nExit: A = the cursor's column.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "4718": {"synopsis":"Makes the working range's first column (iy-58) and first row (iy-57)/(iy-56) the position\n(iy-110)-(iy-108) and looks the slot up there (jumps to L_D797).\nEntry: the working range set.\nExit: Fc = 0: IX = the slot; Fc = 1: there is none."},
        "4730": {"synopsis":"Looks up the slot at the working range's first column (iy-58) and last row (iy-54)/(iy-53)\n(jumps to L_D7AD; the position (iy-110)-(iy-108) is not changed).\nEntry: the working range set.\nExit: Fc = 0: IX = the slot; Fc = 1: there is none."},
        "4742": {"synopsis":"Loads the marked block, (iy-67)-(iy-62) put in order, into the working range (iy-58)-(iy-53)\nthrough L_D014. When no block is marked it reports \"No marked block\" (C = 9) through L_EB07\nand drops its caller's return address, abandoning the caller.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0; the working range set."},
        "4753": {"synopsis":"The Edit Expression command (MTH code 52, <>X): opens the cursor's slot for editing as an\nexpression. Returns at once when L_B398 refuses or an expression is already being edited\n(bit 6 of (iy-71)). Empties the edit line at ($1D3D) (L_B56E); a slot that exists is\nexpanded into it through L_BB7B, but a page break slot (bits 7 and 6 of byte 3 set) ends the\ncommand. Falls into L_9276.\nEntry: none."},
        "4780": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_925B, also called when typing starts an expression: records the cursor's\nposition (L_D0E2) in (iy-107) (column) and (iy-106)/(iy-105) (row), sets bit 6 of (iy-71)\n(an expression is being edited), passes the pointer at ($1D63) to L_CA39, sets the flags of\nL_8687 and L_B569, updates the display (L_EF91) and puts the edit cursor at the start\n(L_8D45).\nEntry: the edit line at ($1D3D) prepared."},
        "4814": {"synopsis":"The Recalculate command (MTH code 13, <>A): returns when L_B398 refuses, otherwise falls\ninto L_929B."},
        "4817": {"synopsis":"Recalculates the sheet. Visits every slot, down each column when bit 4 of (iy-69) is set,\notherwise along each row, through the position (iy-110)-(iy-108), the column stepped by\nL_9313. A slot that is not text (bit 7 of byte 3 clear) is evaluated through L_B575 when bit\n5 of its byte 3 is set or bit 4 of (iy-72) asks for every slot; a slot with bit 5 set then\ngoes through L_C9CA. L_EF34 runs between columns or rows. At the end it clears bits 1 and 4\nof (iy-72) and restores the status (L_EFBB).\nEntry: none."},
        "4937": {"synopsis":"Steps the column (iy-110) on by one.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = the new column; Fc = 1 when it is past the last column (count in (iy-98)).\nChanges: AF."},
        "4948": {"synopsis":"The New command (MTH code 12, <>BNEW): clears the document after asking. Refused with\n\"Editing expression\" (L_B388) while an expression is being edited; asks \"Overwrite text?\"\n(L_98DC) and returns unless the answer is Y; then clears the document (L_98CD), creates the\ndefault columns (L_D749) and sets bit 7 of (iy-99) (L_CA8D).\nEntry: none."},
        "4964": {"synopsis":"Dialog definition for the Name command, read by L_D98A: control bytes and the field text\n\"New name of file\", zero-terminated."},
        "4985": {"synopsis":"The Name command (MTH code 60, <>FC): gives the document a new name. Returns when L_B398\nrefuses or the dialog (NameFilePrompt, L_D98A) is left with Fc = 1. A name that is empty or\nonly spaces (L_DFD3) removes the name: L_A05A, then bit 3 of (iy-71) cleared. Otherwise the\nname at $1FAA becomes the document's (L_ED32), the list file is dropped (L_A05A), the name\nis expanded and given to the Index (L_ED3F) and bit 3 of (iy-71) is set.\nEntry: none."},
        "5028": {"synopsis":"Puts the document's name in the filename buffer at $1FAA (L_ED2A copies it from ($1D75))\nwhen it has one (bit 3 of (iy-71) set); otherwise empties the buffer.\nEntry: none.\nExit: $1FAA = the name or an empty string.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5041": {"synopsis":"Dialog definition for the Load command, read by L_D98A: control bytes and the field texts\n\"Name of file to load\", \"Insert at slot\", \"Limit to range of rows\" and \"Load as plain text\",\neach zero-terminated. The answers come back as bits 0-2 of A."},
        "5129": {"synopsis":"The Load command (MTH code 58, <>FL): loads a document or a list file.\n1. Returns when L_B398 refuses or the dialog (LoadFilePrompt, L_D98A) is left with Fc = 1;\nkeeps the options in (iy-102): bit 0 insert at slot, bit 1 limit rows, bit 2 plain text.\n2. Without insert: asks \"Overwrite text?\" (L_98DC) when the text has changed (bit 0 of\n(iy-71)), makes the typed name the document's (L_ED32), clears the document (L_98CD) and,\nfor plain text, creates the default columns (L_D749). L_9F34 then looks for a list file of\nthat name: when one is read, the first file of the list is loaded (L_A019), otherwise the\nname itself (L_ED2A).\n3. Loads the file (L_9444), reports any error through L_EB07, sets bit 7 of (iy-99) (L_CA8D)\nand falls into L_941C.\nEntry: none."},
        "5202": {"synopsis":"Shared exit of the Load command and the loader: creates the default columns (L_D749) when\nthe sheet has none ((iy-98) = 0).\nEntry: AF = the result to return.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "5212": {"synopsis":"Goes to the first file of the list file: returns Fv = 0 at once when the current file\n(iy-73) is already the first. Otherwise saves the current file if it has changed (L_999B),\nmakes entry 0 current with its name in $1FAA (L_A019) and falls into L_9434.\nEntry: a list file loaded.\nExit: Fv = 0: the file loaded.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "5226": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_9426: restores the current list entry's start values (L_9CB6) and falls into\nL_9437.\nEntry: (iy-73) = the list entry; its name in $1FAA."},
        "5229": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_9426: loads the file named at $1FAA in place of the current one. Frees the\noptions list and the slots (L_98D6), resets the sheet's variables (L_D6D9), puts the current\nlist entry's name in $1FAA (L_A01D), clears the load options (iy-102) and falls into L_9444.\nThe list file stays loaded.\nEntry: (iy-73) = the list entry.\nExit: Fv = 0: loaded.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "5242": {"synopsis":"Loads the file named at $1FAA with the options in (iy-102) (bit 0 insert at slot, bit 1\nlimit rows, bit 2 plain text).\n1. Clears the row counter (iy+3)/(iy+4). Starts at column 0, row 0, or when inserting at the\nslot in (iy+56), (iy+57)/(iy+58), which also becomes the working range (L_985D).\n2. Opens the file for input with GN_Opf. \"File not found\" (C = $14) when RC_Onf, any other\nerror through L_9FFF. Unless inserting, the expanded name becomes the document's (L_ED32).\nThe handle is kept at ($1D57).\n3. Reads each line into the buffer at ($1D3D) through L_9D78, up to $F3 bytes; CR, LF and\nthe pairs CR LF and LF CR end a line. In plain text a TAB ends a slot and the next slot goes\none column right. Otherwise every \"%code%\" is looked up (L_973C) and either changes the\nslot's type and format in (iy-43)/(iy-44), runs a handler from L_97CE, or stays as text.\n4. Stores each slot with L_967B and moves on (next column after a TAB in plain text,\notherwise the next row).\n5. At the end restores the status, frees the file buffer (L_9E30), recalculates (L_8FC1) and\ncloses the file (L_9FE2). A whole load clears the changed flag (bit 0 of (iy-71)), sets the\nnamed flag (bit 3), gives the name to the Index (L_ED3F) and resets the position (L_82A2);\nan insert sets the changed flag. A failed whole load drops the list file and the Index name\n(L_A05A).\nEntry: $1FAA = the name; (iy-102) = the options.\nExit: Fv = 0: loaded.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "5700": {"synopsis":"A RET. The Next Option command (MTH code 55, <>J) uses it as its handler, so it does nothing\nin the sheet; L_967B passes its address to L_B78D as a handler that does nothing. It is also\nthe end of L_9444."},
        "5809": {"synopsis":"Stores the slot the loader has read (text at ($1D3D), type (iy-43), format (iy-44)) at the\nposition (iy-110)-(iy-108).\n1. A pending option line ((iy-9) not 0, set by L_98BC) goes to the options list at $1D43\ninstead (L_960F; not when inserting).\n2. With the row limit (bit 1 of (iy-102)) the row counter (iy+3)/(iy+4) is stepped and rows\noutside (iy+51)/(iy+52) to (iy+54)/(iy+55) are skipped.\n3. Converts the text through L_BC66 unless it is a page break; stores the length in (iy-40)\nand the type in (iy-42).\n4. Inserting: stores it through L_8CAE and sets the changed flag (L_B3C1); otherwise creates\nthe slot (L_B8C7), an empty one being skipped. A page break keeps its number in byte 5,\nother slots get their text (L_B490), and a slot that is not text its format in byte 9. When\ninserting, it then calls L_B7BE (A = 0, BC = 1, L_960E given to L_B78D) with the last column\nand row of the working range set to the position. When storing fails and the file buffer can\nbe given back ((iy-5) not 0), frees it (L_9E30) and tries again.\nEntry: the slot read; the position set.\nExit: Fc = 0: stored or skipped.\nError: Fc = 1."},
        "6002": {"synopsis":"Looks up the format code that the loader found between two '%' signs in the table L_977B.\nThe code starts after the '%' at (iy-52)/(iy-51); codes need (iy-4) >= 3 (at least one\ncharacter). A table name matches when its letters match and the next character is not a\nletter (ValidateAlphabetic).\nEntry: (iy-52)/(iy-51) = the '%'; (iy-4) = the count.\nExit: Fc = 0: IX = the last letter of the matching entry, (IX+1)-(IX+3) its action; HL = the\ncharacter after the code.\nError: Fc = 1: no match.\nChanges: AF, HL, IX."},
        "6065": {"synopsis":"Table of the format codes that the loader (L_973C) understands between '%' signs. Each entry\nis the code's letters, the last with bit 7 set, then three bytes: an action and an AND and\nan OR mask. An action with bit 7 set is an offset into L_97CE (a handler); otherwise it is\nthe offset from (iy-44) of the byte that is ANDed and ORed with the masks (offset 1, the\nslot type; 0, the format). Codes: V, JL, JR, L, R, C, LCR, P, CO, H, D, B, LC, TC, F, OP, PC\nand DF. A zero byte ends it."},
        "6148": {"synopsis":"Table of 5 words: the handlers of the load codes with an action byte, at offsets 0-8: L_97D8\n(CO), L_9878 (H), L_989F (D), L_98BC (OP) and L_9874 (PC)."},
        "6158": {"synopsis":"Load handler of \"%CO:col,width,margin%\": selects the column the next slots go to. Reads the\ncolumn letters (L_BD91) into (iy-110). Without insert: makes sure the column exists (L_D8BF)\nand stores the width and the margin, when given (GN_Gdn through L_EE29), in its column table\nentry (L_984D); the row restarts at 0. When inserting, columns are placed relative to the\ninsert column, the first CO setting the base in (iy+56); a column past 63 gives \"Edge\" (C =\n$1D). Clears the row counter (iy+3)/(iy+4).\nEntry: HL = the ':' after CO.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: done; Fv = 0, Fc = 1: not valid, the code stays as text.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "6275": {"synopsis":"Points HL at the column table entry of the load column (iy-110) (L_D890).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = the entry.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "6291": {"synopsis":"Makes the working range one slot: first and last column A, first and last row BC. The first\ncolumn (iy-58) is stored with bit 7 set.\nEntry: A = the column; BC = the row.\nExit: A = the column without bit 7.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6314": {"synopsis":"Load handler of \"%PC%\": puts a '%' character into the slot text at the code's place (the\npointer (iy-52)/(iy-51), stepped on).\nEntry: (iy-52)/(iy-51) = the '%' that opened the code.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0."},
        "6318": {"synopsis":"Load handler of \"%Hn%\": puts highlight code n (1-9) into the slot text as the character $17\n+ n at the code's place (shares L_988C with L_9874). Reads n with GN_Gdn (L_EE29).\nEntry: HL = the text after H.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: done; Fv = 0, Fc = 1: no number or not 1-9, the code stays as text."},
        "6357": {"synopsis":"Load handler of \"%Dn%\": sets the slot's decimal places to n (0-10): (iy-44) keeps bits 7, 5\nand 4, takes n in bits 0-3 and sets bit 6.\nEntry: HL = the text after D.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: done; Fv = 0, Fc = 1: no number or above 10, the code stays as text."},
        "6386": {"synopsis":"Load handler of \"%OP%\": marks the line as an options line by pointing (iy-10)/(iy-9) at the\ncharacter after the code's '%'; L_967B then stores it in the options list.\nEntry: (iy-52)/(iy-51) = the '%' that opened the code.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0."},
        "6403": {"synopsis":"Clears the document: drops the list file and the Index name (L_A05A), frees the options list\nand the slots (L_98D6) and resets the sheet's variables (jumps to L_D6CB).\nEntry: none."},
        "6412": {"synopsis":"Frees the options list at $1D43 (L_A072) and the slots of every column (jumps to L_A093).\nEntry: none."},
        "6418": {"synopsis":"Asks \"Overwrite text?\" on the message line (L_B2C2, OS_Pout) and reads the answer (L_E006),\nthen clears the line (L_EFD5).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fz = 1: the answer is Y or y; Fz = 0: anything else, or Fc = 1 from L_E006."},
        "6458": {"synopsis":"Dialog definition for the Save command, read by L_D98A: control bytes and the field texts\n\"Name of file to save\", \"Save only range of columns\", \"Save selection of rows\", \"Save marked\nblock\" and \"Save plain text\", each zero-terminated. The answers come back as bits of A (bit\n0 columns, bit 1 rows, bit 2 plain text, bit 3 marked block)."},
        "6575": {"synopsis":"Unless bit 3 (marked block) of the save or search options in A is set, sets bit 6, so that\nL_B2CC takes the whole sheet instead of the marked block.\nEntry: A = the options.\nExit: A = the options.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6581": {"synopsis":"The Save command (MTH code 59, <>FS): returns when L_B398 refuses. Offers the document's\nname (L_936E), or the current list entry's when a list file is loaded (L_A01D), in the\ndialog (SaveFilePrompt, L_D98A), returns when it is left with Fc = 1, then saves through\nL_99AF and reports any error through L_EB07.\nEntry: none."},
        "6608": {"synopsis":"Saves the current file before another is loaded. Puts the current list entry's name in $1FAA\n(L_A01D). Returns Fv = 0 when the text has not changed (bit 0 of (iy-71) clear), \"No name\nfor save\" (C = $1C) when the document has none (bit 3 of (iy-71) clear); otherwise saves the\nwhole document (A = 0, falls into L_99AF).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fv = 0: saved or nothing to save.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "6628": {"synopsis":"Saves the document to the file named at $1FAA with the options in A (bit 0 range of columns,\nbit 1 selection of rows, bit 2 plain text, bit 3 marked block).\n1. Sets the working range (L_997A, L_B2CC): the marked block (bit 7 then set) or the whole\nsheet, limited to (iy+53)-(iy+54) for bit 0; keeps the options in (iy-102). Asking for the\nmarked block when there is none gives \"No marked block\" (C = 9).\n2. Opens the file for output with GN_Opf (errors through L_9FFF); the handle goes to\n($1D57).\n3. Unless saving a block or plain text, writes each option of the options list as a line\n\"%OP%\" + its text (L_9CDF, L_9CE4).\n4. For each column, unless plain text, writes \"%CO:col,width,margin%\". Then writes the slots\n(L_9B06) row by row, honouring the row selection (L_B30E): in plain text across the columns\nwith TABs between them and CR at the end of a row; otherwise down the column, a CR after\neach slot, until a row without a slot.\n5. Flushes the buffer (L_9EC5), frees it (L_9E30), restores the status and closes the file\n(L_9FE2). A whole save clears the changed flag (bit 0 of (iy-71)).\nEntry: A = the options; $1FAA = the name.\nExit: Fv = 0: saved.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "6971": {"synopsis":"Writes slot IX to the save file. A page break (bits 7 and 6 of byte 3 set) is \"%Pn%\" with n\nfrom byte 5, nothing in plain text. Unless plain text, a slot that is not text starts with\n\"%V%\", and the alignment in bits 1-3 of byte 3 is written as its code from L_9BD0. A slot\nthat is not text then gets the format codes from byte 9: \"%B%\", \"%LC%\", \"%TC%\", and \"%Dn%\"\nor \"%DF%\" when bit 6 is set. Last, the contents are expanded through L_BB7E with L_9BE2\nwriting each character ('%' as \"%PC%\" unless plain text).\nEntry: IX = the slot; (iy-102) = the save options.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7141": {"synopsis":"Writes the two-letter format code C followed by 'C' (\"%LC%\", \"%TC%\") when the slot's format\nbyte (IX+9) has a bit of mask A set (shares the rest of L_9BB4).\nEntry: A = the mask; C = the first letter; IX = the slot.\nExit: Fv = 0: written or not needed.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error).\nKeeps: IX."},
        "7145": {"synopsis":"Writes the one-letter format code C (\"%B%\") when the slot's format byte (IX+9) has a bit of\nmask A set: puts the code into the code buffer (L_9CCB) and writes it (L_9D00).\nEntry: A = the mask; C = the letter; IX = the slot.\nExit: Fv = 0: written or not needed.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error).\nKeeps: IX."},
        "7164": {"synopsis":"Reads byte A of the alignment table L_9BD0.\nEntry: A = the index.\nExit: A = the byte; HL = its address.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "7173": {"synopsis":"Table of 18 bytes for the alignment codes. The first 8 bytes give, for each alignment 0-7\n(bits 1-3 of a slot's byte 3), the offset in this table of its letters, 0 for none (0 and\n5). The letters follow, the last of each code with bit 7 set: L, C, R, LCR, JL, JR."},
        "7234": {"synopsis":"The Bottom File command (MTH code 64, <>FB): goes to the last file of the list file one file\nat a time (L_9C4F) while L_A004 finds a next one. Returns when L_B398 refuses; without a\nlist file reports \"No list file\" (L_9C60).\nEntry: none."},
        "7250": {"synopsis":"The Previous File command (MTH code 62, <>FP): loads the file before the current one in the\nlist file. Returns when L_B398 refuses; \"No list file\" without one (L_9C60), \"End of list\"\n(L_A00A, C = $1B) at the first file. Saves the current file if it has changed (L_999B),\nmakes the previous entry current (iy-73) and loads it (L_9434); errors go to L_EB07.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0 when loaded."},
        "7281": {"synopsis":"The Top File command (MTH code 63, <>FT): goes to the first file of the list file (L_9426).\nReturns when L_B398 refuses; \"No list file\" without one (L_9C60); errors go to L_EB07.\nEntry: none."},
        "7294": {"synopsis":"The Next File command (MTH code 61, <>FN): returns when L_B398 refuses; \"No list file\"\nwithout one (L_9C60); then falls into L_9C4F.\nEntry: none."},
        "7300": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_9C49, also used by L_9C0D: goes to the next file of the list file (L_9C6B,\nwhich gives \"End of list\" after the last) and loads it (L_9437). Errors go to L_EB07.\nEntry: a list file loaded.\nExit: Fc = 0 when loaded."},
        "7317": {"synopsis":"Checks that a list file is loaded (bit 3 of (iy-70)). When not, drops the caller's return\naddress and reports \"No list file\" (C = $1A) through L_EB07, abandoning the command.\nEntry: none."},
        "7328": {"synopsis":"Prepares the move to the next file of the list file.\n1. Stores the current file's start values (iy+12), (iy+10)/(iy+11) in its list entry\n(L_A03C).\n2. Finds the next entry (L_A004); without one returns Fc = 1 with C = $1B (\"End of list\").\n3. Saves the current file if it has changed (L_999B).\n4. Makes the next entry current in (iy-73), with its name in $1FAA.\n5. Works out the next file's start values through L_D3F0 and L_D35D: (iy+12) from (iy-94)\nand (iy+10)/(iy+11) from (iy-93)/(iy-92); 0 and one less when L_D35D returns Fc = 1.\nEntry: a list file loaded.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: the next entry is current.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = the message number (0: an OZ error); or Fv = 0, Fc = 1 at the end of\nthe list."},
        "7403": {"synopsis":"Restores the current file's start values (iy+12), (iy+10) and (iy+11) from the first three\nbytes of its entry ((iy-73)) in the list at $1D41 (L_EA7C).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "7424": {"synopsis":"Puts a format code of one or two letters into the code buffer at (iy+35): C, then B when B\nis not 0; the length goes to (iy-74).\nEntry: C = the first letter; B = the second, or 0.\nExit: C = the length (1 or 2).\nChanges: F, C.\nKeeps: A, B."},
        "7441": {"synopsis":"Writes the one-letter format code A as \"%A%\" (C = A, B = 0, falls into L_9CDF).\nEntry: A = the letter.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7444": {"synopsis":"Writes the format code of letters C and B (B = 0 for one letter) between '%' signs: puts it\ninto the code buffer (L_9CCB) and writes it (L_9D00).\nEntry: C, B = the letters.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7449": {"synopsis":"Writes character A of a slot's contents to the save file. A highlight code ($18-$1F, L_CE2A)\nbecomes \"%Hn%\" with n = A - $17, or nothing in plain text (bit 2 of (iy-102)); any other\ncharacter goes to L_9D1A.\nEntry: A = the character.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7466": {"synopsis":"Writes the format code letter A followed by the decimal number C between '%' signs (\"%Pn%\",\n\"%Dn%\", \"%Hn%\"): puts A into the code buffer at (iy+35), appends the digits of C (L_EE88)\nand falls into L_9D00.\nEntry: A = the letter; C = the number.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7477": {"synopsis":"Writes the code in the code buffer at (iy+35), (iy-74) characters, between two '%' signs\n(L_9D18, L_9D1A).\nEntry: the code buffer filled.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7501": {"synopsis":"Writes a '%' to the save file: A = $25, falls into L_9D1A.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7503": {"synopsis":"Writes character A to the save file through its buffer. In plain text (bit 2 of (iy-102)) a\nTAB is not written at once but counted in (iy+5); the counted TABs are written before the\nnext character that is not a CR, and a CR drops them, so a line carries no trailing TABs.\nThe buffer at (iy-104)/(iy-103) is filled through (iy-12)/(iy-11), with (iy-8)/(iy-7) bytes\nfree, and written out with OS_Mv (L_9EC5) when full.\nEntry: A = the character.\nExit: Fv = 0: written.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE); C = the PipeDream message number (0: an OZ error)."},
        "7549": {"synopsis":"Writes the byte in A to the file buffer. When no buffer is set up yet ((iy-103) = 0) it sets\none up with L_9E84; when the buffer is full (count (iy-8/-7) = 0) it first writes it to the\nfile with L_9EC5. Then it stores A at the buffer pointer (iy-12/-11), advances the pointer\nand counts the byte off (iy-8/-7).\nEntry: A = byte to write.\nExit: Fv = 0; A kept.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = message number (0: OZ error code in A), from the buffer write.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "7597": {"synopsis":"Reads the next byte from the file buffer. When no buffer is set up ((iy-103) = 0) or its\ncount (iy-8/-7) is 0, it refills it from the file with L_9DAB. It reads the byte at the\npointer (iy-12/-11), advances the pointer and counts the byte off.\nEntry: ($1D57) = file handle.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: A = byte, Fz = 1 when it is 0; Fv = 0, Fc = 1: end of file.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = message number (0: OZ error code in A).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "7648": {"synopsis":"Refills the file buffer from the file ($1D57). It sets up a buffer with L_9E84 (a quarter of\nthe free memory) when there is none, adds the bytes used to the file position (iy-2..+1)\nwith L_9E53, and moves the file pointer to that position with OS_Fwm (FA_PTR) when OS_Frm\nreports a different one. It then reads up to the buffer size (iy-14/-13) with OS_Mv into the\nbuffer (iy-104/-103), resets the pointer (iy-12/-11) and sets the count (iy-8/-7) to the\nbytes read. An end of file during the read is kept in bit 7 of (iy-6); when the position is\nunchanged and that bit is set, it returns at once.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: buffer refilled; Fv = 0, Fc = 1: end of file, nothing read.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = message number (0: OZ error code in A).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "7781": {"synopsis":"Releases the file buffer when it was allocated with OS_Mal (bit 0 of (iy-5) set). It adds\nthe bytes used to the file position with L_9E53, clears (iy-103) and (iy-5) and jumps to\nL_D976 to free the memory. L_D976 frees the block addressed by (iy-117/-116), so the buffer\naddress loaded into HL here is not used.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "7816": {"synopsis":"Adds the bytes used in the file buffer (L_9E75) to the 32-bit file position at (iy-2),\n(iy-1), (iy+0), (iy+1).\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = 0; HL = high word of the new position.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "7850": {"synopsis":"Works out how many bytes of the file buffer are used: the pointer (iy-12/-11) minus the\nstart (iy-104/-103).\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = bytes used.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "7865": {"synopsis":"Sets up the file buffer. It asks OS_Nq NQ_Mfs for the free memory and takes DE as the size,\na quarter of it (D shifted right twice) when Fc = 1 on entry. When the high byte is not 0 it\nallocates that size with L_D96E (OS_Mal) and sets bit 0 of (iy-5); otherwise it uses the\n256-byte area at $1EAA and clears (iy-5). It stores the size in (iy-14/-13) and the start in\n(iy-104/-103) and the pointer (iy-12/-11).\nEntry: Fc = 1 to use a quarter of the free memory.\nExit: HL = buffer start.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "7930": {"synopsis":"Writes the used part of the file buffer to the file ($1D57) with OS_Mv and resets the buffer\npointer (iy-12/-11) to the start (iy-104/-103). The count (iy-8/-7) and the file position\nare not changed.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = message number (0: OZ error code in A).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "7964": {"synopsis":"Resets the file state before a file is opened: clears the flags (iy-6) and (iy-5), the file\nposition (iy-2..+1), the buffer start's high byte (iy-103), the count (iy+5) and the file\nhandle ($1D57).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7996": {"synopsis":"Reads one line from the file with OS_Gb into the buffer at $1DAA. A CR or a 0 ends the line\nand is stored as 0.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: line read, C = its length with the terminator, HL = its 0 Fv = 0, Fc =\n1: end of file; HL = the byte after the last one stored.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = message number (0: OZ error code in A); C = $18 when the line\nreaches 50 bytes.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL."},
        "8041": {"synopsis":"Loads the list of files that goes with the file name at ($1D75). It frees the old list\n(L_A05A) and copies the name to $1FAA (L_ED2A). When the name's extension is the single\nletter L, or the name with the extension \"l\" (L_9FE0) does not exist, it returns Fc = 1.\nOtherwise it opens that file (GN_Opf) and reads it line by line (L_9F07), adding each line\nas an entry of the list at $1D41 (L_EA9C) numbered from 0 in (iy+13). It sets bit 3 of\n(iy-70) (list loaded) and closes the file through L_9FE6.\nEntry: ($1D75) = file name.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 1: no list file; Fv = 0, Fc = 0: list loaded.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = message number (0: OZ error code in A); C = $18 when the last line\nhas no end.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "8047": {"comment":"read filename extension"},
        "8080": {"comment":"write filename extension"},
        "8116": {"comment":"file not found..."},
        "8213": {"synopsis":"The file name extension of a list file: \"l\" and a 0, written by L_9F34 with GN_Esa."},
        "8215": {"synopsis":"Closes the file whose handle is in ($1D57) with GN_Cl. L_9FE6 is the entry for a handle\nalready in IX. Nothing is closed when the handle is 0.\nEntry: none (L_9FE6: IX = handle).\nExit: AF and BC as on entry.\nError: Fv = 1 and C = 0 when GN_Cl fails, A and the other flags as on entry.\nChanges: IX."},
        "8244": {"synopsis":"Shared error exit for an OZ error: sets C = 0 and Fv = 1 through L_F9B7, keeping the OZ\nerror code in A.\nEntry: A = OZ error code.\nExit: Fv = 1, C = 0.\nChanges: F, C."},
        "8249": {"synopsis":"Looks up the next entry of the file list ((iy-73) + 1) through L_A020 and copies its name to\n$1FAA. (iy-73) is not changed.\nEntry: (iy-73) = current entry.\nExit: Fc = 1: A = the next entry's number, name at $1FAA Fc = 0: no such entry, C = $1B.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8255": {"synopsis":"Looks up the previous entry of the file list ((iy-73) - 1) through L_A020 and copies its\nname to $1FAA; returns Fc = 0, C = $1B at once when the current entry is 0. (iy-73) is not\nchanged.\nEntry: (iy-73) = current entry.\nExit: Fc = 1: A = the previous entry's number, name at $1FAA Fc = 0: no such entry, C = $1B.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8270": {"synopsis":"Makes entry 0 the current entry of the file list ((iy-73) = 0); falls into L_A01D.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_A020.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8274": {"synopsis":"Copies the name of the current entry of the file list ((iy-73)) to $1FAA; falls into L_A020.\nEntry: (iy-73) = current entry.\nExit: as L_A020.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8277": {"synopsis":"Finds entry C of the file list at $1D41 (L_EA7C) and copies its name, from the entry's\noffset 8, to $1FAA.\nEntry: C = entry number.\nExit: Fc = 1: name copied Fc = 0: no such entry, C = $1B.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8305": {"synopsis":"Stores (iy+12), (iy+10) and (iy+11) in the three bytes at offset 5 of the current entry of\nthe file list ((iy-73)). It does not check that the entry exists.\nEntry: (iy-73) = current entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8326": {"synopsis":"Loads C with the current entry of the file list ((iy-73)); falls into L_A054.\nEntry: none.\nExit: C = (iy-73); B = 0; HL = $1D41.\nChanges: BC, HL."},
        "8329": {"synopsis":"Sets B = 0 and HL = $1D41, the head of the file list.\nEntry: none.\nExit: B = 0; HL = $1D41.\nChanges: B, HL."},
        "8335": {"synopsis":"Frees the file list. It clears bit 3 of (iy-70) (list loaded), sets the application name to\nan empty one with DC_Nam, and when the list at ($1D41) is not empty clears ($1D42) and frees\nits entries one by one with L_D976 (L_A07C), each entry holding the next one's address in\nits first word and its size at offset 2.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8359": {"synopsis":"Frees the list whose head is at ($1D43) the same way as L_A05A frees the file list: clears\n($1D44) and frees each entry with L_D976 (L_A07C). Does nothing when the list is empty.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8418": {"synopsis":"The Search command's dialog for L_D98A: the prompt \"String to search for\" and the options\n\"Search only range of columns\", \"Equate upper and lower case\", \"Search only marked block\",\n\"Search from current file\" and \"Search all files in list\", each with its control bytes."},
        "8585": {"synopsis":"The Search command (<>BSE). It asks for the search string and options (L_A0AD through\nL_D98A), prepares the search with L_A2CB and goes into the search loop: L_A743 looks for the\nnext match and L_A2A3 puts the cursor on it. When the sheet has no more matches and the\noptions name the file list, L_A318 loads the next file of the list and the search goes on;\nwhen there is none, L_A19C shows the number found. Errors are reported with L_EB07.\nEntry: none."},
        "8603": {"synopsis":"The Next Match command (<>BNM). It reports message 8 through L_EB07 when no search string is\nset up (bit 6 of (iy+29) clear). Otherwise it starts one character after the cursor ((iy-87)\n+ 1), or past the end of the slot when the current slot is not text, and enters the Search\ncommand's loop (inside L_A154).\nEntry: none."},
        "8657": {"synopsis":"Shows the number of matches found ((iy+30/31), through L_EE7C) followed by \" found\", sets\n(iy-84) = $0B and leaves through L_EFE9.\nEntry: none."},
        "8685": {"synopsis":"The Replace command's dialog for L_D98A: the prompts \"String to search for\" and \"Replace\nwith\" and the options \"Search only range of columns\", \"Equate upper and lower case\", \"Ask\nfor confirmation\", \"Search only marked block\" and \"Search all files in list\", each with its\ncontrol bytes."},
        "8863": {"synopsis":"The Replace command (<>BRP). It asks for the strings and options (L_A1B9 through L_D98A),\nprepares with L_A2CB, then finds each match with L_A743 and replaces it with L_A34A. When\nthe sheet has no more matches and the options name the file list, it moves on to the next\nfile of the list (L_A33B, L_A318). At the end L_A19C shows the number found; errors are\nreported with L_EB07. It leaves through L_A33B and L_929B.\nEntry: none."},
        "8919": {"synopsis":"Puts the cursor on a match: stores the slot as the current one with L_82A6, sets the offset\nin the slot (iy-87) to the match start (iy-123/-122) less the slot's text address (0 when\nthe slot is not text), clears (iy-88) and sets bit 7 of (iy-100).\nEntry: A = column; BC = row of the slot with the match.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "8959": {"synopsis":"Prepares a search or a replace from the dialog's options. It stores the options in (iy+34)\n(bit 6 added by L_997A when bit 3 is clear), clears the found flag (bit 0 of (iy+29)) and\nthe number found (iy+30/31). When the options name the file list (bits 1 or 4) it needs a\nloaded list, and unless bit 4 is set it loads the list's first file (L_9426). Then L_A2FE\nsets up the range.\nEntry: A = options from the dialog.\nExit: Fc = 0: A = column; C, B = row of the range's first slot.\nError: Fc = 1, C = message: $17 for options bits 7 and 1 together, $1A for no list loaded;\nFv = 1 also when loading the first file fails.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "9010": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_A2CB: shows status $1B (L_EF80), sets up the range of slots from the options\n(iy+34) with L_B2CC and clears the offset (iy-44).\nEntry: (iy+34) = options.\nExit: Fc = 0: A = (iy-58) column; C, B = (iy-57/-56) row of the range's first slot.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "9036": {"synopsis":"Moves the search on to the next file of the file list: L_9C6B steps to the next entry,\nL_9437 loads it and L_A2FE sets up the range again.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fv = 0, Fc = 0: A = column; C, B = row of the range's first slot Fv = 0, Fc = 1: no\nnext file.\nError: Fv = 1 (PE), C = message number (0: OZ error code in A)."},
        "9051": {"synopsis":"Decides whether a search goes on to the next file of the file list. It returns Fc = 1 when\nno list is loaded (bit 3 of (iy-70)), when option bit 7 is set, when neither option bit 1\nnor 4 is set, or when Escape was pressed (L_F023).\nEntry: (iy+34) = options.\nExit: Fc = 0: go on to the next file; Fc = 1: stop.\nChanges: AF."},
        "9071": {"synopsis":"Sets display and state flags after a search moved between files: L_CA8D, L_B411, L_B3C1 and\nL_8B80, then L_CA7C.\nEntry: none."},
        "9086": {"synopsis":"Replaces one match. It puts the cursor on it (L_A5A2) and stores the slot in (iy+2..+4).\nWith option bit 5 (ask for confirmation) it shows \"Replace: N, Y?\" and reads a key: on\nEscape it returns Fc = 1, C = 4; on any key but Y it sets (iy-44) to the offset of the\nmatch's end and returns. Otherwise (L_A3AD) it rebuilds the slot's text in the line buffer\nat ($1D3D): the text before the match, then the replace string at ($1D6B), whose tokens (a 0\nand a code) are run through the table L_A5D0, with the letter case following the found text\nwhen option bit 2 is set.\nEntry: A = column; C, B = row of the match.\nExit: Fc = 0: A = column; BC = row to go on searching from, (iy-44) = offset in it.\nError: Fc = 1, C = message.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "9371": {"synopsis":"Replace token 2 (^R), entered with DE at the token's 0: when the line buffer has no room for\n4 more bytes it leaves with C = $1E through L_A4A0. After \"#\" and a number it adds that\nreference found by the search (list at $1DAA, L_A5DE), otherwise the 4-byte slot reference\nthat follows. Goes on with the next byte of the replace string (L_A44F)."},
        "9434": {"synopsis":"Replace token 4 (^#n), entered with DE at the token's 0: adds the text that wildcard n\nmatched (list at $1DAA+$48, L_A5DE) to the line buffer with L_A662. Goes on with the next\nbyte of the replace string."},
        "9454": {"synopsis":"Replace token 6 (^?n), entered with DE at the token's 0: adds the character that\nsingle-character wildcard n matched (list at $1DAA+$33, L_A5DE) to the line buffer with\nL_A662. Goes on with the next byte of the replace string."},
        "9470": {"synopsis":"Replace token 8 (^S), entered with DE at the token's 0: adds a space to the line buffer with\nL_A680. Goes on with the next byte of the replace string."},
        "9478": {"synopsis":"Replace token 12 (^1 to ^9), entered with DE at the token's 0: adds the byte that follows\nthe code to the line buffer with L_A680. Goes on with the next byte of the replace string."},
        "9486": {"synopsis":"Replace token 0, entered with DE at the token's 0: adds nothing and goes on with the next\nbyte of the replace string."},
        "9528": {"synopsis":"Replace token 10, the end of the replace string. It skips the found text up to the match's\nend (L_A63E, L_A5FB), copies the rest of the slot's text after the match into the line\nbuffer (4 bytes for a reference), writes the buffer back with L_A6B0, and sets the match\nstart (iy-123/-122) and (iy-44) to the end of the replaced text so that the search goes on\nafter it.\nExit: Fc = 0: A = column; BC = row of the slot.\nError: Fc = 1, C = message (through L_A4A0 or L_A49E)."},
        "9644": {"synopsis":"When the replace added or removed slots ((iy-3) not 0), sets (iy-58..-56) to the match's\nslot (iy+2..+4) with bit 7 set in the column, calls L_B7B9 with BC = (iy-3) sign-extended\nand L_CA8D.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "9685": {"synopsis":"Puts the cursor on the match with L_A2A3 and, with option bit 5 (ask for confirmation),\nshows it (L_929B, L_BE08). It calls L_B411 and keeps (iy-60/-59).\nEntry: A = column; BC = row of the match.\nExit: A = column; BC = row, as on entry.\nChanges: F, DE, HL, IX."},
        "9731": {"synopsis":"Table of 7 words: the handler of each replace string token (L_A34A), indexed by the token's\ncode 0, 2, ... 12: L_A4DB, L_A468 (^R), L_A4A7 (^#n), L_A4BB (^?n), L_A4CB (^S), L_A505\n(end) and L_A4D3 (^1 to ^9)."},
        "9745": {"synopsis":"Finds entry A of one of the lists the search fills at $1DAA: C = $00 for references, $33 for\nsingle characters, $48 for wildcard texts. Each list starts with its count of entries; each\nentry ends with a 0.\nEntry: A = entry number from 0; C = the list's offset.\nExit: Fc = 0: BC = address of the entry; Fc = 1: no such entry.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "9774": {"synopsis":"Takes the next byte of the found text at HL for the replace, counting the bytes of a slot\nreference in (iy-44). At the end of a slot's text inside the match, it writes the line\nbuffer out (L_A6B0) and returns Fv = 1 to tell its caller to start again on the next slot;\nwhen that fails it drops its caller and leaves through L_A49E.\nEntry: HL = text address.\nExit: A = byte; HL = past it; Fc = 1 when the match's end is reached (L_A63E); Fv = 1 at a\nslot change.\nChanges: AF, C, HL."},
        "9841": {"synopsis":"Compares the position in the found text (row (iy+3/+4), address HL) with the match's end\n(row (iy-9/-8), address (iy-120/-119)).\nEntry: HL = text address.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the position is at or past the match's end; A kept.\nChanges: F, C."},
        "9877": {"synopsis":"Adds A to the line buffer with L_A680, adjusting the case of a letter when case matching is\non ((iy-13) not 0): the letter is made lower case unless (iy-12) is not 0, in which case it\nis made upper case and (iy-12) is counted down. Falls into L_A680.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: as L_A680.\nChanges: AF."},
        "9907": {"synopsis":"Adds A to the line buffer at ($1D3D) + (iy-40) and counts it in (iy-40). The buffer holds\n245 bytes; when it is full the byte that follows is set to 0 and, when bit 7 of (iy-42) is\nset, the buffer is written out to a new slot with L_A6FB; otherwise it fails.\nEntry: A = byte.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1: C = $15 when the buffer is full and bit 7 of (iy-42) is clear; BC as on entry\nwhen L_A6FB fails.\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "9955": {"synopsis":"Writes the line buffer out to a new slot (L_A6FB), then removes the match's slot (iy+2..+4)\nwith L_8B61 and counts down (iy-3) and the rows (iy-11/-10), (iy-9/-8) and (iy-60/-59). It\nsets (iy-42) to the type byte of the slot now at (iy+2..+4).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = message.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10030": {"synopsis":"When the line buffer holds text ((iy-40) not 0), inserts a slot at column (iy+2), row\n(iy-11/-10) with L_8CA2, copies the buffer into it (L_B493) and empties the buffer. It\ncounts the slot in (iy-3), moves the rows (iy-11/-10) and (iy-60/-59) on by one and sets\nbits 0 of (iy-42) and 3 of (iy-72).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = 1 when the slot cannot be inserted.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10102": {"synopsis":"Looks for the next match of the search string at ($1D69) from the slot A, BC and the offset\n(iy-44), within the range set by the options (iy+34).\n1. It returns Fc = 1 when the slot is outside the range's columns or rows.\n2. It finds the start address in the slot's text (L_A8C5) and clears the three lists of\nfound references, characters and wildcard texts at $1DAA.\n3. It tries the string word by word with L_A901, skipping spaces in both, moving one text\nitem on (L_A8BB) when it fails, and to the next slot of the range (L_FB93, L_A8C4) at the\nend of a slot's text.\n4. On a match it sets bit 0 of (iy+29), counts the match in (iy+30/31) and stores the start\n(iy-123/-122) and the last byte (iy-120/-119).\nEntry: A = column; BC = row; (iy-44) = offset in the slot.\nExit: Fc = 0: A = column; C, B = row of the slot with the match Fc = 1: no more matches.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10459": {"synopsis":"Copies the current slot (iy-110..-108) to (iy-61..-59).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = column; C, B = row.\nChanges: A, BC."},
        "10478": {"synopsis":"Moves HL past one item of a slot's text: 4 bytes for a slot reference (A in $10-$13,\nL_FE32), 1 byte otherwise.\nEntry: A = byte at HL; HL = text address.\nExit: HL = next item.\nChanges: F, HL."},
        "10487": {"synopsis":"Sets A = 0 (offset 0); falls into L_A8C5."},
        "10488": {"synopsis":"Finds the text of the slot (iy-61..-59) at offset A.\nEntry: A = offset in the text.\nExit: Fc = 0: HL = text address; IX = slot; B = size of the slot's header; C = type bits\n7-6; Fz = 1 when the offset is 0 Fc = 1: no such slot, or its type bits 7-6 are both set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10532": {"synopsis":"Search token 4 (^#), entered with DE at the token's code: starts a wildcard. It opens a new\nentry of the wildcard text list (L_AA66; none when the list is full), sets bit 7 of C\n(wildcard open) and bit 0 when there is an entry, then goes on through L_A909."},
        "10548": {"synopsis":"Tries to match the search string at DE against the text at HL. L_A909 is the restart point\nfor a wildcard: it keeps the text address after the current item (iy-40/-39) and the string\naddress (iy-42/-41). For each byte of the string it compares the text character (upper case\nwith option bit 2, L_AAA5) or runs a token through the table L_AA97. On a mismatch after a\nwildcard, it adds the text character to the wildcard text and starts again after it.\nEntry: DE = search string; HL = text address.\nExit: Fz = 1, Fc = 1: the whole string matched; HL = past the match Fz = 1, Fc = 0: matched\nup to a space in the string Fz = 0, A = 1: no match.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10611": {"synopsis":"Search token 0 (^B): matches only when HL is at the start of the slot's text (L_B500); goes\non through L_A9EE."},
        "10628": {"synopsis":"Search token 2 (^R): the text item must be a slot reference. After \"#\" any reference matches\nand is stored in the reference list at $1DAA (L_AA7C, L_AA47); otherwise its 3 bytes must\nequal those that follow in the string."},
        "10686": {"synopsis":"Search token 12 (^1 to ^9): compares the byte after the code with the text character through\nL_A999."},
        "10694": {"synopsis":"Search token 8 (^S): fails at the end of the text, otherwise compares a space with the text\ncharacter through L_A999."},
        "10760": {"synopsis":"Search token 6 (^?): matches any character but a space and stores it in the single-character\nlist at $1DAA+$33 (L_AA71, L_AA53)."},
        "10807": {"synopsis":"Search token 10, the end of the search string. It reports a match (L_AA20: Fz = 1, Fc = 1)\nwhen an item matched since the last restart (bit 1 of C); with a wildcard open (bit 7 of C)\nit adds a non-space text character to the wildcard and tries again; otherwise no match."},
        "10841": {"synopsis":"Closes an open wildcard: when bit 7 of C is set, ends its text entry with a 0 (L_AA33) when\nbit 0 is set, and clears bits 7 and 0 of C.\nEntry: C = match state.\nChanges: C (and AF when an entry is ended)."},
        "10854": {"synopsis":"Sets A = 0; falls into L_AA34, which adds A to the wildcard text list at $1DAA + (iy-7) and\nmoves (iy-7) on (a 0 is stored instead once (iy-7) reaches $FE).\nExit: Fc = 1 when the list is full.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10855": {"synopsis":"Entry inside the pattern matcher (L_AA33 sets A = 0 and falls in here): appends A to the\nthird list of the match buffer at $1DAA, at index (iy-7), and increments (iy-7). When the\nindex is already $FE or more it stores 0 instead of A. Shares its tail with L_AA47 and\nL_AA53.\nEntry: A = byte to append; (iy-7) = index.\nExit: A = index used; Fc = 1 when the list was full and 0 was stored.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10874": {"synopsis":"Appends A to the first list of the match buffer at $1DAA at index (iy-9) and increments\n(iy-9). No limit is checked here: L_AA7C makes room first.\nEntry: A = byte to append; (iy-9) = index.\nExit: A = index used.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10886": {"synopsis":"Appends A to the second list of the match buffer at $1DAA at index (iy-8) and increments\n(iy-8). No limit is checked here: L_AA71 makes room first.\nEntry: A = byte to append; (iy-8) = index.\nExit: A = index used.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10905": {"synopsis":"Checks that the third list of the match buffer at $1DAA has room ((iy-7) below $FD) and,\nwhen it has, increments its count byte at $1DAA+$48.\nEntry: (iy-7) = next index of the list.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the count was incremented; Fc = 1 when the list is full (nothing changed).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10916": {"synopsis":"Checks that the second list of the match buffer at $1DAA has room ((iy-8) below $45) and,\nwhen it has, increments its count byte at $1DAA+$33.\nEntry: (iy-8) = next index of the list.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the count was incremented; Fc = 1 when the list is full (nothing changed).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10927": {"synopsis":"Checks that the first list of the match buffer at $1DAA has room ((iy-9) below $2D) and,\nwhen it has, increments its count byte at $1DAA+0.\nEntry: (iy-9) = next index of the list.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the count was incremented; Fc = 1 when the list is full (nothing changed).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "10946": {"synopsis":"Returns HL pointing at byte A of the match buffer at $1DAA.\nEntry: A = offset.\nExit: HL = $1DAA + A.\nChanges: F, DE, HL."},
        "10954": {"synopsis":"Table of 7 words: the handlers the pattern matcher jumps to (at L_A921) when the pattern\nholds a 0 byte; the byte after it is the byte offset into this table (0, 2, ... 12). The\nhandlers are L_A940, L_A951, L_A8F1, L_A9D5, L_A993, L_AA04 and L_A98B."},
        "10968": {"synopsis":"Converts A to upper case (GetUppercase) when bit 2 of (iy+34) is set; otherwise returns it\nas it is. The pattern matcher compares both sides through it.\nEntry: A = character; (iy+34) = options.\nExit: A = character, upper case when bit 2 of (iy+34) is set."},
        "10976": {"synopsis":"Option list of the Print command (PrintCommand), read by L_D98A: control bytes and the\nzero-terminated texts \"Print only range of columns\", \"Select rows to print\" and \"Wait\nbetween pages\", closed by $84, $00."},
        "11052": {"synopsis":"The Print command (<>PO, command table entry 83): stores a pending edit (L_B398), asks for\nthe options of PrintPrompt (L_D98A; returns when cancelled), sets the block to print with\nL_B2CC, keeps the options in (iy-46) and prints through L_AB10, reporting an error it\nreturns with L_EB07.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when cancelled or after a reported error."},
        "11075": {"synopsis":"Prints the block (iy-58..-53) row by row for PrintCommand, with the options in (iy-46).\n1. Saves SP in ($1D59), sets bits 6 and 0 of (iy-70) and starts the output (L_ED6C).\n2. Clears the page state: (iy-85) = 0, line count (iy-86) = 1, page number (iy-91..-90) = 1;\nwhen the whole sheet is printed (bit 7 of (iy-46) clear) the page number comes from\n(iy+10..11), and with bit 3 of (iy-70) set L_9426 is run first.\n3. For each row from L_FBBD on: skips it when \"Select rows to print\" (bit 1 of (iy-46)) is\nset and L_B30E rejects it, otherwise prints it with L_ABC6; stops on Escape (L_F023).\n4. With bit 3 of (iy-70) set and no marked block, continues through L_9C6B and L_9437 and\nprints again from step 2; finally ends the page (L_AD32) and leaves through L_ABBB.\nEntry: (iy-46) = options from L_B2CC; block in (iy-58..-53).\nExit: Fc = 0 when the run ends; Fc = 1 after an error was reported (L_EB07)."},
        "11246": {"synopsis":"Shared exit of the print run: acknowledges Escape (L_E097), ends the output (L_ED53), puts\nthe row-selection expression back to its first row (L_B363) and returns Fc = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0."},
        "11257": {"synopsis":"Prints row (iy-60..-59) of the block for L_AB10. When column 0 of the row holds a slot with\nflag bits 7 and 6 both set (L_D24C), it is not printed but handled as a page control through\nL_D263 and L_AC9D. Otherwise it starts a new page when needed (L_AC9D), resets the page\nnumber (L_AC84), prints the left margin (L_AD28) and each column from (iy-58) to (iy-55)\n(L_C917, L_D54A, L_D797, L_C9B8, L_CB0E, L_EDE6, L_C5EA), sends (iy+8) carriage returns\n(L_AD1B) and advances the line count (iy-86) with L_D28D. Bit 6 of (iy-72) is set while the\nrow is printed.\nEntry: (iy-60..-59) = row; (iy-61) = first column.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the page change was abandoned (Escape at the \"Page\" wait); Fc = 0\notherwise."},
        "11447": {"synopsis":"Clears bit 0 of (iy-85); when that bit was set, also copies the start page number\n(iy+10..11) into the page number (iy-91..-90).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = the old bit 0 of (iy-85).\nChanges: AF."},
        "11472": {"synopsis":"Page change of the print run; does nothing when the page length (iy+7) is 0. When a page is\nopen (bit 7 of (iy-85)) it ends it (L_AD37), increments the page number (L_D2BB, then L_D315\non Fc = 1) and returns when C is not 0. Otherwise, or with C = 0, it opens a new page: sets\nbit 7 of (iy-85); with \"Wait between pages\" (bit 2 of (iy-46)) it shows \"Page n..\" and waits\nfor a key (L_E006), where C clears the option and any key other than M restarts the output\n(L_ED6C); then it prints option $0F carriage returns, the header text of option $14 (L_AD6D)\nand option $10 carriage returns.\nEntry: C = 0 to open a new page after ending one, other values to end the page only.\nExit: Fc = 1 when Escape was pressed at the wait; Fc = 0 otherwise."},
        "11596": {"synopsis":"Sends A carriage returns ($0D) to the print output through L_ED93; nothing when A = 0.\nL_AD1E is the same loop for the character in A, C times.\nEntry: A = count.\nExit: C = 0; A = $0D.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "11609": {"synopsis":"Sends the number of spaces given by page-layout option $13 (read with L_E790) to the print\noutput, through the loop in L_AD1B.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "11619": {"synopsis":"Ends the current page when one is open (bit 7 of (iy-85)); falls into L_AD37.\nEntry: none."},
        "11624": {"synopsis":"Ends the current page of the print run. When the text of option $15 is not empty (L_E54F,\nL_E8C3) it sends carriage returns to reach the end of the page (option $11, plus the lines\nleft from the page length (iy+7) and the line count (iy-86)) and prints that text (L_AD6D).\nThen it sends a form feed ($0C), clears bit 7 of (iy-85) and sets the line count (iy-86) to\n1.\nEntry: none."},
        "11678": {"synopsis":"Prints the header or footer text at HL. Returns Fc = 1 at once when the text is empty or\nonly spaces (L_E8C3). With a page number (iy-91..-90) other than 0 it stores HL in ($1D4D),\nprints the left margin (L_AD28), adds up the widths of the block's columns (L_D54A, L_D551)\ninto (iy-36) and prints the text through L_CE31, L_CBD9 and L_EDE6. It ends with one\ncarriage return (L_AD1B).\nEntry: HL = zero-terminated text.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the text was empty."},
        "11764": {"synopsis":"Option list of the Sort command (SortBlock), read by L_D98A: control bytes and the\nzero-terminated texts \"Sort on column\", \"Sort in reverse order\" and \"Don't update\nreferences\"."},
        "11833": {"synopsis":"The Sort command (<>BSO, command table entry 6): sorts the rows of the marked block on one\ncolumn.\n1. Stores a pending edit (L_B398) and runs L_9250; makes sure every column of the block has\na slot on its last row (L_B8B6, L_B8C7), reporting an error that fails.\n2. Asks for SortColumnPrompt (L_D98A; returns when cancelled): the options go to (iy-44) and\nthe key column from (iy+53) to (iy-46). Returns when the block has only one row.\n3. Sorts with a gap that is halved each pass (a Shell sort; gap in (iy+3..4)), comparing and\nexchanging rows with L_AF08, then finishes with L_8FC4 and L_EFBB.\nEntry: block in (iy-58..-53)."},
        "12059": {"synopsis":"Gets the sort key of row BC: the slot in the key column (iy-46), through L_FA07. Rows whose\ncolumn 0 holds a slot with flag bits 7 and 6 both set (L_D24C) have no key.\nEntry: BC = row.\nExit: P/V = 1 (pe) when the row has no key; otherwise P/V = 0, Fc = 1 for a text key (HL, B\nlocate it) and Fc = 0 for a numeric one (in the FPP registers), C = the key's type."},
        "12089": {"synopsis":"Compares the sort keys of rows (iy-28..-27) and (iy-103..-102) and exchanges the two rows\nwith L_AF97 when they are out of order. A first row without a key is passed over by moving\n(iy-28..-27) down to the next row with one. Numbers compare with Fp_cmp, text with L_F7DF;\nkeys of different types are ordered by type; bit 1 of (iy-44) (reverse order) inverts the\nresult.\nEntry: (iy-28..-27), (iy-103..-102) = rows; (iy-46) = key column.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the rows were exchanged, or a row without a key ended the comparison; Fc =\n0 when they were in order."},
        "12232": {"synopsis":"Exchanges the slots of rows (iy-28..-27) and (iy-103..-102) in every column of the block,\nfrom (iy-58) to (iy-55) (L_D797, L_D7AD, L_B0B9 and the slot-list routines L_BAC8 to\nL_BB69). Unless bit 0 of (iy-44) (\"Don't update references\") is set, it then runs L_B052\nover the references of every slot of the sheet, so that references to either row follow the\nexchange.\nEntry: rows in (iy-28..-27) and (iy-103..-102)."},
        "12500": {"synopsis":"Compares the two bytes at HL with (IX+1) and (IX+2) (a row number against a reference's\nrow).\nEntry: HL = row word; IX = reference minus 1.\nExit: Fz = 1 when both bytes are equal.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "12511": {"synopsis":"Compares row BC with the last row of the block (iy-54..-53).\nEntry: BC = row.\nExit: Fc = 1 when BC is lower; Fz = 1 when it is equal.\nChanges: AF."},
        "12522": {"synopsis":"Gets the flag byte of the current slot through L_B0C0 and writes it back to (IX+3), clearing\nbit 6 when L_B0C0 does.\nEntry: (iy-127..-125) = current slot.\nExit: IX = slot; A = new flag byte.\nChanges: AF, C, IX."},
        "12529": {"synopsis":"Returns the flag byte (IX+3) of the current slot (L_B518), with bit 6 cleared when bits 7-6\nare %01 and (IX+4) is 0. The slot itself is not changed.\nEntry: (iy-127..-125) = current slot.\nExit: IX = slot; A = C = flag byte.\nChanges: AF, C, IX."},
        "12554": {"synopsis":"Option list of the Replicate command (L_B103), read by L_D98A: control bytes and the\nzero-terminated texts \"Range to copy from\" and \"Range to copy to\"."},
        "12596": {"synopsis":"The Replicate command (<>BRE, command table entry 2): copies a range of slots over another\nrange, adjusting the references of each copy.\n1. Stores a pending edit (L_B398) and asks for L_B0D9 (L_D98A; returns when cancelled).\nCopies the \"from\" range (iy+53..58) to (iy-4..+1) and the \"to\" range (iy+59..64) to the\nblock (iy-58..-53).\n2. Measures both with L_B29D; reports \"bad range\" ($0E) when one is reversed. A single\ntarget slot is widened to the source's size (\"Edge\", $1D, past the sheet's limits); a\none-row source over a one-column target (or the other way) repeats the source along it (bit\n0 of (iy-13)); other shapes are a bad range.\n3. For each target position (L_FBBD) copies the source slot (L_9128, L_B8C4, L_913E), stores\nthe offset (iy-32..-30) and adjusts the copy's references (L_B6FF with L_B6D7); Escape stops\n($04). Ends with L_B411, L_EFD5, L_EFBB and L_8FBE.\nEntry: none."},
        "13006": {"synopsis":"Measures the range held at IX+3 (first column, first row word) and IX+6 (last column, last\nrow word).\nEntry: IX = range minus 3.\nExit: Fc = 1; A = E = last column minus first; BC = last row minus first; D bit 7 = more\nthan one column, D bit 6 = more than one row.\nError: Fc = 0 when the last column is before the first.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "13043": {"synopsis":"Runs L_EFD5, then moves the cursor to column $28 of line 0 with the SOH 3 @ sequence\n(L_EEE4).\nEntry: none."},
        "13053": {"synopsis":"Sets the block (iy-58..-53) for a command from its options in A. With bit 6 of A set, or\nwhen no block is marked (L_D014), it is the whole sheet: columns 0 to (iy-98)-1, rows 0 to\n(iy-97..-96)-1. Otherwise it is the marked block, copied by L_D014. With bit 0 of A set, the\nfirst and last columns are then taken from (iy+53) and (iy+54).\nEntry: A = options.\nExit: A = options, with bit 7 set when the marked block is used; Fc = 1 when it is the whole\nsheet.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE."},
        "13119": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the row-selection expression at ($1D73) (L_F06F) for row (iy-60..-59), with the\ncurrent slot set to column 0 of that row and (iy-61..-53) saved around the evaluation. Then\nmoves the expression's row references down one row (offset 1 through L_B37E), ready for the\nnext row.\nEntry: (iy-60..-59) = row.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the result is a number that Fp_cmp finds equal to 1 (the row is printed);\nFc = 1 for any other result."},
        "13204": {"synopsis":"When \"Select rows to print\" is on (bit 1 of (iy-46)), falls into L_B368; otherwise returns.\nEntry: (iy-46) = print options."},
        "13209": {"synopsis":"Moves the row references of the row-selection expression at ($1D73) back by the rows it was\nadvanced: the offset is the block's first row (iy-57..-56) minus the current row\n(iy-60..-59), with column offset 0; falls into L_B37E.\nEntry: none."},
        "13231": {"synopsis":"Adjusts every slot reference of the expression at ($1D73) by the offset in (iy-32..-30),\nthrough L_B708 with L_B6D7 as the handler.\nEntry: (iy-32) = column offset; (iy-31..-30) = row offset.\nChanges: IX."},
        "13241": {"synopsis":"Refuses a command while bit 6 of (iy-71) is set: reports \"Editing expression\" ($19, L_EB07)\nand returns to the caller's caller. Otherwise returns at once.\nEntry: none.\nError: Fc = 1, the calling command is abandoned."},
        "13253": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 1 of (iy-72) and falls into L_B398.\nEntry: none."},
        "13257": {"synopsis":"Stores a pending edit line into its slot (L_B39E). When that fails, the error has been\nreported and it returns to the caller's caller, abandoning the calling command.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0."},
        "13263": {"synopsis":"Stores a pending edit line into its slot. Does nothing (Fc = 0) while bit 6 of (iy-71) is\nset. With bit 0 of (iy-72) set it also sets bit 1; then L_B3C6 stores the line. On a failure\nit sets the redraw flags (L_CA73) and reports the error (L_EB07).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0 when done or nothing to do.\nError: Fc = 1 after the error was reported."},
        "13289": {"synopsis":"Sets bits 4 and 1 of (iy-72).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "13298": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 0 of (iy-71).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "13303": {"synopsis":"Writes the edit line back into the current slot when it holds one (bit 7 of (iy-72)) and it\nwas changed (bit 0 of (iy-72)). Finds the slot (L_D249, L_D0E2, L_D77E), then from L_B3D6:\nsets bit 0 of (iy-71), converts the line at ($1D3D) into $1DAA with L_BC66 (Fc = 1 on\nentry), builds the flag byte in (iy-42) ($80, or $A0 when L_BC66 returns P/V = 1, keeping\nbits 1-3 of an existing text slot) and the length in (iy-40), makes room (L_B8C7) and copies\nthe body (L_B490). It clears bits 0 and 7 of (iy-72) at the end (L_B410, L_B411).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0 when stored or nothing to do.\nError: Fc = 1, C = error number (from L_BC66, which leaves the bits of (iy-72) set, or\nL_B8C7)."},
        "13319": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_B3C6, used also by L_B4A6: when bit 0 of (iy-72) is set, converts the edit\nline at ($1D3D) with L_BC66 (Fc = 1 on entry) and stores it into the current slot\n(iy-110..-108); otherwise only clears bits 0 and 7 of (iy-72).\nEntry: (iy-110..-108) = slot position.\nExit: Fc = 0 when stored or nothing to do.\nError: Fc = 1, C = error number."},
        "13378": {"synopsis":"Clears bits 0 and 7 of (iy-72), the edit-line state; the flags are kept.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "13387": {"synopsis":"Marks the edit as going to the slot (iy-107..-105): L_82A2 sets bit 7 of (iy-100) and copies\nthat position to (iy-104..-102); falls into L_B426.\nEntry: (iy-107) = column; (iy-106..-105) = row."},
        "13399": {"synopsis":"Stores the edit line as an expression into the slot at (iy-104..-102), when bit 0 of (iy-72)\nsays it was changed. Looks up the slot at A, BC (L_D797), sets bit 0 of (iy-71) and converts\nthe line at ($1D3D) with L_BC66 (Fc = 0 on entry); an empty result goes to L_B3D6 instead.\nThe flag byte in (iy-42) is built from the old one ($80 for a new slot): bits 1-4 kept, bits\n1-3 set to %011 when it was a text slot, bit 5 set when L_BC66 returns P/V = 1; byte 9 of an\nold expression slot is kept. It makes room (L_B8C4), copies the body (L_B490), evaluates it\n(L_B575) and ends in L_B410.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row; (iy-104..-102) = target slot.\nExit: Fc = 0 when stored or nothing to do.\nError: Fc = 1, C = error number."},
        "13505": {"synopsis":"Copies the converted slot body from $1DAA into the current slot; falls into L_B493.\nEntry: (iy-40) = length including the terminator."},
        "13508": {"synopsis":"Copies (iy-40) - 1 bytes from HL into the body of the current slot (L_B500) and writes a 0\nafter them.\nEntry: HL = source; (iy-40) = length including the terminator.\nExit: A = 0; DE = address of the 0 written; HL = after the source bytes.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "13527": {"synopsis":"The Number<>Text command (<>ENT, command table entry 56): converts each slot of the block\nbetween expression and text. Refused while an expression is edited (L_B388); stores a\npending edit (L_B398) and runs L_88C6. For each slot (L_FBBD, L_FB93) that is not of the\nkind with flag bits 7 and 6 both set, it loads its text into the edit line (L_BB7B), marks\nit changed and stores it back: an expression slot as text (L_B3D6), a text slot as an\nexpression (L_82A6, L_B426); then it sets bit 1 of (iy-72) and runs L_C9CA. Ends with\nL_CA73.\nEntry: block in (iy-58..-53)."},
        "13610": {"synopsis":"Reads a 3-byte slot reference (column, row word) at HL.\nEntry: HL = reference.\nExit: A = column; BC = row; HL = HL + 3.\nChanges: A, BC, HL."},
        "13617": {"synopsis":"Finds the body of the current slot: binds it (L_B518) and falls into L_B503.\nEntry: (iy-127..-125) = current slot.\nExit: as L_B503, with IX = slot."},
        "13620": {"synopsis":"Returns the body of the slot at IX: it starts at offset 4 for a text slot (bit 7 of the flag\nbyte (IX+3) set) and at offset 10 otherwise.\nEntry: IX = slot.\nExit: A = flag byte; B = offset of the body; HL = IX + B; Fz = 1 when bit 7 is clear.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE."},
        "13641": {"synopsis":"Points IX at the current slot (iy-127..-126), binding its bank (iy-125) through L_D887 when\nit is not the bank in (iy-111).\nEntry: (iy-127..-125) = current slot.\nExit: IX = slot.\nChanges: AF, IX.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "13662": {"synopsis":"Adds the offset of a slot's body to A: 4 when bit 7 of B (the flag byte) is set, 10\notherwise.\nEntry: A = value; B = flag byte.\nExit: A = A + 4 or A + 10.\nChanges: AF."},
        "13670": {"synopsis":"Adds the offset of the body of the slot at IX (L_B503) to A.\nEntry: A = value; IX = slot.\nExit: A = A + offset; B = offset; HL = body.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "13677": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the offset of the body of the slot at IX (L_B503) from A.\nEntry: A = value; IX = slot.\nExit: A = A - offset; B = offset; HL = body.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "13684": {"synopsis":"Loads the current slot into the edit line, unless the line already holds one (bit 7 or bit 0\nof (iy-72)). When there is no slot (L_D7AA) the edit line is emptied (L_B56E). A text slot\n(flag bit 7 set, bits 7-6 not both set) is put into the line with L_BB7B unless bit 6 of\n(iy-71) is set; bit 7 of (iy-72) then marks the line as loaded. Other slots leave the line\nalone.\nEntry: none."},
        "13722": {"synopsis":"Shared exit of L_B543: sets bit 7 of (iy-72), the \"edit line loaded\" flag.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "13727": {"synopsis":"Empties the edit line (a 0 at the address in ($1D3D)) and marks it loaded (bit 7 of\n(iy-72)).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: HL."},
        "13734": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the body of the current slot (L_B500, L_F06F) and stores the result in the slot,\nby the result type in (iy-79): type 2 is stored by L_F2DC at IX+4; type 0 puts L in IX+4 and\nsets bit 4 of the flag byte; type 5 puts 1 in IX+4 and L in IX+5; type 8 is converted\n(L_FE8A, L_FEDA) and stored as 4 bytes at IX+5 with 2 in IX+4; any other puts the 3 bytes at\nHL in IX+5 with 0 in IX+4. The flag byte (IX+3) keeps bits 0-3 and 5, gets $40 for types 5,\n8 and others, and bit 5 when bit 7 of (iy-44) is set.\nEntry: (iy-127..-125) = current slot.\nExit: IX = slot."},
        "13919": {"synopsis":"Adjusts the references of every slot in the block by the offset (iy-32..-30): walks the\ncolumns from (iy-58) (bit 7 cleared) to (iy-55) and the rows from (iy-57..-56) to\n(iy-54..-53), running L_B6FF with L_B6D7 on each slot found (L_D79A).\nEntry: block in (iy-58..-53); offset in (iy-32..-30)."},
        "14017": {"synopsis":"Sets the reference offset: column A in (iy-32), row BC in (iy-31..-30). L_B671 falls into it\nto restore the offset it saved.\nEntry: A = column offset; BC = row offset.\nChanges: none."},
        "14084": {"synopsis":"Adjusts both the column and the row of the reference at HL (C = 0); jumps into L_B6D8.\nEntry: HL = reference."},
        "14089": {"synopsis":"Adjusts the 3-byte slot reference at HL (column, row word) by the offset in (iy-32..-30):\nadds (iy-32) to the column unless bit 1 of C is set, and (iy-31..-30) to the row unless bit\n0 of C is set. A column of $40 or more, or a row that turns negative, sets bit 7 of the\ncolumn byte. L_B6D7 enters with C = B, the reference's marker byte.\nEntry: HL = reference; C = bits 1 and 0 for a column and a row that stay fixed.\nExit: HL unchanged; Fc = 0 when bit 7 was set.\nChanges: AF."},
        "14124": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 6 of the byte at HL (the column byte of a reference) and returns Fc = 0.\nEntry: HL = reference.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: F."},
        "14128": {"synopsis":"Runs a routine on every cell reference in an expression slot. Returns at once when bit 5 of\nthe slot's type byte is clear; otherwise walks the slot's content after its header to the\nterminating zero and, for each reference token ($10-$13), calls the routine with HL on the\n3-byte reference that follows the token.\nEntry: IX = slot (bank bound); HL = routine to call.\nExit: IX = the routine; the routine is called with B = token, C = 0, HL = reference.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX, and what the routine changes."},
        "14159": {"synopsis":"Sets the start of the reference range (iy-58..56) to the cursor's column, with no row bound\n(bit 7 of (iy-56) set); falls into L_B721.\nEntry: none.\nExit: (iy-58) = cursor column; (iy-57/56) = cursor row with bit 7 of the high byte set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14162": {"synopsis":"Sets the start of the reference range from the cursor position (L_D0E2): (iy-58) = cursor\ncolumn OR A, (iy-57) = row low, (iy-56) = row high OR C. In the column byte bit 7 limits the\nrange to that one column and bits 7 and 6 together accept every column; bit 7 of the row\nhigh byte removes the row bound.\nEntry: A = bits for the column byte; C = bits for the row high byte.\nExit: (iy-58..56) = range start.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14181": {"synopsis":"Stores a shift (L_B690) and sets the end of the reference range (iy-55..53) from its start.\nFor a negative shift the end is start + |shift| - 1 (the cells that go); for a positive one\nit is the start; an unbounded start gives end column $40 or end row $7FFF. A negative shift\nin either direction then installs L_B6F7 as the in-range routine (L_B78A); otherwise L_B785\nremoves the column end.\nEntry: A = column shift; BC = row shift (signed); (iy-58..56) = range start.\nExit: (iy-32..30) = shift; (iy-55..53) = range end; (iy-20/19) = L_B6F7 when a shift is\nnegative.\nChanges: AF, BC, E, HL."},
        "14262": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 7 of the range's end column (iy-55), so the range has no column end. Shared tail of\nL_B734.\nEntry: none."},
        "14267": {"synopsis":"Installs L_B6F7 as the routine L_B8A0 runs for a reference inside the range; L_B6F7 marks\nthe reference invalid by setting bit 7 of its column byte. Falls into L_B78D.\nEntry: none.\nExit: (iy-20/19) = L_B6F7.\nChanges: BC."},
        "14270": {"synopsis":"Stores BC in (iy-20/19) as the routine L_B8A0 runs for a reference inside the range.\nEntry: BC = routine.\nExit: (iy-20/19) = BC."},
        "14277": {"synopsis":"Adjusts the cell references after the cursor's column is deleted: references to that column\nbecome invalid (bit 7 of the column byte) and those to later columns move one column left.\nEntry: none (the cursor's column).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "14284": {"synopsis":"Adjusts the cell references after a column is inserted at the cursor: references to the\ncursor's column and later ones move one column right.\nEntry: none (the cursor's column).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "14294": {"synopsis":"Adjusts the cell references after the cursor's row is deleted: the range starts at the\ncursor (L_B721 with C = 0) and the row shift is -1, so references to the row become invalid\nand those to later rows move one row up. Falls through L_B7B9.\nEntry: A = column bits for L_B721 ($80 = the cursor's column only, $C0 = every column).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "14314": {"synopsis":"Shifts the cell references in a range: sets the range end from the shift (L_B734), then\nadjusts every reference with L_B8A0.\n1. Saves (iy-42). For each column (iy-110) from 0 to (iy-98) - 1, and for each row from 0\nwhile L_D79A finds a slot, runs L_B8A0 on every reference of the slot (L_B6FF).\n2. Runs L_B8A0 (C = 0) on the block marks at (iy-67..65) and (iy-64..62) when they are set\n(bit 7 of the column clear).\n3. Clears both marks with L_89F8 when either one's bit 7 changed, then restores (iy-42).\nEntry: A = column shift; BC = row shift (signed); (iy-58..56) = range start.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; (iy-110..108)."},
        "14319": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_B7B9 for a caller that has set the range start, end and in-range routine\nitself: stores the shift (L_B690) and adjusts every reference and the block marks.\nEntry: A = column shift; BC = row shift (signed); (iy-58..53) = range; (iy-20/19) = in-range\nroutine.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; (iy-110..108)."},
        "14430": {"synopsis":"Tests the cell reference at HL against the range (iy-58..53). A reference before the start\n(column or row) is left alone. One inside the range in both column and row returns Fc = 1.\nOne at or after the start but past the end in a direction is shifted by L_B6D8 (C selects\nthe directions) and returns Fc = 0. A start column with bit 7 set accepts only that column,\nwith bits 7 and 6 every column; an end column with bit 6 set leaves references past it\nalone; bit 7 of the end column or of the start row high byte removes that bound.\nEntry: HL = reference (column, row low, row high); C = L_B6D8 flags (0 = shift both).\nExit: Fc = 1 inside the range; Fc = 0 otherwise; HL unchanged.\nChanges: AF, B, DE."},
        "14545": {"synopsis":"The routine L_B7B9 runs on each reference. A reference whose column byte has bit 6 set is\nonly cleared of it. Otherwise L_B82D tests and shifts it, and a reference inside the range\nis passed to the routine at (iy-20/19).\nEntry: HL = reference (column, row low, row high); C = L_B6D8 flags.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, IX, and what the in-range routine changes."},
        "14565": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine at IX; \"call L_B8B4\" calls it.\nEntry: IX = routine."},
        "14567": {"synopsis":"Sets the type and length for the next new slot to $80 and 1: (iy-42) = $80, (iy-40) = $01\n(the values of L_B8C0).\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = $8001.\nChanges: BC."},
        "14577": {"synopsis":"Loads BC with $8001: type $80 and content length 1, the slot used to fill empty rows.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = $8001."},
        "14581": {"synopsis":"Stores the column and row (L_D77E) and falls into L_B8C7 to make sure a slot exists there.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: as L_B8C7.\nError: as L_B8C7."},
        "14584": {"synopsis":"Makes sure a slot of type (iy-42) and content length (iy-40) exists at column (iy-110), row\n(iy-109/108).\n1. When L_D79A finds a slot there, L_B95D gives it the type and size.\n2. Otherwise makes sure the column exists (L_D8BF). An empty column (bit 7 of byte 3 of its\ncolumn entry) gets a first slot of type $80 at row 0, recorded in the entry, and the search\nstarts again.\n3. Otherwise appends slots after the column's last slot up to the row: type $80, length 1\nfor the rows in between, the requested type and length for the last. Each one is allocated\n(L_D926), cleared (L_D8F2), linked after the previous one (L_BA44), recorded as the column's\ncached position (L_B9D6) and its row recorded with L_CA0E.\nEntry: (iy-110..108) = column and row; (iy-42) = type; (iy-40) = content length.\nExit: Fc = 0; the slot is the current one ((iy-127..125)).\nError: Fc = 1 when memory runs out."},
        "14785": {"synopsis":"Gets the size of the current slot: 6 when bits 7 and 6 of its type are both set, otherwise\nthe bytes from the slot's start to its terminating zero (references counted as 4 bytes by\nL_A8BB).\nEntry: (iy-127..125) = current slot.\nExit: B = size; IX = slot (bank bound).\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "14809": {"synopsis":"Links the current slot (iy-127..125) into its column's list between the slots at (iy+65..67)\nand (iy+68..70) (L_BA44 twice), records it as the column's cached position at the current\nrow (L_B9D6) and binds its bank.\nEntry: (iy-127..125) = slot; (iy+65..70) = the neighbours; (iy-110..108) = column and row.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14839": {"synopsis":"Records a cached position one row back: when HL is not 0, decrements the current row\n(iy-109/108); then falls into L_B9D6.\nEntry: HL, C = slot; DE, B = next slot.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, and as L_B9D6."},
        "14855": {"synopsis":"Writes the cached position of column (iy-110) into its column entry: bytes 2-3 the row, 4-6\nthe slot, 7-9 the next slot. With HL = 0 the cache is reset: to the slot at DE, B as row 0\n(its link giving the next slot), or to row $8000 (an empty column) with no slots when DE is\n0 too.\nEntry: HL, C = slot at the current row (iy-109/108); DE, B = next slot.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14933": {"synopsis":"Unlinks the cached slot of column A from the column's list: reads the column entry (L_BAC8)\nand falls into L_BA27.\nEntry: A = column.\nExit: as L_BA27."},
        "14936": {"synopsis":"Unlinks a slot from its XOR-linked list. Afterwards the slot's link is 0 and neither\nneighbour points at it; the neighbours are not linked to each other.\nEntry: HL, C = slot; DE, B = next slot.\nExit: (iy-117..115) = the removed slot; (iy+65..67) = previous slot; (iy+68..70) = next\nslot; HL, C = previous slot; DE, B = removed slot.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "14939": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_BA27 after the first L_BA44: the slot's link already holds only its previous\nslot. Saves the slot and the next one, reads the previous slot from the link and unlinks it.\nEntry: HL, C = slot; DE, B = next slot.\nExit: as L_BA27."},
        "14965": {"synopsis":"Toggles the link between two slots of an XOR-linked list: XORs the address and bank of each\ninto the other's 3-byte link field (bytes 0-2). Does nothing when either address is 0.\nEntry: HL, C = one slot; DE, B = the other.\nExit: HL, DE unchanged; the bank of DE is bound.\nChanges: AF."},
        "15012": {"synopsis":"Finds where a slot goes in at column A, row BC: stores the column and row (L_D77E), finds\nthe slot at the row before (L_D7AD) and stores the neighbours the new slot goes between.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: (iy+65..67) = slot at row BC - 1 (0 for row 0); (iy+68..70) = slot at row BC.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "15047": {"synopsis":"Loads the current slot pointer: HL = (iy-127/126), C = bank (iy-125).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL, C = slot.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "15057": {"synopsis":"Loads the pointer at (iy-117..115): HL = address, C = bank.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL, C = slot.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "15067": {"synopsis":"Stores HL, C as the current slot pointer (iy-127..125).\nEntry: HL, C = slot."},
        "15077": {"synopsis":"Stores HL, C at (iy-117..115).\nEntry: HL, C = slot."},
        "15087": {"synopsis":"Loads the current slot pointer into DE, B: DE = (iy-127/126), B = bank (iy-125).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE, B = slot.\nChanges: B, DE."},
        "15097": {"synopsis":"Reads the cached position of column A from its 10-byte column entry (L_D890): the slot\n(bytes 4-6) and the next slot (bytes 7-9).\nEntry: A = column.\nExit: HL, C = slot; DE, B = next slot; A = column + 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "15117": {"synopsis":"Swaps the pointer at (iy+65..67) with the one at (iy+71..73) and the one at (iy+68..70) with\nthe one at (iy+74..76). Ends with L_BAF1.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "15138": {"synopsis":"Stores HL, C at (iy+74..76).\nEntry: HL, C = pointer."},
        "15148": {"synopsis":"Stores HL, C at (iy+71..73).\nEntry: HL, C = pointer."},
        "15158": {"synopsis":"Stores HL, C at (iy+68..70).\nEntry: HL, C = pointer."},
        "15168": {"synopsis":"Stores HL, C at (iy+65..67).\nEntry: HL, C = pointer."},
        "15188": {"synopsis":"Stores DE, B at (iy+68..70).\nEntry: DE, B = pointer."},
        "15198": {"synopsis":"Stores DE, B at (iy+65..67).\nEntry: DE, B = pointer."},
        "15208": {"synopsis":"Loads HL, C from (iy+71..73).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL, C = pointer.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "15218": {"synopsis":"Loads HL, C from (iy+68..70).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL, C = pointer.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "15228": {"synopsis":"Loads HL, C from (iy+65..67).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL, C = pointer.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "15238": {"synopsis":"Loads DE, B from (iy+74..76).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE, B = pointer.\nChanges: B, DE."},
        "15248": {"synopsis":"Loads DE, B from (iy+71..73).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE, B = pointer.\nChanges: B, DE."},
        "15258": {"synopsis":"Loads DE, B from (iy+68..70).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE, B = pointer.\nChanges: B, DE."},
        "15268": {"synopsis":"Writes the current slot's content as text to the screen, at most A characters: sets L_BC17\n(writes with OS_Out while the count (iy-36) lasts, skipping zero bytes) as the output\nroutine and continues in L_BB7E.\nEntry: A = maximum number of characters.\nExit: as L_BB7E; (iy-34) = characters written.\nError: as L_BB7E."},
        "15276": {"synopsis":"Writes the current slot's content as text into the buffer at ($1D3D): sets L_BC07 (stores at\n($1D3D) + (iy-34) and counts) as the output routine and falls into L_BB7E.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_BB7E; (iy-34) = bytes written.\nError: as L_BB7E."},
        "15279": {"synopsis":"Turns the current slot's content back into text through the output routine in BC (stored at\n$1D4B, called with the character in A). Token $14 is written as '\"', a reference token\n($10-$13) as a cell reference (L_BC2C, with '$' before the column when bit 1 of the token is\nset and before the row when bit 0 is), and other bytes as they are; a zero is written at the\nend. SP is kept at $1D47 so an output routine can abandon the work.\nEntry: BC = output routine; (iy-127..125) = current slot.\nExit: (iy-34) = 0 at start, counted by the output routine; F = 0 (P/V = 0).\nError: an output routine that overflows reloads SP from ($1D47) and returns to the caller\nwith P/V = 1 (as L_8AA9 does)."},
        "15344": {"synopsis":"Writes the cell reference in A (column) and BC (row) as text without '$' markers; falls into\nL_BBC6 with Fc and P/V clear.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row (from 0).\nExit: as L_BBC6."},
        "15351": {"synopsis":"Writes a cell reference as text through the output routine at ($1D4B): '%' first when bit 7\nof the column is set, '$' when Fc = 1, the column letters (L_BC39), '$' when P/V = 1, then\nthe row + 1 in decimal (L_BC60).\nEntry: A = column (bit 7 = invalid); BC = row (from 0); Fc = absolute column; P/V = absolute\nrow.\nExit: (iy-74) = 0.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX."},
        "15383": {"synopsis":"Writes the (iy-74) bytes of the text buffer at IY+35 through the output routine (L_BBFA).\nEntry: (iy-74) = count (not 0).\nExit: (iy-74) = 0; HL = after the last byte.\nChanges: F, DE, HL."},
        "15399": {"synopsis":"Writes '$' through the output routine (L_BBFC).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: A."},
        "15403": {"synopsis":"Writes the byte at HL through the output routine and advances HL; falls into L_BBFC.\nEntry: HL = byte.\nExit: HL + 1; A = the byte.\nChanges: A, HL."},
        "15405": {"synopsis":"Calls the output routine whose address is at $1D4B with the character in A; keeps AF and HL.\nEntry: A = character.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "15453": {"synopsis":"Writes the cell reference stored at HL (column, row low, row high) as text with L_BBC6; Fc\nand P/V on entry select the '$' markers.\nEntry: HL = reference; Fc = absolute column; P/V = absolute row.\nExit: HL = after the reference.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, IX."},
        "15466": {"synopsis":"Puts the letters of column A at the start of the text buffer at IY+35: falls into L_BC3B\nwith C = 0.\nEntry: A = column (from 0).\nExit: as L_BC3B."},
        "15468": {"synopsis":"Puts the letters of column A at offset C in the text buffer at IY+35: one letter for columns\n0-25 (A-Z), two for later ones (AA, AB, ...).\nEntry: A = column (from 0); C = offset.\nExit: (iy-74) = C + the letters written.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL."},
        "15505": {"synopsis":"Puts BC + 1 in decimal, without leading zeros, at the start of the text buffer at IY+35\n(L_EE87).\nEntry: BC = row (from 0).\nExit: (iy-74) = number of digits.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "15511": {"synopsis":"Compiles the text at ($1D3D) into the token buffer at $1DAA (L_BC6D with IX and HL set).\nCharacters are copied; control characters are dropped and '\"' becomes $14, toggling a string\nstate. Outside strings a '$' or a letter that does not follow a letter or digit starts a\ncell reference (L_BD57), compiled as a token $10-$13 (bit 1 = '$' before the column, bit 0 =\nbefore the row) with the column and the row word. A zero ends the buffer. With Fc = 1 on\nentry (text mode) characters are copied as they are and a reference is compiled only after a\nsingle '@' and when '@' follows it.\nEntry: ($1D3D) = zero-terminated text; Fc = text mode.\nExit: Fc = 0; B = bytes written, terminator included; IX = after them; P/V = 1 when a\nreference was compiled; (iy-110..108) unchanged.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $15 when the buffer reaches 245 bytes."},
        "15732": {"synopsis":"Stores A at IX in the token buffer, advances IX and counts the byte in (iy-38).\nEntry: A = byte; IX = buffer position.\nExit: Fc = 0; A kept.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $15 when the count reaches 245.\nChanges: F, B, C, IX."},
        "15752": {"synopsis":"Parses a cell reference in text after skipping spaces (L_BDBE): an optional '$', the column\nletters (L_BD91), an optional '$' and the row number (L_EE29, which must be at least 1).\nEntry: HL = text.\nExit: Fc = 0; (iy-110) = column; (iy-109/108) = row - 1; C = '$' flags (bit 1 before the\ncolumn, bit 0 before the row); A = next character; HL = after the reference.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is no valid reference."},
        "15810": {"synopsis":"Parses one or two column letters at HL into (iy-110): A-Z is 0-25, two letters give (first +\n1) * 26 + second, which must be below 64.\nEntry: HL = text.\nExit: Fc = 0; (iy-110) = column; HL = after the letters.\nError: Fc = 1 (A = 0 when the first character is not a letter)."},
        "15855": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces from HL; falls into L_BDBF.\nEntry: HL = text.\nExit: HL = first character that is not a space; A = it; Fz = 1 at the terminating zero.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "15865": {"synopsis":"Tests A for a letter (ValidateAlphabetic) and turns it into 0-25, either case.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: Fc = 1 and A = 0-25 for a letter; Fc = 0 otherwise.\nChanges: AF."},
        "15875": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine whose address is at $1D53 (set to L_BDD6 at start-up).\nEntry: as the routine."},
        "15879": {"synopsis":"Resets the display and falls into L_BE08. Sends the window set-up (L_E0B3 with A = 0), sets\nbits 1 and 2 of (iy-99), clears bit 5 of (iy-70), writes the value OS_Nq NQ_WBOX returns in\nC (L_EEFE) into byte 5 of each 6-byte entry of the table at ($1D61) (L_D590 gives the\ncount), runs L_EEDD and L_EFDC, sets the redraw flag (L_CA8D) and clears bit 5 of (iy-68).\nEntry: none."},
        "15929": {"synopsis":"Updates the display after a command (called from the main loop). Stores the cursor's column\nand row (L_D0E2) at (iy+2..4). When bit 6 of (iy-99) is set it recomputes the rows on screen\n(L_D104, L_C9F9, then L_D403 or L_D8AB and L_D452); when bit 1 is set the columns (L_D0D0,\nL_D198). Then it acts on the pending cursor move in (iy-100) and (iy-101): none goes to\nL_C1F8, a negative one to L_C1A6, otherwise (iy-101) = 0, 1 and 2 go to L_C018, L_BF0F and\nL_BEC0, and other values move the column pointer ($1D5D) on.\nEntry: none."}
      }
    },
