      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "39": {"synopsis":"Moves the current row forward by A rows (L_BFFC), then copies the current row (IY-26/25) to\n(IY-24/23) (L_C0DB).\nEntry: A = number of rows; (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: as L_BFFC; (IY-24/23) = (IY-26/25).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "45": {"synopsis":"Steps the current row (IY-26/25) forward one row at a time until A rows have been passed.\nRows found among the leading line-table entries (L_D5D1) are passed without being counted.\nStops early when the next row would reach the row count (IY-97/96) (L_C9F9).\nEntry: A = number of rows; (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = 0; (IY-26/25) = the row reached.\nError: Fc = 1 when the row count was reached; A = rows still to go.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "265": {"synopsis":"Moves the current row back by A rows (L_C0E8), then falls into L_C0DB, which copies the\ncurrent row (IY-26/25) to (IY-24/23).\nEntry: A = number of rows; (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: as L_C0E8; (IY-24/23) = (IY-26/25).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "281": {"synopsis":"Steps the current row (IY-26/25) back one row at a time (L_CA21) until A rows have been\npassed. Rows found among the leading line-table entries (L_D5D7) are not counted.\nEntry: A = number of rows; (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = 0; (IY-26/25) = the row reached.\nError: Fc = 1 when row 0 was reached; A = rows still to go, counting the one refused.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "300": {"synopsis":"Works out how many rows L_BFCC and L_C0AE move by. Takes the number of text lines on the\nscreen (L_D590), less the line-table entries with bit 7 set (L_D0F1), less the text lines\ndivided by (IY+7) when (IY+7) is not 0, less 1; the result is at least 1. Also makes the row\nof the current line entry ($1D63) the current row (L_D8A1).\nEntry: ($1D61) = line table; ($1D63) = current line entry; (IY+7).\nExit: A = number of rows (1 or more); (IY-34) = count of entries with bit 7 set; (IY-26/25)\n= row of the current line entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "346": {"synopsis":"Copies the three bytes at (IY-94..IY-92) to (IY-61..IY-59). L_C13A copies them back.\nEntry: none.\nExit: (IY-61..IY-59) = (IY-94..IY-92).\nChanges: AF, B, IX."},
        "363": {"synopsis":"Copies the three bytes at (IY-61..IY-59) to (IY-94..IY-92); the reverse of L_C129.\nEntry: none.\nExit: (IY-94..IY-92) = (IY-61..IY-59).\nChanges: AF, B, IX."},
        "380": {"synopsis":"Returns at once when bit 5 of the current line entry ($1D63) is set. Otherwise drops its\ncaller's return address and continues at L_C152: sets bit 5 of (IY-72), marks lines and\ncells to redraw (L_CA39, L_C9DF) and ends at L_C1F8, so the caller's caller resumes.\nEntry: ($1D63) = current line entry.\nExit: returns to the caller only when bit 5 of the entry is set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX (on the L_C152 path)."},
        "1166": {"synopsis":"Redraws the line-editor buffer at ($1D3D) from screen column (IY-28) on screen line (IY-27).\n1. The field is (IY-89) characters wide, cut to A - (IY-28).\n2. Moves the start offset (IY-88) so that the edit position (IY-87) lies in the field: at\nits end when it was past it (in the middle when (IY-100) bit 7 is set), at its start when it\nwas before it; returns without drawing when it was already in the field and (IY-72) bit 5 is\nclear.\n3. Prints the buffer from that offset, codes below $20 through L_CADB; at its end, unless\n(IY-85) bit 7 is set, clears up to column (IY-42) with spaces (L_C5EA). With (IY-85) bit 7\nset the rest of the field is filled with spaces.\n4. Ends any highlight left on (L_CA92).\nEntry: A = right limit (screen column).\nExit: A = column after the last character drawn, relative to (IY-28); Fc = 1 when A = 0;\n(IY-88) = new offset.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "1314": {"synopsis":"Redraws the screen line of line-table entry HL when the bit of the display flags (IY-99)\ngiven in A is set; otherwise returns Fz = 1. Falls into L_C4F6.\nEntry: A = flag mask ($20 or $10); HL = line-table entry.\nExit: as L_C4F6 when the bit is set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "1318": {"synopsis":"Redraws one screen line, the one of line-table entry HL.\n1. Keeps HL in (IY-44/43) and clears bit 5 or 4 of (IY-99) when HL is the first or last line\nwaiting for redraw ((IY-52/51), (IY-50/49)); makes the entry's row current.\n2. Bit 5 of the entry set: fills the line with '^' characters across (IY-81) columns.\n3. Otherwise moves to the line's start (L_CB02). When the 6-character left margin is on\n(L_D5A7), prints the row number (L_BC60) padded to 5 with '_' (a leading entry) or spaces,\nthen a space.\n4. When the row's column-0 cell has type bits %11 (L_D252), prints a line of '~' or the text\nbuilt by L_EE4E; otherwise draws each column of the column table (L_C612).\n5. Clears with spaces what is left of the previous drawing (byte 5 of the entry) and stores\nthe new width there.\nEntry: HL = line-table entry.\nExit: Fc = 0; byte 5 of the entry = columns drawn.\nError: Fc = 1 when L_C612 returned Fc = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "1562": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces. On screen it sends SOH '3N' with the count and a space (repeat character);\nwhen (IY-70) bit 6 is set it calls L_ED8A A times instead. Does nothing when A = 0.\nEntry: A = number of spaces.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "1602": {"synopsis":"Draws the cell of one column on the screen line being drawn (line entry (IY-44/43)).\n1. Takes the column from the column-table entry into (IY-38), keeps column and row in\n(IY-110..IY-108) (L_D77E) and makes the line's row current (L_D24C); returns Fc = 1 at once\nwhen that row's column-0 cell has type bits %11.\n2. Works out the cell's width with overflow into empty columns (L_C917, (IY-40)), whether it\nholds anything to show (L_D79A, L_C9B8), its screen position (L_D08D: column (IY-32), line\n(IY-31)) and cuts the width at the screen width (IY-81).\n3. When the cell is empty or has type bits %10 and is the cursor's slot ($1D5D on line\n($1D63)) with (IY-71) bit 6 clear, only raises (IY-42) to the cell's right edge.\n4. Otherwise sets the highlight for the marked block (L_CA99), copies bytes 3-4 of the line\nentry to (IY-91/90) and draws the contents (L_CB0E) when there are any, then pads with\nspaces (L_C5EA) and updates (IY-42) and byte 5 of the line entry.\nEntry: HL = column-table entry.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = the column-table entry.\nError: Fc = 1 as in step 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, IX."},
        "1982": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column (IY-32), line (IY-31) (L_EEE4) unless bit 7 of (IY-31) is set,\nand then sets that bit, so the move is made only once.\nEntry: (IY-32) = column; (IY-31) = line.\nExit: bit 7 of (IY-31) set.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "2005": {"synopsis":"Clears bit 2 of (IY-99) and, when the left margin is on (L_D5A7), redraws the column heading\nline: moves to line 1, prints 6 spaces, then for each column-table entry the column's\nletters (L_BC39) at the right of its width, the width before them filled with '_' (bit 7\nset), $A0 (the cursor's column) or '.'. The cursor column's character at its second width\nbyte (L_D551) is marked (L_C834). Pads the rest of the line with spaces.\nEntry: ($1D5B) = column table; ($1D5D) = cursor's entry.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "2148": {"synopsis":"Prints one character of the column heading for L_C7A5 and counts the columns left in\n(IY-36). When the countdown in (IY-38) reaches 0 on this character, prints SOH $FA instead\nof $A0 or '.', or prints the character between two SOH 'B' (L_CD74).\nEntry: A = character; (IY-36) = columns left; (IY-38) = countdown (0 = none).\nExit: Fz = 1 when (IY-36) reached 0.\nChanges: F, C, E, (IY-36), (IY-38).\nKeeps: A, HL."},
        "2198": {"synopsis":"Draws the cursor's slot reference at the window's top-left: moves the cursor to column 0,\nline 0, points ($1D4B) at L_BC17 as the output routine, prints the column and row of the\ncursor's slot (L_D0E2, L_BBBF) and pads the field to 7 characters with spaces.\nEntry: ($1D63), ($1D5D) = cursor's line and column entries.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "2228": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the text area: defines window 3 over it (SOH '6#3'; from line 1, or line 2 when the\nleft margin is on, (IY-81) wide, (IY-80) less 1 or 2 lines high), selects it (SOH '2H3'),\nsends SOH and A, selects the window that was current again (SOH '2H') and sends SOH '2D3'.\nEntry: A = SD_UP ($FE) or SD_DWN ($FF).\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "2229": {"comment":"A = 0, get current window information"},
        "2309": {"synopsis":"Shifts byte 5 (the drawn width) of the line-table entries one entry towards the start: each\nentry takes the value of the next, for the screen's text lines (L_D590) plus one. Used with\nL_C884 when the screen scrolls.\nEntry: ($1D61) = line table.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, IX."},
        "2334": {"synopsis":"Shifts byte 5 (the drawn width) of the line-table entries one entry towards the end: from\nthe last text line (L_D590) back to the second, each entry takes the value of the one\nbefore. The reverse of L_C8D9.\nEntry: ($1D61) = line table.\nExit: IX = ($1D61).\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2371": {"synopsis":"Works out how many characters the cell at column A of the current row may use: its column\nwidth (L_D54A), extended over the following columns while they are empty (L_C989), up to the\ncolumn's second width byte (L_D551). Returns at once when that byte is not above the width,\nor when (IY-71) bit 6 is set and the slot is the cursor's.\nEntry: A = column; (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: A = width, the smaller of the two.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2485": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the slot at column A of the current row has anything to show (L_D7B3, L_C9B8).\nEntry: A = column; (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the column is 0 or the slot is in the marked block (L_CFE0, tested only\nwhen (IY-70) bit 6 and (IY-67) bit 7 are clear), with Fz = 1 when it has no cell. Otherwise\nFc = 0, Fz = 1 when there is no cell or it is blank; Fc = 1, Fz = 0 when it holds text other\nthan spaces. A = column; IX = cell when there is one.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2532": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the current cell (L_B500) holds text other than spaces.\nEntry: (IY-127..IY-125) = current cell.\nExit: Fz = 1, Fc = 0 when the cell's type bits are %11; otherwise Fc = 1 when its text is\nempty or only spaces, or Fc = 0, Fz = 0 and A = the first other character, HL past it.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "2550": {"synopsis":"Marks the slot kept in (IY-110..IY-108) for redraw when it has a cell (L_D79A) and both its\nrow (L_D56B) and its column (L_D55D) are on the screen; falls into L_C9DF.\nEntry: (IY-110) = column; (IY-109/108) = row.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the cell was marked.\nError: Fc = 1 when it was not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2571": {"synopsis":"Marks the current cell for redraw: sets bit 0 of its flags byte (byte 3) and bit 3 of\n(IY-72).\nEntry: (IY-127..IY-125) = current cell.\nExit: IX = cell.\nChanges: A, IX."},
        "2583": {"synopsis":"Adds 1 to the current row (IY-26/25) and falls into L_C9F9 to compare it with the row count.\nEntry: (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: BC = new row; flags as L_C9F9.\nChanges: F, BC.\nKeeps: A."},
        "2597": {"synopsis":"Compares row BC with the row count (IY-97/96).\nEntry: BC = row.\nExit: Fc = 0 when BC is below the count; Fc = 1 when it is not, with Fz = 1 when equal.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC."},
        "2618": {"synopsis":"Adds 1 to BC and falls into L_CA0F, so the row count becomes at least BC + 2.\nEntry: BC = row; A = value for (IY-95).\nExit: as L_CA0F.\nChanges: F, BC."},
        "2619": {"synopsis":"Raises the row count (IY-97/96) to BC + 1 when it is lower, storing A in (IY-95) as well.\nEntry: BC = row; A = value for (IY-95).\nExit: BC = row + 1.\nChanges: F, BC."},
        "2634": {"synopsis":"Adds 1 to BC and compares it with the row count (L_C9F9).\nEntry: BC = row.\nExit: BC = row + 1; flags as L_C9F9.\nChanges: F, BC."},
        "2637": {"synopsis":"Moves the current row (IY-26/25) back by one, through L_CA2A.\nEntry: (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: Fc = 0; (IY-26/25) one less.\nError: Fc = 1 when the row was 0; nothing changes.\nChanges: F."},
        "2646": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_CA21: subtracts 1 from the current row (IY-26/25) without testing it.\nEntry: (IY-26/25) = current row.\nExit: (IY-26/25) one less.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "2661": {"synopsis":"Adds line-table entry HL to the lines waiting for redraw. When none is waiting, HL becomes\nthe first ((IY-52/51), bit 5 of (IY-99)); when one is, HL becomes the second ((IY-50/49),\nbit 4), and the two swap places when their high bytes differ. When two are already waiting,\ndraws line HL at once (L_C4F6).\nEntry: HL = line-table entry.\nExit: (IY-99) and the two pointers updated.\nChanges: AF, C, DE (and all of L_C4F6 on that path)."},
        "2719": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 5 of (IY-72) and bit 3 of the display flags (IY-99).\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "2728": {"synopsis":"Sets bits 0 and 6 of the display flags (IY-99).\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "2737": {"synopsis":"Sets bits 7 (L_CA8D) and 1 of the display flags (IY-99).\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "2745": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 7 of the display flags (IY-99), the flag that has every screen line redrawn.\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "2750": {"synopsis":"Ends a highlight left on: when bit 0 of (IY-85) is set, toggles it off and sends SOH 'R'\n(L_CAF0).\nEntry: (IY-85).\nExit: bit 0 of (IY-85) clear.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A."},
        "2757": {"synopsis":"Sets the highlight state (IY-85) for the slot at column (IY-38) of the current row: $81 when\nit is in the marked block (L_CFE0, only when (IY-67) bit 7 is clear), else 0. When (IY-71)\nbit 6 is set and the slot is the cursor's (L_D0E2), the value is toggled. When bit 7 ends up\nset, sends SOH 'R' (L_EFEF).\nEntry: (IY-38) = column; (IY-26/25) = row.\nExit: (IY-85) set.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "2823": {"synopsis":"Prints control code A in reverse video: a code $18-$1F (L_CE2A) as the digit 1-8, a lower\ncode as A + $40, between two toggles of reverse (L_CAF0).\nEntry: A = control code below $20.\nExit: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "2844": {"synopsis":"Toggles bit 0 of (IY-85) and sends SOH 'R' (L_EFEF) once, so the reverse-video state on\nscreen follows it.\nEntry: (IY-85).\nExit: bit 0 of (IY-85) toggled.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "2862": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the start of the screen line of line entry (IY-44/43) (L_D0B1, L_EEE3).\nEntry: (IY-44/43) = line-table entry.\nExit: B = screen line.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "2874": {"synopsis":"Draws the current cell's contents in a field of A columns and returns how many columns were\nwritten. Points ($1D4D) at the cell's text (L_FAB1) and looks at its flags byte:\n1. Bit 4 set: prints message (byte 4) of the table at L_EC31 through L_EB4D, sending it to\nL_F020, or to L_ED93 when (IY-70) bit 6 is set; returns from there.\n2. Type bits %00: formats a number through L_FE72 and L_FEF0 (byte 9), then L_FB76. Type\n%01: evaluated by L_FA25; Fc = 0 goes on as %00; result type 0 prints a message as in 1, 8 a\ndate (L_D077), others copy the result text (L_CE31).\n3. Type %11: the text built by L_EE4E. Other text: copied to $1EAA with fields expanded\n(L_CE31); for format 8 its first character (not '@') separates three parts.\n4. Prints the text aligned by format bits 3-1 (L_CBD9).\nEntry: A = field width; (IY-127..IY-125) = current cell.\nExit: A = (IY-34) = columns written.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "3070": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_CBB2 (three-part text): pads up to column A of the field, A - (IY-34) spaces,\nand prints the next part through L_CC72.\nEntry: A = column; (IY-34) = columns written so far.\nExit: as L_CC72.\nError: Fc = 1, nothing printed, when A is below (IY-34).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3077": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at ($1D4D) in a field of (IY-36) columns, aligned by bits 3-1 of A.\n1. 0: no padding. 2, 4, 6: padding before the text of none, half or all the free columns\n(L_CDF2 measures it). 8: three NUL-separated parts (L_CBB2).\n2. $0A, $0C: spreads the free columns over the gaps between words (L_CDEF), keeping a byte\nper gap in a table on the stack ((IY-30/29), (IY-78) gaps), worked out with L_F048 and\nL_F05E.\n3. Prints the text through the loop at L_CC8D: highlight codes $18-$1F (L_CD49), other\ncontrol codes (L_CADB), $7F as a space, gaps widened (L_CDA6); stops when the field is full;\nthen frees the gap table and, on screen, ends highlights still on (L_CD74).\nEntry: A = format; (IY-36) = field width; ($1D4D) = text.\nExit: (IY-34) = columns written; (IY-36) = columns left.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "3230": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces, at most the (IY-36) columns left (L_C5EA), adds them to (IY-34) and takes\nthem from (IY-36). Then prints the text at ($1D4D), its leading spaces skipped, through the\nloop at L_CC8D (see L_CBD9).\nEntry: A = spaces; (IY-36) = columns left; (IY-34) = columns written; ($1D4D) = text.\nExit: (IY-34), (IY-36) updated.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "3445": {"synopsis":"Handles highlight code A ($18-$1F) in the text output: toggles bit A - $18 of D. On screen\ncodes $18-$1B send SOH and a letter from L_CD90, and codes $1C-$1F are shown as a reverse\ndigit (L_CADB). When (IY-70) bit 6 is set, sends $05, '1' and the letter from L_CD94.\nEntry: A = code; D = highlights on.\nExit: D updated; Fc = 1 when a sequence was sent, Fc = 0 for a digit shown.\nChanges: AF, BC, D.\nKeeps: E, HL."},
        "3488": {"synopsis":"Sends SOH and letter E of the table L_CD90 ('U', 'B', 'G', 'T'), through L_CD9C.\nEntry: E = 0-3.\nExit: Fc = 1.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: DE, HL."},
        "3516": {"synopsis":"Table of 4 bytes: the letters 'U', 'B', 'G', 'T' sent after SOH for the highlight codes\n$18-$1B on screen (L_CD74, L_CD49)."},
        "3520": {"synopsis":"Table of 8 bytes: the letters 'U', 'B', 'X', 'I', 'L', 'R', 'A', 'E' sent after $05 '1' for\nthe highlight codes $18-$1F when output goes through L_ED93 (L_CD49)."},
        "3528": {"synopsis":"Outputs character A: on screen through OS_Out, or through L_ED93 when (IY-70) bit 6 is set.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: none.\nChanges: as OS_Out or L_ED93."},
        "3538": {"synopsis":"Returns how many columns gap E between words takes when text is spread out: the byte kept\nfor it in the gap table ((IY-30/29), (IY-78) entries), passed to L_CDCD. With no table it\ngives 1; with E past the table, as L_CDCA.\nEntry: E = gap number.\nExit: Fc = 0, C = columns; Fc = 1 when the gap is set as a pitch change (L_CDCD), A = the\ntable byte.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "3574": {"synopsis":"Takes C from (IY+28) and falls into L_CDCD.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_CDCD.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "3577": {"synopsis":"When (IY-70) bits 7 and 4 are both set: if C differs from (IY-89), stores it there and sends\nit with code $48 through L_EDF5; returns C = 1, Fc = 1. Otherwise C = 1, Fc = 0.\nEntry: C = value.\nExit: C = 1; Fc as above.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "3611": {"synopsis":"Measures the text at ($1D4D) counting its leading spaces; sets Fc and falls into L_CDF3, the\nbody of L_CDF2.\nEntry: ($1D4D) = text.\nExit: as L_CDF2.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3614": {"synopsis":"Measures the text at ($1D4D): its length up to its last character other than a space,\nhighlight codes $18-$1F not counted and leading spaces not counted (L_CDEF counts them), and\nthe number of gaps between words.\nEntry: ($1D4D) = text.\nExit: C = length; B = gaps; HL at the closing NUL.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3670": {"synopsis":"Tests for a highlight code.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: Fc = 1 when A is $18-$1F.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A."},
        "3677": {"synopsis":"Copies the text at ($1D4D) into the buffer at $1EAA, at most 255 bytes, with its @ fields\nexpanded (L_CEEC), and points ($1D4D) at the copy.\nEntry: B = 0: one string; B = 1: C is a separator: the first character is skipped when C is\nnot 0, each separator becomes a NUL and two more NULs end the copy.\nExit: ($1D4D) = $1EAA.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "3864": {"synopsis":"Copies text from HL to IX (L_CF9A) until a NUL is stored, expanding '@' fields: a compiled\nreference ($10-$13) through L_CE71, '@T' through L_CEB8, '@D' as today's date (GN_Gmd,\nGN_Pdt), '@P' as the number in (IY-91/90) (0 when L_D27D gives Fc = 0), and '@@' as '@'. An\n'@' not starting a field is copied.\nEntry: HL = text; IX = buffer; E = character stored as NUL; (IY-34) = room left.\nExit: B = last character copied; IX past the copy.\nError: Fc = 1 when the room ran out.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4038": {"synopsis":"Stores character A at (IX) and advances IX, storing NUL when A equals E. Counts the room in\n(IY-34): when it reaches 0 a NUL is stored instead; when it is already 0 nothing is.\nEntry: A = character; E = character turned into NUL; IX = buffer; (IY-34) = room left.\nExit: Fz = 1 when a NUL was stored; Fc = 1 when the room is used up.\nChanges: AF, D, IX.\nKeeps: C, E, HL."},
        "4071": {"synopsis":"Skips HL past the current string and its NUL and points ($1D4D) at the next one, then\nmeasures that one (L_CDF2).\nEntry: A = field width; HL = text.\nExit: A = entry A; Fz = 1 when the next string is empty; otherwise C = A - its length - 1 (0\nwhen negative).\nError: Fc = 1 when (IY-36) is 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4108": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the slot at column A of the current row is inside the marked block (L_D014):\ncolumns (IY-58) to (IY-55), rows (IY-57/56) to (IY-54/53).\nEntry: A = column; (IY-26/25) = row.\nExit: Fc = 1 when inside; Fc = 0 when outside or when there is no mark.\nChanges: AF, BC, E, IX."},
        "4160": {"synopsis":"Orders the marked block's corners: copies the marks (IY-67..IY-62), column then row, to\n(IY-58..IY-53) and swaps so that (IY-58), (IY-57/56) hold the first column and row and\n(IY-55), (IY-54/53) the last. With no second mark ((IY-64) bit 7 set), both corners are the\nfirst mark.\nEntry: (IY-67..IY-62) = marks.\nExit: Fc = 0; corners set.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is no mark ((IY-67) bit 7 set).\nChanges: AF, BC, IX."},
        "4259": {"synopsis":"Converts the internal date at ($1D4D) to text at IY+35 (GN_Pdt, A = $A0, '.' between the\nparts) and ends it with a NUL.\nEntry: ($1D4D) = 3-byte date.\nExit: text at IY+35.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4281": {"synopsis":"Works out where a slot appears on screen: adds the widths (L_D547) of the column-table\nentries before BC, plus 6 when the left margin is on, and finds the line of entry HL\n(L_D0B1).\nEntry: HL = line-table entry; BC = column-table entry.\nExit: A = screen column; B = screen line.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4317": {"synopsis":"Finds the screen line of line-table entry HL: its place in the table counted from 1, plus 1\nwhen the left margin is on (L_D5A7).\nEntry: HL = line-table entry.\nExit: A = B = screen line; C = place in the table from 0; DE = ($1D61).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4348": {"synopsis":"Finds the first column-table entry with bit 7 clear; when the end marker comes first,\nreturns the first entry.\nEntry: ($1D5B) = column table.\nExit: HL = entry; A and flags as L_D0E8.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "4366": {"synopsis":"Gives the cursor's row (L_D8B5, from line entry ($1D63)) and falls into L_D0E5 for its\ncolumn.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = row; HL = ($1D5D); A and flags as L_D0E8.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "4369": {"synopsis":"Reads the cursor's column-table entry ($1D5D) through L_D0E8.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = ($1D5D); A and flags as L_D0E8.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "4372": {"synopsis":"Reads column-table entry HL.\nEntry: HL = entry.\nExit: A = column (bits 6-0); Fc = 1 for the end marker (bit 6); Fz = 1 when bit 7 is clear.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4381": {"synopsis":"Counts the line-table entries with bit 7 set, up to the end marker (bit 6).\nEntry: ($1D61) = line table.\nExit: A = B = count.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL."},
        "4400": {"synopsis":"Makes the row of the first line-table entry with bits 7 and 5 clear (L_D10E) the current row\n(IY-26/25).\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = row; HL = entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4410": {"synopsis":"Finds the first line-table entry with bits 7 and 5 both clear; when the end marker comes\nfirst, takes the first entry. Reads its row (L_D8B8).\nEntry: ($1D61) = line table.\nExit: HL = entry; BC = row.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4436": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the column table so that column A is on screen and is the cursor's column. When A\nis not already in the table, chooses the first column so that A comes near the middle of the\nwidth left beside the bit-7 entries, moving one column if A would be first; then falls into\nL_D198.\nEntry: A = column.\nExit: as L_D198.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4548": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the column table at ($1D5B) from column A. Entries with bit 7 set are kept; the\nothers take the next columns from A upwards, skipping those already in the table (L_D5B0)\nand those of width 0, until the screen width (L_D59D) is used, the columns run out or 64\nentries are filled. Points ($1D5D) at column (IY-38)'s entry and ($1D5F) at the last, and\nsets bit 6 (end marker) on the entry after it.\nEntry: A = first column; (IY-38) = cursor's column.\nExit: table rebuilt.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4629": {"synopsis":"Sets the row count (IY-97/96) to 1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "4638": {"synopsis":"Looks for the column to show after the last column-table entry with bit 7 clear: the next\ncolumn from it (or that column itself when it is the only such entry, or is not the last\nentry ($1D5F)) whose width is not 0 and that is not in the table (L_D5B0).\nEntry: ($1D5B) = column table.\nExit: Fc = 0, B = column; HL = the last entry with bit 7 clear.\nError: Fc = 1 when there is none; HL = that entry, or the last entry with bit 7 set when all\nhave it.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4725": {"synopsis":"Makes the cursor's row (L_D8B5) current and falls into L_D24C.\nEntry: ($1D63) = cursor's line entry.\nExit: as L_D252.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4728": {"synopsis":"Makes row BC the current row (IY-26/25) and falls into L_D252.\nEntry: BC = row.\nExit: as L_D252.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4734": {"synopsis":"Tests the current row's column-0 cell (L_D7B3).\nEntry: (IY-26/25) = row.\nExit: Fc = 1 when it exists and its type bits (byte 3, bits 7-6) are %11, IX = cell;\notherwise Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4751": {"synopsis":"Stores A in byte 4 of cell IX and falls into L_D266, which tests A and byte 5 against\n(IY+7): Fc = 1 when byte 5 is 0, when A is above (IY+7), or when byte 5 is at least (IY+7) -\nA.\nEntry: A = value; IX = cell.\nExit: flags as above.\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "4754": {"synopsis":"Conditional break test for the break cell at IX: compares the lines left on the page with\nthe count in the cell's byte 5. A = the line on the page; the page length is (IY+7).\nEntry: A = line number; IX = cell.\nExit: Fc = 1 when byte 5 of the cell is 0, when A is beyond the page length, or when byte 5\nis at least the page length minus A; Fc = 0 otherwise.\nChanges: AF, DE."},
        "4772": {"synopsis":"Tests whether pagination applies: returns at once with Fz = 1 and Fc = 0 when the page\nlength (IY+7) is 0, otherwise falls into L_D27D.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fz = 1, Fc = 0 when the page length is 0; else as L_D27D.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4777": {"synopsis":"Tests the first entry of the row table at ($1D61) and bit 6 of (IY-70): Fc = 0 only when bit\n7 of that entry's flag byte is set and bit 6 of (IY-70) is clear.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 otherwise.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "4793": {"synopsis":"Advances a line number by the line spacing: A = 0 gives A = 1; any other A has (IY+8) added\nand falls into L_D293.\nEntry: A = line number.\nExit: A = the next line number, as L_D293 returns it.\nChanges: AF, E."},
        "4799": {"synopsis":"Brings a line number into the page: with page length (IY+7) of 0 returns A = 1. A value\nbelow the page length is returned unchanged (Fc = 1), one equal to it as is (Fz = 1). A\nvalue past it, or one with bit 7 set, gives A = 0 when L_D278 returns Fc = 1 and A = 1\notherwise.\nEntry: A = line number.\nExit: A = the line number on the page.\nChanges: AF, E."},
        "4826": {"synopsis":"Decrements the 16-bit page number at (IY-91) and (IY-90).\nEntry: none.\nExit: page number one lower.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4839": {"synopsis":"Increments the 16-bit page number at (IY-91) and (IY-90).\nEntry: none.\nExit: page number one higher.\nChanges: F."},
        "4847": {"synopsis":"Steps the pagination state over the row (IY-26)/(IY-25): forwards, or backwards when Fc = 1\non entry (kept in bit 7 of (IY-34)). Starts from the saved page number (IY-93)/(IY-92) and\nthe line (IY-94), and writes the new line to (IY-94) and the page number back to\n(IY-93)/(IY-92).\n1. Copies the saved page number to the working one (IY-91)/(IY-90).\n2. When L_D252 finds a break cell in column 0 at this row (L_B518 gives IX = cell), forwards\nit stores the current line (or page length plus spacing at line 0) in the cell's byte 4 and\nstarts a new page (line 1) when L_D263 says the break applies; backwards it restores the\nline from byte 4 and steps back a page when L_D266 says so.\n3. Otherwise (L_D326) it adds or subtracts the line spacing (IY+8), stepping the page at\nline 0, and normalises the line through L_D293; a result of 0 is stored with Fc = 1.\nEntry: Fc = direction (1 = backwards); (IY-26)/(IY-25) = row.\nExit: (IY-94) = line on the page; (IY-93)/(IY-92) = page number.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4929": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_D2C3: when the line (IY-94) is 0, copies the saved page number to the working\none and continues at L_D326, the step for a row without a break cell; returns at once when\nthe line is not 0.\nEntry: Fc = direction, as L_D2C3; (IY-34) bit 7 already set from it.\nExit: as L_D2C3.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "4995": {"synopsis":"Brings the pagination state to the row of the first suitable row-table entry: L_D3E9 resets\nthe state to the document start (row 0, start page, first line) and L_D104 puts that entry's\nrow in (IY-26)/(IY-25); then falls into L_D35D.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_D35E.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5001": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_D35E with Fc = 0: works out the pagination state at the row (IY-26)/(IY-25)\nfrom the row (IY-20)/(IY-19), whose state is in (IY-94) to (IY-92).\nEntry: (IY-26)/(IY-25) = target row; (IY-20)/(IY-19) = start row.\nExit: as L_D35E.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5002": {"synopsis":"Walks the pagination state from the row (IY-20)/(IY-19) to the target row (IY-26)/(IY-25),\none row at a time through L_D2C3, forwards or backwards. When the target is row 0 it only\nresets the state (L_D3F0).\n1. Swaps the two rows (L_D3C1), so (IY-26)/(IY-25) is the moving row.\n2. With Fc = 0 on entry and the line (IY-94) at 0, steps forwards over the start row first\nwhen it holds no break cell.\n3. Steps the row towards the target, applying L_D2C3 to each; a break that applies is\nstepped over again and the result kept in bit 7 of (IY-36).\n4. At the target swaps the rows back.\nEntry: (IY-26)/(IY-25) = target row; (IY-20)/(IY-19) = start row; Fc = 1 skips step 2.\nExit: (IY-20)/(IY-19) = (IY-26)/(IY-25) = target row; (IY-94) to (IY-92) = its state; Fc =\nthe bit last kept in bit 7 of (IY-36).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5101": {"synopsis":"Swaps the row (IY-26)/(IY-25) with the row (IY-20)/(IY-19), then rotates (IY-36) left\nthrough the carry.\nEntry: none.\nExit: rows swapped; Fc = old bit 7 of (IY-36).\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "5130": {"synopsis":"Moves the row (IY-26)/(IY-25) one back (L_CA2A) when Fc = 1, otherwise falls into L_D3E1 and\nmoves it one forward.\nEntry: Fc = direction (1 = back).\nExit: row stepped.\nChanges: F."},
        "5133": {"synopsis":"Increments the 16-bit row number at (IY-26) and (IY-25).\nEntry: none.\nExit: row one higher.\nChanges: F."},
        "5141": {"synopsis":"Sets the row (IY-20)/(IY-19) to 0 and falls into L_D3F0, which resets the pagination state.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_D3F0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "5148": {"synopsis":"Resets the pagination state to the document start: the line (IY-94) from (IY+12) and the\nsaved page number (IY-93)/(IY-92) from the start page (IY+10)/(IY+11).\nEntry: none.\nExit: state reset.\nChanges: A."},
        "5167": {"synopsis":"Rebuilds the row table at ($1D61) (6-byte entries: flag byte, row number, page number) for\nthe screen with row BC as the cursor row.\n1. Limits BC to the last row (one below the row count (IY-97)/(IY-96), L_C9F9) and stores it\nin (IY-24)/(IY-23) and (IY-26)/(IY-25).\n2. Counts the entries with bit 7 set, then moves the top row back from BC by half of the\nlines L_D590 gives minus one minus that count, not counting rows those entries hold\n(L_D5D7).\n3. Continues at L_D452.\nEntry: BC = cursor row.\nExit: row table rebuilt; ($1D63) = the cursor row's entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5246": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_D403: sets (IY-20)/(IY-19) to the row of the first suitable row-table entry\n(L_D10E); unless the first entry has bit 7 set, brings the pagination state to the top row\n(IY-26)/(IY-25) through L_D35E; then continues at L_D469.\nEntry: (IY-26)/(IY-25) = top row; (IY-24)/(IY-23) = cursor row.\nExit: as L_D469.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5269": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_D403: fills the row table at ($1D61) (6-byte entries: flag byte, row number,\npage number) from the top row (IY-26)/(IY-25) with the pagination state in (IY-94) to\n(IY-92), one entry for each of the lines L_D590 gives. Each entry gets its row and page\nnumber. A line where a page break falls gets flag bit 5 and does not use up a row; entries\nwith bit 7 set keep their own row while it is below the row count. The table ends with $40\nat the first line past the last row. ($1D63) is set to the entry of the cursor row\n(IY-24)/(IY-23).\nEntry: (IY-26)/(IY-25) = top row; (IY-24)/(IY-23) = cursor row.\nExit: row table rebuilt.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5491": {"synopsis":"Reads the column number from the column list byte at HL (L_D0E8) and falls into L_D54A.\nEntry: HL = column list entry.\nExit: A = byte 0 of that column's record.\nChanges: AF."},
        "5494": {"synopsis":"Returns byte 0 of column A's 10-byte record at ($1D3F) (the column's width; L_D8D1 sets 12\nfor a new column).\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: A = byte 0 of the record.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "5501": {"synopsis":"Returns byte 1 of column A's 10-byte record at ($1D3F), or byte 0 when byte 1 is 0.\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: A = byte 1 of the record, or byte 0.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "5513": {"synopsis":"Searches the column list at ($1D5B) from its start for the column A (bit 7 of each entry\nignored, L_D0E8), up to the entry with bit 6 set.\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1, HL = the matching entry.\nError: Fc = 1 when the end of the list is reached.\nChanges: AF, E, HL."},
        "5527": {"synopsis":"Looks up row BC in the row table at ($1D61) (6-byte entries: flag byte, row number, page\nnumber), skipping entries with bit 5 set, up to the entry with bit 6 set.\nEntry: BC = row number.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1, HL = the entry.\nError: Fc = 1, HL = the end entry, when the row is not in the table.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "5564": {"synopsis":"Returns the number of entries the row table ($1D61) covers: (IY-80) minus 1, minus one more\nwhen bit 1 of (IY-69) is set (L_D5A7).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = number of lines; E = (IY-80) - 1; Fc as L_D5A7.\nChanges: AF, E."},
        "5577": {"synopsis":"Returns (IY-81), less 6 when bit 1 of (IY-69) is set (L_D5A7).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = (IY-81) or (IY-81) - 6.\nChanges: AF."},
        "5587": {"synopsis":"Tests bit 1 of (IY-69).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the bit is set; A = (IY-69) AND 2.\nChanges: AF."},
        "5596": {"synopsis":"Searches the column list at ($1D5B) for column A, among the entries that have bit 7 set,\nstopping at the first entry without it or after 64 entries.\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: Fc = 1 when found, Fc = 0 when not; A = column number.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "5629": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the row (IY-26)/(IY-25) and falls into L_D5D7.\nEntry: BC = row number.\nExit: as L_D5D7.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5635": {"synopsis":"Looks for the row (IY-26)/(IY-25) among the leading entries of the row table at ($1D61)\n(6-byte entries: flag byte, row number, page number) that have flag bit 7 set and bit 6\nclear.\nEntry: (IY-26)/(IY-25) = row number.\nExit: Fc = 1, HL = the entry, when one of them holds the row.\nError: Fc = 0 at the first entry with bit 7 clear or bit 6 set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "5665": {"synopsis":"Table of 12 entries of 4 bytes read by L_D631: a word with a block size and the address of\nthe word that receives the block allocated for it (sizes $41, $41, $32, $100, $0F, $0F, $3C,\n$3C, $32, $32, $64, $64 for the pointers at $1D5B, $1D61, $1D75, $1D3D, $1D65, $1D67, $1D69,\n$1D6B, $1D6D, $1D6F, $1D71, $1D73)."},
        "5725": {"synopsis":"Sets up PipeDream's memory and workspace at start-up.\n1. Opens a memory pool for segment 0 (OS_Mop, handle in $1D39) and allocates the 12 blocks\nof L_D5F5 from it (L_D96E), storing each address in its pointer.\n2. Allocates a $E5-byte block, points IY $7F bytes into it and binds its bank into segment 0\n(OS_Mpb); clears some flags and variables.\n3. Opens a second pool for segment 1 with multiple banks (handle in $1D3B) and builds the\nfast bank switching code for segment 1 at $1D7F (OS_Fc).\n4. Clears the column list ($1D5B) and the row table ($1D61); reads the PA_Iov panel setting\n(OS_Nq) and sets bit 2 of (IY-71) unless it is 'I'; calls L_E0EA.\n5. Sets the start page to 1 and (IY+12) to 1 and continues at L_D6D9. On a failure to open a\npool it leaves with OS_Bye and RC_Room; on a failed allocation it first closes the pool\n(OS_Mcl).\nEntry: none.\nExit: workspace ready; IY = workspace pointer."},
        "5893": {"synopsis":"Resets the document to an empty sheet: keeps only bit 2 of (IY-71), zeroes a set of\nvariables (among them the column count (IY-98)), empties the strings at ($1D6D), ($1D6F) and\n($1D71), sets the column pointers $1D5D and $1D5F to ($1D5B) and $1D63 to ($1D61), calls\nL_D1E9, clears the 64 column records at ($1D3F) and the column list, clears the flags of the\nfirst 8 row-table entries, calls L_E7CA and continues at L_D758, which ends both tables with\n$40, lays out the screen from row 0 (L_D403) and leaves through L_D128 with A = 0.\nEntry: none."},
        "6005": {"synopsis":"Creates six columns (L_D8CD), sets byte 1 of their records from 72 through L_D76C (A = 0, C\n= $48) and continues at L_D758: ends the row table and the column list with $40, lays out\nthe screen from row 0 (L_D403) and leaves through L_D128 with A = 0.\nEntry: none."},
        "6040": {"synopsis":"Stores C in byte 1 of the record of column A, then for each following column (up to 63)\nsubtracts the previous column's byte 0 from C and stores the result, stopping when the\nsubtraction goes below 0.\nEntry: A = first column; C = value for that column.\nExit: B = column after the last one written.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "6058": {"synopsis":"Saves A, C and B in (IY-110), (IY-109) and (IY-108).\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: values saved.\nChanges: none."},
        "6068": {"synopsis":"Returns the word in bytes 2 and 3 of column A's record, or 0 when its bit 15 is set.\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: BC = the word, or 0.\nChanges: F, BC, HL."},
        "6083": {"synopsis":"Saves A and BC through L_D77E, then looks up the cell they name (falls into L_D79A).\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: as L_D7B3.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6086": {"synopsis":"Looks up the cell whose column and row L_D77E saved in (IY-110) to (IY-108), through L_D7AD\nand L_D7B3.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_D7B3; A, BC = the saved column and row.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6097": {"synopsis":"Looks up the cell of column A at row $7FFF (through L_D7AD and L_D7B3).\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: as L_D7B3.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6102": {"synopsis":"Looks up the cell under the cursor: the row from the current row-table entry ($1D63) and the\ncolumn from the column list entry at ($1D5D) (L_D0E2), then L_D7AD.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_D7B3.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6105": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the row (IY-26)/(IY-25) and falls into L_D7B3.\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: as L_D7B3.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6111": {"synopsis":"Looks up the cell of column A at the row (IY-26)/(IY-25). Each column's 10-byte record at\n($1D3F) remembers a row (bytes 2-3, bit 15 set when the column has no cells) and the cell\nthere with its neighbour (bytes 4-6 and 7-9, address and bank). The cells form a list whose\nlinks are the XOR of the neighbours' addresses and banks; the routine walks it forwards or\nbackwards from the remembered row, binding each cell's bank in segment 1 (L_D887), and\nstores the position it reaches back in the record.\nEntry: A = column; (IY-26)/(IY-25) = row.\nExit: Fc = 0: IX = the cell, (IY-127) to (IY-125) = its address and bank, bank bound in\nsegment 1.\nError: Fc = 1 when A is not below the column count (IY-98), the column has no cells or no\ncell has that row.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6323": {"synopsis":"Binds bank A into segment 1 through the fast bank switching code at $1D7F (set up by OS_Fc)\nand records it in (IY-111).\nEntry: A = bank.\nExit: bank bound.\nChanges: none known (the code at $1D7F is built by OS_Fc)."},
        "6329": {"synopsis":"Returns the record of the current column: the column number from the column list entry at\n($1D5D) (L_D0E5), then L_D890.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = column number; HL = its record.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "6332": {"synopsis":"Returns the address of column A's 10-byte record: ($1D3F) + 10 * A.\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: HL = the record.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE."},
        "6349": {"synopsis":"Stores the row of the current row-table entry ($1D63) in (IY-26)/(IY-25).\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = the row; HL = the entry.\nChanges: BC, HL."},
        "6359": {"synopsis":"Stores the row of the current row-table entry ($1D63) in (IY-24)/(IY-23).\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = the row; HL = the entry.\nChanges: BC, HL."},
        "6369": {"synopsis":"Returns the row of the current row-table entry: HL = ($1D63), then L_D8B8.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = the row; HL = the entry.\nChanges: BC, HL."},
        "6372": {"synopsis":"Returns the row number held in bytes 1 and 2 of the row-table entry at HL.\nEntry: HL = entry.\nExit: BC = the row.\nChanges: BC.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "6379": {"synopsis":"Adds columns (L_D8CD) until column A exists, that is until A is below the column count\n(IY-98).\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the column exists.\nError: Fc = 1, C = 5 when the 64-column limit is reached.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "6393": {"synopsis":"Adds a column after the last one, unless there are already 64 (L_D8E9), and falls into\nL_D8D1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_D8D1.\nError: Fc = 1, C = 5 when there are 64 columns.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "6397": {"synopsis":"Initialises the record of column A: byte 0 = 12, bytes 1-9 = 0 except byte 3 = $80 (no\nremembered row), and increments the column count (IY-98).\nEntry: A = column number.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = record + 3; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "6421": {"synopsis":"Tests the column count (IY-98) against the limit of 64 (falls into L_D8EC).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = column count; Fc = 1 and C = 5 when it is 64 or more.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "6424": {"synopsis":"Tests A against the limit of 64 columns.\nEntry: A = column count or number.\nExit: Fc = 1 when A is 64 or more, Fc = 0 otherwise; C = 5.\nChanges: F, C."},
        "6430": {"synopsis":"Initialises the cell block last allocated by L_D926: L_D948 makes it current; the three link\nbytes are cleared, byte 3 gets the cell flags (IY-36), and one more byte (bit 7 of the flags\nset) or six more bytes (clear) are cleared.\nEntry: (IY-36) = cell flags.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = the block, its bank bound in segment 1.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "6476": {"synopsis":"Allocates a cell block for C = (IY-40) and B = (IY-42) (falls into L_D926).\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_D926.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL, IX."},
        "6482": {"synopsis":"Allocates a cell block from the segment 1 pool ($1D3B) with OS_Mal: C plus 4 bytes, plus 6\nmore when bit 7 of B is clear; B is saved as the cell flags in (IY-36). The block's address\nand bank go to $1D36-$1D38 (the previous bank there is passed to OS_Mal in A).\nEntry: B = cell flags; C = length.\nExit: Fc = 0, block allocated.\nError: Fc = 1, C = 1 when OS_Mal fails.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL, IX."},
        "6516": {"synopsis":"Makes the block at $1D36-$1D38 the current cell: copies its address and bank to (IY-127) to\n(IY-125) and binds the bank in segment 1 when it is not already (L_D887).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = block address; A = its bank.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "6538": {"synopsis":"Frees the block at (IY-117)/(IY-116) in the bank bound in segment 1 (IY-111) to the segment\n1 pool ($1D3B) with OS_Mfr.\nEntry: BC = block size.\nExit: as OS_Mfr: Fc = 0 on success.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, HL, IX."},
        "6554": {"synopsis":"Allocates BC bytes from the segment 0 pool ($1D39) with OS_Mal (A = 0).\nEntry: BC = size.\nExit: Fc = 0, BHL = the block.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "6562": {"synopsis":"Frees the block at (IY-117)/(IY-116) to the segment 0 pool ($1D39) with OS_Mfr, taking the\nbank from the binding of segment 0 (OS_Mgb).\nEntry: BC = block size.\nExit: as OS_Mfr: Fc = 0 on success.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, HL, IX."},
        "6582": {"synopsis":"Runs a form of prompts and fields (a dialog) described at HL, and returns when the user\nconfirms or leaves it. After a leading byte each item is a type byte (bits 0-3: type 1-12,\nbit 7: it has a Yes/No part, bit 6: type 1 reads the \"NAME\" mailbox), its zero-ended prompt,\nfour more bytes for type 7, and a byte giving the Yes/No part's start value; a 0 ends the\nlist. Each type has a text buffer (L_DBF7) and a check routine (table L_DD1A).\n1. With bit 6 of (IY-71) set it reports error 25 (L_EB07) instead.\n2. Records the form in (IY-32)/(IY-31) and the Yes/No states at IY+$4D onwards.\n3. Draws the prompts (L_DC5C) and edits the fields one at a time (L_DC91); the keys of\nL_DBD1 edit the text, others move between items or toggle Yes/No.\n4. On confirm checks each used field with its routine and reports a failure (L_EB07), going\nback to editing; otherwise closes the form (L_DBB4).\nEntry: HL = form description.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = the Yes/No states ORed together (Fz = 1 when none is set).\nError: Fc = 1 when the form is left with the escape key code ($35).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "6799": {"synopsis":"Zero-ended name \"NAME\": the mailbox L_D98A reads with OS_Sr (SR_RPD) into the type 1 buffer\nat $1FAA (50 bytes) for an item that has bit 6 set."},
        "7135": {"synopsis":"Closes a form: L_E0D4 and the sequence 1, \"2D2\" sent with OS_Pout, then L_B411, L_BDD2 and\nL_B411 again, which it leaves through.\nEntry: none."},
        "7154": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 7 of C when the type byte of form item B has bit 7 set (the item has a Yes/No\npart).\nEntry: B = item number.\nExit: C bit 7 set for such an item; A = type byte.\nChanges: AF, C, E, HL."},
        "7163": {"synopsis":"Key code list for the form editor (L_D98A, through L_E593): 11 codes that are passed to\nMthKeyAction while a text field is edited, ended by $FF."},
        "7175": {"synopsis":"When bit 0 of (IY-72) is set, clears it and copies the zero-ended edit buffer at ($1D3D) to\nthe text buffer of form item B (L_DBF7).\nEntry: B = item number.\nExit: buffer updated.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "7201": {"synopsis":"Returns the text buffer of form item B: jumps through the table L_DC1D by the item's type\n(bits 0-3 of its type byte).\nEntry: B = item number.\nExit: HL = buffer; C = its size (0 when the type has none).\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL."},
        "7220": {"synopsis":"Returns form item B of the form at (IY-32)/(IY-31): skips B items (L_DD05).\nEntry: B = item number.\nExit: HL = the item; A = its type byte.\nChanges: AF, E, HL."},
        "7239": {"synopsis":"Table of 12 words: for each form item type 1-12, the routine that returns its text buffer in\nHL and its size in C (L_DC35 to L_DC59), read by L_DBF7."},
        "7263": {"synopsis":"Text buffer of form item type 1: HL = $1FAA, C = 50.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = buffer; C = size.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "7269": {"synopsis":"Text buffer of form item types 3, 7 and 12: HL = ($1D67), C = 15.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = buffer; C = size.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "7275": {"synopsis":"Text buffer of form item types 2, 5, 10 and 11: HL = ($1D65), C = 15.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = buffer; C = size.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "7281": {"synopsis":"Text buffer of form item type 6: HL = ($1D71), C = 100.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = buffer; C = size.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "7287": {"synopsis":"Text buffer of form item type 8: HL = ($1D6D), C = 50.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = buffer; C = size.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "7293": {"synopsis":"Text buffer of form item type 9: HL = ($1D6F), C = 50.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = buffer; C = size.\nChanges: C, HL."},
        "7299": {"synopsis":"Form item type 4 has no text buffer: C = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: C = 0.\nChanges: C."},
        "7302": {"synopsis":"Draws the form at (IY-32)/(IY-31): each item's prompt on its own line from column 1\n(L_EEE4), then its field (L_DC91 with C = 0) and, for an item with a Yes/No part, that part\ntoo (C = $80).\nEntry: none.\nExit: form drawn.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7355": {"synopsis":"Shows the field of form item B: with bit 7 of C set, or for a type with no text buffer,\nwrites \"Yes\" or \"No\" from the item's state (L_DCCB); otherwise copies the item's buffer to\nthe edit buffer ($1D3D) and displays it for editing (L_E585, L_E5C5). The field starts at\ncolumn $28, or $2C for the text part of an item with a Yes/No part; (IY-28)/(IY-27) get its\ncolumn and line, (IY-86) the buffer size.\nEntry: B = item number; C bit 7 = the Yes/No part.\nExit: Fc = 0 when a text field is ready for editing, Fc = 1 when Yes/No was written.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "7413": {"synopsis":"Shows a dialog field's Yes/No state: puts the cursor at column $28 of row B + 1, prints \"No\n\" or \"Yes\" by the field's state byte (L_DCEF), and puts the cursor back at column $28, row B\n+ 1.\nEntry: B = field number; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7447": {"synopsis":"Reads a dialog field's Yes/No state byte (at IY+$4D+B, L_DCF7) and tests it.\nEntry: B = field number; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: A = the state byte; Fz = 1 when it is zero (No).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7455": {"synopsis":"Returns the address of a dialog field's Yes/No state byte: IY + $4D + B.\nEntry: B = field number; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: HL = IY + $4D + B.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "7469": {"synopsis":"Steps over one entry of a dialog's field list. An entry is a type byte, a zero-terminated\nprompt, four more bytes when the type's low nibble is 7, and a last byte (the initial Yes/No\nstate when bit 7 of the type is set).\nEntry: HL = the entry's type byte.\nExit: HL = the entry's last byte.\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "7490": {"synopsis":"Table of 12 words: the routine that checks and stores a dialog field's text, for field types\n1 to 12 (the low nibble of the field's type byte). L_DB47 calls the entry through L_B8B4\nwith HL = ($1D65) and DE = the field's entry; a routine returns Fc = 1 with C = the message\nnumber when the text is not accepted."},
        "7514": {"synopsis":"Field type 1 (L_DD1A): parses the file name in the buffer at $1FAA with GN_Prs.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0; C = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_xxx); C = 0, so the OZ error is reported."},
        "7525": {"synopsis":"Field type 4 (L_DD1A): a Yes/No field has no text, so it accepts at once.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: F."},
        "7527": {"synopsis":"Field type 3 (L_DD1A): reads two decimal numbers from the text at ($1D67) (L_DFFB) and\nstores them as words at IY+51 and IY+54.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; IY+51/IY+52 = the first number; IY+54/IY+55 = the second.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $0E when a number is missing.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7556": {"synopsis":"Field type 5 (L_DD1A): reads a column (L_DDBB) into IY+53 and an optional second column\n(L_DFEA) into IY+54; a missing second column repeats the first.\nEntry: HL = the field's text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $21 when the first column is missing; Fc = 1, C = $0E when the second\ncolumn comes before the first."},
        "7579": {"synopsis":"Field type 6 (L_DD1A): continues in L_BC6D (bank 5) with HL = ($1D71), the type's text\nbuffer (L_DC47), IX = ($1D73) and Fc = 0.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "7590": {"synopsis":"Field type 7 (L_DD1A): reads a decimal number from the text at ($1D67) (L_DFFB), stores it\nas a word at IY+51 and checks it against the minimum and maximum words that follow the\nprompt in the field's entry. An empty text gives 0.\nEntry: DE = the field's entry (its type byte); IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; IY+51/IY+52 = the number.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $11 when the number is out of range.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7651": {"synopsis":"Field type 10 (L_DD1A), also called by L_DD5C: reads a column (L_DFEA) and stores it at\nIY+53.\nEntry: HL = the field's text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = the column; IY+53 = the column.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $21 when no column is given."},
        "7665": {"synopsis":"Field type 11 (L_DD1A): reads a slot reference (L_DFE0) and stores it at IY+$35 and IY+$38,\nthen reads an optional second one into IY+$38; then L_DE4A copies the six bytes from IY+$35\nto IY-$3A and checks them through L_FBBD.\nEntry: HL = the field's text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $0B when a reference is not valid; Fc = 1, C = $0E when L_FBBD rejects\nthe pair."},
        "7709": {"synopsis":"Field type 2 (L_DD1A): reads a slot reference (L_DFE0), or takes the current slot (L_D0E2,\nL_D77E) when the text is blank, and stores its three bytes at IY+$38 (L_DE0D).\nEntry: HL = the field's text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = IY + $3B.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $0B when the reference is not valid."},
        "7733": {"synopsis":"Copies the three bytes at IY-110, IY-109 and IY-108 (the column and row the last slot\nreference parse left there) to (HL) onwards and advances HL past them. Entry inside L_DDF5.\nEntry: HL = destination; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: HL = HL + 3.\nChanges: A, HL."},
        "7749": {"synopsis":"Field type 12 (L_DD1A): the same as L_DDC9 for the text at ($1D67): reads one or two slot\nreferences into IY+$3B and IY+$3E, then L_DE4A copies the six bytes from IY+$3B to IY-$3A\nand checks them through L_FBBD.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $0B when a reference is not valid; Fc = 1, C = $0E when L_FBBD rejects\nthe pair."},
        "7820": {"synopsis":"Field type 8 (L_DD1A): compiles the text at ($1D6D) into the buffer at ($1D69) (L_DEAA) with\nbits 6 and 7 of IY+29 clear, then sets bit 6 and stores the end of the compiled bytes at\nIY+32/IY+33.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; bit 6 of IY+29 set.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $20 when the text is blank or compiles to nothing (bit 6 left clear); Fc\n= 1 with L_DEAA's C when it fails."},
        "7870": {"synopsis":"Field type 9 (L_DD1A): compiles the text at ($1D6F) into the buffer at ($1D6B) (L_DEAA) and\nsets bit 7 of IY+29 when that succeeds, clears it when it fails.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; bit 7 of IY+29 set.\nError: Fc = 1 with L_DEAA's C; bit 7 of IY+29 clear."},
        "7890": {"synopsis":"Compiles a text into a byte string. Characters are copied as they are; a \"^\" and the next\ncharacter (in upper case) is looked up in L_DFA8: \"^^\" gives \"^\", the others run a routine\nof L_DFC7 that appends a zero and a code byte (and for some an argument). The string ends\nwith $00, $0A. The output pointer is kept at IY-36/IY-35 and the count at IY-38 (L_DF88).\nEntry: HL = the text (ends at a zero or CR); DE = destination.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = number of bytes written; HL = past the text and its CR.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $1F for an unknown \"^\" code, $1E when the string grows to 60 bytes, or\nthe code of a failed slot reference."},
        "7990": {"synopsis":"\"^R\" in L_DEAA (L_DFC7): appends $00, $02, then either \"#\" and an optional digit (L_DF77) or\n$10 and the three bytes of the slot reference that follows (L_DFE0).\nEntry: HL = the \"R\" in the text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = the reference's last character.\nError: Fc = 1 when nothing or no valid reference follows."},
        "8038": {"synopsis":"\"^B\" in L_DEAA (L_DFC7): appends $00, $00; refused (Fc = 1) when bit 6 of IY+29 is set.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1.\nChanges: AF, E."},
        "8048": {"synopsis":"\"^#\" in L_DEAA (L_DFC7): appends $00, $04 and an optional digit (L_DF77).\nEntry: HL = the \"#\" in the text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $1F or $1E (L_DF77, L_DF88).\nChanges: AF, C, E, HL."},
        "8052": {"synopsis":"\"^?\" in L_DEAA (L_DFC7): appends $00, $06 and an optional digit (L_DF77); shares its tail\nwith L_DF48.\nEntry: HL = the \"?\" in the text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $1F or $1E (L_DF77, L_DF88).\nChanges: AF, C, E, HL."},
        "8068": {"synopsis":"\"^1\" to \"^9\" in L_DEAA (L_DFC7): appends $00, $0C and the digit's character code minus $19.\nEntry: HL = the digit in the text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $1E (L_DF88).\nChanges: AF, C, E."},
        "8082": {"synopsis":"\"^S\" in L_DEAA (L_DFC7): appends $00, $08.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $1E (L_DF88).\nChanges: AF, C, E."},
        "8095": {"synopsis":"Reads the optional digit after a \"^#\", \"^?\" or \"^R#\" code (L_DEAA). Returns at once when bit\n6 of IY+29 is clear; otherwise the next character must be \"1\" to \"9\", and its value minus\none is appended (falls into L_DF88).\nEntry: HL = the code character; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = the digit when one was read.\nError: Fc = 1, C = $1F, and the caller's return address is dropped (returns to its caller).\nChanges: AF, C, HL."},
        "8112": {"synopsis":"Appends a byte to the compiled string of L_DEAA: stores A at the pointer in IY-36/IY-35,\nadvances it and counts it in IY-38.\nEntry: A = byte; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: when the count reaches 60: Fc = 1, C = $1E, and the caller's return address is\ndropped (returns to its caller).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "8144": {"synopsis":"Table of the \"^\" codes L_DEAA knows, as pairs of a character and a code, ending with $00:\n\"1\" to \"9\" give $8A, \"B\" $88, \"R\" $80, \"#\" $82, \"?\" $84, \"^\" \"^\" and \"S\" $86. A code with\nbit 7 set selects a routine of L_DFC7 (bits 0-6 are its offset); one without is stored as it\nis."},
        "8175": {"synopsis":"Table of 6 words: the routines of L_DEAA's \"^\" codes, by the offset in L_DFA8's code: L_DF0E\n(\"R\"), L_DF48 (\"#\"), L_DF4C (\"?\"), L_DF6A (\"S\"), L_DF3E (\"B\"), L_DF5C (\"1\"-\"9\")."},
        "8187": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces in a text.\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: HL = the first character that is not a space; A = that character; Fz = 1 when it is a\nzero or a CR (the end of the text).\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "8200": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces and parses a slot reference (L_BD57); the column and row are left at IY-110 to\nIY-108.\nEntry: HL = the text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fz = 0; Fc = 0; HL = past the reference; E = 1.\nError: Fz = 1, Fc = 1 when the text is blank; Fz = 0, Fc = 1 when the reference is not\nvalid."},
        "8210": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces and parses a column name (L_BD91).\nEntry: HL = the text; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fz = 0; A = the column (IY-110); E = 1; HL = past the column name.\nError: Fz = 1 when the text is blank or holds no column name."},
        "8227": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces and reads a decimal number (L_EE29, GN_Gdn).\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 0: BC = the number, HL = past it; Fc = 0, Fz = 1: no number.\nError: Fz = 1, Fc = 1 when the text is blank.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "8238": {"synopsis":"Waits for a one-key answer: purges the keyboard buffer (L_EB49) and reads a key without a\ntimeout (L_E02C). Callers use it for questions such as \"Overwrite text?\".\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0: A = the character, a command code below $20, or $20 for any other command.\nError: Fc = 1, A = $1B for ESCAPE; Fc = 1, A = RC_Esc after a pre-emption has redrawn the\nscreen (L_BDD2); Fc = 1, A = RC_OK or RC_Time otherwise."},
        "8276": {"synopsis":"Reads a key: switches the cursor on, waits with OS_Tin (L_E090), switches the cursor off,\nfetches a command with OS_In after a zero, and ignores control codes. RC_Quit leaves\nPipeDream (Exit_PipeDream).\nEntry: Fc = 1 for a timeout of $2D centiseconds (unless bit 5 of IY-68 is set); Fc = 0 waits\nwithout a timeout.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fv = 0: A = the character (>= $20); Fc = 1, Fv = 0: A = the MTH command code\nminus one (for MthKeyAction); ESCAPE gives A = $35.\nError: Fv = 1 (Fc = 0): A = RC_OK after the timeout, RC_Esc after RC_Draw (pre-emption),\nRC_Time for any other error.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "8376": {"synopsis":"Reads a byte with OS_Tin and acknowledges an ESCAPE (L_E097).\nEntry: BC = timeout in centiseconds.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = the byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_xxx).\nChanges: AF."},
        "8383": {"synopsis":"Acknowledges an ESCAPE and flushes the input buffer (OS_Esc, SC_ACK).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A."},
        "8391": {"synopsis":"Puts the cursor back at the position L_E0A7 saved in $1D7D (L_EEE4).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = column + $20; BC = the saved position.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "8399": {"synopsis":"Saves the cursor position of the current window (OS_Nq, NQ_WCUR) in $1D7D for L_E09F.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = the position (C = column, B = row)."},
        "8411": {"synopsis":"Defines window 1, PipeDream's text window, at the top left of the screen with 8 rows and\nselects it (falls into L_E0D4). With A = 0 the width leaves room for the map (L_E0EA);\notherwise it is A columns.\nEntry: A = 0, or the width; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: IY-81 = width - 1; IY-80 = 8."},
        "8443": {"synopsis":"Selects window 1 (VDU 1, \"2H1\").\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "8447": {"synopsis":"Selects window 2 (VDU 1, \"2H2\"); shares its tail with L_E0D4.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "8465": {"synopsis":"Defines the map in window 5 with OS_Map (MP_DEF) at the panel's width; stores the map's\npixel width at IY+100 (0 when there is no map) and 64 rows at IY+101; then sets the text\nwindow's size from the columns left over (falls into L_E0FC).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: IY-81 = $5D - the map's character width (the text window's width - 1); IY-80 = 8."},
        "8483": {"synopsis":"Sets the text window's size variables: IY-81 = A - 1 (width - 1) and IY-80 = 8 (rows).\nEntry: A = width; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: A = A - 1.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8492": {"synopsis":"Draws the page map when the panel has one (IY+100 > 0); the main loop calls it when it has\nwaited for a key without one coming.\n1. Clears the map's variables at $1D77-$1D7B and its pixel line at $1FDD (L_E309).\n2. Lays the current page out again from its first row with the output routine L_E1F9, which\nturns each printed character into a pixel (L_E2A9) and each line into a map line (L_E2D8).\n3. Stops when a key is waiting (L_E31D), ESCAPE is pressed (L_F023) or the map is full,\nwrites the remaining lines and restores the saved row variables.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the map was finished; Fc = 1 when it was stopped."},
        "8912": {"synopsis":"Sets the map pixel of the current column ($1D77) in the pixel line at $1FDD (bit 7 is the\nleftmost pixel of each byte), then advances the column (falls into L_E2CB).\nEntry: none.\nExit: as L_E2CB.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "8946": {"synopsis":"Advances the map column $1D77 by one unless that reaches the map's width (IY+100).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0 when advanced.\nError: Fc = 1 at the right edge (column unchanged).\nChanges: AF."},
        "8959": {"synopsis":"Writes the pixel line at $1FDD to the map at row $1D78 (OS_Map, MP_WR, window 5), clears it\n(L_E309), sets the column $1D77 to 0 and advances the row. When the row reaches IY+101 it\nsets bit 7 of $1D79 (the map is full).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 when the map is (or becomes) full.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "9008": {"synopsis":"Clears the map's pixel line at $1FDD: (IY+100 + 7) / 8 bytes.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: A = 0; B = 0; HL = past the line.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "9028": {"synopsis":"Examines the input with OS_Xin (is a key or pre-emption waiting).\nEntry: none.\nExit: as OS_Xin: Fc = 0 when input is waiting.\nChanges: AF."},
        "9031": {"synopsis":"Runs the command whose MTH code minus one is in A, through MthKeyJmpTable. A code of $5F or\nabove is not a command and returns at once.\nEntry: A = command code - 1 (as L_E02C returns it).\nExit: as the command's routine; Fc = 0 when A >= $5F.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, and what the command changes."},
        "9033": {"comment":"this is not an MTH key press.."},
        "9047": {"synopsis":"Table of 95 words: the routine of each PipeDream command, by its MTH command code minus one\n(the codes of mthcmd in mth/appmth.asm): 0 Mark Block, 6 Sort, 18 ENTER, 32 the COBRA easter\negg, 52 Swap Case, 57 Load, 58 Save, 59 Name, 81 Options Page, 82 Print, ... Read by\nMthKeyAction.","comment":"0  ($00), <>Z, Mark block"},
        "9049": {"comment":"1  ($01)"},
        "9051": {"comment":"2  ($02)"},
        "9053": {"comment":"3  ($03)"},
        "9055": {"comment":"4  ($04)"},
        "9057": {"comment":"5  ($05)"},
        "9059": {"comment":"6  ($06), <>BSO, Sort block"},
        "9061": {"comment":"7  ($07)"},
        "9063": {"comment":"8  ($08)"},
        "9065": {"comment":"9  ($09)"},
        "9067": {"comment":"10 ($0A)"},
        "9069": {"comment":"11 ($0B)"},
        "9071": {"comment":"12 ($0C)"},
        "9073": {"comment":"13 ($0D)"},
        "9075": {"comment":"14 ($0E)"},
        "9077": {"comment":"15 ($0F)"},
        "9079": {"comment":"16 ($10)"},
        "9081": {"comment":"17 ($11)"},
        "9083": {"comment":"18 ($12), ENTER"},
        "9085": {"comment":"19 ($13)"},
        "9087": {"comment":"20 ($14)"},
        "9089": {"comment":"21 ($15), Cursor Right"},
        "9091": {"comment":"22 ($16), Cursor Left"},
        "9093": {"comment":"23 ($17), Cursor Down"},
        "9095": {"comment":"24 ($18), Cursor Up"},
        "9097": {"comment":"25 ($19)"},
        "9099": {"comment":"26 ($1A)"},
        "9101": {"comment":"27 ($1B)"},
        "9103": {"comment":"28 ($1C)"},
        "9105": {"comment":"29 ($1D)"},
        "9107": {"comment":"30 ($1E)"},
        "9109": {"comment":"31 ($1F)"},
        "9111": {"comment":"32 ($20)"},
        "9113": {"comment":"33 ($21)"},
        "9115": {"comment":"34 ($22)"},
        "9117": {"comment":"35 ($23)"},
        "9119": {"comment":"36 ($24)"},
        "9121": {"comment":"37 ($25)"},
        "9123": {"comment":"38 ($26)"},
        "9125": {"comment":"39 ($27)"},
        "9127": {"comment":"40 ($28)"},
        "9129": {"comment":"41 ($29)"},
        "9131": {"comment":"42 ($2A)"},
        "9133": {"comment":"43 ($2B)"},
        "9135": {"comment":"44 ($2C)"},
        "9137": {"comment":"45 ($2D)"},
        "9139": {"comment":"46 ($2E)"},
        "9141": {"comment":"47 ($2F)"},
        "9143": {"comment":"48 ($30)"},
        "9145": {"comment":"49 ($31)"},
        "9147": {"comment":"50 ($32)"},
        "9149": {"comment":"51 ($33)"},
        "9151": {"comment":"52 ($34), <>S, Swap Case"},
        "9153": {"comment":"53 ($35)"},
        "9155": {"comment":"54 ($36)"},
        "9157": {"comment":"55 ($37)"},
        "9159": {"comment":"56 ($38)"},
        "9161": {"comment":"57 ($39), <>FL, Load file"},
        "9163": {"comment":"58 ($3A), <>FS, Save file"},
        "9165": {"comment":"59 ($3B), <>FC, Name file"},
        "9167": {"comment":"60 ($3C)"},
        "9169": {"comment":"61 ($3D)"},
        "9171": {"comment":"62 ($3E)"},
        "9173": {"comment":"63 ($3F)"},
        "9175": {"comment":"64 ($40)"},
        "9211": {"comment":"<>PO, Print"},
        "9237": {"synopsis":"The Options Page command (<>O). Shows the page (L_E614) and lets the user edit the 22\noptions of L_E8F4. IY-44 holds the current option.\n1. Cursor Up and Down, ENTER, move between the options, wrapping round; each move stores the\nedited value first (L_E747).\n2. A typed character is inserted (numbers in overtype); in a field with choices it must be\none of the choices and replaces the value; Next Option (<>J) steps through the choices.\n3. Other commands run only when they are in L_E5A2 (MthKeyAction); the rest beep.\n4. ESCAPE or <>O again stores the value, applies the options (L_E7CA), restores the text\nwindow and redraws the screen (L_BDD2).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "9578": {"synopsis":"Copies the current option's field width (the byte before its code, at (IY-48) - 1) to IY-86.\nEntry: IY-48/IY-47 = the option's code (L_E7A5).\nExit: A = IY-86 = the width.\nChanges: A, HL."},
        "9590": {"synopsis":"Returns the text of an option of L_E8F4: its value in the document's option list when it has\none (L_EA7C), otherwise its default (falls into L_E559).\nEntry: A = option number (1-22); IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: HL = the zero-terminated value.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; IY-4, IY-48/IY-47 (L_E7A5)."},
        "9600": {"synopsis":"Copies the current option's default value to IY+$23: the whole text after the two-letter\ncode for a number, only its first character for a text or a field with choices.\nEntry: IY-48/IY-47 = the option's code; IY-4 = its flags (L_E7A5).\nExit: HL = IY + $23 (the default, zero-terminated).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "9644": {"synopsis":"Copies a zero-terminated string to the edit buffer at ($1D3D).\nEntry: HL = the string.\nExit: HL = its terminator; DE = the copy's terminator.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "9658": {"synopsis":"Looks up a command code in a $FF-terminated list of bytes, comparing bits 0-6 of each.\nEntry: A = code; HL = the byte before the list.\nExit: Fc = 0; B = the matching byte (bit 7 is the entry's flag); HL = its address.\nError: Fc = 1 when the code is not in the list.\nChanges: AF, B, E, HL."},
        "9673": {"synopsis":"List of the command codes (MTH code minus one) the Options Page (L_E3EE) lets run, ending\nwith $FF; bit 7 of an entry is a flag L_E3EE tests after the command. Searched by L_E593."},
        "9708": {"synopsis":"Sets bit 5 of IY-72 and shows the edit line (falls into L_E5C9).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "9712": {"synopsis":"Shows the edit line in the current field and puts the cursor at the edit position. The end\ncolumn is the field width IY-86, plus the field's column IY-28 when the width is less than\nthe text window's (IY-81); it goes to IY-42 and IY-89, IY-85 is cleared, then L_C45E (with A\n= the window's width - 1) and L_C43C do the work.\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "9743": {"synopsis":"Starts editing the current option (IY-44): copies its value (L_E54F) to the edit buffer\n(L_E585), takes its width (L_E543) and sets its screen position (L_E7A5, falls into L_E5FC).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: as L_E5FC."},
        "9763": {"synopsis":"Sets the screen position of an option's value: the column after its label plus one space to\nIY-28 and its row to IY-27.\nEntry: HL = the option's entry in L_E8F4 (its column byte); IY-48/IY-47 = its code.\nExit: A = the column; B = the row; HL = the entry's row byte.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL."},
        "9787": {"synopsis":"Draws the Options Page: defines and clears the text window, prints the file name (or \"No\nFile\"), \"Insert\" or \"Overtype\", \"Microspace\" when it is on, the page number and the free\nmemory (OS_Nq, NQ_Mfs) on the right, then each of the 22 options of L_E8F4 with its label\nand its value (L_E54F).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "10058": {"synopsis":"Starts editing the current option (L_E5E8), puts the cursor at its value, points IY-52/IY-51\nat its choices (two bytes past its code) and marks the edit line unchanged (bit 0 of IY-72\nclear, bit 7 set).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "10087": {"synopsis":"Stores the edited value of the current option when it was changed (bit 0 of IY-72): makes a\nnode for it in the document's option list (L_EA9C) and copies the text into it (L_E775); an\nempty value only removes the old node. A failure is reported (L_EB07).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "10133": {"synopsis":"Binds the option node (L_B518) and copies a zero-terminated string into it from IX+5.\nEntry: HL = the string; IY-127..IY-125 = the node's address.\nExit: HL = past the terminator; IX = past the copy."},
        "10147": {"synopsis":"Reads the current option's two-letter code into BC and points HL at the option list's head.\nEntry: IY-48/IY-47 = the code's address (L_E7A5).\nExit: C = the first letter; B = the second; HL = $1D43.\nChanges: BC, HL."},
        "10160": {"synopsis":"Reads an option's value (L_E54F). For an option that holds a number (bit 0 of IY-4) it\nconverts the text with GN_Gdn (L_EE29); otherwise it returns its first character.\nEntry: A = option number (1-22); IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = the first character, or the number's low byte (BC = the number).\nError: Fc = 1, A = 0 when a number option does not hold a number.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10181": {"synopsis":"Finds an option's entry in L_E8F4 and records its flags in IY-4 and the address of its\ntwo-letter code in IY-48/IY-47.\nEntry: A = option number (1-22).\nExit: HL = the entry (its column byte); DE = the entry's terminator.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL."},
        "10218": {"synopsis":"Applies the options to the workspace: decimal places to IY+9, line spacing to IY+8, the\nstart page to IY+10-IY+12, the lines per page left after the margins, header and footer\n(L_E8CF, L_E8DE) to IY+7, the leading and trailing characters to IY+$16 and IY+$10 (lengths\nat IY+14 and IY+15), and the flags in IY-69: Text (bit 5), Columns (4), Auto (3), Minus (2),\nInsert on wrap Row (0), Borders (1, redrawing them when changed), Justify (6), Wrap (7).\nEntry: IY = PipeDream's workspace."},
        "10419": {"synopsis":"Sets the bit mask A in IY-69 when option B is \"Y\", clears it otherwise (falls into L_E895\nwith C = \"Y\").\nEntry: A = mask; B = option number; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10421": {"synopsis":"Sets the bit mask A in IY-69 when the first character of option B (in upper case) is C,\nclears it otherwise.\nEntry: A = mask; B = option number; C = the letter; IY = PipeDream's workspace.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10455": {"synopsis":"Copies a zero-terminated string from HL to DE + 1 onwards and counts its characters.\nEntry: HL = the string; DE = the byte before the destination.\nExit: B = the length; HL, DE = the terminator and its copy.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL."},
        "10467": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces and tests for the end of the text.\nEntry: HL = the text.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = the first character that is not a space; HL = its address.\nError: Fc = 1 at the zero terminator.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "10479": {"synopsis":"Adds up the numeric values (L_E790) of options $0F to $0E + B (the top, header, footer and\nbottom margins of L_E8F4).\nEntry: B = number of options.\nExit: A = C = the sum; B = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10494": {"synopsis":"Counts the non-blank options among $14 and $15 (the header and footer texts, L_E8C3).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = the count (0-2).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10516": {"synopsis":"The Options Page's 22 options. Each entry is a column and a row, the label (right-aligned in\nthree columns), a flag byte ($80 text, $81 number, $82 choices, $83 choices and number), the\nfield width, the two-letter code the option is saved under, and the default (for a field\nwith choices, the choices), zero-terminated. Read by L_E7A5 and L_E614."},
        "10908": {"synopsis":"Finds an option in the document's option list: follows the chain of nodes from the word at\n(HL) to one whose code (IX+3, IX+4) is C, B. A word with a zero high byte ends the chain.\nEntry: HL = the head (or a link); BC = the two-letter code.\nExit: Fc = 1, Fz = 0: found; IX = the node; HL = its value (IX+5); DE = the link to it.\nError: Fc = 0 when not found; DE = the last link.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX."},
        "10940": {"synopsis":"Replaces an option's node in the document's option list: allocates A + 6 bytes (L_D96E),\nunlinks and frees the old node with this code (L_D976), and links the new one at the end of\nthe chain with its size and code. With A = 0 it only removes the old node.\nEntry: A = the value's length; BC = the two-letter code; HL = the list's head.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = the new node (bound, L_B518) when A > 0.\nError: Fc = 1, C = 1 when the memory cannot be allocated.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "11045": {"synopsis":"The COBRA easter egg command (MTH code 33): reports message $25 through L_EB07 (falls into\nit with C = $25).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: as L_EB07."},
        "11047": {"synopsis":"Shows an error message on the status line (row 0, from column 7) after a beep, then purges\nthe keyboard buffer. C = 0 prints the last OZ error's own text (OS_Erc, GN_Esp); C = $14\nprints the file name in the buffer at $1FAA followed by \" not found\"; any other C is a\nPipeDream message number from the L_EC31 table, expanded by L_EB4D. The printed length is\nkept in (iy-84) so that L_EFC4 can erase it.\nEntry: C = message number (1-37), or 0 for the last OZ error.\nExit: Fc = 1; (iy-84) = length of the message; bit 2 of (iy-72) set (by L_EED0).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; IX for a numbered message."},
        "11112": {"synopsis":"Shared exit of L_EB07: purges the keyboard buffer with OS_Pur and returns Fc = 1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1."},
        "11116": {"synopsis":"Expands message number A of the compressed table at L_EC31 and writes it, one character at a\ntime, through the routine in IX, at most C characters. The table's messages follow one\nanother, each ending with a byte that has bit 7 set; in a message a byte whose low 7 bits\nare below $20 stands for that word (1-based) of the dictionary at L_EBDB. The first\ncharacter written is made upper case.\nEntry: A = message number (1-based); C = room for characters; IX = output routine (A =\ncharacter).\nExit: A = E = number of characters written; (iy-74) = room left.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "11183": {"synopsis":"Writes one character of an expanded message (for L_EB4D). When there is room (C not 0) it\nwrites A with bit 7 cleared through the routine in IX, upper case when it is the first (E =\n0, through GetUppercase), and counts it.\nEntry: A = message or dictionary byte; C = room left; E = characters written so far; IX =\noutput routine.\nExit: A = byte as given; Fs = its bit 7 (end of word or message); Fc = 0; C one less and E\none more when the character was written."},
        "11203": {"synopsis":"Prints the text of the last OZ error (OS_Erc, then GN_Esp for its message), reading it with\nGN_Rbe and writing it with OS_Out, at most C characters.\nEntry: C = room for characters (not 0).\nExit: C = number of characters printed; Fz = 1 when the whole message was printed.\nChanges: AF, BC, E, HL."},
        "11224": {"synopsis":"Sets C to the width of the current window (L_EEFE), keeping AF.\nEntry: none.\nExit: C = window width.\nChanges: C."},
        "11231": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's error handler, installed with OS_Erh and called by OZ with A = error code, Fz =\n1 for a fatal error and Fc = 1.\n1. A fatal error returns at once with Fc = 1, so OZ shows its error box.\n2. RC_Quit leaves PipeDream through Exit_PipeDream.\n3. RC_Dvz to RC_Exr ($46-$4B), the arithmetic errors, return Fc = 0, Fz = 0 and HL = L_F3AD:\nOZ then jumps to L_F3AD, which unwinds the function call in progress (SP from $1D55) and\nturns the error into a PipeDream error value.\n4. Every other code, RC_Bdn included, returns Fz = 1, Fc = 0, and the error goes back to the\ncall that raised it.\nEntry: A = error code; Fz = 1 if fatal; Fc = 1.\nExit: as above."},
        "11258": {"synopsis":"Data: the dictionary of 16 words used by the messages at L_EC31, each ending with a byte\nthat has bit 7 set: \"bad \", \"field\", \"file\", \"not \", \"error\", \"no \", \"too many \",\n\"overflow\", \"column\", \"too \", \"long\", \"expression\", \"range\", \"list\", \"mark\", \"argument\".\nL_EB4D finds word n by counting end bytes from L_EBDB-1."},
        "11344": {"synopsis":"Data: PipeDream's 37 messages, compressed. The label is the last byte of the dictionary at\nL_EBDB; message 1 starts at the next byte. Each message ends with a byte that has bit 7 set,\nand a byte whose low 7 bits are below $20 stands for a dictionary word. They are 1 \"Memory\nfull\", 2 \"FP overflow\", 3 \"Stack overflow\", 4 \"Escape\", 5 \"too many columns\", 6 \"Divide by\n0\", 7 \"-ve root\", 8 \"bad argument\", 9 \"no marked block\", 10 \"Typing error\", 11 \"bad slot\",\n12 \"Loop\", 13 \"Log range\", 14 \"bad range\", 15 \"Lookup\", 16 \"bad index\", 17 \"bad number\", 18\n\"too few arguments\", 19 \"Propagated\", 20 \"file not found\", 21 \"Line too long\", 22 \"bad\ndate\", 23 \"bad option\", 24 \"bad list file\", 25 \"Editing expression\", 26 \"no list file\", 27\n\"End of list\", 28 \"no name for save\", 29 \"Edge\", 30 \"too long\", 31 \"bad ^ field\", 32 \"no\ntarget\", 33 \"bad column\", 34 \"All columns zero width\", 35 \"Overlap\", 36 \"Exp range\", 37\n\"mark Colton\". Read by L_EB4D."},
        "11593": {"synopsis":"Copies 51 ($33) bytes from the buffer that ($1D75) points to into the buffer at $1FAA.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = 0.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "11601": {"synopsis":"Copies 51 ($33) bytes from the buffer at $1FAA into the buffer that ($1D75) points to.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = 0.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "11614": {"synopsis":"Reads the last segment of the file name that ($1D75) points to (GN_Esa, A = 0, B = -1) into\nthe buffer at $1FAA and names the current activity with it through DC_Nam.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = $1FAA.","comment":"filename"},
        "11617": {"comment":"read filename"},
        "11618": {"comment":"start at the filename (B=-1), buffer space of $32"},
        "11621": {"comment":"destination buffer"},
        "11634": {"synopsis":"Clears bits 6 and 0 of (iy-70) and falls into L_ED5B.\nEntry: none."},
        "11642": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_ED53: when bit 7 of (iy-70) is set, clears it and sends the printer filter\nsequence $05 \"1]\" (filter off) through the output vector (L_EDC2).\nEntry: none."},
        "11654": {"comment":"LEDE1 string: $05 \"1]\", 0 (printer filter off)"},
        "11659": {"synopsis":"Points the output vector at the routine that sends characters to the printer filter with\nOS_Prt (L_EDCF) and falls into L_ED6F.\nEntry: none."},
        "11662": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_ED6C: sets the output vector ($1D49) to HL and clears the pending space count\n(iy-83) and (iy-89). When bit 0 of (iy-70) is set it then sends the printer filter sequence\n$05 \"1[\" (filter on) through the vector and sets bit 7 of (iy-70).\nEntry: HL = output routine (takes the character in A)."},
        "11680": {"comment":"LEDE1 string: $05 \"1[\", 0 (printer filter on)"},
        "11689": {"synopsis":"Writes a space: to the screen through L_F015 when bit 6 of (iy-70) is clear, otherwise\nthrough L_ED93.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = $20 when written to the screen."},
        "11698": {"synopsis":"Writes character A through the output vector ($1D49), holding spaces back: a space only adds\none to the count in (iy-83), unless bit 4 of (iy-70) is set; a CR drops the count; any other\ncharacter first writes the counted spaces.\nEntry: A = character.\nChanges: AF."},
        "11728": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine in the output vector ($1D49) with the character in A, keeping HL (a jump\nthrough the vector).\nEntry: A = character."},
        "11745": {"synopsis":"Writes the zero-terminated string that follows the call instruction through the output\nvector (L_EDB1) and returns to the byte after its terminator.\nEntry: the string follows the CALL.\nExit: A = 0."},
        "11781": {"synopsis":"Sends the printer filter sequence $05 \"1S\" (reset the attributes) through the output vector.\nEntry: none."},
        "11784": {"comment":"LEDE1 string: $05 \"1S\", 0 (printer: reset attributes)"},
        "11789": {"synopsis":"Gets the value L_E790 returns for A = 5 and sends it as the printer filter's page length:\nfalls into L_EDF5 with C = \"P\".\nEntry: none."},
        "11796": {"synopsis":"Sends the printer filter sequence $05 \"2\", C, A + $20 through the output vector (L_EDC2,\nL_EDB1). The source shows the inline string's terminator and the following LD A,C as one LD\n(nn),A.\nEntry: A = parameter; C = command letter.\nExit: A as given."},
        "11800": {"comment":"LEDE1 string: $05 \"2\", 0 (printer code prefix; code in A)"},
        "11816": {"synopsis":"Validate character A is alphabetic, and return\nupper-case variant.\nExits with Fc=0 if character was not alphabetic."},
        "11823": {"synopsis":"Return Fc=1 if character A is numeric."},
        "11830": {"synopsis":"Return Fc=1 if character A is alphanumeric.\nOZ source name: ValidateAlphanumeric."},
        "11834": {"synopsis":"fall through\nReturn Fc=1 if character A is alphabetic.\nOZ source name: ValidateAlphabetic."},
        "11848": {"synopsis":"Reads a decimal number at (HL) with GN_Gdn, at most 30 characters, into BC.\nEntry: HL = text.\nExit: a number was read: A = 1, Fz = 0, BC = value; otherwise Fz = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "11866": {"synopsis":"Writes the zero-terminated text in the buffer at IY+$23 with OS_Out, stopping early when the\ncount in (iy-74) runs out.\nEntry: (iy-74) = most characters to write (not 0).\nExit: (iy-74) counted down.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "11885": {"synopsis":"Builds \"~ \" and the number in (ix+5) of the record L_B518 points IX to, in decimal, as a\nzero-terminated text in the buffer at IY+$23.\nEntry: none.\nExit: (iy-74) = length of the text plus one.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "11909": {"synopsis":"Stores A in the buffer at IY+$23 at index (iy-74) and adds one to (iy-74). The output\nroutine L_EE88 gives L_EE8F.\nEntry: A = character.\nChanges: none but (iy-74)."},
        "11931": {"synopsis":"Writes HL in decimal to the screen (OS_Out through L_F020), without leading zeros.\nEntry: HL = value.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "11937": {"synopsis":"Appends A in decimal to the buffer at IY+$23 (L_EE66), without leading zeros.\nEntry: A = value; (iy-74) = index of the next character.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "11942": {"synopsis":"Writes HL in decimal at the start of the buffer at IY+$23: falls into L_EE88 with A = 0.\nEntry: HL = value."},
        "11943": {"synopsis":"Writes HL in decimal into the buffer at IY+$23 from index A, without leading zeros. Then\nL_EE8F (also reached from L_EE7C) divides HL by each power of ten in L_EEC6 and passes each\ndigit to the routine in DE through L_EEBA.\nEntry: A = index; HL = value.\nExit: (iy-74) = index after the last digit.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "11993": {"synopsis":"Passes digit A, as ASCII, to the routine in DE, unless it is a leading zero (A = 0 while bit\n7 of B is clear); B becomes $FF once a digit is written.\nEntry: A = digit (0-9); B = 0 before the first digit written; DE = output routine.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "12005": {"synopsis":"Data: the words 10000, 1000, 100 and 10 and a zero word that ends the table; the divisors of\nthe decimal conversion in L_EE8F."},
        "12015": {"synopsis":"Erases the status message (L_EFC4), sets bit 2 of (iy-72) and moves the cursor to column 7\nof row 0 (L_EEE4).\nEntry: none."},
        "12028": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 7 of row 0 of the current window (L_EEE4).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "12034": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 0 of row B: falls into L_EEE4 with A = 0.\nEntry: B = row."},
        "12035": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor of the current window to column A, row B, with the VDU sequence $01 \"3@\" x\ny (OS_Out).\nEntry: A = column; B = row.\nExit: A = column + $20.\nChanges: AF."},
        "12061": {"synopsis":"Returns the width of the current window: OS_Nq NQ_Wbox for window 0, keeping BC.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = width in characters.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "12065": {"comment":"get current window information  !! xor a"},
        "12072": {"synopsis":"Data: the activity words \"Load\", \"Save\", \"Sort\", \"Calculat\", \"Replicat\" and \"Search\", each\nending with a byte that has bit 7 set. L_EF34 shows the word at the byte offset in bits 0-6\nof (iy+6) and adds \"ing\"."},
        "12105": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the status line is free for an activity message.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fz = 0 when bit 2 of (iy-72) or bit 6 of (iy-70) is set; Fz = 1 when both are clear.\nChanges: F."},
        "12115": {"synopsis":"Shows the activity message (\"Loading\", \"Saving\", ...) once the small timer has run out. It\nreturns at once when L_EF2A gives Fz = 0 or the message is already shown (bit 7 of (iy+6)).\nIt reads the small timer with OS_Ust, putting the old value back when it has not run out.\nWhen it has run out it sets bit 7 of (iy+6), prints the word from L_EF09 at offset (iy+6)\nand \"ing\" in flash and reverse from column 7 of row 0, stores the length in (iy-84) and\nstops the timer (L_EF7B).\nEntry: BC = value given to OS_Ust for a moment (put back when the timer has not run out).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12184": {"synopsis":"Stops the small timer: OS_Ust with BC = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BC = the timer's old value; Fz = 1 when it had run out.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "12189": {"synopsis":"Starts an activity: stores its code in (iy+6) and, unless bit 6 of (iy-70) is set, clears\nthe status line (L_EFBB) and starts the small timer at 30 ($1E) with OS_Ust, after which\nL_EF34 shows the activity's name.\nEntry: A = byte offset of the activity's word in L_EF09.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "12206": {"synopsis":"When bit 2 of (iy-72) is set it clears that bit and returns. Otherwise it calls L_D7AA, and\nunless that gives Fc = 1 or bit 7 of (ix+3) is set, writes text from column 7 of row 0\nthrough L_BB73 (with A = space), records its length (iy-34) in (iy-84) and writes spaces\nover the rest of a longer old message (L_C5EA). In the other cases it erases the status\nmessage (L_EFC4)."},
        "12248": {"synopsis":"Stops the small timer (L_EF7B) and, when L_EF2A gives Fz = 1, erases the status message\n(L_EFC4).\nEntry: none."},
        "12257": {"synopsis":"Erases the status message: when its length (iy-84) is not 0, moves the cursor to column 7 of\nrow 0, sets (iy-84) to 0 and writes that many spaces (L_C5EA).\nEntry: none."},
        "12274": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 40 ($28) of row 0 and clears to the end of the line (L_EFDC).\nEntry: none."},
        "12281": {"synopsis":"Clears the current window's line from the cursor to its end: the VDU sequence $01 \"2C\" $FD\n(OS_Pout).\nEntry: none."},
        "12289": {"synopsis":"Writes a form feed ($0C), which clears the current window, with OS_Out (L_F020).\nEntry: none."},
        "12293": {"synopsis":"Sounds the bell: writes $07 with OS_Out.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1."},
        "12299": {"synopsis":"Toggles reverse video: the VDU sequence $01 \"R\" (OS_Out).\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "12310": {"synopsis":"Turns the cursor off: falls into the VDU sequence $01 \"2-C\" (OS_Out).\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "12315": {"synopsis":"Turns the cursor on: the VDU sequence $01 \"2+C\" (OS_Out).\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "12348": {"synopsis":"Tests for Escape with OS_Esc (SC_BIT).\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1 when an Escape is pending, otherwise Fc = 0.\nKeeps: A."},
        "12361": {"synopsis":"Writes the zero-terminated string at HL with OS_Out and counts its characters.\nEntry: HL = string.\nExit: C = number of characters; HL = byte after the terminator; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, C, HL."},
        "12372": {"synopsis":"Multiplies HL by A (shift and add, 8 steps).\nEntry: HL = multiplicand; A = multiplier.\nExit: HL = product; A = high byte of the product; Fc = 1 when the product is over 255.\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "12394": {"synopsis":"Divides HL by A (restoring division, 8 steps).\nEntry: HL = dividend, H less than A; A = divisor.\nExit: L = quotient; A = remainder; H = 0.\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "12411": {"synopsis":"Evaluates an expression. It sets up the evaluation stack (($1D45) = $1EAA, growing down to\n$1DAA) and the source pointer ($1D4F), saves SP in ($1D47) for the error exit L_F0A6, and\nparses with L_F0AF; anything left before the end token ($0F) is a \"Typing error\" (message\n10). The result is taken off the stack (L_F309) and passed to L_F9D2. An error leaves type 0\nwith the message number in ($1D4D).\nEntry: HL = expression; B = its bank (stored in (iy-112)).\nExit: C = type of the result (iy-79); HL = ($1D4D), the result or a pointer to it; B =\n(iy-124)."},
        "12475": {"synopsis":"Parses an expression at the lowest precedence: operands parsed by L_F0CA, joined by OR\n(operator token C = $0D, L = $2A, FuncID_Or). Each operator is applied through L_F225 to the\ntwo values on the evaluation stack.\nEntry: the next token waiting (L_FD0C, L_FD2E).\nExit: the value pushed on the evaluation stack."},
        "12502": {"synopsis":"Parses operands of L_F0E5 joined by AND (operator token L = $1E, FuncID_And), applying each\nthrough L_F225. One level of the expression parser under L_F0AF."},
        "12529": {"synopsis":"Parses operands of L_F103 joined by a comparison (operator tokens L = $23-$28, FuncID_Less\nto FuncID_GreaterEqual), applying each through L_F225. One level of the expression parser."},
        "12559": {"synopsis":"Parses operands of L_F122 joined by + or - (operator tokens L = $20, $21), applying each\nthrough L_F225. One level of the expression parser."},
        "12590": {"synopsis":"Parses operands of L_F141 joined by * or / (operator tokens L = $1F, $22), applying each\nthrough L_F225. One level of the expression parser."},
        "12621": {"synopsis":"Parses operands of L_F15F joined by ^ (operator token L = $29, FuncID_Raise), applying each\nthrough L_F225. One level of the expression parser."},
        "12651": {"synopsis":"Parses a unary operand of the expression parser and pushes its value.\n1. A leading +, - or NOT (operator token L = $20, $21, $1D) parses a further operand here; +\nadds nothing, - applies FuncID_Negate and NOT applies FuncID_Not (L_F225).\n2. \"(\" parses a whole expression (L_F0AF) and needs \")\".\n3. A value token (type $03, $05, $07 or $08) is pushed as it is (L_F237).\n4. A function token ($0E) gives the function ID in bits 0-5 of L and its arguments in bits\n6-7: none, one in brackets, or a list in brackets (L_F1E0); the function is then applied\nthrough L_F225. Anything else is a \"Typing error\" (message 10, L_F1DB)."},
        "12780": {"synopsis":"Parses a function's argument list, each argument through L_F1FE, separated by commas, and\npushes the number of arguments as a type 1 value (L_FD3F, L_F237).\nEntry: the first argument's token waiting.\nExit: the arguments and their count on the evaluation stack."},
        "12810": {"synopsis":"Parses one function argument: a type $04 token is taken and pushed as it is (L_F237);\nanything else is parsed as a whole expression (L_F0AF)."},
        "12849": {"synopsis":"Applies function or operator L: calls its routine from FunctionRoutineTable through L_F3A3,\nwhich keeps SP in ($1D55) for the error handler. When the routine returns Fc = 1, its A\nbecomes an error value (L_F339). Then the current value, type (iy-79) at ($1D4D), is pushed\non the evaluation stack: it reserves the type's size (L_F375), fails with \"Stack overflow\"\n(message 3) when the stack reaches $1DAA, stores the value through the type's handler\n(L_F291, L_F281) and the type byte below it (L_F273).\nEntry: L = FuncID_xxx.\nExit: the result pushed on the evaluation stack."},
        "12941": {"synopsis":"Data: table of 8 words, the handlers that store a value pushed on the evaluation stack\n(L_F225), selected through L_F291: L_F29C, L_F2BE, L_F2C2, L_F2C6, L_F2A1, L_F2D4, L_F2F1,\nL_F2A5."},
        "12957": {"synopsis":"Data: 11 bytes, one per value type 0-10: the index of the type's store handler in L_F281 (0,\n0, 1, 2, 3, 0, 2, 5, 4, 6, 7). L_F344 uses the same index with L_F366 when it takes a value\noff the stack."},
        "12968": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value types 0, 1 and 5: stores the byte in ($1D4D) at HL.\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nChanges: A."},
        "12973": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value type 8: copies 4 bytes from the value that ($1D4D) points to\n(L_F2C8).\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "12977": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value type 10: converts the floating-point value in the FPP registers to\nan integer with FP_INT and stores its 4 bytes as a type 8 value.\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nExit: (iy-79) = 8."},
        "13002": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value type 2: copies 5 bytes from the value that ($1D4D) points to\n(L_F2C8).\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "13006": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value types 3 and 6: copies 3 bytes from the value that ($1D4D) points to\n(L_F2C8).\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "13010": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value type 4: copies 7 bytes from the value that ($1D4D) points to.\nL_F2C8, shared by the copying handlers, copies C bytes downwards so that the last lands at\nHL.\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "13024": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value type 7: stores it as a type 2 value, copying the 5 bytes at\n$1D96-$1D9A (L_F2DC).\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nExit: (iy-79) = 2.\nChanges: DE, HL."},
        "13032": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_F2D4: copies the 5 bytes at $1D96-$1D9A to HL upwards.\nEntry: HL = destination.\nChanges: A, DE, HL."},
        "13053": {"synopsis":"Store handler for value type 9: stores the floating-point value in the FPP registers as a\n5-byte type 2 value.\nEntry: HL = last byte of the new stack entry.\nExit: (iy-79) = 2."},
        "13077": {"synopsis":"Takes the top value off the evaluation stack and makes it the current value: (iy-79) = its\ntype and ($1D4D) a pointer to it, or for types 0, 1 and 5 its byte in ($1D4D) (L_F344).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = C = type; B = 0; HL = ($1D45), the new top.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "13096": {"synopsis":"Fetches an argument of a function that takes an argument list; the top of the evaluation\nstack holds the number of arguments. When there are more than A, it makes argument A\n(counted from 0) the current value (L_F325) and returns Fc = 1. Otherwise the current value\nbecomes the error \"too few arguments\" (message 18), the arguments and the count are dropped\n(L_F380), and it returns to its caller's caller.\nEntry: A = argument index.\nExit: Fc = 1 with the argument current; or the error, returned past the caller.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "13105": {"synopsis":"Reads argument A of a function's argument list. The item at the top of the evaluator stack\n(pointer in ($1D45)) is the argument count (type 1); when the count is above A, L_F341 skips\nto argument A (arguments are numbered from the deepest) and reads it. Otherwise the current\nitem becomes error $12 through L_F339.\nEntry: A = argument index (0 = first).\nExit: Fc = 1; C = item type, also in (iy-79); B = item size; HL and ($1D4D) = its data (for\na one-byte item ($1D4D) holds the byte itself).\nError: Fc = 0; A = $12; (iy-79) = 0, ($1D4D) = $12.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "13125": {"synopsis":"Shared exit: makes the current evaluator item an error: (iy-79) = 0 (type error) and the\nerror number in ($1D4D). Flags are left as they are.\nEntry: A = PipeDream error number.\nChanges: none (memory only)."},
        "13133": {"synopsis":"Skips A items from the top of the evaluator stack (L_F38D) and falls into L_F344 to read the\nitem reached.\nEntry: A = number of items to skip.\nExit: as L_F344.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "13136": {"synopsis":"Reads the evaluator stack item at HL: its type byte goes to C and (iy-79), ($1D4D) is set to\nthe data after it, and B gets the item's size from L_F375. Then it continues through the\nhandler of the type's class (L_F29D, a table outside this slice, indexes L_F366): for class\n0 (types 0, 1 and 5, one byte of data) L_F370 puts the data byte itself in ($1D4D).\nEntry: HL = item (its type byte).\nExit: C = type; B = size in bytes, type byte included; HL = data; (iy-79), ($1D4D) set.\nChanges: A (class 0), BC, DE, HL."},
        "13170": {"synopsis":"Table of 5 words: the handler L_F344 runs for each class of item type (class from the table\nat $F29D). Class 0 is L_F370, which copies the data byte into ($1D4D); classes 1-4 are\nL_F374, a plain return. Only types 0-6 and 8 (classes 0-4) are kept on the stack: the push\ncode stores result types 7, 9 and 10 as type 2 or 8."},
        "13180": {"synopsis":"Class 0 handler of L_F344: stores the item's one data byte at (HL) in ($1D4D), replacing the\npointer's low byte; falls into L_F374.\nEntry: HL = item data.\nChanges: A."},
        "13184": {"synopsis":"Shared exit: a plain return. The class 1-4 handler of L_F344 (table L_F366)."},
        "13185": {"synopsis":"Table of 11 bytes: the size in bytes, type byte included, of an evaluator stack item of each\ntype 0-10 (2, 2, 6, 4, 8, 2, 4, 6, 5, 6, 5). Read when items are pushed (L_F237) and skipped\n(L_F38D, L_F344)."},
        "13196": {"synopsis":"Drops a function's argument list from the evaluator stack: reads the count from the top\nitem, skips count + 1 items (the count item and the arguments) and stores the new top in\n($1D45). L_F386 is the entry that drops A items.\nEntry: count item at the top of the stack ($1D45).\nExit: ($1D45) and HL = new top of the stack.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "13209": {"synopsis":"Steps over A items of the evaluator stack, starting at its top ($1D45), adding each item's\nsize from L_F375.\nEntry: A = number of items.\nExit: HL = the item reached ($1D45 itself when A = 0); B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "13231": {"synopsis":"Calls a function routine: saves SP in ($1D55) and jumps to the routine at DE (through\nL_9223, JP (HL)). A floating point error inside it ends at L_F3AD, which restores SP and\nreturns from here with Fc = 1 and A = a PipeDream error number.\nEntry: DE = routine address (from FuncRoutineTable).\nExit: Fc = 0; result as the routine leaves it ((iy-79), ($1D4D) or HL'HLC).\nError: Fc = 1, A = PipeDream error number (from L_F3AD)."},
        "13264": {"synopsis":"Table of 4 bytes: the OZ floating point errors that L_F3AD translates: RC_Dvz ($46), RC_Nvr\n($48), RC_Lgr ($49) and RC_Exr ($4B)."},
        "13268": {"synopsis":"Table of 4 bytes: the PipeDream error numbers for L_F3C4's errors. CPIR leaves BC = entries\nafter the match, so the order is reversed: RC_Exr gives $24, RC_Lgr $0D, RC_Nvr $07 and\nRC_Dvz $06. Any other error gives $02."},
        "13272": {"synopsis":"Table of 44 words: the routine of each spreadsheet function and operator, in FuncID order\n(fnAbs ... fnYear, then fnNot, fnAnd, the arithmetic and comparison operators, fnRaise, fnOr\nand fnNegate). L_F225 indexes it with the function ID ($3F mask) and calls the routine\nthrough L_F3A3.\nOZ source name: FunctionRoutineTable."},
        "13360": {"synopsis":"ABS function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_ABS. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13363": {"synopsis":"Entry inside fnAbs: applies FP_ABS to the number in HL'HLC and returns.\nEntry: HL'HLC = number.\nExit: HL'HLC = absolute value."},
        "13366": {"synopsis":"ACS function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_ACS. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13372": {"synopsis":"ASN function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_ASN. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13378": {"synopsis":"ATN function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_ATN. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13384": {"synopsis":"CHOOSE function: returns the argument chosen by the first one. The first argument must be a\nnumber from 1 to 65535 (L_FBFE), else error $10; the count goes to (iy-30..29) and L_FADF\nwalks the arguments from the second on, ranges slot by slot, with L_F46A counting down. The\nitem reached becomes the result; when the list runs out the result is error $12. The\nargument list is dropped.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: result in (iy-79) and ($1D4D)."},
        "13451": {"synopsis":"COL function: returns the current column (iy-110) plus 1 as a number, through L_F666.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL'HLC = column number (integer form); (iy-79) = 9."},
        "13459": {"synopsis":"COS function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_COS. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13465": {"synopsis":"COUNT function: counts the numeric, non-blank values among its arguments, ranges slot by\nslot (L_FADD with L_F4A4 counting in (iy-30..29)), and returns the count as a number.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = count (integer form); (iy-79) = 9."},
        "13500": {"synopsis":"DAY function: takes a date argument through L_F924 and returns its day of the month (bits\n4-0 of C from GN_Die) as a number.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = day (integer form); (iy-79) = 9.\nError: a non-date argument gives error $16 (L_F924)."},
        "13512": {"synopsis":"DEG function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_DEG. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13518": {"synopsis":"EXP function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_EXP. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13524": {"synopsis":"IF function: evaluates the first argument; when it is a non-zero number the second argument\nis the result, when it is zero or not a number the third one is. The chosen argument goes\nthrough L_F9BE, its type becomes (iy-79), and the argument list is dropped.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: result in (iy-79) and ($1D4D)."},
        "13558": {"synopsis":"INDEX function: takes a column and a row number (both from 1, through L_FC0C and L_FBFE;\notherwise error $10) and returns a reference to that slot (L_FB68, type 3, column - 1 and\nrow - 1). The argument list is dropped.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: (iy-79) = 3; ($1D4D) = the reference at (iy+35)."},
        "13615": {"synopsis":"INT function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_INT. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13621": {"synopsis":"LN function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_LN. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13627": {"synopsis":"LOG function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_LOG. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13633": {"synopsis":"LOOKUP function: finds the first argument in the range given as the second and returns the\nslot at the same position in the range given as the third.\n1. A numeric key is stored at $1DA0; a string key's address and bank go to (iy-120..118). An\nerror or range key gives error $0F.\n2. Walks the second range (L_FB35, L_FB55), counting in (iy-28..27), until a slot of the\nkey's type matches: FP_CMP for numbers, L_F7DF (with wildcards) for strings.\n3. Walks the third range the same number of steps and makes its slot the result. A missing\nmatch, a range argument that is not a range or a range too short gives error $0F. The\nargument list is dropped.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: result in (iy-79) and ($1D4D)."},
        "13827": {"synopsis":"MAX function: clears bit 7 of (iy-30) for MAX and continues in fnMin's body (L_F5FB), which\nreturns the largest numeric value among the arguments, ranges slot by slot. Non-numeric and\nblank values are ignored; without any number the result is zero.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "13830": {"synopsis":"MIN function: sets bit 7 of (iy-30) and returns the smallest numeric value among the\narguments, ranges slot by slot. The value kept so far is at $1DA0; bit 7 of (iy-29) marks\nthe first number, and L_F61F compares each number with it. Non-numeric and blank values are\nignored; without any number the result is zero.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "13910": {"synopsis":"MONTH function: takes a date argument through L_F924 and returns its month (B from GN_Die)\nas a number.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = month (integer form); (iy-79) = 9.\nError: a non-date argument gives error $16 (L_F924)."},
        "13919": {"synopsis":"PI function: returns pi (FP_PI).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL'HLC = pi; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "13926": {"synopsis":"RAD function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_RAD. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13932": {"synopsis":"ROW function: returns the current row (iy-109..108) plus 1 as a number, falling into L_F666.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL'HLC = row number (integer form); (iy-79) = 9."},
        "13949": {"synopsis":"SGN function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_SGN. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13955": {"synopsis":"SIN function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_SIN. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13961": {"synopsis":"SQR function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_SQR. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "13967": {"synopsis":"SUM function: adds the numeric values among its arguments, ranges slot by slot, into the\ntotal at $1DA0 (L_FADD with L_F69F); non-numeric and blank values are ignored.\nEntry: argument list at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = sum; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14020": {"synopsis":"TAN function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_TAN. A non-numeric\nargument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "14026": {"synopsis":"YEAR function: takes a date argument through L_F924 and returns the year modulo 100 (GN_D24\ndivides GN_Die's year by 100) as a number.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = year mod 100 (integer form); (iy-79) = 9.\nError: a non-date argument gives error $16 (L_F924)."},
        "14043": {"synopsis":"NOT operator: takes a numeric operand through L_FAC7 and returns 1 when it is zero, 0\notherwise.\nEntry: operand at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 0 or 1 (integer form); (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14053": {"synopsis":"AND operator: takes both operands through L_F93F and returns 1 when both are non-zero, 0\notherwise (L_F6EE on each). A non-numeric operand becomes the result instead.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 0 or 1 (integer form); (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14074": {"synopsis":"Turns the number in HL'HLC into a truth value with FP_TST.\nEntry: HL'HLC = number.\nExit: A = 0 and Fz = 1 when it is zero; A = 1 and Fz = 0 otherwise.\nChanges: AF."},
        "14082": {"synopsis":"Multiplication operator: takes both operands through L_F93F and applies FP_MUL. A\nnon-numeric operand becomes the result instead.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = result type from L_F93F."},
        "14088": {"synopsis":"Addition operator: takes both operands through L_F93F and applies FP_ADD. A non-numeric\noperand becomes the result instead.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = result type from L_F93F."},
        "14094": {"synopsis":"Subtraction operator: takes both operands through L_F93F and applies FP_SUB. When both\noperands are dates (type $0A) the result type is 9, a plain number. A non-numeric operand\nbecomes the result instead.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = result type from L_F93F."},
        "14110": {"synopsis":"Division operator: takes both operands through L_F93F and applies FP_DIV. A non-numeric\noperand becomes the result instead.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = result type from L_F93F."},
        "14116": {"synopsis":"\"<\" operator: compares the two operands with L_F770 and returns 1 (L_F732) when the left\noperand is less than the right one, 0 (L_F769) otherwise. Operands that cannot be compared\ngive 0.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 1 or 0; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14123": {"synopsis":"\"<=\" operator: compares the two operands with L_F770 and returns 1 (L_F732) when the left\noperand is less than or equal to the right one, 0 (L_F769) otherwise. Operands that cannot\nbe compared give 0.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 1 or 0; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14130": {"synopsis":"\"<>\" operator: compares the two operands with L_F770 and returns 1 (L_F732) when the\noperands differ, 0 (L_F769) otherwise. Operands that cannot be compared give 0.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 1 or 0; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14137": {"synopsis":"\"=\" operator: compares the two operands with L_F770 and returns 1 (L_F732) when the operands\nare equal, 0 (L_F769) otherwise. Operands that cannot be compared give 0.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 1 or 0; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14149": {"synopsis":"\">\" operator: compares the two operands with L_F770 and returns 1 (L_F732) when the left\noperand is greater than the right one, 0 (L_F769) otherwise. Operands that cannot be\ncompared give 0.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 1 or 0; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14156": {"synopsis":"\">=\" operator: compares the two operands with L_F770 and returns 1 (L_F732) when the left\noperand is greater than or equal to the right one, 0 (L_F769) otherwise. Operands that\ncannot be compared give 0.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 1 or 0; (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14163": {"synopsis":"Power (^) operator operator: takes both operands through L_F93F and applies FP_PWR. A\nnon-numeric operand becomes the result instead.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = result type from L_F93F."},
        "14169": {"synopsis":"OR operator: takes both operands through L_F93F and returns 1 when either is non-zero, 0\notherwise (L_F6EE on each). A non-numeric operand becomes the result instead.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = 0 or 1 (integer form); (iy-79) = 9."},
        "14187": {"synopsis":"Unary minus function: takes its numeric argument through L_FAC7 and applies FP_NEG. A\nnon-numeric argument (a slot reference resolved first) becomes the result as it is.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = result; (iy-79) = 9 (number)."},
        "14204": {"synopsis":"Compares the two operands of a comparison operator and drops them from the evaluator stack.\n1. Reads the left operand (L_F97F, A = 1) and the right one (A = 0). An error operand, or\none L_F909 does not accept, drops both and returns from the operator with 0 (L_F765).\n2. Keeps the left type in (iy-36), a left string's address and bank in (iy-123..121), a\nright one's in (iy-120..118), and a left number at $1DA5. A blank ($0C) takes the other\noperand's type; any other type mismatch gives 0.\n3. Numbers, dates and blanks are compared with FP_CMP; strings with L_F7DF.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: Fz = 1 when equal; Fc = 1 when the left operand is the smaller (as fnLess reads it)."},
        "14315": {"synopsis":"Compares the string at (iy-123..121) (address, bank) with the one at (iy-120..118), ignoring\nletter case and leading spaces and codes $18-$1F (L_F8B4, L_F8CB). The second string may\nhold wildcards read by L_F8E8: ^? matches any one character, ^# any run of characters (with\nbacktracking through (iy-36..33)), ^^ a caret. Trailing spaces are ignored. Banks are bound\nthrough L_D887 as needed. Also called by fnLookup.\nEntry: strings in (iy-123..118).\nExit: Fz = 1 on a match; otherwise flags of comparing the first differing characters (Fc = 1\nwhen the first string's is lower; codes $C0 and above are adjusted by L_F874)."},
        "14528": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces and codes $18-$1F (L_CE2A) in the string at HL, binding its bank C first when\nit is not (iy-111) (L_D887); each character is passed with L_A8BB.\nEntry: HL = string; C = its bank.\nExit: HL = first other character; A = that character."},
        "14551": {"synopsis":"Skips spaces and codes $18-$1F (L_CE2A) in the string at DE, binding its bank B first when\nit is not (iy-111) (L_D887); each character is passed with L_A8BB.\nEntry: DE = string; B = its bank.\nExit: DE = first other character; A = that character."},
        "14569": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the string at HL ends after any spaces and codes $18-$1F (L_F8B4), leaving HL\nwhere it was, and falls into L_F8E2.\nEntry: HL = string; C = its bank.\nExit: Fz = 1 when the next other character is $00 or $14; A = that character."},
        "14574": {"synopsis":"Tests A for a string end: Fz = 1 when A is $00 or $14.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: Fz = 1 for $00 or $14.\nChanges: F."},
        "14580": {"synopsis":"Reads a pattern character at HL (bank C bound first when it is not (iy-111)) and decodes the\ncaret escapes: ^^ gives '^', ^? gives $16 and ^# gives $15, HL then on the escape's second\ncharacter. Any other character, a lone '^' included, is returned with HL unchanged.\nEntry: HL = pattern; C = its bank.\nExit: A = character or $15/$16; HL as above.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "14613": {"synopsis":"Classifies a comparison operand's type: $09 (number), $0A (date) and $0C (blank) are\naccepted as they are; $05 and $06 (strings) are accepted as type $0B; anything else is\nrefused.\nEntry: C = type.\nExit: Fc = 1 when accepted, C = type ($0B for a string); Fc = 0 when refused.\nChanges: AF, C."},
        "14640": {"synopsis":"Takes a date argument for DAY, MONTH and YEAR: pops the top item (L_F309), resolves it\n(L_F9D2) and, when it is a date (type 8), converts its 3-byte internal date with GN_Die.\nOtherwise, or when GN_Die fails, the current item becomes error $16 and it returns from its\ncaller as well.\nEntry: argument at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: C = day of month (bits 4-0) and weekday (bits 7-5); B = month; DE = year.\nError: returns to the caller's caller with (iy-79) = 0, ($1D4D) = $16."},
        "14667": {"synopsis":"Takes the two operands of an arithmetic or logical operator and drops them from the\nevaluator stack.\n1. Reads the left operand (L_F97F, A = 1) and keeps it at $1DA5, then the right one (A = 0).\nWhen either is not a number it drops both and returns from the operator, the non-number\nbeing the result.\n2. The result type in (iy-79) is $0A when the left operand is a date, 8 when the right type\nis 8, otherwise 9.\nEntry: two operands at the top of the evaluator stack.\nExit: HL'HLC = left operand; DE'DEB = right operand; A = left type; Fz = 1 when both types\nare equal."},
        "14726": {"synopsis":"Drops the two top items of the evaluator stack (L_F386 with A = 2).\nEntry: none.\nExit: ($1D45) = new top.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL, IX."},
        "14731": {"synopsis":"Reads the item A below the top of the evaluator stack (L_F341) and resolves it (L_F9D2) into\nan operand.\nEntry: A = items to skip (0 = top).\nExit: a number: Fc = 0, P/V = 0, DE'DEB = value, C = 9; a blank: Fc = 0, P/V = 0, DE'DEB =\n0, C = $0C; a date in a slot: Fc = 0, DE'DEB = its value with B = 0, C = $0A.\nError: Fc = 1, C = type for any other item; P/V = 1 when it is an error (type 0)."},
        "14752": {"synopsis":"Shared exit: clears the P/V flag, keeping A and the other flags.\nChanges: F."},
        "14787": {"synopsis":"Shared exit: sets the P/V flag, keeping A and the other flags (marks a blank or error\nvalue).\nChanges: F."},
        "14794": {"synopsis":"Resolves the current item with L_F9D2 and requires a number. A date (type 8) or a range\n(type 4) makes the current item error $08.\nEntry: current item in C (type) and ($1D4D).\nExit: Fc = 0: a number at HL (or a blank, P/V = 1).\nError: Fc = 1 for anything else; C = type, or (iy-79) = 0 with error $08."},
        "14814": {"synopsis":"Resolves the current evaluator item into a value. A slot reference (type 3) is looked up\n(L_D887, L_FA04) and gives the slot's value; a number (type 2) returns Fc = 0 with HL = its\n5 bytes. A string in the expression text (type 5) gives HL = (iy-114..113) + offset and B =\n(iy-112); a date (type 8) gives B = (iy-124). Every other type returns Fc = 1.\nEntry: C = type; ($1D4D) = data.\nExit: Fc = 0: a number at HL (P/V = 1 for a blank slot); Fc = 1: another value, C = type, HL\n= its data (B = bank for a text); P/V = 1 when it is an error item."},
        "14864": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_F9D2's slot lookup: reads a slot reference at HL (L_B4F9: column A, row BC)\nand falls into L_FA07.\nEntry: HL = reference (3 bytes).\nExit: as L_FA07."},
        "14867": {"synopsis":"Finds the slot at column A, row BC (L_D7AD) and makes its value the current item. The slot's\nflags at (ix+3) decide:\n1. Column $80 or above: error $0B. No slot: number zero marked blank (P/V = 1).\n2. Bit 7 (text): a text of only spaces is blank; otherwise a string (type 6) at slot + 4.\n3. Bit 4: error $0C when (ix+4) is $0C, otherwise error $13.\n4. Bits 7-6 = 11: number zero (L_FA50); 00: the number at slot + 4 (L_FAB1).\n5. Bits 7-6 = 01 (L_FA25): (ix+4) = 0 is a reference to another slot, followed (error $0C\nwhen it is the current slot); 2 a date (type 8) at slot + 5; else a string (type 6) at slot\n+ 10 + (ix+5).\nEntry: A = column; BC = row.\nExit: (iy-79) = type; ($1D4D) or HL, B = data; Fc and P/V as L_F9D2, except that the errors\nmade here return Fc = 1 with P/V = 0."},
        "14897": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_FA07 for a slot whose flag bits 7-6 are 01: binds the slot (L_B518) and reads\n(ix+4). Zero means the slot refers to the slot at (ix+5..7), which is followed through\nL_FA07, or error $0C when that is the current slot ((iy-110..108)). 2 gives a date (type 8)\nat slot + 5; other values a string (type 6) at slot + 10 + (ix+5).\nEntry: slot found by L_D7AD ((iy-127..125)).\nExit: as L_FA07."},
        "14940": {"synopsis":"Makes the current item the number zero: FP_ZER stored at $1D9B, ($1D4D) = $1D9B, (iy-79) =\n2, then returns with Fc = 0 and P/V = 0.\nEntry: none.\nExit: (iy-79) = 2; ($1D4D) = $1D9B; HL'HLC = 0; Fc = 0."},
        "15037": {"synopsis":"Points ($1D4D) at offset 4 of the slot found by L_D7AD (address in (iy-127..126)), the\nslot's number, and copies the slot's bank (iy-125) to (iy-124). L_FAB3 is the entry with\nanother offset in A.\nEntry: slot in (iy-127..125).\nExit: ($1D4D) = HL = slot + 4; B = bank.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "15039": {"synopsis":"Entry inside L_FAB1 (which loads A = 4): points the value pointer at $1D4D at offset A into\nthe block whose address is held at (IY-127)/(IY-126), and copies the bank byte (IY-125) to B\nand to (IY-124), the bank that goes with $1D4D.\nEntry: A = offset; (IY-127)/(IY-126) = block address; (IY-125) = its bank.\nExit: HL = ($1D4D) = block address + A; B = (IY-124) = (IY-125).\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "15059": {"synopsis":"Fetches the single argument of a one-argument function (fnAbs, fnCos, fnSin and the like) as\na number. L_F309 loads the next item of the argument list at ($1D45) and steps past it, and\nL_F9D2 resolves it. When L_F9D2 returns Fc = 0 (a number), the number at ($1D4D) is loaded\ninto HL' HL C with L_FE8E and the result type (IY-79) becomes 9, so the caller can apply its\nFPP operation and return. Otherwise the routine drops its caller's return address and\nreturns to the caller's caller with the value L_F9D2 left.\nEntry: ($1D45) = argument list pointer.\nExit: HL' HL C = the number; IX = ($1D4D); (IY-79) = 9."},
        "15081": {"synopsis":"Runs the callback in IX for every value in the current function's argument list, from the\nfirst argument: C = 0, then falls into L_FADF. fnCount, fnMax, fnMin and fnSum use it.\nEntry: IX = callback.\nExit: as L_FADF."},
        "15083": {"synopsis":"Runs the callback in IX for every value in the current function's argument list, from\nargument C on (counted from 0); a range argument is visited cell by cell. fnChoose starts at\nargument 1.\n1. Stores the argument number in (IY-38) and sets bit 7 of (IY-40) (not inside a range).\n2. Loads argument (IY-38) with L_F325 and resolves it with L_F9D2.\n3. A range (type 4) is set up with L_FB35, which makes its first cell the current value; bit\n7 of (IY-40) is cleared and the cell is resolved by L_F9D2 again.\n4. Any other value goes to the callback (through L_B8B4) with the flags from L_F9D2 (Fc = 0\nfor a number); a callback returning Fc = 1 stops the walk.\n5. Inside a range, L_FB55 moves to the next cell and the walk goes back to L_F9D2; at the\nrange's end bit 7 of (IY-40) is set again.\n6. Steps (IY-38) to the next argument until it reaches the count at ($1D45)+1, then sets\n(IY-79) = 7. Last, L_F380 steps ($1D45) past the function's argument list.\nEntry: IX = callback; C = first argument number; ($1D45) = argument list pointer.\nExit: Fc = 0 when every value was visited.\nError: Fc = 1 when the callback stopped the walk, or a range was empty (error $0E, L_FB35).\nKeeps: IX."},
        "15169": {"synopsis":"Starts the walk through the range value at ($1D4D): copies the range's first reference\n(column, row word) to (IY-58)..(IY-56) and the second, past its marker byte, to\n(IY-55)..(IY-53), sets the current cell (IY-61)..(IY-59) to the first with L_FBBD and, when\nthe range is not empty, makes that cell the current value (type 3) through L_FB68.\nEntry: ($1D4D) = address of the range's two 3-byte references, with a marker byte between\nthem.\nExit: Fc = 0; C = 3; ($1D4D) = IY+35, holding the first cell's reference.\nError: Fc = 1 when the range is empty, with error $0E set by L_F339.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "15201": {"synopsis":"Moves the range walk at IY-61 to its next cell with L_FB93 and makes that cell the current\nvalue (type 3) with L_FB68; its tail, L_FB5A, also ends L_FB35.\nEntry: the range block at (IY-61)..(IY-53) (layout at L_FB9D).\nExit: Fc = 0, C = 3 and ($1D4D) = IY+35, holding the next cell's reference; Fc = 1 when the\nrange is finished.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "15220": {"synopsis":"Makes a cell reference the current value: writes column A and row CB (C low, B high) at\n(IY+35)..(IY+37), sets the result type (IY-79) to 3 and falls into L_FB76, which points\n$1D4D at that copy.\nEntry: A = column; C = row low byte; B = row high byte.\nExit: C = 3; HL = ($1D4D) = IY+35; A = (IY-124) = (IY-111).\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL."},
        "15234": {"synopsis":"Points the value pointer $1D4D at the reference buffer at IY+35 and sets its bank byte\n(IY-124) to (IY-111), the bank L_D887 last bound.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL = ($1D4D) = IY+35; A = (IY-124) = (IY-111); DE = $0023.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "15251": {"synopsis":"Copies 3 bytes from (HL) to (IX).\nEntry: HL = source; IX = destination.\nExit: HL and IX advanced by 3; A = last byte copied; B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, HL, IX."},
        "15263": {"synopsis":"Moves the range walk in the block at IY-61 to the next cell: IX = IY-61, then falls into\nL_FB9D. Callers outside the formula evaluator use the same block.\nEntry: the range block at (IY-61)..(IY-53).\nExit: as L_FB9D; IX = IY-61.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX."},
        "15273": {"synopsis":"Moves a range walk to the next cell: the next column along the row, and after the last\ncolumn the first column of the next row. The block at IX holds the current cell at (IX+0)\n(column) and (IX+1)/(IX+2) (row), the first cell at (IX+3)..(IX+5) and the last at\n(IX+6)..(IX+8).\nEntry: IX = range block.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the new current cell is inside the range; Fc = 0 when the walk has passed\nthe last row.\nChanges: AF."},
        "15305": {"synopsis":"Starts the range walk in the block at IY-61: IX = IY-61, then falls into L_FBC7.\nEntry: the first and last cells at (IY-58)..(IY-53).\nExit: as L_FBC7; IX = IY-61.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX."},
        "15315": {"synopsis":"Starts a range walk: copies the first cell (IX+3)..(IX+5) to the current cell (IX+0)..(IX+2)\nand checks that the range is not empty, the first column not after the last (IX+6) and the\nfirst row not after the last (IX+7)/(IX+8); falls into L_FBE1 for the row.\nEntry: IX = range block (layout at L_FB9D).\nExit: Fc = 1 when the range holds at least one cell; Fc = 0 when it is empty.\nChanges: AF."},
        "15341": {"synopsis":"Compares the current row (IX+1)/(IX+2) of a range walk with its last row (IX+7)/(IX+8).\nEntry: IX = range block (layout at L_FB9D).\nExit: Fc = 1 when the current row is not after the last row; Fc = 0 when it is.\nChanges: AF."},
        "15358": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the current row of the range block at IY-61 has passed its last row: IX =\nIY-61, then L_FBE1.\nEntry: the range block at (IY-61)..(IY-53).\nExit: as L_FBE1; IX = IY-61.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX."},
        "15370": {"synopsis":"Converts the number in HL' HL C to an integer of 1 to 65535 with FP_FIX: it is accepted when\nthe high word of the result (HL) is 0 and the low word (HL') is not. The routine executes\nEXX before testing the low word, so it returns with the register sets exchanged and the\nvalue in BC of the set now current.\nEntry: HL' HL C = number.\nExit: Fc = 0; BC = the integer.\nError: Fc = 1 with error $10 set through L_FC14 ((IY-79) = 0, ($1D4D) = $10); a zero value\nfails after the EXX, a large or negative one before it."},
        "15384": {"synopsis":"Converts the number in HL' HL C to an integer with L_FBFE and rejects one whose low byte is\n0; fnIndex reads its column number with it. B is not tested, so a value over 255 with a\nnon-zero low byte also passes.\nEntry: HL' HL C = number.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = C = low byte of the integer.\nError: Fc = 1 with error $10 set through L_FC14."},
        "15392": {"synopsis":"Makes error $10 the current value: A = $10, then L_F339 sets the result type (IY-79) to 0\nand stores the code at $1D4D. The flags are not changed; L_FC13, the instruction before it,\nsets Fc = 1.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = $10; (IY-79) = 0; ($1D4D) = $10; flags as on entry.\nChanges: A."},
        "15397": {"synopsis":"Binary search tree of functions."},
        "15403": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for ACS: data byte FuncID_Acs + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: the ASN node; less link: the ABS node; then \"ACS\" with bit 7 set on its last letter.\nEvery node is laid out this way: the data byte (function ID in bits 5-0, the argument form\nin bits 7-6, which the parser tests after L_FD64 returns a function token), the offset + 1\nfrom FunctionTree of the node to try when the name sorts after this one, the same for a name\nthat sorts before it (0 = none), then the name in capitals. L_FD64 searches the tree with\nBinaryTreeSearch."},
        "15409": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for ASN: data byte FuncID_Asn + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: none; then \"ASN\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15415": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for ATN: data byte FuncID_Atn + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: the CHOOSE node; less link: the ACS node; then \"ATN\" with bit 7 set on its last\nletter."},
        "15421": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for CHOOSE: data byte FuncID_Choose + $80 (an argument list in brackets);\ngreater link: none; less link: none; then \"CHOOSE\" with bit 7 set on its last letter.\nOZ source name: FunctionTreeChoose."},
        "15430": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for COL: data byte FuncID_Col (bits 7-6 = 0: no argument list); greater\nlink: the EXP node; less link: the ATN node; then \"COL\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15436": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for COS: data byte FuncID_Cos + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: none; then \"COS\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15442": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for COUNT: data byte FuncID_Count + $80 (an argument list in brackets);\ngreater link: the DAY node; less link: the COS node; then \"COUNT\" with bit 7 set on its last\nletter.\nOZ source name: FunctionTreeCount."},
        "15450": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for DAY: data byte FuncID_Day + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: the DEG node; less link: none; then \"DAY\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15456": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for DEG: data byte FuncID_Deg + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: none; then \"DEG\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15462": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for EXP: data byte FuncID_Exp + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: the INT node; less link: the COUNT node; then \"EXP\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15468": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for IF: data byte FuncID_If + $80 (an argument list in brackets); greater\nlink: the INDEX node; less link: none; then \"IF\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15473": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for INDEX: data byte FuncID_Index + $80 (an argument list in brackets);\ngreater link: none; less link: none; then \"INDEX\" with bit 7 set on its last letter.\nOZ source name: FunctionTreeIndex."},
        "15481": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for INT: data byte FuncID_Int + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: the LN node; less link: the IF node; then \"INT\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15487": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for LN: data byte FuncID_Ln + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: none; then \"LN\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15492": {"synopsis":"FunctionTreeRoot, the root of FunctionTree, where L_FD64 starts BinaryTreeSearch: the node\nfor LOG (FunctionTreeLog in the source). Data byte FuncID_Log + $40 (one argument in\nbrackets); greater link: the ROW node; less link: the COL node; then \"LOG\" with bit 7 set on\nits last letter."},
        "15498": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for LOOKUP: data byte FuncID_Lookup + $80 (an argument list in brackets);\ngreater link: the MAX node; less link: none; then \"LOOKUP\" with bit 7 set on its last\nletter.\nOZ source name: FunctionTreeLookup."},
        "15507": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for MAX: data byte FuncID_Max + $80 (an argument list in brackets);\ngreater link: none; less link: none; then \"MAX\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15513": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for MIN: data byte FuncID_Min + $80 (an argument list in brackets);\ngreater link: the RAD node; less link: the LOOKUP node; then \"MIN\" with bit 7 set on its\nlast letter."},
        "15519": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for MONTH: data byte FuncID_Month + $40 (one argument in brackets);\ngreater link: none; less link: none; then \"MONTH\" with bit 7 set on its last letter.\nOZ source name: FunctionTreeMonth."},
        "15527": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for PI: data byte FuncID_Pi (bits 7-6 = 0: no argument list); greater\nlink: none; less link: the MONTH node; then \"PI\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15532": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for RAD: data byte FuncID_Rad + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: the PI node; then \"RAD\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15538": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for ROW: data byte FuncID_Row (bits 7-6 = 0: no argument list); greater\nlink: the SUM node; less link: the MIN node; then \"ROW\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15544": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for SGN: data byte FuncID_Sgn + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: none; then \"SGN\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15550": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for SIN: data byte FuncID_Sin + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: the SQR node; less link: the SGN node; then \"SIN\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15556": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for SQR: data byte FuncID_Sqr + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: none; then \"SQR\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15562": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for SUM: data byte FuncID_Sum + $80 (an argument list in brackets);\ngreater link: the TAN node; less link: the SIN node; then \"SUM\" with bit 7 set on its last\nletter."},
        "15568": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for TAN: data byte FuncID_Tan + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: the YEAR node; less link: none; then \"TAN\" with bit 7 set on its last letter."},
        "15574": {"synopsis":"FunctionTree node for YEAR: data byte FuncID_Year + $40 (one argument in brackets); greater\nlink: none; less link: none; then \"YEAR\" with bit 7 set on its last letter. The last node of\nFunctionTree; OperatorTree starts after it at $FCDD with the node for \"!\" (NOT)."},
        "15581": {"synopsis":"Binary search tree of operators."},
        "15585": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"&\": data byte FuncID_And; greater link: none; less link: the \"!\"\nnode; then \"&\" with bit 7 set on its last character. The nodes have FunctionTree's layout\n(data byte, greater link, less link, text); the data byte is the plain function ID, which\nL_FD64 returns in L with token type $0D."},
        "15589": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"*\": data byte FuncID_Multiply; greater link: the \"+\" node; less link:\nthe \"&\" node; then \"*\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeMultiply."},
        "15593": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"+\": data byte FuncID_Add; greater link: none; less link: none; then\n\"+\" with bit 7 set on its last character."},
        "15597": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"-\": data byte FuncID_Subtract; greater link: the \"/\" node; less link:\nthe \"*\" node; then \"-\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeSubtract."},
        "15601": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"/\": data byte FuncID_Divide; greater link: the \"<\" node; less link:\nnone; then \"/\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeDivide."},
        "15605": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"<\": data byte FuncID_Less; greater link: none; less link: none; then\n\"<\" with bit 7 set on its last character."},
        "15609": {"synopsis":"OperatorTreeRoot, the root of OperatorTree, where L_FD64 starts BinaryTreeSearch: the node\nfor \"<=\" (OperatorTreeLessEqual in the source). Data byte FuncID_LessEqual; greater link:\nthe \">=\" node; less link: the \"-\" node; then \"<=\" with bit 7 set on its last character."},
        "15614": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"<>\": data byte FuncID_NotEqual; greater link: none; less link: none;\nthen \"<>\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeNotEqual."},
        "15619": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"=\": data byte FuncID_Equal; greater link: the \">\" node; less link:\nthe \"<>\" node; then \"=\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeEqual."},
        "15623": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \">\": data byte FuncID_Greater; greater link: none; less link: none;\nthen \">\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeGreater."},
        "15627": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \">=\": data byte FuncID_GreaterEqual; greater link: the \"^\" node; less\nlink: the \"=\" node; then \">=\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeGreaterEqual."},
        "15632": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"^\": data byte FuncID_Raise; greater link: the \"|\" node; less link:\nnone; then \"^\" with bit 7 set on its last character.\nOZ source name: OperatorTreeRaise."},
        "15636": {"synopsis":"OperatorTree node for \"|\": data byte FuncID_Or; greater link: none; less link: none; then\n\"|\" with bit 7 set on its last character."},
        "15640": {"synopsis":"Returns the next token of the formula text without taking it. It first checks the stack:\nwhen SP is below the word at $1D51 (saved from DE by main_entry), the parse is abandoned\nthrough L_F27C (error 3, L_F0A6). A token already waiting in (IY-77)..(IY-75) (bit 7 of\n(IY-77) clear) is returned again; otherwise L_FD2E scans one and it is kept there as the\nwaiting token.\nEntry: none.\nExit: C = token type; HL = token value (see L_FD64); (IY-79) = C, ($1D4D) = HL and (IY-124)\n= (IY-112) (L_FD3F).\nError: an invalid token abandons the parse through L_F0A6."},
        "15674": {"synopsis":"Takes the next token of the formula text. A token waiting from L_FD0C (bit 7 of (IY-77)\nclear) is taken and marked as used; otherwise the text's bank (IY-112) is bound with L_D887\nwhen it is not the one in (IY-111), L_FD64 scans the token at ($1D4F) and $1D4F moves past\nit. Ends in L_FD3F.\nEntry: ($1D4F) = position in the formula text.\nExit: C = token type; HL = token value; (IY-79) = C; ($1D4D) = HL; (IY-124) = (IY-112).\nError: an invalid token abandons the parse through L_F0A6 with L_FD64's error code."},
        "15691": {"synopsis":"Makes a token the current value: stores the type C in (IY-79), the value HL at $1D4D and the\nformula text's bank (IY-112) in (IY-124). The parser also calls it with C = 1 and L = the\nargument count at the end of an argument list.\nEntry: C = token type; HL = token value.\nExit: A = (IY-112).\nChanges: A."},
        "15728": {"synopsis":"Scans one token of the formula text at HL and returns its type in C.\n1. A zero byte ends the text: C = $0F (DE is not changed).\n2. A letter starts a function name, looked up in FunctionTree with BinaryTreeSearch: C =\n$0E, L = node data (function ID and argument form); for INDEX, ROW and COL (table L_FDB5)\nbit 7 of (IY-44) is set. An unknown name is error $0A.\n3. A digit or \".\" is a number read with FP_VAL into $1D96 (HL'), $1D98 (HL) and $1D9A (C): C\n= 7. When FP_VAL fails the text is read as a date with GN_Gdt into IY+35: C = 8, HL = IY+35;\na failure there is error $16.\n4. A byte $10-$13 (L_FE32) starts a cell reference: C = 3, HL = address of its 3 bytes; a\nsecond reference straight after makes a range, C = 4.\n5. A $14 byte starts a string that runs to the next $14: C = 5, HL = offset of its first\ncharacter from the text start (IY-114)/(IY-113); a missing end is error $0A.\n6. Anything else is looked up in OperatorTree: C = $0D, L = function ID; a character that is\nno operator is returned as itself, C = the character.\nEntry: HL = position in the formula text.\nExit: Fc = 0; C = token type; HL = token value; DE = address after the token.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code ($0A or $16)."},
        "15782": {"comment":"failed to find match"},
        "15785": {"comment":"A=function node data"},
        "15809": {"synopsis":"Table of 3 function IDs that L_FD64 checks a function name against: FuncID_Index ($0C),\nFuncID_Row ($16) and FuncID_Col ($05). A formula that calls one of them gets bit 7 of\n(IY-44) set."},
        "15933": {"synopsis":"Loads A from (HL) and falls into L_FE32.\nEntry: HL = address of the byte.\nExit: as L_FE32; A = (HL).\nChanges: AF."},
        "15934": {"synopsis":"Tests whether A is $10-$13, a marker byte that starts a cell reference in formula text\n(L_FD64), or $14, the string delimiter.\nEntry: A = byte.\nExit: Fc = 1 when A is $10-$13; Fz = 1 when A is $14.\nChanges: F."},
        "15941": {"synopsis":"Search binary tree for text match.\n\nEach tree node consists of the following data:\n+0: node data\n+1: offset of right subnode + 1 (0=no subnode)\n+2: offset of left subnode + 1 (0=no subnode)\n+3..N: node text, uppercase, bit 7-terminated\n\nNode offsets are from table base.\nEntry: HL=string start, null-terminated; DE=base address of tree - 1; A=offset of first node\nto search + 1.\nExit: Fc=1, failed to find match; HL=string start; Fc=0, match found; DE=address in string\nfollowing match; L = node data.","comment":"save string start"},
        "15942": {"comment":"save tree base"},
        "15943": {"comment":"calculate DE=next node address"},
        "15948": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: BinaryTreeGotNode."},
        "15949": {"comment":"IX=node address"},
        "15953": {"comment":"DE=address of node text"},
        "15954": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: BinaryTreeNodeCompare.","comment":"get next character from string"},
        "15955": {"comment":"check for null terminator"},
        "15962": {"comment":"C=next character to match"},
        "15963": {"comment":"A=next character from table entry"},
        "15964": {"comment":"mask out terminator bit"},
        "15969": {"comment":"get right node if string >"},
        "15974": {"comment":"get left node if string <"},
        "15977": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: BinaryTreeNodeFail.","comment":"restore tree base"},
        "15978": {"comment":"and string start"},
        "15980": {"comment":"loop back for more nodes"},
        "15982": {"comment":"Fc=1, failure"},
        "15984": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: BinaryTreeCharMatch.","comment":"refetch table entry character"},
        "15987": {"comment":"loop back unless end of table entry text"},
        "15990": {"comment":"discard tree base"},
        "15991": {"comment":"discard string start, stack current string address"},
        "15992": {"comment":"DE=address in string following match"},
        "15993": {"comment":"L=node data"},
        "15996": {"comment":"Fc=0, match found"},
        "15998": {"synopsis":"Copies the 5-byte number at ($1D4D) to the number buffer: the first word to $1D96, the\nsecond to $1D98 and the fifth byte (the exponent) to $1D9A, the layout L_FD64 writes and\nL_FEF0 reads.\nEntry: ($1D4D) = address of the number.\nExit: HL = address after it; DE = second word; A = exponent.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "16022": {"synopsis":"Loads the 5-byte number at ($1D4D) into the first FPP operand: IX = ($1D4D), then L_FE8E.\nEntry: ($1D4D) = address of the number.\nExit: HL' HL C = number; IX = ($1D4D).\nChanges: C, HL, IX, HL'."},
        "16026": {"synopsis":"Loads the 5-byte number at IX into the first FPP operand: (IX+0)/(IX+1) to HL',\n(IX+2)/(IX+3) to HL and (IX+4), the exponent, to C.\nEntry: IX = address of the number.\nExit: HL' HL C = number.\nChanges: C, HL, HL'."},
        "16044": {"synopsis":"Stores the first FPP operand HL' HL C as a 5-byte number at IX (layout at L_FE8E).\nEntry: IX = destination; HL' HL C = number.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "16062": {"synopsis":"Loads the 5-byte number at ($1D4D) into the second FPP operand: IX = ($1D4D), then L_FEB6.\nEntry: ($1D4D) = address of the number.\nExit: DE' DE B = number; IX = ($1D4D).\nChanges: B, DE, IX, DE'."},
        "16066": {"synopsis":"Loads the 5-byte number at IX into the second FPP operand: (IX+0)/(IX+1) to DE',\n(IX+2)/(IX+3) to DE and (IX+4), the exponent, to B.\nEntry: IX = address of the number.\nExit: DE' DE B = number.\nChanges: B, DE, DE'."},
        "16084": {"synopsis":"Stores the second FPP operand DE' DE B as a 5-byte number at IX (layout at L_FEB6).\nEntry: IX = destination; DE' DE B = number.\nExit: none.\nChanges: none."},
        "16102": {"synopsis":"Exchanges the two FPP operands: HL' with DE', HL with DE and C with B.\nEntry: HL' HL C and DE' DE B = numbers.\nExit: the two numbers exchanged; A = the old B.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL, DE', HL'."},
        "16124": {"synopsis":"Converts the number in the number buffer ($1D96..$1D9A) to text at IY+35, formatted by the\nbyte in A.\n1. Unless bit 6 of A is set, L_88E0 adds the default options: bit 7 when bit 2 of (IY-69) is\nclear, and the bits of (IY+9).\n2. The width B is (IY-36). Bit 4 reserves room for the trailing text at IY+16 ((IY+15)\nbytes); bit 5 for the leading text at IY+22 ((IY+14) bytes), which is copied first with\nL_FF99.\n3. With bit 7 a negative number is written in brackets, and a positive one gets a $7F byte\nwhere the \")\" would go; without it a negative number gets \"-\".\n4. FP_STR writes the digits: the low 4 bits of A are the decimal places, or, when they are\n$F, the general format with as many digits as fit, at most 10.\n5. Bit 4 appends the trailing text with L_FF99; the text ends in a zero byte. When the width\nruns out the text is \"%\" and (IY-74) is set to 1 (L_FEE3).\nEntry: A = format byte; number at $1D96 (HL'), $1D98 (HL) and $1D9A (C); (IY-36) = width.\nExit: IY+35 = text, zero-terminated."},
        "16294": {"synopsis":"Copies A bytes from the workspace at IY+DE to (HL).\nEntry: A = count (0 copies 256 bytes); DE = offset from IY; HL = destination.\nExit: HL = address after the copy; E = 0; IX = IY+DE+count.\nChanges: AF, E, HL, IX."}
      }
    },
