        "434": {"comment":"destroy hl"},
        "436": {"comment":"skip zero separator"},
        "440": {"comment":"entry start"},
        "442": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=optionChar, B=maxWidth, IX=optionList."},
        "446": {"comment":"char count"},
        "450": {"comment":"null or -1? exit loop"},
        "452": {"comment":"!! unnecessary"},
        "455": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "461": {"comment":"pad with (b-c) spaces"},
        "482": {"comment":"move cursor to start of string"},
        "492": {"synopsis":"Table of 15 words: the handler of each command code $20-$2E, in order CmdEscape, CmdEnter,\nCmdLeft, CmdRight, CmdUp, CmdDown, CmdNextOption, CmdChgPage (twice, $27 and $28), CmdLoad,\nCmdSave, CmdName, CmdNew, CmdUpdate and CmdTranslations. MainLoop indexes it with (code -\n$20) * 2.","comment":"$20"},
        "494": {"comment":"$21"},
        "496": {"comment":"$22"},
        "498": {"comment":"$23"},
        "500": {"comment":"$24"},
        "502": {"comment":"$25"},
        "504": {"comment":"$26"},
        "506": {"comment":"$27"},
        "508": {"comment":"$28"},
        "510": {"comment":"$29"},
        "512": {"comment":"$2A"},
        "514": {"comment":"$2B"},
        "516": {"comment":"$2C"},
        "518": {"comment":"$2D"},
        "520": {"comment":"$2E"},
        "522": {"synopsis":"The Enter command ($21). In the Panel it applies every setting (CmdUpdate) and leaves\nthrough Exit; in PrinterEd it moves to the next entry like CmdDown.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: PrinterEd: p_ubEntryID = the next entry. Panel: does not return.","comment":"panel? handle as escape"},
        "525": {"comment":"else handle as cursor down"},
        "527": {"comment":"apply and exit if panel"},
        "533": {"synopsis":"The Escape command ($20): acknowledges the escape (ClearEsc). The Panel then leaves through\nExit without applying anything; PrinterEd returns to the main loop.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: PrinterEd only: A = the page ID; Fz = 0."},
        "536": {"comment":"panel? exit"},
        "542": {"synopsis":"Acknowledges a pending escape with OS_Esc (SC_ACK).\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "549": {"synopsis":"The cursor-up command ($24): selects the previous entry of the page; from the first entry\n($20) it wraps to the last one.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: p_ubEntryID = the new entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"!! ld c,a, then jr z below"},
        "554": {"comment":"first entry on page? wrap"},
        "569": {"comment":"had more? loop"},
        "576": {"synopsis":"The cursor-down command ($25): selects the next entry of the page; after the last one it\nwraps to the first ($20). CmdEnter falls back on it in PrinterEd.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: p_ubEntryID = the new entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "584": {"comment":"had more? don't wrap"},
        "592": {"synopsis":"The page commands ($27, $28): in PrinterEd switches between page 1 and page 2 (from the\ntranslation page it goes to page 1), selects the first entry and redraws the screen through\nDrawScreenLabels. The Panel has one page and returns at once.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: p_ubPageID and p_ubEntryID set; the screen redrawn."},
        "614": {"synopsis":"The translations command ($2E): selects the first entry of PrinterEd's ISO translation page\n(page $22) and redraws the screen through DrawScreenLabels.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: p_ubPageID = $22; p_ubEntryID = $20."},
        "624": {"synopsis":"!! this could be made much shorter if we relied on correct list order"},
        "631": {"comment":"x"},
        "633": {"comment":"y"},
        "644": {"comment":"[-1,-1,-1,-1,x,y]"},
        "651": {"comment":"next entry"},
        "659": {"comment":"no more? end"},
        "661": {"comment":"x"},
        "663": {"comment":"y"},
        "696": {"comment":"so store this"},
        "708": {"comment":"and loop"},
        "714": {"comment":"prepare for wrap"},
        "721": {"comment":"otherwise use stored"},
        "735": {"synopsis":"The cursor-left command ($22): selects the entry that comes before the current one in\nreading order (the nearest one above it, or left of it on the same row), comparing the\nfields' screen positions. With none before it, it wraps to the last entry of the page. Keeps\na 6-byte work area on the stack and leaves through CmdRight's ending.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: p_ubEntryID and p_ubPageID = the new entry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "742": {"comment":"x"},
        "744": {"comment":"y"},
        "755": {"comment":"[0,0,0,0,x,y]"},
        "762": {"comment":"next entry"},
        "770": {"comment":"no more? end"},
        "772": {"comment":"x"},
        "774": {"comment":"y"},
        "805": {"comment":"so store this"},
        "817": {"comment":"and loop"},
        "819": {"comment":"prepare for wrap"},
        "831": {"comment":"otherwise use stored"},
        "845": {"synopsis":"The next-option command ($26) for a number field with an option list (the baud rates): finds\nthe buffer's text in the list (MatchComboOption), takes the option after it, copies that\ntext into the buffer, stores it (ValidateInput) and prints an error if that fails. Does\nnothing for a field without a list.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: the buffer and the setting hold the next option."},
        "854": {"comment":"yes/no? exit"},
        "861": {"comment":"copy entry text into buffer"},
        "879": {"synopsis":"Exit: Fc=0, HL=optionText; Fc=1, HL=first option if not found."},
        "893": {"synopsis":"compare buffer with current optionText","comment":"skip leading spaces"},
        "900": {"comment":"end at space"},
        "911": {"comment":"not same? try next option"},
        "914": {"comment":"not end? continue compare"},
        "916": {"comment":"return matched entry"},
        "919": {"comment":"skip rest of option text"},
        "927": {"comment":"not end of list? compare next"},
        "929": {"comment":"return first entry"},
        "932": {"comment":"and carry"},
        "934": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: GetNextComboOption.\nEntry: HL=optionText, IX=optionList.\nExit: HL=optionText, A=optionChar."},
        "947": {"comment":"else ret default"},
        "951": {"comment":"and get OptionChar"},
        "952": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=optionText.\nExit: HL=optionText, A=optionChar."},
        "957": {"comment":"ret if separator"},
        "961": {"comment":"ret if end of table"},
        "966": {"comment":"ret if number"},
        "971": {"comment":"ret if not alpha"},
        "975": {"comment":"loop if not upper"},
        "980": {"comment":"ret with first char as OptionChar"},
        "982": {"synopsis":"The New command ($2C): resets every parameter of every page to its default with OS_Sp (A =\n255), and in PrinterEd the printer name (PA_Ptr) too, then reads the settings back\n(StoreDefSettings) and redraws the screen through DrawScreenLabels.\nEntry: IY = the variables."},
        "988": {"comment":"no more entries?"},
        "996": {"comment":"set parameter"},
        "1005": {"comment":"do next page"},
        "1010": {"comment":"panel? skip"},
        "1017": {"comment":"set printer name"},
        "1025": {"synopsis":"The Load command ($29): asks for a file name (AskFilename), starts a new setting list\n(is_1), opens the file and reads it line by line: each line is the entry ID, the page ID and\nthe value text, stored through vi_4. The end of the file ends it. On an error the file name\nis cleared and the settings are read back from OZ (StoreAllSettings). Then closes the file,\nredraws the screen and prints any error (CmdSave's ending).\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nError: printed; ERR_BadFile for a line without its two ID bytes or a last line without a CR."},
        "1031": {"comment":"init settings"},
        "1036": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1050": {"comment":"open file"},
        "1055": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1068": {"comment":"length=0? exit"},
        "1076": {"comment":"entryID"},
        "1079": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1085": {"comment":"pageID"},
        "1088": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1091": {"comment":"store setting"},
        "1094": {"comment":"and loop"},
        "1108": {"synopsis":"The Save command ($2A): asks for a file name (AskFilename), opens it for output and writes\none line for every entry of every page that has a saved value: the entry ID, the page ID,\nthe value text and a CR (SaveBuffer). Then closes the file, redraws the screen and prints\nany error.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nError: printed (PrintError); 0 means the system error."},
        "1119": {"comment":"??"},
        "1125": {"comment":"open file/stream (or device)"},
        "1130": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1143": {"comment":"no more? try next page"},
        "1146": {"comment":"not found? skip"},
        "1153": {"comment":"entryID"},
        "1155": {"comment":"pageID"},
        "1157": {"comment":"copy data from IX to HL"},
        "1165": {"comment":"have more? loop"},
        "1171": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1173": {"comment":"next entry"},
        "1174": {"comment":"and loop"},
        "1180": {"comment":"have more? loop"},
        "1182": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "1184": {"comment":"close file if it's open"},
        "1198": {"comment":"no error? skip"},
        "1201": {"comment":"program error? print it"},
        "1203": {"comment":"else system error"},
        "1215": {"synopsis":"The Name command ($2B): asks for a file name (AskFilename) and redraws the screen with it,\nor prints the error. In PrinterEd the name is the printer's name (PA_Ptr), and its file part\nnames the application.\nEntry: IY = the variables."},
        "1227": {"synopsis":"Clears the file name and the flag that says the setting pool is bound in, then falls into\nis_1: selects the first entry, frees the setting pool and opens a new one.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: Fc = 0; p_pSettingPool = the new pool; p_pSettings = 0 (no settings).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Mop.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "1232": {"comment":"not bound in yet"},
        "1235": {"synopsis":"Entry inside InitSettings that keeps the file name: selects the first entry of the first\npage (InitPagePtrs), closes the setting pool if one is open, opens a new one in segment 1\nwith OS_Mop and empties the setting list. CmdLoad uses it.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: Fc = 0; p_pSettingPool = the new pool; p_pSettings = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Mop.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "1242": {"comment":"free memory if it's allocated"},
        "1260": {"comment":"open new pool, segment 1"},
        "1267": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "1268": {"comment":"!! move this above ret to save clearing above"},
        "1275": {"comment":"no setting memory allocated"},
        "1279": {"synopsis":"Writes the buffer as one line of a saved file: replaces its 0 terminator with a CR and\nwrites the text and the CR to the open file with OS_Mv.\nEntry: the buffer = a 0-terminated text; p_pPrinterFileHandle = the file.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = 0 (the system error; OS_Erc gives it).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "1283": {"comment":"terminate with linefeed"},
        "1299": {"comment":"save buffer"},
        "1301": {"comment":"system error (if Fc=1)"},
        "1304": {"synopsis":"Exit: E=length; Fc=1, A=error."},
        "1313": {"comment":"get byte"},
        "1315": {"comment":"no error? save byte"},
        "1320": {"comment":"system error"},
        "1328": {"comment":"bytes without CR? error"},
        "1329": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "1331": {"comment":"bump length"},
        "1332": {"comment":"end at CR"},
        "1339": {"comment":"NULL? end"},
        "1342": {"comment":"ctrl char? ignore"},
        "1347": {"synopsis":"Exit: Fc=status."},
        "1374": {"comment":"has data, return special"},
        "1381": {"comment":"input line"},
        "1390": {"comment":"error? redraw"},
        "1394": {"comment":"enter? ok"},
        "1398": {"comment":"not esc? loop"},
        "1414": {"synopsis":"Opens the file name window: defines window 2 (60 by 8 characters at column 10, with a\nborder), selects and clears it and prints \"Filename\" at row 1.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "1443": {"synopsis":"Closes the file name window: selects window 1 again and sends 1,\"2D2\" for window 2.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "1463": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=error code.\nExit: Fc=status, A=error code."},
        "1494": {"comment":"reposition cursor"},
        "1511": {"synopsis":"Leaves the Panel or PrinterEd: closes the setting pool and the memory pool with OS_Mcl and\ncalls OS_Bye with A = 0. Also reached from MayRedraw and ErrorHandler on RC_Quit.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return."},
        "1526": {"synopsis":"Hangs in a loop to itself: OS_Bye does not come back.","comment":"never reached"},
        "1529": {"comment":"return FPP errors ($46-$4c) to system"},
        "1535": {"comment":"c=1, z=0"},
        "1540": {"comment":"c=0, z=1"},
        "1542": {"comment":"position"},
        "1553": {"comment":"max 16 chars"},
        "1555": {"comment":"read byte from error string"},
        "1559": {"comment":"end? exit"},
        "1569": {"synopsis":"Prints the last system error: falls into PrintError with A = 0, which sounds the bell and\nprints OZ's text for the error (OS_Erc, GN_Esp), at most 16 characters, on row 2.\nEntry: the error to print is OZ's last one.\nExit: Fc = 1."},
        "1570": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=error code."},
        "1597": {"comment":"strlen"},
        "1606": {"comment":"center to 16 char field"},
        "1616": {"comment":"x position"},
        "1631": {"comment":"!! or a; jr p"},
        "1637": {"synopsis":"Table of 7 words: the texts of the program's own errors ERR_OutOfMemory (1) to ERR_BadName\n(7), indexed by the code - 1. PrintError reads it."},
        "1651": {"synopsis":"Error text 1 (ERR_OutOfMemory): \"Out of memory\", bit 7 set on the last letter."},
        "1664": {"synopsis":"Error text 2 (ERR_BadFile): \"Bad file\", bit 7 set on the last letter."},
        "1672": {"synopsis":"Error text 3 (ERR_Escape): \"Escape\", bit 7 set on the last letter."},
        "1678": {"synopsis":"Error text 4 (ERR_BadCodeString): \"Bad code string\", bit 7 set on the last letter.\nOZ source name: BadCodeString_txt."},
        "1693": {"synopsis":"Error text 5 (ERR_StringTooLong): \"String too long\", bit 7 set on the last letter.\nOZ source name: StringTooLong_txt."},
        "1708": {"synopsis":"Error text 6 (ERR_BadValue): \"Bad value\", bit 7 set on the last letter."},
        "1717": {"synopsis":"Error text 7 (ERR_BadName): \"Bad name\", bit 7 set on the last letter."},
        "1725": {"synopsis":"Sounds the bell: writes BEL with OS_Out.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "1730": {"synopsis":"Hides the cursor: writes 1,\"2-C\" through CursorOn's ending (CursorOnOff).\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "1735": {"synopsis":"Shows the cursor: writes 1,\"2+C\".\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "1757": {"synopsis":"Clears the message line: moves to row 2, column 0 and writes 15 spaces.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "1769": {"synopsis":"Prints the 0-terminated text that follows the CALL and returns past it. A byte $A0-$BF is a\nmove: with the next byte it makes a cursor position, row = byte - $A0, column = next byte -\n$20 (KprintSpecial). Other bytes go out with OS_Out.\nEntry: the text after the CALL.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "1779": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "1785": {"synopsis":"KPrint's handler for a byte with bit 7 set. For $A0-$BF it writes 1,\"3@\", the next byte\n(column + $20) and the byte with bit 7 cleared (row + $20), and returns the byte after the\npair for KPrint to print. Other bytes are returned unchanged.\nEntry: A = the byte; HL = its address.\nExit: A = the byte to print; HL = its address.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "1794": {"comment":"MoveTo"},
        "1799": {"comment":"20-3F"},
        "1804": {"comment":"x"},
        "1807": {"comment":"y"},
        "1812": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=char.\nExit: A=char."},
        "1819": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=char.\nExit: Fc=1 if A is alphabetic."},
        "1833": {"synopsis":"Entry: A=char.\nExit: Fc=1 if A is numeric."},
        "1840": {"synopsis":"Draws the whole screen: defines window 1 (92 by 8 characters), selects and clears it, prints\nthe current page's labels (ShowPanel, ShowPrEdPg1, ShowPrEdPg2 or ShowPrEdTrans) and every\nentry's value. In PrinterEd with a printer name it also prints \"PRINTER\" and the name\ncentred under it, and names the application (DC_Nam) after the name's file part.\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "1858": {"comment":"select between different pages"},
        "1891": {"comment":"!! ld c, $20-1"},
        "1898": {"comment":"has more? loop"},
        "1903": {"comment":"panel? we're done"},
        "1911": {"comment":"no printer name? end"},
        "1934": {"comment":"print centered"},
        "1966": {"comment":"end? done"},
        "1973": {"comment":"extract filename part"},
        "1984": {"comment":"read/write filename segments"},
        "1987": {"comment":"name application"},
        "1994": {"synopsis":"Toggles tiny and reverse text: writes 1,\"T\",1,\"R\".\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "2003": {"synopsis":"print comboox/number data"},
        "2006": {"comment":"done? exit"},
        "2014": {"comment":"not combo? skip"},
        "2017": {"comment":"remember width"},
        "2018": {"comment":"a=selected"},
        "2021": {"comment":"b=width"},
        "2028": {"comment":"max width"},
        "2029": {"comment":"not string? skip"},
        "2031": {"comment":"print saved data"},
        "2043": {"comment":"pad with spaces"},
        "2063": {"comment":"Fz=0"},
        "2066": {"synopsis":"move cursor"},
        "2074": {"comment":"x"},
        "2078": {"comment":"y"},
        "2084": {"synopsis":"Copies the 0-terminated text at IX into the buffer (p_pMem_Buffer_100).\nEntry: IX = the text.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2107": {"synopsis":"Entry: B=pageID, C=entryID.\nExit: A=flags67, D=field width, E=flags0-3, HL=entrydata, IX=saved data; Fz=1 if not found."},
        "2117": {"comment":"(c-$20)*5"},
        "2118": {"comment":"de=entry offset"},
        "2119": {"comment":"select page data"},
        "2134": {"comment":"just below"},
        "2157": {"comment":"x"},
        "2159": {"comment":"-1? Fz=1 and Fc=1"},
        "2162": {"comment":"field width"},
        "2164": {"comment":"flags"},
        "2166": {"comment":"bits 6&7"},
        "2174": {"comment":"byte4, bits3-0"},
        "2178": {"synopsis":"Exit: B=pageID, C=entryID."},
        "2179": {"comment":"force PrEd page 1"},
        "2187": {"comment":"BC=PANELPAGE|$20"},
        "2190": {"synopsis":"Entry: B=pageID.\nExit: B=pageID, C=entryID; Fc=1 if no more pages."},
        "2193": {"comment":"panel? exit"},
        "2195": {"comment":"first entry"},
        "2198": {"comment":"wrap to PrEdPg1? set Z"},
        "2202": {"synopsis":"Says whether the Panel is running: reads the page ID and compares it with the Panel's page\n($2A).\nEntry: IY = the variables.\nExit: A = the page ID; Fz = 1 for the Panel, 0 for PrinterEd.\nChanges: AF."},
        "2208": {"synopsis":"Returns an entry's OS_Sp/OS_Nq reason: $80 and the entry record's fifth byte.\nEntry: HL = the entry record (from GetEntryData).\nExit: BC = the reason; HL = HL + 4.\nChanges: BC, HL."},
        "2216": {"synopsis":"Checks the buffer's text for the current entry and stores it as its setting.\n1. A number field with an option list (the baud rates) must match one option (ERR_BadValue).\n2. In the Panel the default device and directory are parsed as names (CheckName,\nERR_BadName); in PrinterEd text is checked as a code string (EncodeTranslate).\n3. Falls into vi_4 to store it. Option-list fields skip the checks.\nEntry: IY = the variables; the buffer = the text.\nExit: Fc = 0, the setting stored.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (ERR_xxx); out of memory is printed here.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2225": {"comment":"combo?"},
        "2229": {"comment":"yes/no? skip"},
        "2231": {"comment":"validate (only for baud rate)"},
        "2243": {"comment":"printered? check number"},
        "2245": {"comment":"else check device/dir"},
        "2262": {"synopsis":"Entry inside ValidateInput: stores a text as the setting of one entry, replacing the one it\nhad (StoreSetting), and copies the text into the new record. CmdLoad stores each line's\nvalue through it.\nEntry: HL = the 0-terminated text; B = the page ID; C = the entry ID.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1; \"Out of memory\" printed (PrintError).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2277": {"comment":"error? exit"},
        "2281": {"comment":"no data? end"},
        "2282": {"comment":"else copy to allocated memory"},
        "2295": {"synopsis":"Returns the length of the 0-terminated text in the buffer; falls into StrLen.\nEntry: the buffer = the text.\nExit: A = the length; HL = past the terminator; BC = - the length.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "2298": {"synopsis":"a=stren(hl)"},
        "2308": {"synopsis":"Entry: B=pageID, C=entryID, HL.\nExit: DE=prev, HL=data; Fc=1 if not found.","comment":"de=this"},
        "2310": {"comment":"hl=next(this)"},
        "2319": {"comment":"do pageID & entryID match?"},
