        "2423": {"comment":"entry#"},
        "2426": {"comment":"page#"},
        "2436": {"synopsis":"Entry: BC=size.\nExit: HL=memory; Fc=1 if error."},
        "2442": {"comment":"no mempool? error"},
        "2454": {"comment":"already bound in"},
        "2457": {"comment":"bind it in S1"},
        "2464": {"synopsis":"Entry: BC=allocation size, IX=memory handle.\nExit: BHL=memory; Fc=1 if no memory."},
        "2468": {"synopsis":"Entry: BC=size, HL=memory."},
        "2483": {"synopsis":"Applies every setting (the Panel's Enter): for every entry of every page sends its value to\nOZ with OS_Sp. A Panel number is converted with FP_VAL, FP_ABS and FP_FIX and sent as a byte\nor a word; a PrinterEd code string is encoded (EncodeTranslate), and for a field with a\nplaceholder (flags bit 5) a non-zero placeholder byte is sent to reason + 3 first; text goes\nas it is; an entry without a value is sent with A = 255. PrinterEd also sends the printer\nname (PA_Ptr). Ends with OS_Sp PA_Gfi, which installs the changed settings. Errors are\nprinted (PrintSysError).\nEntry: IY = the variables."},
        "2496": {"comment":"save Fc from FindSetting()"},
        "2500": {"comment":"not num? skip"},
        "2505": {"comment":"not panel? jump"},
        "2509": {"comment":"no saved data? skip"},
        "2511": {"comment":"str->num"},
        "2515": {"comment":"fix(abs(val(str))) !! might use int() instead of fix()"},
        "2526": {"comment":"return 2 bytes for word, 1 for byte"},
        "2541": {"comment":"no saved data? skip"},
        "2560": {"comment":"has saved data?"},
        "2573": {"comment":"placeholder, length"},
        "2578": {"comment":"placeholder"},
        "2580": {"comment":"no placeholder? skip !! should there be way to disable it?"},
        "2582": {"comment":"single byte"},
        "2584": {"comment":"reason+3"},
        "2604": {"comment":"entryID++"},
        "2607": {"comment":"pageID++"},
        "2610": {"comment":"has more? loop"},
        "2612": {"comment":"panel? skip"},
        "2635": {"comment":"install changed settings"},
        "2638": {"synopsis":"Exit: B=length, C=wild; Fc=1, A=error.","comment":"output buffer"},
        "2642": {"comment":"max 32 bytes, no wildchar"},
        "2649": {"comment":"end?"},
        "2654": {"comment":"comma? skip"},
        "2658": {"comment":"space? skip"},
        "2663": {"comment":"digit? number"},
        "2667": {"comment":"quote? string"},
        "2671": {"comment":"$? hhex"},
        "2675": {"comment":"'?'? wildcard"},
        "2679": {"comment":"^? control char"},
        "2684": {"comment":"alpha? name"},
        "2691": {"comment":"return integer in BC"},
        "2696": {"comment":"ASCII to integer conversion"},
        "2700": {"comment":"not number?"},
        "2704": {"comment":">255?"},
        "2709": {"comment":"store char"},
        "2714": {"comment":"end?"},
        "2718": {"comment":"quote? done"},
        "2720": {"comment":"store and loop"},
        "2736": {"comment":"not hex?"},
        "2744": {"comment":"single digit hex?"},
        "2758": {"comment":"store char"},
        "2761": {"comment":"has wildchar"},
        "2763": {"comment":"store and loop if room"},
        "2770": {"comment":"else error"},
        "2777": {"comment":"only allow $00-$1f"},
        "2782": {"comment":"!! unnecessary"},
        "2802": {"comment":"control char? jump"},
        "2805": {"comment":"negative? exit"},
        "2816": {"comment":"same? continue compare"},
        "2818": {"comment":"skip current ASCII name"},
        "2824": {"comment":"restore string pointer and loop"},
        "2832": {"comment":"was alpha? try next"},
        "2834": {"comment":"get control char"},
        "2836": {"comment":"and store it"},
        "2841": {"comment":"length of data"},
        "2844": {"comment":"no wild? skip"},
        "2849": {"comment":"length"},
        "2856": {"comment":"match? try smaller one"},
        "2858": {"comment":"loop until done"},
        "2860": {"comment":"replace wild with e"},
        "2871": {"comment":"and return placeholder"},
        "2875": {"synopsis":"!! bug $: -> $3a-$30=10 -> 10-7=3 -> valid hex?\nEntry: A=char.\nExit: A=nibble; Fc=1 if not hex."},
        "2891": {"synopsis":"Entry: HL=path.\nExit: Fc=0 if ok; Fc=1, A=error."},
        "2896": {"comment":"default device"},
        "2900": {"comment":"default directory"},
        "2910": {"comment":"space? skip"},
        "2913": {"comment":"null? exit"},
        "2914": {"comment":"parse filename"},
        "2921": {"comment":"dir/device/wildcards? error"},
        "2923": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "2924": {"comment":"parse filename segment"},
        "2931": {"comment":"no filename/directory/wildcards? Fc=0"},
        "2936": {"synopsis":"!! it's possible to crash by overflowing stack buffer\nwith translation string like \"zzzzz\" where there are\nmore than 63 characters"},
        "2940": {"synopsis":"Entry inside StoreDefSettings, after InitSettings: reads every entry's current value from OZ\n(OS_Nq) and stores it as a text setting. A Panel number becomes decimal text (FP_STR); a\nPrinterEd code becomes a comma-separated list of decimal numbers (GN_Pdn, built on the\nstack); text is kept. PrinterEd first reads the printer name (PA_Ptr) into the file name\nbuffer.\nEntry: IY = the variables; a setting pool open.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 when memory runs out.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "2954": {"comment":"get printer name"},
        "2962": {"comment":"end of page? skip"},
        "2975": {"comment":"get parameter"},
        "2977": {"comment":"save #bytes"},
        "2982": {"comment":"not number? skip"},
        "2985": {"comment":"no data? skip"},
        "2990": {"comment":"not panel? show chr list"},
        "2992": {"comment":"get byte/word into DE"},
        "3002": {"comment":"de=00=general format, no digits"},
        "3009": {"comment":"HLhlC=00hl0=integer hl"},
        "3014": {"comment":"integer to ASCII"},
        "3021": {"comment":"has more pages? loop"},
        "3025": {"synopsis":"character list into buffer","comment":"reserve 256 bytes from stack"},
        "3028": {"comment":"for comma-separated numbers"},
        "3042": {"comment":"BC to (DE) as ASCII"},
        "3048": {"comment":"end of data? stop"},
        "3052": {"comment":"comma delimeter and loop"},
        "3057": {"comment":"zero terminate"},
        "3060": {"comment":"copy stack data into buffer"},
        "3069": {"comment":"BC=length"},
        "3076": {"comment":"copy into buffer"},
        "3080": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "3118": {"synopsis":"Table of control character names for PrinterEd's code strings: each record is the name in\ncapitals followed by its code ($00-$1F), from \"NUL\" to \"US\", with synonyms such as \"BELL\",\n\"TAB\", \"XON\" and \"XOFF\"; -1 ends it. EncodeTranslate looks names up in it."},
        "3257": {"synopsis":"Entry table format\n00     x+$20\n01     y+$20\n02     field width\n03     b7      numeric (if b4 as well then it's list of numbers)\nb6      combo\nb5      has placeholder? (only for reasons PA_OnX+3)\nb4      string\nb3-b0   combo type 0:[Y|N],2:[Ins|Ovr],4:[Eur|Am],6:[N|S|M|O|E],8:[Baud rates],10:[Localization]\n04     OS_Sp reason code low byte"},
        "3378": {"synopsis":"Prints the labels of PrinterEd's page 1 (the printer codes 1-8 and their ON, OFF and Off at\nCR fields) through KPrint.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "3611": {"synopsis":"Entry table of PrinterEd's page 2: 25 records (printer on and off, end of page, allow line\nfeed, the HMI prefix, suffix and offset, then the nine translations' characters and codes),\n-1 ends it. Each record is 5 bytes: x + $20, y + $20, the field width, the flags (bit 7\nnumber, bit 6 option list, bit 5 has a placeholder, bit 4 text (with bit 7, a list of\nnumbers), bits 3-0 the option list's offset in ComboBox_tbl) and the low byte of the\nOS_Sp/OS_Nq reason ($80xx). GetEntryData reads it."},
        "3737": {"synopsis":"Prints the labels of PrinterEd's page 2 (printer on/off, end of page, line feed, HMI and the\ntranslations A to C) through KPrint.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4008": {"synopsis":"Entry table of PrinterEd's ISO translation page: 64 records in 8 columns of 8, alternating a\ncharacter (a number, width 5) and what it changes to (a code string, width 8), for reasons\n$80-$BF; $FF ends it. Each record is 5 bytes: x + $20, y + $20, the field width, the flags\n(bit 7 number, bit 6 option list, bit 5 has a placeholder, bit 4 text (with bit 7, a list of\nnumbers), bits 3-0 the option list's offset in ComboBox_tbl) and the low byte of the\nOS_Sp/OS_Nq reason ($80xx). GetEntryData reads it."},
        "4329": {"synopsis":"Prints the labels of PrinterEd's ISO translation page (Ch and To on alternate rows) through\nKPrint.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4438": {"synopsis":"Entry table of the Panel: 15 records (auto repeat, keyclick, insert/overtype, default device\nand directory, timeout, sound, map, map size, date format, the baud rates, parity, Xon/Xoff\nand the keyboard), -1 ends it. Each record is 5 bytes: x + $20, y + $20, the field width,\nthe flags (bit 7 number, bit 6 option list, bit 5 has a placeholder, bit 4 text (with bit 7,\na list of numbers), bits 3-0 the option list's offset in ComboBox_tbl) and the low byte of\nthe OS_Sp/OS_Nq reason ($80xx). GetEntryData reads it."},
        "4514": {"synopsis":"Prints the Panel's labels and its \"PRESS ENTER TO UPDATE\" note through KPrint.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "4763": {"synopsis":"Table of 6 words: the option lists YesNoTxt_tbl, CursorTxt_tbl, FormatTxt_tbl,\nParityTxt_tbl, BaudTxt_tbl and Keymap_tbl, indexed by bits 3-0 of an entry's flags (0, 2,\n... 10). GetComboBox reads it."},
        "4775": {"synopsis":"Option list \"Yes\" and \"No\": the texts separated by 0, -1 ends it. An option's key is its\nfirst capital letter or digit."},
        "4782": {"synopsis":"Option list \"Insert\" and \"Overtype\", separated by 0, -1 ends it."},
        "4798": {"synopsis":"Option list of the date format, \"European\" and \"American\", separated by 0, -1 ends it."},
        "4816": {"synopsis":"Option list of the parity: \"None\", \"Space\", \"Mark\", \"Odd\" and \"Even\", separated by 0, -1\nends it."},
        "4841": {"synopsis":"Option list of the baud rates: 9600, 19200, 38400, 75, 300, 600, 1200 and 2400, separated by\n0, -1 ends it. CmdNextOption steps through it."},
        "4880": {"synopsis":"Option list of the keyboard layouts: \"Uk\", \"France\", \"Denmark\", \"Sweden\", \"finLand\",\n\"Germany\", \"usA\", \"sPain\", \"Italy\" and \"Norway\", separated by 0, -1 ends it. The capital\nletter is each option's key.","comment":"U"},
        "4883": {"comment":"F"},
        "4890": {"comment":"D"},
        "4898": {"comment":"S"},
        "4905": {"comment":"L"},
        "4913": {"comment":"G"},
        "4921": {"comment":"A"},
        "4925": {"comment":"P"},
        "4931": {"comment":"I"},
        "4937": {"comment":"N"},
        "4945": {"synopsis":"Gbs 2011/01/29: Uncomment each layout below, when implemented, first \"Italy\", then \"Norway\", etc...\n\ndefm    \"sWitzerland\",0                 ; W\ndefm    \"iCeland\",0                     ; C\ndefm    \"Japan\",0                       ; J\ndefm    \"Turkey\"                        ; T\ndefm    -1"},
        "5120": {"comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
