        "5790": {"comment":"column"},
        "5798": {"comment":"row"},
        "5811": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: Main."},
        "5814": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: main_1."},
        "5819": {"synopsis":"The Calculator's Enter key: presses the highlighted button. Drops the return address that\nIndirectJump left, takes the character of button row * 5 + column from Key2Button_tbl and\ndispatches it as a typed key (main_5).\nOZ source name: main_2.\nEntry: IY = the Calculator's variables (calc_ActiveRow, calc_ActiveCol)."},
        "5827": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: main_3."},
        "5833": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: main_4."},
        "5844": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: main_5."},
        "5850": {"comment":"key #"},
        "5855": {"comment":"no more keys"},
        "5864": {"comment":"key #"},
        "5874": {"comment":"button column"},
        "5875": {"comment":"button row"},
        "5904": {"synopsis":"Table of the Calculator's keys, a 0 at the end: the 25 buttons row by row (C, DEL, S, R, +,\n7, 8, 9, U, *, 4, 5, 6, Y, -, 1, 2, 3, I, /, 0, ., %, F, =), the convert keys P, T, X, M, D,\n\\ and E, then the cursor keys ($FF, $FE, $FC, $FD), Enter, Escape and $12. A key's place\ngives the button's row and column and its handler in KeyTable."},
        "5944": {"synopsis":"Table of 39 words: the handler of each key in Key2Button_tbl, in the same order. The main\nloop calls it through IndirectJump with the key's number."},
        "6022": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the digit keys (KeyTable). Clears a shown error (ClrError). With no\ncommand pending the digit goes to the number being typed (PutNum); with StoM, RclM or Fix\nwaiting for its digit, it calls the command's handler in CmdTable (DoStoM, RclM, Fix)\nthrough IndirectJump.\nEntry: A = key, '0' to '9'; IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: to PutNum; or to the command's handler with A = digit (0-9); DE = IX = address of the\nbyte after the command code in calc_CmdBuffer."},
        "6055": {"synopsis":"Calculator: the StoM command, reached from key_Num through CmdTable. Takes the shown value\n(ldFH_F1NumBuf) into FReg1 and Float1, points IX at memory A (GetMemPtrA) and jumps through\nStoM_tbl, indexed by the operator stored after StoM (none, +, -, x, /), to store, add,\nsubtract, multiply or divide the value into that memory. The memory's address is left on the\nstack for StoM_plain.\nEntry: A = memory number (0-9); DE = address of the operator byte in calc_CmdBuffer (0 for\nnone, 5-8 for + - x /); IY = calculator workspace."},
        "6092": {"synopsis":"Calculator: table of 5 words, the StoM handlers: StoM_plain, StoM_add, StoM_sub, StoM_mul\nand StoM_div. DoStoM indexes it with 0 for a plain StoM or the operator byte minus 4 (1-4)."},
        "6102": {"synopsis":"Calculator: StoM+. Loads the memory into FReg2 (RclM_FReg2), adds it to the value (FpAdd)\nand goes on to StoM_plain to store the sum in the memory.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = value; IX = memory slot; the slot's address on the stack."},
        "6110": {"synopsis":"Calculator: StoM-. Loads the memory into FReg2 (RclM_FReg2), computes memory - value (FpSub)\nand goes on to StoM_plain to store the result in the memory.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = value; IX = memory slot; the slot's address on the stack."},
        "6118": {"synopsis":"Calculator: StoMx. Loads the memory into FReg2 (RclM_FReg2), multiplies it by the value\n(FpMul) and goes on to StoM_plain to store the product in the memory.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = value; IX = memory slot; the slot's address on the stack."},
        "6126": {"synopsis":"Calculator: StoM/. Loads the memory into FReg2 (RclM_FReg2), computes memory / value (FpDiv)\nand falls into StoM_plain to store the quotient in the memory.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = value; IX = memory slot; the slot's address on the stack."},
        "6132": {"synopsis":"Calculator: plain StoM, and the end of every StoM handler. Pops the memory slot's address\ninto IX, stores FReg1 in it (StoM_FReg1) and falls into ClearCommand.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = value to store; the memory slot's address on the stack."},
        "6137": {"synopsis":"Calculator: ends a command. Resets the command flag (CF_B_Command) and empties the command\nbuffer (calc_CmdBuffer).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nChanges: F, DE, HL.\nKeeps: A, BC."},
        "6151": {"synopsis":"Calculator: the RclM command, reached from key_Num through CmdTable. Drops the number being\ntyped, loads memory A into FReg1 and Float1 (the shown value) and goes to ClearCommand.\nEntry: A = memory number (0-9); IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Float1 = memory A."},
        "6166": {"synopsis":"Calculator: the Fix command, reached from key_Num through CmdTable. Stores 2 * A + 1 in\nvarFix (bit 0 marks a Fix as set; the display code, sub_FEBC, takes A back as the number of\ndecimals, 9 selecting a different FP_STR format) and goes to ClearCommand.\nEntry: A = digit (0-9); IY = calculator workspace."},
        "6173": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the '.' and 'E' keys (KeyTable). Ignores the key when the number\nbeing typed already holds that character; otherwise falls into PutNum, which also starts a\nnew number with it.\nEntry: A = '.' or 'E'; IY = calculator workspace."},
        "6189": {"comment":"'.' or 'E' already entered"},
        "6194": {"synopsis":"Calculator: adds a character to the number being typed (calc_NumBuffer, at most 17\ncharacters). Ignored while a command is pending. Starts an empty buffer when no number is\nbeing typed (sets CF_B_HasNumBuf), and a new character other than '.' replaces a leading '0'\nthat is not followed by '.'. A full buffer drops the character (NumBufferFull).\nEntry: A = character; IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: calc_BufferPos advanced; buffer zero-terminated.\nChanges: F, C, DE, HL."},
        "6270": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the Clear key (KeyTable). Cancels a pending command (ClearCommand),\nclears the number-entry, operator, error, constant and CF_B_3 flags, and falls into ZeroNums\nto zero X and Y (Float1 and Float2).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL."},
        "6273": {"comment":"!! and these away"},
        "6293": {"synopsis":"clear X & Y","comment":"2*fp"},
        "6300": {"synopsis":"<>R - clear all memories"},
        "6306": {"comment":"10*fp+fix"},
        "6311": {"synopsis":"Fills B bytes from HL with zero. Reached from ZeroNums, from key_DiamR (falls in, clearing\nthe memories and varFix) and from the start-up code (the workspace).\nEntry: HL = start; B = byte count (1-256).\nExit: HL = byte after the block; A = 0; B = 0.\nChanges: AF, B, HL."},
        "6317": {"synopsis":"Calculator: clears a shown error. When CF_B_Error is set, it resets it and the number-entry\nand operator flags (CF_B_HasNumBuf, CF_B_Symbol).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nChanges: F.","comment":"!! use and"},
        "6335": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the RclM key (KeyTable). A = CC_RCLM and on to PutCmd, which starts\nthe command; the memory number comes with the next digit (key_Num).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "6339": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the Fix key (KeyTable). A = CC_FIX and on to PutCmd, which starts the\ncommand; the number of decimals comes with the next digit (key_Num).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "6343": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the StoM key (KeyTable). A = CC_STOM and falls into PutCmd, which\nstarts the command (ignored while an error is shown or a command is pending); an operator\nand the memory number follow (loc_F9AB, key_Num).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "6359": {"synopsis":"Calculator: appends a byte to the zero-terminated command buffer (calc_CmdBuffer): a command\ncode (CC_xxx, 4 for Unit) or an operator byte (5-8 for + - x /) after StoM.\nEntry: A = byte; IY = calculator workspace.\nChanges: F, C, DE, HL."},
        "6378": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the Unit key (KeyTable): the unit conversions. Ignored while an error\nis shown or a command is pending.\n1. Stores Unit (4) in the command buffer, shows it (sub_FBA0), sets CF_B_Convert, redraws\nthe calculator button and selects window 4, the convert window.\n2. UnitLoop: redraws the convert buttons (UpdConvButton), reads a key (ReadKey, ToUpper),\nlooks it up in UnitKey_tbl, ignoring keys not there, and calls its handler from UnitCmd_tbl\nwith A = key; it loops while the handler returns Fc = 0.\n3. Clears CF_B_Convert, redraws the convert button, selects window 5 again, redraws the\ncalculator button and ends with ClearCommand.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "6430": {"comment":"no more keys"},
        "6470": {"synopsis":"Calculator: the keys of the unit conversion, 20 bytes and a zero terminator: 'C', DEL ($7F),\nLeft ($FC), Right ($FD), Up ($FF), Down ($FE), '=', Enter ($0D), Esc ($1B), '0' to '9' and\n'.'. key_Unit's loop uses the index of the key found to pick its handler in UnitCmd_tbl."},
        "6491": {"synopsis":"Calculator: table of 20 words, the unit conversion's key handlers in UnitKey_tbl's order:\nckey_Clr, ckey_Del, ckey_Left, ckey_Right, ckey_Up, ckey_Down, ckey_EquEnter twice ('=' and\nEnter), ckey_Esc, ckey_Num ten times and ckey_Dot. A handler returning Fc = 1 ends the\nconversion."},
        "6531": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: a digit key. Adds it to the number being typed (PutNum) and\ngoes on to ckey_numdot to show it.\nEntry: A = '0' to '9'; IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0 when OS_Pout succeeds, so the conversion goes on."},
        "6536": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the '.' key. Adds it to the number being typed (key_DotE), then\nckey_numdot selects window 5, redraws the value (PrintStatusRow), selects window 4 again and\nreturns.\nEntry: A = '.'; IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0 when OS_Pout succeeds, so the conversion goes on."},
        "6557": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the Clear key. Clears the calculator (key_Clr) and falls into\nckey_Del, which ends the conversion.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Fc = 1."},
        "6560": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the DEL key, and the end of ckey_Clr. Ends the conversion\nwithout converting.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1.\nChanges: F."},
        "6562": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the Up key. Moves the highlight up a row (cDecRow); from the\ntop row it wraps to the bottom row and falls into cDecCol to step back a column as well.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6566": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active convert column left, from column 0 wrapping to column 1. Also\nthe end of ckey_Up.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: A = old column; Fz = 1 when it wrapped; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6582": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the Left key. Moves the highlight a column left (cDecCol); from\ncolumn 0 it wraps to column 1 and falls into cDecRow to step up a row as well.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6586": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active convert row up, from row 0 wrapping to row 6. Also the end of\nckey_Left.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: A = old row; Fz = 1 when it wrapped; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6602": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the Right key. Moves the highlight a column right (cIncCol);\nfrom column 1 it wraps to column 0 and falls into cIncRow to step down a row as well.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6606": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active convert row down, from row 6 wrapping to row 0. Also the end of\nckey_Right.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: A = new row; Fz = 1 when it wrapped; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6624": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the Down key. Moves the highlight down a row (cIncRow); from\nrow 6 it wraps to row 0 and falls into cIncCol to step right a column as well.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6628": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active convert column right, from column 1 wrapping to column 0. Also\nthe end of ckey_Down.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: A = new column; Fz = 1 when it wrapped; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6646": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the '=' and Enter keys. Converts the shown value with the\nactive conversion and ends the conversion. Takes the value into Float1 (ldFH_F1NumBuf),\nloads the active row's factor from ConvNumTable (GetNumC, FpVal) into FReg1 and jumps\nthrough ConvertCmd_tbl, indexed by the row, with A = the active column (0 converts into the\nleft unit, 1 into the right one). The handler leaves the result in Float1.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Float1 = converted value; Fc = 1."},
        "6675": {"synopsis":"Calculator: table of 7 words, the conversion of each convert row: loc_F71D (multiply by the\nfactor) for Gallons/Litres, Miles/km, Acres/Hectares, lb/kg and oz/g, loc_F72C for\nMPG/l/100km and loc_F73A for DegF/DegC. ckey_EquEnter indexes it with the active row."},
        "6689": {"synopsis":"Calculator: converts by a factor. Inverts the factor for column 1 (sub_F76F), multiplies the\nvalue by it and falls into loc_F727, which stores the result in Float1 and sets Fc. Column 0\nconverts into the left unit (litres to gallons), column 1 into the right one.\nEntry: A = active column; FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = factor; Float1 = value.\nExit: Float1 = result; Fc = 1."},
        "6704": {"synopsis":"Calculator: converts between MPG and l/100km, the same in both directions: result = factor /\nvalue, with factor 282.4691303. Ends at loc_F727, which stores the result in Float1 and sets\nFc.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = factor; Float1 = value.\nExit: Float1 = result; Fc = 1."},
        "6718": {"synopsis":"Calculator: converts between degrees Fahrenheit and Celsius with the factor 1.8. Column 0\ncomputes value * 1.8 + 32 (Celsius to Fahrenheit), column 1 (value - 32) / 1.8 (Fahrenheit\nto Celsius). Ends at loc_F727, which stores the result in Float1 and sets Fc.\nEntry: A = active column; FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = factor 1.8; Float1 = value.\nExit: Float1 = result; Fc = 1."},
        "6769": {"synopsis":"Calculator, unit conversion: the Esc key. Ends the conversion without converting.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 1.\nChanges: F."},
        "6771": {"synopsis":"Calculator: replaces FReg1 with its reciprocal (OnePerFloat), unless it is zero (FpTst).\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = number.\nExit: FReg1 = 1 / number, or 0 unchanged."},
        "6778": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_F76F","comment":"\".219978442\""},
        "6783": {"comment":"return string in (HL)"},
        "6784": {"comment":"skip string"},
        "6791": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the convert window's highlight. Redraws the previously active convert\nbutton and the active one (PrintConvButton), and records the active one as the previous.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: C = active column; B = active row.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6816": {"synopsis":"Calculator: draws one button of the convert window, at column 12 * C + 1 of line B + 1, in\nsmall type: the 8-character unit name from CvtStrings_tbl (row B, column C), reversed when\nthe conversion is active (CF_B_Convert) and it is the active button. At column 10 of the\nline it then writes \"<-\" (active column 0) or \"->\" (column 1) when B is the active row, else\ntwo spaces.\nEntry: B = row (0-6); C = column (0-1); IY = calculator workspace.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "6866": {"comment":"16*B+8*C"},
        "6877": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "6882": {"comment":"active"},
        "6925": {"synopsis":"End of function PrintConvButton","comment":"!! shorten these"},
        "6933": {"comment":"!! 54 bytes to gain"},
        "7037": {"synopsis":"Calculator: table of 7 zero-terminated decimal strings, one conversion factor per convert\nrow, read by GetNumC and FP_VAL. This first one is row 0's, \".219978442\": gallons per litre.","comment":"!! change these to fp values"},
        "7048": {"synopsis":"Calculator: conversion factor of row 1 (Miles/km), \".621371192\" and a zero: miles per\nkilometre. Part of ConvNumTable.","comment":"!! 36 bytes to gain"},
        "7059": {"synopsis":"Calculator: conversion constant of row 2 (MPG/l/100km), \"282.4691303\" and a zero: l/100km =\nconstant / MPG, and the other way round (loc_F72C). Part of ConvNumTable."},
        "7071": {"synopsis":"Calculator: conversion factor of row 3 (Acres/Hectares), \"2.47104395\" and a zero: acres per\nhectare. Part of ConvNumTable."},
        "7082": {"synopsis":"Calculator: conversion factor of row 4 (lb/kg), \"2.204622345\" and a zero: pounds per\nkilogram. Part of ConvNumTable."},
        "7094": {"synopsis":"Calculator: conversion factor of row 5 (oz/g), \".03527399\" and a zero: ounces per gram. Part\nof ConvNumTable."},
        "7104": {"synopsis":"Calculator: conversion factor of row 6 (DegF/DegC), \"1.8\" and a zero: Fahrenheit degrees per\nCelsius degree; loc_F73A adds or removes the offset 32. The last of ConvNumTable."},
        "7108": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the DEL key (KeyTable). Clears a shown error (ClrError), then cancels\na pending command (ClearCommand); or removes the last character of the number being typed,\nending number entry when the buffer becomes empty; or, with no number typed, sets X (Float1)\nto zero.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7115": {"comment":"cancel command"},
        "7122": {"comment":"no number, display zero"},
        "7151": {"comment":"buffer not empty"},
        "7163": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the % key (KeyTable). Ignored while a command is pending or when no\noperator is pending (CF_B_Symbol). Takes the shown value x into FReg1 and Float1, loads the\nfirst operand y (Float2) into FReg2 and jumps through PercCmd_tbl, indexed by the pending\noperation (calc_Operation).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7193": {"synopsis":"Calculator: table of 4 words, the % handlers by pending operation: PercAdd, PercSub, PercMul\nand PercDiv (OP_ADD to OP_DIV). key_Perc jumps through it."},
        "7201": {"synopsis":"Calculator: y + x %. Computes y / (1 - x / 100), then ends at loc_F963: the result goes to\nFloat1, the operator and the constant mode are cleared and Float2 is zeroed.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = x; FReg2 (DE, DE', B) = y."},
        "7219": {"synopsis":"Calculator: y - x %. Computes 100 * (y - x) / x, the change from x to y in per cent, then\nends at loc_F963: the result goes to Float1, the operator and the constant mode are cleared\nand Float2 is zeroed.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = x; Float1 = x; FReg2 (DE, DE', B) = y."},
        "7239": {"synopsis":"Calculator: y x x %. Computes x * y / 100 into Float1 and sets CF_B_3, keeping the operator\nand Float2: a following + or - then adds it to or takes it from y at once (loc_FA07 through\nsub_FA1A); x and / clear CF_B_3.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = x; FReg2 (DE, DE', B) = y."},
        "7258": {"synopsis":"Calculator: y / x %. Computes 100 * y / x, then falls into loc_F963: the result goes to\nFloat1, the operator and the constant mode are cleared and Float2 is zeroed.\nEntry: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = x; FReg2 (DE, DE', B) = y."},
        "7285": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the P key (KeyTable). Makes the + button (row 0, column 4) the active\none and falls into key_Add.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7293": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the + key (KeyTable). C = OP_ADD and on to the operator code\n(loc_F9AB): after StoM it adds the operator to the command; after PercMul (CF_B_3) it\napplies it to the first operand at once; otherwise it finishes a pending operation\n(sub_FA1A), makes the shown value the first operand (Float2) and records the operator. The\nsame operator twice toggles the constant mode (CF_B_Constant).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7297": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the M key (KeyTable). Makes the - button (row 2, column 4) the active\none and falls into key_Sub.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7305": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the - key (KeyTable). C = OP_SUB and on to the operator code\n(loc_F9AB), as key_Add.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7309": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the T and X keys (KeyTable). Makes the x button (row 1, column 4) the\nactive one and falls into key_Mul.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7317": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the * key (KeyTable). Clears CF_B_3, then C = OP_MUL and on to the\noperator code (loc_F9AB), as key_Add.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7325": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the D and \\ keys (KeyTable). Makes the / button (row 3, column 4) the\nactive one and falls into key_Div.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7333": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the / key (KeyTable). Clears CF_B_3, then C = OP_DIV and falls into\nthe operator code (loc_F9AB), as key_Add.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7436": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the = key (KeyTable). Clears CF_B_3; ignored while a command is\npending or when no operator is pending (CF_B_Symbol); otherwise falls into sub_FA1A to\ncompute the result.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7450": {"synopsis":"Calculator: carries out the pending operation. Computes y op x, y being the first operand\n(Float2), x the shown value (the number being typed or Float1) and op the pending operation\n(calc_Operation, through OpCmd_tbl: FpAdd, FpSub, FpMul, FpDiv), and stores the result in\nFloat1. Clears CF_B_3. Unless the constant mode is on, also clears the operator\n(CF_B_Symbol) and zeroes Float2; in constant mode y and the operator stay for the next =.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: Float1 = result; FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = result, or 0 when Float2 was zeroed."},
        "7489": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_FA1A"},
        "7497": {"synopsis":"Calculator: handler of the Y key, Y<>x (KeyTable). Ignored while a command is pending. Takes\nthe shown value into Float1 and swaps Float1 and Float2 (X and Y).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace."},
        "7520": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads the shown value into FReg1: Float1, or, when a number is being typed\n(CF_B_HasNumBuf), the value of calc_NumBuffer (FP_VAL), ending the number entry. Float1\nitself is not written.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: FReg1 (HL, HL', C) = value."},
        "7543": {"synopsis":"End of function ldFH_F1NumBuf"},
        "7687": {"synopsis":"Calculator: tests whether the number being typed still has room. Measures the text in\ncalc_NumBuffer, from its start to the end pointer calc_BufferPos/calc_BufferPosH.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace; A = any (kept).\nExit: Fc = 1 when the text is shorter than 17 characters (room for one more); Fc = 0 when it\nis full; HL = end pointer of the text; DE = start of calc_NumBuffer.\nChanges: F, C, DE, HL.\nKeeps: A, B."},
        "7712": {"synopsis":"End of function NumBufferFull"},
        "7716": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active button one row up, wrapping from the top row to the bottom row\n(4). key_Left falls into it after DecCol has wrapped, so moving left past the first column\ngoes to the row above.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: calc_ActiveRow updated; Fz = 1 when it wrapped to row 4, Fz = 0 otherwise; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7732": {"synopsis":"End of function DecRow"},
        "7736": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active button one column left, wrapping from the first column to the\nlast (4). key_Up falls into it after DecRow has wrapped.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: calc_ActiveCol updated; Fz = 1 when it wrapped to column 4, Fz = 0 otherwise; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7752": {"synopsis":"End of function DecCol"},
        "7756": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active button one row down, wrapping from the bottom row (4) to the\ntop. key_Right falls into it after IncCol has wrapped.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: calc_ActiveRow updated; Fc = 1 when it moved down, Fc = 0 when it wrapped to row 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7772": {"synopsis":"End of function IncRow"},
        "7776": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the active button one column right, wrapping from the last column (4) to\nthe first. key_Down falls into it after IncRow has wrapped.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: calc_ActiveCol updated; Fc = 1 when it moved right, Fc = 0 when it wrapped to column\n0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "7792": {"synopsis":"End of function IncCol"},
        "7799": {"synopsis":"Calculator: leaves the popdown with OS_Bye (A = 0). key_Esc falls into it when no command is\npending; ReadKey and ErrorHandler jump here on RC_Quit. A loop on itself follows the call.\nOZ source name: Exit.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return."},
        "7804": {"synopsis":"Calculator: points IX at memory A, one of the ten 5-byte floating-point memories in the\nMemories array.\nEntry: A = memory number (0-9).\nExit: IX = Memories + 5 * A; A = 5 * A.\nChanges: AF, IX.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "7813": {"comment":"5*E"},
        "7820": {"synopsis":"Calculator: jumps to entry C of a table of handler addresses. The caller executes EXX, loads\nC (and IX) in the other register set and calls this; the routine switches back with EXX, so\nthe handler starts with the caller's original registers, except that IX takes the value of\nDE. The handler returns to the instruction after the call.\nEntry: IX = table of words; C = index (in the set active at the call); DE (other set) =\nvalue for IX.\nExit: at the handler, with IX = DE; return address of the caller on the stack.\nChanges: BC and IX of the set active at the call; IX."},
        "7840": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints the command line at column 2, row 2: the names of the commands queued in\ncalc_CmdBuffer (each from GetCmdNameA, followed by a space) and a \"?\", in tiny type, when\ncommand mode is on. Then pads with spaces over what the previous line left and records the\nnew length in calc_StatusLineLen.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: calc_StatusLineLen = length of the line printed.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "7880": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "7894": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "7913": {"synopsis":"Calculator: finds the name of a command in the list at aStom by skipping A zero-terminated\nnames.\nEntry: A = command number (0 = StoM, 1 = RclM, 2 = Fix, 3 = Unit, 4-7 = + - * /).\nExit: DE = the command's name.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "7915": {"comment":"\"StoM\""},
        "7922": {"comment":"skip string"},
        "7931": {"synopsis":"Calculator: table of 3 words, the handlers of the commands that wait for a digit: DoStoM,\nRclM and Fix, in the order CC_STOM, CC_RCLM, CC_FIX (index = command - 1). key_Num jumps\nthrough it with IndirectJump when a digit completes a command."},
        "7937": {"synopsis":"Calculator: the command names, each zero-terminated: StoM, RclM, Fix, Unit, +, -, *, /.\nGetCmdNameA finds one by number; sub_FBA0 prints those of the pending command."},
        "7964": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints the status row. At column 8, row 1, shows right-justified in 17 columns\nthe text \"Error\" when the error flag is set, otherwise the number being typed\n(calc_NumBuffer) or, when there is none, Float1 formatted by sub_FEBC. At column 28 it then\nprints the symbol of the pending operation from Symbol_tbl (or a space), a space, and a tiny\n\"K\" when the constant flag is set (otherwise a space).\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the FPP registers when Float1 is formatted."},
        "8018": {"comment":"strlen"},
        "8030": {"comment":"pad left"},
        "8057": {"comment":"\"+-x/\""},
        "8067": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "8088": {"synopsis":"Calculator: four characters \"+-x/\", the symbol of each operation (calc_Operation: OP_ADD,\nOP_SUB, OP_MUL, OP_DIV), printed by PrintStatusRow."},
        "8092": {"synopsis":"Calculator: the text \"Error\",0, copied (6 bytes) into calc_StrBuffer by PrintStatusRow when\nthe error flag is set."},
        "8098": {"synopsis":"Calculator: draws the calculator window's frame: the centred tiny title \"CALCULATOR\" on a\nreverse, underlined bar 33 characters wide, then a vertical bar (PrntVBar) at columns 6 and\n26 of row 1, either side of the number display.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "8164": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints the screen-driver sequence 1,$7C, the vertical bar between buttons and\naround the display.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8170": {"synopsis":"Calculator: redraws the previously active button as a plain button and the active one\nhighlighted (PrintCalcButton), then records the active column and row as the previous ones.\nEntry: IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: C = calc_ActiveCol; B = calc_ActiveRow; calc_PrevActCol/calc_PrecActRow set to them.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "8195": {"synopsis":"Calculator: draws one keypad button at column 6 * C + 2, row B + 3: its five characters from\nButtonTxt_tbl (entry 5 * B + C), in tiny type except in the last column, in reverse when it\nis the active button (not while the Convert window is active), underlined except on the\nbottom row, followed by a vertical bar except in the last column.\nEntry: C = column (0-4); B = row (0-4); IY = calculator workspace.\nChanges: AF, HL.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "8198": {"comment":"B+3"},
        "8204": {"comment":"6*C+2"},
        "8212": {"comment":"last column"},
        "8239": {"comment":"active?"},
        "8242": {"comment":"last row?"},
        "8250": {"comment":"5*B"},
        "8252": {"comment":"5*B+C"},
        "8256": {"comment":"25*B+5*C"},
        "8267": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "8273": {"comment":"active"},
        "8279": {"comment":"not last row"},
        "8286": {"comment":"not last col"},
        "8290": {"comment":"not last col"},
        "8301": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints the sequence 1,\"2+U\", which sets underline on.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8309": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints the sequence 1,\"U\", which toggles underline.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8315": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints the sequence 1,\"T\", which toggles tiny type.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8321": {"synopsis":"Calculator: the texts of the 25 keypad buttons, five characters each, row by row: \"Clear\", \"\nDEL \", \"StoM \", \"RclM \", \" + \"; 7, 8, 9, Unit, x; 4, 5, 6, Y<>x, -; 1, 2, 3, sIgn, /; 0, .,\n%, Fix, =. PrintCalcButton prints entry 5 * row + column.","comment":"!! shorten"},
        "8346": {"comment":"!! 41 bytes from trailing spaces"},
        "8446": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads Float1 into FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL', HL, C = Float1; A = its exponent.\nChanges: A, C, HL, HL'."},
        "8459": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads Float1 into FPP register 2 (DE' low word, DE high word, B exponent).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE', DE, B = Float1; A = its exponent.\nChanges: A, B, DE, DE'."},
        "8474": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads Float2 into FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent).\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL', HL, C = Float2; A = its exponent.\nChanges: A, C, HL, HL'."},
        "8487": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads Float2 into FPP register 2 (DE' low word, DE high word, B exponent).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE', DE, B = Float2; A = its exponent.\nChanges: A, B, DE, DE'."},
        "8502": {"synopsis":"Calculator: stores FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent) in Float1.\nEntry: HL', HL, C = number.\nExit: Float1 = the number; A = C.\nChanges: A."},
        "8515": {"synopsis":"Calculator: stores FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent) in Float2.\nEntry: HL', HL, C = number.\nExit: Float2 = the number; A = C.\nChanges: A."},
        "8543": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads the 5-byte number at IX (a memory, from GetMemPtrA) into FPP register 1\n(HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent).\nEntry: IX = number.\nExit: HL', HL, C = number.\nChanges: C, HL, HL'."},
        "8561": {"synopsis":"Calculator: stores FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent) in the 5 bytes at\nIX (a memory, from GetMemPtrA).\nEntry: IX = destination; HL', HL, C = number.\nExit: (IX) to (IX+4) = the number.\nChanges: none."},
        "8579": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads the 5-byte number at IX (a memory, from GetMemPtrA) into FPP register 2\n(DE' low word, DE high word, B exponent).\nEntry: IX = number.\nExit: DE', DE, B = number.\nChanges: B, DE, DE'."},
        "8597": {"synopsis":"Calculator: sets FPP register 1 to zero with FP_ZER.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL', HL, C = 0."},
        "8600": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads the integer 32 into FPP register 2 (exponent byte B = 0 marks an integer),\nfor the Celsius and Fahrenheit conversion (loc_F73A).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE' = 32; DE = 0; B = 0.\nChanges: B, DE, DE'."},
        "8601": {"comment":"!! jr below"},
        "8611": {"synopsis":"Calculator: loads the integer 100 into FPP register 2 (exponent byte B = 0 marks an\ninteger), for the percentage operations (PercAdd to PercDiv).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE' = 100; DE = 0; B = 0.\nChanges: B, DE, DE'."},
        "8622": {"synopsis":"Calculator: converts the text at HL to a number with FP_VAL.\nEntry: HL = text.\nExit: HL', HL, C = the number.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP."},
        "8625": {"synopsis":"Calculator: formats FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent) as text into\ncalc_StrBuffer with FP_STR (entry FpStr). The format goes in D' and E': D' = 2, E' = 2 when\nno Fix is set (varFix = 0); after Fix n, E' = n, and D' = 0 when n is 9.\nEntry: HL', HL, C = number; IY = calculator workspace.\nExit: the text in calc_StrBuffer.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP."},
        "8657": {"synopsis":"Calculator: exchanges FPP register 1 (HL' HL C) and FPP register 2 (DE' DE B).\nEntry: HL', HL, C and DE', DE, B = the two numbers.\nExit: the two numbers swapped; A = the old B.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL, DE', HL'."},
        "8665": {"synopsis":"Calculator: tests FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent) with FP_TST.\nEntry: HL', HL, C = number.\nExit: Fz = 1 when it is zero; Fc = 1 when it is negative (A = $80 when it is not zero).\nChanges: AF."},
        "8669": {"synopsis":"Calculator: sets FPP register 1 to one with FP_ONE.\nEntry: none.\nExit: HL', HL, C = 1."},
        "8672": {"synopsis":"Calculator: adds the FPP registers with FP_ADD: register 1 = register 1 + register 2.\nEntry: HL', HL, C and DE', DE, B = the operands.\nExit: HL', HL, C = the sum.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP."},
        "8675": {"synopsis":"Calculator: negates FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent): swaps it into\nregister 2, sets register 1 to zero and falls into FpSub, which gives 0 - number.\nEntry: HL', HL, C = number.\nExit: HL', HL, C = minus the number.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP."},
        "8681": {"comment":"!! jr would be smaller"},
        "8684": {"synopsis":"Calculator: subtracts with FP_SUB after exchanging the registers, so register 1 = register 2\n- register 1 (the earlier operand or the memory minus the new value).\nEntry: HL', HL, C = subtrahend; DE', DE, B = minuend.\nExit: HL', HL, C = the difference.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP."},
        "8690": {"synopsis":"Calculator: multiplies the FPP registers with FP_MUL: register 1 = register 1 * register 2.\nEntry: HL', HL, C and DE', DE, B = the operands.\nExit: HL', HL, C = the product.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP."},
        "8693": {"synopsis":"Calculator: replaces FPP register 1 (HL' low word, HL high word, C exponent) by its\nreciprocal: puts the number in register 2 and 1 in register 1, and falls into FpDiv, which\ngives 1 / number.\nEntry: HL', HL, C = number.\nExit: HL', HL, C = 1 / number.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP (RC_Dvz for zero)."},
        "8702": {"synopsis":"Calculator: divides with FP_DIV after exchanging the registers, so register 1 = register 2 /\nregister 1.\nEntry: HL', HL, C = divisor; DE', DE, B = dividend.\nExit: HL', HL, C = the quotient.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from the FPP."},
        "8708": {"synopsis":"Calculator: moves the cursor to column A, row B of the current window by printing\n1,\"3@\",A+$20,B+$20.\nEntry: A = column; B = row.\nExit: A = column + $20.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "8734": {"synopsis":"Calculator: purges the keyboard buffer (OS_Pur) and waits for a key with OS_In. An extended\nkey (0 followed by a code) returns the second code. RC_Quit leaves through Exit_calc; Escape\nis acknowledged (OS_Esc, SC_ACK) and returned as $1B; any other error is ignored and the\nread repeats.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = key, Fc = 0; or A = $1B, Fc = 1 after Escape.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8742": {"comment":"return normal char"},
        "8745": {"comment":"return expanded char"},
        "8755": {"comment":"!! move this after OS_Esc"},
        "8758": {"comment":"!! this can be removed if above is done"},
        "8760": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "8765": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: ErrorHandler."},
        "8785": {"synopsis":"Calculator: converts a letter to upper case; other characters pass unchanged.\nOZ source name: ToUpper.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: A = the character, upper case when it is a letter; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8792": {"synopsis":"Calculator: tests whether A is a decimal digit.\nOZ source name: IsNum.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: Fc = 1 when A is \"0\" to \"9\".\nChanges: F."},
        "8799": {"synopsis":"!! unused"},
        "8803": {"synopsis":"Calculator: tests whether A is a letter. The unused IsAlphaNum, before it, falls into it.\nOZ source name: IsAlpha.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: Fc = 1 when A is \"A\" to \"Z\" or \"a\" to \"z\".\nChanges: F."},
        "8817": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints character 12, which clears the current window.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8821": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints character 7 (the bell).\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = 7; Fc = 1.\nChanges: F."},
        "8827": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints the sequence 1,\"R\", which toggles reverse video.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: none (AF is kept)."},
        "8854": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "8857": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints A spaces with the repeat sequence 1,\"3N\",A+$20,\" \" (the space is\nPrntSpace's, which it falls into). Prints nothing when A is 0.\nEntry: A = count.\nExit: A = \" \" (A = 0 when nothing was printed).\nChanges: AF."},
        "8871": {"synopsis":"Calculator: prints one space.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = \" \".\nChanges: AF."},
        "9216": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: the popdown's entry point (IXP_ENT): jumps to app_main. The SCF and RET after\nthe jump are not reached from it.\nEntry: IX = information block from the Index."},
        "9221": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: starts the popdown and runs its command loop. Never returns.\n1. Checks that the Index gave it 5 pages of contiguous RAM ((IX+2) = $20 + IXP_BAD), else\nleaves with OS_Bye (A = 7). Checks the OZ version (OS_Nq, NQ_Voz), else leaves with OS_Bye\n(A = 0).\n2. Sets IY = WorkSpace, enables Escape detection and installs ErrHandler (OS_Erh), then\ndraws the window (InitWd).\n3. Loads the XY-modem settings, acknowledges Escape and asks for X, Y, B, E, R or S, reading\none character with GN_Sip (MayQuit, MayExit and Backspace_C handle its errors).\n4. Finds the character in CmdChars_tbl and calls the matching CmdFuncs_tbl entry; a bad one\nprints \"Bad response\". A command returning Fc = 1 redraws the window; then the loop repeats.\nEntry: IX = information block from the Index.\nExit: does not return (OS_Bye).","comment":"IX points at information block"},
        "9224": {"comment":"get end page+1 of contiguous RAM"},
        "9226": {"comment":"end page OK, RAM allocated..."},
        "9228": {"comment":"No Room for Imp/Export, return to Index"},
        "9230": {"comment":"Imp/Export suicide..."},
        "9232": {"comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "9237": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "9241": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: not_compatible."},
        "9242": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "9244": {"comment":"IY points at base of WorkSpace area"},
        "9261": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: Main.","comment":"load XY-modem configuration (if available)"},
        "9377": {"comment":"Key"},
        "9380": {"comment":"Number of Command entries"},
        "9394": {"comment":"C = C*2 and B=0"},
        "9400": {"comment":"DE=func"},
        "9403": {"comment":"HL=entry of command"},
        "9407": {"comment":"for the ret"},
        "9409": {"comment":"ret here"},
        "9418": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: table of 6 words, the command handlers in the reverse order of CmdChars_tbl:\nCmd_Xmodem, Cmd_Ymodem, Cmd_BatchRcv, Cmd_EndBatch, Cmd_Receive, cmd_Send. app_main indexes\nit with the count CPIR leaves in BC."},
        "9430": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: the six command keys \"SREBYX\" (Send, Receive, End batch, Batch receive, Ymodem,\nXmodem), searched with CPIR by app_main."},
        "9436": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: X command: clears the ymodem bit of state_prg and jumps to xymodem_init for an\nXMODEM transfer.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace."},
        "9443": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: Y command: sets the ymodem bit of state_prg and jumps to xymodem_init for a\nYMODEM transfer.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace."},
        "9450": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: after a failed GN_Sip, leaves the popdown (Exit_impexp) when the error is\nRC_Esc.\nEntry: A = error code.\nExit: Fc = 1 (any other error).\nChanges: F."},
        "9456": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: after a failed GN_Sip, falls into Exit_impexp when the error is RC_Quit.\nEntry: A = error code.\nExit: Fc = 1, Fz = 0 (any other error).\nChanges: F."},
        "9460": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: leaves the popdown with OS_Bye (A = 0), repeating the call if it returns.\nMayQuit falls into it; MayExit and ErrHandler jump to it.\nOZ source name: Exit.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return."},
        "9465": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: the error handler installed with OS_Erh. Returns at once for a fatal error (Fz =\n1); leaves the popdown (Exit_impexp) on RC_Quit; returns any other error to the failing call\nwith Fz = 1, Fc = 0.\nEntry: A = error code; Fz = 1 when the error is fatal.\nChanges: F."},
        "9477": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: B command, batch receive: receives files with Receive one after another,\nstarting a new line after each that ends with end of file, until a transfer ends any other\nway (end of batch, an error or Escape). Its opening CALL C, PrntError does nothing from the\ndispatcher, which enters with Fc = 0.\nEntry: Fc = 0; IY = WorkSpace.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = status code of the last transfer."},
        "9492": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: E command, end batch: sends ESC \"Z\" through the serial port (MaySendB_EscA) and\nprints the error when that fails (Escape or a serial port error).\nEntry: Fc = 0; IY = WorkSpace.\nExit: Fc = 0."},
        "9494": {"comment":"batch end"},
        "9515": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: S command, send: asks for a file name and sends the file, or every file a\nwildcard matches, through the serial port.\n1. Asks for the name (AskFilename), again while it is empty, and expands it (GN_Fex). A\nwildcard opens a handle (GN_Opw); each file match (GN_Wfn) is printed and sent.\n2. Opens the file (GN_Opf), sends ESC \"N\", the name and ESC \"F\", then the file block by\nblock (loadbuffer, sendbuffer) and ESC \"E\". Bytes outside the printable characters, CR, LF\nand TAB go as ESC \"B\" and two hex digits (SendChar).\n3. Closes the file and takes the next wildcard match; when there is none it reports \"All\nsent\". SndRcv_End closes the handles and prints any error.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace.\nExit: Fc = 1 when the name could not be read (an error other than Escape), which makes\napp_main redraw the window; otherwise Fc = 0."},
        "9557": {"comment":"open wildcard handler"},
        "9575": {"comment":"get next filename match from wc.handler"},
        "9578": {"comment":"no more files?"},
        "9582": {"comment":"not file? skip"},
        "9591": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "9610": {"comment":"open file/stream (or device)"},
        "9619": {"comment":"line number = 1"},
        "9622": {"comment":"name start"},
        "9649": {"comment":"name end, data start"},
        "9656": {"comment":"load new block into buffer..."},
        "9659": {"comment":"eof reached..."},
        "9665": {"comment":"start of buffer"},
        "9675": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export: sends BC bytes from the buffer at HL through the serial port with SendChar,\nprinting the line number in DE at every CR or LF (PrntLineNum). On a failure it ends the\ntransfer with SndRcv_End (closing the file and printing the error).\nEntry: HL = buffer; BC = byte count (not 0); DE = line number.\nExit: Fc = 0; HL = past the buffer; BC = 0; DE = next line number.\nError: Fc = 1, after SndRcv_End.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"get byte from file (buffer)"},
        "9700": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_transfer_file.","comment":"eof"},
        "9728": {"synopsis":"Sends the byte in A over the serial port in Imp/Export's encoding: a printable character\n($20-$7E), CR, TAB or LF goes out as it is (MaySendB); any other byte goes out as ESC 'B'\nfollowed by its two hex digits, upper case (ItoH, sent by calling itself).\nEntry: A = byte to send.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = ERR_Esc (5) if Escape is pending, ERR_System (0) if OS_Si fails.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "9753": {"comment":"binary"},
        "9786": {"synopsis":"Converts the value 0-15 in A to its ASCII hex digit, '0'-'9' or 'A'-'F'.\nEntry: A = value, 0 to 15.\nExit: A = hex digit.\nChanges: AF."},
        "9794": {"synopsis":"The R)eceive command: asks for a local file name with AskFname_impexp and returns if that\nfails or is escaped; otherwise falls into Receive (an empty name means the remote name is\nused).\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace.\nExit: as Receive."},
        "9804": {"synopsis":"Receives one file in Imp/Export's own protocol over the serial port and ends through\nSndRcv_End. The sender's stream is plain text with escape sequences: ESC 'N' name ESC 'F'\ngives the remote name, ESC 'B' hh a binary byte, ESC 'E' the end of the file and ESC 'Z' the\nend of the batch.\n1. Clears FileHandle, WildHandle and RemoteName; tests Escape before every byte (RcvB).\n2. An ESC goes to RcvFilename: a name sets RemoteName, a hex byte is stored as data, end of\nfile or batch leaves the loop.\n3. Data before any name (local or remote) is ignored. The first data byte creates the file\nwith GN_Opf (OP_Out) under the local name if one was given, else the remote one (GetName),\nand prints \"Using supplied name:\" or \"Using remote name:\" with the name.\n4. Each byte shows the line number on CR/LF (PrntLineNum) and is written through the buffer\n(byte2file); at end of file or batch the buffer is flushed (flushbuffer).\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace; LocalName = local file name or empty.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = MSG_Eof (4) after a file, MSG_Eob (3) at the end of a batch, or the error\nnumber that SndRcv_End has printed (ERR_Esc, ERR_Data, 0 for an OZ error).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "9862": {"comment":"HL points to filename (local or remote)"},
        "9880": {"comment":"file created, based on remote filename"},
        "9884": {"comment":"HL points to filename (local or remote)"},
        "9937": {"comment":"display filename in IMp/Export window"},
        "9943": {"comment":"Line number = 1"},
        "9946": {"comment":"prepare buffer for reception"},
        "9953": {"comment":"write received byte to file (buffer)"},
        "9961": {"comment":"abort file reception and display OZ error."},
        "9972": {"comment":"EOF or EOB occurred, ensure to flush buffer to file before closing."},
        "9975": {"comment":"signal system error message display"},
        "9977": {"comment":"restore original status code for SndRcv_End..."},
        "9978": {"comment":"signal error condition for correct message display"},
        "9979": {"synopsis":"Ends a send or a receive: closes the file (CloseFile), prints the message for A when Fc = 1\n(PrntError), and closes the wildcard handler in WildHandle with GN_Wcl if there is one. If\nthe close fails and no error was pending, the OZ error is printed instead (A = 0).\nEntry: A = message number (ERR_xxx or MSG_xxx; 0 = the last OZ error); Fc = 1 to print it.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = message number; Fz = 1 if it is 0.\nChanges: AF, HL, IX; BC and DE when a message is printed."},
        "10015": {"synopsis":"Returns the name to create a received file under: LocalName if the user gave one, else\nRemoteName.\nExit: HL = LocalName, Fz = 0; or HL = RemoteName, Fz = 1 if LocalName is empty.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "10021": {"comment":"!! ld l,<RemoteName"},
        "10025": {"synopsis":"Handles an escape sequence of Receive, after its ESC: reads the command letter (upper cased)\nand acts on it. 'N' reads the remote name (at most 50 characters, up to the next ESC) into\nRemoteName, null-terminated, and expects 'F' after it; 'F' ends a name; 'B' reads two hex\ndigits (GetHexB); 'E' and 'Z' end the file and the batch.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace.\nExit: Fc = 0. After a name or 'F': F = P/V only (Fpe, ignore). After 'B': A = byte, F = 0\n(Fpo, store A).\nError: Fc = 1, A = MSG_Eof (4) on 'E', MSG_Eob (3) on 'Z', ERR_Data (2) on a bad letter, a\nbad hex digit or a name that is too long, ERR_System (0) if a byte does not arrive.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "10034": {"comment":"name end? return"},
        "10038": {"comment":"file end?"},
        "10042": {"comment":"batch end?"},
        "10069": {"comment":"name too long"},
        "10080": {"comment":"name end"},
        "10086": {"comment":"V flag?"},
        "10112": {"comment":"C=A<<4"},
        "10129": {"comment":"clear flags"},
        "10134": {"synopsis":"Fc=0, A=hex digit\nFc=1 if bad char"},
        "10150": {"synopsis":"Closes the file in FileHandle with GN_Cl if one is open, and clears FileHandle.\nEntry: FileHandle = file handle or 0.\nExit: A = 0; Fc = 0 (Fz = 1 if no file was open).\nError: Fc = 1 if GN_Cl fails (A = 0, so PrntError shows the OZ error).\nChanges: AF; HL and IX when a file was open."},
        "10161": {"comment":"close file/stream"},
        "10172": {"synopsis":"Display line number in DE, if byte (to be sent, or has been received)\nis a CR or a LF.\n\nDE increased if displayed (for next time)"},
        "10184": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "10190": {"comment":"IX=outhandle"},
        "10192": {"comment":"BC=DE"},
        "10194": {"comment":"convert BC"},
        "10197": {"comment":"no formatting"},
        "10198": {"comment":"DE=0, write to IX"},
        "10209": {"synopsis":"Gets a byte from the serial port with OS_Si (SI_Gbt), timeout BC = 60000 (the source says 60\ns), and clears its bit 7: data is 7-bit, binary bytes come as ESC 'B' hh.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = byte, $00-$7F.\nError: Fc = 1, A = ERR_System (0).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "10211": {"comment":"60s timeout"},
        "10216": {"comment":"get a byte from serial port"},
        "10225": {"comment":"only allow 7bit Ascii reception"},
        "10227": {"comment":"(8bit binary data is received through ESC B xx)"},
        "10230": {"synopsis":"Sends ESC (27) and then the byte in A over the serial port, each through MaySendB.\nEntry: A = byte to send after ESC.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = ERR_Esc (5) if Escape is pending, ERR_System (0) if OS_Si fails.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "10239": {"synopsis":"Sends the byte in A over the serial port with OS_Si (SI_Pbt, timeout BC = 60000) unless\nEscape is pending (TestEsc).\nEntry: A = byte to send.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = ERR_Esc (5) if Escape is pending, ERR_System (0) if OS_Si fails.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "10246": {"comment":"60s timeout"},
        "10251": {"comment":"send a byte to serial port"},
        "10262": {"synopsis":"Tests for a pending Escape condition with OS_Esc (SC_BIT).\nExit: Fc = 1 if Escape is pending, else Fc = 0.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A."},
        "10265": {"comment":"Examine special condition"},
        "10267": {"comment":"!! ex (sp),hl; ld a,h; pop hl; ret"},
        "10275": {"synopsis":"Fc=1 if error, FZ=1 if ESC (ESC never returned, so checking it is unnecessary)\nOZ source name: AskFilename."},
        "10290": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: afn_1."},
        "10306": {"comment":"suspended? clear line and re-read filename"},
        "10315": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: afn_2."},
        "10320": {"comment":"empty name? return"},
        "10328": {"comment":"no error? return"},
        "10340": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: afn_3.","comment":"Fc=0, Fz=0"},
        "10344": {"synopsis":"A = byte to write to file (buffer flushed automatically when full)"},
        "10346": {"comment":"entry of buffer"},
        "10349": {"comment":"put byte into buffer"},
        "10351": {"comment":"save adr of next entry into buffer"},
        "10354": {"comment":"current size of buffer"},
        "10357": {"comment":"updated with new byte"},
        "10358": {"comment":"save back new buffer length"},
        "10361": {"comment":"size of buffer"},
        "10365": {"comment":"is buffer full?"},
        "10369": {"comment":"clear carry if set (indicate no error)..."},
        "10372": {"comment":"yes, write to file, return Fc = 1 if error while writing..."},
        "10377": {"comment":"return, fetch next byte..."},
        "10378": {"synopsis":"flush current buffer contents to file, defined by (FileHandle)\nreturn Fc = 1, if memory is full in RAM device"},
        "10387": {"comment":"no file is opened.."},
        "10389": {"comment":"also called directly if eof before"},
        "10403": {"comment":"write buffer to file."},
        "10411": {"comment":"c detection in calling program"},
        "10412": {"synopsis":"load file contents into buffer, returns Fz = 1, if EOF.\n(databuflen) contains size of current buffer\n\nAF changed on return"},
        "10426": {"comment":"eof"},
        "10428": {"comment":"size of buffer"},
        "10444": {"comment":"actual length of buffer"},
        "10451": {"synopsis":"Empties the file buffer: next_pos = data_buf0 and databuflen = 0.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: none (memory only)."},
        "10466": {"synopsis":"Opens Imp/Export's window with OS_Pout: defines window 1 (SOH '7' '#', 92 columns by 8 rows\nfrom the left of the screen), then selects and clears it, turns the cursor on and sends SOH\n'S'.\nEntry: none."},
        "10489": {"synopsis":"Prints a message with a bell (PrntBell_impexp), on a new line if the cursor is not in column\n0. A = 0 prints the last OZ error (OS_Erc, GN_Esp, read with GN_Rbe); 1 to 7 print\nImp/Export's own message from ErrorTable.\nEntry: A = message number (ERR_xxx or MSG_xxx).\nExit: Fc = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL; DE for messages 1 to 7."},
        "10500": {"comment":"x<>0? crlf"},
        "10508": {"comment":"A=0? print system error"},
        "10544": {"synopsis":"Table of 7 words: the address of Imp/Export's message for each message number 1 to 7\n(Error_1 to Error_7), read by PrntError at number - 1."},
        "10558": {"synopsis":"Message 1, ERR_Response: \"Bad response\", null-terminated (ErrorTable)."},
        "10571": {"synopsis":"Message 2, ERR_Data: \"Poor data received\", null-terminated (ErrorTable)."},
        "10590": {"synopsis":"Message 3, MSG_Eob: \"End of batch\", null-terminated (ErrorTable)."},
        "10603": {"synopsis":"Message 4, MSG_Eof: \"End of file\", null-terminated (ErrorTable)."},
        "10615": {"synopsis":"Message 5, ERR_Esc: \"Escape\", null-terminated (ErrorTable)."},
        "10622": {"synopsis":"Message 6, ERR_Name: \"Bad name\", null-terminated (ErrorTable)."},
        "10631": {"synopsis":"Message 7, MSG_AllSent: \"All sent\", null-terminated (ErrorTable)."},
        "10640": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export's bell: writes BEL (7) with OS_Out.\nOZ source name: PrntBell.\nEntry: none."},
        "10645": {"synopsis":"Called after GN_Sip was left (suspended): moves the cursor back over the C characters of the\ninput line with backspaces, and returns A = 1 so that the next GN_Sip edits the text already\nin the buffer. The flags are kept.\nEntry: C = cursor position on the line (from GN_Sip).\nExit: A = 1; F unchanged.\nChanges: A, B."},
        "10663": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export's upper-case conversion: a letter in A (IsAlpha_impexp) has bit 5 cleared; any\nother character is returned as it is.\nOZ source name: ToUpper.\nEntry: A = character.\nExit: A = character, upper case if a letter.\nChanges: AF."},
        "10670": {"synopsis":"Fc=1 if alpha\nOZ source name: IsAlpha."},
        "10684": {"synopsis":"Starts the X/Y-modem part of Imp/Export (from the X)modem and Y)modem commands): installs\nerror_handler with OS_Erh and calls app_main_xymodem. When that returns, falls into kill:\ncloses the file (file_close), gives the serial port back (hw_close_com) and leaves\nImp/Export with OS_Bye. Does not return.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace; state_prg bit ymodem = protocol chosen."},
        "10735": {"synopsis":"The X/Y-modem main loop. Clears the window, takes over the UART (hw_open_com), and if the\nmailbox \"NAME\" (OS_Sr SR_RPD) holds a file name, sends that file first (send_file). Then\nshows the menu (main_menu): protocol, /Checksum or /CRC, -1K, E)nd batch for Ymodem, and the\ncommands, and reads a key with OS_In: X or Y selects the protocol, C toggles CRC, K toggles\n1K blocks (each saved with save_xymodem_cfg); E sends the end of a batch (send_end_batch); R\nreceives (Ymodem: receive_ymodem; Xmodem: asks a name with get_filename, then receive_file);\nS asks a name, expands it (GN_Fex) and sends every file that matches it (GN_Opw, GN_Wfn,\nsend_file) until one is escaped. Timer interrupts are off while receiving (di_tick) and back\non at the menu (ei_tick). ESC is ignored; B does nothing.\nOZ source name: app_main.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace.\nExit: returns to xymodem_init on Shift+Enter (key code 209)."},
        "10737": {"comment":"clear window for XY-Modem"},
        "10746": {"comment":"Address of input buffer"},
        "10752": {"comment":"Read mailbox"},
        "10762": {"comment":"991216"},
        "10806": {"comment":"new line  991216"},
        "10809": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: no_new_line_first_time."},
        "10863": {"comment":"address of menu string"},
        "10866": {"comment":"write string"},
        "10869": {"comment":"read character from standard input"},
        "10873": {"synopsis":"JR NC,read_ok\nCP rc_esc\nRET Z\nJR read_char"},
        "10875": {"comment":"991217"},
        "10877": {"comment":"Shift + Enter  991217"},
        "10954": {"synopsis":".toggle_g\nCP 'G'\nJR NZ,batch\nLD A,(state+state_prg)\nXOR 2^g\nLD (state+state_prg),A\ncall save_xymodem_cfg\nJP main_menu"},
        "10958": {"synopsis":"JR receive_ymodem"},
        "11030": {"comment":"Local buffer, length 51"},
        "11033": {"comment":"Source"},
        "11037": {"comment":"Destination"},
        "11038": {"comment":"expand a filename"},
        "11046": {"comment":"address of wildcard string"},
        "11056": {"comment":"address of explicit file name buffer"},
        "11076": {"comment":"991217"},
        "11093": {"synopsis":"Asks for a file name: prints \"Filename? \" on a new line and reads up to 51 characters into\nfname_buf with GN_Sip, then checks it with GN_Prs. A suspended input is read again keeping\nits text; any other input error or an invalid name asks again.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace.\nExit: Fc = 0; fname_buf = file name; DE = fname_buf.\nError: Fc = 1 if the input ended with ESC (after a new line).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"address of input buffer"},
        "11096": {"comment":"input mode 0"},
        "11097": {"synopsis":"LD C,A                  ;cursor position","comment":"address of filename prompt string"},
        "11100": {"comment":"write string"},
        "11103": {"comment":"length of input buffer"},
        "11105": {"comment":"system input line routine"},
        "11122": {"comment":"new line"},
        "11131": {"comment":"parse filename"},
        "11137": {"synopsis":"Resets the expected file size before a receive, for a sender that gives none: filesize =\n$FFFFFFFF, blocks = $7FFF, bytes = 0, and clears date_rx in state_rx.\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace.\nChanges: DE."},
        "11167": {"synopsis":"Receives a batch of files with Ymodem; its second half, from receive_file, also receives one\nXmodem file.\n1. Takes CRC or checksum mode from state_prg into state_rx, expects block 0 and sends NAK or\n'C' (CRC) to start (send_NAKs). Each wait has at most 10 tries (update_retries), with the\ninput purged before every NAK.\n2. A block is SOH (128 bytes) or STX (1024 bytes), the block number and its complement, the\ndata and a checksum or a CRC-16 (update_crc). A bad block is answered with NAK; a repeat of\nthe previous block too; any other number ends with Out of sync. CAN CAN cancels; EOT ends\nthe file.\n3. Block 0 is the Ymodem header: an empty name ends the batch. Else the name, the size\n(FP_VAL) and the octal modification time (seconds since 1970) are read, the time is turned\ninto a Z88 date and time with the FPP, and the file is opened (open_file) from block 1.\n4. Data blocks are written with OS_Mv, the last one cut to the file size, then ACKed with a\nspinner character.\n5. At EOT the file is closed; Xmodem returns, Ymodem sets the file's update date and time\n(OS_Dor) if the header had one, and goes back for the next file. An error sends CANs\n(cancel), prints its message and closes the file (quit_to_main).\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace; state_prg = protocol options.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX and the alternate registers."},
        "11183": {"comment":"block 0"},
        "11189": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: receive_ymodem_header."},
        "11194": {"comment":"No filename - End of batch     991216"},
        "11205": {"comment":"enough"},
        "11210": {"comment":"Start of file size string"},
        "11213": {"comment":"space"},
        "11215": {"comment":"Max 9,999,999"},
        "11220": {"comment":"if not found"},
        "11229": {"comment":"Returns the numeric value of a string"},
        "11240": {"comment":"Start of file date time"},
        "11262": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: next_date_time_digit."},
        "11298": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: get_file_date_time_end."},
        "11308": {"comment":"(60*60*24)/$10000"},
        "11312": {"comment":"(60*60*24)%$10000"},
        "11318": {"comment":"get days since 1970-01-01"},
