        "11817": {"comment":"get byte with timeout"},
        "11831": {"synopsis":"Drains the serial input: reads bytes with hw_rxbt (A = 1) until none arrives within the\ntimeout (or a key is pressed).\nExit: Fc = 1.\nChanges: AF, AF', BC'."},
        "11839": {"synopsis":"Cancels a transfer: purges the input (purge) and sends CAN eight times.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 if a byte cannot be sent (hw_txbt).\nChanges: AF, B, AF', BC'."},
        "11846": {"comment":"CAN"},
        "11853": {"synopsis":"Sets the retry counter: retries = 11 (10 tries, it is decremented before each).\nChanges: A."},
        "11859": {"synopsis":"Adds the byte in A to the CRC-16 in DE (the Xmodem CRC, polynomial $1021, most significant\nbit first).\nEntry: A = byte; DE = CRC so far.\nExit: DE = new CRC.\nChanges: AF, DE, AF'.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "11927": {"synopsis":"Sends the file named in fname_buf with Xmodem or Ymodem.\n1. Opens its DOR (GN_Opf, OP_DOR) to get the explicit name; anything but a RAM device\n(\":RAM\") is skipped. Because data_buf0 follows fname_buf, the Ymodem header's name is the\nexplicit name without its ':'.\n2. Adds to the header the size (DOR dt_ext, written with GN_Pdn), a space and the update\ntime (dt_upd) as 11 octal digits of seconds since 1970, worked out with the FPP; pads with\nzeros.\n3. Counts the blocks (calc_blocks_and_bytes), picks 1K blocks if chosen and opens the file\n(open_file).\n4. Ymodem sends the header as block 0 when the receiver asks with NAK, 'C' or 'G', then\nwaits for that again; Xmodem starts at block 1. NAK selects checksum, 'C' CRC, 'G' Ymodem-G\n(no ACK waited for).\n5. Each block is read with OS_Mv (the last padded with zeros), sent with SOH or STX, its\nnumber, the complement, the data and the checksum or CRC; NAK resends it, ACK goes on, CAN\nCAN cancels; a spinner shows progress (indicate).\n6. At end of file EOT is sent up to 10 times until ACKed. An error prints its message and\ncloses the file (quit_to_main).\nEntry: IY = WorkSpace; fname_buf = file name; state_prg = protocol options.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX and the alternate registers.","comment":"address of file name string"},
        "11931": {"comment":"address of explicit name buffer"},
        "11932": {"comment":"HL string is local (B = 0), size of explicit name buffer"},
