      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The System Token Table: the token base shared by the MTH of most built-in applications and\npopdowns, whose application DORs (dorappl in mth/appdors.asm) point at it. Layout: byte 0,\nthe recursive token boundary ($80); byte 1, the number of tokens ($80, so tokens $80-$FF);\nthen $81 words, each an offset from SysTokenBase: the start of tokens $80 to $FF in order\nand, last, the end of the table (end_tokens). A token's length is the next offset minus its\nown; the token texts follow the offsets, from token80 on. OS_Wrt reads it (WriteToken in\nos/token.asm): a byte $80-$FF is looked up in the active application's token base (set by\nOS_Wtb). With bit 7 of the boundary set, as here, every byte of a token goes back through\nOS_Wrt, so tokens nest; with bit 7 clear, only tokens from $80 + boundary upwards do. A $7F\nbyte in a token prints CR, LF.","comment":"recursive token boundary"},
        "1": {"comment":"number of tokens"},
        "260": {"synopsis":"System token $80: the VDU sequence SOH \"T\" (2 bytes, $01 and \"T\"), which toggles the tiny\nfont. Help texts put it on both sides of a word (\"A $80FAIL$80 message\" in mth/appmth.asm)\nto show that word in tiny characters."},
        "262": {"synopsis":"System token $81: the text \"ou\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "264": {"synopsis":"System token $82: the text \"e \" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "266": {"synopsis":"System token $83: the text \" returns \" (7 bytes). Bytes: \" \", token $8D, \"turn\", token $8E.","comment":"\" returns \" (19)"},
        "273": {"synopsis":"System token $84: the text \"t \" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "275": {"synopsis":"System token $85: the text \"in\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "277": {"synopsis":"System token $86: the text \"er\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "279": {"synopsis":"System token $87: the text \"tion\" (3 bytes). Bytes: \"ti\", token $BC.","comment":"\"tion\""},
        "282": {"synopsis":"System token $88: the text \"th\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "284": {"synopsis":"System token $89: the text \"of \" (3 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "287": {"synopsis":"System token $8A: the text \"olumn\" (5 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "292": {"synopsis":"System token $8B: the text \"le\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "294": {"synopsis":"System token $8C: the text \"ar\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "296": {"synopsis":"System token $8D: the text \"re\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "298": {"synopsis":"System token $8E: the text \"s \" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "300": {"synopsis":"System token $8F: the text \"or\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
        "302": {"synopsis":"System token $90: the text \"ig\" (2 bytes), stored as plain characters."},
