        "667": {"synopsis":"End of the system token strings: the 129th offset in SysTokenBase points here, which gives\ntoken $FF its length. No byte of its own; CopyrightMsg follows."},
        "852": {"synopsis":"Tokenised text of the Hall of Fame page: the developers of OZ, those of the Cambridge\nComputer releases up to V4.0 and those of the later versions. $7F breaks a line; a 0 ends\nit. MTH_HallOfFame prints it with MTHFullPage (system tokens forced); cursor left on the\ncopyright page reaches it."},
        "1033": {"synopsis":"MTH for Index popdown..."},
        "1050": {"synopsis":"Index's MTH commands: the command block that IndexDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH\ncode (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nCommands (15 commands, 2 of them hidden: HARD and NQ) and Info (2 entries, \"Description\" and\n\"Card insertion\", each with a help page). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one mthcmd record per\ncommand (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help page offset high\nbyte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP (1) between\ntopics; CMD_MARK."},
        "1264": {"comment":"Command topic separator"},
        "1295": {"synopsis":"Index's help pages: the main page, \"The application manager.\", tokenised text with $7F for a\nnew line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it; the help page offsets of the topics and commands\ncount from here."},
        "1309": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Info topic: empty, a single 0."},
        "1310": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Info entry \"Description\": what the popdown does: launching,\nreviving or killing suspended activities, installing or removing applications, and system\ninformation."},
        "1414": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Info entry \"Card insertion\": cards are inserted and removed only\nfrom the Index, a ROM card in use stays in, and a FAIL message needs a reset."},
        "1576": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Commands topic: empty, a single 0."},
        "1577": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Card Display command (<>CARD): the resources of the inserted\ncards, the free space of the selected RAM device and its graphic map of used and free\nmemory."},
        "1762": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Install Application command (<>INS): enter the name of a .app file\n(it can be marked in the Filer); the ap0... files must be in the same directory."},
        "1884": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Remove Application command (<>RMV): the application's suspended\nactivities must be killed first; an installation of several applications is removed by\nselecting the first one."},
        "1995": {"synopsis":"Index's help page for the Update OZ command (<>UPD): updates OZ in slot 0 or 1 from the\nupdate package files on the RAM device."},
        "2068": {"synopsis":"MTH for PipeDream application..."},
        "2114": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's MTH commands: the command block that PipeDreamDOR points to, read by the\nkernel's MTH code (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command\nkeys. Topics: Info (10 entries, each with a help page: the function groups, operators and\nwildcards), Blocks (13), Cursor (22, 2 hidden), Edit (25, 2 hidden), Files (7), Layout (17),\nOptions (1) and Print (13). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one mthcmd record per command (length,\ncommand code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help page offset high byte first when\nCMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK.\nOZ source name: PipeDreamCommands."},
        "2242": {"comment":"Command topic separator"},
        "3379": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help pages: the main page, \"PipeDream is a combined Word-processor, Spreadsheet\nand Database application.\", tokenised text with $7F for a new line, ended by 0. The DOR\npoints to it; the help page offsets of the topics and commands count from here."},
        "3428": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info topic: \"Describes functions, operators and wildcards.\"\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc0."},
        "3461": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Trig. Functions\": COS, SIN, TAN, ACS, ASN, ATN,\nRAD and DEG.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc1."},
        "3615": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Log. Functions\": LN, LOG and EXP.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc2."},
        "3692": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"List Functions\": CHOOSE, COUNT, MAX, MIN and SUM.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc3."},
        "3878": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Slot Functions\": COL, INDEX, LOOKUP and ROW.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc4."},
        "4057": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Integer & Date Functions\": ABS, DAY, MONTH, PI,\nSGN, SQR and YEAR.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc5."},
        "4195": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Conditionals\": IF(boolean,then,else) with an\nexample.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc6."},
        "4299": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Operators\": the arithmetic operators + - * / and\n^.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc7."},
        "4345": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Logical Operators\": & (AND), | (OR) and ! (NOT).\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc8."},
        "4367": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Relational Operators\": < <= <> = > and >=.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc9."},
        "4432": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's help page for the Info entry \"Wildcards\": ^? for any single character and ^# for\nany number of characters.\nOZ source name: PipeDream_help_itpc10."},
        "4460": {"synopsis":"MTH for Diary application..."},
        "4481": {"synopsis":"Diary's MTH commands: the command block that DiaryDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH\ncode (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nBlocks (10 commands), Cursor (23), Edit (14, 2 hidden) and Files (2). Layout: CMD_MARK (0);\none mthcmd record per command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name,\nhelp page offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again);\nTPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK."},
        "4934": {"synopsis":"Diary's help pages: the main page, \"A 'Page a Day' diary.\", tokenised text with $7F for a\nnew line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it; the help page offsets of the topics and commands\ncount from here. The page adds that the Calendar popdown, selected from the Diary, views\nactive days and moves between them."},
        "5026": {"synopsis":"MTH for PrinterEd application..."},
        "5036": {"synopsis":"PrinterEd's MTH commands: the command block that PrEdDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH\ncode (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nCursor (10 commands, among them Page 1/2, Page 2/2 and ISO Translations) and Files (5, among\nthem Update Driver). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one mthcmd record per command (length, command\ncode, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help page offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is\nset, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK.\nOZ source name: PrinterEdCommands."},
        "5191": {"synopsis":"PrinterEd's help pages: the main page, \"The printer driver editor.\", tokenised text with $7F\nfor a new line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it; the help page offsets of the topics and\ncommands count from here. The page adds that the default driver is Epson FX and that File\nUpdate installs the edited settings."},
        "5296": {"synopsis":"MTH for Panel popdown..."},
        "5306": {"synopsis":"Panel's MTH commands: the command block that PanelDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH\ncode (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nCursor (7 commands) and Files (3: Load, Save, New). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one mthcmd record\nper command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help page offset high\nbyte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP (1) between\ntopics; CMD_MARK."},
        "5388": {"synopsis":"Panel's help pages: the main page, \"The Panel controls system preference settings.\",\ntokenised text with $7F for a new line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it; the help page\noffsets of the topics and commands count from here."},
        "5423": {"synopsis":"MTH for Filer popdown..."},
        "5429": {"synopsis":"Filer's MTH commands: the command block that FilerDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH\ncode (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nCommands (25 commands, 1 hidden: TAB for Select Extra File). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one\nmthcmd record per command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help\npage offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP\n(1) between topics; CMD_MARK."},
        "5689": {"synopsis":"Filer's help pages: the main page, \"The File manager application.\", tokenised text with $7F\nfor a new line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it; the help page offsets of the topics and\ncommands count from here. The page adds that a file marked in the Filer, opened from an\napplication's File Load, saves typing its name."},
        "5804": {"synopsis":"MTH for Alarm popdown..."},
        "5810": {"synopsis":"Alarm's MTH commands: the command block that AlarmDOR points to, read by the kernel's MTH\ncode (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nCommands (6 commands: Set, Clear and View Alarm, Exit, Load and Save Alarms). Layout:\nCMD_MARK (0); one mthcmd record per command (length, command code, key sequence and 0,\ntokenised name, help page offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes,\nlength again); TPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK."},
        "5895": {"synopsis":"Alarm's help pages: the main page, \"Set either single or repeating alarm events ...\",\ntokenised text with $7F for a new line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it; the help page\noffsets of the topics and commands count from here. The page goes on: the alarm sounds the\nbell or executes commands that launch applications or resources."},
        "5969": {"synopsis":"MTH for Terminal popdown..."},
        "5975": {"synopsis":"Terminal's MTH commands: the command block that TerminalDOR points to, read by the kernel's\nMTH code (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nCommands (25 commands: control codes such as BS, BEL, CR, XON/XOFF and ESC, cursor keys and\nFunctions 1 to 4; 1 hidden: SHIFT DEL as Backspace). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one mthcmd record\nper command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help page offset high\nbyte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP (1) between\ntopics; CMD_MARK."},
        "6196": {"synopsis":"Terminal's help pages: the main page, \"Terminal allows Digital VT52 communication to another\ncomputer using the Serial Port.\", tokenised text with $7F for a new line, ended by 0. The\nDOR points to it; the help page offsets of the topics and commands count from here."},
        "6250": {"synopsis":"MTH for Imp/Export popdown..."},
        "6261": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export's MTH commands: the command block that ImpExpDOR points to, read by the kernel's\nMTH code (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nInfo (1 entry, \"XY-modem transfer protocol\", with a help page). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one\nmthcmd record per command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help\npage offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP\n(1) between topics; CMD_MARK."},
        "6291": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export's help pages: the main page, \"This File Transfer Program allows Files to be\nshared with other computers.\", tokenised text with $7F for a new line, ended by 0. The DOR\npoints to it; the help page offsets of the topics and commands count from here. The page\nadds that the serial port's speed and protocol are set in the Panel."},
        "6370": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export's help page for the Info topic: empty, a single 0.\nOZ source name: ImpExp_help_itpc0."},
        "6371": {"synopsis":"Imp/Export's help page for the Info entry \"XY-modem transfer protocol\": the X, Y, C and K\nkeys (Xmodem or Ymodem, checksum or CRC, 128-byte or 1K blocks) and the settings advised for\nspeed.\nOZ source name: ImpExp_help_itpc1."},
        "6538": {"synopsis":"MTH for Eazylink popdown"},
        "6544": {"synopsis":"EazyLink's MTH commands: the command block that EasyLinkDOR points to, read by the kernel's\nMTH code (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command keys. Topics:\nCommands (2 commands, codes $80 and $81: enable and disable RS232 logging). Layout: CMD_MARK\n(0); one mthcmd record per command (length, command code, key sequence and 0, tokenised\nname, help page offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is set, CMDF_* attributes, length\nagain); TPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK."},
        "6594": {"synopsis":"EazyLink's help pages: the main page, \"Fast Client/Server Remote File Management between Z88\nand desktop ...\", tokenised text with $7F for a new line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it;\nthe help page offsets of the topics and commands count from here. The page goes on:\nincluding support for PC-LINK II clients."},
        "6674": {"synopsis":"MTH for FlashStore popdown..."},
        "6682": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's MTH commands: the command block that FlashstoreDOR points to, read by the\nkernel's MTH code (GetAppCommands, os/mth0.asm) for the menus, the help and the command\nkeys. Topics: Commands (16 commands, 3 hidden: CE, ER and EF, aliases of CF, FE and FL; 11\nhave a help page). Layout: CMD_MARK (0); one mthcmd record per command (length, command\ncode, key sequence and 0, tokenised name, help page offset high byte first when CMDF_HELP is\nset, CMDF_* attributes, length again); TPC_SEP (1) between topics; CMD_MARK.\nOZ source name: FlashStoreCommands."},
        "6959": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help pages: the main page, \"Rakewell Flash Cards and Ram File manager.\",\ntokenised text with $7F for a new line, ended by 0. The DOR points to it; the help page\noffsets of the topics and commands count from here."},
        "6991": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the Commands topic: empty, a single 0."},
        "6992": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the Select Card command (<>SC): \"Select which File Card to use\nwhen you have more than one.\""},
        "7024": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the Catalogue Card Files command (<>CF): \"Lists Filenames on File\nCard Area to PipeDream File.\""},
        "7054": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the Select Ram device command (<>SV): \"Changes default Ram device\nfor this session.\""},
        "7084": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the Save Files to Card command (<>FS): \"Saves Files from Ram\ndevice to File Card Area.\""},
        "7107": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the Fetch File from Card command (<>FL): \"Fetches a File from\nFile Card Area to Ram device.\""},
        "7135": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the <>FE command (Erase File from Card): \"Marks a File in File\nCard Area as deleted.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF are tokens from\nSysTokenBase, $00 ends it. Its offset from FlashStoreHelp is in the command's mthcmd entry\nin FlashStoreCommands."},
        "7158": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the <>BF command (Backup Files from Ram): \"Saves all Files from\nRam device to File Card Area.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF are tokens from\nSysTokenBase, $00 ends it. Its offset from FlashStoreHelp is in the command's mthcmd entry\nin FlashStoreCommands."},
        "7184": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the <>RF command (Restore Files to Ram): \"Fetches all Files from\nFile Card Area to Ram device.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF are tokens from\nSysTokenBase, $00 ends it. Its offset from FlashStoreHelp is in the command's mthcmd entry\nin FlashStoreCommands."},
        "7213": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the <>FFA command (Format File Area): \"Formats and erases\ncomplete File Card Area.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF are tokens from\nSysTokenBase, $00 ends it. Its offset from FlashStoreHelp is in the command's mthcmd entry\nin FlashStoreCommands."},
        "7238": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the <>TFV command (Toggle File View): \"Changes between browsing\nonly saved Files or also Files marked as deleted.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line,\n$80-$FF are tokens from SysTokenBase, $00 ends it. Its offset from FlashStoreHelp is in the\ncommand's mthcmd entry in FlashStoreCommands."},
        "7286": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's help page for the <>FC command (Copy all Files to Card): \"Copy saved Files in\ncurrent File Card Area to another flash card in a different Slot.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a\nnew line, $80-$FF are tokens from SysTokenBase, $00 ends it. Its offset from FlashStoreHelp\nis in the command's mthcmd entry in FlashStoreCommands."},
        "7333": {"synopsis":"BBC BASIC's help pages: the main help page only, \"A BBC BASIC language. A built-in Z80\nassembler enables compilation and embedding of machine code inside your programs.\" Tokenised\ntext: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF are tokens from SysTokenBase, $00 ends it. BBC BASIC has no\nMTH topics or commands; BasicDOR's help record points here."},
        "7422": {"synopsis":"Calculator's help pages: the main help page only, \"A simple pocket calculator with some\nuseful Imperial to Metric conversion functions.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF\nare tokens from SysTokenBase, $00 ends it. Calculator has no MTH topics or commands;\nCalculatorDOR's help record points here."},
        "7483": {"synopsis":"Calendar's help pages: the main help page only, \"A monthly view calendar. To manually jump\nto a date, press the ENTER key. Use the Cursor keys together with the shift and diamond keys\nto navigate through days, months and years. A mark on a day indicates an entry is made in\nthe Diary.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF are tokens from SysTokenBase, $00\nends it. Calendar has no MTH topics or commands; CalendarDOR's help record points here."},
        "7632": {"synopsis":"Clock's help pages: the main help page only, \"Displays the current day, date and time. Set\nthe current date and time here to ensure that alarm events execute on time and applications\nuse correct data.\" Tokenised text: $7F is a new line, $80-$FF are tokens from SysTokenBase,\n$00 ends it. Clock has no MTH topics or commands; ClockDOR's help record points here."},
        "7726": {"synopsis":"Index's application DOR, the first in the ROM's chain: the front DOR at $3FC0 (romhdr.asm)\nlinks to it. Built by dorappl (def/macros.def), the layout every application DOR here\nshares:\n1. Three 3-byte pointers (offset, bank): parent, brother (the next application DOR) and son;\nonly the brother is set.\n2. Type Dm_Rom ($83) and the length of the rest.\n3. Dt_Inf ($40) record: 2 reserved bytes, key letter, continuous RAM pages, environment\nestimate, unsafe and safe stack workspace (words), entry address (word), the banks bound\ninto S0-S3 on entry, type (AT_xxx) and type 2 (AT2_xxx).\n4. Dt_Hlp ($48) record: 3-byte pointers to the MTH topics, commands, help page and token\nbase (SysTokenBase); an absent one points at the DOR's own zero parent pointer.\n5. Dt_Nam ($4E) record: the name, zero-terminated; then $FF ends the DOR. Index: key 'I',\nAT_Good|AT_Popd|AT_Ones (a popdown, one instance), entry IDX_ENT with IDX_BNK in S3; MTH\nIndexTopics, IndexCommands, IndexHelp; next DiaryDOR."},
        "7780": {"synopsis":"Diary's application DOR (\"Diary\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'D', AT_Good\n(multiple diaries allowed; was AT_Good|AT_Ones), entry DIA_ENT with DIA_BNK in S3; MTH\nDiaryTopics, DiaryCommands, DiaryHelp; next PipeDreamDOR."},
        "7834": {"synopsis":"PipeDream's application DOR (\"Pipedream\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'P', AT_Good,\nentry PDR_ENT with PDR_BNK in S2 and PDR_BNK+1 in S3 (its 32K of code); MTH PipeDreamTopics,\nPipeDreamCommands, PipeDreamHelp; next BasicDOR."},
        "7892": {"synopsis":"BBC BASIC's application DOR (\"BBC Basic\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'B',\nAT_Bad|AT_Draw, AT2_Cl (Caps Lock set on entry), entry BAS_ENT with BAS_BNK in S3; no topics\nor commands, help page BasicHelp; next CalculatorDOR."},
        "7950": {"synopsis":"Calculator's application DOR (\"Calculator\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'R',\nAT_Good|AT_Popd (a popdown), entry CCL_ENT with CCL_BNK in S3; no topics or commands, help\npage CalculatorHelp; next CalendarDOR."},
        "8009": {"synopsis":"Calendar's application DOR (\"Calendar\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'C',\nAT_Good|AT_Popd, AT2_Ie (ignore error returns), entry CAL_ENT with CAL_BNK in S3; no topics\nor commands, help page CalendarHelp; next ClockDOR."},
        "8066": {"synopsis":"Clock's application DOR (\"Clock\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'T', AT_Good|AT_Popd,\nAT2_Ie, entry CLK_ENT with CLK_BNK in S3; no topics or commands, help page ClockHelp; next\nAlarmDOR."},
        "8120": {"synopsis":"Alarm's application DOR (\"Alarm\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'A', AT_Good|AT_Popd,\nAT2_Ie, entry ALM_ENT with ALM_BNK in S3; MTH AlarmTopics, AlarmCommands, AlarmHelp; next\nFilerDOR."},
        "8174": {"synopsis":"Filer's application DOR (\"Filer\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'F',\nAT_Good|AT_Popd|AT_Film (the file manager), entry FLR_ENT with FLR_BNK in S3; MTH\nFilerTopics, FilerCommands, FilerHelp; next FlashstoreDOR."},
        "8228": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's application DOR (\"FlashStore\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'J',\nAT_Ugly|AT_Popd (killed on pre-emption), entry FST_ENT with FST_BNK in S3; MTH\nFlashStoreTopics, FlashStoreCommands, FlashStoreHelp; next PrEdDOR."},
        "8287": {"synopsis":"PrinterEd's application DOR (\"PrinterEd\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'E',\nAT_Good|AT_Ones (one instance), entry PED_ENT with PED_BNK in S3; MTH PrinterEdTopics,\nPrinterEdCommands, PrinterEdHelp; next PanelDOR."},
        "8345": {"synopsis":"Panel's application DOR (\"Panel\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'S', AT_Good|AT_Popd,\nentry PNL_ENT with PNL_BNK in S3; MTH PanelTopics, PanelCommands, PanelHelp; next\nTerminalDOR."},
        "8399": {"synopsis":"Terminal's application DOR (\"Terminal\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'V',\nAT_Good|AT_Ones|AT_Draw, AT2_Ie, entry TRM_ENT with TRM_BNK in S3; MTH TerminalTopics,\nTerminalCommands, TerminalHelp; next ImpExpDOR."},
        "8456": {"synopsis":"Imp-Export's application DOR (\"Imp-Export\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'X',\nAT_Ugly|AT_Popd, entry IXP_ENT with IXP_BNK in S3; MTH ImpExpTopics, ImpExpCommands,\nImpExpHelp; next EasyLinkDOR."},
        "8515": {"synopsis":"EazyLink's application DOR (\"EazyLink\"), laid out as IndexDOR (dorappl): key 'L',\nAT_Ugly|AT_Popd, entry EAZ_ENT with EAZ_BNK in S2 and nothing in S3; MTH EazyLinkTopics,\nEazyLinkCommands, EazyLinkHelp; the last DOR of the chain: its brother pointer is zero."},
        "8572": {"synopsis":"Panel default values\nFormat : pointer to default value, data length is next_ptr-ptr\nDefault ISO translations refers to Epson FX-80 compatible printers"},
        "8573": {"comment":"timeout"},
        "8574": {"comment":"repeat"},
        "8575": {"comment":"click"},
        "8576": {"comment":"sound"},
        "8577": {"comment":"bad process size"},
        "8578": {"comment":"country"},
        "8579": {"comment":"07-0F unused"},
        "8588": {"comment":"insert/overwrite"},
        "8589": {"comment":"date format"},
        "8590": {"comment":"pipedream map"},
        "8591": {"comment":"map size"},
        "8592": {"comment":"default dir \"\""},
        "8593": {"comment":"default dev"},
        "8594": {"comment":"tx baud rate"},
        "8595": {"comment":"rx baud rate"},
        "8596": {"comment":"xon/xoff"},
        "8597": {"comment":"parity"},
        "8598": {"comment":"1a-1f unused"},
        "8604": {"comment":"printer name"},
        "8605": {"comment":"allow linefeed"},
        "8606": {"comment":"printer on"},
        "8607": {"comment":"printer off \"\""},
        "8608": {"comment":"end of page"},
        "8609": {"comment":"HMI prefix"},
        "8610": {"comment":"HMI suffix"},
        "8611": {"comment":"HMI offset"},
        "8612": {"comment":"underline"},
        "8616": {"comment":"bold"},
        "8620": {"comment":"extended"},
        "8624": {"comment":"italics"},
        "8628": {"comment":"subscript"},
        "8632": {"comment":"superscript"},
        "8636": {"comment":"alt font"},
        "8640": {"comment":"user defined"},
        "8644": {"comment":"tr1"},
        "8646": {"comment":"tr2"},
        "8648": {"comment":"tr3"},
        "8650": {"comment":"tr4"},
        "8652": {"comment":"tr5"},
        "8654": {"comment":"tr6"},
        "8656": {"comment":"tr7"},
        "8658": {"comment":"tr8"},
        "8660": {"comment":"tr9"},
        "8662": {"comment":"here for previous pointer length"},
        "8663": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Mct (timeout in minutes): one byte, 5. PrefTbl1's entry $01 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $00 (PA_Gfi) points here too,\nwith length 0. OS_Nq's panel reasons (NqPanel, os/spnq1.asm) return it through\nGetDefPrefDest when no saved value exists."},
        "8664": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Rep (keyboard repeat rate): one byte, 6. PrefTbl1's entry $02 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8665": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Kcl (keyclick): 'N'. PrefTbl1's entry $03 holds its offset; the length\nis the next entry minus this one."},
        "8666": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Snd (sound): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $04 holds its offset; the length is\nthe next entry minus this one."},
        "8667": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Bad (default bad process size in K): one byte, 40. PrefTbl1's entry $05\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8668": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Loc (country keyboard letter): 'U', the UK keyboard (CL_UK). PrefTbl1's\nentry $06 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one.","comment":"default keyboad is UK"},
        "8669": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Iov (insert or overtype): 'I', insert. PrefTbl1's entry $10 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entries $07-$0F (unused) point here\ntoo, each with length 0."},
        "8670": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Dat (date format): 'E' (the other value is 'A'). PrefTbl1's entry $11\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8671": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Map (PipeDream map): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $12 holds its offset; the\nlength is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8672": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Msz (map size in pixels): 'P'. PrefTbl1's entry $13 holds its offset;\nthe length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8673": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Dev (default device): \":RAM.0\", 6 bytes with no terminator. PrefTbl1's\nentry $15 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $14 (PA_Dir,\nthe default directory) points here too, with length 0: an empty string."},
        "8679": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Txb (transmit baud rate): the word 9600. PrefTbl1's entry $16 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8681": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Rxb (receive baud rate): the word 9600. PrefTbl1's entry $17 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8683": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Xon (Xon/Xoff): 'N', no Xon/Xoff. PrefTbl1's entry $18 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one.","comment":"default no XON/XOFF"},
        "8684": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Par (parity): 'N', no parity. PrefTbl1's entry $19 holds its offset;\nthe length is the next entry minus this one.","comment":"default no PARITY"},
        "8685": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Ptr (printer name): \"Epson\" and a zero byte. PrefTbl1's entry $20 holds\nits offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entries $1A-$1F (unused) point here\ntoo, each with length 0."},
        "8691": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Alf (allow linefeed): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $21 holds its offset; the\nlength is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8692": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Pon (printer on sequence): 5 bytes 27,64,27,82,0: ESC @ and ESC R 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $22 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8697": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_Eop (end of page sequence): one byte, 12 (form feed). PrefTbl1's entry\n$24 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $23 (PA_Pof, the\nprinter off sequence) points here too, with length 0: no sequence."},
        "8698": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On1 (underline on): 3 bytes 27,45,1: ESC - 1. PrefTbl1's entry $28\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entries $25-$27 (PA_Mip,\nPA_Mis, PA_Mio, the HMI sequences) point here too, each with length 0."},
        "8701": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On1+1 (underline off): 3 bytes 27,45,0: ESC - 0. PrefTbl1's entry $29\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8704": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On1+2 (underline off at CR): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $2A holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8705": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On2 (bold on): 2 bytes 27,69: ESC E. PrefTbl1's entry $2C holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $2B (PA_On1+3, underline's\nspecial character) points here too, with length 0."},
        "8707": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On2+1 (bold off): 2 bytes 27,70: ESC F. PrefTbl1's entry $2D holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8709": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On2+2 (bold off at CR): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $2E holds its offset; the\nlength is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8710": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On4 (italics on): 2 bytes 27,52: ESC 4. PrefTbl1's entry $34 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entries $2F-$33 (bold's special\ncharacter and all of highlight 3, the extended sequence) point here too, each with length 0."},
        "8712": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On4+1 (italics off): 2 bytes 27,53: ESC 5. PrefTbl1's entry $35 holds\nits offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8714": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On4+2 (italics off at CR): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $36 holds its offset;\nthe length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8715": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On5 (subscript on): 3 bytes 27,83,1: ESC S 1. PrefTbl1's entry $38\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $37 (PA_On4+3) points\nhere too, with length 0."},
        "8718": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On5+1 (subscript off): 2 bytes 27,84: ESC T. PrefTbl1's entry $39 holds\nits offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8720": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On5+2 (subscript off at CR): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $3A holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8721": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On6 (superscript on): 3 bytes 27,83,0: ESC S 0. PrefTbl1's entry $3C\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $3B (PA_On5+3) points\nhere too, with length 0."},
        "8724": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On6+1 (superscript off): 2 bytes 27,84: ESC T. PrefTbl1's entry $3D\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8726": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On6+2 (superscript off at CR): 'Y'. PrefTbl1's entry $3E holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8727": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On7 (alternate font on): one byte, 15 (SI). PrefTbl1's entry $40 holds\nits offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $3F (PA_On6+3) points here\ntoo, with length 0."},
        "8728": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On7+1 (alternate font off): one byte, 18 (DC2). PrefTbl1's entry $41\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8729": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On7+2 (alternate font off at CR): 'N'. PrefTbl1's entry $42 holds its\noffset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8730": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On8 (user defined highlight on): 3 bytes 27,120,1: ESC x 1. PrefTbl1's\nentry $44 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $43\n(PA_On7+3) points here too, with length 0."},
        "8733": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On8+1 (user defined highlight off): 3 bytes 27,120,0: ESC x 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $45 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one."},
        "8736": {"synopsis":"Panel default for PA_On8+2 (user defined highlight off at CR): 'N'. PrefTbl1's entry $46\nholds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one. Entry $47 (PA_On8+3) has\nlength 0."},
        "8737": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr1, the character to translate when printing: one byte, 161 (inverted\nexclamation mark). PrefTbl1's entry $48 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus\nthis one. Defaults for an Epson FX-80 compatible printer. OS_Nq's panel reasons (NqPanel,\nos/spnq1.asm) return it through GetDefPrefDest when no saved value exists.","comment":"Â¡"},
        "8738": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr1+1, the sequence printed for character 161: 7 bytes 27,82,7,91,27,82,0,\nwhich is ESC R 7 (select international character set 7), the character 91, then ESC R 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $49 holds its offset."},
        "8745": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr2, the character to translate when printing: one byte, 163 (pound sign).\nPrefTbl1's entry $4A holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one.","comment":"Â£"},
        "8746": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr2+1, the sequence printed for character 163: 7 bytes 27,82,3,35,27,82,0,\nwhich is ESC R 3 (select international character set 3), the character 35, then ESC R 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $4B holds its offset."},
        "8753": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr3, the character to translate when printing: one byte, 167 (section sign).\nPrefTbl1's entry $4C holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one.","comment":"Â§"},
        "8754": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr3+1, the sequence printed for character 167: 7 bytes 27,82,1,93,27,82,0,\nwhich is ESC R 1 (select international character set 1), the character 93, then ESC R 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $4D holds its offset."},
        "8761": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr4, the character to translate when printing: one byte, 176 (degree sign).\nPrefTbl1's entry $4E holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one.","comment":"Â°"},
        "8762": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr4+1, the sequence printed for character 176: 7 bytes 27,82,1,91,27,82,0,\nwhich is ESC R 1 (select international character set 1), the character 91, then ESC R 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $4F holds its offset."},
        "8769": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr5, the character to translate when printing: one byte, 191 (inverted\nquestion mark). PrefTbl1's entry $50 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus\nthis one.","comment":"Â¿"},
        "8770": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr5+1, the sequence printed for character 191: 7 bytes 27,82,7,93,27,82,0,\nwhich is ESC R 7 (select international character set 7), the character 93, then ESC R 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $51 holds its offset."},
        "8777": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr6, the character to translate when printing: one byte, 196 (A with\ndiaeresis). PrefTbl1's entry $52 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this\none.","comment":"Ã"},
        "8778": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr6+1, the sequence printed for character 196: 7 bytes 27,82,2,91,27,82,0,\nwhich is ESC R 2 (select international character set 2), the character 91, then ESC R 0.\nPrefTbl1's entry $53 holds its offset."},
        "8785": {"synopsis":"Default for PA_Tr7, the character to translate when printing: one byte, 197 (A with ring).\nPrefTbl1's entry $54 holds its offset; the length is the next entry minus this one.","comment":"Ã"},
