      "lineAnnotations": {
        "5": {"synopsis":"EazyLink's entry point, reached through the JP at $8000. Checks that the Index gave it its\ncontiguous RAM (IX+2, the end page + 1, must be $20+EAZ_BAD) and that it runs on the OZ it\nwas built for (OS_Nq NQ_Voz); otherwise it leaves through OS_Bye (A = RC_ROOM or 0). Then it\nenables Escape detection, clears MenuBarPosn and UserToggles (line feed conversion and\ntranslations off), calls Appl_Main and jumps to KillPopdown.\nEntry: IX = the application's information block.\nExit: does not return (OS_Bye).","comment":"IX points at information block"},
        "8": {"comment":"get end page+1 of contiguous RAM"},
        "10": {"comment":"end page OK, RAM allocated..."},
        "12": {"comment":"No Room for EazyLink, return to Index"},
        "14": {"comment":"EazyLink suicide..."},
        "16": {"comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "21": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "26": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "28": {"comment":"Enable escape detection"},
        "33": {"comment":"Display Menu Bar at top line the first time..."},
        "36": {"comment":"Linefeed conversion OFF, Translations OFF"},
        "39": {"comment":"Call the code..."},
        "44": {"synopsis":"EazyLink's error handler, called with the code of a failed serial port or keyboard read\n(from PollInput, the keyboard scan and the byte I/O's timeout check). RC_esc is acknowledged\n(OS_Esc SC_ACK) and, like RC_quit, ends EazyLink: it falls into KillPopdown. Every other\ncode (RC_susp included) returns unchanged.\nEntry: A = error code; Fc = 1.\nExit: A and F unchanged (codes other than RC_esc and RC_quit).\nChanges: none."},
        "59": {"comment":"acknowledge ESC detection"},
        "63": {"synopsis":"Entry inside Errhandler: ends EazyLink. Closes any open transfer file (Close_file) and the\nserial port dump files (Close_serportdump_filehandles), restores the Panel's original serial\nport settings, purges the keyboard buffer, sets the Escape state (OS_Esc SC_SET) and quits\nwith OS_Bye, A = 0 (no error message), returning to the Index.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nExit: does not return.","comment":"close any opened/created file"},
        "66": {"comment":"close streams to serial port dump files (if open)"},
        "69": {"comment":"restore original Panel Settings"},
        "72": {"comment":"purge keyboard buffer"},
        "74": {"comment":"ESC pressed."},
        "78": {"comment":"no error messages on quit"},
        "79": {"comment":"perform suicide, focus to Index..."},
        "81": {"synopsis":"EazyLink's main program. Opens the log window (\"3\") and the command window (\"2\"), resets\nboth translation tables to identity and loads the translations, zeroes the I/O handles,\nswitches automatic translation and CRLF conversion off (ESC_T_cmd2, ESC_C_cmd2), saves the\nPanel's serial settings and installs EazyLink's own (Init_PanelSets), points IX at the\nworkspace ($2000) and clears its runtime flags. It writes 'Running', shows the baud rate and\nversion, draws the menu bar and loops in Fetch_synch for ever.\nEntry: none.\nExit: does not return."},
        "87": {"comment":"load translations file or install"},
        "90": {"comment":"reset all I/O handles to zero"},
        "93": {"comment":"standard IBM - Z88 translation table."},
        "96": {"comment":"No Auto translation"},
        "99": {"comment":"No CR conversion"},
        "102": {"comment":"set Transmit & Receive baud rates and store original values temporarily."},
        "105": {"comment":"point at base of workspace variable area"},
        "109": {"comment":"all runtime flags OFF"},
        "113": {"comment":"'Running'"},
        "119": {"comment":"Display EazyLink version & protocol in bottom of topic window"},
        "122": {"comment":"Display initial menubar"},
        "125": {"comment":"111112 & 555556 synch and ESC cmds"},
        "130": {"synopsis":"Display Command Window - use window \"2\""},
        "145": {"synopsis":"Text the command window shows (GN_Sop): select window \"2\", the SD_DTS character, then the\nfive menu lines in tiny type (\"2+T\" ... \"2-T\"): toggle translation mode, toggle linefeed\nmode, use ISO translations, load translations, quit EazyLink. Null-terminated."},
        "268": {"synopsis":"Display Log Window - use window \"3\""},
        "277": {"synopsis":"Draws the menu bar in the command window: selects window \"2\" without a cursor, moves to\ncolumn 0, row MenuBarPosn and applies reverse video to 26 characters ($1A).\nEntry: MenuBarPosn = row of the bar (0-4).\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "285": {"comment":"(old menu bar will be overwritten)"},
        "291": {"comment":"display menu bar at (0,Y)"},
        "295": {"comment":"get Y position of menu bar"},
        "298": {"comment":"VDU..."},
        "302": {"comment":"now display menu bar at cursor"},
        "311": {"synopsis":"VDU string 1, \"3@\", 0: the start of a cursor move; DisplMenuBar and RemoveMenuBar follow it\nwith the column and the row, each + 32."},
        "315": {"synopsis":"VDU string selecting the command window: 1, \"2H2\" (window \"2\"), 1, \"2-C\" (cursor off),\nnull-terminated. Used by DisplMenuBar and RemoveMenuBar.","comment":"activate menu window, no Cursor..."},
        "324": {"synopsis":"VDU string that draws the menu bar at the cursor: 1, \"2+R\" (reverse on), then 1, \"2A\",\n32+$1A (apply the attributes to 26 characters), null-terminated.","comment":"set reverse video"},
        "328": {"comment":"XOR 'display' menu bar (20 chars wide)"},
        "333": {"synopsis":"Removes the menu bar from the command window: selects window \"2\" without a cursor, moves to\ncolumn 0, row MenuBarPosn and applies normal video (MenuBarOff) to 26 characters.\nEntry: MenuBarPosn = row of the bar (0-4).\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "341": {"comment":"(old menu bar will be overwritten)"},
        "347": {"comment":"display menu bar at (0,Y)"},
        "351": {"comment":"get Y position of menu bar"},
        "354": {"comment":"VDU..."},
        "358": {"comment":"now display menu bar at cursor"},
        "367": {"synopsis":"VDU string that removes the menu bar at the cursor: 1, \"2-R\" (reverse off), then 1, \"2A\",\n32+$1A (apply to 26 characters), null-terminated.","comment":"set reverse video"},
        "371": {"comment":"apply 'display' menu bar (20 chars wide)"},
        "376": {"synopsis":"Waits for a byte from the serial port while it runs the menu. Each key from PollInput is\nhandled here: Cursor Down and Up move the menu bar (wrapping between rows 0 and 4), ENTER\nruns the command under the bar (through Command_lookup), and the codes\nEazyLink_CC_dbgOn/dbgOff ($80/$81) switch serial port logging on and off. When a serial byte\narrives, PollInput returns straight to Poll's caller.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nExit: A = byte received from the serial port.","comment":"Serial port data or key-press?"},
        "382": {"comment":"no shortcut cmd, ENTER ?"},
        "386": {"comment":"Cursor Down ?"},
        "390": {"comment":"Cursor Up ?"},
        "396": {"comment":"<>D, Enable Serial port logging"},
        "401": {"comment":"<>Z, Disable Serial port logging"},
        "404": {"comment":"ignore keypress, get another..."},
        "409": {"comment":"get Y position of menu bar"},
        "410": {"comment":"has m.bar already reached bottom?"},
        "415": {"comment":"update new m.bar position"},
        "419": {"comment":"display new m.bar position"},
        "431": {"comment":"get Y position of menu bar"},
        "432": {"comment":"has m.bar already reached top?"},
        "437": {"comment":"update new m.bar position"},
        "452": {"comment":"use menu bar position as index to command"},
        "453": {"comment":"then execute..."},
        "459": {"synopsis":"Polls the serial port and the keyboard. Resets PopDownTimeout to $FFFF (about ten minutes),\nthen loops: OS_Si Si_Gbt with a 1/10 second timeout; on a timeout it gives\nCheckHandshakeMode the chance to switch the handshake mode, passes the error to Errhandler\nand scans the keyboard (OS_Tin, 1 cs), whose timeouts count PopDownTimeout down to ShutDown.\nA menu key returns to Poll; a serial byte is dumped to the log file when logging is on, then\nPollInput discards its own and Poll's return addresses and jumps to Poll's caller with the\nbyte.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 0, A = key code (IN_ENT, IN_DWN, IN_UP, $80 or $81) to Poll; or A =\nserial byte, returned to Poll's caller (Fetch_synch)."},
        "462": {"comment":"reset timeout to approx 10 minutes"},
        "465": {"comment":"keyboard polled, now check for serial port in 1/10 sec..."},
        "470": {"comment":"get a byte from serial port, using OZ standard interface"},
        "472": {"comment":"probably timeout from serial port, check for handshake signal"},
        "475": {"comment":"no byte available (or ESC pressed)..."},
        "478": {"comment":"then let it be processed by main loop."},
        "480": {"comment":"scan the keyboard, if no byte from serport"},
        "485": {"comment":"when using MTH, command window gets reset, so re-display when KD is used."},
        "488": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, return Key Code in A..."},
        "495": {"comment":"dump to debugging serport input file (if enabled)"},
        "498": {"comment":"remove this RETurn address"},
        "499": {"comment":"get RETurn address to Fetch_synch"},
        "501": {"synopsis":"When there is a pause in the byte stream (a timeout occurred), check if a serial port\nhandshake change was signaled in the previous main Fetch synch loop.\nIf a change was signaled and the current serial port handshake settings are\ndifferent to the signaled handshake mode, then re-configure the serial port while\nthere is no communication activity from the client.\nOZ source name: CheckHandshakeMode."},
        "503": {"comment":"get timeout counter for handshake check"},
        "509": {"comment":"we're not allowing a handshake check until 0.5 second has passed"},
        "514": {"comment":"get current serial handshake mode"},
        "519": {"comment":"no handshake change was signaled"},
        "522": {"comment":"synch loop signaled current handshake"},
        "526": {"comment":"change from Hardware Handshake to Xon/Xoff Handshake"},
        "529": {"comment":"change from Xon/Xoff Handshake to Hardware Handshake"},
        "532": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: no_handshake_change."},
        "533": {"comment":"clear handshake signal change flag"},
        "536": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_handshake_change.","comment":"update timeout counter for next call to this routine"},
        "542": {"synopsis":"Scan keyboard, and return key codes for <ENTER>, <UP> and <DOWN> in A register.\nReturn 0, if other keys are pressed, or keyboard timeout."},
        "562": {"comment":"<>D"},
        "565": {"comment":"<>Z"},
        "578": {"comment":"return error to caller of ScanKeyboard"},
        "590": {"comment":"10 minute timeout reached, switch off"},
        "593": {"comment":"return 0, no valid key pressed"},
        "595": {"synopsis":"Switches the Z88 off (OS_Off) when the keyboard has been idle for the pop-down timeout\n(about ten minutes), then returns.\nEntry: none."},
        "599": {"synopsis":"Activate command defined by index in A","comment":"index word boundary..."},
        "603": {"comment":"base of table"},
        "606": {"comment":"point at command index"},
        "607": {"comment":"get pointer to subroutine"},
        "610": {"comment":"HL points at command subroutine"},
        "611": {"comment":"activate"},
        "612": {"synopsis":"Table of 6 words: the routine for each menu row, indexed by MenuBarPosn: toggle translation,\ntoggle line feed conversion, ISO translations, load translations, KillPopdown, and\ndisp_running. Read by ActivateCommand, which jumps to the entry.","comment":"toggle File Translation"},
        "614": {"comment":"toggle File Linefeed Conversion"},
        "616": {"comment":"Use explicitly the ISO/IBM translations"},
        "618": {"comment":"re-load \"translate.dat\" translations"},
        "620": {"comment":"Terminate EazyLink"},
        "624": {"synopsis":"Menu command: toggles bit 1 of UserToggles and switches automatic file translation on\n(ESC_T_cmd1) or off (ESC_T_cmd2) to match; then writes 'Running' (falls through to\ndisp_running).\nOZ source name: User_ToggleTranslation.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "635": {"comment":"File Translation OFF"},
        "639": {"comment":"File Translation ON"},
        "645": {"synopsis":"Menu command: toggles bit 0 of UserToggles and switches automatic CRLF conversion on\n(ESC_C_cmd1) or off (ESC_C_cmd2) to match; then writes 'Running' (jumps to disp_running).\nOZ source name: User_ToggleLineFeed.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "656": {"comment":"CR conversion OFF"},
        "660": {"comment":"CR conversion ON"},
        "666": {"synopsis":"Menu command: installs the standard ISO/IBM translation tables (Use_StdTranslations), then\nwrites 'Running' (jumps to disp_running).\nOZ source name: User_StdTranslations.","comment":"Use ISO/IBM translations..."},
        "671": {"synopsis":"Menu command: loads the translation tables again from the external \"translate.dat\" file\n(LoadTranslations), then falls into disp_running.\nOZ source name: User_LoadTranslations.","comment":"Load external \"translate.dat\" file..."},
        "674": {"synopsis":"Writes the 'Running' message (message1) to the log window through Write_message.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, HL.","comment":"'Running'"},
        "680": {"synopsis":"EazyLink's main loop, which never returns. Waits for a byte through Poll. $01 starts the\nEazyLink synch (extended_synch): when Check_synch confirms it, the handshake counter is\ncleared, the synch is acknowledged (Send_synch) and Extended_ESC_commands runs one command.\n$05 starts the PCLINK II synch (pclink_synch): after Check_synch it also signals Xon/Xoff\nhandshaking (SignalSerportMode), acknowledges, shows the flashing 'PCLINK II' text and runs\none PCLINK II command (removing the text when that fails). Other bytes, bad synchs and\nfailed acknowledgements are ignored.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nExit: does not return.","comment":"get byte from serial port (and manage menu)"},
        "683": {"comment":"extended command protocol synch?"},
        "691": {"comment":"start and body of sequense..."},
        "694": {"comment":"end of sequense..."},
        "697": {"comment":"is it really a synch?"},
        "700": {"comment":"timeout or bad synch..."},
        "703": {"comment":"reset timeout counter for handshake check"},
        "706": {"comment":"acknowledge synch to terminal"},
        "709": {"comment":"return on system error or timeout - communication stopped"},
        "711": {"comment":"synch sent - wait for command"},
        "714": {"comment":"wait for new synch & command"},
        "716": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: check_pclink_synch."},
        "718": {"comment":"ignore byte..."},
        "724": {"comment":"start and body of sequense..."},
        "727": {"comment":"end of sequense..."},
        "730": {"comment":"is it really a synch?"},
        "733": {"comment":"return on system error or timeout - communication stopped"},
        "736": {"comment":"reset timeout counter for handshake check"},
        "739": {"comment":"Pclink II protocol..."},
        "741": {"comment":"signal that Xon/Xoff handshake is needed"},
        "744": {"comment":"acknowledge - B = length of synch"},
        "747": {"comment":"return on system error or timeout - communication stopped"},
        "749": {"comment":"display a flashing 'PCLINK II' text in topic window"},
        "752": {"comment":"synch sent - wait for commands"},
        "758": {"comment":"wait for new synch & command"},
        "760": {"synopsis":"Runs one command of the EazyLink protocol after a synch: fetches the ESC command\n(FetchBytes) and looks its letter up in EscCommands, jumping to the matching routine of the\nsubroutines table, which returns to the caller. A plain byte instead of ESC <letter> is a\nprotocol error (Msg_Protocol_error); an unknown letter returns.\nOZ source name: Extended_ESC_commands.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nError: Fc = 1 when the serial port failed or timed out."},
        "763": {"comment":"serial port error or timeout - communication stopped"},
        "764": {"comment":"no ESC id (normal byte), protocol error..."},
        "767": {"comment":"Find command, and execute"},
        "769": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: PClink_ESC_commands."},
