        "2211": {"synopsis":"Command ESC \"c\" (and the menu): switches automatic CRLF conversion on. Writes 'Auto CRLF ON'\nto the log window and sets BB_LnfdConv in the runtime flags.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "2217": {"comment":"Remote activation of auto CRLF conversion"},
        "2222": {"synopsis":"Command ESC \"C\" (and the menu, and start-up): switches automatic CRLF conversion off. Writes\n'Auto CRLF OFF' to the log window and clears BB_LnfdConv in the runtime flags.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "2228": {"comment":"Remote de-activation of auto CRLF conversion"},
        "2233": {"synopsis":"Command ESC \"t\" (and the menu): switches automatic character translation on. Writes 'Auto\nTranslation ON' and sets BB_CharTrans and its copy BB_CharTransCpy.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "2239": {"comment":"Remote activation of auto translation"},
        "2248": {"synopsis":"Command ESC \"T\" (and the menu, and start-up): switches automatic character translation off.\nWrites 'Auto Translation OFF' and clears BB_CharTrans and BB_CharTransCpy.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "2254": {"comment":"Remote de-activation of auto translation"},
        "2263": {"synopsis":"Starts serial port logging (the <>D key code): creates the dump files\n(Create_serportdump_files) and writes 'Serial port logging enabled' to the log window.\nOZ source name: EnableSerportLogging.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "2281": {"synopsis":"Stops serial port logging (the <>Z key code): closes the dump files\n(Close_serportdump_filehandles) and writes 'Serial port logging disabled'.\nOZ source name: DisableSerportLogging.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, HL."},
        "2299": {"synopsis":"Closes the serial port dump files: GN_Cl on serfile_in_handle and serfile_out_handle when\nnon-zero, then zeroes both handles and clears BB_SerportLog in the runtime flags.\nOZ source name: Close_serportdump_filehandles.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, HL, IX."},
        "2308": {"comment":"serport dump IN file not open"},
        "2321": {"comment":"serport dump OUT file not open"},
        "2329": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_Close_serportdump_filehandles."},
        "2341": {"comment":"indicate disabled serial port logging"},
        "2347": {"synopsis":"Creates the serial port dump files: closes open ones first, then creates \"/rs232rcv.log\" and\n\"/rs232snd.log\" in the default RAM device (CreateFilename), moves their handles from\nfile_handle to serfile_in_handle and serfile_out_handle, and sets BB_SerportLog. When a file\ncannot be created, both are closed (but BB_SerportLog is still set on the way out).\nOZ source name: Create_serportdump_files.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF, BC, HL, IX."},
        "2360": {"comment":"filename is local..."},
        "2412": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_Create_serportdump_files."},
        "2414": {"comment":"indicate enabled serial port logging"},
        "2422": {"synopsis":"Switches character translation on for one transfer and remembers the user's setting:\nBB_CharTransCpy gets the current BB_CharTrans, then BB_CharTrans is set. Restore_Traflag\nundoes it.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF (works in AF', exchanged back)."},
        "2445": {"synopsis":"Restores the translation flag saved by Set_TraFlag: BB_CharTrans is set again when\nBB_CharTransCpy is set, and cleared otherwise.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nKeeps: AF (works in AF', exchanged back)."},
        "2464": {"synopsis":"Saves the Panel's serial port settings (Fetch_PanelSets) and installs EazyLink's own: 9600\nbaud transmit and receive, no parity, RTS/CTS handshaking (Define_PanelSettings); then falls\ninto EzLinkSerTimeout.\nOZ source name: Init_PanelSettings.\nEntry: none."},
        "2470": {"synopsis":"Entry inside Init_PanelSets: sets the OS_Si block I/O timeout to EazyLink_DefaultTimeout\n(3000 cs, 30 seconds) through OS_Si SI_TMO.\nOZ source name: EazyLinkSerPortTimeout.\nEntry: none."},
        "2475": {"comment":"set default timeout for OS_Si Block I/O"},
        "2478": {"synopsis":"Copies the Panel's serial port settings to the workspace so KillPopdown can restore them:\ntransmit and receive baud rates (each as a length byte and a word, Cpy_PA_Txb and\nCpy_PA_Rxb), Xon/Xoff (Cpy_PA_Xon) and parity (Cpy_PA_Par), read through OS_Nq.\nOZ source name: Fetch_PanelSettings.\nEntry: none.\nError: an OS_Nq failure is reported through System_error (GN_Err) and returned, Fc = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"max 2 bytes (word)"},
        "2480": {"comment":"Transmit Baud rate"},
        "2483": {"comment":"buffer for baud rate"},
        "2493": {"comment":"remember length of PA_Txb"},
        "2509": {"comment":"remember length of PA_Rxb"},
        "2539": {"synopsis":"Default Serial port parameters: 9600 baud, Xon/Xoff No, Parity No\n(Hardware handshaking is default when OZ/EazyLink starts up)\nOZ source name: Define_PanelSettings.","comment":"word size"},
        "2541": {"comment":"new transmit baud rate, 9600"},
        "2549": {"comment":"new receive baud rate, 9600"},
        "2554": {"comment":"Parity No"},
        "2565": {"synopsis":"Sets the Panel's Xon/Xoff parameter to No (hardware handshaking, OS_Sp PA_Xon), then falls\ninto InstallPanelSets.\nOZ source name: SetPanel_HardwareHandshaking.\nEntry: none."},
        "2567": {"comment":"Xon/Xoff No (hardware handshaking)"},
        "2577": {"synopsis":"Sets the Panel's Xon/Xoff parameter to Yes (software handshaking, OS_Sp PA_Xon), then falls\ninto InstallPanelSets.\nOZ source name: SetPanel_SoftwareHandshaking.\nEntry: none."},
        "2579": {"comment":"Xon/Xoff Yes"},
        "2587": {"synopsis":"Installs the Panel's serial port parameters (OS_Sp PA_Gfi with A = 0), which applies them to\nthe serial port.\nOZ source name: InstallPanelSettings.\nEntry: none."},
        "2588": {"comment":"install new parameters"},
        "2594": {"synopsis":"Restore Panel settings to original values that was present before\nMultiLink was called.\nOZ source name: Restore_PanelSettings.","comment":"fetch length of parameter (Transmit baud rate)"},
        "2600": {"comment":"address of parameter"},
