        "3662": {"synopsis":"EazyLink command ESC \"b\": receives a batch of files from the PC (ImpExp protocol). Each ESC\n\"N\" <name> is followed by the file's data: a RAM file is created and filled\n(ReceiveRamFile); an \":EPR.x\" name is saved in the slot's file area when it can be written\n(FileEprSaveFile, the older entry of the same name is deleted). On an error the rest of the\nfile is read and ignored up to ESC \"E\". ESC \"Z\" ends the batch.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.","comment":"send files to Z88, using ImpExp protocol."},
        "3665": {"comment":"'ImpExp Receive files...'"},
