        "3997": {"comment":"start of buffer"},
        "4008": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_transfer_file."},
        "4011": {"comment":"send EOF file marker to terminal"},
        "4014": {"synopsis":"EazyLink command ESC \"k\": backs up files to the PC (ImpExp protocol). Writes 'Backup Files',\nfetches the path and sends the matching files (SearchFilesystem); then writes 'Scanning\ndirectories...', collects the directories of all RAM devices in a file (Get_Directories),\nsends that file and ends with ESC \"Z\".\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.","comment":"Backup files to terminal, using ImpExp protocol."},
        "4023": {"comment":"without ACKN protocol..."},
        "4032": {"comment":"display pathname on screen..."},
        "4035": {"comment":"backup files..."},
        "4038": {"comment":"system error or timeout on serial port"},
        "4042": {"comment":"\"Searching file system...\""},
        "4045": {"comment":"for directories in all RAM devices"},
        "4051": {"comment":"send file with found directories"},
        "4063": {"comment":"end of files..."},
        "4066": {"synopsis":"HL points at string, A = wildcard search specifier"},
        "4073": {"comment":"reset counters for found names"},
        "4079": {"comment":"read names matching wildcard"},
        "4084": {"comment":"Fc = 0, signal completed all names.."},
        "4087": {"comment":"found the wanted file type?"},
        "4088": {"comment":"no, get next filename match..."},
        "4096": {"comment":"pointer to start name"},
        "4113": {"synopsis":"Receives an ESC-terminated path name (the protocol's 'Z', 'F' or 'N' byte ends it) into\nfilename_buffer, at most 256 bytes, through FetchBlock; the name is null-terminated.\nEntry: IX = start_workspace.\nExit: Fz = 1, A = ESC terminator byte; BC = length; HL = filename_buffer.\nError: Fc = 1 (serial port error or timeout).\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"upper limit of bytes of filename path to receive (probably never happens)"},
        "4119": {"comment":"receive block, ESC terminated 'Z','F' or 'N' byte"},
        "4122": {"synopsis":"Scan all slots for File Areas, and send \":EPR.x\" accordingly."},
        "4128": {"comment":"all slots polled for Epr file area..."},
        "4138": {"comment":"ready for next slot"},
        "4139": {"comment":"this slot had no file area (no card)... try next"},
        "4141": {"comment":"this slot had no file area (car, but no file area)... try next"},
        "4143": {"comment":"preserve slot poll number"},
        "4144": {"comment":"current slot as '0', '1', '2' or '3'"},
        "4152": {"comment":"abort if serial port timed out..."},
        "4154": {"comment":"pointer to start of EPR.x name"},
        "4165": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: completed_Send_Epr_device.","comment":"return Fc = 0, Fz = 0..."},
        "4166": {"comment":"ESC Z has to be sent"},
        "4167": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_Send_Epr_device."},
        "4168": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_Send_Epr_device."},
        "4169": {"synopsis":"Builds the device name \":EPR.x\" in filename_buffer, where x is the slot digit in A, and\nnull-terminates it. Send_Epr_devices sends the result for each slot with a file area.\nEntry: A = slot digit ('0' to '3').\nExit: DE = filename_buffer; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "4181": {"comment":"append slot number"},
        "4184": {"comment":"null-terminate"},
        "4187": {"synopsis":"Check if there is a File Area in slot A = \"0\", \"1\", \"2\" or \"3\"\n\nreturns Fz = 1, Fc = 0, if file area found, DE = size of cards in 16K banks\notherwise Fc 1 or Fz = 0\nOZ source name: CheckFileAreaOfSlot.","comment":"strip to raw slot number number (0 - 3)"},
        "4198": {"comment":"C -> DE = size of card in 16K banks"},
        "4201": {"synopsis":"Path begins with \":RAM.\" ?\n\nHL = pointer to path containing device / dir names\n\nreturns A = slot number ('0', '1', '2' or '3' or '-'), if :RAM.x device recognized (Fz = 1)"},
        "4214": {"synopsis":"Path begins with \":EPR.\" ?\n\nHL = pointer to path containing device / dir names\n\nreturns A = slot number ('0', '1', '2' or '3'), if :EPR.x device recognized (Fz = 1)"},
        "4227": {"synopsis":"Path begins with \":XXX.\"\n\nHL = pointer to path containing device / dir names\nDE = pointer to device name pattern\n\nreturns A = slot number ('0', '1', '2', '3' or '-'), if device is recognized"},
        "4235": {"comment":"Fz = 0, no match"},
        "4240": {"comment":"Fz = 1, match!"},
        "4241": {"comment":"get slot number of file area"},
        "4243": {"synopsis":"Set \":EPR.x\" device name at (filename_buffer)\nEntry: A = slot number ('0', '1', '2' or '3')."},
        "4265": {"synopsis":"Get pointer to first file entry. If only active files are currently displayed,\ndeleted file entries are skipped until an active file entry is found.\nEntry: C = slot number of File area.\nExit: Fc = 1, No file area or no file entries in file area.; Fc = 0; BHL = pointer to first\nfile entry."},
        "4271": {"comment":"an active file entry was found..."},
        "4272": {"synopsis":"Fz = 1, skip deleted file(s) until active file is found\nGet pointer to next file entry. If only active files are currently displayed,\ndeleted file entries are skipped until an active file entry is found.\nEntry: BHL = current file entry pointer.\nExit: Fc = 1, End of list reached; Fc = 0; BHL = pointer to next file entry."},
        "4278": {"comment":"an active file entry was found..."},
        "4279": {"comment":"only active files, scan forward until active file.."},
        "4281": {"synopsis":"Relative offset definitions for allocated work buffer on stack"},
        "4282": {"comment":"preserve CDE"},
        "4283": {"comment":"preserve original IY"},
        "4285": {"comment":"use alternate registers temporarily"},
        "4290": {"comment":"create temporary work buffer on stack"},
        "4298": {"comment":"preserve a copy of original SP on return"},
        "4302": {"comment":"preserve slot number of File Eprom Card"},
        "4308": {"comment":"preserve pointer to external IO buffer"},
        "4321": {"comment":"File size = 0 (will grow as stream is incoming)"},
        "4324": {"comment":"preserve ptr. to filename..."},
        "4328": {"comment":"B = 0, C = size of heap"},
        "4331": {"comment":"point at workspace for File Entry Header..."},
        "4333": {"comment":"DE points at space for File Entry"},
        "4334": {"comment":"preserve pointer to File Entry"},
        "4335": {"comment":"B=0 (local ptr), C = max. size of exp. filename"},
        "4337": {"comment":"first byte of File entry is length of file name, DE = ready for '/'"},
        "4339": {"comment":"reached null-terminator of filename?"},
        "4340": {"comment":"yes, successfully copied filename into entry"},
        "4344": {"comment":"B = size of filename"},
        "4348": {"comment":"max filename length reached..."},
        "4353": {"comment":"(length byte) - This is start of File Entry Header..."},
        "4355": {"comment":"length of filename..."},
        "4356": {"comment":"length of file entry not yet known (file stream to be received)"},
        "4358": {"comment":"DE points to 4-byte length of file image"},
        "4365": {"comment":"last byte of file size always 0 (24 bit > 1Mb!)"},
        "4366": {"comment":"File Entry now ready..."},
        "4367": {"comment":"scan File Eprom in slot X for eprom card type"},
        "4378": {"comment":"not a flash chip, abort with Fc = 1..."},
        "4380": {"comment":"preserve card type of chip in slot C"},
        "4383": {"comment":"is OZ running in slot C?"},
        "4387": {"comment":"yes, saving file to file area in OZ ROM (slot 0 or 1) requires LCD turned off"},
        "4390": {"comment":"read system time, to know elapsed time of received file"},
        "4393": {"comment":"HL = ptr. to File Entry in stack variable area"},
        "4394": {"comment":"Now, receive file from serial port and blow it to Flash file area..."},
        "4397": {"comment":"Fz indicates EOF (normally, the file has been received and blown to card)"},
        "4400": {"comment":"then always turn on screen after save file operation"},
        "4403": {"comment":"BHL <- (IY + FileEntry)"},
        "4408": {"comment":"install original SP"},
        "4410": {"comment":"original IY restored"},
        "4413": {"comment":"original C restored"},
        "4416": {"synopsis":"Whenever a byte has been loaded into the buffer, update the total file size.\nWhen the File has been blown completely to the file area, the file size is\npost-updated into the File Entry Header.\nOZ source name: FileEntrySizeCounter.\nEntry: None.\nExit: Updated 3-byte file size in (IY+FileSize)."},
        "4424": {"comment":"FileSize++ didn't go to zero (Fc = 1)"},
        "4438": {"synopsis":"Post-update the length of the file entry from IY + FileSize\nto File Entry.\nOZ source name: BlowFileEntrySize.\nEntry: None."},
        "4439": {"comment":"preserve IX runtime status base register"},
        "4441": {"comment":"get BHL pointer to start of File Entry in file area"},
        "4445": {"comment":"get length of file entry (file)name"},
        "4451": {"comment":"CDE = length of filename"},
        "4452": {"comment":"adjust length to point at first byte of file length block"},
        "4453": {"comment":"BHL points at low byte of (4-byte) file image length"},
        "4458": {"comment":"length of File Entry in IX"},
        "4467": {"comment":"point at 24-bit file length \"block\", IY+FileSize"},
        "4468": {"comment":"C = Flash card type"},
        "4471": {"comment":"blow three bytes"},
        "4477": {"comment":"use segment 1 to blow bytes..."},
        "4481": {"comment":"blow File Entry file size from DE to Flash Eprom at BHL"},
        "4488": {"synopsis":"Entry: C = slot number to blow file entry; HL = pointer to File Entry.\nExit: Fc = 1, serial port problems."},
        "4491": {"comment":"BHL = ptr. to free file space on File Eprom Card for new File Entry"},
        "4500": {"comment":"preserve pointer to new File Entry"},
        "4504": {"comment":"length of filename"},
        "4505": {"comment":"total size = length of filename + 1 (file length byte)"},
        "4507": {"comment":"+ 4 (32bit file length)"},
        "4511": {"comment":"Blow File Entry Header of C length to Flash"},
        "4514": {"comment":"Ups, saving of File Entry header failed..."},
        "4515": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: save_flash_file_loop.","comment":"Receive block of bytes from serial port into buffer"},
        "4522": {"comment":"block done in File Area, more file data to come from serial port..."},
        "4524": {"comment":"end of file or timeout - blow file size and leave file \"active\""},
        "4527": {"synopsis":"Writes the bytes the last ReceiveBuffer put into the I/O buffer to the file entry in the\nflash card, then decides how the reception goes on.\n1. When (IY+IObufCtr) is not 0, blows that many bytes from (IY+IObuffer) with OS_Fep\nFEP_Wrbl at the image pointer (IY+FeImgPtr), through segment 1, and stores the advanced\npointer back.\n2. If blowing fails, marks the new entry deleted (MarkDeleted) and blows the size received\nso far (BlowFileEntrySize).\n3. Otherwise adds the block to the file size (AddBlk2FileSize). If the receive status had\nFc = 1, shows \"File aborted.\" and takes the same error path as step 2.\nEntry: AF = the status ReceiveBuffer returned (Fc = 1 serial port error, Fz = 1 end of file\nor timeout); IY = save workspace; IX = EazyLink runtime variables.\nExit: Fc = 0; Fz = 1 at end of file, Fz = 0 when more file data is to come.\nError: Fc = 1 (write or serial port error; the entry is marked deleted).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"preserve error condition of the received block"},
        "4532": {"comment":"no file bytes were received into buffer (nothing to write to File area)"},
        "4537": {"comment":"preserve EazyLink runtime variable base pointer"},
        "4539": {"comment":"C = get card type of inserted Flash Card"},
        "4548": {"comment":"current pointer to FE. image (to blow current buffer)"},
        "4553": {"comment":"use segment 1 to blow bytes..."},
        "4556": {"comment":"IX = size of block to blow"},
        "4561": {"comment":"pointer to Buffer Start"},
        "4566": {"comment":"blow File Entry file size from DE to Flash Eprom at BHL"},
        "4575": {"comment":"preserve update FE image ptr for next iteration"},
        "4582": {"comment":"remove previous buffer status - now irrelevant.."},
        "4583": {"comment":"error blowing this block to file area, File not blown properly - try to mark as deleted.."},
        "4586": {"comment":"also blow actual file size (even if incomplete!), return Fc = 1"},
        "4589": {"comment":"FileSize += buffer size"},
        "4592": {"comment":"block was succesfully blown to file area, check received buffer status"},
        "4596": {"comment":"serial port error, mark File Entry deleted with incomplete file size."},
        "4599": {"synopsis":"Adds the size of the current I/O buffer, (IY+IObufCtr), to the 24-bit file size at\n(IY+FileSize).\nOZ source name: AddBlock2FileSize.\nEntry: IY = save workspace.\nChanges: F, BC, HL."},
        "4614": {"comment":"updated total file entry size with buffer size"},
        "4622": {"synopsis":"Save File Entry to File Area in Flash card at BHL\nOZ source name: SaveFlashFileEntry.\nEntry: C = length of file entry header; DE = (local) pointer to File Entry; BHL = pointer to\nfree space on File Eprom.\nExit: Fc = 0, File Entry successfully saved to File Eprom; A = FE_xx chip type; BHL =\npointer beyond last byte of file entry; Fc = 1, save failed...; BHL = pointer to File Entry\nmarked as deleted.; A = RC_xxx error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE, IX, IY.","comment":"preserve EazyLink runtime variable base pointer"},
        "4627": {"comment":"DE = ptr. to File Entry"},
        "4628": {"comment":"length of File Entry in IX"},
        "4630": {"comment":"BHL = pointer to free space on Eprom"},
        "4631": {"comment":"flash chip card type..."},
        "4636": {"comment":"use segment 1 to blow bytes..."},
        "4640": {"comment":"blow File Entry to Flash Eprom"},
        "4654": {"comment":"Fc = 0, A = FE_xx chip type"},
        "4655": {"synopsis":"File Entry was not blown properly, mark it as 'deleted'...\nMark File Entry as deleted, if possible\nEntry: None.\nExit: BHL = pointer to File Entry.\nChanges: B, HL.\nKeeps: AF, C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "4656": {"comment":"BHL <- (IY + FileEntry)"},
        "4661": {"comment":"mark entry as deleted"},
        "4666": {"synopsis":"Receive file stream via protocol level 9 data block to Flash File Entry\nOZ source name: FetchFileEntryCrcBlock.","comment":"file reception is now enabled through Protocol level 9"},
        "4670": {"comment":"HL = pointer to buffer"},
        "4675": {"comment":"receive approx. 128 bytes, but never more than IObufSize bytes..."},
        "4681": {"comment":"error or timeout - communication stopped"},
        "4683": {"comment":"block was not ESC terminated!"},
        "4685": {"comment":"fetched an ESC id, should be ESC 'N'... (C = total size of block received)"},
        "4688": {"comment":"CRC-16 of received block in DE"},
        "4693": {"comment":"ESC 'N' was expected - protocol error..."},
        "4700": {"comment":"fetch 4 bytes of Ascii CRC-16 to validate received block..."},
        "4703": {"comment":"error or timeout - communication stopped"},
        "4705": {"comment":"sub-block was not ESC terminated!"},
        "4709": {"comment":"ESC ']' was expected, protocol error"},
        "4711": {"comment":"convert Ascii CRC-16 at (ScratchBuffer) to integer, return in HL"},
        "4714": {"comment":"CRC-16 match?"},
        "4716": {"comment":"Yes, CRC-block received successfully"},
        "4721": {"comment":"less max retries..."},
        "4722": {"comment":"respond with ESC Z to terminal to re-send block"},
        "4728": {"comment":"A = ']', Fc = 1 if ESC 'Z' failed to be transmitted..."},
        "4729": {"comment":"timeout, terminal didn't fetch the acknowledge"},
        "4731": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: signal_received_block."},
        "4740": {"comment":"Pointer to Buffer Start"},
        "4748": {"comment":"use translation on received block, before blowing to FE"},
        "4751": {"comment":"flush successfully received CRC-block to File Entry..."},
        "4759": {"comment":"signal I/O error / No Room to Terminal"},
        "4763": {"comment":"fatal error, abort file entry reception"},
        "4768": {"comment":"reset to max CRC-block retries for new block"},
        "4770": {"comment":"and respond with ESC Y to terminal to acknowledge"},
        "4778": {"comment":"ESC 'Y' sent successfully, await next block or ESC 'E'"},
        "4779": {"comment":"ignore return address of this call to abort file reception"},
        "4780": {"comment":"indicate no buffer contents to blow (protocol failure)"},
        "4785": {"synopsis":"Receive a chunk from the file through the serial port into buffer of <BufferSize> bytes\n\nFc = 0, Fz = 0, buffer loaded with file contents...\n(IY + IObufCtr) = actual size of buffer to save, less than or equal to <IObufsize>.\n\nRegister changed after return:\nA.BC..HL/IXIY same\n.F..DE../.... different\nEntry: None.\nExit: Fz = 1, if EOF or Serial port timeout was reached...; Fc = 1, Serial port related\nerror was reached..."},
        "4786": {"comment":"preserve current BHL pointer to file entry data image"},
        "4791": {"comment":"file reception is by default std. protocol"},
        "4797": {"comment":"reset CRC-block retries to 128 attempts for block (relevant for protocol level 9 only)"},
        "4800": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: receive_fentry_bytes_loop."},
        "4803": {"comment":"serial port error or timeout - communication stopped"},
        "4805": {"comment":"received byte to file"},
        "4809": {"comment":"ESC '[', protocol level 9 CRC-16 data block is being sent..."},
        "4814": {"comment":"ESC ']', CRC-block completed, get another block or wait for EOF.."},
        "4816": {"comment":"ESC 'E', EOF?"},
        "4822": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: check_crcblock_retry."},
        "4831": {"comment":"CRC-block retry exhausted, abort file (signal EOF!)..."},
        "4833": {"synopsis":"byte in A to file...\nOZ source name: byte_to_fileentry."},
        "4837": {"comment":"we're in Protocol level 9, skip any noise because of Blink UART"},
        "4839": {"comment":"is it a line feed?"},
        "4843": {"comment":"CRLF flag active?"},
        "4847": {"comment":"- ignore LF (reverse CRLF) and fetch next byte..."},
        "4849": {"comment":"put byte into buffer"},
        "4852": {"comment":"buffer full..."},
        "4854": {"comment":"fetch next byte from serial port"},
        "4858": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, make sure NOT to indicate EOF or error!"},
        "4859": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_receivebuffer."},
        "4860": {"comment":"restore original A"},
        "4864": {"synopsis":"Stores the received byte in the I/O buffer and counts it, then tells whether the buffer is\nfull.\nEntry: A = byte; HL = next free position in the buffer; IY = save workspace.\nExit: HL = HL + 1; (IY+IObufCtr) incremented; Fc = 0, Fz = 1 when the count equals\n(IY+IObufSize), the buffer is full.\nChanges: F, DE, HL.","comment":"put byte into buffer"},
        "4865": {"comment":"ready for next byte"},
        "4866": {"comment":"current size of buffer updated with new byte"},
        "4879": {"comment":"Max Buffer Size"},
        "4881": {"comment":"is buffer full (total received bytes == buffer size)?"},
        "4884": {"comment":"return Fc = 0, Fz = 1, if buffer full"},
        "4885": {"synopsis":"Empties the flash save routine's I/O buffer: HL points at its start and the byte count\n(IY+IObufCtr) is reset to 0.\nEntry: IY = save workspace.\nExit: HL = (IY+IObuffer).\nChanges: HL."},
        "4888": {"comment":"Pointer to Buffer Start"},
        "4896": {"synopsis":"BHL <- (IY + FileEntry)"},
        "4902": {"comment":"get File Entry pointer"},
        "4906": {"synopsis":"Get slot number C (embedded in Bank number B).\nEntry: B = absolute bank number.\nExit: C = slot number which bank B is part of.\nChanges: C.\nKeeps: AF, B, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4912": {"comment":"slot C (of bank B)"},
        "4915": {"synopsis":"Validate the Flash Card/UV Eprom erase/write functionality in the specified slot.\nIf the Card in the specified slot contains an Intel chip, the slot must be 3 for format,\nsave and delete functionality.\nIf the Card in the specified slot contains an UV Eprom, the slot must be 3 for erasing,\nsaving files and creating file header.\nReport an error to the caller with Fc = 1, if an Intel Flash chip was recognized\nin all slots except 3.\nReport an error if to the caller with Fc = 1, if an UV Eprom (with a file area) was\nrecognized in all slots except 3.\nEntry: C = slot number.\nExit: Fz = 1, if a Flash Card is available in the current slot (Fz = 0, no Flash Card\navailable!); B = size of card in 16K banks; Fc = 1, if no erase/write support is available\nfor current slot.\nChanges: F, B.\nKeeps: A, C, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4933": {"comment":"Fz = 0, indicate no Flash Card available in slot"},
        "4934": {"comment":"Fc = 1, indicate no erase/write support either..."},
        "4939": {"comment":"Fz = 0, indicate UV Eprom"},
        "4940": {"comment":"Fc = 1, no erase/write support"},
        "4947": {"comment":"erase/write works for all flash cards in slot 3 (Fc=0, Fz=1)"},
        "4952": {"comment":"Intel flash chip found in slot 0,1 or 2."},
        "4954": {"comment":"No, we found an AMD/compatible Flash chip (Fc=0, Fz=1)"},
        "4957": {"comment":"(Fz=1, indicate that Flash is available..)"},
        "4958": {"comment":"no erase/write support in slot 0,1 or 2 with Intel Flash..."},
        "4960": {"comment":"A restored (f changed)"},
        "4962": {"comment":"C restored (B = total of 16K banks on card)"},
        "4963": {"comment":"DE restored"},
        "4964": {"comment":"HL restored"},
        "4967": {"comment":"A restored (f changed)"},
        "4972": {"synopsis":"Transmit file (image) from File Eprom Card, identified by File Entry at BHL\n(B=00h-FFh embedded slot mask, HL=0000h-3FFFh bank offset) to serial port.\n\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF, File Eprom or File Entry was not found in slot\nA = RC_xxx, I/O error during saving process.\nFz = 1, Time out on serial port\n\nDesign & programming (based on original FileEprFetchFile):\nGunther Strube, March 2011\nEntry: BHL = pointer to Eprom File Entry (bits 7,6 of B is the slot mask).\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 0; File Image transferred successfully to serial port.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "4977": {"comment":"get size of file in CDE, of entry BHL"},
        "4980": {"comment":"there was no File Eprom Entry at BHL!"},
        "4983": {"comment":"preserve size of file (in CDE)"},
        "4986": {"comment":"get pointer to file image in BHL"},
        "4991": {"comment":"file size in CDE'"},
        "4995": {"comment":"file size = 0 ?"},
        "4999": {"comment":"No, bytes still left to transfer to RAM..."},
        "5005": {"comment":"Yes, completed Eprom Image transfer to serial port!"},
        "5007": {"comment":"get size of block to transfer in HL'"},
        "5010": {"comment":"then transfer block at BHL to serial port..."},
        "5013": {"comment":"Serial port I/O error occurred, abort..."},
        "5022": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0, indeicate successful file image transfer.."},
        "5025": {"comment":"return Fc = 1, error code \"Object not found\""},
        "5031": {"synopsis":"Transfer File Block, at (BHL), size hl to serial port\nOZ source name: TransferFileBlock.\nEntry: BHL = pointer to file block; hl' = size of block to transfer.\nExit: Fc = ?, file I/O status; A = RC_xxx, if I/O error occurred; BHL = updated to point at\nfirst byte of next block to save (or EOF).","comment":"preserve bank number of ext. address"},
        "5036": {"comment":"pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "5038": {"comment":"page in bank at C = Safe MS_S1 segment"},
        "5039": {"comment":"preserve original bank binding of segment"},
        "5042": {"comment":"preserve remaining file size..."},
        "5044": {"comment":"HL = source (inside current bank B)"},
        "5045": {"comment":"BC = length of block to transfer to serial port"},
        "5051": {"comment":"restore remaining file size..."},
        "5054": {"comment":"restore previous segment bank binding..."},
        "5055": {"comment":"transmitting current block failed, exit..."},
        "5063": {"comment":"we're still inside the current bank after block save..."},
        "5064": {"comment":"set offset at start of new bank"},
        "5065": {"comment":"always returns Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "5066": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: err_TransferFileBlock."},
        "5068": {"synopsis":"Sends every file that matches a wildcard name to the remote computer for the ImpExp backup.\nOpens a wildcard handler with A = 0 (files before directories) and runs filenames_loop when\nit succeeds.\nEntry: HL = wildcard filename; IX = EazyLink runtime variables.\nExit: Fc = 0 when all names are processed.\nError: Fc = 1 (no wildcard handler, or a transmission error).\nKeeps: IX.","comment":"wildcard search specifier - files before directories"},
        "5070": {"comment":"get handle for wildcard"},
        "5081": {"synopsis":"The loop of SearchFilesystem. Fetches the next name from the wildcard handler; for each file\nwhose creation and update date stamps are equal (compare_dates), sends its name\n(Transfer_filename) and contents (Transfer_RamfileImage), then opens it for update and\ncloses it, which gives it a new update date stamp. Directories and other files are skipped.\nExit: Fc = 0 when there are no more names (the wildcard handler is left open).\nError: Fc = 1 on a transmission error, after Close_wcard_hnd has released the handler.","comment":"next file in wildcard search..."},
        "5084": {"comment":"no more files from a wildcardcard search..."},
        "5095": {"comment":"equal date stamps, proces file ..."},
        "5097": {"comment":"already updated, continue ..."},
        "5102": {"comment":"transfer file without ACKN protocol..."},
        "5105": {"comment":"Ups - transmission error"},
        "5108": {"comment":"transfer file without ACKN protocol..."},
        "5111": {"comment":"Ups - transmission error"},
        "5114": {"comment":"Open for Update..."},
        "5124": {"comment":"Update file with new date stamp."},
        "5127": {"comment":"fetch next file name"},
        "5129": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: stop_wcard_search."},
        "5132": {"comment":"open type"},
        "5134": {"comment":"create \"DIRECTORIES.CLI\" file,"},
        "5145": {"comment":"length of cli_cmd2"},
        "5156": {"comment":"current length of file = 3"},
        "5159": {"comment":"close file and"},
        "5162": {"comment":"re-open (update)"},
        "5164": {"comment":"\"DIRECTORIES.CLI\" file,"},
        "5170": {"comment":"to be ignored by search_filer..."},
        "5173": {"comment":"PRINT#ch,\"#F\""},
        "5176": {"comment":"length of string at pointer"},
        "5177": {"comment":"to \"directories.CLI\""},
        "5180": {"comment":"close file and return to caller"},
        "5182": {"comment":"tmp close - DOR processing..."},
        "5185": {"comment":"wildcard search specifier..."},
        "5190": {"comment":"now get RAM devices through wildcard handler"},
        "5195": {"comment":"handle for wildcard search"},
        "5202": {"comment":"save handle for next RAM device fetch"},
        "5204": {"comment":"is a RAM device?"},
