        "5252": {"comment":"get wildcard search handle"},
        "5254": {"comment":"file system search completed"},
        "5257": {"comment":"all directories stored as CLI commands."},
        "5258": {"synopsis":"Writes a line to DIRECTORIES.CLI for every directory below the current one, recursively.\n1. Moves to the first entry with OS_Dor DR_SON; returns Fc = 0 when there is none.\n2. Pushes its name on the path (push_dir_name). For a directory, writes its path\n(prt_dir_path), calls itself for its contents and reopens it (fetch_cur_dir).\n3. Moves to each sibling with DR_SIB, replacing the last path name (upd_dir_name), and\nhandles directories the same way.\n4. When there are no more siblings, removes the name from the path (pop_dir_name).\nEntry: IX = DOR handle of the directory; file_buffer holds its path; (directory_ptr) = top\nof the directory name stack.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1 (a directory DOR could not be reopened).","comment":"go to directory..."},
        "5262": {"comment":"no elements found"},
        "5264": {"comment":"file name, add to list ..."},
        "5267": {"comment":"a directory?"},
        "5274": {"comment":"exit on write error"},
        "5275": {"comment":"check for names in subdirectory"},
        "5279": {"comment":"handle for current directory"},
        "5282": {"comment":"read names in current directory"},
        "5286": {"comment":"no more names in current directory"},
        "5288": {"comment":"exchange old file name with new."},
        "5291": {"comment":"new name, a directory?"},
        "5298": {"comment":"file error..."},
        "5299": {"comment":"check for names in subdirectory"},
        "5302": {"comment":"return on error..."},
        "5303": {"comment":"handle for current directory"},
        "5308": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_subdirectory.","comment":"reset CARRY. indicate no error"},
        "5309": {"comment":"remove current filename in list"},
        "5312": {"comment":"(unstack current filename)"},
        "5313": {"comment":"reset CARRY flag."},
        "5314": {"comment":"indicate no error to caller..."},
        "5315": {"synopsis":"Appends the CLI line of the directory whose path is in file_buffer to DIRECTORIES.CLI. Frees\nthe current DOR handle, opens the file for update, moves to its end ((file_ptr)), writes\ncli_cmd3, the path and cli_cmd5, and closes it. Then adds the length written to (file_ptr)\nand reopens the directory's DOR (fetch_cur_dir).\nOZ source name: print_directory_path.\nEntry: IX = DOR handle; file_buffer = path; (file_ptr) = current length of the file.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = DOR handle of the directory in file_buffer.\nError: Fc = 1 when the DOR cannot be reopened (a write error is reported by System_error,\nnot in Fc).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5317": {"comment":"free current DOR handle"},
        "5327": {"comment":"open CLI directory file"},
        "5332": {"comment":"move file pointer to end of file."},
        "5337": {"comment":"write CLI command at the end"},
        "5346": {"comment":"search for null-terminator in"},
        "5347": {"comment":"buffer to fetch length of filename"},
        "5350": {"comment":"buffer area"},
        "5353": {"comment":"find byte..."},
        "5355": {"comment":"file name without terminator"},
        "5356": {"comment":"reset Fc (if set)"},
        "5363": {"comment":"length of file name"},
        "5364": {"comment":"indicate BC = length of string"},
        "5365": {"comment":"HL = pointer to beginning of directory path"},
        "5366": {"comment":"write string to file..."},
        "5371": {"comment":"PRINT#ch,\"~E\""},
        "5374": {"comment":"Fc = 0, length of string at (HL)"},
        "5378": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_print_directory_path.","comment":"close \"DIRECTORY.CLI\" file"},
        "5381": {"comment":"get length of file name"},
        "5383": {"comment":"length of cli_cmd3 + cli_cmd5"},
        "5388": {"comment":"result in BC"},
        "5389": {"comment":"get current length of file"},
        "5392": {"comment":"and add length of filename and cli's"},
        "5393": {"comment":"store new length"},
        "5396": {"comment":"continue to read DOR information"},
        "5400": {"synopsis":"Opens the DOR of the path held in file_buffer (OP_DOR through open_file).\nOZ source name: fetch_current_directory.\nEntry: file_buffer = path.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = DOR handle.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_xxx).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5402": {"comment":"filename of current directory"},
        "5411": {"synopsis":"Appends the name of the current DOR to the path in file_buffer and pushes it on the\ndirectory name stack. Puts a '/' before the free position the stack's top points at, reads\nthe name there (DT_NAM, up to 17 bytes) and pushes a pointer past its terminator.\nOZ source name: push_directory_name.\nEntry: IX = DOR handle; (directory_ptr) = top of the stack (in ScratchBuffer).\nExit: (directory_ptr) and IY = new top of the stack.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: AF.","comment":"save flags"},
        "5412": {"comment":"pointer to top of stack"},
        "5419": {"comment":"DE pointer to new directory name"},
        "5422": {"comment":"pointer to end of previous name"},
        "5423": {"comment":"delimeter for directory names"},
        "5426": {"comment":"original pointer"},
        "5427": {"comment":"save directory name to pointer"},
        "5428": {"comment":"(IX = DOR handle)"},
        "5431": {"comment":"search for null-terminator in"},
        "5433": {"comment":"buffer for directory name."},
        "5434": {"comment":"read max 17 letters."},
        "5437": {"comment":"find byte..."},
        "5439": {"comment":"adress of next directory name"},
        "5441": {"comment":"increase directory stack pointer"},
        "5446": {"comment":"save pointer to free bytes"},
        "5449": {"comment":"new top of stack."},
        "5453": {"comment":"restore flags"},
        "5455": {"synopsis":"Pops the last name off the directory name stack: clears the top entry, moves (directory_ptr)\ndown and null-terminates the path in file_buffer where that name began.\nOZ source name: pop_directory_name.\nEntry: (directory_ptr) = top of the stack.\nExit: (directory_ptr) and IY = new top of the stack.\nChanges: HL, IY.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "5456": {"comment":"adress of top of directory stack"},
        "5460": {"comment":"remove pointer of cur. cat. name"},
        "5472": {"comment":"new top of stack"},
        "5479": {"comment":"pointer to new name"},
        "5482": {"comment":"move to end of previous name"},
        "5485": {"comment":"null-terminate file name."},
        "5488": {"synopsis":"Replaces the last name of the path with the name of the current DOR: pop_dir_name, then\npush_dir_name.\nOZ source name: update_directory_name.\nEntry: IX = DOR handle.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL, IY.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "5492": {"comment":"stack new directory name"},
        "5497": {"synopsis":"Print string to file.\nEntry: local pointer to string in HL; Fc = 1, length of string in C, other length of string\nat (HL)."},
        "5508": {"comment":"from memory to file..."},
        "5516": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: init_dir_pointers."},
        "5520": {"comment":"top of stack"},
        "5526": {"comment":"point at beginning of path"},
        "5532": {"comment":"point at end of ram device name..."},
        "5537": {"comment":"write filename of current DOR"},
        "5538": {"comment":"record at (DE)"},
        "5543": {"comment":"filename of 16 bytes & terminator"},
        "5550": {"synopsis":"Fetch date stamp of RAM file\nDE = pointer to date buffer"},
        "5552": {"comment":"H  = dr_rd | dr_wr"},
        "5553": {"comment":"L  = Creation, Update date"},
        "5554": {"comment":"pointer to file name"},
        "5556": {"comment":"open DOR information to file."},
        "5566": {"comment":"buffer to date"},
        "5568": {"comment":"A = dr_rd | dr_wr"},
        "5569": {"comment":"B = ASC\"C\" | ASC\"U\""},
        "5570": {"comment":"C = buf. length (of date) => (DE)"},
        "5576": {"comment":"close DOR to file."},
        "5586": {"synopsis":"Reads the creation and update date stamps of the file named in filename_buffer into\ncreation_date and update_date (rw_date, 6 bytes each) and compares them.\nEntry: filename_buffer = filename.\nExit: A = $FF when the stamps are equal, A = 0 when they differ.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "5630": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_compare_dates."},
        "5634": {"synopsis":"Opens a file or resource with GN_Opf, for a filename in local memory and an explicit name\nbuffer of 128 bytes.\nEntry: A = open mode (OP_xxx); HL = filename; DE = buffer for the explicit filename.\nExit: Fc = 0; IX = handle; DE = end of the explicit name; B = segments, C = characters in\nthe name.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_xxx).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, IX.","comment":"HL = local pointer to filename, C = buffer length"},
        "5637": {"comment":"IX = handle for file."},
        "5641": {"synopsis":"The name of the CLI file the backup writes the RAM devices' directories to,\n\":RAM.-/DIRECTORIES.CLI\", null-terminated."},
        "5664": {"synopsis":"Length-prefixed text written first to DIRECTORIES.CLI: 3, then \"#F\" and CR."},
        "5668": {"synopsis":"Length-prefixed text written before each directory path in DIRECTORIES.CLI: 5, then \"|CD|D\"."},
        "5674": {"synopsis":"Length-prefixed text written after each directory path in DIRECTORIES.CLI: 3, then \"~E\" and\nCR."},
        "5678": {"synopsis":"H = <startsynch>, L = <end_synch> ID","comment":"byte in A."},
        "5681": {"comment":"system error or timeout"},
        "5682": {"comment":"check end synch byte"},
        "5683": {"comment":"eof synch..."},
        "5684": {"comment":"receive next synch byte?"},
        "5685": {"comment":"synch byte, continue..."},
        "5687": {"comment":"exit broken synch sequnce.."},
        "5689": {"synopsis":"Sends a synch sequence to the remote computer: the start byte twice, then the end byte.\nEntry: H = start byte; L = end byte.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (ESC pressed or timeout).\nChanges: AF, B."},
        "5691": {"comment":"start, body of synch..."},
        "5692": {"comment":"B = length of synch..."},
        "5695": {"comment":"return if ESC pressed or timeout"},
        "5698": {"comment":"end of synch..."},
        "5701": {"synopsis":"Receives a byte from the serial port (RxByte) and, when character translation is on\n(BB_CharTrans), translates it; falls into TransIncoming.\nEntry: IX = EazyLink runtime variables.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_xxx).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL.","comment":"receive a byte from serial port via OZ"},
        "5709": {"comment":"skip, translation not enabled.."},
        "5710": {"synopsis":"Translates a byte received from the remote computer through the table at TraTableOut.\nOZ source name: TranslateIncoming.\nEntry: A = byte.\nExit: A = translated byte.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "5714": {"comment":"A = byte received & translated"},
        "5719": {"synopsis":"Translates a byte to send to the remote computer through the table at TraTableIn.\nOZ source name: TranslateOutgoing.\nEntry: A = byte.\nExit: A = translated byte.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "5723": {"comment":"A = byte received & translated"},
        "5728": {"synopsis":"byte in A.","comment":"HL >> Translation Table"},
        "5732": {"comment":"Offset calculated to translated byte... (Fc = 0 always)"},
        "5733": {"comment":"get translated byte..."},
        "5736": {"synopsis":"Receives a byte from the serial port with OS_Si SI_GBT and a 30 second timeout. When serial\nport logging is on (BB_SerportLog), copies the byte to the input log file. A failure goes to\nCheck_timeout.\nEntry: IX = EazyLink runtime variables.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = byte.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Time on timeout).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "5743": {"comment":"get a byte from serial port, using OZ standard interface"},
        "5751": {"comment":"dump to debugging serport input file (if enabled)"},
        "5764": {"comment":"Translate byte before sending..."},
        "5767": {"synopsis":"Sends a byte to the serial port with OS_Si SI_PBT and a 30 second timeout. When serial port\nlogging is on (BB_SerportLog), copies the byte to the output log file. A failure goes to\nCheck_timeout.\nEntry: A = byte; IX = EazyLink runtime variables.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Time on timeout).\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "5782": {"comment":"dump to debugging serport output file (if enabled)"},
        "5787": {"synopsis":"Handles a failed serial port transfer: ErrHandler deals with ESC, suspend and quit, and on a\ntimeout (RC_Time) \"Waiting...\" is written to the log window.\nEntry: A = error code (RC_xxx).\nExit: Fc = 1; A = error code.\nChanges: F, HL."},
        "5790": {"comment":"timeout?"},
        "5796": {"comment":"other errors."},
        "5797": {"synopsis":"Writes \"Waiting...\" (message2) to the log window with Write_message.\nExit: HL = message2.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF.","comment":"'Waiting...'"},
        "5803": {"synopsis":"PCLINK II protocol\nGet byte from serial port and acknowledge","comment":"receive a byte from serial port (OZ or hardware interface)"},
        "5809": {"comment":"acknowledge byte..."},
        "5815": {"comment":"system error, e.g. ESC pressed..."},
        "5820": {"comment":"Translation not enabled"},
        "5823": {"synopsis":"PCLINK II protocol\nGet byte and acknowledge (no translation)...","comment":"receive a byte from serial port via OZ"},
        "5829": {"comment":"acknowledge byte..."},
        "5836": {"synopsis":"PCLINK II protocol\nSend byte to serial port without translation"},
        "5840": {"comment":"receive a byte from serial port via OZ"},
        "5842": {"synopsis":"PCLINK II protocol\nSend byte to serial port with translation"},
        "5846": {"comment":"Translate byte before sending..."},
        "5853": {"comment":"receive acknowledge byte from serial port via OZ"},
        "5855": {"synopsis":"If Serial port input stream copy is enabled,\nBIT  BB_SerportLog,(IX + rtmflags) = 1\nthen dump recently fetched byte into INPUT dump file\nOZ source name: Dump_serport_in_byte."},
        "5862": {"comment":"and dump a copy into debug file"},
        "5868": {"synopsis":"If Serial port output stream copy is enabled,\nBIT  BB_SerportLog,(IX + rtmflags) = 1\nthen dump output byte to serial into OUTPUT dump file\nOZ source name: Dump_serport_out_byte."},
        "5875": {"comment":"and dump a copy into debug file"},
        "5877": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_Dump_serport_out_byte."},
        "5881": {"synopsis":"PCLINK II protocol\nSend sequense of bytes, untranslated.","comment":"HL >> string, 0 terminated..."},
        "5884": {"comment":"check for terminator"},
        "5888": {"comment":"put byte to serial port"},
        "5891": {"comment":"error - stop transmit..."},
        "5893": {"comment":"byte sent , continue"},
        "5896": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_SendString_ackn."},
        "5900": {"comment":"reset Z flag."},
        "5901": {"comment":"restore original contents of A"},
        "5902": {"comment":"restore original contents of BC"},
        "5904": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: err_SendString_ackn.","comment":"save contents of F register"},
        "5907": {"comment":"restore F register"},
