        "8036": {"synopsis":"Z88 ISO - IBM translation table"},
        "8292": {"synopsis":"Table of 256 bytes: the default outgoing (IBM to Z88 ISO) translation, indexed by byte\nvalue. It follows IBM_TraTableIn, and Use_StdTranslations copies both (512 bytes) into\nTraTableIn and TraTableOut."},
        "8548": {"synopsis":"Switch Z88 LCD Screen On or Off.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Aug 2006\nEntry: Fz = 1, Turn LCD screen On; Fz = 0, Turn LCD screen Off.\nExit: None.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "8550": {"comment":"Address of soft copy of COM register"},
        "8554": {"comment":"Screen LCD Off by default"},
        "8556": {"comment":"but caller wants to switch On..."},
        "8560": {"comment":"signal to Blink COM register to do the LCD..."},
        "8565": {"synopsis":"Entry inside SetBlinkScreen: sets the LCD-on bit (BB_COMLCDON) in A, the COM register value\nbeing built.\nEntry: A = COM value.\nExit: A = COM value with the LCD on.\nChanges: A.","comment":"Screen LCD On"},
        "8568": {"synopsis":"Switches the LCD on: calls SetBlinkScreen with Fz = 1, which sets BB_COMLCDON in the\nBLSC_COM soft copy and writes it to the Blink COM register.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "8575": {"synopsis":"Read byte at base record pointer in BHL, offset A.\nByte is returned in A.\n\nIf B<>0, the byte is read from extended address.\nIf B=0, the byte is read from local address space.\n\nRegister affected on return:\n..BCDEHL/IXIY same\nAF....../.... different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, 1997, Sep 2004, Oct 2005, Aug 2012"},
        "8581": {"comment":"add offset to pointer"},
        "8586": {"comment":"pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "8588": {"comment":"page in bank at C = Safe MS_S1 segment"},
        "8589": {"comment":"read byte at extended or local address"},
        "8590": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "8595": {"synopsis":"Add distance CDE (24bit integer) to current pointer address BHL\n\nA new pointer is returned in BHL, preserving original\nslot mask and segment mask.\n\nThis routine is primarily used for File Eprom management.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997\nOZ source name: AddPointerDistance.\nChanges: B, HL.\nKeeps: AF, C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "8598": {"comment":"preserve C register"},
        "8602": {"comment":"preserve segment mask"},
        "8610": {"comment":"preserve slot mask"},
        "8616": {"comment":"preserve distance in ADE"},
        "8617": {"comment":"BHL -> DEBC address"},
        "8624": {"comment":"distance added to DEBC,"},
        "8625": {"comment":"result in DEBC, new abs. address"},
        "8626": {"comment":"new abs. address to BHL logic..."},
        "8631": {"comment":"slot mask restored in bank number"},
        "8634": {"comment":"segment mask restored in offset"},
        "8636": {"comment":"C register restored"},
        "8640": {"synopsis":"Convert 1MB 20bit address to relative pointer in BHL\n(B = 00h - 3Fh, HL = 0000h - 3FFFh).\n\nThis routine is primarily used File Eprom management\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997\nEntry: EBC = 24bit integer (actually 20bit 1MB address).\nExit: BHL = pointer.\nChanges: B, HL.\nKeeps: AF, C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "8649": {"comment":"OFFSET READY..."},
        "8650": {"comment":"now divide top 6 address bit with 16K"},
        "8651": {"comment":"and place it into B (bank) register"},
        "8660": {"comment":"BHL now (relative) ext. address"},
        "8661": {"synopsis":"Convert relative pointer BHL (B = 00h - 3Fh, HL = 0000h - 3FFFh)\nto absolute 20bit 1MB address.\n\nThis routine primarily used for File Eprom Management.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, InterLogic, Dec 1997\nEntry: BHL = pointer.\nExit: DEBC = 32bit integer (actually 24bit).\nChanges: BC, DE.\nKeeps: AF, HL, IX, IY."},
        "8677": {"comment":"DEBC = <BankNumber> * 16K + offset"},
        "8679": {"comment":"DEBC = BHL changed to absolute address in Eprom"},
        "8683": {"synopsis":"File Entry Management:\nInternal support library routine for FileEprFetchFile & FlashEprCopyFileEntry.\n\nDefine a block size to transfer, which is from the current bank offset and within 16K bank boundary,\nconsidering the remaining file size to copy.\nOZ source name: FileEprTransferBlockSize.\nEntry: BHL = current pointer to file block data; cde' = current file size.\nExit: hl' = size of block in File Area to transfer; cde' = updated according to adjusted\nblock size (that can be transferred within the bank boundary).\nChanges: AF, AF', BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "8687": {"comment":"16K bank boundary..."},
        "8690": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "8691": {"comment":"HL = <BankSpace>"},
        "8695": {"comment":"get a copy of current file size (CDE)"},
        "8697": {"comment":"and preserve a copy..."},
        "8700": {"comment":"divisor in CDE (current size of file)"},
        "8701": {"comment":"dividend in BHL (remaining bytes of bank)"},
        "8703": {"comment":"<blocksize> = <FileSize> MOD <BankSpace>"},
        "8708": {"comment":"(restore current file size)"},
        "8718": {"comment":"copy remaining bank space from file inside current bank"},
        "8724": {"comment":"<blocksize> = 0 ?"},
        "8725": {"comment":"no, FileSize > BankSpace"},
        "8728": {"comment":"Yes, FileSize <= BankSpace"},
        "8731": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_TransferBlockSize."},
        "8735": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FileEprTransferBlockSize: the remaining file image fits in the current bank, so\nthe block is the whole remainder.\nEntry: DE' = remaining file size (at most 16K).\nExit: HL' = block size (the file size); DE' = 0.\nChanges: DE', HL'.","comment":"remaining file image to be copied is"},
        "8736": {"comment":"smaller than <BankSpace>, therefore"},
        "8737": {"comment":"the last image block is resident in the"},
        "8740": {"comment":"current bank..."},
        "8741": {"comment":"HL' = FileSize (max. 16K)"},
        "8742": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FileEprTransferBlockSize: the remaining file image crosses the bank boundary,\nso the block is only the space left in this bank.\nEntry: DE = space left in the bank; CDE' = remaining file size; Fc = 0.\nExit: HL' = block size (the bank space); CDE' = file size less the bank space.\nChanges: BC', DE', HL'.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"size of remaining file image crosses current"},
        "8743": {"comment":"bank boundary..."},
        "8744": {"comment":"define block size only of <BankSpace> size."},
        "8755": {"comment":"FileSize = FileSize - BankSpace"},
        "8756": {"comment":"HL' = BankSpace ..."},
        "8760": {"synopsis":"BHL/CDE -> BHL=quotient, CDE=remainder"},
        "8765": {"comment":"alt"},
        "8773": {"comment":"main"},
        "8799": {"comment":"alt"},
        "8807": {"comment":"main"},
        "8815": {"synopsis":"ToUpper - convert character to upper case if possible.\n\n..BCDEHL/IXIY  same\nAF....../....  different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Copyright (C) 1995\nEntry: A = ASCII byte.\nExit: A = converted ASCII byte.","comment":"if A <= 'z'  &&"},
        "8819": {"comment":"if A >= 'a'"},
        "8822": {"comment":"then A = A - 32"},
        "8825": {"comment":"if A <= $FE  &&"},
        "8828": {"comment":"if A >= $E1"},
        "8831": {"comment":"then A = A - 32"},
        "8834": {"synopsis":"Create filename and directory path.\n\nTry to create the specified filename using OP_OUT. If a directory path is\nspecified, it will automatically be created if not defined in the filing\nsystem.\n\nThe filename must not contain wildcards (standard convention). However if a\nRAM device is not specified, it will automatically be included (the current)\ninto the filename.\n\nThe buffer of the filename must have space to get itself expanded with a\ndevice name (additional 6 bytes).\n\nThe filename pointer may not point in segment 2, since GN_FEX is unreliable\nin that segment.\n\nThe routine deletes an existing file without warning.\n\nout, if successful:\nfile handle stored in (file_handle)\nfc = 0, file (and directory) successfully created\n(hl) = filename may have been expanded\n\nout, if failed:\nfc = 1, unable to create file (directory)\na = error code:\nRC_IVF, Invalid filename\nRC_USE, File already in use\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Copyright (C) 1995\nEntry: bhl = pointer to null-terminated filename, (b = 0, means local).\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"preserve original BC"},
        "8835": {"comment":"preserve original DE"},
        "8836": {"comment":"preserve original HL"},
        "8837": {"comment":"preserve original IY"},
        "8842": {"comment":"IY points at start of filename"},
        "8846": {"comment":"pointer to filename is local"},
        "8853": {"comment":"MS_Sx"},
        "8854": {"comment":"page filename into segment"},
        "8855": {"comment":"preserve old bank binding"},
        "8860": {"comment":"preserve error status..."},
        "8861": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "8876": {"synopsis":"Create the filename\nEntry: HL = pointer to filename."},
        "8882": {"comment":"find null-terminator"},
        "8886": {"comment":"length = end - start"},
        "8891": {"comment":"length of buffer + 6 (max. length 255 bytes)"},
        "8892": {"comment":"c = length of buffer"},
        "8895": {"comment":"hl = pointer to filename"},
        "8896": {"comment":"de = pointer to output"},
        "8908": {"comment":"file created successfully, return..."},
        "8911": {"comment":"if error != RC_ONF"},
        "8913": {"comment":"return error"},
        "8915": {"comment":"first expand filename"},
        "8918": {"comment":"invalid filename"},
        "8920": {"comment":"pre-load Fc = 1 & A = RC_IVF, if errors"},
        "8923": {"comment":"wildcards were used..."},
        "8928": {"comment":"filename not specified..."},
        "8929": {"comment":"fc = 0"},
        "8930": {"comment":"deduct filename segment"},
        "8931": {"comment":"deduct device name segment"},
        "8932": {"comment":"hl points at null-terminator"},
        "8933": {"comment":"create directory path..."},
        "8936": {"comment":"then try to create file again..."},
        "8938": {"comment":"couldn't create directory, return..."},
        "8939": {"synopsis":"create directory sub-paths, recursively.\nEntry: hl = pointer to null-terminator; b = number of directory path segments (levels) to\ncreate; c = length of filename.\nExit: fc = 0, directory path created successfully, otherwise fc = 1.","comment":"directory separator at (hl)"},
        "8942": {"comment":"null-terminate directory path segment (level)"},
        "8946": {"comment":"if (pathlevel != 0) createpath(pathlevel, sep)"},
        "8950": {"comment":"sub-path couldn't be created..."},
        "8954": {"comment":"restore directory separator"},
        "8957": {"synopsis":"Creates one directory: opens the path at IY with GN_Opf in OP_DIR mode and frees the DOR\nhandle it returns. A directory that exists (RC_EXIS) or is in use (RC_USE) counts as\nsuccess.\nEntry: IY = pathname, terminated after the level to create; C = buffer length.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, DE, IX.\nKeeps: BC, HL.","comment":"preserve current level in B"},
        "8958": {"comment":"preserve length of scratch buffer in C"},
        "8959": {"comment":"preserve pointer to current separator"},
        "8962": {"comment":"local pointer (filename always paged in)"},
        "8964": {"comment":"HL points at start of filename"},
        "8965": {"comment":"DE points at scratch buffer"},
        "8968": {"comment":"mkdir pathname (returns DOR handle)"},
        "8975": {"comment":"in use (it exists)..."},
        "8979": {"comment":"already created..."},
        "8982": {"comment":"other error occurred"},
        "8986": {"comment":"free dor handle"},
        "8991": {"synopsis":"Create Directory Path.\n\nThe directory name must not contain wildcards (standard convention).\nHowever if a RAM device is not specified, it will automatically be included\n(the current) into the directory name.\n\nThe buffer of the directory name must have space enough to get itself expanded\nwith a device name (additional 6 bytes).\n\nThe filename pointer may not point in segment 2, since GN_FEX is unreliable\nin that segment.\n\nout, if successful:\nfc = 0, directory successfully created\n(hl) = filename may have been expanded\n\nout, if failed:\nfc = 1, unable to create directory\na = error code:\nRC_IVF, Invalid directory path name\nRC_USE, Directory in use\nRC_EXIS, Directory already exists\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Copyright (C) 1997\nEntry: bhl = pointer to null-terminated directory path name, (b = 0, means local).\nChanges: AF, IX.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"preserve original BC"},
        "8992": {"comment":"preserve original DE"},
        "8993": {"comment":"preserve original HL"},
        "8996": {"comment":"preserve original IY"},
        "8999": {"comment":"IY points at start of filename"},
        "9003": {"comment":"pointer to filename is local"},
        "9010": {"comment":"MS_Sx"},
        "9011": {"comment":"page filename into segment"},
        "9012": {"comment":"preserve old bank binding"},
        "9017": {"comment":"preserve error status..."},
        "9018": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "9033": {"synopsis":"Create the filename\nEntry: HL = pointer to directory path.","comment":"filename available in address space"},
        "9035": {"comment":"HL points at start of filename"},
        "9036": {"comment":"DE points at scratch buffer"},
        "9039": {"comment":"try to open directory path (DOR record)..."},
