        "10319": {"synopsis":"Opens f_SourceName with OpenFile (GN_Opf): as a DOR (OP_DOR) when bit 4 of f_CmdFlags is\nset, otherwise for reading (OP_IN). Stores IX in f_SourceHandle and A in f_SourceType, also\nafter an error.\nEntry: f_SourceName = name; f_CmdFlags.\nExit: Fc = 0, IX = handle; A = DOR type.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "10325": {"comment":"source is DOR?"},
        "10327": {"comment":"DOR info"},
        "10331": {"comment":"read"},
        "10344": {"synopsis":"Reads the source file name into f_SourceName at column 21, row 1 of the current window;\nfalls into InputLine.\nEntry: f_SourceName = the text to edit Exit, Error: as InputLine."},
        "10350": {"synopsis":"Lets the user edit a file name and checks it: shows the cursor, edits the buffer with GN_Sip\nat the given position (redrawing after RC_Susp), parses the result with GN_Prs, and shows a\nbad name with GN_Err. Ends through ToggleCrsr, which hides the cursor again.\nEntry: DE = buffer, holding the text to edit; B = column, C = row.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = key that ended the input; C = GN_Prs flags.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
