        "10819": {"comment":"!! nc?"},
        "10835": {"synopsis":"directory window"},
        "10911": {"comment":"Unsigned 16bit division"},
        "10959": {"synopsis":"scroll window down and clear the first line"},
        "10973": {"synopsis":"scroll window up and move to the last line"},
        "10987": {"synopsis":"Draws the whole Filer screen.\n1. Reads the filename match string (GetMatchString); clears f_NumDirEntries.\n2. Opens the command window with GN_Win and sets up the directory window.\n3. Prints the title: \"NM\" when the match string is not \"*\", \"DIRECTORY \" and the current\ndirectory, expanded with GN_Fex and compressed with GN_Fcm.\n4. If IX is 0, opens the current directory's DOR into f_CurrentDirHandle, freeing it again\nwhen it is not a device or a directory.\n5. Draws the directory window (DrawDirWindow) when there is a directory, then the command\nwindow, and the selector bar (ApplyReverse).\nEntry: IX = current directory DOR handle, or 0."},
        "11049": {"comment":"if match string is not \"*\" display \"NM\""},
        "11052": {"comment":"in left corner of dir window"},
        "11084": {"comment":"\".\""},
        "11101": {"comment":"get std. output"},
        "11111": {"comment":"compress to stdout"},
        "11116": {"comment":"reverse title"},
        "11181": {"synopsis":"End of function InitDisplay"},
        "11182": {"synopsis":"Zero-terminated \".\", the current directory. The byte before it (ParentDir_txt) makes \"..\".\nInitDisplay expands it to show the current path."},
        "11184": {"synopsis":"Draws the command window: selects and clears window 1, then prints up to 7 command names\nfrom f_SelectedCmd onwards, one a line, stopping at the last command.\nEntry: f_SelectedCmd."},
        "11202": {"comment":"send newline (CR/LF) to std. output"},
        "11213": {"synopsis":"Draws the directory window: selects and clears window 2, then prints up to 7 lines of 3\nmatching entries, starting with entry f_TopDirEntry (SkipBCMatches). When the top entry lies\npast the end, it is reset to 0 and the window drawn again. Sets f_NumDirEntries to the\nnumber shown.\nEntry: IX = directory DOR handle.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "11215": {"comment":"init and clear wd2"},
        "11237": {"comment":"TopDirEntry=0"},
        "11276": {"comment":"NumDirEntries=3*(7-C)+B"},
        "11289": {"synopsis":"Prints one line of up to 3 directory entries, starting with the current match: a bullet\narrow for a selected entry, the name padded to 16 characters (directories between PrntDir\ntoggles), and a space. FindMatch moves on to the next entry.\nEntry: IX = DOR of a matching entry, its name in f_StrBuffer.\nExit: B = number of entries printed; Fc = 0 when 3 were printed.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code when the entries ran out (B < 3)."},
        "11303": {"comment":"Print selection marker if needed"},
        "11308": {"comment":"bullet arrow right"},
        "11315": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11317": {"comment":"print files normally,"},
        "11320": {"comment":"dirs in tiny caps"},
        "11338": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11344": {"comment":"return 3-mod(B,3) in B"},
        "11351": {"synopsis":"Sends the VDU sequence 1, \"B\", which toggles bold; Print3Matches prints a directory name\nbetween two of them.\nEntry: none."},
        "11357": {"synopsis":"Print until ctrl char, max 16 bytes, fill rest with blanks\nEntry: hl = string.\nExit: hl = end of string."},
        "11365": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11372": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11377": {"synopsis":"Moves to match number BC of a directory: duplicates the directory DOR, takes its first child\nwith OS_Dor (DR_SON) and calls FindMatch BC + 1 times.\nEntry: IX = directory DOR handle (0 gives RC_Eof); BC = matches to skip.\nExit: Fc = 0, IX = DOR of the match, its name in f_StrBuffer.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (RC_Eof when the entries ran out).\nKeeps: BC."},
        "11390": {"comment":"new DOR"},
        "11392": {"comment":"get child DOR"},
        "11404": {"comment":"End Of File"},
        "11431": {"synopsis":"Calls FreeDOR (frees the DOR handle in IX if there is one), keeping AF.\nEntry: IX = DOR handle or 0.\nChanges: DE.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "11437": {"synopsis":"Finds the next directory entry whose name matches f_MatchString: steps to the next sibling\nwith OS_Dor (DR_SIB), unless bit 1 of f_Flags2 says to test the current DOR first, reads its\nname record into f_StrBuffer and matches it with GN_Wsm. Stores the minor type in\nf_SourceType.\nEntry: IX = DOR handle; f_Flags2 bit 1.\nExit: Fc = 0, IX = DOR of the match, its name in f_StrBuffer.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (no more entries).\nKeeps: BC."},
        "11443": {"comment":"continue from brother"},
        "11450": {"comment":"continue with this DOR"},
        "11454": {"comment":"get brother DOR"},
        "11458": {"comment":"minor type"},
        "11467": {"comment":"record type 'N' + buffer length to 17 bytes"},
        "11470": {"comment":"get DOR name record"},
        "11478": {"comment":"match filename segment to wildcard string"},
        "11481": {"comment":"not match, loop back"},
        "11485": {"synopsis":"Reads the current filename match string (OS_Nq, NQ_Fnm) and copies it to f_MatchString with\nCopyExtended.\nEntry: none."},
        "11488": {"comment":"get current filename match string"},
        "11496": {"synopsis":"Get command data\nEntry: a = command.\nExit: hl = command block address (flags byte, code word, name string).","comment":"CmdTable+2*a"},
        "11502": {"comment":"!! removable if table doesn't cross page boundary"},
        "11510": {"synopsis":"Print command string (in command window)\nEntry: hl = command block.\nExit: hl = next command block."},
        "11512": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11520": {"comment":"write string to std. output"},
        "11526": {"synopsis":"Draws the selector bar: switches reverse on, applies it over the selector's field with\nRemoveHighlight, and switches reverse off.\nEntry: f_ActiveWd; f_SelectorPos."},
        "11535": {"synopsis":"Applies the current attributes over the selector's field: 24 characters on row f_SelectorPos\nof the command window, or the 18 characters of entry f_SelectorPos in the directory window.\nWithout reverse set, this removes the highlight.\nEntry: f_ActiveWd (0 = command window); f_SelectorPos.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "11565": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to directory entry A: row A / 3, column 18 * (A mod 3).\nEntry: A = entry number.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "11571": {"comment":"HL/DE -> HL (DE=rem)"},
        "11588": {"synopsis":"End of function CrsrToPosA"},
        "11599": {"comment":"\"Yes\""},
        "11605": {"comment":"\"No \""},
        "11608": {"comment":"write string to std. output"},
        "11611": {"comment":"move to first char"},
        "11619": {"comment":"purge keyboard buffer"},
        "11621": {"comment":"read a byte from std. input"},
        "11656": {"synopsis":"Selects the entry under the selector: stores the path first when the list is empty\n(GetPath), reads the entry's name from the screen, allocates a 22 byte node from f_MemPool,\ncopies the name into it, queues it on the selected list, draws the bullet arrow, counts it\nin f_NumSelected and redraws the bar. An error is shown with GN_Err (RC_Room when 255 are\nselected).\nEntry: f_SelectorPos.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: IX."},
        "11661": {"comment":"!! use inc"},
        "11669": {"comment":"!! then dec"},
        "11686": {"comment":"Allocate memory"},
        "11690": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "11697": {"comment":"Bind memory into S1"},
        "11704": {"comment":"zero link"},
        "11711": {"comment":"alloc length?"},
        "11719": {"comment":"from (HL)"},
        "11724": {"comment":"restore S1 binding"},
        "11747": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "11751": {"synopsis":"Get path, copy it into SelectedList node"},
        "11763": {"comment":"device name length"},
        "11768": {"comment":"struct overhead"},
        "11777": {"comment":"Allocate memory"},
        "11781": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "11788": {"comment":"bind mem in S1"},
        "11793": {"comment":"zero link"},
        "11802": {"comment":"type=path"},
        "11804": {"comment":"from SourceName"},
        "11811": {"comment":"allocation length"},
        "11814": {"comment":"restore S1 binding"},
        "11820": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "11824": {"synopsis":"End of function GetPath"},
        "11845": {"comment":"Bind bank B in slot C"},
        "11861": {"synopsis":"Empties the selected-file list: frees every node on f_SelectedList through FreeSelNode and\nsets f_NumSelected to 0.\nOZ source name: EmptySelectedList.\nEntry: none.\nExit: f_SelectedList null; f_NumSelected = 0; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; S1 binding.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "11887": {"synopsis":"Remove all file selection marks in current display area, then remove cursor highlight\n(f_NumDirEntries) contains total visible entries in window, max 21 (3 * 7)"},
        "11892": {"comment":"none selected, exit"},
        "11897": {"comment":"total entries are <= 21, OK"},
        "11899": {"comment":"total entries are > 21, truncate!"},
        "11913": {"synopsis":"End of function RemoveSelMarks"},
        "11918": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "11921": {"synopsis":"Remove node BHL from list IY"},
        "11929": {"comment":"no more entries"},
        "11931": {"comment":"compare nodes"},
        "11943": {"comment":"not same node, try next"},
        "11954": {"comment":"found, bind it into S2"},
        "11956": {"comment":"for list removal"},
        "11958": {"comment":"fix high byte for S2"},
        "11967": {"comment":"DE=current, HL=node to remove"},
        "11968": {"comment":"copy link to remove from list"},
        "11975": {"comment":"restore S2"},
        "11976": {"comment":"bind node into S1 to free memory"},
        "11984": {"comment":"allocation size"},
        "11993": {"comment":"Free memory"},
        "11998": {"synopsis":"Reads the three-byte link at IY into CDE (bank in C).\nEntry: IY = a link (offset low, offset high, bank).\nExit: C = bank; DE = offset.\nChanges: C, DE."},
        "12008": {"synopsis":"End of function GetLinkCDE","comment":"return with Fc=1 if no files in list"},
        "12035": {"comment":"compare entry name with SourceName,"},
        "12037": {"comment":"loop back if not same"},
        "12041": {"comment":"name buffer"},
        "12050": {"comment":"name length"},
        "12059": {"comment":"ctrl char, matched"},
        "12084": {"comment":"name buffer"},
        "12088": {"comment":"compare max 17 bytes for match"},
        "12098": {"comment":"ctrl char, return match"},
        "12108": {"comment":"Fc=0"},
        "12112": {"synopsis":"End of function FindNodeByName\nFollow IY to next node"},
        "12120": {"comment":"no next, ret with Cf=1"},
        "12124": {"comment":"next into IY"},
        "12129": {"comment":"bind entry into S1"},
        "12130": {"comment":"ret wit Fc=0, B=bank, IY=new"},
        "12134": {"synopsis":"Reads the name of the directory entry under the selector from the screen. Moves to entry\nf_SelectorPos (CrsrToPosA), one column right, reads 16 characters with OS_Nq NQ_Rds into\nf_StrBuffer, then removes the spaces and zero-terminates it.\nOZ source name: GetSelectedDirEntry.\nEntry: f_SelectorPos = entry number in the directory window.\nExit: f_StrBuffer = the entry's name, zero-terminated; DE = its terminator; A = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "12140": {"comment":"cursor right"},
        "12142": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "12147": {"comment":"#bytes"},
        "12153": {"comment":"read text from the screen"},
        "12155": {"comment":"remove spaces from strbuffer"},
        "12175": {"synopsis":"Prints the right bullet arrow character (VDU 1,$F5) with OS_Pout.\nOZ source name: PrntRightBulletArrow.\nEntry: none."},
        "12177": {"comment":"Bullet arrow Right"},
        "12181": {"synopsis":"Clears the current window from the cursor to the end of the line (VDU 1,\"2C\",$FD).\nEntry: none."},
        "12189": {"synopsis":"Prints the prompt \"Name :\" at column 13, row 1 of the current window.\nEntry: none."},
        "12204": {"synopsis":"Prints the prompt \"New name :\" at column 9, row 3 of the current window.\nEntry: none."},
        "12223": {"synopsis":"Clear current window and reset line count"},
        "12240": {"synopsis":"Selects window 1, the Filer's commands window (VDU 1,\"2I1\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12248": {"synopsis":"Selects window 2, the Filer's directory window (VDU 1,\"2I2\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12256": {"synopsis":"Selects window 3, the window a command works in (VDU 1,\"2I3\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12264": {"synopsis":"Sets normal justification in the current window (VDU 1,\"2JN\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12272": {"synopsis":"Sets centre justification in the current window (VDU 1,\"2JC\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12280": {"synopsis":"Sends VDU 1,\"2.]\", which the screen driver passes to DC_Gen: it stops the output of the\ncurrent CLI going to the printer (sets CLIF_B_DISABLEPRT). PrntDotOpen undoes it.\nEntry: none."},
        "12288": {"synopsis":"Sends VDU 1,\"2.[\", which the screen driver passes to DC_Gen: it lets the output of the\ncurrent CLI go to the printer again (clears CLIF_B_DISABLEPRT).\nEntry: none."},
        "12296": {"synopsis":"Toggles the cursor of the current window (VDU 1,\"C\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12302": {"synopsis":"Toggles the tiny font and the capitals attribute (VDU 1,\"T\",1,\"L\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12310": {"synopsis":"Toggles underline (VDU 1,\"U\"), then falls into PrntReverse to toggle reverse video.\nEntry: none."},
        "12315": {"synopsis":"Toggles reverse video (VDU 1,\"R\").\nEntry: none."},
        "12321": {"synopsis":"Prints \" IN SLOT n\", n being the default File Card slot; DoCmd adds it to the title of a\ncommand whose block ends in 'S'.\nEntry: f_filecardslot = slot (0-3).\nChanges: AF."},
        "12341": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor of the current window to column B, row C (VDU 1,\"3@\",32+B,32+C).\nEntry: B = column; C = row.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "12349": {"comment":"' '"},
        "12351": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "12354": {"comment":"' '"},
        "12356": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "12360": {"synopsis":"Apply screen changes to next A-32 bytes"},
        "12366": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "12369": {"synopsis":"GN_Win block of the commands window, read by InitDisplay: byte $91 (@10010000 with window ID\n1), position word $0000, size word $0818, then the address of the banner text (cmds_banner)."},
        "12376": {"synopsis":"The commands window's banner, \"COMMANDS\", zero-terminated."},
        "12385": {"synopsis":"\"Yes\", zero-terminated: the answer GetYesNo shows for yes."},
        "12389": {"synopsis":"\"No \", zero-terminated and padded to the width of \"Yes\": the answer GetYesNo shows for no."},
        "12393": {"synopsis":"\" to \", zero-terminated: printed between the source and destination names of a command\n(DoCmd, TreeCopy)."},
        "12398": {"synopsis":"Table of 16 words: the command block of each Filer command, in the order of the MTH command\ncodes $21-$30: Catalogue files, Catalogue File Card, Save to File Card, Fetch from File\nCard, Copy, Rename, Erase, View, Select Directory, Select Device, Select File Card, Execute,\nCreate Directory, Create File Card, Tree copy and Name match. GetCmdData indexes it. A block\nis a flags byte, the handler's address and the name. Flags: bit 0 ask for a destination\nname; 1 display each file (with Confirm each file); 2 the handler does its own input, so\nDoCmd prompts for nothing; 3 ignore the selected files; 4 open the source as a DOR, not a\nfile; 5 page wait; 6 beep when done; 7 empty the selected list when done. DoCmd calls the\nhandler for each source file in turn; it returns Fc = 1, A = error code to stop, and with\nflag 3 set it is called once.","comment":"MTH command code $21"},
        "12400": {"comment":"MTH command code $22"},
        "12402": {"comment":"MTH command code $23"},
        "12404": {"comment":"MTH command code $24"},
        "12406": {"comment":"MTH command code $25"},
        "12408": {"comment":"MTH command code $26"},
        "12410": {"comment":"MTH command code $27"},
        "12412": {"comment":"MTH command code $28"},
        "12414": {"comment":"MTH command code $29"},
        "12416": {"comment":"MTH command code $2a"},
        "12418": {"comment":"MTH command code $2b"},
        "12420": {"comment":"MTH command code $2c"},
        "12422": {"comment":"MTH command code $2d"},
        "12424": {"comment":"MTH command code $2e"},
        "12426": {"comment":"MTH command code $2f"},
        "12428": {"comment":"MTH command code $30"},
        "12430": {"synopsis":"flags in first byte\nbit     mask                                    tcp cpy del cat sve ftc exe sdi mtc ren sde mkd EPR\n0       01      ask destination filename             X               X\n1       02      display each file                    X   X           X\n2       04                                       X           X       X        X   X       X   X   X\n3       08      ignore selected                  X                   X   X    X   X       X   X   X\n4       10      source is DOR                            X                            X\n5       20      page wait enable                             X                                    X\n6       40      beep when done                                   X\n7       80                                       X   X   X   X   X                    X           X"},
        "12443": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Copy \" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $83 (ask\ndestination, display each file, empty the selected list), the handler's address (Copy), then\nthe name \"Copy \" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12446": {"synopsis":"The name text of the Copy command block, \"Copy \", zero-terminated; TreeCopy also prints it\nbefore each file it copies."},
        "12452": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Erase \" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $92 (display\neach file, source as a DOR, empty the selected list), the handler's address (Erase), then\nthe name \"Erase \" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12462": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Catalogue files\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $A4\n(own input, page wait, empty the selected list), the handler's address (CatalogueFiles),\nthen the name \"Catalogue files\" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12481": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Save to File Card\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte\n$C2 (display each file, beep when done, empty the selected list), the handler's address\n(Save), then the name \"Save to File Card\" for the title bar, zero-terminated, followed by\n'S', which makes DoCmd append \" IN SLOT n\" (PrFcSlotNo) to the title."},
        "12503": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Fetch from File Card\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte\n$0D (ask destination, own input, ignore the selected files), the handler's address (Fetch),\nthen the name \"Fetch from File Card\" for the title bar, zero-terminated, followed by 'S',\nwhich makes DoCmd append \" IN SLOT n\" (PrFcSlotNo) to the title."},
        "12528": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Execute \" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $08 (ignore\nthe selected files), the handler's address (Execute), then the name \"Execute \" for the title\nbar, zero-terminated."},
        "12540": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Select Directory\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $0C\n(own input, ignore the selected files), the handler's address (SelectDir), then the name\n\"Select Directory\" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12560": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Name match\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $0C (own\ninput, ignore the selected files), the handler's address (NameMatch), then the name \"Name\nmatch\" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12574": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Rename \" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $90 (source\nas a DOR, empty the selected list), the handler's address (Rename), then the name \"Rename \"\nfor the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12585": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"View\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $80 (empty the\nselected list), the handler's address (View), then the name \"View\" for the title bar,\nzero-terminated."},
        "12593": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Select Device\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $0C\n(own input, ignore the selected files), the handler's address (SelectDevice), then the name\n\"Select Device\" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12610": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Select File Card\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $2C\n(own input, ignore the selected files, page wait), the handler's address (SelectFileCard),\nthen the name \"Select File Card\" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12630": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Create File Card\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $2C\n(own input, ignore the selected files, page wait), the handler's address (CreateFileCard),\nthen the name \"Create File Card\" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12650": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Create Directory\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte $0C\n(own input, ignore the selected files), the handler's address (CreateDir), then the name\n\"Create Directory\" for the title bar, zero-terminated."},
        "12670": {"synopsis":"Command block of the \"Catalogue File Card\" command, one of the CmdTable entries: flags byte\n$2C (own input, ignore the selected files, page wait), the handler's address\n(CatalogueEPROM), then the name \"Catalogue File Card\" for the title bar, zero-terminated,\nfollowed by 'S', which makes DoCmd append \" IN SLOT n\" (PrFcSlotNo) to the title."},
        "12694": {"synopsis":"Copy file resource specified in (f_SourceHandle) handle, to destination resource specified in (f_DestHandle).\nUse a 1K buffer on the system stack to block copy the file using OS_Mv (fast copy).\nEntry: None:.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1, A = RC_EOF: File copied successfully.; Fc = 1, A = RC_xxx, unexpected\nerror occurred.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.\nKeeps: IY."},
        "12699": {"comment":"get current stack pointer"},
        "12704": {"comment":"IY points at start of buffer"},
        "12706": {"comment":"1K byte buffer created..."},
        "12708": {"comment":"preserve original SP"},
        "12721": {"comment":"start of buffer"},
        "12725": {"comment":"copy block of bytes from handle IX to buffer"},
        "12732": {"comment":"an unexpected error occurred when copying from source..."},
        "12734": {"comment":"End Of File, loaded bytes < buffer size"},
        "12737": {"comment":"nothing was copied into buffer, return Fz = 1, A = RC_EOF, file copied successfully"},
        "12739": {"comment":"number of bytes to copy from buffer to destination"},
        "12740": {"comment":"(start of buffer)"},
        "12741": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "12746": {"comment":"write block (in buffer) to handle IX"},
        "12748": {"comment":"done successfully, get another block from source..."},
        "12750": {"comment":"abnormal error occurred, Fc = 1, A = RC_xxx"},
        "12755": {"comment":"point at old SP address"},
        "12758": {"comment":"restored original Stack"},
        "12762": {"synopsis":"The Select Device command (CmdTable): asks for a device name, showing the current one, and\nmakes it the current device.\n1. Copies the current device into f_SourceName (GetDev) and edits it (InputSrcName).\n2. Parses it with GN_Pfs. If that fails with A = 9 (RC_Eof; the source says an extension and\n\"/.\" were used), sets the device to the text anyway (OS_Sp, SP_Dev) and asks again.\n3. Accepts only a name with the device and extension flags and no others, whose DOR (GN_Opf,\nOP_DOR) is a device (Dm_Dev); then sets it with OS_Sp SP_Dev, empties f_SourceName and calls\nChgDir. Anything else is RC_Ivf. An error is shown with GN_Err; after RC_Susp the name is\nasked again. Leaves through ToggleCrsr.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1; A = RC_Esc when ESC was pressed, else the error already shown."},
        "12785": {"comment":"parse filename segment"},
        "12790": {"comment":"extension used and  \"/.\" used"},
        "12801": {"comment":"specify (set) parameter"},
        "12827": {"comment":"open - BHL=name, A=mode, DE=exp. name buffer, C=buflen"},
        "12845": {"comment":"specify (set) parameter"},
        "12856": {"comment":"Invalid filename"},
        "12858": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "12861": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "12869": {"synopsis":"End of function SelectDevice\nUser selects File Card by using keys 0-3 or using <>J to toggle between available\nslots.\nEntry: (f_filecardslot).\nExit: Selected File Card slot, stored in (f_filecardslot)."},
        "12872": {"synopsis":"Lets the user choose a File Card slot. SelectFileCard falls into it with its own prompt;\nCreateFileCard calls it with another. Prints the prompt and the help line, then shows the\nslot number (f_filecardslot) under the cursor and reads keys (GetKey): 0-3 choose that slot\nwhen it holds a flash chip (checkflash) or no RAM card (checkram); <>J (LF) moves to the\nnext such slot, wrapping from 3 to 0; ENTER accepts.\nEntry: HL = prompt text, zero-terminated; f_filecardslot = slot shown first.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = IN_ENT; f_filecardslot = the chosen slot.\nError: Fc = 1; A = RC_Esc when ESC was pressed."},
        "12879": {"comment":"get current VDU cursor for current window"},
        "12881": {"comment":"put VDU cursor at (X,Y) = (C,B)"},
        "12889": {"comment":"display the pre-selected destination file card."},
        "12893": {"comment":"put blinking cursor over slot number of device"},
        "12898": {"comment":"user aborted with ESC"},
        "12901": {"comment":"user has selected a file card..."},
        "12904": {"comment":"<>J"},
        "12912": {"comment":"only \"0\" to \"3\" allowed"},
        "12916": {"comment":"check if there is a flash chip in slot X"},
        "12919": {"comment":"found it, register as selected device"},
        "12924": {"comment":"there's a RAM card in selected slot, find a non-RAM card slot.."},
        "12926": {"comment":"and let it be displayed."},
        "12933": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: toggle_device_loop."},
        "12937": {"comment":"scan slots 0 - 3"},
        "12939": {"comment":"check if there is a flash chip in slot X"},
        "12942": {"comment":"found it, register as selected device"},
        "12944": {"comment":"check if there's a RAM card in selected slot A"},
        "12947": {"comment":"This slot contains a RAM card, check next slot"},
        "12949": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: possible_filecard."},
        "12952": {"comment":"toggle was achieved, get back to main input loop.."},
        "12957": {"comment":"toggle was not possible, get back to main loop"},
        "12963": {"synopsis":"Asks whether slot A holds a flash chip (OS_Fep, FEP_CDID).\nEntry: A = slot.\nExit: Fc = 0 when a flash chip was identified, Fc = 1 when not; A = slot.\nKeeps: A, BC."},
        "12973": {"synopsis":"Asks whether slot A holds RAM (OS_Nq, Nq_Mfp); the error code is ignored.\nEntry: A = slot.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the slot has RAM, Fc = 1 when not; A = E = slot.\nKeeps: A, BC, D."},
        "12974": {"comment":"preserve A (current slot number)"},
        "12979": {"comment":"check if there's a RAM card in selected slot A"},
        "12981": {"comment":"returns Fc = 1, if no RAM in slot..."},
        "12982": {"comment":"(ignore RC_ error code)"},
        "12985": {"synopsis":"The Select File Card prompt, \"Select slot for default File Card\", zero-terminated;\nSelectFileCard passes it to SelectSlotPrompt."},
        "13019": {"synopsis":"Init slot selection menu window with dynamic prompt text in HL\nOZ source name: PrntSelectSlotPrompt."},
        "13097": {"synopsis":"Reads a key with OS_In for SelectSlotPrompt; a zero byte (the prefix of an extended key) is\nskipped.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0; A = key code. Another OS_In error than RC_Esc also comes back with Fc = 0 and\nA = the error code.\nError: Fc = 1; A = RC_Esc.","comment":"get another device slot number from user"},
        "13103": {"comment":"user aborted selection"},
        "13108": {"synopsis":"Create or re-format File Card by using keys 0-3 or using <>J to toggle between available\nslots.\nEntry: (f_filecardslot).\nExit: Selected File Card slot, stored in (f_filecardslot)."},
        "13114": {"comment":"user aborted slot selection with ESC..."},
        "13124": {"comment":"no file area found in slot C when checking for files."},
        "13128": {"comment":"no files in file area?"},
        "13129": {"comment":"yes, just return - no need to re-format.."},
        "13181": {"comment":"user aborted command with ESC..."},
        "13183": {"comment":"user selected \"No\" to re-format existing file card contents"},
        "13190": {"comment":"try to create file area in slot C and return error, if any."},
        "13227": {"synopsis":"The Create File Card prompt, \"Select slot to create or re-format File Card\",\nzero-terminated; CreateFileCard passes it to SelectSlotPrompt."},
        "13272": {"synopsis":"The Erase command's handler (CmdTable), called by DoCmd for each source file: frees the\nsource DOR (CloseSource) and deletes the file named in f_SourceName with GN_Del.\nEntry: f_SourceName = expanded file name; f_SourceHandle = its DOR handle (or 0).\nExit: Fc = 0; f_SourceHandle = IX after GN_Del.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code from GN_Del."},
        "13280": {"comment":"delete file"},
        "13288": {"synopsis":"End of function Erase"},
        "13299": {"comment":"preserve slot number..."},
        "13302": {"comment":"File Eprom Card or area available in slot C?"},
        "13312": {"comment":"no file area!"},
        "13318": {"comment":"Empty file area..."},
        "13320": {"comment":"ignore deleted files..."},
        "13329": {"comment":"Get filename of entry into local f_SourceName variable"},
        "13333": {"comment":"write filename to std. output"},
        "13338": {"comment":"preserve pointer to current file entry while waiting for end user.."},
        "13339": {"comment":"Page Wait, of full screen"},
        "13344": {"comment":"act on possible system pre-emption..."},
        "13350": {"comment":"display next file entry name (if it is not a deleted file...)"},
        "13352": {"comment":"Reached last entry..."},
        "13363": {"synopsis":"The View command's handler (CmdTable): closes the source handle, checks that f_SourceName is\na file (ValidateFileType), opens it for reading and shows it as a hex and ASCII dump\n(ViewFile), then closes it.\nEntry: f_SourceName = expanded file name.\nExit: the file closed again (CloseSource).\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code (RC_Ftm when it is not a file)."},
        "13370": {"comment":"file not found or wrong type..."},
        "13390": {"synopsis":"The Save to File Card command's handler (CmdTable), called for each source file: closes the\nsource handle, checks that f_SourceName is a file (ValidateFileType) and writes it into the\nfile area of the default slot with OS_Epr EP_NewFile.\nEntry: f_SourceName = expanded file name; f_filecardslot = slot.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code (RC_Ftm when it is not a file, else from OS_Epr)."},
        "13397": {"comment":"file not found or wrong type..."},
        "13406": {"comment":"default slot of file area to save file in"},
        "13409": {"comment":"blow RAM file to Flash or UV Eprom in slot C"},
        "13413": {"synopsis":"End of function Save"},
        "13420": {"comment":"copy src to dest"},
        "13450": {"comment":"write"},
        "13467": {"comment":"search for filename in default File area..."},
        "13476": {"comment":"signal \"not found\""},
        "13477": {"comment":"found a match"},
