        "13914": {"synopsis":"Asks for the name of an existing directory or device, for TreeCopy. Edits the buffer\n(InputLine), expands it in place (ExpandFname) and opens its DOR (OpenFile, OP_DOR); the\ntype must be Dm_Dev or Dn_Dir, else RC_Ftm. An error other than RC_Esc is shown with GN_Err,\nand after RC_Susp the input starts again.\nEntry: DE = name buffer (NBUFSIZE); B = column, C = row of the input.\nExit: Fc = 0; buffer = the expanded name.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code (RC_Esc not shown).\nKeeps: BC, DE."},
        "13926": {"comment":"DOR information"},
        "13944": {"comment":"File Type Mismatch"},
        "13951": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "13957": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "13966": {"synopsis":"Finds the end of a file name: moves HL to its first byte below $21.\nEntry: HL = name.\nExit: HL = the terminator; A = it; Fc = 1.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "13967": {"comment":"loop unti ctrl char found"},
        "13973": {"synopsis":"The Create Directory command (CmdTable): asks for a name in an empty input line and creates\nthe directory by opening it with OP_DIR (OpenFile), then frees the handle (FreeDOR). An\nerror other than RC_Esc is shown with GN_Err; after RC_Susp the name is asked again. Leaves\nthrough ToggleCrsr.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code (RC_Esc when ESC was pressed)."},
        "13985": {"comment":"Escape condition (e.g. ESC pressed)"},
        "13990": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "13993": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "14016": {"synopsis":"The Catalogue files command (CmdTable): lists files with their dates and sizes.\n1. With no files selected, asks for a name (an empty one becomes \"*\"), expands it and opens\na wildcard handler (GN_Opw, forward scan, full path).\n2. Takes each match (GN_Wfn), or each selected file (GetNextSelected), counts its segments\n(GN_Prs) and indents it by one space per segment after the first.\n3. Opens its DOR: a file is printed by CatFile, anything else by its name; then a new line\nwith page wait (PntLF_pagewait).\n4. Closes the wildcard handler at the end (RC_Eof) or on an error; an error other than\nRC_Esc is shown with GN_Err, and after RC_Susp the name is asked again.\nEntry: f_NumSelected, f_SelectedList.\nExit: Fc = 0 when the list ended.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code (RC_Esc when ESC was pressed)."},
        "14045": {"comment":"system input line routine"},
        "14050": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "14059": {"comment":"if buffer is empty, use \"*\""},
        "14068": {"comment":"null-terminate string"},
        "14075": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "14078": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "14091": {"comment":"forward scan, full path"},
        "14096": {"comment":"open wildcard handler"},
        "14133": {"comment":"get next filename match from wc.handler"},
        "14148": {"comment":"close wildcard handler"},
        "14172": {"comment":"parse filename"},
        "14175": {"comment":"#segments"},
        "14182": {"comment":"get DOR info"},
        "14197": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "14213": {"comment":"write string to std. output"},
        "14240": {"synopsis":"Prints one line of the catalogue for a file: its name (N record, PrntStr16), its creation\nand update dates (C and U records, GN_Sdo) and its size (X record, GN_Pdn), separated by\nspaces. The records are read into a 17-byte buffer on the stack (ReadSrcRecord); without an\nX record the size is left out.\nEntry: f_SourceHandle = the file's DOR handle.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "14248": {"comment":"get N record"},
        "14256": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "14261": {"comment":"get C record"},
        "14264": {"comment":"convert real time to time to elapse"},
        "14269": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "14274": {"comment":"get U record"},
        "14277": {"comment":"convert real time to time to elapse"},
        "14282": {"comment":"write a byte to std. output"},
        "14287": {"comment":"get X record"},
        "14295": {"comment":"enquire (fetch) parameter"},
        "14302": {"comment":"Integer to ASCII conversion"},
        "14311": {"synopsis":"Read source DOR record into stack buffer\nSet BC before calling"},
        "14323": {"comment":"read DOR record"},
        "14332": {"comment":"command window, exit"},
        "14353": {"comment":"expand a filename"},
        "14363": {"comment":"DOR info"},
        "14371": {"comment":"dir"},
        "14389": {"comment":"command window"},
        "14408": {"synopsis":"The Select Directory command (CmdTable): asks for a directory, showing the current one\n(GetDir), then checks it and makes it current (falls into ChgDir). In ChgDir: an empty name\ngoes straight to setting it; otherwise the name's DOR (OpenFile, OP_DOR) must be a directory\nor device, else RC_Ftm. An error is shown with GN_Err; after RC_Susp the name is asked\nagain. Then VerifiedChDir sets it.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code (RC_Esc when ESC was pressed)."},
        "14434": {"comment":"system input line routine"},
        "14442": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "14453": {"synopsis":"Check that (HL) is directory or device"},
        "14460": {"comment":"DOR info"},
        "14478": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "14481": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "14488": {"synopsis":"Entry inside ChgDir (SelectDir), also called by ChDir: sets the current directory and, when\nfiles are selected, records it in the selected list.\n1. Parses f_SourceName with GN_Pfs and ignores the flags (the source asks what this does and\ncalls it a probable bug); GN_Pfs leaves HL at the end of the first segment.\n2. Sets the current directory from the text at HL (OS_Sp, SP_Dir); ChgDir's empty name\nenters here at this step.\n3. With files selected, walks to the last node of f_SelectedList; a path node there (type 1)\nis freed (FreeSelNode). Then adds the current path as a new node (GetPath).\nEntry: f_SourceName = expanded directory name.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"!! what is this trying to do?"},
        "14490": {"comment":"!! probable bug"},
        "14493": {"comment":"!! should check for some A flags?"},
        "14499": {"comment":"Set current directory"},
        "14501": {"comment":"exit if none selected"},
        "14507": {"comment":"count entries in list"},
        "14528": {"comment":"type not 1"},
        "14545": {"synopsis":"The Name match command (CmdTable): edits the current name match string (OS_Nq, NQ_Fnm) and\nsets the new one (OS_Sp, SP_Fnm). The text must parse as one name segment (GN_Pfs) without\ndirectory or device parts (flags $7C), else RC_Ivf. An error other than RC_Esc is shown with\nGN_Err; after RC_Susp the input starts again. Leaves through ToggleCrsr.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code (RC_Esc when ESC was pressed)."},
        "14551": {"comment":"enquire (fetch) parameter"},
        "14564": {"comment":"Escape condition (e.g. ESC pressed)"},
        "14569": {"comment":"Display an interactive error box"},
        "14572": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "14584": {"comment":"parse filename segment"},
        "14591": {"comment":"Invalid filename"},
        "14601": {"comment":"specify (set) parameter"},
        "14607": {"synopsis":"End of function NameMatch"},
        "14621": {"comment":"send newline (CR/LF) to std. output"},
        "14625": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key at the end of a page of output when that is allowed: clears the line count\n(f_OutLnCnt) and, when the output is not teed (the NQ_Tot handle is 0) and the command\nenables page wait (f_CmdFlags bit 5), calls OS_Sr SR_PWT, repeating it after RC_Susp.\nEntry: f_CmdFlags.\nExit: Fc = 0; f_OutLnCnt = 0.\nError: Fc = 1; A = error code from SR_PWT (RC_Esc when ESC was pressed).\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: HL, IX."},
        "14635": {"comment":"get output-T handle"},
        "14642": {"comment":"output redirected, no page wait"},
        "14647": {"comment":"page wait enable?"},
        "14649": {"comment":"no pw for this command"},
        "14653": {"comment":"Page wait"},
        "14657": {"comment":"Suspicion of pre-emption"},
        "14664": {"synopsis":"End of function MayPageWait"},
        "14678": {"comment":"type=1?"},
        "14685": {"comment":"copy node name to SourceName"},
        "14705": {"comment":"add '/ into Sourcename if it doesn't"},
        "14706": {"comment":"end with that yet"},
        "14729": {"comment":"find end of SourceName"},
        "14740": {"comment":"point DE after last '/'"},
        "14747": {"comment":"append name from node"},
        "14766": {"synopsis":"Removes the first node of the selected list and frees it (GetLinkBHL, FreeSelNode). It sits\ninside GetNextSelected's code, which calls it and branches around it.\nEntry: f_SelectedList not empty.\nExit: IY = f_SelectedList.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IY; S1 binding."},
        "14797": {"comment":"get next filename match from wc.handler"},
        "14828": {"synopsis":"Prints the prompts \"Source :\" at column 11, row 1 and \"Destination :\" at column 6, row 3,\nthen falls into ResetSrcDestName.\nEntry: none.\nExit: f_SourceName and f_DestName empty; A = 0."},
        "14862": {"synopsis":"Empties f_SourceName and f_DestName by zeroing their first bytes.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = 0.\nChanges: A."},
        "14870": {"synopsis":"Tests whether the three-byte link at IY is null.\nEntry: IY = a link.\nExit: Fz = 1 when it is null; A = OR of its bytes.\nChanges: AF."},
        "14880": {"synopsis":"Reads the three-byte link at IY into BHL (bank in B).\nEntry: IY = a link (offset low, offset high, bank).\nExit: B = bank; HL = offset.\nChanges: B, HL."},
        "14890": {"synopsis":"DE=name","comment":"re-use name as expanded name buffer"},
        "14895": {"comment":"expand a filename"},
        "14899": {"synopsis":"HL=name, A=mode","comment":"re-use name as expanded name buffer"},
        "14908": {"synopsis":"return Fc=0, Fz=1, A=DN_Fil, if (f_SourceName) name is an existing file\nreturn Fc=1, A=error code, if file not found or is of wrong type.."},
