        "15061": {"comment":"in main input loop."},
        "15062": {"synopsis":"The key loop of the View command's dump (ViewFile): sets up the windows and shows the first\n128 bytes (ResetCurPos, InitView), then moves the cursor on each key (VFGetKey, which works\nout the CRC-32 while no key is pressed). Keys: code $20 (the source says TAB) switches\nbetween the hex and ASCII cursor; left and right move a byte; up and down a line of 16\nbytes, scrolling at the edges; SHIFT up and down ($31, $32) 128 bytes; DIAMOND up and down\ngo to the start and the end of the file.\nEntry: f_SourceHandle open on the file; vf_fptr, vf_fsize set (ViewFile).\nExit: Fc = 1; A = RC_Esc when ESC was pressed.","comment":"intialise cursor pos. in window"},
