        "15507": {"comment":"add rel. horisontal start in window"},
        "15508": {"comment":"CX position in window ready."},
        "15512": {"comment":"get CY"},
        "15513": {"comment":"display cursor at CX,CY"},
        "15520": {"synopsis":"Load 128 bytes (or less) from file, using current file pointer (vf_fptr),\ninto view buffer and reset DE to point at start of buffer."},
        "15525": {"comment":"handle of open file for viewing"},
        "15529": {"comment":"set file pointer to base of view buffer, defined by (vf_fptr)"},
        "15535": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "15540": {"comment":"fetch 128 bytes (or less!) from file and dump into view buffer"},
        "15542": {"comment":"EOF is handled automatically via cursor movement..."},
        "15544": {"synopsis":"Dump 128 bytes in Hex and ASCII format from current buffer address in DE\nDE will point +128 bytes on return","comment":"after return, DE points at start of buffer"},
        "15549": {"comment":"clear view buffer window"},
        "15551": {"comment":"display 8 x 16 byte lines of hex dump"},
        "15554": {"comment":"dump 1 line (16 bytes)"},
        "15561": {"synopsis":"Dump 16 bytes in Hex and ASCII format from current address in DE\nDE will point +16 (or less if EOF) of view buffer bytes on return.\n\nAF, B, DE, L  different on return"},
        "15564": {"comment":"the DE dump offset is already beyond EOF.."},
        "15566": {"comment":"add base file pointer (BC = converted offset of DE)"},
        "15576": {"comment":"adjust overflow of added DE offset.."},
        "15577": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: disp_highbyte_int."},
        "15582": {"comment":"display 16bit hex"},
        "15583": {"comment":"- the current dump address"},
        "15594": {"comment":"save a copy for ASCII dump"},
        "15602": {"comment":"also display Ascii section... before EOF is reached.."},
        "15604": {"comment":"get byte at true dump address"},
        "15605": {"comment":"dump address ready for next fetch"},
        "15606": {"comment":"display in 8bit HEX"},
        "15619": {"comment":"now dump same bytes in ASCII format"},
        "15623": {"comment":"prepare VDU cursor for Ascii section..."},
        "15636": {"comment":"get byte at true dump address"},
        "15637": {"comment":"dump address ready for next fetch"},
        "15648": {"comment":"display '.' if A = [0;31] [128;255]"},
        "15659": {"synopsis":"Validate that DE(in) (ptr to current line of buffer to display) is not beyond EOF\nreturn offset from start of buffer in BC (0 - X)."},
        "15661": {"comment":"before displaying dump, calculate the file"},
        "15664": {"comment":"offset to be displayed first in left side"},
        "15666": {"comment":"get display offset from top of buffer"},
        "15674": {"comment":"if Fc = 1, then DE offset is beyond EOF!"},
        "15676": {"synopsis":"Setup view file windows and pre-load buffer with start of file."},
        "15681": {"comment":"begin dump from start of file"},
        "15688": {"comment":"then display the cursor"},
        "15694": {"synopsis":"Set cursor at X,Y position in dump file window\n\nRegister status after return:\n..BCDEHL/IXIY  same\nAF....../....  different\nEntry: C,B = (X,Y)."},
        "15698": {"comment":"VDU 1,'3','@',32+C,32+B"},
        "15715": {"synopsis":"Converts an ASCII hex digit to its value: a code below '@' has 48 subtracted, any other 55.\nIt does not check the digit. Nothing in the Filer calls it.\nEntry: A = '0'-'9' or 'A'-'F'.\nExit: A = 0-15.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"digit >= \"A\"?"},
        "15717": {"comment":"digit is in interval \"A\" - \"F\""},
        "15719": {"comment":"digit is in interval \"0\" - \"9\""},
        "15722": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: hex_alpha."},
        "15725": {"synopsis":"INTEGER to HEX conversion\nHL(in) = integer to be converted to an ASCII HEX string\nFc = 1 convert 16 bit integer, otherwise byte integer\n\nPrints the string to the current window\n\nRegister status after return:\n\nAFBCDEHL/IXIY  same\n......../....  different"},
        "15731": {"comment":"NC = display only a byte"},
        "15743": {"comment":"string sent..."},
        "15753": {"comment":"same as 'IntHexDisp_H', but with a"},
        "15755": {"comment":"trailing 'H' hex identifier..."},
        "15759": {"synopsis":"INTEGER to HEX conversion\nHL(in) = integer to be converted to an ASCII HEX string\nFc = 1 convert 16 bit integer, otherwise byte integer\n\nReturns ASCII representation in DEBC, e.g. '3FFF' -> D='3', E='F', B='F', C='F'\n(8 bit ASCII only in BC)\n\nRegister status after return:\n\nAF....HL/IXIY  same\n..BCDE../....  different"},
        "15760": {"comment":"convert only byte"},
        "15768": {"comment":"DE = low byte ASCII"},
        "15776": {"synopsis":"byte in A, will be returned in ASCII form in DE"},
        "15777": {"comment":"copy of A"},
        "15784": {"comment":"high nibble of H"},
        "15791": {"comment":"low nibble of A"},
        "15799": {"synopsis":"A(in) = 4 bit integer value, A(out) = ASCII HEX byte"},
        "15810": {"synopsis":"The 16 hex digit characters \"0123456789ABCDEF\", indexed by CalcHexNibble."},
        "15826": {"synopsis":"Validate that Increase file pointer at (vf_fptr) with BC bytes\ndoesn't go beyond end of file. Returns Fc = 1, if \"overflow\"\nOZ source name: ValidateIncreaseFptr."},
        "15829": {"comment":"offset is from 0, so +1 to convert offset 0 = 1st byte of file"},
        "15830": {"comment":"get current file pointer (base of buffer)"},
        "15840": {"comment":"adjust overflow for 24bit adress"},
        "15841": {"comment":"CDE = vf_fptr + BC(in)"},
        "15847": {"comment":"(vf_fptr + BC(in)) > vf_fptr + BC(in)?"},
        "15850": {"comment":"return Fc = 1, if overflow..."},
        "15855": {"synopsis":"Increase file pointer at (vf_fptr) with BC bytes"},
        "15857": {"comment":"get current file pointer (base of buffer)"},
        "15869": {"comment":"adjust overflow for 24bit adress"},
        "15873": {"synopsis":"Validate that Decrease file pointer at (vf_fptr) with BC bytes\ndoesn't go beyond start of file.\nReturns Fc = 1, if overflow\nOZ source name: ValidateDecreaseFptr."},
        "15874": {"comment":"get current file pointer (base of buffer)"},
        "15883": {"comment":"adjust overflow for 24bit adress (add carry with B always = 0)"},
        "15884": {"comment":"and Fc = 1, if original BC offset goes beyond Start of file.."},
        "15886": {"synopsis":"Decrease file pointer at (vf_fptr) with BC bytes"},
        "15891": {"comment":"remove RET.."},
        "15892": {"comment":"BC decrease goes beyound start of file..."},
        "15897": {"comment":"get current file pointer (base of buffer)"},
        "15911": {"comment":"adjust overflow for 24bit adress"},
        "15915": {"synopsis":"Calculate CRC-32 of current viewed file, in chunks of 256 bytes\nper call of this function.\n\nA temporary handle (f_TmpFileHandle) refers to the file being\nprocessed. Once the file is completed, the CRC-32 is displayed\nand file closed.\n\nFuture calls to this function exits immediately (handle = 0)"},
        "15926": {"comment":"CRC-32 already processed..."},
        "15930": {"comment":"temp CRC-32 buffer, NBUFSIZE"},
        "15936": {"comment":"use Crc-32 from (f_crc32), initially FFFFFFFFh"},
        "15939": {"comment":"process CRC-32 of Open file, partially"},
        "15946": {"comment":"updated CRC-32"},
        "15950": {"comment":"partly scanned CRC-32 of a block of the file"},
        "15954": {"comment":"select info window, \"3\""},
        "15958": {"comment":"use Tiny font"},
        "15960": {"comment":"VDU Cursor at (8,1)"},
        "15970": {"comment":"display high-word of CRC-32"},
        "15976": {"comment":"display low-word of CRC-32"},
        "15981": {"comment":"select dump window, \"2\""},
        "15986": {"comment":"CRC-32 file scanning completed."},
        "15992": {"comment":"File processing done, OS_Tin now waits for key press"},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"Draws the View command's screen: defines window 2 for the dump (column 1, 73 by 8) and\nwindow 3 for the information panel (column 76, 16 by 8), prints the \"VIEW FILE\" banner, the\nCRC-32 caption, a divider and the key help (start/end, page, cursor, hex/ASCII, quit), then\nselects and clears window 2. Called by InitView.\nEntry: none."},
        "16002": {"comment":"Dump window"},
        "16011": {"comment":"Dump Info window"},
        "16020": {"comment":"select info window"},
        "16024": {"comment":"Tiny & reverse applied at top line"},
        "16033": {"comment":"Cursor at top left corner - Display banner centre justified"},
        "16051": {"comment":"normal justification"},
        "16086": {"comment":"divider line"},
        "16229": {"comment":"select & clear window '2' for dump output"}
      }
    },
