      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"Entry point for ugly popdown..."},
        "5": {"synopsis":"FlashStore Error Handler"},
        "20": {"comment":"acknowledge ESC detection"},
        "24": {"comment":"all other RC errors are returned to caller"},
        "27": {"comment":"perform suicide, focus to Index..."},
        "31": {"synopsis":"On entry, FlashStore has 7 * 256 (1.5K) bytes contigous memory from $2000...","comment":"IX points at information block from OZ"},
        "34": {"comment":"get end page+1 of contiguous RAM"},
        "36": {"comment":"end page OK, RAM allocated..."},
        "38": {"comment":"No Room for FlashStore, return to Index"},
        "40": {"comment":"FlashStore suicide..."},
        "42": {"comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "47": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "52": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "58": {"comment":"display only active files in file area (default)"},
        "64": {"comment":"enable ESC detection"},
        "71": {"comment":"then install Error Handler..."},
        "73": {"comment":"Get the default RAM device slot number from the system Panel"},
        "81": {"comment":"define default slot"},
        "84": {"comment":"user selects a File Eprom Area in one of the ext. slots."},
        "87": {"comment":"no File Area available, or Flash didn't have write support in found slot"},
        "90": {"comment":"user aborted"},
        "93": {"comment":"get watermark of current slot"},
        "96": {"comment":"initialize File Bar to first active file in File Area"},
        "99": {"comment":"just clear whole window area available"},
        "103": {"comment":"bar placed in menu bar by default"},
        "108": {"comment":"Display menu bar initially at top line of command window"},
        "114": {"comment":"main menu aborted, leave popdown..."},
        "116": {"synopsis":"FlashStore's main command loop. It draws the command and file windows and the right-hand\nwindow (file card statistics when the bar is in the menu window, browse help when it is in\nthe file window), pushes its own address as the return address of every command, and then\nreads keys until ESC leaves the application.\n1. Shows the active bar (DisplBar), reads a key (rdch) and removes the bar again; a read\nerror retries.\n2. Polls the current slot's file card watermark (PollFileCardWatermark); when the file area\ndisappeared (Fc = 1) or changed (Fz = 1) it redraws the command and file windows and the\nstatistics.\n3. Dispatches the key: ESC jumps to suicide; the command shortcuts (catalogue, save, fetch,\nbackup, restore, format, select card, erase, default RAM, file view, file area copy) jump to\ntheir commands; the cursor keys move the menu bar (rows 1 to 7, wrapping) or the file bar;\nleft and right switch between the menu and file windows; ENTER (or 'F') runs the menu bar's\ncommand or fetches the selected file; DEL or 'D' marks a file deleted, 'C' copies, 'V' views\na file and 'M' views bank memory. Other keys are ignored.\nEntry: (MenuBarPosn), (barMode), (curslot) set up by the initialisation.\nExit: never returns to its caller while running; ESC leaves through suicide."},
        "126": {"comment":"cursor in menu window: right hand side window displays File statistics"},
        "130": {"comment":"cursor in file window: right hand side window displays Browse help"},
        "136": {"comment":"return address for functions..."},
        "152": {"comment":"same card still available in current slot?"},
        "161": {"comment":"file area disappeared, redraw file window"},
        "167": {"comment":"file area changed, redraw file window"},
        "181": {"comment":"Catalogue file (trad. listing of files)"},
        "184": {"comment":"Save Files to File Card"},
        "189": {"comment":"Fetch File from File Card"},
        "194": {"comment":"Backup RAM Card"},
        "199": {"comment":"Restore Files"},
        "204": {"comment":"Format File Area"},
        "209": {"comment":"Select Card"},
        "214": {"comment":"File Erase"},
        "219": {"comment":"Select RAM Device"},
        "224": {"comment":"Change File View"},
        "229": {"comment":"File Area Copy"},
        "239": {"comment":"no shortcut cmd, ENTER ?"},
        "244": {"comment":"Cursor Down ?"},
        "249": {"comment":"Cursor Up ?"},
        "254": {"comment":"<> Cursor Up ?"},
        "258": {"comment":"<> Cursor Down?"},
        "262": {"comment":"SHIFT Up?"},
        "266": {"comment":"SHIFT Down?"},
        "270": {"comment":"Cursor Left ?"},
        "274": {"comment":"Cursor Right ?"},
        "281": {"comment":"press 'D' (alternative to DEL) to mark file as deleted"},
        "286": {"comment":"press 'C' to copy file entry to another file area"},
        "291": {"comment":"press 'F' (alternative to ENTER) to fetch a file"},
        "296": {"comment":"press 'V' to view a file"},
        "303": {"comment":"press 'M' to view memory contents"},
        "306": {"comment":"ignore keypress, get another..."},
        "315": {"comment":"indicate that cursor has moved to menu window"},
        "318": {"comment":"right hand side window displays File Card stats"},
        "324": {"comment":"(A)BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "329": {"comment":"no files to browse..."},
        "334": {"comment":"indicate that cursor has moved to file window"},
        "337": {"comment":"right hand side window displays Browse help"},
        "346": {"comment":"<>Up no effect in main menu"},
        "358": {"comment":"<>DWN no effect in main menu"},
        "370": {"comment":"SHIFT UP no effect in main menu"},
        "382": {"comment":"SHIFT DWN no effect in main menu"},
        "396": {"comment":"get Y position of menu bar"},
        "399": {"comment":"has m.bar already reached bottom?"},
        "404": {"comment":"update new m.bar position"},
        "407": {"comment":"display new m.bar position"},
        "429": {"comment":"get Y position of menu bar"},
        "432": {"comment":"has m.bar already reached top?"},
        "437": {"comment":"update new m.bar position"},
        "440": {"comment":"display new m.bar position"},
        "457": {"comment":"'C' key pressed - copy file to another file area"},
        "460": {"comment":"command only works when cursor is in file area"},
        "466": {"comment":"Refresh file area contents."},
        "472": {"comment":"DEL key pressed - mark file as deleted"},
        "475": {"comment":"delete file command only works when"},
        "478": {"comment":"cursor is in file area, view File entry contents"},
        "485": {"comment":"Refresh file area contents."},
        "495": {"comment":"DEL key pressed - mark file as deleted"},
        "498": {"comment":"delete file command only works when"},
        "501": {"comment":"cursor is in file area"},
        "505": {"comment":"Refresh file area contents."},
        "512": {"comment":"cursor browsing files or at left side menu?"},
        "517": {"comment":"use menu bar position as index to command"},
        "558": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: ToggleFileViewMode."},
        "562": {"comment":"only active files are displayed, swap to all files..."},
        "574": {"comment":"refresh file area contents at current file entry"},
        "580": {"synopsis":"Reads the bar mode: whether the cursor bar is in the menu window or in the file window.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = (barMode); Fz = 1 when the bar is in the menu window, Fz = 0 (A = $FF) when it is\nin the file window; Fc = 0.\nChanges: AF."},
        "588": {"comment":"refresh file area contents."},
        "594": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: InitFormatCommand.","comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "609": {"synopsis":"Toggles the cursor bar in the active window: the 17-character menu bar on row (MenuBarPosn)\nof the command window, or the 53-character file bar on row (FileBarPosn) of the file window.\nThe bar is drawn by XOR, so the main loop calls it once to show it and once to remove it.\nEntry: (barMode), (MenuBarPosn), (FileBarPosn).\nChanges: BC, HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "615": {"synopsis":"Entry inside DisplBar, the menu window case: selects window 1 (SelectMenuWindow), places the\ncursor at column 1 of row (MenuBarPosn) with VduCursor and toggles the menu bar (MenuBar).\nIt ends with POP AF, so it is entered only from DisplBar with AF pushed.\nEntry: AF on the stack; (MenuBarPosn) = row of the menu bar.\nChanges: BC, HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "621": {"comment":"get Y position of menu bar"},
        "630": {"comment":"now display menu bar at cursor"},
        "644": {"comment":"get Y position of File Bar"},
        "661": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2H1\"): selects window 1, the command window, for the menu bar. Sent by\nDisplMenuBar.","comment":"activate menu window for menu bar control"},
        "666": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence: selects window 2, the file window, and switches its cursor and vertical\nscrolling off (1,\"2H2\", 1,\"2-C\", 1,\"2-S\"). Sent by DisplBar for the file bar.","comment":"activate file window for file bar control"},
        "679": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that draws the menu bar: reverse video on, the attribute applied by XOR over 17\ncharacters from the cursor (1,\"2E\",32+17), reverse video off. Sending it twice removes the\nbar again.","comment":"set reverse video"},
        "683": {"comment":"XOR 'display' menu bar (15 chars wide)"},
        "687": {"comment":"back to normal video"},
        "692": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that draws the file bar: reverse video on, the attribute applied by XOR over 53\ncharacters from the cursor (1,\"2E\",32+53), reverse video off.","comment":"set reverse video"},
        "696": {"comment":"XOR 'display' file bar (53 chars wide)"},
        "700": {"comment":"back to normal video"},
        "705": {"synopsis":"Draws the command window and its menu, like dispcw, and keeps AF.\nEntry: (curslot) = current slot.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "711": {"synopsis":"Draws the command window (window 1, 17 x 8 at the left, banner \"COMMANDS\") with GN_Win from\nCmdWindowDef and writes the seven menu entries (menu_msg). When the card in the current slot\nhas no write or erase support (SlotWriteSupport returns Fc = 1), it greys out SAVE TO CARD\nand BACKUP FROM RAM (grey_wrercmds).\nEntry: (curslot) = current slot.\nChanges: AF, C (other registers through SlotWriteSupport not traced)."},
        "725": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "731": {"comment":"flash supports write/erase in slot."},
        "732": {"comment":"grey out commands that has no effect in current slot"},
        "739": {"synopsis":"Scan external slots and display available File Eprom's from which the\nuser selects an item.\n\nIf no File Eprom Area was found, then slots 1-3 are examined for a Flash\nCard to be created with a File Eprom Area (whole card or part).\nIf found and user acknowledges, then selected slot will be created with a File\nArea and selected as default.\n\nA small array, <availslots> is used to store the size of each File Eprom\nwith the first byte indicating the total of File Eproms available."},
        "743": {"comment":"no file areas found, investigate slots 1-3 for Flash Cards that can be formatted"},
        "764": {"comment":"User selects a slot from a list..."},
        "767": {"synopsis":"Get current slot in C"},
        "774": {"synopsis":"Entry: DE = pointer to banner."},
        "783": {"synopsis":"Display Window bar (below windows title) with caption text identified by HL pointer"},
        "801": {"synopsis":"Clears the whole application window area: redefines window 1 as the full 94 x 8 area and\nclears it (winbackground).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: HL."},
        "808": {"synopsis":"Writes a null-terminated string and a newline (GN_Sop, GN_Nln).\nEntry: HL = local pointer to the string.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "817": {"synopsis":"Greys the whole screen area by defining window 8 over it and switching grey on there\n(grey_msg); used before a pop-up window is drawn.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "826": {"synopsis":"Removes the grey from the whole screen area (ungrey_msg), the reverse of greyscr.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "835": {"synopsis":"Clears window 2, the main window on the right of the command window (clsvdu).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "844": {"synopsis":"Reads a key with OS_In. An extended key (a 0 code first) is read as its second code, and an\nescape condition is returned as the ESC key.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = key code (IN_ESC when ESC was pressed).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_In (for example RC_SUSP after pre-emption).\nChanges: AF."},
        "863": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key with OS_Sr SR_PWT (page wait), repeating the wait when it returns RC_SUSP.\nAn extended key (a 0 code first) is read as its second code with OS_In.\nEntry: none.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = key code.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code from OS_Sr.\nChanges: AF."},
        "881": {"synopsis":"Asks a yes/no question. It runs the routine at HL, which displays the question, then shows\nthe current answer (the message at DE) and reads keys: 'Y' selects Yes, any other key No,\nENTER accepts the answer shown and ESC aborts. Keys in the input buffer are purged first and\npre-emption is ignored.\nEntry: HL = routine that displays the question (it returns into yesno); DE = default answer,\nyes_msg or no_msg.\nExit: Fc = 0; Fz = 1 for Yes, Fz = 0 for No or ESC.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "885": {"comment":"call display message"},
        "891": {"comment":"make sure no keys in sys. inp. buffer..."},
        "896": {"comment":"ignore pre-emption..."},
        "909": {"comment":"Yes, Fc = 0, Fz = 1"},
        "912": {"comment":"No, Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "914": {"comment":"ESC pressed"},
        "915": {"comment":"return Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "932": {"synopsis":"User is prompted with \"Press SPACE to Resume\". The keyboard is then scanned\nfor the SPACE or as alternative the ESC key. The routine returns when the user\nhas pressed SPACE, ENTER or ESC.\nChanges: AF changed, IN_ESC or IN_SPACE keys returned."},
        "957": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "959": {"synopsis":"Switches the VDU to centre justification (centerjustify).\nOZ source name: VduEnableCentreJustify.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "963": {"comment":"enable centre justify VDU"},
        "968": {"synopsis":"Switches the VDU back to normal (left) justification (leftjustify).\nOZ source name: VduEnableNormalJustify.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "972": {"comment":"enable centre justify VDU"},
        "977": {"synopsis":"Text & VDU constants."},
        "986": {"synopsis":"VDU text of the command window's menu: selects window 1, grey off, tiny font on, then the\nseven entries at rows 0 to 6 (TOGGLE FILE VIEW, SELECT CARD, SAVE TO CARD, FETCH FROM CARD,\nBACKUP FROM RAM, RESTORE TO RAM, DEFAULT RAM), each placed with 1,\"3@\",x,y; cursor off.\nWritten by dispcw."},
        "1139": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that greys out the SAVE TO CARD (row 2) and BACKUP FROM RAM (row 4) entries of\nthe command window over 17 characters each, then switches grey off. Sent by dispcw when the\ncard in the current slot cannot be written."},
        "1170": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence: defines window 8 at (0,0), 94 x 8 (1,\"6#8\"), selects it and greys it\n(1,\"2G+\"). Sent by greyscr."},
        "1187": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence: defines window 8 at (0,0), 94 x 8, selects it and removes the grey (1,\"2G-\").\nSent by ungreyscr."},
        "1204": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence sent by cls: clears window 2 (1,\"2C2\"), then 1,'S' and a form feed (12)."},
        "1212": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence sent by ClearWindowArea: defines window 1 at (0,0), 94 x 8 (1,\"7#1\") and clears\nit (1,\"2C1\")."},
        "1226": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that starts a window bar under the banner: tiny, underline and reverse on,\ncentre justification and the cursor at (0,0). Sent by wbar before the caption."},
        "1242": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that ends a window bar: cursor at (0,0), the attributes applied over 53\ncharacters (1,\"2A\",85), tiny, underline and reverse off, normal justification. Sent by wbar\nafter the caption."},
        "1262": {"synopsis":"Message \"Last file failed.\", null-terminated; shown by the fetch and copy commands."},
        "1280": {"synopsis":"The \"Yes\" answer of yesno: CR, cursor on, \" Yes\" and three backspaces, null-terminated.\nyesno compares DE with this address to tell Yes from No."},
        "1293": {"synopsis":"The \"No\" answer of yesno: CR, cursor on, \" No \" and three backspaces, null-terminated."},
        "1306": {"synopsis":"VDU text of the resume prompt: selects window 2, centre justification, flash and tiny on,\n\"PRESS SPACE OR ENTER TO RESUME\" with the key symbols, attributes and cursor off, normal\njustification and CR LF. Written by ResSpace."},
        "1356": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"3-SC\"): no vertical scrolling and no blinking cursor in the window.","comment":"no vertical scrolling & no blinking cursor in window"},
        "1362": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2+G\"): grey text on."},
        "1367": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2-G\"): grey text off."},
        "1372": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2-T\"): tiny font off."},
        "1377": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2+T\"): tiny font on."},
        "1382": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2JC\"): centre justification. Sent by VduCentreJustify."},
        "1387": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2JN\"): normal (left) justification. Sent by VduNormalJustify."},
        "1392": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence (1,\"2JR\"): right justification."},
        "1397": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the command window: window 1 with bars, shelf brackets and banner\n(1 | 128), at (0,0), 17 wide and 8 high, banner \"COMMANDS\". Used by dispcw."},
        "1404": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the main window: window 2 with bars, shelf brackets and banner (2\n| 128), at (19,0), 53 wide and 8 high; the banner pointer is 0, so the caller gives it in\nDE. Used by DispMainWindow."},
        "1409": {"comment":"dynamic banner pointer in DE"},
        "1411": {"synopsis":"Display slot selection window to choose another Flash Card Device\nOZ source name: SelectCardCommand."},
        "1414": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "1420": {"comment":"if no file areas were found, then"},
