        "1542": {"comment":"HL / 4 = free space in K"},
        "1555": {"comment":"display free space in DE"},
        "1567": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: poll_for_rom_card.","comment":"preserve a copy of slot number..."},
        "1576": {"comment":"C = size of physical card"},
        "1585": {"comment":"display PadLock (FlashStore only supports Eprom writing in slot 3)"},
        "1590": {"comment":"display size of card as defined by ROM header"},
        "1610": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "1615": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "1620": {"comment":"the Eprom Application Card had no file area..."},
        "1627": {"comment":"display size of sub file area in K on Eprom"},
        "1645": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: poll_for_eprom_card.","comment":"poll slot C..."},
        "1648": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "1655": {"comment":"C = size of File Area in 16K banks (if Fz = 1)"},
        "1658": {"comment":"D = size of card in 16K banks"},
        "1667": {"comment":"display PadLock (FlashStore only supports Eprom writing in slot 3)"},
        "1672": {"comment":"display size of card as defined by ROM header"},
        "1681": {"comment":"display \"Files xxxxK\""},
        "1696": {"comment":"the slot is empty (or contains an empty Eprom Card)"},
        "1699": {"comment":"draw a grey outline box"},
        "1715": {"comment":"and write \"empty slot\" in the middle of the grey box"},
        "1723": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: flashcard_detected."},
        "1724": {"comment":"size of Flash Card in 16K banks"},
        "1727": {"comment":"display flash label"},
        "1731": {"comment":"Intel flash in slot 1 or 2 (display padlock)"},
        "1737": {"comment":"get manufacturer ID of current flash card"},
        "1746": {"comment":"flash card ID was Amd"},
        "1748": {"comment":"flash card ID was Intel"},
        "1757": {"comment":"prepare for \"applications\" text"},
        "1759": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "1778": {"comment":"prepare for \"files \" text"},
        "1783": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "1788": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "1819": {"comment":"display cached VDU sequences (the current card box)"},
        "1832": {"comment":"preset menu bar at first available card file area"},
        "1841": {"comment":"user aborted selection"},
        "1848": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "1854": {"comment":"user selected apparently void or illegal slot"},
        "1856": {"comment":"initialize File Bar cursor for new slot.."},
        "1859": {"comment":"auto-poll watermark in file header for selected slot"},
        "1862": {"comment":"indicate slot was successfully selected"},
        "1867": {"comment":"restore previous slot selection..."},
        "1871": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: check_empty_flcard."},
        "1874": {"comment":"no Flash Card in slot..."},
        "1876": {"comment":"empty flash card in slot (no file area, and erase/write support)"},
        "1893": {"comment":"Intel Flash Card found in slot, but no erase/write support in slot"},
        "1898": {"synopsis":"IN\nA = box draw args (padlock etc)\nHL = label (\"FLASH\", \"EPROM\", \"RAM\")\nDE = pointer to Flash Card label (if A.3 is set)\n(free) = size of card in 16K banks\nOUT\nBC = (Y,X) of start of displayed label"},
        "1904": {"comment":"Y++"},
        "1910": {"comment":"display device name (in HL)..."},
        "1913": {"comment":"A = size of slot in 16K banks"},
        "1916": {"synopsis":"Entry inside DisplayCard (also called by FileEpromStatistics): appends the card size, A x 16\nfollowed by 'K', to the VDU cache at (vdubufptr).\nEntry: A = size of the card in 16K banks; (vdubufptr) = end of the VDU cache.\nExit: (vdubufptr) advanced past the text.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL."},
        "1925": {"comment":"size in DE..."},
        "1938": {"synopsis":"Appends the free space of the current slot's file area, in K followed by 'K', to the VDU\ncache at (vdubufptr). The free bytes come from OS_Epr EP_FreSp; the value written is the\nquotient of the bytes / 1024 (GN_D24) plus one.\nEntry: (curslot) = slot; (vdubufptr) = end of the VDU cache.\nExit: (vdubufptr) advanced past the text.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "1940": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "1950": {"comment":"DEBC -> BHL"},
        "1953": {"comment":"BHL / 1024"},
        "1961": {"comment":"no. of K free"},
        "1972": {"synopsis":"Lets the user choose a slot in the card selection window: the flashing bar under the current\ncard box moves with cursor left and right (wrapping between 0 and 3), keys 0 to 3 select a\nslot directly, ENTER accepts the slot under the bar and ESC aborts. Other keys are ignored.\nEntry: (curslot) = slot of the bar at the start.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1, (curslot) = selected slot (0 to 3).\nError: Fc = 1 when ESC was pressed.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "1984": {"comment":"ESC?"},
        "1988": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "1991": {"comment":"Cursor Right ?"},
        "1995": {"comment":"Cursor Left ?"},
        "2001": {"comment":"smaller than '0'"},
        "2005": {"comment":">= '4'"},
        "2007": {"comment":"['0'; '3'] keys selected"},
        "2015": {"comment":"has m.bar already reached right edge?"},
        "2020": {"comment":"update new m.bar position"},
        "2021": {"comment":"display new m.bar position"},
        "2027": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: MVbar_left."},
        "2028": {"comment":"has m.bar already reached left edge?"},
        "2033": {"comment":"update new m.bar position"},
        "2040": {"synopsis":"HL = MenuBar ON/OFF VDU\nOZ source name: DisplMenuBar."},
        "2055": {"comment":"display menu bar at (Y,6) of card box"},
        "2057": {"comment":"display menu bar at bottom line of card box"},
        "2063": {"comment":"now display menu bar at cursor"},
        "2070": {"synopsis":"Shows the flashing reverse menu bar under the current slot's card box: HL = MenuBarOn and\njumps into the card selection's DisplMenuBar ($C7F8).\nEntry: (curslot) = slot.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "2075": {"synopsis":"Removes the menu bar under the current slot's card box: HL = MenuBarOff and jumps into the\ncard selection's DisplMenuBar ($C7F8).\nEntry: (curslot) = slot.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC."},
        "2080": {"synopsis":"Poll all slots (0 - 3) for file areas and return A = count of found file areas,\nor 0 if none were found."},
        "2083": {"comment":"point to slot 0"},
        "2087": {"comment":"begin with internal slot 0, then external 1-3"},
        "2089": {"comment":"counter of available file eproms"},
        "2091": {"comment":"preserve slot number..."},
        "2094": {"comment":"File Eprom Card or area available in slot C?"},
        "2101": {"comment":"no header was found, but a card was available of some sort"},
        "2103": {"comment":"File Eprom found"},
        "2105": {"comment":"size of file eprom in 16K banks"},
        "2111": {"comment":"indicate no file eprom"},
        "2123": {"comment":"store total of File Eprom's found"},
        "2129": {"comment":"Fc = 0, A = no. of found file cards..."},
        "2131": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: SelectDefaultSlot.\nEntry: C = -1 (FFh) select first found slot containing a file area; C = X (0-3) select first\nfound slot containing a file area that is not X.\nExit: Fc = 0, A = found slot number; Fc = 1, no slot was pre-selected."},
        "2134": {"comment":"beginning from slot 3, towards slot 1..."},
        "2152": {"comment":"the found slot is to be avoided..."},
        "2154": {"comment":"return this slot as default..."},
        "2158": {"synopsis":"Draw a minimalistic Z88 Card outline using VDU Box characters.\nEntry: A = BIT 0: draw card box in grey colour; A = BIT 1: draw only outline (not the card\nlabel line); A = BIT 2: draw Padlock on left bottom edge.; A = BIT 3: draw 'AMD' or 'INTEL'\nlabel on left top edge.; BC = (Y,X); DE = pointer to Flash Card label ('AMD' or 'INTEL')."},
        "2165": {"comment":"draw the card box in grey colour."},
        "2177": {"comment":"set VDU Cursor at (Y,X)"},
        "2180": {"comment":"draw top edge of card box"},
        "2188": {"comment":"display Flash card label?"},
        "2194": {"comment":"set VDU Cursor at (Y,X+1)"},
        "2203": {"comment":"Y++"},
        "2207": {"comment":"Y++"},
        "2208": {"comment":"set VDU Cursor at (Y,X)"},
        "2222": {"comment":"draw middle line of card box"},
        "2228": {"comment":"Y++"},
        "2232": {"comment":"Y++"},
        "2236": {"comment":"Y++"},
        "2240": {"comment":"Y++"},
        "2241": {"comment":"set VDU Cursor at (Y,X)"},
        "2244": {"comment":"draw bottom edge of card box"},
        "2263": {"comment":"(Y,X+9)"},
        "2266": {"comment":"set VDU cursor for slot number (bottom right edge)"},
        "2277": {"comment":"-> Ascii slot number"},
        "2294": {"comment":"(Y,X+7)"},
        "2310": {"synopsis":"BC = Y,X"},
        "2311": {"comment":"set VDU Cursor at (Y,X)"},
        "2318": {"comment":"draw left side"},
        "2325": {"comment":"set VDU Cursor at (Y,X+13)"},
        "2329": {"comment":"draw right side"},
        "2334": {"synopsis":"Place window cursor at (Y,X)\nB = Y window coordinate, C = X window Coordinate"},
        "2336": {"comment":"temp buffer at bottom of system stack"},
        "2345": {"comment":"execute VDU"},
        "2351": {"synopsis":"Place window cursor at (Y,X)\nB = Y window coordinate, C = X window Coordinate"},
        "2359": {"comment":"X"},
        "2365": {"comment":"Y"},
        "2374": {"synopsis":"Appends a 16-bit number in decimal to the VDU cache at (vdubufptr): converts it to text in\nbuf1 (IntAscii) and copies it with CacheVduString.\nEntry: DE = number.\nExit: (vdubufptr) advanced past the digits; HL = end of the digits in buf1.\nChanges: BC, HL.\nKeeps: AF, DE."},
        "2386": {"synopsis":"Cache VDU sequence in buffer pointed to by (vdubufptr)\nEntry: HL = local pointer to null-terminated VDU sequence.\nExit: HL points at null-terminator of string."},
        "2401": {"comment":"updated VDU Cache pointer"},
        "2408": {"synopsis":"Cache VDU character in buffer pointed to by (vdubufptr)\nEntry: A = char."},
        "2417": {"comment":"null-terminate by default"},
        "2418": {"comment":"updated VDU Cache pointer"},
        "2425": {"synopsis":"Return VDU Card Box (0,X) coordinate for slot X (0-3) fetched in (curslot)\nExit: BC = (Y,X)."},
        "2430": {"comment":"X coord multiply counter"},
        "2431": {"comment":"first card box displayed at (0,0)"},
        "2444": {"synopsis":"Create help window in right side of screen and display help text string by HL"},
        "2454": {"comment":"Display small help text in right side window"},
        "2458": {"synopsis":"Text constants"},
        "2480": {"synopsis":"Message \"No Flash Cards found in slots 1-3.\" between bold toggles (1,\"B\"), null-terminated."},
        "2519": {"synopsis":"VDU prefix of a cursor move (1,\"3@\"); CacheVduCursor follows it with X+32 and Y+32."},
        "2523": {"synopsis":"VDU text of a card box's top line: the top left corner (1,\"2*C\"), 12 horizontal lines\n(1,\"2*E\") and the top right corner (1,\"2*F\"), null-terminated. Drawn by DrawCardBox.","comment":"Top left corner"},
        "2551": {"comment":"Top right corner"},
        "2580": {"synopsis":"VDU text of a card box's middle line: the left T-section (1,\"2*K\"), 12 horizontal lines and\nthe right T-section (1,\"2*N\"), null-terminated.","comment":"Left T-section"},
        "2608": {"comment":"Rigth T-section"},
        "2637": {"synopsis":"VDU text of a card box's bottom line: the bottom left corner (1,\"2*I\"), 12 horizontal lines\nand the bottom right corner (1,\"2*L\"), null-terminated.","comment":"Bottom left corner"},
        "2665": {"comment":"Bottom right corner"},
        "2694": {"synopsis":"VDU text of a card box's side: one vertical line (1,\"2*J\"), null-terminated."},
        "2699": {"synopsis":"VDU text of the AMD logo: defines user characters J, K, L and M (each 1,138,'=',char and 8\npixel rows) and displays each after its definition (1,\"2?\",char); null-terminated."},
        "2764": {"synopsis":"VDU text of the Intel logo: defines user characters N, O, P and Q (8 pixel rows each) and\ndisplays each after its definition; null-terminated."},
        "2829": {"synopsis":"VDU text of the padlock symbol: defines user character Z (8 pixel rows) and displays it\nbetween two spaces; null-terminated."},
        "2848": {"synopsis":"Help text of the card selection window: centre justification, no scrolling or cursor, then\n\"Select card with 0 - 3 (bold) or move cursor over card, ENTER to select\" on separate lines;\nnull-terminated."},
        "2930": {"synopsis":"Card label \"EPROM \" in tiny font, null-terminated."},
        "2941": {"synopsis":"Card label \"FLASH \" in tiny font, null-terminated."},
        "2952": {"synopsis":"Card label \"RAM \" in tiny font, null-terminated."},
        "2961": {"synopsis":"Text \" FREE \" in tiny font, null-terminated."},
        "2972": {"synopsis":"Text \"APPLICATIONS\" in tiny font, null-terminated."},
        "2989": {"synopsis":"Text \"NO FILE AREA\" in tiny font, null-terminated."},
        "3006": {"synopsis":"Text \"SLOT \", null-terminated."},
        "3012": {"synopsis":"Text \": \", null-terminated."},
        "3015": {"synopsis":"Text \"EMPTY SLOT\" in tiny font, then tiny off; null-terminated."},
        "3034": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence: no vertical scrolling and no cursor (1,\"3-SC\"), then tiny font on.","comment":"no vertical scrolling, no cursor"},
        "3044": {"synopsis":"The card selection's SelectMenuWindow: selects window 2 and switches its cursor off\n(1,\"2H2\", 1,\"2-C\"). Sent by its DisplMenuBar before the bar is placed.\nOZ source name: SelectMenuWindow.","comment":"activate menu window, no Cursor..."},
        "3053": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that shows the card selection bar: flash and reverse on (1,\"4+F+R\") and the\nattributes applied over 3 characters (1,\"2A\",32+3). Sent by ShowMenuBar.","comment":"enable flash and inverse video"},
        "3059": {"comment":"XOR 'display' menu bar (3 chars wide)"},
        "3064": {"synopsis":"VDU sequence that removes the card selection bar: flash and reverse off (1,\"4-F-R\") and the\nattributes applied over 3 characters. Sent by RemoveMenuBar.","comment":"disable flash & set normal video"},
        "3070": {"comment":"apply 'display' menu bar (3 chars wide)"},
        "3075": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the card selection window: window 2 with bars, shelf brackets and\nbanner (2 | 128), at (16,0), 56 wide and 8 high; the banner pointer is 0, so the caller\ngives it in DE."},
        "3080": {"comment":"dynamic banner pointer in DE"},
        "3082": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the help window on the right: window 3 with left and right bars\nonly (3 | 64), at (75,0), 18 wide and 8 high. Used by DispHelpText."},
        "3087": {"synopsis":"system definitions\nFlashStore popdown variables\n\nSelect Default RAM Device.\nOZ source name: DefaultRamCommand."},
        "3108": {"comment":"remember selected RAM Device slot no ('0' - '3')."},
        "3112": {"synopsis":"User selects RAM device by using keys 0-3,'-' or using <>J to toggle between available\ndevices.\nExit: A = Ascii Slot Number ('0' - '3', '-') of selected RAM Device."},
        "3115": {"comment":"the default RAM device at (buf1)"},
        "3126": {"comment":"get current VDU cursor for current window"},
        "3128": {"comment":"put VDU cursor at (X,Y) = (C,B)"},
        "3134": {"comment":"display the current RAM device."},
        "3139": {"comment":"put blinking cursor over slot number of RAM device"},
        "3141": {"comment":"get RAM device slot number"},
        "3146": {"comment":"user aborted selection"},
        "3150": {"comment":"user has selected a RAM device"},
        "3154": {"comment":"<>J"},
        "3158": {"comment":"allow for \"-\""},
        "3162": {"comment":"only \"0\" to \"3\" allowed"},
        "3168": {"comment":"preserve Ascii slot number"},
        "3174": {"comment":"there's no RAM card in selected slot, ignore input"},
        "3177": {"comment":"update slot number in RAM device"},
        "3180": {"comment":"and let it be displayed."},
        "3187": {"comment":"wrap from :RAM.- to :RAM.0"},
        "3191": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: toggle_device_loop."},
        "3194": {"comment":"only scan slots 0 - 3, then automatically select :RAM.-"},
        "3197": {"comment":"RAM device at slot A?"},
        "3200": {"comment":"yes!"},
        "3203": {"comment":"try next slot..."},
        "3205": {"comment":"check slot 0 for a RAM device"},
        "3221": {"comment":"restore current default RAM Device"},
        "3224": {"comment":"indicate abort command"},
        "3225": {"comment":"return Ascii Slot Number of RAM Device"},
        "3229": {"synopsis":"Asks OZ whether slot A holds a RAM device (OS_Nq Nq_Mfp).\nEntry: A = slot number.\nExit: Fc = 0, a RAM device: A = total banks of the RAM card; DE = free pages (256 bytes).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_ONF when the slot has no RAM device.\nChanges: AF, DE.\nKeeps: BC, HL.","comment":"preserve VDU X,Y cursor..."},
        "3233": {"comment":"check if there's a RAM card in selected slot A"},
        "3237": {"synopsis":"Get FlashStore's Default RAM Device at (DE).\nOZ source name: GetDefaultRamDevice."},
        "3252": {"comment":"null terminate RAM device name"},
        "3255": {"synopsis":"Define the default Ascii RAM Device slot number at (ramdevno)\nOZ source name: GetDefaultPanelRamDev."},
        "3257": {"comment":"Read default device"},
        "3260": {"comment":"buffer for device name"},
        "3263": {"comment":"save pointer to buffer"},
        "3269": {"comment":"actual length of string..."},
        "3273": {"comment":"get slot number of RAM device"},
        "3278": {"synopsis":"constants"},
        "3304": {"synopsis":"Text \":RAM.\", null-terminated: the device name prefix that GetDefaultRamDevice copies before\nthe slot number."},
        "3310": {"synopsis":"Message CR LF \" Select RAM device.\" CR LF, null-terminated."},
        "3334": {"synopsis":"Message shown under the RAM device prompt: \" Use keys 0-3 or <diamond>J to toggle. ENTER to\nselect.\", with VDU symbol codes, null-terminated. Shown by DefaultRamCommand, the backup\ncommand and the copy command before SelectRamDevice."},
        "3380": {"synopsis":"system definitions\nFlashStore popdown variables\nInitialize file statistics window"},
        "3400": {"synopsis":"Eprom Statistics from current File Eprom (Area)\n\nFetch the following information:\n\n(file) = number of files\n(fdel) = number of deleted files\n(free) = free space\nOZ source name: FileEpromStatistics.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nKeeps: IX, IY."},
        "3406": {"synopsis":"Body of FileEpromStatistics: fills the file statistics window for the current slot.\n1. Builds the window banner \"SLOT n\" at buf1 from slot_bnr; slot 1 is set left, slot 3\nright, the others centred.\n2. Asks OS_Epr (EP_Req) for a file area in the slot; without one it goes to no_filearea.\n3. Counts the files (FilesAvailable), reads the free space (EP_FreSp) into (free) and the\nactive and deleted space (EP_TotSp) into (active), (deleted) and their sum (total).\n4. Opens the window (InitWindow) and shows the card type (the flash chip's text, or the UV\nEPROM size), the file area size (DisplayEpromSize), the free and used bytes, the counts of\nsaved and deleted files, and the free space bar (DispFreeSpaceBar).\nEntry: (curslot) = slot.\nExit: (file), (fdel), (free), (active), (deleted), (total) updated.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3430": {"comment":"display \"slot 1\" left aligned.."},
        "3436": {"comment":"display \"slot 3\" right aligned.."},
        "3440": {"comment":"null-terminate banner"},
        "3441": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "3447": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "3453": {"synopsis":"Entry inside dispstats, taken when the slot has no file area or its free space cannot be\nread: opens the file statistics window (InitWindow) and shows \"No File Area\" (nofepr_msg).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "3463": {"comment":"update file count on current File Eprom"},
        "3466": {"synopsis":"(file) = active files, (fdel) = deleted files","comment":"c = slot number..."},
        "3470": {"comment":"get free space on current File Eprom"},
        "3486": {"comment":"get total used space on current File Eprom (active & deleted)"},
        "3493": {"comment":"remember total active file space"},
        "3501": {"comment":"remember total deleted file space"},
        "3513": {"comment":"remember total used space (active+deleted)"},
        "3523": {"comment":"centre justify..."},
        "3532": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "3546": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "3551": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "3563": {"comment":"display string at BHL"},
        "3577": {"comment":"VDU (X,Y) = (3,1)"},
        "3599": {"comment":"\"xxxx free\""},
        "3611": {"comment":"just display the free space bar on an empty file area"},
        "3629": {"comment":"\"xxxx used\""},
        "3639": {"comment":"convert 16bit integer in BC to Ascii..."},
        "3658": {"comment":"convert 16bit integer in BC to Ascii..."},
        "3680": {"synopsis":"Shows the size of the current slot's file area at (1,1) of the statistics window, in tiny\ntext: the size in K followed by \"K FILE AREA\". It keeps the size in 16K banks at\n(bytesperline), where FillFreeSpaceBar picks it up.\nEntry: (curslot) = slot; the slot holds a file area.\nExit: (bytesperline) = size of the file area in 16K banks.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "3683": {"comment":"VDU Cursor at (1,1)"},
        "3686": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "3691": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "3695": {"comment":"remember size of file area in 16K banks"},
        "3700": {"comment":"C = total of banks as defined by File Eprom Header"},
        "3704": {"comment":"size in DE..."},
        "3706": {"comment":"get relative top bank number..."},
        "3708": {"comment":"is header located in top bank?"},
        "3710": {"comment":"Yes - real File Eprom found..."},
        "3756": {"synopsis":"Shows the number in DE in decimal at the cursor (IntAscii, GN_Sop).\nEntry: DE = number.\nChanges: BC, HL."},
        "3764": {"comment":"display size of File Eprom"},
        "3768": {"synopsis":"Convert integer in HL (or BC) to Ascii string, which is written to (buf1)\nand null-terminated.\n\nHL points at Ascii string, null-terminated."},
        "3784": {"synopsis":"Multiply HL * 16, result in HL."},
        "3788": {"comment":"banks * 16K = size of card in K"},
        "3792": {"synopsis":"Display Intel Flash Eprom Device Code and return information of chip.\nEntry: C = Slot Number.\nExit: Fc = 0, Flash Eprom Recognized in slot C; BHL = pointer to flash Card text; Fc = 1,\nFlash Eprom not found in slot X, or Device code not found."},
        "3798": {"comment":"get Flash card data"},
        "3802": {"comment":"return BHL = chip description text string"},
        "3804": {"synopsis":"Display the graphical free space bar containing a graphical presentation of\nof how deleted space, used space and free space is available"},
        "3808": {"comment":"get pointer in BHL to LORES0 (UDG 6x8 pixel font table)"},
        "3813": {"comment":"get Z88 machine state (standard or expanded)"},
        "3820": {"comment":"return Fz = 1, if Z88 is expanded"},
        "3824": {"comment":"point at 'Q' UDG in LORES0 when Z88 is unexpanded"},
        "3829": {"comment":"point at 'Q' UDG in LORES0 when Z88 is expanded"},
        "3835": {"comment":"modify offset pointer to use segment 1."},
        "3837": {"comment":"HL is base pointer at first UDG character, 'Q'"},
        "3842": {"comment":"bind LORES font memory into segment 1 ($4000-$7FFF)"},
        "3843": {"comment":"preserve old bank binding"},
        "3844": {"comment":"Initialize (reset) the horisontal bar"},
        "3847": {"comment":"fill bar with information about deleted and active file space"},
        "3851": {"comment":"restore old bank binding in segment 1."},
        "3855": {"comment":"display the free space graphic bar in file statistics window"},
        "3859": {"synopsis":"Empty/reset demographic horisontal view of the deleted / used space of the file\narea. The Bar is 7 pixels high, using 1 pixel border around the bar, displaying a\n5 high pixel 'bar'.\nOZ source name: ResetFreeSpaceBar.","comment":"get base pointer to UDG 'Q' - '@'"},
        "3862": {"comment":"left side of bar"},
        "3876": {"comment":"right side of bar"},
        "3881": {"synopsis":"HL = pointer to base of VDU char\nC = 5 pixel line 'middle'"},
        "3882": {"comment":"top of bar"},
        "3891": {"comment":"bottom of bar"},
        "3899": {"synopsis":"Draws the deleted and the active space of the file area into the free space bar's UDG\ncharacters. It divides the file area's size by 106 to get the bytes one vertical line of the\nbar stands for, draws the deleted space as stippled lines from line 1, then the active space\nas filled lines after them (DispBarLine).\nEntry: (bytesperline) = size of the file area in 16K banks; (deleted), (active) = 24-bit\nbyte counts; (FreeSpaceBar) = base of the bar's UDGs, bound into segment 1.\nExit: (bytesperline) = bytes per bar line.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"get size of File Area in 16K banks"},
        "3910": {"comment":"banksize = no-of-banks * 16384 = size of file area in bytes"},
        "3919": {"comment":"banksize / 106 = no of bytes per vertical line in free space bar"},
        "3930": {"comment":"bhl = deleted space"},
        "3933": {"comment":"cde = bytes per line"},
        "3934": {"comment":"BHL = deleted space / bytes per line"},
        "3937": {"comment":"draw X lines of deleted space..."},
        "3938": {"comment":"starting at line 1"},
        "3942": {"comment":"no deleted space to be drawn..."},
        "3944": {"comment":"adjust for integer division rounding"},
        "3945": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: draw_delspace_loop.","comment":"indicate stippled vertical line"},
        "3951": {"comment":"flip-flop bit 0"},
        "3954": {"comment":"remember position of line pointer"},
        "3961": {"comment":"BHL = Active file space"},
        "3968": {"comment":"Active file space / bytes per line"},
        "3971": {"comment":"draw X lines of active file space..."},
        "3974": {"comment":"(get line counter)"},
        "3975": {"comment":"no active file space to display"},
        "3976": {"comment":"indicate filled vertical line"},
        "3977": {"comment":"adjust for integer division rounding"},
        "3978": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: draw_actspace_loop."},
        "3982": {"comment":"draw active file space..."},
        "3985": {"synopsis":"H = bar line to draw (0 - 107).\n\nA = 0: draw filled line\nA = 128 (bit 7): draw stippled line - first pixel not drawn\nA = 129 (bit 7,0): draw stippled line - first pixel drawn"},
        "3990": {"comment":"get UDG char base address and pixel mask"},
        "3994": {"comment":"the vertical line consists of 5 pixels in the bar, top -> down"},
        "3997": {"comment":"draw a filled, vertical line..."},
        "3999": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: draw_stippled_line_loop.","comment":"skip drawing a pixel?"},
        "4021": {"synopsis":"ORs the pixel mask in C into the UDG byte at (HL): one pixel of a vertical bar line.\nEntry: C = pixel mask; HL = UDG byte.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL."},
        "4024": {"comment":"mask new 5 pixel line into bar"},
        "4027": {"synopsis":"Entry: H = bar line to draw (0 - 107).\nExit: HL = first address of UDG row to draw vertical pixel line; C = pixel mask representing\nvertical pixel line.","comment":"line DIV 6, get relative UDG character position"},
        "4032": {"comment":"(the pixel line bit position of UDG char)"},
        "4036": {"comment":"(each UDG character consists of 8 bytes pixel data)"},
        "4040": {"comment":"DE = (line DIV 8) * 8, base of UDG character"},
        "4042": {"comment":"get base pointer to UDG space bar, 'Q' - '@'"},
        "4045": {"comment":"HL points at first pixel line of UDG char to draw line"},
        "4046": {"comment":"move past top line, ready for first vertical pixel"},
        "4051": {"comment":"pixel line is already at offset 0 of UDG char"},
        "4052": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: pixel_line_adjust."},
        "4054": {"comment":"pixel line adjusted correctly within byte"},
        "4057": {"synopsis":"constants"},
        "4060": {"synopsis":"Text \"FILE AREA\" followed by the VDU code that turns tiny text off, null-terminated.\nDisplayEpromSize shows it after the size."},
        "4074": {"synopsis":"Banner text for the file statistics window: the VDU code for centred text followed by \"SLOT\n\". dispstats copies its first 9 bytes to buf1, changes the justify letter for slots 1 and 3\nand adds the slot digit."},
        "4084": {"synopsis":"Text \"FREE\", null-terminated: follows the free space in the statistics window."},
        "4089": {"synopsis":"Text \"USED\", null-terminated: follows the used space in the statistics window."},
        "4094": {"synopsis":"Text \" FILES SAVED\", null-terminated: follows the count of active files."},
        "4107": {"synopsis":"Text \" FILES DELETED\", null-terminated: follows the count of deleted files."},
        "4122": {"synopsis":"Message for a slot without a file area: two new lines, then \"No File Area\" centred and\nflashing; it ends by restoring normal justification and turning flashing and the cursor off.\nShown by no_filearea."},
        "4156": {"synopsis":"UDG's used for space bar (18 chars of 6x8 pixels), left - right order: QPONMLKJIHGFEDCBA@"},
        "4234": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the file statistics window (InitWindow): window 3 with bars,\nbrackets and a banner (byte $83), at X = $4A, Y = 0, 18 wide and 8 high; the banner pointer\nis 0, so the banner is the dynamic one passed in DE (buf1)."},
        "4239": {"comment":"dynamic banner pointer in DE"},
        "4241": {"synopsis":"system definitions\nFlashStore popdown variables\nDisplay name and size of stored files on Flash Eprom."},
        "4247": {"comment":"DE = banner for file area window"},
        "4256": {"comment":"file area not available"},
        "4259": {"comment":"Fz = 1, no files available in file area..."},
        "4262": {"synopsis":"Entry inside DispFilesWindow: clears the file area window and lists up to 7 file entries\n(DisplayFile), starting with the window's top entry at (WindowFilePtr). Reached by\nMoveToFirstFile and at the end of the page up and page down moves.\nEntry: (WindowFilePtr) = top file entry of the window.\nExit: Fc = 0 when 7 lines were shown; Fc = 1 when the end of the list was reached (\"END\"\nshown).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; (linecnt)."},
        "4269": {"comment":"BHL <-- (WindowFilePtr), top file entry of the window"},
        "4276": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: get_next_filename.","comment":"get pointer to next File Entry in BHL..."},
        "4300": {"synopsis":"Sends norm_sq (tiny and grey text off) to the window: the attributes for an active file\nentry.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "4305": {"synopsis":"Sends tiny_sq to the window: tiny, grey text, a grey \"DEL\" mark, then grey off; the\nattributes for a deleted file entry.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "4310": {"synopsis":"Sends the VDU code for right-justified text to the window.\nEntry: none.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "4315": {"synopsis":"Sends the VDU code for normal, left-justified text to the window; falls into the shared\noutput code (dispsq).\nEntry: none.\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "4324": {"synopsis":"Shows the browse keys help (browsehelp) in the right-hand help window (DispHelpText): shown\nwhile the cursor is in the file window.\nEntry: none.\nKeeps: HL."},
        "4328": {"comment":"display help text window"},
        "4333": {"synopsis":"Make the banner for the card file area window.\nDepending on the current view state, the banner text is dynamically created\nas defined in .filearea_banner .allfiles_banner .savedfiles_banner\n\"CARD FILE AREA - CURSOR SELECTS SAVED & DELETED FILES\" or\n\"CARD FILE AREA - CURSOR SELECTS ONLY SAVED FILES\"\nOZ source name: FileAreaBannerText.\nEntry: HL = Base banner text; C = length of banner text.\nExit: DE = pointer to banner text."},
        "4348": {"comment":"all files are displayed"},
        "4350": {"comment":"only saved files displayed"},
        "4355": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: append_viewtypetext."},
        "4358": {"comment":"null-terminate completed banner string"},
        "4359": {"comment":"return pointer to start of banner text."},
        "4361": {"synopsis":"Initialize File Bar (CursorFilePtr) to first point at first file entry in File Area.\n\nReturns\nFc = 0\nBHL = pointer to first file\n(CursorFilePtr) = BHL\n\nIf no file area were found, or no files present in file area:\nFc = 1\n(CursorFilePtr) = 0\n(WindowFilePtr) = 0"},
        "4362": {"comment":"File Bar at top of window"},
        "4365": {"comment":"any files available in File Area?"},
        "4368": {"comment":"no file area..."},
        "4371": {"comment":"no files available..."},
        "4374": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "4377": {"comment":"get BHL of first file in File area in slot C"},
        "4380": {"comment":"hmm.."},
        "4383": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4386": {"comment":"BHL --> (WindowFilePtr)"},
        "4391": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "4393": {"synopsis":"Move the File Bar to top of file list, place window cursor at top line in window\nand display the file list.","comment":"File Bar placed at first file in area"},
        "4396": {"comment":"no files"},
        "4397": {"comment":"update file area window."},
        "4402": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "4404": {"synopsis":"Move the File Bar to the last file entry (top of file area) and try to fill the\nlist with 6 file entries above.","comment":"get a cache of all file entries"},
        "4405": {"comment":"and return BHL = last file entry in file area"},
        "4408": {"comment":"no file entries or no File Area available..."},
        "4411": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4416": {"comment":"move 6 file entries upwards, if possible. C return no of entries left of 6"},
        "4422": {"comment":"File Bar at last file entry in window"},
        "4428": {"comment":"update the file entry pointer that is the top entry in the window"},
        "4433": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr), CursorFilePtr = FileEprLastFile(slot)"},
        "4438": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "4440": {"synopsis":"Move the File Bar one file up the list - scroll the window contents one line\ndownwards and display previous file line, when file bar goes beyond the window bottom","comment":"BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4443": {"comment":"get a cache of all file entries until"},
        "4445": {"comment":"file entry in BHL, DE = pointer to cached entry"},
        "4448": {"comment":"no file entries or no File Area available..."},
        "4452": {"comment":"File Bar at top of file list, wrap to last..."},
        "4454": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4469": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: scroll_filearea_down.","comment":"new top window file entry pointer..."},
        "4480": {"comment":"(0,0) - the start of the top line in the file area window"},
        "4491": {"synopsis":"Move the File Bar one file down the list - scroll the window contents one line\nupwards and display next file line, when file bar goes beyond the window bottom","comment":"BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4497": {"comment":"File Bar at end of file list, wrap to first..."},
        "4499": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr), CursorFilePtr = GetNextFilePtr(CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4509": {"comment":"file cursor in window not yet reached bottom line..."},
        "4513": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "4515": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: scroll_filearea_up.","comment":"one line upwards and display the next file"},
        "4516": {"comment":"at bottom line of window"},
        "4523": {"comment":"update the top window file entry to the next file entry..."},
        "4532": {"comment":"get Y position of File Bar"},
        "4536": {"comment":"start of line..."},
        "4548": {"comment":"Fc = 0, Fz = 0"},
        "4550": {"synopsis":"Move the File Bar one page up (7 items) in the list of file entries -\nClear window and position the Bar cursor at the top line and list file entries.\nOZ source name: MoveFileBarPageUp.","comment":"BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4553": {"comment":"get a cache of all file entries until"},
        "4555": {"comment":"file entry in BHL, DE = pointer to cached entry"},
        "4558": {"comment":"no file entries or no File Area available..."},
        "4559": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4563": {"comment":"File Bar at top of window"},
        "4566": {"comment":"move 7 file entries upwards, if possible"},
        "4568": {"synopsis":"Loop inside MoveFileBarPageUp, also called by MoveToLastFile: moves the file cursor up C\nentries through the file entry cache, making each new entry the window's top entry too, then\nredraws the window (DispFiles). It stops early at the top of the list.\nEntry: C = entries to move up; DE = current entry in the cache (from CacheFileEntries);\n(CursorFilePtr) = current entry.\nExit: C = entries left of the C asked for (source comment); (CursorFilePtr), (WindowFilePtr)\nupdated.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4574": {"comment":"reached top of list, update file area window"},
        "4576": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4579": {"comment":"the top window file entry will be the same as the new file entry"},
        "4588": {"synopsis":"Move the File Bar one page down (7 items) in the list of file entries -\nClear window and position the Bar cursor at the top line and list file entries.\nOZ source name: MoveFileBarPageDown."},
        "4589": {"comment":"File Bar at top of window"},
        "4592": {"comment":"move 7 file entries downwards, if possible"},
        "4594": {"comment":"BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4600": {"comment":"reached bottom of list, update file area window"},
        "4602": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr), CursorFilePtr = GetNextFilePtr(CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4605": {"comment":"the top window file entry will be the same as the new file entry"},
        "4614": {"synopsis":"Get pointer to first file entry. If only active files are currently displayed,\ndeleted file entries are skipped until an active file entry is found.\nEntry: C = slot number of File area.\nExit: Fc = 1, No file area or no file entries in file area.; Fc = 0; BHL = pointer to first\nfile entry."},
        "4625": {"comment":"an active file entry was found..."},
        "4626": {"comment":"are deleted files to be displayed in file area?"},
        "4630": {"comment":"skip deleted file(s) until active file is found"},
        "4633": {"comment":"(and return BHL to that entry)"},
        "4634": {"synopsis":"Get pointer to next file entry. If only active files are currently displayed,\ndeleted file entries are skipped until an active file entry is found.\nEntry: BHL = current file entry pointer.\nExit: Fc = 1, End of list reached; Fc = 0; BHL = pointer to next file entry."},
        "4645": {"comment":"an active file entry was found..."},
        "4646": {"comment":"are deleted files to be displayed in file area?"},
        "4650": {"comment":"only active files, scan forward until active file.."},
        "4652": {"comment":"return 'marked as deleted' file entry"},
        "4653": {"synopsis":"Get pointer to previous file entry. If only active files are currently displayed,\ndeleted file entries are skipped until an active file entry is found.\nEntry: BHL = current file entry pointer.\nExit: Fc = 1, Top of list reached; Fc = 0; BHL = pointer to previous file entry."},
        "4664": {"comment":"an active file entry was found..."},
        "4665": {"comment":"are deleted files to be displayed in file area?"},
        "4669": {"comment":"only active files, scan backward until active file.."},
        "4671": {"comment":"return 'marked as deleted' file entry"},
        "4672": {"synopsis":"Poll current file area, and update File entry pointer if necessary.\n\nReturn Fc = 1, if no file area is available (possibly card was removed)\nReturn Fz = 1, if no files are available in file area","comment":"same card still available in current slot?"},
        "4675": {"comment":"no file area found in slot"},
        "4678": {"comment":"Ups, the card has been changed in the current slot!"},
        "4680": {"comment":"same card still present, check if files area available..."},
        "4683": {"comment":"no files in file area"},
        "4686": {"comment":"File Area Window top line points at file entry according to view setting"},
        "4689": {"comment":"no files in file area"},
        "4692": {"comment":"Current file Entry File Bar adjusted to match adjusted Window File File Ptr"},
        "4695": {"comment":"BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "4700": {"comment":"File Entry was zero, initialize to first in file area"},
        "4704": {"synopsis":"Reset file area window to point at first file and refresh the entire file window"},
        "4705": {"comment":"Place the file cursor at the beginning of the file list"},
        "4708": {"comment":"and redraw the entire file area window"},
        "4713": {"synopsis":"For the current slot, compare the random ID and size of the file area\n(identified as the watermark) with the current stored values at (watermark).\n\nreturn Fc = 1, if no file area was found (watermark reset to 0)\nreturn Fz = 1, if a new file area was found (watermark updated to new value)\nOZ source name: PollFileCardWatermark."},
        "4719": {"comment":"Ups, no card available in current slot"},
        "4728": {"comment":"a new card with a different size file area has been inserted"},
        "4730": {"comment":"get Random ID of file header in DEBC..."},
        "4738": {"comment":"compare previous stored watermark with current from file area"},
        "4745": {"comment":"watermark doesn't match - a new file area was found in slot"},
        "4747": {"comment":"Fz = 0, indicate same file area..."},
        "4748": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_PollFileCardWatermark."},
        "4752": {"comment":"get Random ID of file header in DEBC..."},
        "4763": {"comment":"size of file area in 16K banks"},
        "4766": {"comment":"Fz = 1, indicate new file area"},
        "4769": {"synopsis":"Reads the random ID of the current slot's file area header (at $3FF8 of the header bank) and\nthe file area's size: the two make the card's watermark. Part of PollFileCardWatermark.\nEntry: (curslot) = slot.\nExit: Fc = 0: DEBC = random ID; A = size of the file area in 16K banks.\nError: Fc = 1, no file area in the slot.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, BC', DE', HL' (it swaps the register sets).","comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "4774": {"comment":"BHL points to File Area header"},
        "4779": {"comment":"BHL + $38, position of Random ID is 3ff8h..."},
        "4784": {"comment":"A = total banks in file area"},
        "4786": {"comment":"return Random IF in BCDE"},
        "4789": {"synopsis":"Clears the 5-byte watermark (random ID and size of the last seen file area) to zero. It\nleaves the flags alone, so PollFileCardWatermark's Fc = 1 survives it.\nEntry: none.\nExit: A = 0; HL = 0; (watermark) = 0.\nKeeps: F, BC, DE."},
        "4803": {"synopsis":"Display file name and size information to current VDU cursor in current active\nwindow, as defined by file entry BHL."},
        "4808": {"comment":"Ups - last file(name) has been displayed..."},
        "4810": {"comment":"active file, display..."},
        "4813": {"comment":"fc = 0..."},
        "4818": {"comment":"ignore deleted file(name)..."},
        "4836": {"comment":"display filename"},
        "4845": {"comment":"get size of File Entry in CDE"},
        "4867": {"comment":"display size of current File Entry"},
        "4885": {"synopsis":"Fetches the filename of the current file entry (supplied as BHL) The filename is\ncompressed using GN_Fcm to use max. 45 characters (so that a very long filename\ncan be displayed sensibly in the file area window).\n\nbuf1 is used internally, so should not be used as external pointer (otherwise\nno compression will be executed).\nOZ source name: CompressedFileEntryName.\nEntry: DE = local pointer to put (optionally) compressed filename; BHL = pointer to current\nFile Entry (B = absolute bank number).\nExit: DE = DE(in)."},
        "4890": {"comment":"local pointer to filename"},
        "4892": {"comment":"copy filename from current file entry at (DE)"},
        "4899": {"comment":"complete filename fits within 43 characters"},
        "4901": {"comment":"remember buffer pointer"},
        "4903": {"comment":"HL pointer to local filename"},
        "4905": {"comment":"compressed filename max. 45 chars (including '/..')"},
        "4907": {"comment":"make compressed filename at buf1"},
        "4919": {"comment":"preset the filename with '/..' before compressed filename"},
        "4921": {"comment":"compress filename.."},
        "4925": {"comment":"null-terminate"},
        "4927": {"comment":"start of original buffer"},
        "4929": {"comment":"copy compressed filename (including null-terminator) to original buffer"},
        "4935": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: end_GetCompressedFilename."},
        "4939": {"synopsis":"Check if there's active/deleted files availabe in the current File Area.\nIf current file display setting signals also display of deleted files, Fz = 1 is\nreturned if there are also no deleted files.\n\nreturn Fz = 1, if no files available, and Fc = 1 if no file area available."},
        "4945": {"comment":"reset active files count"},
        "4948": {"comment":"deleted"},
        "4951": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "4956": {"comment":"any files available in File Area?"},
        "4959": {"comment":"no file area!"},
        "4961": {"comment":"update active files count"},
        "4964": {"comment":"deleted"},
        "4970": {"comment":"active files available..."},
        "4972": {"comment":"no active files, are deleted files to be displayed in file area?"},
        "4976": {"comment":"no, only active files are displayed, then signal no files..."},
        "4979": {"comment":"If no deleted files are available, then Fz = 0..."},
        "4984": {"synopsis":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr)\nOZ source name: StoreCursorFilePtr."},
        "4988": {"comment":"real last file pointer"},
        "4992": {"synopsis":"BHL <-- (CursorFilePtr)"},
        "5000": {"synopsis":"BHL --> (WindowFilePtr)\nOZ source name: StoreWindowFilePtr."},
        "5004": {"comment":"real last file pointer"},
        "5008": {"synopsis":"BHL <-- (WindowFilePtr)"},
        "5016": {"synopsis":"Adjust the top window line File entry to point at a file entry that matches the\ncurrent display setting, if necessary.\nIf the current file entry is marked as deleted and file view setting is\n\"only saved files\", then try to move to next or previous saved file without wrapping\nbeyond end or start of list.\n\nreturn Fc = 1, if File Entry couldn't be updated (list is empty according to view setting)\nOZ source name: AdjustWindowFileEntryPtr."},
        "5020": {"comment":"BHL = 0?"},
        "5023": {"comment":"nothing to update!"},
        "5030": {"comment":"top window line is an active file, no adjustment needed"},
        "5035": {"comment":"top file entry is marked as deleted, and deleted file view is active"},
        "5039": {"comment":"updated the top line File entry to an active file"},
        "5043": {"comment":"reached end of list,"},
        "5046": {"comment":"try to get a previous active file entry"},
        "5049": {"comment":"and update to that..."},
        "5051": {"comment":"no active files available, return Fc = 1"},
        "5054": {"synopsis":"adjust the current file entry pointer relative to the Window top line file entry\nOZ source name: AdjustFileEntryPtr."},
        "5060": {"comment":"position File Cursor relative to Window File Ptr"},
        "5066": {"comment":"File Entry cursor relocated according to file bar position in window"},
        "5067": {"comment":"get next file entry according to display setting"},
        "5070": {"comment":"reached end of list before the current File Bar position"},
        "5075": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: adjustFileBarPosn."},
        "5079": {"comment":"the new File Bar Position points at last file entry in list"},
        "5087": {"comment":"BHL --> (CursorFilePtr), indicate no files (pointer = 0)"},
        "5090": {"comment":"BHL --> (WindowFilePtr), indicate no files (pointer = 0)"},
        "5093": {"comment":"get cursor out of file window into menu window..."},
        "5097": {"synopsis":"Cache file entries for current view mode from beginning of file card until current\nfile entry in BHL, or all file entries.\n\nCaching is used for fast display of <Last File Entry> and <Page Up> browsing.\n\nThe file entries will be be stored as three-byte entities beginning at (buffer+3),\nonwards. (buffer) contains three zeroes to indicate bottom-of-file-list.\nA pointer (16bit) will be returned that indicates the current file entry. The cache\ncan store 512 entries. This size is defined by size of <buffer> + <buf1> + <buf2> +\n<buf3> = 1024 + 128 + 128 + 256 = 1536 / 3 = 512.\nLast entry + 1 contains three zeroes to define top of file list.\n\nThe cache needs to be built be before each <Page Up> or <Top File> cursor move\ncommand.\nEntry: A = 0: cache all file entries in file area (BHL not used); A <> 0: cache only file\nentries until current current entry.; BHL = current file entry.\nExit: Fc = 1; No entries or no file area found.; Fc = 0; A(in) = 0,; DE = pointer to last\nfile entry in file area cache (current view).; BHL = last file entry pointer in current\nslot; A(in) <> 0,; DE = pointer to current file entry in file area cache (current view).;\nBHL = BHL(in)."},
        "5108": {"comment":"remember current file entry"},
        "5115": {"comment":"(buffer) = 0, DE points at first cache entry"},
        "5118": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "5124": {"comment":"couldn't get the first file entry..."},
        "5126": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: cache_entries_loop.","comment":"(DE) <- BHL, DE = DE + 3"},
        "5130": {"comment":"build cache to current file entry?"},
        "5133": {"comment":"BHL = GetNextFileEntry(BHL) (current view)"},
        "5136": {"comment":"reached end of file area.."},
        "5140": {"comment":"Fc = 0, indicate no error"},
        "5143": {"comment":"point at start of current cached file entry in BHL"},
        "5145": {"comment":"BHL <- (DE)"},
        "5152": {"synopsis":"Called by CacheFileEntries for each cached entry when it caches only up to the current\nentry: compares BHL with the entry at (IX+0..2) (flentry). When they match, it drops its\nreturn address and leaves CacheFileEntries with Fc = 0 and the cache ending at this entry;\notherwise it returns.\nEntry: BHL = file entry; IX = flentry, the entry to stop at.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL (when not equal)."},
        "5171": {"comment":"stop caching at found BHL file entry..."},
        "5172": {"comment":"(pop return address)"},
        "5173": {"comment":"Fc = 0..."},
        "5176": {"comment":"caching not reached file entry..."},
        "5178": {"synopsis":"Stores the 3-byte file entry pointer BHL at (DE) in the order L, H, B, and advances DE.\nEntry: BHL = file entry; DE = cache slot.\nExit: DE = DE + 3.\nKeeps: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"store BHL at (DE), DE = DE+3"},
        "5202": {"synopsis":"Get previous cached file entry.\nOZ source name: GetPrevCachedFilePtr.\nEntry: DE = pointer to current cached file entry."},
        "5205": {"synopsis":"Entry inside GetPrevCachedFilePtr: reads the cached file entry at (DE) into BHL. An all-zero\nentry marks either end of the cached list.\nOZ source name: GetCachedFileEntry.\nEntry: DE = cache slot.\nExit: Fc = 0: BHL = file entry.\nError: Fc = 1, BHL = 0: beyond the end of the list.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE."},
        "5218": {"comment":"reached beyond first file entry"},
        "5221": {"synopsis":"constants"},
        "5385": {"synopsis":"Start of the file area window's banner, \"FILE AREA - CURSOR SELECTS \" (no terminator):\nFileAreaBannerText copies it and appends allfiles_banner or savedfiles_banner."},
        "5412": {"synopsis":"End marker of filearea_banner, used to compute its length, and the start of allfiles_banner,\n\"SAVED & DELETED FILES\" (no terminator), the banner ending while deleted files are shown.\nOZ source name: filearea_banner_end."},
        "5433": {"synopsis":"End marker of allfiles_banner, and the start of savedfiles_banner, \"ONLY SAVED FILES\" (no\nterminator), the banner ending while only active files are shown.\nOZ source name: allfiles_banner_end."},
        "5449": {"synopsis":"End marker of savedfiles_banner, and the start of norm_sq: the VDU code turning tiny and\ngrey text off, null-terminated, sent by NormalAttrText.\nOZ source name: savedfiles_banner_end."},
        "5455": {"synopsis":"VDU string sent by TinyAttrText before a deleted file entry: tiny and grey on, \"DEL\", grey\noff; null-terminated."},
        "5468": {"synopsis":"Marker shown after the last file entry: grey off, then \" END \" in tiny, underlined, reverse\ntext; null-terminated. Shown by DisplayFile."},
        "5490": {"synopsis":"VDU code 1, SD_UP (stdio.def: scroll upwards), null-terminated; MoveFileBarUp sends it\nbefore drawing a new top line."},
        "5493": {"synopsis":"VDU code 1, SD_DWN (stdio.def: scroll downwards), null-terminated; MoveFileBarDown sends it\nbefore drawing a new bottom line."},
        "5496": {"synopsis":"system definitions\nFlashStore popdown variables\n\nDisplay name and size of stored files on Flash Eprom."},
