        "5630": {"synopsis":"Writes the catalogue line for one file entry to the listing file: an \"F \" (active) or \"d \"\n(deleted) mark, the file name padded with spaces, the size right-justified, and a CR; the\n54-byte line goes out through WriteLine (OS_Mv).\nEntry: Fz = 0 active, Fz = 1 deleted (from EP_Stat); BHL = file entry; name at buffer+2; IX\n= file handle.\nChanges: AF, DE; (flen).\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "5640": {"comment":"get size of File Entry in CDE"},
        "5659": {"comment":"find null-terminator"},
        "5664": {"comment":"and pad with spaces after filename"},
