        "5671": {"comment":"the 24bit integer..."},
        "5677": {"comment":"null-terminate string"},
        "5680": {"comment":"HL = length of Ascii integer, DE = start of Ascii integer"},
        "5683": {"comment":"DE = length of..."},
        "5688": {"comment":"DE = pointer to new right-justified Ascii integer location"},
        "5690": {"comment":"Ascii integer right-justified"},
        "5701": {"comment":"List file data to Pipedream document"},
        "5707": {"synopsis":"Puts the mark \"F \" (active file) at buffer for CatalogueFile; falls into the shared store\n(dispsq). The flags are left alone.\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE = buffer + 1.\nChanges: A, DE."},
        "5711": {"synopsis":"Puts the mark \"d \" (deleted file) at buffer for CatalogueFile. The flags are left alone.\nEntry: none.\nExit: DE = buffer + 1.\nChanges: A, DE."},
        "5713": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: dispsq."},
        "5722": {"synopsis":"Entry: bc = length of data; hl = pointer to data; ix = file handle."},
        "5728": {"synopsis":"Copies the default listing file name, \"/filearea.pdd\" and its terminator, to (DE), after the\nRAM device name that GetDefaultRamDevice wrote.\nOZ source name: GetDefaultListingFilename.\nEntry: DE = destination.\nExit: DE = past the terminator; BC = 0.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL."},
        "5737": {"synopsis":"Base banner of the catalogue command's window, \"CATALOGUE FILES [\" and a terminator, passed\nto FileAreaBannerText with its length (catlg_banner_end - catlg_banner)."},
        "5755": {"synopsis":"End marker of catlg_banner, and the start of catlg_msg: \" List Catalogue to PipeDream file.\"\nafter a new line, null-terminated."},
        "5792": {"synopsis":"Prompt \" Filename: \" with the cursor turned on, null-terminated: the catalogue command's\nfile name prompt."},
