        "10829": {"comment":"redraw main catalogue window for format command interaction..."},
        "10835": {"comment":"the selected slot..."},
        "10838": {"synopsis":"Formats the file area in the current slot (curslot), after asking:\n1. Clears the greyed screen, updates the statistics (FileEpromStats) and opens the \"FORMAT\nFILE AREA ON FLASH CARD\" window.\n2. Looks for a file area with OS_Epr EP_Req. With one, it warns \"Re-format File Area in slot\nn (All data is lost).\"; without one, it says there is no file area for the card's\napplications (NoAppFileAreaMsg) or that the Flash Card is empty.\n3. Asks \"Format (create new) file area in slot n?\" (default No) and returns on No.\n4. Formats with OS_Fep FEP_FFMT, then resets the file area information (PollFileArea).\n5. Shows \" File Area formatted.\" and waits for SPACE; on an error it shows \"File Area not\nformatted properly!\" and resets the watermark (ResetWatermark).\nEntry: (curslot) = slot to format.\nExit: Fc = 0, Fz = 1, formatted; Fz = 0, the user answered No or ESC."},
        "10850": {"comment":"C = (curslot)"},
        "10856": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "10863": {"comment":"C = slot number..."},
        "10874": {"comment":"\"Empty Flash Card in slot x\""},
        "10882": {"comment":"\"Re-format File Area (All data will be lost).\""},
        "10894": {"comment":"signal No to caller..."},
        "10906": {"comment":"C = current slot"},
        "10909": {"comment":"erase blocks of file area in slot C, and blow \"oz\" header at top"},
        "10913": {"comment":"reset file area information"},
        "10917": {"comment":"or at top of free area."},
        "10931": {"comment":"Signal success (Fc = 0, Fz = 1)"},
        "10945": {"synopsis":"Return no of formatable file areas, available in Flash Cards in slots 0-3.\nOZ source name: PollFileFormatSlots.\nEntry: None.\nExit: A = formatable file areas (one for each slot, 0 - 3).; C = slot number for a default\nformatable File Area (if A>0)."},
        "10948": {"comment":"point to slot 0"},
        "10952": {"comment":"begin with slot 0"},
        "10954": {"comment":"counter of available file eproms"},
        "10956": {"comment":"preserve slot number..."},
        "10959": {"comment":"check if there's a File Card in slot C"},
        "10966": {"comment":"active or potential file area found, check if there's format support"},
        "10971": {"comment":"Formatable Flash Card found in slot"},
        "10973": {"comment":"size of Flash File Area in 16K banks"},
        "10985": {"comment":"empty, formattable flash card has B banks available..."},
        "10989": {"comment":"indicate no formatable flash file area"},
        "11001": {"comment":"store total of Formatable Flash File Areas"},
        "11005": {"comment":"no formatable file areas found..."},
        "11010": {"comment":"get default formatable slot in c, starting at 3..."},
        "11011": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: check_default_loop."},
        "11022": {"comment":"orignal B restored"},
        "11024": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "11026": {"synopsis":"Validate the Flash Card/UV Eprom erase/write functionality in the specified slot.\nIf the Card in the specified slot contains an Intel chip, the slot must be 3 for format,\nsave and delete functionality.\nIf the Card in the specified slot contains an UV Eprom, the slot must be 3 for erasing,\nsaving files and creating file header.\nReport an error to the caller with Fc = 1, if an Intel Flash chip was recognized\nin all slots except 3.\nReport an error if to the caller with Fc = 1, if an UV Eprom (with a file area) was\nrecognized in all slots except 3.\n\n(This routine is called by format, save & delete functionality in FlashStore)\nEntry: C = slot number.\nExit: Fz = 1, if a Flash Card is available in the current slot (Fz = 0, no Flash Card\navailable!); B = size of card in 16K banks; Fc = 1, if no erase/write support is available\nfor current slot.\nChanges: F, B.\nKeeps: A, C, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11042": {"comment":"Fz = 0, indicate no Flash Card available in slot"},
        "11043": {"comment":"Fc = 1, indicate no erase/write support either..."},
        "11049": {"comment":"is UV Eprom in slot 3?"},
        "11053": {"comment":"Fz = 0, indicate UV Eprom"},
        "11054": {"comment":"Fc = 0, write/erase files supported"},
        "11056": {"comment":"Fz = 0, indicate UV Eprom"},
        "11057": {"comment":"Fc = 1, no erase/write support"},
        "11064": {"comment":"erase/write works for all flash cards in slot 3 (Fc=0, Fz=1)"},
        "11069": {"comment":"Intel flash chip found in slot 0,1 or 2."},
        "11071": {"comment":"No, we found an AMD/compatible Flash chip (Fc=0, Fz=1)"},
        "11074": {"comment":"(Fz=1, indicate that Flash is available..)"},
        "11075": {"comment":"no erase/write support in slot 0,1 or 2 with Intel Flash..."},
        "11077": {"comment":"A restored (f changed)"},
        "11079": {"comment":"C restored (B = total of 16K banks on card)"},
        "11080": {"comment":"DE restored"},
        "11081": {"comment":"HL restored"},
        "11084": {"comment":"A restored (f changed)"},
        "11089": {"synopsis":"Check/Fetch Flash Card ID (Manufacturer & Device Code)\nEntry: C = Slot Number.\nExit: Register status from FlashEprCardId library routine; (flashid) variable updated: FFFF\n= no Flash Card found, otherwise HL -> (flashid)."},
        "11107": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: disp_filefmt_ask_msg."},
        "11116": {"synopsis":"constants"},
        "11203": {"synopsis":"String: \"File Area not formatted properly!\", CR LF, 0. Shown by formaterr."},
        "11239": {"synopsis":"String: \"FORMAT FILE AREA ON FLASH CARD\", 0. The banner of the format command's window."},
        "11270": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, flash on (1,\"F\"), \" Formatting File Area ... \", flash off, 0. Printed while\nOS_Fep formats the file area."},
        "11303": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, \" File Area formatted.\", CR LF, 0. Shown after a successful format."},
        "11329": {"synopsis":"Table of 2 words for DispSlotErrorMsg: the addresses of reformat1_msg and reformat2_msg,\nprinted on either side of the slot number."},
        "11333": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, bold on (1,\"B\"), \"Re-format File Area in slot \", 0. The first half of the\nre-format warning (reformat_msgs)."},
        "11366": {"synopsis":"String: \" (All data is lost).\", bold off (1,\"B\"), 0. The second half of the re-format\nwarning (reformat_msgs)."},
        "11389": {"synopsis":"Table of 2 words for DispSlotErrorMsg: the addresses of filefmt_ask1_msg and\nfilefmt_ask2_msg, printed on either side of the slot number."},
        "11393": {"synopsis":"String: cursor on (1,\"2+C\"), CR, \"Format (create new) file area in slot \", 0. The first half\nof the format question (filefmt_msgs)."},
        "11437": {"synopsis":"String: \"? \", 0. The second half of the format question (filefmt_msgs)."},
        "11440": {"synopsis":"Evaluate Standard Z88 Application ROM Format (Front DOR/ROM Header).\n\nReturn Standard Application ROM \"OZ\" status in slot x (0, 1, 2 or 3).\n\nFailure:\nFc = 1,\nA = RC_ONF, Application Eprom not found\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Apr-Aug 1998, Aug 2006, Aug 2012\nEntry: C = slot number (0, 1, 2 or 3).\nExit: Success:; Fc = 0,; A = Application Eprom type (with Rom Front Dor):; $80 = external\nEPROM,; $81 = system/internal OZ ROM,; $82 = external RAM; B = size of reserved Application\nspace in 16K banks.; C = size of physical Application Card in 16K banks.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11442": {"comment":"slot C"},
        "11445": {"comment":"top 256 byte page of top bank in slot C"},
        "11448": {"comment":"Convert to physical pointer..."},
        "11456": {"comment":"get Application ROM type ($80 or $81)"},
        "11457": {"comment":"offset $FC"},
        "11462": {"comment":"size of reserved Application space, $3FFC"},
        "11466": {"comment":"\"OZ\" watermark not found..."},
        "11468": {"comment":"Application Rom found"},
        "11471": {"comment":"invalid Application Type Code..."},
        "11473": {"comment":"If FRONT DOR is located in a RAM card, return type $82"},
        "11476": {"comment":"D = size of reserved Application space (16K bank entities)"},
        "11477": {"comment":"E = Application ROM Type Code ($80 or $81)"},
        "11482": {"comment":"C = physical card size (16K bank entities)"},
        "11483": {"comment":"B = size of reserved Application space (16K bank entities)"},
        "11484": {"comment":"A = Application ROM Type Code ($80 or $81)"},
        "11485": {"comment":"original HL restored"},
        "11486": {"comment":"original DE restored"},
        "11494": {"synopsis":"Calculate physical size of Card by scanning for \"OZ\" header from\nbank $3E downwards in available 1MB slot.\n\nHL = offset $3F00 (mapped to free segment in address space).\nEntry: B = top bank of slot containing Front DOR.; A = size of reserved Application space\n(16K bank entities).\nExit: A = physical size of card in 16K entities.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11495": {"comment":"preserve top bank number in slot"},
        "11498": {"comment":"TopBank - ReservedSpace"},
        "11499": {"comment":"begin parsing at bank below reserved appl. space"},
        "11502": {"comment":"parse max. 64 - ReservedSpace banks..."},
        "11512": {"comment":"slot size always max 64 * 16K banks..."},
        "11519": {"comment":"Card Size = TopBank - TopBank' (0-64)"},
        "11520": {"comment":"Fc = 0..."},
        "11523": {"comment":"Card was 1MB..."},
        "11526": {"synopsis":"Entry: A = original Application Card Type Code ($80 or $81); BHL = <top bank> $3F00.\nExit: A = $82, if FRONT DOR in RAM card, otherwise original code.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11531": {"comment":"get low byte card ID"},
        "11538": {"comment":"try to write another value to \"RAM\""},
        "11543": {"comment":"then read it back"},
        "11546": {"comment":"changed?"},
        "11549": {"comment":"Eprom Card - return original type code"},
        "11555": {"comment":"write back original card id"},
        "11558": {"comment":"return $82 for RAM based application card"},
        "11560": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: exit_CheckRamCard."},
        "11564": {"synopsis":"Check for \"OZ\" watermark at bank B, offset $3FFE.\n\nFailure:\nFz = 0,\n\"OZ\" watermark not found.\nEntry: B = Bank (usually $3F, mapped to slot X) containing possible Front DOR.; HL = offset\n$3F00 (mapped to free segment).\nExit: Success:; Fz = 1,; \"OZ\" watermark found in bank B.\nChanges: F.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "11575": {"comment":"'OZ' ?"},
        "11579": {"comment":"original A restored"},
        "11581": {"comment":"Fz = ?"},
        "11582": {"synopsis":"Convert relative BHL pointer for slot number A (0 to 3) to absolute\npointer, addressed for binding MS_S1 segment.\n\nInternal Support Library Routine.\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, April 1998, July 2006, Aug 2012\nEntry: A = slot number (0 to 3); BHL = relative pointer.\nExit: BHL pointer, absolute addressed for physical slot A, and free segment.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IX, IY."},
        "11584": {"comment":"clear before masking to assure proper effect..."},
        "11586": {"comment":"only slot 0 - 3 allowed..."},
        "11589": {"comment":"Slot number A converted to slot mask"},
        "11593": {"comment":"slot 0 rom bank range is $00 - $1F"},
        "11596": {"comment":"B = converted to physical bank of slot A"},
        "11601": {"comment":"for bank I/O (outside this executing code)"},
        "11602": {"comment":"offset mapped for MS_S1 segment"},
        "11604": {"synopsis":"Read byte at base record pointer in BHL, offset A.\nByte is returned in A.\n\nIf B<>0, the byte is read from extended address.\nIf B=0, the byte is read from local address space.\n\nRegister affected on return:\n..BCDEHL/IXIY same\nAF....../.... different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, 1997, Sep 2004, Oct 2005, Aug 2012"},
        "11610": {"comment":"add offset to pointer"},
        "11615": {"comment":"pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "11617": {"comment":"page in bank at C = Safe MS_S1 segment"},
        "11618": {"comment":"read byte at extended or local address"},
        "11619": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "11624": {"synopsis":"Read 16bit word at record defined as extended (base) address in BHL, offset A.\n\nIf B<>0, the 16bit word is read from extended address.\nIf B=0, the 16bit word is read from local address space.\n\nReturn 16bit word in DE.\n\nRegister affected on return:\nA.BC..HL/IXIY same\n.F..DE../.... different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, July 1998, Sep 2004, Oct 2005"},
        "11629": {"comment":"add offset to pointer"},
        "11634": {"comment":"pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "11636": {"comment":"page in bank at C = Safe MS_S1 segment"},
        "11639": {"comment":"read 16bit word at extended or local address"},
        "11640": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "11644": {"synopsis":"Read long integer in de'bc' at base record pointer in BHL, offset A.\n\nlong integer is read from extended address.\n\nRegister affected on return:\nA.BCDEHL/IXIY .......  same\n.F....../.... afbcdehl different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, 1997, Sep 2004, Oct 2005"},
        "11650": {"comment":"add offset to pointer"},
        "11655": {"comment":"pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "11657": {"comment":"page in bank at C = Safe MS_S1 segment"},
        "11669": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "11674": {"synopsis":"Set byte in C, at base record pointer in BHL, offset A.\n\nRegister affected on return:\nA.BCDEHL/IXIY same\n.F....../.... different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, 1995-97, Sep 2004, Oct 2005, Aug 2012"},
        "11680": {"comment":"add offset to pointer"},
        "11685": {"comment":"pointer adjusted for reading bank in segment 1"},
        "11687": {"comment":"page in bank at C = Safe MS_S1 segment"},
        "11689": {"comment":"write byte at extended or local address"},
        "11690": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "11692": {"comment":"original BC restored..."},
        "11696": {"synopsis":"Unsigned 8bit division\nEntry: H = Dividend; L = Divisor.\nExit: Fc = 0, division completed; H = Quotient; L = Remainder; Fc = 1,; A = RC_Dvz (divide\nby 0).\nChanges: ......./IXIY same, AF...HL/.... different."},
        "11709": {"comment":"advancing a bit"},
        "11711": {"comment":"..."},
        "11712": {"comment":"checking if the divisor divides the digits chosen (in A)"},
        "11713": {"comment":"if not, advance without subtraction"},
        "11715": {"comment":"subtracting the divisor"},
        "11716": {"comment":"and setting the next digit of the quotient"},
        "11719": {"comment":"H = quotient, L = remainder"},
        "11723": {"synopsis":"ToLower - convert character to lower case if possible.\n\n..BCDEHL/IXIY  same\nAF....../....  different\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Copyright (C) InterLogic 1995\nEntry: A = ASCII byte.\nExit: A = converted ASCII byte.","comment":"if A <= 'Z'  &&"},
        "11727": {"comment":"if A >= 'A'"},
        "11730": {"comment":"then A = A + 32"},
        "11733": {"comment":"if A <= $DE  &&"},
        "11736": {"comment":"if A >= $C0"},
        "11739": {"comment":"then A = A + 32"},
        "11742": {"synopsis":"Create filename and directory path.\n\nTry to create the specified filename using OP_OUT. If a directory path is\nspecified, it will automatically be created if not defined in the filing\nsystem.\n\nThe filename must not contain wildcards (standard convention). However if a\nRAM device is not specified, it will automatically be included (the current)\ninto the filename.\n\nThe buffer of the filename must have space to get itself expanded with a\ndevice name (additional 6 bytes).\n\nThe filename pointer may not point in segment 2, since GN_FEX is unreliable\nin that segment.\n\nThe routine deletes an existing file without warning.\n\nout, if successful:\nix = file handle\nfc = 0, file (and directory) successfully created\n(hl) = filename may have been expanded\n\nout, if failed:\nfc = 1, unable to create file (directory)\na = error code:\nRC_IVF, Invalid filename\nRC_USE, File already in use\n\nDesign & programming by Gunther Strube, Copyright (C) 1995\nEntry: bhl = pointer to null-terminated filename, (b = 0, means local).\nChanges: AF, IX.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, IY.","comment":"preserve original BC"},
        "11743": {"comment":"preserve original DE"},
        "11744": {"comment":"preserve original HL"},
        "11745": {"comment":"preserve original IY"},
        "11748": {"comment":"IY points at start of filename"},
        "11752": {"comment":"pointer to filename is local"},
        "11759": {"comment":"MS_Sx"},
        "11760": {"comment":"page filename into segment"},
        "11761": {"comment":"preserve old bank binding"},
        "11766": {"comment":"preserve error status..."},
        "11767": {"comment":"restore previous bank binding"},
        "11780": {"synopsis":"Create the filename\nEntry: HL = pointer to filename."},
        "11786": {"comment":"find null-terminator"},
        "11790": {"comment":"length = end - start"},
        "11795": {"comment":"length of buffer + 6 (max. length 255 bytes)"},
        "11796": {"comment":"c = length of buffer"},
        "11799": {"comment":"hl = pointer to filename"},
        "11800": {"comment":"de = pointer to output"},
        "11806": {"comment":"file created successfully, return..."},
        "11809": {"comment":"if error != RC_ONF"},
        "11811": {"comment":"return error"},
        "11813": {"synopsis":"Entry inside openfile, taken when GN_Opf fails with RC_ONF (object not found): expands the\nfilename with GN_Fex, creates the missing directories of its path (createpath) and jumps\nback to openfile to create the file again.\nEntry: HL = filename (local pointer, B = 0); DE = scratch buffer; C = its size.\nExit: as openfile (Fc = 0, IX = handle of the file opened for output).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_IVF when the name has wildcards or no file name; Fc = 1, A = error\ncode of GN_Fex or of a directory that could not be made.","comment":"first expand filename"},
        "11816": {"comment":"invalid filename"},
        "11818": {"comment":"pre-load Fc = 1 & A = RC_IVF, if errors"},
        "11821": {"comment":"wildcards were used..."},
        "11826": {"comment":"filename not specified..."},
        "11827": {"comment":"fc = 0"},
        "11828": {"comment":"deduct filename segment"},
        "11829": {"comment":"deduct device name segment"},
        "11830": {"comment":"hl points at null-terminator"},
        "11831": {"comment":"create directory path..."},
        "11834": {"comment":"then try to create file again..."},
        "11836": {"comment":"couldn't create directory, return..."},
        "11837": {"synopsis":"create directory sub-paths, recursively.\nEntry: hl = pointer to null-terminator; b = number of directory path segments (levels) to\ncreate; c = length of filename.\nExit: fc = 0, directory path created successfully, otherwise fc = 1."},
        "11839": {"synopsis":"Entry inside createpath, the loop that scans backwards from HL for a '/' separator. At the\nseparator (found_separator) it ends the path there with a 0, creates the parent levels first\n(createpath again while B > 0), makes this level with mkdir and puts the '/' back.\nEntry: A = '/'; HL = position to scan back from; B = path levels to create; IY = name.\nExit: Fc = 0, the directory path exists.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL."},
        "11840": {"comment":"directory separator found at (hl)"},
        "11845": {"comment":"null-terminate directory path segment (level)"},
        "11849": {"comment":"if (pathlevel != 0) createpath(pathlevel, sep)"},
        "11853": {"comment":"sub-path couldn't be created..."},
        "11857": {"comment":"restore directory separator"},
        "11860": {"synopsis":"Creates one directory with GN_Opf OP_DIR, the name being the 0-terminated path at IY, and\nfrees the returned DOR handle with OS_Dor DR_FRE. A directory that already exists (RC_USE or\nRC_EXIS) counts as success.\nEntry: IY = directory path name.\nExit: Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code.\nKeeps: BC, HL.","comment":"preserve current level in B"},
        "11861": {"comment":"preserve length of scratch buffer in C"},
        "11862": {"comment":"preserve pointer to current separator"},
        "11865": {"comment":"local pointer (filename always paged in)"},
        "11867": {"comment":"HL points at start of filename"},
        "11868": {"comment":"DE points at scratch buffer"},
        "11871": {"comment":"mkdir pathname (returns DOR handle)"},
        "11878": {"comment":"in use (it exists)..."},
        "11882": {"comment":"already created..."},
        "11885": {"comment":"other error occurred"},
        "11889": {"comment":"free dor handle"},
        "11894": {"synopsis":"system definitions\nFlashStore popdown variables"},
        "11900": {"synopsis":"Display a centre-justified message, which is defined by two null-terminated strings.\nThe current slot number is displayed between the two strings.\nEntry: HL = Pointer to address block, containg (string1), (string2).\nChanges: HL.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, IX, IY."},
        "11931": {"synopsis":"Reads the address word at HL, for DispSlotErrorMsg's two-string tables.\nEntry: HL = pointer to a word.\nExit: HL = the word; DE = pointer past the word.\nChanges: DE, HL."},
        "11937": {"synopsis":"Shows, bold and centred, \"No File Area available on Card in slot n.\" with the current slot\n(DispSlotErrorMsg).\nEntry: (curslot) = slot number.\nChanges: HL."},
        "11943": {"synopsis":"Shows, bold and centred, \"Flash Card is empty in slot n.\" with the current slot\n(DispSlotErrorMsg).\nOZ source name: disp_empty_flcard_msg.\nEntry: (curslot) = slot number.\nChanges: HL."},
        "11949": {"synopsis":"Shows, centred, \"File Area not detected in slot n.\" with the current slot, greys the command\nwindow (DispCmdWindow) and jumps to FileEpromStats to update the file area statistics\nwindow. The commands jump here when the current slot has no file area.\nOZ source name: disp_no_filearea_msg.\nEntry: (curslot) = slot number."},
        "11955": {"comment":"Update the command window (Grey out)"},
        "11958": {"comment":"Update the File Area Statistics window"},
        "11961": {"synopsis":"Tells the user there are no files to show, without waiting for a key (DispErrMsgNoWait): \"NO\nFILES AVAILABLE IN FILE AREA\" when the file area has neither active nor deleted files (file)\n+ (fdel) = 0, otherwise \"NO FILES AVAILABLE IN CURRENT FILE VIEW\". The commands jump here\nwhen FilesAvailable gives Fz = 1.\nEntry: (file) = active files; (fdel) = deleted files.\nExit: Fz = 1 when the file area holds no files at all.\nChanges: DE, HL.","comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "11962": {"comment":"total active files"},
        "11965": {"comment":"total deleted files"},
        "11982": {"synopsis":"Fz & Fc flags are set according to SlotWriteSupport routine."},
        "12000": {"comment":"\"Press SPACE to resume\" ..."},
        "12006": {"synopsis":"Write Error message centre justified.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"preserve error status..."},
        "12021": {"synopsis":"Write Error message, and wait for SPACE key to be pressed.\nChanges: none.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, IY.","comment":"preserve error status..."},
        "12034": {"comment":"\"Press SPACE to resume\" ..."},
        "12041": {"comment":"ignore old AF..."},
        "12042": {"comment":"override the error status with RC_ESC"},
        "12048": {"synopsis":"constants\nOZ source name: no_appflarea_msgs."},
        "12052": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, bold on (1,\"B\"), \"No File Area available on Card in slot \", 0. The first half\nof NoAppFileAreaMsg's message (no_appflarea_msgs).\nOZ source name: no_appflarea1_msg."},
        "12096": {"synopsis":"String: \".\", bold off (1,\"B\"), 0. The second half of NoAppFileAreaMsg's message.\nOZ source name: no_appflarea2_msg."},
        "12100": {"synopsis":"Table of 2 words for DispSlotErrorMsg: the addresses of empty_fcard1_msg and\nempty_fcard2_msg, used by disp_emptycd_msg.\nOZ source name: empty_flcard_msgs."},
        "12104": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, bold on (1,\"B\"), \"Flash Card is empty in slot \", 0. The first half of\ndisp_emptycd_msg's message.\nOZ source name: empty_flcard1_msg."},
        "12137": {"synopsis":"String: \".\", bold off (1,\"B\"), 0. The second half of disp_emptycd_msg's message.\nOZ source name: empty_flcard2_msg."},
        "12141": {"synopsis":"Table of 2 words for DispSlotErrorMsg: the addresses of intslot_err1_msg and\nintslot_err2_msg, used by DispIntelSlotErr for an Intel Flash Card outside slot 3."},
        "12145": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, bold on (1,\"B\"), \"Intel Flash Card found in slot \", 0. The first half of the\nIntel Flash slot message (intelslot_msgs).\nOZ source name: intelslot_err1_msg."},
        "12181": {"synopsis":"String: \".\", bold off, CR LF, \"You can only format file area, save files or\", CR LF, \"delete\nfiles in slot 3.\", CR LF, 0. The second half of the Intel Flash slot message.\nOZ source name: intelslot_err2_msg."},
        "12258": {"synopsis":"Table of 2 words for DispSlotErrorMsg: the addresses of eprslot_err1_msg and\neprslot_err2_msg, used by DispIntelSlotErr for an EPROM outside slot 3."},
        "12262": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, bold on (1,\"B\"), \"EPROM found in slot \", 0. The first half of the EPROM slot\nmessage (epromslot_msgs).\nOZ source name: epromslot_err1_msg."},
        "12287": {"synopsis":"String: \".\", bold off, CR LF, \"You can only save files to Eprom in slot 3.\", CR LF,\n\"Further, files or EPROMs cannot be erased in the Z88.\", CR LF, 0. The second half of the\nEPROM slot message.\nOZ source name: epromslot_err2_msg."},
        "12393": {"synopsis":"Table of 2 words for DispSlotErrorMsg: the addresses of nofilearea1_msg and nofilearea2_msg,\nused by disp_no_fra_msg."},
        "12397": {"synopsis":"String: CR LF, bold on (1,\"B\"), \"File Area not detected in slot \", 0. The first half of\ndisp_no_fra_msg's message (nofilearea_msgs)."},
        "12433": {"synopsis":"String: \".\", CR LF, 0. The second half of disp_no_fra_msg's message. It has no bold toggle,\nso the bold switched on by nofilearea1_msg is not switched off here."},
        "12437": {"synopsis":"String: tiny on (1,\"2+T\"), \"NO FILES AVAILABLE IN FILE AREA\", tiny off (1,\"2-T\"), CR LF, 0.\nShown by no_files and by both no_active_files exits."},
        "12479": {"synopsis":"String: tiny on (1,\"2+T\"), \"NO FILES AVAILABLE IN CURRENT FILE VIEW\", tiny off (1,\"2-T\"), CR\nLF, 0. Shown by no_files when the file area has files but none in the current view."}
      }
