        "520": {"comment":"syntax error"},
        "523": {"synopsis":"Opens the file named at HL for output: sets the mode to OP_OUT and continues in OpenRead's\ncommon part (skip leading spaces, open with GN_Opf).\nEntry: HL = filename (local pointer).\nExit: IX = file handle; Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (from GN_Opf).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "527": {"synopsis":"Opens the file named at HL for input. Skips leading spaces, then calls GN_Opf with B = 0\n(local name), DE = 3 so no explicit name is kept, and C = $FF. OpenWrite enters the same\ncode with OP_OUT.\nEntry: HL = filename (local pointer).\nExit: IX = file handle; Fc = 0; HL = first non-space of the name.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (from GN_Opf).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX.\nKeeps: BC."},
        "531": {"comment":"skip spaces"},
        "540": {"comment":"NUL, ignore name"},
        "551": {"synopsis":"CLI script \".T>:PRT\", CR, \".S\", 0: tees the CLI's output to the printer, then ends its\ninput. DC_Alt starts it with DC_Icl ([]+P) when no CLI is running."},
        "562": {"synopsis":"CLI script \".T<:RAM.-/K.sgn\", CR, \".S\", 0: tees keyboard input into the file K.sgn, then\nends its input. DC_Alt starts it with DC_Icl ([]+K) when no CLI is running."},
        "565": {"synopsis":"Entry inside RedirInKsgn_cli: the filename \":RAM.-/K.sgn\", ended by CR. DC_Alt opens it with\nOpenWrite to rebind a running CLI's input tee ([]+K)."},
        "581": {"synopsis":"CLI script \".T>:RAM.-/S.sgn\", CR, \".S\", 0: tees the screen output into the file S.sgn, then\nends its input. DC_Alt starts it with DC_Icl ([]+S) when no CLI is running."},
        "584": {"synopsis":"Entry inside RedirOutSsgn_cli: the filename \":RAM.-/S.sgn\", ended by CR. DC_Alt opens it\nwith OpenWrite to rebind a running CLI's output tee ([]+S)."},
