        "3503": {"synopsis":"Reads CLI input up to and including the next CR, then clears CLIF_B_NOTBOL (at the start of\na line again).\nEntry: IY = CLI block (bound).\nExit: Fc = 0; A = CR.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (from ReadCliChar).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL."},
        "3516": {"synopsis":"Reads the rest of the CLI line as a filename and opens it for input (GetRedirectName,\nOpenRead).\nEntry: IY = CLI block (bound).\nExit: IX = file handle; Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "3523": {"synopsis":"Reads the rest of the CLI line as a filename and opens it for output (GetRedirectName,\nOpenWrite).\nEntry: IY = CLI block (bound).\nExit: IX = file handle; Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code."},
        "3530": {"synopsis":"Fills the CLI line buffer up to the end of the line (sets CLIF_B_FILLALL, FillCLIBuffer),\nthen falls into GetLineBuffer to point HL at it.\nEntry: IY = CLI block (bound).\nExit: HL = cli_LineBuffer in the CLI block; Fc = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (from FillCLIBuffer).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX."},
        "3538": {"synopsis":"Points HL at the CLI's line buffer.\nEntry: IY = CLI block (bound).\nExit: HL = IY + cli_LineBuffer; Fc = 0.\nChanges: F, HL.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "3549": {"synopsis":"Get running CLI, check for abort\nExit: Fc=0, IY=CLI; Fc=1."},
        "3554": {"comment":"acknowledge CLI/Escape, reset shift / <>"},
        "3556": {"comment":"no escape"},
        "3561": {"comment":"restore flags"},
        "3564": {"comment":"<>"},
        "3568": {"comment":"ESC - abort"},
        "3584": {"comment":"bind CLI into S1"},
        "3585": {"comment":"Fc = 0"},
        "3588": {"comment":"<> ESC - abort all"},
        "3593": {"synopsis":"BC stream offset, A stream bit"},
        "3602": {"comment":"stream not open"},
        "3604": {"comment":"close old stream and clear flag"},
        "3611": {"comment":"close file/stream"},
        "3616": {"comment":"!! 'ld a,c; cpl'"},
        "3625": {"comment":"set stream, set flag if not NULL"},
        "3644": {"synopsis":"Takes the next character of CLI input: tops up the line buffer with FillCLIBuffer, removes\nthe first byte and moves the rest down.\nEntry: IY = CLI block (bound).\nExit: A = C = character; Fc = 0; Fz = 1 when the character is 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code (from FillCLIBuffer).\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.\nKeeps: DE, IX."},
        "3670": {"comment":"move data to the beginning of buffer"},
        "3685": {"synopsis":"Reads the CLI's input stream into the free end of its line buffer with OS_Gbt and the stored\ntimeout. It reads one byte, or, when CLIF_B_FILLALL is set (it is then cleared), up to a CR\nor until the buffer is full. Bytes below $20 other than CR are dropped.\nEntry: IY = CLI block (bound).\nExit: Fc = 0 (also when the read failed but the buffer holds bytes).\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code when the read failed and the buffer is empty.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX (IX = input stream)."},
        "3692": {"comment":"IX=instream"},
        "3713": {"comment":"read one byte or buffer full"},
        "3726": {"comment":"read bytes until 0D or 20-FF"},
        "3730": {"comment":"get byte with timeout"},
        "3750": {"comment":"end at CR"},
        "3764": {"synopsis":"Reads the head of the CLI list, the most recently invoked CLI.\nEntry: none.\nExit: BHL = CLI block; Fz = 1 when no CLI is running; A = B or H or L.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: IY."},
        "3779": {"synopsis":"Update OZ in slot 0/1, defined via \"ozupdate.cfg\" file and OZ ROM bank files stored in :RAM.*\n\nThe config file has been parsed for OZ ROM target and bank files by Index command. This system call\nerases the AMD 512K flash chip, blows the bank files from RAM into the slot, completed by\na soft reset.\n\nThere's no fall-back if a partial update fails; the end-user must recover OZ manually.\n\nDesign & programming by:\nGunther Strube,\n(RomUpdate) Dec 1997-Apr 1998, Aug 2004, Aug 2006\n(OZ backport) Aug 2016\nOZ optimisations:\nThierry Peycru, Aug 2016\nEntry: B = total of OZ ROM banks to flash; C = slot 0/1 to blow OZ ROM; IX = points to array\nspace of max. 64 OZ ROM banks (1024K). Each entry has the following format:; byte 0: byte 1:\nbyte 2:; [first 64 byte sector of file] [bank of first sector] destination bank in slot.\nExit: Success:; Z88 soft rest and return to Index in new, booted OZ.; Failure:; Fc = 1; A =\nRC_Btl, Batt Low condition; A = RC_NFE, flash card not found in slot; A = RC_Wp, Intel Flash\nis \"write-protected\" in slot 0/1."},
        "3781": {"comment":"check for flash chip in slot C"},
        "3788": {"comment":"card not found in slot..."},
        "3791": {"comment":"A = flash type is FE_29F or FE_28F, is this an Intel flash chip?"},
        "3793": {"comment":"No, we found an AMD/STM/AMIC Flash chip (erase/write allowed in slot 0/1, Fc=0, Fz=1)"},
        "3795": {"comment":"indicate that Intel Flash is \"write-protected\".."},
        "3797": {"comment":"no erase/write support in slot 0,1 or 2 with Intel Flash..."},
        "3800": {"comment":"OS_Fep, A = FEP_CDID returned B = size of chip in 16K banks"},
        "3813": {"comment":"Disable Z80 CPU maskable int's"},
        "3814": {"comment":"ret ($C9) instruction replacing jump ($C3)"},
        "3816": {"comment":"ret will avoid NMI in case of power failure, flap open, card insertion"},
        "3819": {"comment":"address of soft copy of com register"},
        "3823": {"comment":"screen lcd off"},
        "3826": {"comment":"signal to blink com register to do the lcd..."},
        "3832": {"comment":"(update soft copy first)"},
        "3835": {"comment":"no interrupts get out of blink (GINT = 0)"},
        "3846": {"comment":"copied erase + flash routines to RAM area"},
        "3848": {"comment":"C = slot number"},
        "3851": {"comment":"B = card size (total banks) in slot C"},
        "3854": {"comment":"Execute on bottom of LOWRAM Stack, then soft reset..."},
        "3857": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: STARTFLASHROUTINE.","comment":"Erase the individual sectors, one at a time"},
        "3859": {"comment":"total of 16K banks on card -> total of 64K sectors on card."},
        "3861": {"comment":"sectors, from (total sectors-1) downwards and including 0"},
        "3862": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: erase_2xF_card_blocks."},
        "3864": {"comment":"sector number range is only 0 - 15..."},
        "3866": {"comment":"sector number * 4 (16K * 4 = 64K!)"},
        "3867": {"comment":"(convert to first bank no of sector)"},
        "3870": {"comment":"only slots 0, 1, 2 or 3 possible"},
        "3872": {"comment":"we're in slot 0, so flash chip can only be in lower 512K of slot 0"},
        "3874": {"comment":"then use upper 512K address lines (to be compatible with hybrid card)"},
        "3877": {"comment":"Converted to Slot mask $40, $80 or $C0"},
        "3878": {"comment":"the absolute bank which is the bottom of the sector"},
        "3879": {"comment":"preserve a copy of bank number in D"},
        "3880": {"comment":"bind sector to"},
        "3881": {"comment":"segment 1 (segment 2 & 3 contains OZ kernel banks)"},
        "3883": {"comment":"HL points into segment"},
        "3890": {"comment":"Erase sector in LOWRAM (ignore AF status of erased sector - we can't go back now),"},
        "3893": {"comment":"total sectors left to erase..."},
        "3900": {"comment":"total of banks to update to slot X..."},
        "3903": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: update_ozrom_loop."},
        "3904": {"comment":"start of bank (in S2) for destination in slot"},
        "3908": {"comment":"preserve destination pointer to current card bank"},
        "3912": {"comment":"get first sector number"},
        "3915": {"comment":"bank (of sector) to bind into segment..."},
        "3918": {"comment":"Use segment 1 to bind in bank of sector"},
        "3920": {"comment":"current sector bound into segment..."},
        "3928": {"comment":"HL = 00eeeeee 00000000"},
        "3930": {"comment":"-> 0000eeee ee000000"},
        "3932": {"comment":"HL points to start of sector in segment 1"},
        "3936": {"comment":"get next file sector number"},
        "3938": {"comment":"get bank of next file sector number"},
        "3939": {"comment":"point at start of current file sector contents"},
        "3942": {"comment":"preserve sector for next iteration of blow bank file"},
        "3943": {"comment":"if bank number = 0: then this is the last sector (c = length of sector)"},
        "3945": {"comment":"if bank number <> 0, then (complete) sector contents is 62 bytes..."},
        "3947": {"comment":"sector to be blown to bank no. in slot X"},
        "3952": {"comment":"remove slot mask of original destination bank number for bank file"},
        "3954": {"comment":"slot number"},
        "3958": {"comment":"slot number -> slot mask"},
        "3960": {"comment":"bank number in ozupdate.cfg converted to specified slot \"OZ.x\" number"},
        "3961": {"comment":"preserve size of sector in A (temporarily)"},
        "3964": {"comment":"segment 2 is now bound with bank of slot to be blown"},
        "3966": {"comment":"DE = current destination offset into bank (bound in S2)"},
        "3976": {"comment":"address of byte to be flashed in 'hl"},
        "3979": {"comment":"get byte from sector"},
        "3980": {"comment":"HL points at address to flash byte"},
        "3981": {"comment":"prepare the AMD command mode sequence"},
        "3984": {"comment":"and blow the byte to the flash chip"},
        "3993": {"comment":"blow next byte of sector..."},
        "3998": {"comment":"sector has been flashed, preserve pointer to next byte in bank to be blown for next sector"},
        "4003": {"comment":"(bank of) last sector was 0 (EOF)?"},
        "4004": {"comment":"all sectors flashed of 16K RAM bank file in slot, get next RAM bank file..."},
        "4006": {"comment":"still more sectors to flash; A = next sector number, B = bank of next sector"},
        "4013": {"comment":"point at next bank data entry"},
        "4016": {"comment":"blow next bank to slot..."},
        "4020": {"comment":"update successful"},
        "4027": {"comment":"enable interrupts from blink"},
        "4030": {"comment":"interrupts get out of blink (GINT = 1)"},
        "4032": {"comment":"jump instruction"},
        "4034": {"comment":"enable NMI"},
        "4037": {"comment":"ensure that RTC int's can fire again"},
        "4041": {"comment":"acknowledge any RTC interrupts that were signalled during update"},
        "4045": {"comment":"enable INT"},
        "4046": {"comment":"then soft reset to boot into new OZ ROM code"},
        "4047": {"synopsis":"Prepare AMD Command Mode sequense addresses.\nHL points into bound bank of Flash Memory\nOZ source name: AM29Fx_PrepCmdMode.\nExit: BC = $aa55; DE = address $x2AA (derived from HL); HL = address $x555 (derived from\nHL)."},
        "4048": {"comment":"B = Unlock cycle #1 code, C = Unlock cycle #2 code"},
        "4058": {"comment":"HL = address $x555"},
        "4061": {"comment":"DE = address $x2AA"},
        "4067": {"comment":"default error handler"},
        "4069": {"comment":"OZ V4.5 and later implements OS_Nq, NQ_Voz (verify OZ)"},
        "4074": {"comment":"This application only runs on latest ROM by principle"},
        "4079": {"comment":"return to Index in current running OZ... (not the OZ of these sources)"},
        "4081": {"synopsis":"Filename \":EPR.?/Boot.cli\", 0: a Boot.cli in any file area. Index tries it after RamBootCLI\nwhen it is started the first time.","comment":"The global EPR /Boot.cli filename (anywhere in any file area)"},
        "4097": {"synopsis":"Filename \":RAM.?/Boot.cli\", 0: a Boot.cli in any RAM device. Index tries it first when it is\nstarted the first time.","comment":"The global RAM /Boot.cli filename (anywhere in any RAM)"},
        "4113": {"synopsis":"Opens the named file for input (GN_Opf, with a 256-byte explicit name buffer on the stack)\nand starts a new CLI that reads it (DC_Icl with BHL = 0, IX = the file). When DC_Icl fails\nthe file is closed again.\nEntry: HL = filename (local pointer).\nExit: Fc = 0 when the CLI was started; when DC_Icl failed, Fc as OS_Cl returns it.\nError: Fc = 1, A = error code when the file cannot be opened.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX, AF'.","comment":"filename in DE"},
        "4119": {"comment":"filename in HL, stackbuffer in DE for explicit filename"},
        "4123": {"comment":"schedule a \"/Boot.cli\" to be executed by CLI..."},
        "4125": {"comment":"open - BHL=name (B=0, HL=local ptr), A=mode, DE=exp. name buffer, C=buflen"},
        "4135": {"comment":"Ups, not possible (file not found)..."},
        "4140": {"comment":"Invoke new CLI and use file as input..."},
        "4144": {"comment":"CLI could not be scheduled, close file handle"},
        "4147": {"comment":"and continue Index initialisation"},
        "4148": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: IndexEntry."},
