        "4227": {"comment":"Second, try to execute \":Epr.*/Boot.cli\""},
        "4233": {"synopsis":"Index's entry after its first run (and after the boot scripts were tried).\n1. When an application is marked to start at boot (pIdxAutoRunAppl), clears the mark and\nenters it.\n2. Otherwise reads the \"NAME\" mailbox (OS_Sr, SR_RPD) into App_Buff1; when it holds a name,\ngoes to AskInstall.\n3. Otherwise falls into IndexRedraw.\nEntry: none."},
        "4242": {"comment":"don't run again"},
        "4251": {"synopsis":"check mailbox for an install"},
        "4256": {"comment":"read mailbox"},
        "4258": {"comment":"with a file"},
        "4273": {"synopsis":"Redraws Index and falls into MainLoop. When an application ended with an error (IDXF2_ERROR\nin ubIdxFlags2), goes to ShowExitError instead. The commands jump here after changing the\ndisplay.\nEntry: none."},
        "4284": {"synopsis":"Index's command loop: reads a key with OS_In (marking IDXF1_B_INSIDEOZ while waiting) and\ncalls MayInitIndex before and after. On an error, RC_Quit exits Index with OS_Bye, RC_Draw\ngoes to IndexRedraw, anything else reads again. A key goes to main_2.\nEntry: none."},
        "4294": {"comment":"read a byte from std. input"},
        "4311": {"synopsis":"Entry inside MainLoop: dispatches a key. '0'-'3' go to cmd_ramcrd_sel, 'Y'/'N'/'y'/'n' to\ncmd_insrmv_sel, other plain keys are ignored. A 0 is followed by a command code; codes 1-15\njump through the table at main_3, others are ignored.\nEntry: A = key from OS_In."},
        "4351": {"comment":"if it isn't extended we ignore it"},
        "4359": {"comment":"read a byte from std. input"},
        "4369": {"comment":"validate input"},
        "4374": {"comment":"fetch command vector and execute"},
        "4384": {"synopsis":"Table of 15 words: Index's command handlers for command codes 1-15: right, left, up, down,\nenter, escape, kill, card, 0 (the purge command, removed), info, install, remove, nq,\nupdate, hard reset. Code 9 would jump to address 0."},
        "4400": {"comment":"cmd_purge"},
        "4415": {"comment":"Application exit"},
        "4417": {"synopsis":"Clears IDXF1_B_INSIDEOZ. When IDXF1_B_INIT is set, clears it and rebuilds Index: resets the\nselection (InitIndex), rescans the application keys (InitKeys) and redraws (DrawWindow).\nEntry: HL = ubIdxPubFlags.\nKeeps: AF."},
