        "5881": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column B, row C of the current window (1, \"3@\", X, Y).\nEntry: B = column; C = row.\nChanges: AF."},
        "5890": {"comment":"X pos"},
        "5895": {"comment":"Y pos"},
        "5898": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column A of the current line (1, \"2X\", X).\nEntry: A = column.\nChanges: AF."},
        "5911": {"synopsis":"Toggles the tiny font (1, \"T\").\nEntry: none."},
        "5917": {"synopsis":"Toggles reverse video (1, \"R\").\nEntry: none."},
        "5931": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to the top left of the current window and clears to the end of the window\n(1, \"2C\", $FE), clearing all of it.\nEntry: none."},
        "5944": {"synopsis":"Selects and initialises window 2, the application window (1, \"2I2\").\nEntry: none."},
        "5952": {"synopsis":"Selects and initialises window 3, the process window (1, \"2I3\").\nEntry: none."},
        "5960": {"synopsis":"Scrolls the current window up (1, $FF).\nEntry: none."},
        "5966": {"synopsis":"Applies the toggled display attributes to A characters from the cursor (1, \"2A\", A).\nEntry: A = number of characters.\nKeeps: A."},
        "5977": {"synopsis":"Index command \"card\" (code 8). Fills CardData, 3 bytes per slot 0-3 (RAM banks, file area\nbanks, ROM banks): RAM from OS_Nq NQ_Mfp, an application card's size from its header byte at\n$3FFC of the top bank (NQ_Slt says BU_ROM), the file area from OS_Epr EP_Req. Then it makes\nthe card window active (ubIdxActiveWindow = 2) and goes to IndexRedraw.\nEntry: none."},
        "5980": {"comment":"each device info block is 3 bytes"},
        "5985": {"comment":"start scan with slot 3, downwards..."},
        "5996": {"comment":"poll for total RAM in slot D"},
        "6004": {"comment":"no RAM found, is there a ROM / App Card?"},
        "6006": {"comment":"size of RAM card in 16K banks..."},
        "6009": {"comment":"top bank of slots 1-3 for ROM / App Cards is $3f"},
        "6015": {"comment":"top bank of ROM in slot 0 is $1f"},
        "6020": {"comment":"read slot type information"},
        "6022": {"comment":"no card?"},
        "6032": {"comment":"slot number -> to slot mask"},
        "6034": {"comment":"absolute (top) bank number of ROM / App Card"},
        "6041": {"comment":"size of ROM / App Card in 16K banks"},
        "6048": {"comment":"File Area in slot D?"},
        "6054": {"comment":"no File area, look in next slot.."},
        "6056": {"comment":"size of file area in 16K banks..."},
        "6063": {"comment":"loop thru slots 0-3"},
        "6065": {"comment":"card display"},
        "6203": {"synopsis":"GN_Win block of the CARDS window: window 4 with bars, shelf brackets and an 8-pixel banner,\ndrawn as a pop-up on a grey screen; X = 9, Y = 0, width 46, height 8; banner text at\ncards_banner."},
        "6210": {"synopsis":"Banner text \"CARDS\", 0, of CardWdBlock."},
        "6216": {"synopsis":"Prints the rows of the card window for slots 3 down to 0 (GetCardData, DisplayCard).\nEntry: CardData filled by cmd_card.\nExit: D = $FF; IY = slot 0's bytes in CardData."},
        "6232": {"synopsis":"Prints one slot's row of the card window: moves to column 0, row slot + 1, and prints the\nROM size at column 15, the file area at 25 and the RAM at 35 (PrintCardSize).\nEntry: D = slot; IY = the slot's 3 bytes in CardData (RAM, file area, ROM banks).\nKeeps: DE."},
        "6245": {"comment":"ROM"},
        "6253": {"comment":"EPROM"},
        "6261": {"comment":"RAM"},
        "6266": {"synopsis":"Prints a size in 16K banks as kilobytes at a column: C * 16 in a 4-character field followed\nby 'K' (GN_Pdn to the standard output), or \" -\" when C = 0.\nEntry: A = column; C = size in 16K banks.\nKeeps: DE."},
        "6274": {"comment":"get stdout"},
        "6284": {"comment":"*16"},
        "6307": {"comment":"BC to ASCII, 4 chars"},
        "6316": {"synopsis":"point IY to data of card A"},
        "6331": {"synopsis":"Clears the current line and prints \"Are you sure ? \" with the answer in ubIdxYesNo (\"Yes\" or\n\"No\"), then moves the cursor back onto the answer and switches the cursor on.\nEntry: ubIdxYesNo = 'Y'/'y' for yes, anything else for no.\nChanges: AF."},
        "6333": {"comment":"clear line"},
        "6392": {"synopsis":"Writes the centred \"PRESS ESC TO RESUME\" line in tiny font (ESC as its key symbol) with\nOS_Pout, then turns centring off again. Used by the info, install, remove and update windows\nbefore they wait for ESC.\nEntry: none (writes to the current window)."},
        "6426": {"synopsis":"Entry of FreeRAM command"},
        "6454": {"comment":"define a map of 64 pixels, associated with segment 2"},
        "6457": {"comment":"and create it..."},
        "6464": {"comment":"preserve pointer to base area of graphics"},
        "6467": {"comment":"read max. 10 characters"},
        "6469": {"comment":"read default device"},
        "6472": {"comment":"buffer for device name"},
        "6475": {"comment":"save pointer to buffer"},
        "6484": {"comment":"get (slot) number of default RAM device"},
        "6485": {"synopsis":"also called from Index main input loop, A = '0', '1', '2' or '3'.\nOZ source name: UpdateFreeSpaceRamCard."},
        "6488": {"comment":"slot number"},
        "6490": {"comment":"as internal integer"},
        "6493": {"comment":"get RAM device info"},
        "6496": {"comment":"- if available"},
        "6502": {"comment":"display \":RAM.\" at top of window"},
        "6530": {"comment":"then current select device number"},
        "6534": {"comment":"BACKSPACE (cursor on top of number)"},
        "6536": {"comment":"back to main index loop..."},
        "6537": {"synopsis":"Shows the FreeRAM details of a RAM card: the size column (DispCardSizeClmn), a cleared and\nredrawn page map (DispFreeRamMap), the card size and then jumps to the free space text\n(bytes and percentage).\nEntry: slotno, cardsize and freespace set by GetFreeSpace."},
        "6540": {"comment":"reset graphics map (no card present)"},
        "6543": {"comment":"display graphical view of card"},
        "6551": {"synopsis":"Shows FreeRAM for a slot without a RAM card: clears window 2 and the page map, then selects\nand clears window 3 and writes \"(None)\" there.\nEntry: A = error code from GetFreeSpace.\nKeeps: AF."},
        "6555": {"comment":"reset graphics map (no card present)"},
        "6558": {"comment":"select (and clear) window #3, then write \"(None)\""},
        "6578": {"synopsis":"Writes the card size as \"(<n>K)\" in window 3, where n = cardsize * 16.\nEntry: cardsize = size of the card in 16K banks."},
        "6597": {"comment":"cardsize * 16 (K)"},
        "6614": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: DispFreeSpaceInfo."},
        "6671": {"comment":"TotalBytes = <cardsize> * 16384"},
        "6690": {"comment":"FreeSpace / TotalBytes"},
        "6702": {"comment":"FreeSpace / TotalBytes * 100 (%)"},
        "6720": {"comment":"display free space in %"},
        "6729": {"synopsis":"Asks OS_Nq NQ_Mfp for the RAM in the slot held in slotno and stores the card size in banks\nin cardsize and the free space in bytes (free pages * 256) in freespace.\nEntry: slotno = slot number (0-3).\nExit: Fc = 0; cardsize, freespace (32-bit, low word first) set.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Onf when the slot holds no RAM device.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"scan slot x"},
        "6738": {"comment":"size of card in 16K banks..."},
        "6741": {"comment":"store free space in bytes..."},
        "6745": {"comment":"<free pages> * 256 bytes"},
        "6751": {"comment":"low byte, high byte sequense"},
        "6757": {"synopsis":"Draws the FreeRAM page map: one pixel for each used 256-byte page of the RAM card, each 16K\nbank being an 8x8 pixel character block, eight blocks to a row (128K).\n1. Binds the card's bottom bank, which holds the allocation table (slot 0: $21), into\nsegment 1, and the HIRES0 map area (GetMapAddress) into segment 2.\n2. For a card below 8 banks it computes a pixel factor by rotating 8 right once per bank\nabove one; otherwise one pixel per page.\n3. Reads the table from $4100 (2 bytes per page, non-zero = used) and plots each used page\n(plot_usedpage) while moving the pixel position (update_pixelptr) per pixel.\n4. Restores the segment 2 and segment 1 bindings.\nEntry: slotno, cardsize.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, AF', BC', DE', HL'."},
        "6761": {"comment":"slot number converted to bottom bank"},
        "6765": {"comment":"bottom bank in slot 0 for MAT is $21"},
        "6767": {"comment":"get bank of memory allocation table (MAT)"},
        "6768": {"comment":"(bottom of RAM card)"},
        "6770": {"comment":"and bind into segment 1."},
        "6773": {"comment":"Map area base address in BHL"},
        "6778": {"comment":"bind in map area in segment 2"},
        "6780": {"comment":"row counter in 8x8 matrix (0 - 7)"},
        "6783": {"comment":"D = column bit in 8x8 matrix (begin with leftmost)"},
        "6786": {"comment":"E = 8, eight 8x8 pixel matrixes per row"},
        "6787": {"comment":"size of card in 16K banks..."},
        "6790": {"comment":"actual number of banks"},
        "6791": {"comment":"data start at $0100"},
        "6794": {"comment":"parse table of B(anks) * 64 pages"},
        "6795": {"comment":"calculate the pixel scaling, if RAM card < 128K"},
        "6797": {"comment":"default 1 pixel per used page"},
        "6801": {"comment":"A = card size"},
        "6812": {"comment":"A = pixel factor"},
        "6817": {"comment":"total of pages in a bank..."},
        "6821": {"comment":"must be 00 if free"},
        "6830": {"comment":"page used, plot a pixel (scaled for current 128K row in map..."},
        "6834": {"comment":"prepare for next pixel position"},
        "6847": {"comment":"restore segment 2 binding.."},
        "6849": {"comment":"restore segment 1 binding.."},
        "6851": {"synopsis":"Plots one pixel of the page map: ORs the column bit D' into the byte at HL' + BC' (the\ncurrent row of the current 8x8 block). Works in the alternate set.\nEntry: HL' = block base; BC' = row (0-7); D' = column bit; map bound in segment 2.\nChanges: none (AF and HL' are kept)."},
        "6854": {"comment":"ptr to current row in matrix"},
        "6855": {"comment":"get current row of matrix"},
        "6857": {"comment":"\"plot\" point identifying used page"},
        "6862": {"synopsis":"Moves the page map's pixel position one row down in the current 8x8 block; after the eighth\nrow it calls new_column. Works in the alternate set.\nEntry: HL', BC', D', E' = the map position (see DispFreeRamMap).\nChanges: F, C', D', E', HL'."},
        "6863": {"comment":"next row of matrix..."},
        "6871": {"synopsis":"Moves the page map's pixel position to the next pixel column (column bit rotated right);\nwhen the bit leaves the block it calls next_matrix. Then starts again at row 0. Runs with\nthe alternate set swapped in by update_pixelptr.\nEntry: C = 8; D = column bit; HL = block base; E = blocks left in the row.\nExit: C = 0; D = next column bit.","comment":"in next pixel column (bit 7 -> bit 0)"},
        "6873": {"comment":"when bit arrives in Fc, all 64 bits (8x8 pixels) done"},
        "6876": {"comment":"begin at first row (next 8x8 pixel block)"},
        "6879": {"synopsis":"Moves the page map's position to the next 8x8 block: HL += BC (8 bytes on); counts the\nblocks of the row in E and reloads it with 8 when a row of eight blocks is done. Runs with\nthe alternate set swapped in.\nEntry: HL = block base; BC = 8; E = blocks left in the row.\nExit: HL = next block; E = blocks left (8 after a full row).","comment":"in next matrix"},
        "6881": {"comment":"8x8 matrix row still not complete"},
        "6885": {"synopsis":"Clears window 2 and writes the size labels beside the page map, right justified: one line\nper 128K row with the running card size in K (\"128K\", \"256K\", ...), or the card size alone\nfor a card below 128K.\nOZ source name: DispCardSizeColumn.\nEntry: cardsize = size of the card in 16K banks.","comment":"select (and clear) window #2"},
        "6890": {"comment":"window \"2\", right justify, ; no cursor no scrolling"},
        "6902": {"comment":"B = card size (in 16K banks)"},
        "6903": {"comment":"X = 0"},
        "6908": {"comment":"while B > 0"},
        "6909": {"comment":"if B-8 < 0 then"},
        "6913": {"comment":"i = B"},
        "6914": {"comment":"else"},
        "6916": {"comment":"i = 8"},
        "6920": {"comment":"X = X + i"},
        "6923": {"comment":"B = B - i"},
        "6927": {"comment":"X*16"},
        "6935": {"comment":"print str$(X*16) + \"K\""},
        "6940": {"synopsis":"Inline OS_Pout text inside DispCardSizeClmn: \"K \", CR, LF, null, written after each size\nlabel; the code continues after it with the jump back to the label loop."},
        "6945": {"comment":"end while"},
        "6947": {"synopsis":"Multiply HL * 16, result in HL."},
        "6952": {"synopsis":"Convert integer in HL (or BC) to Ascii string, which is written to (AscBuf)\nand null-terminated."},
        "6965": {"comment":"display integer"},
        "6971": {"synopsis":"Return base of Map area in BHL, adjusted for segment 2 address space"},
        "6975": {"comment":"get base address of map area (hires0) in BHL"},
        "6980": {"comment":"Base of map area adjusted to segment 2 for BHL"},
        "6982": {"comment":"preserve base of graphics area"},
        "6990": {"synopsis":"Clear graphics area, i.e. reset all bits in graphics (map)\nwindow of width x height (64 x 64) pixels."},
        "7003": {"comment":"de = base_graphics+1"},
        "7005": {"comment":"reset graphics window"},
        "7010": {"synopsis":"Selects and clears window 2 with OS_Pout (1,\"2C2\"). Shared by FreeRAM and the Index's ESC\nhandling.\nEntry: none."},
        "7012": {"comment":"select (and clear) window #2"},
        "7018": {"synopsis":"\"FREE RAM\" Window definition"},
        "7025": {"synopsis":"The FreeRAM window's banner text: \"FREE RAM\", null-terminated, named by FreeRamWindowDef."},
        "7034": {"synopsis":"Index command <>INFO (entry in the command table): shows the SYSTEM INFORMATION window.\n1. Gets the :OUT handle (NQ_Ohn) for the number output, opens the window (InfoWdBlock) and\nwrites the captions OZ, BUILD, MACHINE, TYPE, FREE MEMORY, BATTERY, FREE HANDLES.\n2. OZ version and slot (disp_ver); \"Z88\"; type \"expanded\" or \"unexpanded\" from OS_Frm\nFA_EOF; battery \"good\" or \"low\" from NQ_Btl.\n3. Revision (disp_rev) and the build's date and time, assembled in as constants, through\nGN_Dei, GN_Pdt and GN_Ptm.\n4. Free memory in K (OS_Frm FA_EXT divided by 1024) and free handles (OS_Frm FA_PTR).\n5. Sets the active window to 3 (info window, closed by ESC) and jumps to MainLoop.\nEntry: none. Does not return: jumps to MainLoop (IX is kept)."},
        "7039": {"comment":"stream to :OUT, used by GN_Pdt below"},
        "7052": {"comment":"invisible window area for entries"},
        "7161": {"comment":"left area"},
        "7195": {"comment":"MACHINE TYPE"},
        "7229": {"comment":"right area, 2 first row"},
        "7256": {"comment":"COMPILATION DATE & TIME"},
        "7262": {"comment":"convert to internal format"},
        "7276": {"comment":"century, C delimeter, zero blanking"},
        "7278": {"comment":"condensed form, '/' delimeter"},
        "7281": {"comment":"display compilation date"},
        "7307": {"comment":"display compilation time"},
        "7310": {"comment":"right area, 2 last row"},
        "7331": {"comment":"FREE MEMORY"},
        "7336": {"comment":"shift right deb 2 times on the right (div by 4)"},
        "7348": {"comment":"shift right debc 8 times i.e. 0deb (div by 256)"},
        "7353": {"comment":"in 64 bits buffer"},
        "7368": {"comment":"convert to decimal"},
        "7378": {"comment":"FREE HANDLES"},
        "7396": {"comment":"for cmd_escape"},
        "7404": {"synopsis":"Updated info window call"},
        "7405": {"comment":"reset updated flag in preserved area"},
        "7418": {"comment":"invisible window area for entries"},
        "7508": {"comment":"beep"},
        "7526": {"comment":"ESC command number (defined in MTH)"},
        "7531": {"synopsis":"Sub-routines"},
        "7537": {"comment":"result in DEBC"},
        "7545": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the info windows (SYSTEM INFORMATION and the <>NQ windows):\nwindow 2 with bars, shelf brackets and an 8-pixel banner on a greyed screen, at X = 9, Y =\n0, 64 wide and 8 high; banner pointer 0, so the banner comes in DE."},
        "7552": {"synopsis":"Banner text of the info window: \"SYSTEM INFORMATION\", null-terminated."},
        "7571": {"synopsis":"Writes \"rev. \" and the OZ revision as 8 hex digits: OS_Nq NQ_Roz returns it in DEBC, written\nD, E, B, C with OS_Hout.\nEntry: none.","comment":"REVISION NUMBER"},
        "7597": {"synopsis":"Writes the OZ version as \"<major>.<minor>\" from the low byte of OS_Frm FA_PTR (high nibble\nmajor, low nibble minor), then \" in slot 1\" when OS_Ploz says OZ is not running from slot 0.\nEntry: none.","comment":"MAJOR AND MINOR VERSION NUMBER"},
        "7609": {"comment":"I know that I'll have to handle version 10.10 one day !"},
        "7624": {"comment":"test slot 0"},
        "7628": {"comment":"internal"},
        "7643": {"synopsis":"The text \"unexpanded\", null-terminated. cmd_info writes it for an unexpanded Z88 and writes\nfrom 2 bytes on (\"expanded\") for an expanded one."},
        "7654": {"synopsis":"The text \"good\", null-terminated: cmd_info's battery state."},
        "7659": {"synopsis":"The text \"low\", null-terminated: cmd_info's battery state when NQ_Btl reports low."},
        "7663": {"synopsis":"Index command <>INS (entry in the command table): opens the INSTALL APPLICATION window and\nasks for the .APP filename with GN_Sip into App_Buff1 (up to 128 characters). On ENTER it\ngoes to AskInstall; otherwise it sets the active window to 0 and redraws the Index\n(IndexRedraw).\nEntry: none. Does not return."},
        "7698": {"comment":"ENTER command"},
        "7709": {"synopsis":"Sets the active window to 4 (install), redraws the install window and shows \"Install\n<filename>\", then asks \"Are you sure ?\" with Yes as the default (AreYousure) and jumps to\nMainLoop; ENTER there runs DoInstall.\nEntry: App_Buff1 = filename. Does not return."},
        "7751": {"synopsis":"Opens the INSTALL APPLICATION window (GN_Win with InstallWdBlock) and defines window 2 as\nits text area (58 x 6 at column 13, row 2), selected and cleared.\nEntry: none."},
        "7759": {"comment":"invisible window area"},
        "7775": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the install window: window 2 with bars, shelf brackets and an\n8-pixel banner on a greyed screen, at X = 9, Y = 0, 64 wide and 8 high; banner\nInstallBanner."},
        "7782": {"synopsis":"Banner text of the install window: \"INSTALL APPLICATION\", null-terminated."},
        "7802": {"synopsis":"Installs an application from RAM files: the .APP header and the .AP0 to .AP6 bank files\nnamed by App_Buff1. Run by ENTER after AskInstall.\n1. Unless the answer was 'y', sets window 0 and redraws the Index. Otherwise draws the\ninstall window and saves SP in App_Stack for the error exit.\n2. Copies 40 bytes of the .APP file to App_Tag (ci_copyfile) and checks the tag (APF_TAG),\nat most 8 banks and no patches; RC_Ftm otherwise.\n3. Opens a memory handle (OS_Mop) and allocates an installation handle (OS_Fn FN_AH,\nHND_INST) that keeps the memory handle.\n4. For each bank entry: works out the pages needed, finds a bank (OS_Fma, even when its\nApp_Even bit is set), allocates the area (OS_Axm) and loads the .AP<n> file into it\n(ci_copyfile); bank, offset page and length go to the Fma table (Fma_AP0, 4 bytes each).\n5. Takes the application DOR (App_DOR, or the son pointer at $3FC6 of relative bank 63 when\nit is 0), stores it in the installation handle and chains it after the last DOR under the\n:APP.- front DOR ($4060 in bank $21).\n6. Walks the new DOR chain and translates each DOR's bank numbers (segments, topics,\ncommands, help, tokens, brother) with ci_TranslateBank, counting the applications.\n7. Restores SP, polls the keys again (InitKeys), writes \"Installation completed.\" and waits\nfor ESC (PressEsc), then jumps to MainLoop.\nError: frees the installation handle, memory and file, stores the error code in\nubIdxErrorCode, sets IDXF2_B_ERROR and redraws the Index. Does not return."},
        "7803": {"comment":"Wd #0 if 'No'"},
        "7816": {"comment":"just an info wd"},
        "7826": {"comment":"save stack for return and error box"},
        "7831": {"comment":"UWS is in bank $20"},
        "7836": {"comment":"copy 40 bytes (patches are not handled)"},
        "7842": {"comment":"identifier"},
        "7859": {"comment":"no more than 8 banks"},
        "7866": {"comment":"patches non implemented"},
        "7885": {"comment":"allocate new handle"},
        "7887": {"comment":"type = installation handle"},
        "7889": {"comment":"do it (hl is preserved)"},
        "7894": {"comment":"keep MemHnd for uninstallation in INST handle"},
        "7900": {"comment":"given installation handle"},
        "7906": {"comment":"start of memory table (32+32 bytes)"},
        "7910": {"comment":"loop number (0-7)"},
        "7912": {"comment":"reload memory handle"},
        "7916": {"comment":"offset MSB = number of pages required"},
        "7919": {"comment":"length LSB"},
        "7922": {"comment":"length MSB = start page"},
        "7927": {"comment":"page required >= 1"},
