        "8246": {"comment":"could be $3F3FFF"},
        "8252": {"comment":"reload Token bank"},
        "8267": {"comment":"brother bank"},
        "8278": {"comment":"not zero, has brother (s)"},
        "8283": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "8284": {"comment":"repoll keys"},
        "8328": {"synopsis":"subroutines"},
        "8366": {"comment":"restore stack"},
        "8382": {"synopsis":"Frees the installation handle: clears App_InstHnd and calls OS_Fn FN_FH with B = HND_INST.\nEntry: IX = installation handle."},
        "8395": {"synopsis":"Closes the install's (or update's) memory handle: clears App_MemHnd and calls OS_Mcl, which\nfrees the memory allocated through it.\nEntry: IX = memory handle."},
        "8404": {"synopsis":"Closes the install's open file: clears App_FileHnd and calls GN_Cl.\nEntry: IX = file handle.\nExit: IX = 0.\nChanges: AF, HL, IX."},
        "8414": {"synopsis":"Tests IX for a null handle.\nEntry: IX = handle.\nExit: Fz = 1 when IX = 0, Fz = 0 otherwise.\nChanges: AF."},
        "8422": {"synopsis":"Loads one file of the application being installed into memory: puts the extension character\nin A into the third place of App_Buff1's 3-letter extension (which must start with 'A'),\nopens the file (GN_Opf), binds bank B into segment 1, reads DE bytes to the offset HL\n(OS_Mv) and closes the file.\nEntry: A = 'P' or '0'-'7'; B = bank; HL = offset in the bank; DE = length; App_Buff1 =\nfilename.\nExit: file copied; bank B left bound in segment 1; App_FileHnd = 0.\nError: does not return; jumps to the install's error exit (RC_Ftm for a bad extension).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.\nKeeps: BC, IX."},
        "8425": {"comment":"offset"},
        "8426": {"comment":"length"},
        "8427": {"comment":"bank in B"},
        "8428": {"comment":"A=extension type 'P' or '0...7'"},
        "8436": {"comment":"find terminating null of explicit filename"},
        "8444": {"comment":"find extension"},
        "8447": {"comment":"check for correct extension length"},
        "8453": {"comment":"HL points to start of 3-char extension"},
        "8460": {"comment":"first character not A/a"},
        "8465": {"comment":"'P' or '0...7'"},
        "8489": {"comment":"bind bank in S1"},
        "8493": {"comment":"length"},
        "8509": {"comment":"close file"},
        "8522": {"synopsis":"Translates a bank number of an application's DOR from its relative form ($F8-$FF for bank 7\nto bank 0 of the application) to the bank allocated for it, read from the first byte of its\n4-byte entry in the Fma table (Fma_AP0). Bank 0 is left as it is.\nEntry: A = relative bank number.\nExit: A = absolute bank number.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "8523": {"comment":"dont process bank 0"},
        "8526": {"comment":"F8-FF"},
        "8528": {"comment":"00-07"},
        "8532": {"comment":"*4"},
        "8536": {"comment":"first byte of entry in Fma table is bank allocated"},
        "8544": {"synopsis":"Index command <>REM (entry in the command table): starts removing the selected application.\nGets its static handle (GetAppByNum) and keeps it in App_RmvHnd; an application that is not\ninstalled (handle below $80) gives RC_Fail, one that runs (DC_Pol with A = $80) gives\nRC_Use, both shown through the Index's error flag (IDXF2_B_ERROR) and a redraw. Otherwise\nsets the active window to 5, shows \"Remove <name>\" and asks \"Are you sure ?\" with No as the\ndefault, then jumps to MainLoop; ENTER there runs DoRemove.\nEntry: ubIdxTopApplication + ubIdxSelectorPos = the selected application. Does not return."},
        "8555": {"comment":"installed application static handle from $80 to $FF"},
        "8557": {"comment":"store application handle to be removed"},
        "8563": {"comment":"not an installed application"},
        "8565": {"comment":"test if IX application has a running process"},
        "8572": {"comment":"'In use'"},
        "8589": {"comment":"'Cannot satisfy request'"},
        "8611": {"comment":"IX=application static handle"},
        "8614": {"comment":"get application data, name in BHL"},
        "8636": {"synopsis":"Removes an installed application. Run by ENTER after the remove question.\n1. Unless the answer was 'y', sets window 0 and redraws the Index.\n2. Finds the installation handle whose DOR matches the application's (OS_Nq NQ_Ain, OS_Fn\nFN_GH/FN_NH with HND_INST); RC_Fail when none does.\n3. When the handle installed several applications, checks with OS_Poll and DC_Pol that none\nof them runs (RC_Use otherwise).\n4. Lowers the static handle of the processes of later applications by the number removed\n(OS_Uash on each stacked process environment).\n5. Unchains the DORs from the :APP.- front DOR ($4060 in bank $21), linking the son or the\npreceding brother to the DOR after the removed group (GetSmallestBrother).\n6. Closes the memory handle (OS_Mcl), frees the installation handle, polls the keys again\n(InitKeys), writes \"Removal completed.\" and waits for ESC; then MainLoop.\nError: stores the error code in ubIdxErrorCode, sets IDXF2_B_ERROR, sets window 0 and\nredraws the Index. Does not return."},
        "8637": {"comment":"Wd #0 if 'No'"},
        "8652": {"comment":"IX=application static handle"},
        "8655": {"comment":"get application data, DOR in BDE"},
        "8657": {"comment":"DOR in BHL"},
        "8658": {"comment":"start with first handle"},
        "8662": {"comment":"find handle"},
        "8665": {"comment":"type"},
        "8667": {"comment":"no dyn id"},
        "8693": {"comment":"find next handle"},
        "8708": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: VerifyMultipleApps."},
        "8714": {"comment":"shouldn't occur"},
        "8721": {"comment":"one of the installed app is running, exit"},
        "8726": {"synopsis":"Update app static handle in process of other installed application","comment":"reload app handle"},
        "8730": {"comment":"get handle of next application in slot 4"},
        "8733": {"comment":"no more application, continue"},
        "8735": {"comment":"proc at BHL"},
        "8743": {"comment":"in S1"},
        "8758": {"comment":"number of installed application"},
        "8763": {"comment":"app static handle (=IXL too)"},
        "8781": {"comment":"the stacked process environment handle (type 4)"},
        "8784": {"comment":"update applicatio static handle in stacked process environment"},
        "8789": {"comment":"try with same handle in case of several processes for same application"},
