        "8845": {"comment":"chain small brother to APP front DOR"},
        "8856": {"synopsis":"Reads the brother pointer of a DOR: binds the DOR's bank into segment 1, reads its\nDOR_BROTHER field and restores segment 1.\nEntry: BHL = DOR.\nExit: BHL = brother DOR (0 when there is none).\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IY."},
        "8867": {"comment":"in S1"},
        "8870": {"comment":"ld iy, hl"},
        "8890": {"synopsis":"Follows the brother chain from a DOR as many times as the installation handle has\napplications (ihnd_AppNbOf), giving the DOR that comes after the installed group.\nOZ source name: GetSmallestBrother.\nEntry: BHL = first DOR of the group; IX = installation handle.\nExit: BHL = DOR after the group.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.\nKeeps: C, DE, IY."},
        "8921": {"comment":"No brother, not found"},
        "8936": {"comment":"smallest brother in BHL"},
        "8939": {"comment":"grand brother in CDE"},
        "8964": {"comment":"chain small brother to grand brother"},
        "8982": {"comment":"will free whole allocated memory and memory handle"},
        "8987": {"synopsis":"Free Installation handle, refresh key letters and display success"},
        "9007": {"comment":"repoll keys"},
        "9056": {"synopsis":"Opens the remove window (GN_Win with RemoveWdBlock) and defines window 2 as its text area\n(58 x 6 at column 13, row 2), selected and cleared.\nEntry: none."},
        "9064": {"comment":"invisible window area"},
        "9080": {"synopsis":"GN_Win definition block of the remove window: window 2 with bars, shelf brackets and an\n8-pixel banner on a greyed screen, at X = 9, Y = 0, 64 wide and 8 high; banner RemoveBanner."},
        "9087": {"synopsis":"Banner text of the remove window: \"REMOVE APPLICATION\", null-terminated."},
        "9106": {"synopsis":"Index command <>NQ (entry in the command table): shows details of the selected entry. With\nthe application list active (window 0) it shows APPLICATION INFORMATION: name, type (good,\nbad, ugly or popdown), device (ROM.n or APP.-), static handle, segment bindings, entry, and\nthe DOR, brother, topics, commands, help and tokens pointers. With the process list active\nit shows PROCESS INFORMATION for the selected suspended process: PID, name, static and\nprocess handles, flags, associated pointer and length, default device, match string and\ndirectory (nothing for the Index itself or an empty list). Then \"PRESS ESC TO RESUME\",\nactive window 3 and a jump to MainLoop.\nEntry: none. Does not return (IX is kept)."},
        "9111": {"comment":"stream to :OUT"},
        "9137": {"comment":"confused"},
        "9555": {"comment":"for cmd_escape"},
        "9563": {"synopsis":"Display selected process informations"},
        "9567": {"comment":"no suspended processes, exit"},
        "9587": {"comment":"confused"},
        "9617": {"comment":"PID"},
        "9628": {"comment":"activity name"},
        "9823": {"comment":"default device"},
        "9879": {"comment":"default directory"},
        "9910": {"synopsis":"Subroutines"},
        "9913": {"synopsis":"Entry inside nq_cde: writes DE as 4 hex digits (D, then E) with OS_Hout.\nEntry: DE = value.\nChanges: AF."},
        "9920": {"synopsis":"Reads a 3-byte pointer from an extended address with GN_Rbe: CDE = (BHL).\nEntry: BHL = address of the pointer.\nExit: CDE = pointer; HL = address of its last byte.\nChanges: AF, C, D, E, HL."},
        "9935": {"synopsis":"Opens the <>NQ window with the given banner (GN_Win with InfoWdBlock), then selects and\nclears window 2 and toggles tiny font.\nEntry: DE = banner text."},
        "9953": {"synopsis":"Moves the cursor to column 30 of the window (1,\"2X\"), the second column of the <>NQ display.\nEntry: none."},
        "9961": {"synopsis":"Strings"},
        "9985": {"synopsis":"Banner text of the process information window: \"PROCESS INFORMATION\", null-terminated."},
        "10005": {"synopsis":"The text \"good\", null-terminated: an application type name for <>NQ."},
        "10010": {"synopsis":"The text \"bad\", null-terminated: an application type name for <>NQ (AT_Bad set)."},
        "10014": {"synopsis":"The text \"ugly\", null-terminated: an application type name for <>NQ (AT_Ugly set)."},
        "10019": {"synopsis":"The text \"popdown\", null-terminated: an application type name for <>NQ (AT_Popd set)."},
        "10027": {"synopsis":"Mnemonics used to symbolize various identifiers in config file:\nvariable name aliases to existing variable Index Unsafe workspace (not used while OZ Update is processing):","comment":"draw \"Operating System Update\" window"},
