        "10548": {"comment":"update OZ bank files to slot 0 (default)"},
        "10555": {"comment":"\"OZ.\" (part of V3 format)"},
        "10557": {"comment":"no '.', this means default slot 0"},
        "10562": {"comment":"get total no of ROM banks to update .."},
        "10565": {"comment":"OZ slot number specification value was illegal..."},
        "10573": {"comment":"after \"OZ.x\" a \",\" must appear..."},
        "10576": {"comment":"fetch comma..."},
        "10578": {"comment":"not found - signal syntax error..."},
        "10584": {"comment":"a constant after comma identifies total no of ROM banks to update .."},
        "10587": {"comment":"specified destination bank value was illegal..."},
        "10600": {"synopsis":"Parse entries in the configuration file:\n\"<bank file>\",<crc>,<destination bank>\nOZ source name: ReadConfigFileOzBanks.","comment":"get ready for first oz bank entry of [total_ozbanks]"},
        "10604": {"comment":"fetch line containing oz bank specification"},
        "10607": {"comment":"premature EOF!"},
        "10615": {"comment":"skip comments and empty lines..."},
        "10617": {"comment":"found a line with an oz bank entry, collect oz bank data into variables..."},
        "10620": {"comment":"check CRC of oz bank file data just collected..."},
        "10628": {"comment":"prepare for next oz data entry"},
        "10633": {"comment":"total of oz banks to register"},
        "10635": {"comment":"just registered another oz bank"},
        "10636": {"comment":"all registered?"},
        "10637": {"comment":"yes, all successfully registered and CRC checked"},
        "10640": {"synopsis":"Fetch a line from the config file\n\nreturn Fz = 1, if EOF file reached."},
        "10647": {"comment":"bind config file contents to S0 (upper 8K)"},
        "10650": {"comment":"get beginning of new line in buffer"},
        "10663": {"comment":"EOF reached, return Fz = 1..."},
        "10670": {"comment":"{bufferend - lineptr}"},
        "10673": {"comment":"search max characters for CR"},
        "10678": {"comment":"HL points at beginning of new line"},
        "10685": {"comment":"lineno++"},
        "10688": {"comment":"Fz = 0, EOF not reached yet..."},
        "10693": {"synopsis":"Find NEWLINE character ahead. Search for the following newline characters:\n1)   search CR\n2)   if CR was found, check for a trailing LF (MSDOS newline) to be\nbypassed, pointing at the first char of the next line.\n3)   if CR wasn't found, then try to search for LF.\n4)   if LF wasn't found, return pointer to the end of the buffer.\n\n......../IXIY  same\nAFBCDEHL/....  different\nEntry: HL = start of search pointer, BC = max. number of bytes to search.\nExit: HL = pointer to first char of new line or end of buffer.","comment":"HL = line, BC = bufsize"},
        "10697": {"comment":"{"},
        "10698": {"comment":"if ( *line != CR)"},
        "10699": {"comment":"{"},
        "10702": {"comment":"if ( *line++ == LF )"},
        "10704": {"comment":"return line   /* LF */"},
        "10705": {"comment":"}"},
        "10711": {"synopsis":"else {","comment":"if (++*line != LF)"},
        "10712": {"comment":"return line   /* CR */"},
        "10714": {"comment":"else"},
        "10715": {"comment":"return ++line /* CRLF */"},
        "10716": {"comment":"}"},
        "10717": {"synopsis":"}\nwhile (--bufsize)\nparse parse \"<filename>\",<crc>,<dor offset> from line...\nparsed data are stored in [bankfilename], [bankfilecrc] and [bankfilenum] variables.\nOZ source name: ParseBankFileData."},
        "10722": {"comment":"copy RAM device name of \"ozupdate.cfg\" file"},
        "10725": {"comment":"as base of bank filename"},
        "10734": {"comment":"read \"filename\" into (DE)..."},
        "10740": {"comment":"skip comma..."},
        "10745": {"comment":"get bank file image CRC"},
        "10751": {"comment":"specified CRC value was illegal..."},
        "10759": {"comment":"32bit CRC value in 'debc"},
        "10767": {"comment":"skip comma..."},
        "10772": {"comment":"get location of application DOR in bank file"},
        "10775": {"comment":"constant in DEBC"},
        "10778": {"comment":"specified DOR value was illegal..."},
        "10783": {"comment":"bank file number in slot"},
        "10788": {"synopsis":"CRC check bank file, defined by filename in [bankfilename], by loading file into\na buffer and issue a CRC32 calculation, then compare the CRC fetched from the\nconfiguration file in [bankfilecrc].\n\nReturn to caller if the CRC matched, otherwise jump to error routine and exit program","comment":"display progress message for CRC check of bank file"},
        "10791": {"comment":"open file again, just to get low level file data"},
        "10797": {"comment":"get first 64 byte sector number of file"},
        "10800": {"comment":"get bank number of first sector of file"},
        "10807": {"comment":"ensure that bank array is available in S0 (upper 8K)"},
        "10813": {"comment":"save sector details into array"},
        "10819": {"comment":"register destination bank number in slot X to blow oz bank"},
        "10826": {"comment":"ensure that CRC-32 file buffer is available in S0"},
        "10835": {"comment":"initial CRC = FFFFFFFFh"},
        "10840": {"comment":"calculate CRC-32 of bank file, returned in DEBC"},
        "10851": {"comment":"check the CRC-32 of the bank file with the CRC of the config file"},
        "10854": {"comment":"CRC didn't match: the file is corrupt and will not be updated to card!"},
        "10858": {"synopsis":"Compare CRC in DEHL with (BC).\nEntry: DEBC = calculated CRC; HL = pointer to start of CRC in memory.\nExit: Fc = 0 (always); Fz = 1, CRC is valid; Fz = 0, CRC does not match the CRC supplied in\nDEHL; BC points at byte after CRC in memory.\nChanges: AF, BC.\nKeeps: DE, HL, IX, IY."},
        "10876": {"synopsis":"OZ source name: return_crc_status."},
        "10877": {"comment":"return Fc = 0 always"},
        "10878": {"comment":"Fz indicates CRC status"},
        "10879": {"synopsis":"GetSym - read a symbol from the current position of the file's current line.\n\n..BCDEHL/IXIY  same\nAF....../....  different\nEntry: None.\nExit: A = symbol identifier; (sym) contains symbol identifier; (Ident) contains symbol\n(beginning with a length byte); (lineptr) is updated to point at the next character in the\nline."},
