      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"comment":"Fc=0 Fz=1"},
        "168": {"comment":"A= 3*L"},
        "174": {"comment":"return to function"},
        "176": {"comment":"!! put this code sequence"},
        "177": {"comment":"!! into subroutine"},
        "186": {"comment":"HLhl &= DEde"},
        "211": {"comment":"HLhl ^= DEde"},
        "236": {"comment":"HLhl |= DEde"},
        "251": {"synopsis":"HLhlC=MOD(HLhlC,DEdeB)"},
        "261": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPMod (FP_MOD), reached directly when both numbers are integers and called by\nFPIdv: divides the 32-bit integer HLhl by the 32-bit integer DEde. Both are made positive,\nDivision runs the long division, and the remainder takes the sign of the dividend. There is\nno check for a zero divisor.\nEntry: HLhl = dividend; DEde = divisor (two's complement integers; C and B are not read).\nExit: HLhl = remainder (sign of the dividend), C = 0; DEde = quotient's magnitude; A bit 7 =\n1 when the signs of the numbers differ.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'."},
        "262": {"comment":"Fs=1 if signs differ"},
        "263": {"comment":"Fz=1 if HLhl positive"},
        "268": {"comment":"make divident positive"},
        "276": {"comment":"make divisor positive"},
        "279": {"comment":"BCbc=divisor, HLhl=0"},
        "299": {"comment":"HLhl(in) was positive"},
        "300": {"comment":"else negate it"},
        "303": {"synopsis":"HLhlC=Fix(HLhlC/DEdeB)"},
        "330": {"comment":"try integer substraction,"},
        "333": {"comment":"return if no overflow"},
        "334": {"comment":"else restore HLhl"},
        "340": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPSub: flips the sign bit of DEdeB and goes on at add_2, so HLhlC = HLhlC -\nDEdeB for two floats. Called by sub_0_E35F.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = floats.\nExit: as add_2 (HLhlC = difference).\nError: A = RC_Tbg on exponent overflow, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's\nframe (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'.","comment":"negate DEde and add"},
        "346": {"synopsis":"Flips the sign bit of HLhlC and goes on at add_2, so HLhlC = DEdeB - HLhlC for two floats.\nUsed by the sine core to fold an argument (pi/4 - x), by FPAsn for 1 - x^2 and by the ATN\nand ACS tails for pi/2 - x.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = floats.\nExit: as add_2 (HLhlC = DEdeB - HLhlC).\nError: A = RC_Tbg on exponent overflow, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's\nframe (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'.","comment":"negate HLhl and add"},
        "356": {"comment":"try integer addition,"},
        "359": {"comment":"return if no overflow"},
        "360": {"comment":"else restore HLhl"},
        "366": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPAdd: adds two floats, HLhlC = HLhlC + DEdeB. A float has C = exponent + $80\n(value = 1.m * 2^(C - $80)), H bit 7 = sign and the mantissa's top 1 implied; C = 0 is zero.\n1. When DEdeB is zero HLhlC is returned; when HLhlC is zero DEdeB is returned (swapped in).\n2. The number with the smaller exponent is moved into HLhlC and shifted right by Fix until\nthe exponents match; the bits shifted out go into bc'.\n3. Equal signs add the mantissas (a carry shifts back one place and raises the exponent);\ndifferent signs subtract them, negating on a borrow, and NormalizeHLhlC realigns the result.\n4. The result is rounded from bc' (IncHLhl, HalfIncHLhl), gets its sign back in H bit 7, and\na zero result becomes FPZer.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = floats.\nExit: HLhlC = sum (float, or 0).\nError: A = RC_Tbg when the exponent overflows, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP\ncall's frame (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'."},
        "368": {"comment":"DEdeB=0"},
        "371": {"comment":"HLhlC=0"},
        "375": {"comment":"clear extra bits"},
        "381": {"comment":"sign difference in Fs"},
        "382": {"comment":"make sure HLhlC has smaller exponent"},
        "388": {"comment":"set missing bit"},
        "390": {"comment":"match exponents"},
        "394": {"comment":"remember D sign"},
        "395": {"comment":"set missing bit"},
        "397": {"comment":"original signs different"},
        "400": {"comment":"add them"},
        "403": {"comment":"fix mantissa if overflow"},
        "406": {"comment":"set missing bit"},
        "410": {"comment":"sub them"},
        "413": {"comment":"negate mantissa if overflow"},
        "416": {"comment":"normalize mantissa"},
        "419": {"comment":"swap sign to match original H"},
        "420": {"comment":"if bc>$8000 increment HLhl"},
        "439": {"comment":"prepare for positive"},
        "443": {"comment":"it's zero"},
        "448": {"comment":"make it negative"},
        "454": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPDiv: divides two floats, HLhlC = HLhlC / DEdeB. The sign is the XOR of the\nsigns; the mantissas, with their top bits put back, go through Division (a 32-bit long\ndivision), plus one more quotient bit (loc_0_E3FB) when the top bit is clear, and the\nquotient is rounded. The exponent is C - B + $80, adjusted for normalisation. A zero\ndividend returns zero; an underflow returns zero.\nEntry: HLhlC = dividend, DEdeB = divisor (floats).\nExit: HLhlC = quotient.\nError: A = RC_Dvz when DEdeB is zero (B = 0), A = RC_Tbg when the exponent overflows,\nthrough FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'.","comment":"Division by zero if DEdeB=0"},
        "463": {"comment":"0 if HLhlC=0"},
        "464": {"comment":"save sign"},
        "467": {"comment":"insert missing bits"},
        "472": {"comment":"BC=DE, DE=0"},
        "478": {"comment":"bc=de, de=0"},
        "489": {"comment":"D"},
        "523": {"comment":"save sign"},
        "528": {"comment":"make HLhl positive"},
        "536": {"comment":"make DLdl positive"},
        "539": {"comment":"BCbc = HLhl, HLhl = 0"},
        "561": {"comment":"normalize HLhl, adjust DEdeC"},
        "576": {"comment":"adjust DEdeC"},
        "587": {"comment":"HLhl = 2*HLhl +1"},
        "593": {"comment":"high bit not set, do again"},
        "596": {"comment":"return with correct sign"},
        "601": {"synopsis":"FP_MUL: multiplies HLhlC by DEdeB. When both are integers (B = C = 0) the magnitudes are\nmultiplied into a 64-bit product by div_2 (the integer multiply, despite its name), which\nreturns an integer when the product fits in 31 bits and a float otherwise; any float operand\nturns both into floats (FltBoth) and mul_1 multiplies them. Also called by FPPwr for\nrepeated squaring. The callers listed in apps/calculator/calc.asm call the calculator's own\nFpMul, not this routine.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = numbers (exponent 0: 32-bit integer in HLhl; otherwise a float).\nExit: Fc = 0; HLhlC = product.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Tbg when a float product overflows.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'."},
        "609": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPMul: multiplies two floats, HLhlC = HLhlC * DEdeB. The sign is the XOR of the\nsigns; the mantissas, with their top bits put back, are multiplied by sub_0_E40E (plus a\nlast shift by sub_0_E422 on a carry), the 64-bit product is rounded to 32 bits and the\nexponents are added (mul_2). The FPP's main multiply, used by the series and power routines.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = floats.\nExit: HLhlC = product; zero when either is zero or the exponent underflows.\nError: A = RC_Tbg when the exponent overflows, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP\ncall's frame (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'."},
        "611": {"comment":"DEdeB=0, zero"},
        "616": {"comment":"HLhlC=0, zero"},
        "617": {"comment":"sign"},
        "620": {"comment":"insert midding bits"},
        "625": {"comment":"BCbc=HLhl, HLhl=0"},
        "644": {"comment":"cp $8000, DE"},
        "751": {"comment":"(IX)=HLhlC"},
        "1001": {"comment":"HLhl = !HLhl"},
        "1017": {"synopsis":"return PI, 490FDAA2.81"},
        "1045": {"synopsis":"180/PI"},
        "1135": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPSqr for a float: square root of HLhlC. The exponent is halved (the mantissa\nshifted one place first when the exponent is even), sub_0_E441 produces the root's bits by\nthe restoring method, two more steps (sub_0_E441, sub_0_E47A, loc_0_E3FB) give the rounding\nbit, and the root is rounded. Also called by FPAsn.\nEntry: HLhlC = float.\nExit: HLhlC = square root (zero for zero); A = 0.\nError: A = RC_Nvr when HLhlC is negative, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's\nframe (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl'.","comment":"Negative root, error"},
        "1142": {"comment":"Sqr(0), exit"},
        "1247": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPCos for a float: cosine of HLhlC (radians). sub_0_E1DA reduces |x| modulo\npi/4 and returns the count of eighth turns in E; adding 2 (a quarter turn) makes it a sine,\nwhich the shared core loc_0_DCF5 evaluates. Also called by FPTan.\nEntry: HLhlC = float (radians).\nExit: HLhlC = cos x.\nError: A = RC_Acl when |x| >= 2^23, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame\n(IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX."},
        "1258": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPSin for a float: sine of HLhlC (radians). sub_0_E1DA reduces |x| modulo pi/4\n(count of eighth turns in E); the sign of x goes into bit 2 of that count and the code falls\ninto sub_0_DCF1, the core shared with cos_1: an odd eighth is folded (pi/4 - r), eighths 0\nand 3 use the sine series in r^2 times r, 1 and 2 the cosine series, and bit 2 gives the\nsign. Also called by FPTan.\nEntry: HLhlC = float (radians).\nExit: HLhlC = sin x.\nError: A = RC_Acl when |x| >= 2^23, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame\n(IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX."},
        "1295": {"comment":"-2.7366953E-06         -1/365404.21667616"},
        "1300": {"comment":"0.00015913704          1/6283.8923480438"},
        "1305": {"comment":"-0.011749394           -1/85.110770797545"},
        "1310": {"comment":"-0.15397135            -1/6.4947146139275"},
        "1315": {"comment":"; 1.0000"},
        "1338": {"comment":"2.8828843E-05          1/34687.482504451"},
        "1343": {"comment":"-0.0013395552          -1/746.51644671521"},
        "1348": {"comment":"-0.048977532           -1/20.417525343048"},
        "1353": {"comment":"-0.43359375            -1/2.3063063162138"},
        "1358": {"comment":"1.000"},
        "1376": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_DCF1\nHLhlC=1.0"},
        "1387": {"synopsis":"Loads the float 1.0 into DEdeB (DEde = 0, B = $80).\nEntry: none.\nExit: DEdeB = 1.0.\nChanges: B, DE, de'.\nKeeps: AF, C, HL, bc', hl'."},
        "1398": {"synopsis":"End of function LdDEdeB_1\n.7853981629014 1/1.2732395455393"},
        "1434": {"comment":"Exponent function range"},
        "1451": {"comment":".00023102828072297     1/4328.4744052575"},
        "1456": {"comment":".0017504486168036      1/571.28212185173"},
        "1461": {"comment":".011195423547179       1/89.322212400979"},
        "1466": {"comment":".035863519180566       1/27.883487812927"},
        "1471": {"comment":".14483515359461        1/6.9044011428258"},
        "1476": {"comment":".41990659944713        1/2.3814819803181"},
        "1481": {"comment":"-.99609374627471       -1/1.003921572382"},
        "1528": {"synopsis":"Reciprocal: HLhlC = 1 / HLhlC. Loads 1.0 into DEdeB (LdDEdeB_1) and falls into loc_0_DDFB,\nwhich swaps the two and divides. Used by FPPwr for a negative power, by FPExp and by FPAtn\n(arguments above tan(3*pi/8)).\nEntry: HLhlC = float.\nExit: HLhlC = 1 / x.\nError: A = RC_Dvz when HLhlC is zero, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame\n(IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'."},
        "1531": {"synopsis":"Entry inside sub_0_DDF8: swaps HLhlC and DEdeB and jumps to div_1, so HLhlC = DEdeB / HLhlC.\nCalled by FPAsn to form x / sqrt(1 - x^2).\nEntry: HLhlC = divisor, DEdeB = dividend (floats).\nExit: HLhlC = DEdeB / HLhlC.\nError: A = RC_Dvz when HLhlC is zero, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame\n(IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'."},
        "1537": {"synopsis":"Loads ln 2 into DEdeB ($3172:$17F8, exponent $7F: 0.6931472). FPExp then adjusts de' and\nloads bc' = $D1CF for 48 bits of ln 2; sub_0_DE0F multiplies the power of two by it.\nEntry: none.\nExit: DEdeB = ln 2.\nChanges: B, DE, de'.\nKeeps: AF, C, HL, bc', hl'."},
        "1548": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_DE01"},
        "1551": {"synopsis":"Entry inside FPLn for a float: natural logarithm of HLhlC. Also called by FPPwr (x^y as\nexp(y ln x)) and through FPLn by FPLog.\n1. Splits x into m * 2^n with m from sqrt(1/2) to sqrt(2): the exponent is set to $80, and\nto $7F when the mantissa reaches sqrt(2) ($3504F333).\n2. t = (m - 1) / (m + 1) (sub_0_E35F); ln m = t * P(t^2), the series evaluated by sub_0_E37D\nfrom the five coefficients after the call.\n3. Adds n * ln 2 (n made a float from the exponent byte, sub_0_DE01) with add_2.\nEntry: HLhlC = float.\nExit: HLhlC = ln x; A = 0.\nError: A = RC_Lgr when x is zero or negative, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP\ncall's frame (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX.","comment":"Log range"},
        "1594": {"comment":".19609444495291        1/5.0995835207885"},
        "1599": {"comment":".34313199110329        1/2.9143304207359"},
        "1604": {"comment":"-.27509919553995       -1/3.6350524327679"},
        "1609": {"comment":"-.88930762559175       -1/1.1244702858975"},
        "1614": {"comment":"2.0"},
        "1676": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_DE0F"},
        "1694": {"synopsis":"FP_ASN: arc sine of HLhlC, in radians. Computes 1 - x^2 (mul_1, sub_3) and its square root\n(sqr_1); when that is zero (|x| = 1) the result is pi/2 with the sign of x, otherwise x /\nsqrt(1 - x^2) goes to the arc tangent code (loc_0_DEC6 in FPAtn). Also called by FPAcs,\nwhich returns pi/2 minus the result.\nEntry: HLhlC = number (an integer is made a float).\nExit: Fc = 0; HLhlC = arc sine (float).\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Nvr when |x| > 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX."},
        "1792": {"comment":".044422001345083     1/22.511367559325"},
        "1797": {"comment":"-.071006250567734     1/14.083267205414"},
        "1802": {"comment":"-.10852354299277     1/9.2145904236338"},
        "1807": {"comment":".24571692291647     1/4.0697237623309"},
        "1812": {"comment":".21305388584733     1/4.693648257214"},
        "1817": {"comment":".43098195269704     1/2.3202827722648"},
        "1858": {"synopsis":"End of function FPAsn"},
        "2247": {"synopsis":"Loads DEdeB from a 5-byte float at IX in memory order: (IX+0) = e, (IX+1) = d, (IX+2) = E,\n(IX+3) = D, (IX+4) = exponent into B. Reads the coefficient tables of sub_0_E37D and the\nnumber FPPwr keeps on the stack.\nEntry: IX = 5-byte number.\nExit: DEdeB = number.\nChanges: B, DE, de'.\nKeeps: AF, C, HL, IX, bc', hl'."},
        "2265": {"comment":"Bad number"},
        "2270": {"synopsis":"The number reader of FPVal (FP_VAL): reads unsigned decimal digits at IX into HLhlC. Integer\ndigits accumulate in HLhl (sub_0_E16B); once HLhl would overflow, later digits only raise a\ndecimal exponent (C). An optional '.' starts the fraction digits, counted in B (sub_0_E169),\nand an 'E' or 'e' the exponent (sub_0_E13A). Without point and exponent, a value below 2^31\nis returned as an integer; otherwise HLhl is normalised to a float and multiplied or divided\nby the power of ten from sub_0_E3A4 (in steps of 10^38 for very small numbers).\nEntry: IX = first character after the sign; IY = FP call frame (for ReadByteIX).\nExit: HLhlC = unsigned value (integer or float); IX = first character after the number.\nError: A = RC_Bdn for a second decimal point, A = RC_Tbg when the value overflows, through\nFPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX."},
        "2362": {"synopsis":"Reads the exponent after the 'E' of a number for sub_0_E0DE: skips the 'E', blanks and a '+'\nor '-' (GetNumStart), then reads decimal digits into a byte. Two digits give 0 to 99; a\nthird digit or more gives 100. A '-' negates the result.\nEntry: IX = the 'E'; A = 0; IY = FP call frame (for ReadByteIX).\nExit: A = exponent (signed byte); IX = first character after the digits.\nChanges: AF, DE, IX, AF'.\nKeeps: BC, HL."},
        "2382": {"comment":"B=10*B"},
        "2383": {"comment":"!! could use number from ReadNum instead of this"},
        "2409": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_E13A"},
        "2411": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_E169"},
        "2448": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_E16B"},
        "2451": {"comment":"set missing top bit"},
        "2453": {"comment":"/2 until exponent reached"},
        "2464": {"synopsis":"Converts both numbers to integers: FPFix on DEdeB (swapped in and out by ExHLhlC_DEdeB) and\nthen falls into FPFix for HLhlC. Used by the integer operations (AND, OR, EOR, MOD, DIV)\nwhen either operand is a float.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = numbers.\nExit: HLhl, DEde = 32-bit integers, C = B = 0.\nError: A = RC_Tbg when a float is 2^31 or more in size, through FPError, which unwinds to\nthe FP call's frame (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF'."},
        "2473": {"synopsis":"FP_FIX: truncates HLhlC to an integer (towards zero). An integer (C = 0) is returned as it\nis. A float has its top bit put back, is shifted right by Fix until the exponent reaches\n$9F, and is negated when it was negative. Also called by FPNot and FixBoth.\nEntry: HLhlC = number (C = 0: 32-bit two's complement integer in HLhl; otherwise a float, C\n= exponent + $80, H bit 7 = sign).\nExit: Fc = 0; HLhl = integer, C = 0.\nError: Fc = 1, A = RC_Tbg when |x| >= 2^31.\nChanges: AF, C, HL, bc', hl', AF'."},
        "2475": {"comment":"already int"},
        "2476": {"comment":"remember sign"},
        "2484": {"comment":"return with correct sign"},
        "2488": {"synopsis":"Negates the 32-bit integer HLhl (two's complement: HLhl = 0 - HLhl). The tail of FPFix for a\nnegative number.\nEntry: HLhl = integer.\nExit: HLhl = -HLhl.\nChanges: F, HL, hl'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, bc', de'."},
        "2508": {"synopsis":"Negates the 48-bit mantissa HLhl:bc' (bc' holds the extra low bits) and complements A, which\nholds the sign in add_2. Used by add_2 when subtracting the mantissas borrowed.\nEntry: HLhl:bc' = mantissa; A = sign byte.\nExit: HLhl:bc' = 0 - HLhl:bc'; A = NOT A.\nChanges: AF, HL, bc', hl'.\nKeeps: DE, de'."},
        "2510": {"comment":"negate extra bits"},
        "2522": {"synopsis":"Argument reduction for SIN and COS: loads DEdeB = pi/4 (loc_0_DD76) with 16 further bits of\nit in bc' ($2169), and falls into sub_0_E1EA, which reduces |x| modulo pi/4.\nEntry: HLhlC = float.\nExit: HLhlC = remainder, normalised with H bit 7 set (the callers clear it); E = eighth\nturns in x (bit 7 set from 128 on).\nError: A = RC_Acl when |x| >= 2^23 (exponent above $96), through FPError, which unwinds to\nthe FP call's frame (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', IX."},
        "2525": {"comment":"Accuracy lost"},
        "2538": {"synopsis":"Reduces |HLhlC| modulo |DEdeB|, the divisor's mantissa extended by 16 more bits in bc': a\nrestoring long division on the 48-bit mantissas, one quotient bit per exponent step, the low\nbits of the quotient collected in C. The remainder is normalised by NormalizeHLhlC. Called\nby FPExp with ln 2 and by sub_0_E1DA with pi/4.\nEntry: HLhlC = dividend, DEdeB = divisor (floats, signs ignored); bc' = 16 more bits of the\ndivisor.\nExit: HLhlC = remainder, normalised with H bit 7 set; E = quotient's low 7 bits, bit 7 set\nonce the quotient reached 128; D bit 7 set; IX = 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', hl', IX."},
        "2617": {"synopsis":"Normalises a mantissa that carries extra bits: while H bit 7 is clear, shifts HLhl:bc' left\none place and decrements the exponent C. Stops with C = 0 when it runs out (zero or\nunderflow).\nEntry: HLhl:bc' = mantissa; C = exponent.\nExit: H bit 7 set and C reduced, or C = 0.\nChanges: F, C, HL, bc', hl'."},
        "2619": {"comment":"normalized"},
        "2621": {"comment":"shift in extra bits from bc"},
        "2634": {"comment":"zero"},
        "2635": {"synopsis":"Normalises HLhl with zeros shifted in: while H bit 7 is clear, shifts HLhl left one place\nand decrements C. Stops with C = 0 when it runs out. FPFlt, sub_0_E0DE and sub_0_DE0F make\nfloats from integers with it.\nEntry: HLhl = mantissa; C = exponent.\nExit: H bit 7 set and C reduced, or C = 0.\nChanges: F, C, HL, hl'."},
        "2637": {"comment":"normalized"},
        "2639": {"comment":"no extra bits"},
        "2647": {"comment":"zero"},
        "2648": {"synopsis":"Converts both numbers to floats: FPFlt on DEdeB (swapped in and out by ExHLhlC_DEdeB) and\nthen falls into FPFlt for HLhlC. Called by every two-operand function when either operand is\na float.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = numbers.\nExit: HLhlC, DEdeB = floats (an integer zero stays zero).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, de', hl'."},
        "2657": {"synopsis":"FP_FLT: converts an integer in HLhlC to a float. A float (C <> 0) and zero are returned as\nthey are. Otherwise the magnitude is normalised from exponent $9F (Normalize0HLhlC) and H\nbit 7, the implied top bit, is replaced by the sign. A float's value is 1.m * 2^(C - $80).\nEntry: HLhlC = number (C = 0: 32-bit two's complement integer in HLhl).\nExit: Fc = 0; HLhlC = float (C = exponent + $80, H bit 7 = sign).\nChanges: AF, C, HL, hl'.\nKeeps: B, DE, bc', de'."},
        "2659": {"comment":"already float"},
        "2663": {"comment":"zero"},
        "2666": {"comment":"make it positive"},
        "2671": {"comment":"and normalize"},
        "2674": {"comment":"return with correct sign"},
        "2679": {"synopsis":"Adds 1 to the 32-bit HLhl. Used by the rounding steps and by FPInt and FPSgn.\nEntry: HLhl = value.\nExit: HLhl = HLhl + 1; Fc = 1 when it wrapped from $FFFFFFFF to 0; bc' = 1.\nChanges: F, HL, bc', hl'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, de'."},
        "2693": {"synopsis":"clear carry, set HLhl lowest bit"},
        "2699": {"synopsis":"Swaps the numbers HLhlC and DEdeB: exchanges C and B and falls into ExHLhl_DEde.\nEntry: HLhlC, DEdeB = numbers.\nExit: the two swapped; A = old C.\nChanges: A, BC, DE, HL, de', hl'.\nKeeps: F."},
        "2702": {"synopsis":"Swaps the 32-bit HLhl and DEde in both register sets. Used by sub_0_E16B to put back the\nvalue saved before an overflowing multiply by 10.\nEntry: HLhl, DEde = values.\nExit: the two swapped.\nChanges: DE, HL, de', hl'.\nKeeps: AF, BC, bc'."},
        "2707": {"synopsis":"Shifts the mantissa HLhl right one place into the extra bits bc' (the bit leaving c' is\nlost) and ORs b' into A', so that A' turns non-zero once a 1 bit has left HLhl (Fix clears\nA' first). Then falls into IncC to raise the exponent.\nEntry: HLhl:bc' = mantissa; C = exponent.\nExit: HLhl:bc' halved; C = C + 1.\nError: A = RC_Tbg when C wraps to 0, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame\n(IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: F, C, HL, bc', hl', AF'."},
        "2719": {"synopsis":"Increments the exponent C; when it wraps to 0 it falls into ErrTooBig.\nEntry: C = exponent.\nExit: C = C + 1.\nError: A = RC_Tbg when C wraps to 0, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame\n(IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: F, C."},
        "2721": {"comment":"Too big"},
        "2726": {"synopsis":"Test HLhlC for zero"},
        "2732": {"comment":"get negative bit"},
        "2734": {"comment":"set positive bit"},
        "2737": {"synopsis":"Tests the 32-bit HLhl for zero: A = H OR L OR h OR l.\nEntry: HLhl = value.\nExit: Fz = 1 when HLhl is zero; A = the OR of its bytes.\nChanges: AF.\nKeeps: BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl'."},
        "2766": {"synopsis":"signed integer compare, preload FALSE"},
        "2769": {"synopsis":"HLhlC=0"},
        "2779": {"synopsis":"signed float compare, preload FALSE"},
        "2784": {"synopsis":"float compare"},
        "2787": {"synopsis":"integer compare"},
        "2797": {"synopsis":"signed float compare"},
        "2809": {"synopsis":"signed integer compare"},
        "2811": {"comment":"same sign"},
        "2815": {"comment":"sign into Fc"},
        "2817": {"synopsis":"One decade step of FPStr's digit scaling: decrements the decimal exponent B, then multiplies\nthe unnormalised mantissa by 10: C goes up by 3 and HLhl becomes HLhl + HLhl/4 (falls into\nsub_0_E303 and AddHLhl_DEde). The bit carried out of the mantissa comes back in Fc.\nEntry: HLhl = mantissa (top bit set); C = exponent; B = decimal exponent.\nExit: B = B - 1; C = C + 3; HLhl = 1.25 * HLhl (low 32 bits); Fc = carry out; DEde = old\nHLhl.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, de', hl', AF'."},
        "2819": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_E301"},
        "2829": {"synopsis":"Adds the 32-bit DEde to HLhl.\nEntry: HLhl, DEde = values.\nExit: HLhl = HLhl + DEde; Fc = carry out; P/V = signed overflow.\nChanges: F, HL, hl'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, bc', de'."},
        "2835": {"synopsis":"Subtracts the 32-bit DEde from HLhl. FPSub and FPAdd try integer arithmetic with it and\nAddHLhl_DEde first, and turn to floats when P/V shows a signed overflow.\nEntry: HLhl, DEde = values.\nExit: HLhl = HLhl - DEde; Fc = borrow; P/V = signed overflow.\nChanges: F, HL, hl'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, bc', de'."},
        "2843": {"synopsis":"Multiplies the 32-bit unsigned HLhl by 10 as ((HLhl * 4) + HLhl) * 2, keeping the original\nin DEde, and falls into HLhl_x2 for the last doubling. Used by sub_0_E16B to collect decimal\ndigits.\nEntry: HLhl = value.\nExit: HLhl = 10 * HLhl; DEde = old HLhl; Fc = 1 on overflow (HLhl then partly multiplied).\nChanges: F, DE, HL, de', hl'."},
        "2858": {"synopsis":"Doubles the 32-bit HLhl (shift left one place).\nEntry: HLhl = value.\nExit: HLhl = 2 * HLhl; Fc = the bit shifted out.\nChanges: F, HL, hl'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, bc', de'."},
        "2864": {"synopsis":"increment exponent, /2 mantissa"},
        "2865": {"synopsis":"Shifts the 32-bit HLhl right one place (logical; H bit 7 becomes 0). SrlHLhlC0, the entry\nbefore it, also increments C.\nEntry: HLhl = value.\nExit: HLhl = HLhl / 2; Fc = the bit shifted out.\nChanges: F, HL, hl'.\nKeeps: A, BC, DE, bc', de'."},
        "2876": {"synopsis":"Copies the number HLhlC into DEdeB: B = C and falls into LdDEde_HLhl.\nEntry: HLhlC = number.\nExit: DEdeB = HLhlC.\nChanges: B, DE, de'.\nKeeps: AF, C, HL, bc', hl'."},
        "2877": {"synopsis":"Copies the 32-bit HLhl into DEde.\nEntry: HLhl = value.\nExit: DEde = HLhl.\nChanges: DE, de'.\nKeeps: AF, BC, HL, bc', hl'."},
        "2884": {"synopsis":"Squares HLhlC (LdDEdeB_HLhlC, mul_1) and falls into PushHLhlC, which leaves the square on\nthe stack as well: the set-up of the series in SIN, COS, LN and ATN before sub_0_E37D.\nEntry: HLhlC = float x.\nExit: HLhlC = x^2; x^2 pushed on the caller's stack (three words, as PushHLhlC).\nError: A = RC_Tbg when the square overflows, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's\nframe (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX."},
        "2890": {"synopsis":"Pushes the number HLhlC on the caller's stack and returns: takes the return address into IX,\npushes BC, HL and hl' (hl' on top, six bytes) and jumps back through IX. PopDEdeB takes the\nnumber back into DEdeB.\nEntry: HLhlC = number.\nExit: HLhlC on the stack; SP = SP - 6 for the caller.\nChanges: IX.\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl'.","comment":"return address"},
        "2897": {"comment":"return"},
        "2899": {"synopsis":"Pops a number pushed by PushHLhlC into DEdeB and returns: takes the return address into IX,\npops de', DE, then the pushed BC, whose C becomes B. C is kept.\nEntry: a number from PushHLhlC on the stack.\nExit: DEdeB = that number; SP = SP + 6 for the caller; A = C.\nChanges: A, B, DE, de', IX.\nKeeps: F, C, HL, bc', hl'.","comment":"return address"},
        "2909": {"comment":"return"},
        "2911": {"synopsis":"Computes HLhlC = (x - 1) / (x + 1): x + 1 (add_2 with 1.0) is kept on the stack, x - 1 is\nformed by sub_2, and div_1 divides. Used by FPLn on the mantissa and by FPAtn for arguments\nbetween tan(pi/8) and tan(3*pi/8).\nEntry: HLhlC = float x.\nExit: HLhlC = (x - 1) / (x + 1).\nError: A = RC_Dvz when x = -1, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame (IY)\nand returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX."},
        "2941": {"synopsis":"Evaluates a polynomial whose coefficients follow the CALL as 5-byte floats (mantissa low\nbyte first, exponent last), in Horner form: r = t * c0 + c1, r = r * t + c2, and so on.\nCoefficients have exponents below $80; the first with an exponent of $80 or more (1.0 or\n2.0) is the last one, and the routine returns onto it: its bytes run as four NOPs and an\nADD, so execution goes on after the table.\nEntry: HLhlC = t; t also on the stack under the return address (PushHLhlC or sub_0_E344).\nExit: HLhlC = polynomial value; t still on the stack (the caller pops it with PopDEdeB).\nError: A = RC_Tbg on overflow, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's frame (IY)\nand returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl', AF', IX."},
        "2945": {"comment":"IX=table"},
        "2955": {"comment":"IX+=FP_SIZE"},
        "2967": {"comment":"HLhlB=1/2"},
        "2980": {"synopsis":"Builds a power of ten in DEdeB by repeated multiplication by 10 (sub_0_E303, rounded),\nkeeping HLhlC. With A from 0 to $7F, DEdeB = 10^A. With A of $80 or more, A is an exponent\nbyte: it stops at the first power of ten whose exponent byte is above A. FPStr scales by it;\nsub_0_E0DE applies the decimal exponent with it.\nEntry: A = power, or exponent limit; HLhlC = number to keep.\nExit: DEdeB = 10^k (positive float); A = k; HLhlC unchanged.\nError: A = RC_Tbg when the power overflows, through FPError, which unwinds to the FP call's\nframe (IY) and returns from the call.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, bc', de', AF'.\nKeeps: C, HL, hl'."},
        "3040": {"synopsis":"DEde/BCbc -> DEde=quotient, HLhl=remainder"},
        "3049": {"comment":"undo sub"},
        "3067": {"synopsis":"Entry inside Division, called with the alternate register set active: shifts the carry into\nthe remainder HLhl (doubling it), subtracts the divisor BCbc when it fits and shifts the\nquotient bit into DEde, repeating until A counts up to a positive value. With A at 0 or\nabove it gives exactly one more quotient bit; div_1 and sqr_1 use it so.\nEntry: HLhl = remainder; BCbc = divisor; DEde = quotient so far; A = step counter; Fc = bit\nto shift in.\nExit: DEde = quotient with the new bits; HLhl = remainder; A incremented.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, de', hl'."},
        "3086": {"synopsis":"Unsigned shift-and-add multiply, called with the alternate register set active (the callers\nload the numbers and EXX): for each step the 64-bit HLhl:DEde moves right one place and BCbc\nis added to HLhl when the bit leaving DEde is 1. Used by mul_1 (32 steps) and the integer\nmultiply div_2 (33 steps).\nEntry: HLhl = 0; DEde = multiplier; BCbc = multiplicand; A = minus the number of steps.\nExit: HLhl:DEde = product; A = 0; Fc = carry from the last addition (mul_1 then shifts once\nmore with sub_0_E422).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, de', hl'."},
        "3106": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_E40E"},
        "3119": {"synopsis":"End of function sub_0_E422"},
        "3137": {"synopsis":"The square-root loop of sqr_1, called with the alternate register set active: each step\nshifts two bits of the radicand DEde into the remainder HLhl, tries to subtract the trial\nroot formed in BCbc and keeps or restores, adding one bit to the root. Repeats until A\ncounts up to a positive value.\nEntry: HLhl = remainder; DEde = radicand bits to come; BCbc = root so far; A = minus the\nnumber of steps.\nExit: BCbc = root; HLhl = remainder; A = 0 when the steps ran out.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, bc', de', hl'."},
        "3194": {"synopsis":"The last square-root step of sqr_1, with no radicand bits left: doubles the remainder HLhl,\nincrements C and subtracts the trial root BCbc when it fits (undoing it otherwise). When the\ndoubling overflows it subtracts without the test and goes on at the loop's end (loc_0_E46F).\nEntry: HLhl = remainder; BCbc = root; A = step counter (alternate register set active).\nExit: HLhl = new remainder; C incremented when the subtraction stood; A incremented.\nChanges: AF, C, HL, hl'.","comment":"HLhl *= 2"},
        "3202": {"comment":"increment exponent"},
        "3203": {"comment":"HLhl -= BCbc"},
        "3210": {"comment":"undo sub"},
        "3217": {"synopsis":"Read byte, return Fc=1 if it's not number"},
        "3227": {"synopsis":"Read first non-blank, skip + and -"},
        "3234": {"comment":"skip leading blanks"},
        "3245": {"synopsis":"Reads the byte at IX for FPVal's number reader. An address in segment 3 ($C000-$FFFF), where\nthe FPP itself runs, is read through segment 1: the caller's S3 bank (from the call frame,\nIY+OSFrame_S3) is bound into segment 1 for the read and BLSC_SR1 is restored after it.\nEntry: IX = address; IY = FP call frame.\nExit: A = byte; DE = IX.\nChanges: A, DE, A' (segment 3 only: it then holds the old BLSC_SR1).\nKeeps: F, BC, HL, IX."},
        "3248": {"comment":"if DE not in S3 then just read it"},
        "3250": {"comment":"!! 'ld a, (de); ... ; ret z'"},
        "3257": {"comment":"store S1"},
        "3264": {"comment":"caller S3 into S1"},
        "3269": {"comment":"fix DE into S1"},
        "3272": {"comment":"read byte"},
        "3274": {"comment":"restore DE"},
        "3276": {"comment":"restore S1"},
        "3286": {"synopsis":"Writes A to the byte at HL for FPStr. An address in segment 3 ($C000-$FFFF), where the FPP\nitself runs, is written through segment 1: the caller's S3 bank (from the call frame,\nIY+OSFrame_S3) is bound into segment 1 for the write and BLSC_SR1 is restored after it.\nEntry: A = byte; HL = address; IY = FP call frame.\nExit: byte written.\nChanges: A' (segment 3 only: it then holds the old BLSC_SR1).\nKeeps: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"if HL not in S3 then just write it"},
        "3295": {"comment":"store S1"},
        "3299": {"comment":"bind caller S3 into S1"},
        "3307": {"comment":"fix HL into S1"},
        "3310": {"comment":"write byte"},
        "3312": {"comment":"restore HL"},
        "3314": {"comment":"restore S1"}
      }
    },
    "16": {
      "offsetIndex": 0,
      "regions": [
        {"start":0,"end":0,"type":"bytes"},
        {"start":1,"end":12,"type":"bytes","decode":"text"},
        {"start":13,"end":16,"type":"bytes"},
        {"start":17,"end":5459,"type":"bytes","decode":"text"},
        {"start":5460,"end":16383,"type":"bytes","decode":"fill"}
      ],
      "localLabels": [
        {"name":"FileArea","value":0},
        {"name":"WelcomeName","value":1},
        {"name":"WelcomeLength","value":13},
        {"name":"WelcomeData","value":17},
        {"name":"FileAreaFree","value":5460}
      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"The ROM's FlashStore file area, the preset 'oz' file area below the OZ banks. It holds one\nfile entry: the name's length, the name, the file's length (4 bytes, low byte first) and its\nbytes. The rest of the bank is $FF, free space for more entries.","comment":"Length of the file's name"},
        "1": {"synopsis":"The file's name, /welcome.pdd (12 characters)."},
        "13": {"synopsis":"The file's length: $00001543, 5443 bytes."},
        "17": {"synopsis":"The file, a PipeDream document: the OZ 4.7 release notes (filearea/welcome.pdd in the\nOZ source)."},
        "5460": {"synopsis":"Free space to the end of the bank: every byte $FF."}
      }
    },
    "31": {
      "offsetIndex": 0,
      "regions": [
        {"start":0,"end":16319,"type":"bytes","decode":"fill"},
        {"start":16320,"end":16383,"type":"bytes"}
      ],
      "localLabels": [
        {"name":"eprom_header","value":16376},
        {"name":"oz_watermark","value":16382}
      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "16339": {"comment":"blanks to fill-out space."},
        "16364": {"comment":"$3FEC, file area size in 16K banks, reclaim sector (0=not used)"},
        "16366": {"comment":"$3FEE, 'oz' file area watermark."},
        "16368": {"comment":"blanks to fill-out space."},
        "16376": {"synopsis":"The card header at the top of the ROM's last bank, which OZ reads to identify the card in a\nslot: the card ID \"TCL\" (Trinity Concepts Limited), the card type CX_OS ($81, an operating\nsystem card), the ROM's size in 16K banks (ROMSIZE, 14) and the subtype CB_APL (0). The \"OZ\"\nwatermark (oz_watermark) follows. Below it, from $3FC0, lie the front DOR that links to the\nfirst application DOR (the Index's, in the MTH bank) and, at $3FEC, the file area's size in\nbanks (16) and its \"oz\" watermark.","comment":"$3FF8, card ID : Trinity Concepts Limited"},
        "16379": {"comment":"$3FFB, this is an operating system card, otherwise CX_APL for external application card"},
        "16380": {"comment":"$3FFC, size of ROM in banks"},
        "16381": {"comment":"$3FFD, subtype"},
        "16382": {"synopsis":"The card's watermark: the word CT_ROM, the letters \"OZ\", which mark the card as one that\ncontains an OZ operating system with applications. It ends the card header (eprom_header).","comment":"$3FFE card contains an \"OZ\" operating system"}
      }
    }
  },
